// Auto-generated for the Unit Board
window.DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"cards":[{"w":"voracious","p":"adj.","d":"Desiring or consuming great quantities.","c":"貪婪的；貪得無厭的","s":"The voracious reader consumed three novels in a single weekend, her appetite for fiction seemingly boundless and her concentration absolute throughout the marathon reading session that left her exhausted but deeply satisfied.","t":"這位貪婪的讀者在一個週末就讀完了三本小說，她對小說的渴望似乎是無窮無盡的，整個馬拉松式閱讀讓她筋疲力盡但深感滿足。","as":"The voracious caterpillars of certain moth species can strip a mature oak of its foliage within days, a phenomenon that entomologists scrutinize closely because such defoliation may exacerbate the adverse effects of drought on entire forests.","at":"某些蛾類的幼蟲食量驚人，能在數天內啃光一棵成熟橡樹的葉子；昆蟲學家密切研究此現象，因為這種落葉可能使乾旱對整片森林造成的不良影響更加惡化。"},{"w":"indiscriminate","p":"adj.","d":"Choosing at random without careful selection.","c":"不加選擇的；任意的","s":"Environmental scientists condemned the indiscriminate use of pesticides, warning that spraying chemicals without targeting specific pests would devastate beneficial insect populations and contaminate the local water supply for years.","t":"環境科學家譴責不加選擇地使用農藥，警告說不針對特定害蟲噴灑化學品會破壞益蟲種群並多年污染當地水源。","as":"Critics of early pesticide programs argued that the indiscriminate spraying of chemicals was pernicious to songbirds and pollinators alike, since poisons meant to quell a single infestation would inevitably afflict every creature in the treated area.","at":"早期殺蟲劑計畫的批評者主張，不加選擇地噴灑化學藥劑對鳴禽和授粉昆蟲同樣有害，因為原本只為撲滅單一蟲害的毒物，必然會危害噴灑區域內的每一種生物。"},{"w":"eminent","p":"adj.","d":"Of high reputation; outstanding.","c":"傑出的；卓越的","s":"The university awarded an honorary doctorate to the eminent historian whose decades of meticulous archival research had fundamentally transformed scholarly understanding of colonial-era trade networks across three continents.","t":"大學向這位傑出的歷史學家授予榮譽博士學位，他數十年來的細緻研究從根本上改變了學術界對殖民時代三大洲貿易網絡的理解。","as":"The eminent physicist was so cognizant of her own fallibility that she routinely solicited criticism from junior colleagues, a laudable habit that belied the stereotype of the aloof scholar who scoffs at anyone lacking comparable credentials.","at":"這位傑出的物理學家深知自己也會犯錯，因此經常向資淺同事徵求批評；這種值得讚許的習慣，打破了學者高高在上、對資歷不如自己者嗤之以鼻的刻板印象。"},{"w":"steeped","p":"adj.","d":"Soaked, drenched; deeply immersed in.","c":"浸泡的；深浸於…中的","s":"The ancient city of Kyoto, steeped in centuries of imperial tradition, attracts millions of visitors annually who come to experience its meticulously preserved temples, ceremonial gardens, and enduring cultural practices.","t":"古城京都深浸於數百年的皇室傳統之中，每年吸引數百萬遊客前來體驗其精心保存的寺廟、禮儀花園和持久的文化習俗。","as":"Steeped in the folklore of her indigenous community since childhood, the novelist wove ancestral myths into her prolific body of work, creating narratives so poignant that even critics who had once derided her style came to admire them.","at":"這位小說家自幼浸淫於原住民族群的民間傳說，將祖先的神話融入她豐碩的作品中，寫出動人心弦的故事，連曾經嘲諷她文風的評論家也轉而讚賞。"},{"w":"replete","p":"adj.","d":"Completely filled or well-supplied with.","c":"充滿的；飽足的","s":"The newly opened research library was replete with invaluable resources: rare manuscript collections, digitised historical newspapers, specialised academic databases, and a dedicated quiet room for postgraduate scholars.","t":"這座新開放的研究圖書館充滿了珍貴資源：珍本手稿收藏、數位化歷史報紙、專業學術資料庫，以及一間專為研究生設置的安靜室。","as":"The medieval manuscript is replete with marginal sketches of fantastical beasts, and meticulous scholars who peruse its pages have surmised that the monks who copied it found solace from the tedium of their labor in such whimsical doodles.","at":"這份中世紀手抄本的頁緣畫滿了奇幻怪獸的素描；仔細研讀其內容的嚴謹學者推測，抄寫此書的修士藉著這些異想天開的塗鴉，在枯燥的勞動中尋得慰藉。"},{"w":"abound","p":"v.","d":"To exist in great numbers or amounts.","c":"大量存在；充滿","s":"Opportunities for talented young engineers abound in the technology sector, with innovative startups and established corporations alike competing aggressively to recruit graduates with strong analytical and collaborative skills.","t":"在科技行業，有才華的年輕工程師機會大量存在，創新型初創公司和成熟企業都在積極競爭，招募具有強大分析和協作技能的畢業生。","as":"Although myths about the ubiquitous goldfish abound, including the dubious claim that it can remember things for only a few seconds, controlled experiments have corroborated that the fish can retain learned tasks for months.","at":"雖然關於隨處可見的金魚的迷思比比皆是，包括「金魚只有幾秒記憶」這種可疑的說法，但對照實驗已證實，金魚能將學會的任務記住長達數個月。"},{"w":"technology","p":"n.","d":"Branch of knowledge dealing with engineering and applied science.","c":"技術；科技","s":"The agricultural technologyedeveloped by that ancient civilisation—sophisticated irrigation canals, crop rotation systems, and soil enrichment techniques—enabled sustained food production across arid terrain for more than two thousand years.","t":"古代文明所發展的農業技術——複雜的灌溉渠道、輪作制度和土壤改良技術——使乾旱地區的持續糧食生產維持了兩千多年。","as":"Historians caution that no technology possesses an inherent moral value, since the printing press that spread scientific knowledge across Europe also enabled zealous propagandists to inundate cities with scurrilous pamphlets attacking their religious rivals.","at":"歷史學家提醒，任何科技本身都不具備固有的道德價值；將科學知識傳遍歐洲的印刷機，同樣讓狂熱的宣傳者得以用攻擊宗教對手的下流小冊子淹沒各大城市。"},{"w":"prognosticate","p":"v.","d":"To predict or foretell a future event.","c":"預言；預測","s":"Rather than attempting to prognosticate market movements with false certainty, the experienced economist preferred to present multiple plausible scenarios, carefully quantifying the uncertainties that made precise long-term forecasting inherently unreliable.","t":"這位經驗豐富的經濟學家寧願提出多種可能情景，而不是試圖以虛假的確定性預測市場走勢，仔細量化使精確長期預測天生不可靠的不確定性。","as":"Economists who confidently prognosticate the trajectory of markets are often humbled by unforeseen shocks, such as an abrupt political schism or a sudden surge in oil prices, that render even the most comprehensive forecasting models futile.","at":"那些自信滿滿地預測市場走向的經濟學家，常被意料之外的衝擊挫了銳氣，例如突如其來的政治分裂或油價暴漲，使即便是最全面的預測模型也徒勞無功。"},{"w":"abode","p":"n.","d":"A place where one lives; a home or dwelling.","c":"住所；居所","s":"The naturalist chose a remote mountain abode as her base for a three-year field study, a modest stone cottage positioned above the treeline where rare migratory birds gathered during their annual northern passage.","t":"這位自然學家選擇了一個偏遠的山間住所作為她三年野外研究的基地，一座樸素的石頭小屋，位於樹線之上，那裡是稀有候鳥年度北遷時聚集的地方。","as":"For centuries the remote mountain monastery served as the humble abode of monks who had chosen to eschew worldly comforts, and its tranquil courtyards still offer visitors a respite from the clamor of modern cities.","at":"數百年來，這座偏遠的山中修道院一直是捨棄世俗享受之修士的簡樸居所，而其寧靜的庭院至今仍讓遊客得以暫時遠離現代都市的喧囂。"},{"w":"automaton","p":"n.","d":"A machine that operates like a person; a robot.","c":"自動機器人；機械般行動的人","s":"Critics argued that an excessive focus on standardised testing risked producing the automaton, a graduate capable of reproducing memorised information with precision but lacking the creative thinking skills demanded by contemporary employers.","t":"批評者認為，過度關注標準化考試有產生機械人的風險——一個能夠精確複述記憶信息但缺乏當代雇主所要求的創造性思維能力的畢業生。","as":"The eighteenth-century automaton known as the Mechanical Turk astonished European audiences by seemingly playing chess, but the device was an elaborate hoax: a concealed human player moved the pieces, a subterfuge that remained elusive to most spectators for decades.","at":"十八世紀名為「土耳其行棋傀儡」的自動機器，看似會下西洋棋而令歐洲觀眾驚嘆，但這台裝置其實是精心設計的騙局：一名藏身其中的棋手操控棋子，而這個詭計數十年來都讓大多數觀眾難以識破。"},{"w":"paradox","p":"n.","d":"A statement that seems absurd but may prove true.","c":"悖論；矛盾說法","s":"The physicist described a profound paradox at the heart of quantum mechanics: a subatomic particle appears to exist in multiple states simultaneously until the moment of observation, when it instantaneously collapses into a single definite position.","t":"這位物理學家描述了量子力學核心的一個深刻悖論：亞原子粒子在被觀測的那一刻之前似乎同時存在於多種狀態中，然後瞬間坍縮到一個確定的位置。","as":"The so-called paradox of thrift holds that although frugal saving is prudent for any single household, if an entire population simultaneously hoards its cash, the resulting decline in demand may precipitate a recession that leaves everyone poorer.","at":"所謂「節儉的悖論」主張，雖然節儉儲蓄對任何單一家庭而言都是明智之舉，但若全體人民同時囤積現金，隨之而來的需求下滑反而可能引發經濟衰退，讓所有人變得更貧窮。"},{"w":"realm","p":"n.","d":"A special field or domain; a kingdom.","c":"領域；王國","s":"In the realm of contemporary neuroscience, researchers are making astonishing progress in mapping the neural pathways associated with memory consolidation, emotional regulation, and the complex cognitive processes underlying human decision-making.","t":"在當代神經科學領域，研究人員在繪製與記憶鞏固、情緒調節以及人類決策背後複雜認知過程相關的神經通路方面取得了驚人進展。","as":"Once confined to the realm of science fiction, the notion of editing human genes has become feasible, prompting ethicists to admonish researchers that tools capable of eradicating hereditary maladies could also be misused for nefarious purposes.","at":"編輯人類基因的構想曾經只存在於科幻小說的領域，如今卻已切實可行，促使倫理學家告誡研究人員：能夠根除遺傳疾病的工具，也可能被濫用於邪惡的目的。"},{"w":"annals","p":"n.","d":"Historical records arranged year by year.","c":"編年史；歷史記錄","s":"This extraordinary diplomatic achievement will be permanently inscribed in the annals of international relations as a watershed moment, a meticulously documented agreement that future negotiators will study for generations as a model of constructive engagement.","t":"這一非凡的外交成就將被永久載入國際關係的編年史，作為一個分水嶺時刻，一份詳盡記錄的協議，未來的談判代表將研究幾代人。","as":"The annals kept by imperial court historians in ancient China, which recorded events year by year, are an integral resource for modern scholars, though their accounts of rival factions must be carefully evaluated for bias toward the ruling emperors.","at":"中國古代宮廷史官逐年記載大事的編年史，是現代學者不可或缺的資料來源，但其中關於敵對派系的記述，必須審慎評估是否帶有偏袒當朝皇帝的偏見。"},{"w":"compound","p":"v.","d":"To increase, add to, or make worse.","c":"使增加；加重；混合","s":"The manager's decision to withhold critical information from the project team only served to compound the existing difficulties; each day of silence allowed misunderstandings to multiply and preventable errors to accumulate into a serious crisis.","t":"這位經理決定對項目團隊隱瞞關鍵信息，這只會加重現有的困難；每一天的沉默都使誤解增多，可預防的錯誤積累成嚴重危機。","as":"Inclement weather served to compound the hapless farmers' troubles, destroying their remaining crops just as the government, citing a paucity of funds, curtailed the relief program on which they had come to depend.","at":"惡劣的天候讓這些不幸的農民雪上加霜，摧毀了他們僅存的作物；偏偏此時政府又以經費不足為由，縮減了他們賴以維生的救濟計畫。"},{"w":"tinge","p":"n.","d":"A trace, slight degree, or faint colouring.","c":"一絲；淡淡的色彩；輕微感覺","s":"There was an unmistakable tinge of melancholy in the composer's final symphony, a barely perceptible undercurrent of loss and resignation that distinguished it sharply from his earlier triumphant works and moved audiences to unexpected emotion.","t":"作曲家的最後一部交響曲中有一絲無可否認的憂鬱，一種幾乎察覺不到的失落和順從的潛流，使它與他早期的勝利作品截然不同，令觀眾感到意想不到的深刻情感。","as":"Although the composer's late symphonies are often described as jubilant, attentive listeners discern a tinge of melancholy beneath their exuberant surface, a subtle nuance that critics attribute to the privation she endured during the war.","at":"雖然這位作曲家晚期的交響曲常被形容為歡欣鼓舞，細心的聽眾卻能在其熱情洋溢的表面下察覺一絲憂鬱；評論家將這種細微的差異歸因於她在戰時所經歷的困苦。"},{"w":"badger","p":"v.","d":"To pester, nag, or annoy persistently.","c":"糾纏；煩擾；不斷騷擾","s":"The determined investigative journalist continued to badger the government spokesperson with increasingly pointed questions about the undisclosed contracts, refusing to abandon the story despite repeated deflections and formal complaints.","t":"這位堅定的調查記者繼續以越來越尖銳的問題糾纏政府發言人，詢問未公開的合同，儘管屢遭敷衍和正式投訴，仍拒絕放棄這個故事。","as":"Rather than continually badger reticent donors with phone calls, the museum's adroit fundraiser cultivated amicable relationships with them, a strategy that eventually elicited generous contributions without any hint of pressure.","at":"這家博物館手腕高明的募款人並不一再以電話糾纏態度保留的捐款人，而是與他們建立友好的關係；這項策略最終在毫無施壓的情況下，換來了慷慨的捐款。"},{"w":"implore","p":"v.","d":"To plead urgently for aid or mercy.","c":"懇求；哀求；乞求","s":"Standing before the appeals tribunal with tears streaming down her face, the defendant's elderly mother rose to implore the panel to exercise mercy and reconsider the severity of the sentence given her son's previously unblemished record.","t":"被告的老母親淚流滿面地站在上訴法庭前，起身懇求小組成員發揮憐憫心，鑑於她兒子此前無可指責的記錄，重新考慮刑罰的嚴重性。","as":"In a series of impassioned speeches, the abolitionist would implore legislators to repudiate the institution of slavery, castigating those who tolerated such flagrant cruelty merely because it enriched their affluent constituents.","at":"在一連串慷慨激昂的演說中，這位廢奴主義者懇求立法者摒棄奴隸制度，並嚴厲譴責那些只因此制度能讓富裕選民致富，便容忍如此惡劣暴行的人。"},{"w":"drudgery","p":"n.","d":"Unpleasant, dull, or exhausting hard work.","c":"苦工；枯燥乏味的工作","s":"What distinguished the passionate archivist from her colleagues was her ability to extract genuine intellectual pleasure from tasks most professionals considered sheer drudgery: the painstaking hour-by-hour cataloguing of deteriorating manuscripts.","t":"這位充滿熱情的檔案管理員與同事不同之處在於，她能從大多數專業人員認為純粹是苦工的任務中獲得真正的智識樂趣：對劣化手稿進行費力的目錄整理。","as":"Proponents of automation argue that machines will relieve workers of the mundane drudgery of assembly lines, yet skeptics contend that this sanguine vision ignores how such innovations could relegate millions of laborers to precarious, poorly paid jobs.","at":"自動化的支持者主張，機器將讓工人擺脫生產線上單調乏味的苦差事；然而懷疑者認為，這種樂觀的願景忽略了此類創新可能使數百萬勞工淪落到朝不保夕、薪資微薄的工作。"},{"w":"interminable","p":"adj.","d":"Unending; seeming to last forever.","c":"無休止的；冗長的；沒完沒了的","s":"The parliamentary debate on the constitutional amendment stretched into what felt like an interminable session; successive speakers repeated arguments exhausted hours earlier while assembled members grew visibly restless and the chamber's patience finally collapsed.","t":"關於憲法修正案的議會辯論延伸成一個感覺沒完沒了的會議；先後發言的人重複了幾小時前已用盡的論點，議員們明顯焦躁不安，議院的耐心最終崩潰了。","as":"The negotiations seemed interminable, as each acrimonious session ended in deadlock, until an astute mediator proposed a compromise that allowed both delegations to save face and finally brought about a cessation of hostilities.","at":"這場談判似乎永無止境，每一回合都在激烈的爭吵中陷入僵局；直到一位精明的調停者提出折衷方案，讓雙方代表團都能保全顏面，終於促成停戰。"},{"w":"perceive","p":"v.","d":"To understand, become aware of, or recognise.","c":"察覺；感知；理解","s":"Experienced literary critics learn to perceive layers of symbolic meaning beneath a narrative's apparently simple surface, recognising how an author's deliberate word choices and structural patterns create significance that rewards careful, sophisticated close reading.","t":"有經驗的文學評論家學會察覺敘事表面看似簡單之下的象徵意義層次，認識到作者刻意的措辭和結構模式如何創造出值得細心、精深的近距離閱讀的意義。","as":"Psychologists have found that people often perceive ambiguous remarks as hostile when they are already fretful, a cognitive tendency that can turn a laconic email from a supervisor into a source of consternation.","at":"心理學家發現，人在焦躁不安時，常會將模稜兩可的話語視為帶有敵意；這種認知傾向可能讓上司一封簡短的電子郵件，成為令人驚慌失措的來源。"}]},{"unit":2,"cards":[{"w":"laconic","p":"adj.","d":"Expressing much in few words.","c":"簡潔的；言簡意賅的","s":"The veteran detective's responses during the press conference were characteristically laconic; when asked to summarise the three-year investigation, he paused thoughtfully and offered only a single measured sentence that somehow conveyed everything the journalists needed to know.","t":"這位老練偵探在新聞發佈會上的回答一如既往地言簡意賅；當被要求總結三年調查時，他沉思片刻，只說了一句話，卻傳達了記者們所需知道的一切。","as":"Famous for her laconic replies, the reclusive poet answered each of the interviewer's verbose questions with a single sentence, yet every terse response was so incisive that it rendered his elaborate premises almost irrelevant.","at":"這位隱居的詩人以回答簡潔著稱，面對訪問者冗長的提問，每題只回一句話；然而她每一句精簡的回應都一針見血，讓訪問者精心鋪陳的前提幾乎顯得無關緊要。"},{"w":"throng","p":"n.","d":"A crowd; great number of people.","c":"人群；群眾","s":"A throng of enthusiastic supporters gathered outside the concert venue hours before the gates opened, their collective anticipation palpable as the evening darkness fell and the temperature dropped to near freezing across the city.","t":"一大群熱情的支持者在音樂會場地外聚集，在大門開放前數小時就已聚集，隨著夜幕降臨，整個城市氣溫接近冰點，他們共同的期待顯而易見。","as":"When the Berlin Wall was opened in 1989, a throng of jubilant citizens began to jostle one another at the checkpoints, and the guards, lacking orders and unable to repulse the crowd, relented in what many deem a singular moment of the Cold War.","at":"1989年柏林圍牆開放時，成群歡欣的民眾在檢查哨前互相推擠；守衛們沒有接獲命令，也無力驅退人潮，最後只得讓步——許多人認為那是冷戰中無與倫比的一刻。"},{"w":"intrepid","p":"adj.","d":"Brave, fearless in the face of danger.","c":"無畏的；勇敢的","s":"The intrepid mountaineer pressed forward through deteriorating weather conditions, her determination unwavering despite the treacherous ice fields and unpredictable avalanche risks that had forced three previous expeditions to retreat from the summit.","t":"這位無畏的登山者在惡化的天氣條件下繼續前進，儘管危險的冰原和不可預測的雪崩風險已迫使三次先前的探險撤退，她的決心毫不動搖。","as":"Undeterred by excruciating cold and the ominous creaking of the ice beneath them, the intrepid polar explorers persevered across the frozen expanse, though malnutrition had left several of them emaciated by the end of the journey.","at":"刺骨的嚴寒與腳下冰層不祥的嘎吱聲都未能嚇阻這群無畏的極地探險家，他們堅持橫越這片冰原，不過到旅程結束時，營養不良已讓其中幾人骨瘦如柴。"},{"w":"accost","p":"v.","d":"To approach and speak to boldly or aggressively.","c":"搭訕；攔住說話","s":"The aggressive street vendor would regularly accost tourists near the famous landmark, persistently urging them to purchase his counterfeit souvenirs despite their polite refusals and obvious discomfort at being approached so forcefully.","t":"這位積極的街頭小販經常在著名地標附近攔住遊客，儘管遊客禮貌地拒絕並明顯對被如此強硬地搭訕感到不舒適，他仍堅持要求他們購買假冒紀念品。","as":"Tourists complained that touts would accost them outside the train station with fallacious claims about discounted tours, prompting city officials to reprimand the vendors and ultimately oust the most belligerent offenders from the plaza.","at":"遊客抱怨，常有掮客在火車站外上前強行攔住他們，用不實的說法兜售折扣行程；市府官員因此出面訓斥這些攤販，最終將其中最蠻橫的違規者逐出廣場。"},{"w":"reticent","p":"adj.","d":"Inclined to be reserved or silent.","c":"沉默寡言的；保守的","s":"Although she was widely regarded as the department's most brilliant analyst, she remained conspicuously reticenteduring team meetings, rarely volunteering opinions unless directly asked, preferring instead to communicate her carefully considered views through written reports.","t":"儘管她被普遍認為是部門最出色的分析師，但她在團隊會議上仍然明顯沉默寡言，除非被直接詢問，否則很少主動表達意見，更喜歡通過書面報告傳達她深思熟慮的觀點。","as":"Although she was reticent about her own role in the resistance movement and declined to embellish her wartime deeds for eager journalists, archival documents later attested to the remarkable valor she displayed in smuggling refugees to safety.","at":"雖然她對自己在抵抗運動中的角色守口如瓶，也拒絕向熱切的記者渲染自己的事蹟，但後來的檔案文件證實了她冒險將難民偷渡到安全之地時所展現的非凡勇氣。"},{"w":"furtive","p":"adj.","d":"Secret, stealthy, done surreptitiously.","c":"偷偷摸摸的；鬼鬼祟祟的","s":"The security footage captured the suspect's furtive movements through the exhibition hall: crouching behind display cases, glancing repeatedly over his shoulder, and carefully avoiding the direct lines of sight from the three cameras positioned near the entrance.","t":"安全錄像捕捉到嫌疑人在展覽大廳裡偷偷摸摸的動作：蹲在展示櫃後面，一再回頭張望，並仔細避開入口附近三個攝像頭的直接視線。","as":"Throughout the dinner party the protagonist casts furtive glances at the sealed letter, a cryptic detail that serves as a harbinger of the clandestine affair that, the novel later reveals, brought about the family's ruin.","at":"在整場晚宴中，主角不斷偷偷瞄向那封密封的信件；這個隱晦的細節預示了那段祕密戀情，而小說稍後便揭露，正是這段私情導致了整個家族的毀滅。"},{"w":"felon","p":"n.","d":"A person guilty of a serious crime.","c":"重罪犯","s":"The newly enacted legislation significantly increased the mandatory sentencing guidelines for any felon convicted of financial crimes, reflecting the legislature's determination to deter sophisticated fraud schemes that had cost thousands of ordinary investors their retirement savings.","t":"新頒布的法規大幅提高了任何被判金融犯罪的重罪犯的強制量刑標準，反映了立法機構阻止複雜詐騙計劃的決心，這些計劃使數千名普通投資者損失了退休積蓄。","as":"Reformers argue that permanently barring every convicted felon from voting is an arbitrary policy that stymies rehabilitation, yet its advocates contend that such restrictions are a legitimate component of a just penal system.","at":"改革人士主張，永久剝奪所有重罪犯的投票權是一項武斷的政策，會阻礙更生；然而支持者則認為，此類限制是公正刑罰制度中合理的一環。"},{"w":"plethora","p":"n.","d":"An excess or overabundance.","c":"過多；大量","s":"The committee faced a plethora of competing proposals for the urban redevelopment project, each backed by different stakeholder groups with conflicting priorities, making it extraordinarily difficult to identify a single approach that could satisfy the community's diverse and sometimes contradictory needs.","t":"委員會面臨城市重建項目的大量競爭提案，每個提案都由優先事項相互衝突的不同利益相關方支持，這使得找到一個能夠滿足社區多樣化且有時相互矛盾的需求的單一方法變得異常困難。","as":"Psychologists contend that a plethora of options does not necessarily increase consumer satisfaction; confronted with myriad nearly identical products, shoppers often become so engrossed in comparing features that are hardly salient that they abandon the purchase altogether.","at":"心理學家主張，選擇過多未必能提高消費者的滿意度；面對無數幾乎一模一樣的產品，購物者往往埋首比較那些根本不重要的特點，最後乾脆放棄購買。"},{"w":"hapless","p":"adj.","d":"Unfortunate, unlucky, deserving of pity.","c":"倒霉的；不幸的","s":"The hapless traveller had missed his connecting flight, lost his luggage to a baggage handling error, been charged twice for his hotel room, and then discovered that his travel insurance had inadvertently lapsed three days before his departure date.","t":"這位倒霉的旅行者錯過了轉機航班，行李因行李搬運失誤而遺失，酒店費用被收取了兩次，然後發現他的旅行保險在出發日期前三天意外失效。","as":"After an enraged sperm whale sank their ship, the hapless crew of the Essex drifted for months across the turbulent Pacific, and many succumbed to starvation, an ordeal that survivors recounted in such lurid detail that it later helped inspire Moby-Dick.","at":"捕鯨船「艾塞克斯號」遭一頭暴怒的抹香鯨撞沉後，不幸的船員們在波濤洶湧的太平洋上漂流數月，許多人死於飢餓；倖存者以駭人聽聞的細節講述這段磨難，後來更成為《白鯨記》的靈感來源之一。"},{"w":"irate","p":"adj.","d":"Angry, incensed, extremely upset.","c":"暴怒的；憤慨的","s":"The irate customer demanded to speak with the store manager immediately after discovering that the expensive appliance she had purchased less than a week earlier had malfunctioned irreparably, leaving her without a working refrigerator for an entire weekend.","t":"這位暴怒的顧客在發現她不到一週前購買的昂貴電器已無法修復地發生故障後，立即要求與商店經理談話，這使她整個週末都沒有可用的冰箱。","as":"Irate commuters began to bristle at the transit authority's perfunctory apology for a week of delays, deriding the statement as an ineffectual attempt to placate passengers without addressing the underlying problems.","at":"憤怒的通勤族對交通局針對整週延誤所發表的敷衍道歉愈來愈不滿，嘲諷那份聲明不過是想安撫乘客、卻未觸及根本問題的無效之舉。"},{"w":"pretext","p":"n.","d":"A false reason given to justify an action.","c":"藉口；托辭","s":"The auditors suspected that the sudden reorganisation was merely a pretext for eliminating employees who had raised concerns about accounting irregularities, since all three dismissed staff members had filed formal complaints with the compliance department within the previous six months.","t":"審計人員懷疑突然的重組僅僅是消除那些對會計違規行為提出關切的員工的藉口，因為三名被解雇的員工都在前六個月內向合規部門提交了正式投訴。","as":"Historians note that expansionist empires frequently cited the protection of their merchants as a pretext for invasion, deploying gunboats to subjugate coastal kingdoms and wrest control of lucrative trade routes from local rulers.","at":"歷史學家指出，擴張主義的帝國經常以保護本國商人為藉口發動侵略，派遣砲艇征服沿海王國，並從當地統治者手中強行奪取利潤豐厚的貿易路線。"},{"w":"fabricate","p":"v.","d":"To make up, invent, or construct falsely.","c":"捏造；製造","s":"The investigation concluded that the witness had completely fabricate his alibi, presenting a detailed but entirely fictional account of his whereabouts on the evening in question, supported by receipts that forensic accountants subsequently proved had been digitally altered.","t":"調查得出結論，證人完全捏造了他的不在場證明，提供了一個詳細但完全虛假的關於他在涉案當晚下落的陳述，並得到了法證會計師隨後證明已被數字篡改的收據支持。","as":"The scandal erupted when investigators discovered that the once prestigious researcher had chosen to fabricate data in dozens of studies, an egregious breach of ethics that forced journals to expunge his articles from the scientific record.","at":"調查人員發現這位一度聲望卓著的研究者竟在數十篇研究中捏造數據，醜聞隨即爆發；這種嚴重違反學術倫理的行為，迫使各期刊將他的論文從科學紀錄中刪除。"},{"w":"adroit","p":"adj.","d":"Skillful, clever, dexterous.","c":"熟練的；機敏的","s":"The adroit negotiator managed the delicate diplomatic discussions with remarkable finesse, skilfully redirecting contentious exchanges before they escalated, identifying areas of unexpected common ground, and gradually building the mutual trust necessary for a substantive agreement.","t":"這位熟練的談判代表以非凡的技巧管理著微妙的外交討論，在爭議性交流升級之前巧妙地將其轉向，找到意想不到的共同點，並逐漸建立達成實質性協議所需的相互信任。","as":"An adroit negotiator, the envoy could defuse the most fractious disputes with a well-timed quip, persuading implacable rivals to concur on terms that each had previously denounced in public during years of stalled talks.","at":"這位特使是手腕靈巧的談判高手，能以一句恰到好處的妙語化解最棘手的紛爭，說服原本勢不兩立的對手同意彼此先前都曾在多年停滯不前的談判中公開譴責過的條款。"},{"w":"gesticulate","p":"v.","d":"To move the arms energetically while speaking.","c":"打手勢；揮動手臂","s":"The passionate professor would gesticulate wildly throughout his lectures, sweeping his arms across imaginary diagrams, pointing emphatically at invisible equations, and occasionally knocking papers from his desk in moments of particular intellectual excitement during complex theoretical explanations.","t":"這位充滿激情的教授在講課時會瘋狂地打手勢，揮動雙臂穿越假想的圖表，有力地指向看不見的方程式，偶爾在特別興奮的知識時刻，在複雜的理論解釋過程中把文件從桌子上打落。","as":"When the impresario began to gesticulate wildly from the wings, the tenor realized that the orchestra had skipped an entire verse, and his voice grew tremulous, though the audience, dazzled by the flamboyant staging, scarcely noticed the blunder.","at":"當劇院經理在側台開始激動地比手畫腳時，那位男高音才驚覺樂團竟跳過了整段歌詞，聲音頓時顫抖起來；所幸被華麗舞台效果吸引的觀眾幾乎沒有察覺這個失誤。"},{"w":"vigilant","p":"adj.","d":"Watchful, alert, on the lookout.","c":"警惕的；警覺的","s":"Border security personnel are trained to remain constantly vigilant for signs of suspicious behaviour, even during long overnight shifts when fatigue naturally reduces concentration and the probability of an actual incident appears negligibly low to the untrained observer.","t":"邊境安全人員接受訓練，要時刻保持警惕，注意可疑行為的跡象，即使在長時間的夜班期間，當疲勞自然降低注意力，而實際事件發生的可能性對未受訓練的觀察者來說似乎微乎其微。","as":"Public health officials must remain vigilant even during apparent lulls, because detecting an incipient outbreak early is the only reliable way to contain a virulent pathogen that may lie latent in a population for weeks.","at":"即使在疫情看似平息之際，公共衛生官員仍須保持警覺，因為及早發現初期爆發的疫情，是遏止一種可能在人群中潛伏數週的強毒性病原體唯一可靠的方法。"},{"w":"avid","p":"adj.","d":"Eager, enthusiastic, deeply interested.","c":"渴望的；熱切的","s":"An avid collector of early twentieth-century scientific instruments, she had spent thirty years accumulating a remarkable private museum's worth of astrolabes, barometers, and surveying equipment, each piece meticulously restored and accompanied by detailed provenance documentation.","t":"作為一位對二十世紀初科學儀器充滿渴望的收藏家，她花了三十年積累了價值一個私人博物館的星盤、氣壓計和測量設備，每件物品都經過精心修復，並附有詳細的來源文件。","as":"An avid amateur astronomer, the retired schoolteacher was so assiduous in cataloguing variable stars that her meticulous records, compiled over many years, became an invaluable asset to professional researchers tracking stellar changes.","at":"這位退休教師是熱衷的業餘天文學家，她孜孜不倦地為變星編目，多年累積的嚴謹紀錄成為追蹤恆星變化的專業研究人員極其寶貴的資產。"},{"w":"cajole","p":"v.","d":"To coax, persuade using flattery.","c":"哄騙；用甜言蜜語說服","s":"The experienced sales representative had perfected her ability to cajole reluctant clients into signing contracts, combining genuine enthusiasm for her products with carefully calibrated compliments that made even the most sceptical prospects feel understood and valued.","t":"這位經驗豐富的銷售代表已完善了她哄騙不情願的客戶簽訂合同的能力，將她對產品的真誠熱情與精心校準的讚美結合起來，使即使是最持懷疑態度的潛在客戶也感到被理解和重視。","as":"Rather than coerce the reluctant villagers into relocating, the colonial administrator tried to cajole them with lavish gifts and flattering promises, but the village elders soon came to perceive the duplicity behind his generosity.","at":"這位殖民地行政官員並未強迫不情願的村民遷居，而是以豐厚的禮物和諂媚的承諾哄騙他們；然而村中長老很快便看穿了他慷慨背後的欺詐。"},{"w":"rudimentary","p":"adj.","d":"Elementary, basic, undeveloped.","c":"基本的；初步的","s":"The archaeological site revealed surprisingly rudimentary stone tools suggesting that the early inhabitants of the valley possessed only the most fundamental technological capabilities, relying primarily on naturally shaped rocks rather than purposefully crafted implements for their daily survival activities.","t":"考古遺址揭示了令人驚訝的初步石器，表明山谷早期居民只擁有最基本的技術能力，主要依靠天然形狀的石頭而非有目的製作的工具來進行日常生存活動。","as":"Although early steam engines were rudimentary machines that wasted much of their fuel, resourceful inventors continued to modify their designs until the engines could power the mammoth textile mills that would come to dominate industrial Britain.","at":"雖然早期的蒸汽機只是浪費大量燃料的簡陋機器，但足智多謀的發明家不斷改良其設計，直到它們能驅動後來主宰英國工業的巨型紡織廠。"},{"w":"enhance","p":"v.","d":"To intensify, improve, heighten.","c":"提高；增強；改善","s":"Regular aerobic exercise has been shown to significantly enhance cognitive performance in adults over fifty, with neuroimaging studies demonstrating measurable increases in hippocampal volume and corresponding improvements in both working memory capacity and long-term information retention.","t":"有規律的有氧運動已被證明能顯著提高五十歲以上成年人的認知表現，神經影像學研究表明海馬體體積可測量地增加，工作記憶能力和長期信息保留都有相應的改善。","as":"Conservators used multispectral imaging to enhance the faded text of the charred scrolls, a technique that allowed scholars to decipher garbled passages without having to jeopardize the fragile papyrus and yielded incontrovertible evidence of works long presumed lost.","at":"文物保存人員運用多光譜影像技術，使燒焦卷軸上褪色的文字更加清晰，讓學者得以在不危及脆弱莎草紙的情況下解讀原本殘缺難辨的段落，並找到確鑿的證據，證明那些長久以來被認定已失傳的作品確實存在。"},{"w":"nuance","p":"n.","d":"A slight variation in meaning, tone, or colour.","c":"細微差別；微妙之處","s":"The experienced diplomat understood that the most important aspects of international negotiations were rarely the explicit terms but rather the subtle nuance of language — the careful choice of a particular word over its near-synonym — that signalled genuine willingness to compromise on fundamental issues.","t":"這位經驗豐富的外交官明白，國際談判中最重要的方面很少是明確的條款，而是語言的微妙差別——在特定詞語與其近義詞之間的謹慎選擇——這標誌著在基本問題上真正願意妥協。","as":"Translators of classical Chinese poetry face a daunting task, since a single character may carry manifold associations, and any attempt to convey every nuance in English risks producing cumbersome, incoherent lines that betray the original's impeccable economy.","at":"翻譯中國古典詩詞是一項艱鉅的任務，因為單一個字可能蘊含多重聯想；若試圖用英文傳達每一個細微的意涵，往往會寫出累贅又支離破碎的詩句，辜負了原作無懈可擊的精煉。"}]},{"unit":3,"cards":[{"w":"bristle","p":"v.","d":"To stiffen with anger or become irritated.","c":"發怒；豎起","s":"The senior researcher visibly bristle when her junior colleague publicly questioned the methodology of her landmark study, her composure fracturing momentarily before she regained her professional poise and addressed the criticism with measured, carefully chosen words.","t":"當她的初級同事公開質疑她的里程碑式研究方法論時，這位高級研究員明顯地發怒了，她的鎮定瞬間破裂，然後她重新恢復職業風度，用謹慎、精心選擇的言語回應了批評。","as":"Many longtime residents began to bristle at the developer's ostentatious plans for a luxury resort, which they feared would raze the town's historic waterfront, long a haven for the fishing families who had lived there for generations.","at":"許多老居民對開發商浮誇的豪華度假村計畫愈來愈惱火，擔心這項計畫會夷平鎮上歷史悠久的濱水區——那裡長久以來一直是世代定居於此的漁民家庭的避風港。"},{"w":"caustic","p":"adj.","d":"Sarcastic, biting, corrosive.","c":"刻薄的；腐蝕性的","s":"The theatre critic's caustic review of the opening night performance left the director deeply shaken; his demolition of every aspect of the production—the acting, the staging, the script adaptation—was so comprehensive and precisely worded that it became notorious throughout the industry.","t":"劇評家對首夜演出的刻薄評論讓導演深感震驚；他對演出各個方面的徹底批評——表演、舞台設計、劇本改編——如此全面且措辭精確，以至於在整個行業中聲名狼藉。","as":"The critic's caustic review, which disparaged the novel as a labyrinth of pretentious digressions, nettled the author so deeply that he published a lengthy diatribe in response, prolonging a feud that delighted the literary press.","at":"這位評論家尖酸刻薄的書評，貶斥那部小說是一座充滿矯揉造作離題敘述的迷宮，深深激怒了作者，使他發表了一篇長篇抨擊文章作為回應，讓這場令文學媒體樂不可支的筆戰延燒下去。"},{"w":"cessation","p":"n.","d":"A stopping, end, or pause.","c":"停止；中止","s":"The international community welcomed the announced cessation of hostilities as a promising first step toward a durable peace settlement, though veteran diplomats cautioned that previous ceasefires in the region had invariably collapsed within weeks of their initial announcement.","t":"國際社會歡迎宣布的停止敵對行動，將其視為實現持久和平解決方案的有希望的第一步，儘管資深外交官警告說，該地區以前的停火在最初宣布後的幾週內無一例外地崩潰了。","as":"Researchers warn that a cessation of the Atlantic currents that carry warm water northward, though still a matter of conjecture, could wreak havoc on European agriculture and render vast tracts of farmland no longer viable.","at":"研究人員警告，向北輸送暖水的大西洋洋流若停止運行——儘管目前仍屬推測——可能對歐洲農業造成嚴重破壞，使大片農地不再適合耕作。"},{"w":"condolence","p":"n.","d":"An expression of sympathy for grief.","c":"哀悼；慰問","s":"The president sent a formal letter of condolence to the bereaved family, acknowledging the irreplaceable loss represented by the scientist's death and pledging that the nation's research institutions would honour his legacy by continuing the groundbreaking work he had begun.","t":"總統向悲傷的家屬發送了一封正式的哀悼信，承認科學家的去世所代表的無可替代的損失，並承諾國家研究機構將通過繼續他所開創的開創性工作來紀念他的遺產。","as":"Setting aside years of bitter political skirmishes, the senator sent a heartfelt letter of condolence to his rival's widow, an altruistic gesture that surprised his own entourage and earned him the grudging respect of his adversaries.","at":"這位參議員拋開多年來激烈的政治交鋒，寫了一封誠摯的弔唁信給對手的遺孀；這番無私的舉動令他自己的隨行人員都大感意外，也為他贏得了對手們不甘情願的敬意。"},{"w":"dupe","p":"n.","d":"A person easily tricked or deceived.","c":"易受騙的人；被欺騙者","s":"The elaborate investment fraud had operated for nearly six years before investigators uncovered it, leaving thousands of ordinary savers as financial dupes who had been systematically misled by falsified performance records and manipulated account statements.","t":"這個精心設計的投資詐騙在調查人員發現之前運作了近六年，使數千名普通儲蓄者成為財務上被欺騙的人，他們被偽造的業績記錄和操縱的帳戶報表系統性地誤導。","as":"The swindler found an easy dupe in the gullible heir, who, flattered by promises of extraordinary profits, poured his inheritance into a mining venture the swindler had concocted, unaware of the sordid scheme until his fortune had vanished.","at":"這名騙子在那位容易受騙的繼承人身上找到了好下手的冤大頭；繼承人被豐厚獲利的承諾沖昏了頭，把遺產全數投入騙子捏造的礦業投資，直到財產化為烏有才發現這場卑劣的騙局。"},{"w":"euphemism","p":"n.","d":"A mild or indirect expression used instead of a harsh one.","c":"委婉語；婉轉說法","s":"The corporate announcement relied heavily on euphemism to obscure the severity of the financial situation: 'workforce optimisation' replaced 'mass redundancies,' 'strategic consolidation' described the closure of profitable regional offices, and 'rightsizing' signified the elimination of nearly two hundred positions.","t":"公司公告嚴重依賴委婉語來掩蓋財務狀況的嚴重性：'勞動力優化'取代了'大規模裁員'，'戰略整合'描述了盈利區域辦事處的關閉，'合理調整規模'意味著消除近兩百個職位。","as":"Critics argue that describing mass layoffs as a restructuring is a euphemism that conceals the tangible hardships endured by workers, a rhetorical veneer that executives adopt to avoid controversial headlines.","at":"批評者認為，把大規模裁員說成「重組」是一種委婉說法，掩蓋了員工實際承受的苦楚；這層修辭的外衣，不過是企業高層用來避免引發爭議性新聞標題的手段。"},{"w":"inadvertent","p":"adj.","d":"Unintentional, accidental.","c":"無意的；非故意的","s":"The laboratory's inadvertent contamination of the control samples, caused by a technician's failure to replace protective gloves between procedures, rendered three months of carefully conducted clinical trial data scientifically invalid and forced a complete restart of the experimental protocol.","t":"實驗室對對照樣本的無意污染是由技術人員在操作程序之間未能更換防護手套造成的，這使三個月精心進行的臨床試驗數據在科學上無效，並迫使完全重新啟動實驗方案。","as":"The discovery of penicillin was famously inadvertent: Alexander Fleming noticed that a mold contaminating one of his culture plates had thwarted the growth of bacteria, a fortuitous observation that eventually transformed the treatment of lethal infections.","at":"盤尼西林的發現是出了名的無心插柳：亞歷山大・弗萊明注意到，污染了培養皿的黴菌阻止了細菌的生長；這個偶然的觀察最終徹底改變了致命感染的治療方式。"},{"w":"incipient","p":"adj.","d":"Just beginning to exist or appear.","c":"初期的；開始的","s":"The meteorologists identified the incipient tropical storm system gathering strength in the mid-Atlantic as a potential Category 4 hurricane, issuing preliminary advisories to coastal communities while acknowledging considerable uncertainty in predicting its eventual trajectory.","t":"氣象學家確認了在大西洋中部聚集力量的初期熱帶風暴系統可能成為4級颶風，向沿海社區發出初步預警，同時承認預測其最終路徑存在相當大的不確定性。","as":"Because incipient tumors rarely produce overt symptoms, physicians recommend regular screenings that can detect malignant cells early, when treatment is most effective and the outlook for recovery is most propitious.","at":"由於初期腫瘤很少出現明顯症狀，醫師建議定期篩檢，以便及早發現惡性細胞——此時治療的成效最好，康復的前景也最為樂觀。"},{"w":"incongruous","p":"adj.","d":"Out of place, not fitting the surroundings.","c":"不協調的；不相稱的","s":"The ultra-modern glass skyscraper appeared utterly incongruous among the carefully preserved Victorian terraces of the historic neighbourhood, its reflective surfaces and angular geometry creating a jarring visual contrast that divided local residents sharply between those who celebrated it as progressive architecture and those who condemned it as vandalism.","t":"這座超現代的玻璃摩天大樓在歷史街區精心保存的維多利亞式排屋中顯得完全不協調，其反射表面和有棱角的幾何形狀創造了強烈的視覺對比，將當地居民尖銳地分為讚揚其為進步建築的人和譴責其為破壞行為的人。","as":"When I. M. Pei unveiled his glass pyramid for the courtyard of the Louvre, many critics inveighed against it as incongruous with the palace's classical facade, yet the structure, once anathema to Parisian traditionalists, has become a landmark in its own right.","at":"貝聿銘為羅浮宮中庭設計的玻璃金字塔揭曉時，許多評論家猛烈抨擊它與宮殿古典立面格格不入；然而這座一度令巴黎傳統派深惡痛絕的建築，如今已成為一座名副其實的地標。"},{"w":"infamous","p":"adj.","d":"Having a terrible reputation.","c":"臭名昭著的；聲名狼藉的","s":"The infamous financial collapse of 1929 remains the defining economic catastrophe of the twentieth century, its cascading consequences — bank failures, mass unemployment, and political instability — reshaping the global economic order and leaving psychological scars that influenced policy decisions for decades.","t":"1929年臭名昭著的金融崩潰仍然是二十世紀決定性的經濟災難，其連鎖後果——銀行倒閉、大規模失業和政治不穩定——重塑了全球經濟秩序，留下了影響政策決策數十年的心理創傷。","as":"Ponzi schemes take their name from Charles Ponzi, the infamous swindler whose name became an epithet for such fraud; he would perpetrate a scam in which early investors were paid with later investors' money, so its inexorable collapse was assured from the start.","at":"龐氏騙局得名於惡名昭彰的騙子查爾斯・龐茲——他的名字後來成了這類詐騙的代稱；他所犯下的詐欺是用後來投資人的錢支付早期投資人，因此其崩潰從一開始便無可避免。"},{"w":"jostle","p":"v.","d":"To push, bump, or elbow roughly.","c":"推擠；碰撞","s":"Commuters were forced to jostle their way through the unusually dense morning crowd at the railway station, the combination of delayed trains, school holiday traffic, and a major sporting event having created an unprecedented level of congestion that the station's infrastructure was clearly not designed to accommodate.","t":"通勤者被迫推擠穿過火車站異常密集的早晨人群，延誤的列車、學校假期交通和一場重大體育賽事的結合造成了前所未有的擁擠程度，車站的基礎設施顯然沒有被設計成能夠容納這種情況。","as":"During the frenzy of the clearance sale's opening minutes, shoppers began to jostle one another at the entrance, and the timorous store manager, overwhelmed by the clamor, could only scurry to the back office and summon security.","at":"清倉大拍賣一開始的那幾分鐘陷入一片瘋狂，顧客在入口處你推我擠；膽怯的店經理被喧鬧聲嚇得不知所措，只能匆匆躲進後方辦公室，叫保全前來處理。"},{"w":"lackluster","p":"adj.","d":"Lacking brilliance or vitality, dull.","c":"缺乏光澤的；平淡的","s":"The team's lackluster performance during the championship semi-final—characterised by uncharacteristic defensive errors, missed scoring opportunities, and a general absence of the creative energy that had distinguished them throughout the regular season—baffled supporters and sports analysts alike.","t":"球隊在錦標賽半決賽中平淡的表現——以不尋常的防守失誤、錯過的得分機會以及在整個常規賽中使他們與眾不同的創造力普遍缺失為特徵——讓支持者和體育分析人士都感到困惑。","as":"Following a lackluster quarter that many analysts viewed as a barometer of faltering consumer confidence, the retailer's executives abandoned their sporadic experiments with luxury goods and decided to revert to the affordable merchandise that had first made the brand popular.","at":"許多分析師將這一季平淡無奇的業績視為消費者信心動搖的指標；在此之後，這家零售商的高層放棄了斷斷續續推出奢侈品的嘗試，決定回歸當初讓品牌走紅的平價商品。"},{"w":"loathe","p":"v.","d":"To hate, detest intensely.","c":"厭惡；憎恨","s":"She had come to genuinely loathe the daily commute into the city centre — the crowded carriages, the relentless noise, the mechanical announcements — and had begun seriously researching remote working arrangements that might liberate her from two hours of daily underground travel.","t":"她已真正厭惡每天前往市中心的通勤——擁擠的車廂、無情的噪音、機械的廣播——並開始認真研究可能讓她從每天兩小時地下交通中解脫出來的遠程工作安排。","as":"Although he professed to loathe the gregarious world of literary salons, the reclusive author secretly craved the praise of critics, a paradox that his closest confidant described in letters published after his death.","at":"這位隱居的作家雖聲稱厭惡熱鬧喧騰的文學沙龍圈，私底下卻渴望得到評論家的讚揚；他最親近的知己在他死後出版的書信中描述了這種矛盾。"},{"w":"mundane","p":"adj.","d":"Ordinary, of the world, lacking excitement.","c":"平凡的；世俗的","s":"The philosopher argued that genuine wisdom could be discovered in the most mundane activities — the washing of dishes, the folding of laundry, the preparation of an unremarkable meal — provided one approached these everyday tasks with sufficient mindfulness and contemplative attention.","t":"哲學家認為，真正的智慧可以在最平凡的活動中發現——洗碗、疊衣服、準備一頓普通的飯食——前提是一個人以足夠的正念和沉思的注意力來對待這些日常任務。","as":"Archaeologists contend that seemingly mundane artifacts, such as cooking pots and discarded tools, deserve more than the cursory attention they once received, because they illuminate how ordinary people lived, whether as sedentary farmers or as nomadic herders.","at":"考古學家主張，看似平凡無奇的文物，例如炊具和廢棄工具，應受到比過去匆匆一瞥更多的重視，因為它們揭示了一般人的生活樣貌——無論是定居的農民，還是逐水草而居的牧民。"},{"w":"ominous","p":"adj.","d":"Threatening, suggesting something bad.","c":"不祥的；凶兆的","s":"The ominous gathering of dark clouds on the western horizon, combined with the sudden stillness of the air and the barometric pressure readings that had been dropping steadily for six hours, persuaded the regatta organisers to postpone the afternoon's sailing races indefinitely.","t":"西方地平線上不祥的烏雲聚集，加上空氣突然靜止和氣壓計讀數在六小時內持續下降，說服帆船賽組織者無限期推遲下午的帆船比賽。","as":"In the days before Vesuvius erupted, ominous tremors shook the region, but the residents of Pompeii, long accustomed to such rumblings, had grown lax and dismissed any premonition of disaster until the mountain began to emit towering clouds of ash and gas.","at":"維蘇威火山爆發前的幾天，不祥的震動撼動了整個地區，但早已習慣這類隆隆聲的龐貝居民卻掉以輕心，對任何災難的預感都不予理會，直到火山開始噴出高聳的火山灰與氣體雲。"},{"w":"reprimand","p":"v.","d":"To sharply disapprove or criticise officially.","c":"譴責；申斥","s":"The senior partner formally reprimand the associate for his failure to disclose a material conflict of interest before accepting the case, making clear that such lapses in professional judgment would not be tolerated regardless of the pressure of workload or the apparent urgency of client demands.","t":"高級合夥人正式申斥了這位助理，因為他在接受案件前未能披露重大利益衝突，明確表示無論工作量的壓力或客戶需求的明顯緊迫性如何，這種職業判斷上的失誤都不會被容忍。","as":"The league commissioner chose to reprimand the coach publicly after his histrionics on the sideline incited a fray among spectators, warning that any further blatant misconduct would result in his suspension forthwith.","at":"聯盟主席決定公開斥責這位教練，因為他在場邊誇張做作的表演引發觀眾間的鬥毆；主席並警告，若再有任何明目張膽的不當行為，將立即予以停賽。"},{"w":"repudiate","p":"v.","d":"To reject, refuse, or disown.","c":"拒絕；否認；與…斷絕關係","s":"The candidate was forced to publicly repudiate the inflammatory statements made by one of her most prominent campaign supporters, issuing a carefully worded statement that distanced herself from the remarks while avoiding a complete rupture with the donor whose financial backing remained essential.","t":"候選人被迫公開拒絕承認她最著名的競選支持者之一發表的煽動性言論，發表了一份措辭謹慎的聲明，與這些言論保持距離，同時避免與那位財政支持仍然至關重要的捐助者完全決裂。","as":"In his old age the philosopher came to repudiate the theories of his youth, conceding that the utopia he had once envisioned naively ignored the innate selfishness and cupidity that, he now believed, would doom any such experiment.","at":"這位哲學家晚年否定了自己年輕時的理論，坦承他曾構想的那個烏托邦天真地忽視了人類與生俱來的自私與貪婪，而他如今相信，這些天性注定會讓任何類似的實驗失敗。"},{"w":"stipulate","p":"v.","d":"To specify as a required condition.","c":"規定；約定","s":"The contract clearly stipulate that all deliverables must be submitted in both digital and physical formats at least ten working days before the scheduled presentation, with any deviation from this requirement requiring written approval from both the project director and the client's legal representative.","t":"合同明確規定所有可交付成果必須在預定演示前至少十個工作日以數字和實體格式提交，對此要求的任何偏差都需要項目主任和客戶法律代表的書面批准。","as":"The philanthropist's bequest came with strict conditions: the agreement would stipulate that the university use the funds solely for scholarships for indigent students, and any attempt to divert the money would invalidate the gift, a safeguard intended to preclude misuse by future administrators.","at":"這位慈善家的遺贈附帶嚴格的條件：協議將明訂大學只能將這筆資金用於清寒學生的獎學金，任何挪用的企圖都會使整筆捐贈失效——這道防護措施旨在杜絕未來的行政主管濫用資金。"},{"w":"tremulous","p":"adj.","d":"Quivering, shaking, timid.","c":"顫抖的；膽怯的","s":"Her voice was noticeably tremulous as she took the podium to deliver the eulogy for her long-time mentor, the emotional weight of the occasion briefly overwhelming the composure she had carefully maintained throughout the preceding three days of memorial services and private gatherings.","t":"當她走上講台為她的長期導師致悼詞時，她的聲音明顯顫抖，這個場合的情感重量短暫地壓倒了她在此前三天的紀念儀式和私人聚會中精心保持的鎮定。","as":"In a tremulous voice, the octogenarian survivor recounted how soldiers had besieged her village, and her testimony proved pertinent to the tribunal's inquiry into the alleged atrocities committed during the war.","at":"這位八十多歲的倖存者以顫抖的聲音，述說士兵如何包圍她的村莊；她的證詞與法庭針對戰爭期間那些涉嫌暴行所進行的調查息息相關。"},{"w":"wrest","p":"v.","d":"To take away by force, to twist.","c":"奪取；費力取得","s":"The opposition coalition spent three years attempting to wrest political control from the incumbent government, ultimately succeeding when widespread economic discontent and a series of damaging corruption revelations finally persuaded a sufficient number of centrist voters to abandon their traditional allegiances.","t":"反對派聯盟花了三年時間試圖從現任政府手中奪取政治控制權，最終在廣泛的經濟不滿和一系列破壞性腐敗揭露最終說服了足夠多的中間派選民放棄其傳統效忠後取得了成功。","as":"Through a series of daring campaigns, the rebel commander managed to wrest the capital from the regime's monolithic grip, but his victory soured when a coterie of ambitious advisers began to vie for power, plunging the inchoate government into turmoil.","at":"這位叛軍指揮官透過一連串大膽的戰役，從政權鐵板一塊的掌控中奪下首都；然而當一群野心勃勃的幕僚開始爭權奪利，使剛成形的新政府陷入動盪時，他的勝利很快便變了調。"}]},{"unit":4,"cards":[{"w":"alacrity","p":"n.","d":"Brisk and cheerful readiness.","c":"敏捷；活潑；欣然","s":"The young intern responded to every assignment with remarkable alacrity, arriving early, staying late, and completing even tedious administrative tasks with evident enthusiasm that impressed the senior managers and earned her a permanent position before her three-month trial period had concluded.","t":"這位年輕實習生以非凡的欣然回應每一個任務，早到晚退，甚至對繁瑣的行政任務也表現出明顯的熱情，給高級管理人員留下了深刻的印象，並在她三個月試用期結束前獲得了永久職位。","as":"The volunteers responded to the rising floodwaters with remarkable alacrity, building a bulwark of sandbags along the riverbank within hours and offering sanctuary to families whose homes the torrent had begun to saturate.","at":"志工們以驚人的速度欣然投入，因應不斷上漲的洪水，數小時內便沿著河岸堆起一道沙包防線，並為房屋開始被大水浸透的家庭提供避難之所。"},{"w":"aspirant","p":"n.","d":"A person who eagerly seeks advancement.","c":"渴望者；有志者","s":"Every aspirant for the prestigious fellowship was required to submit a fifteen-page research proposal, three letters of academic recommendation, and a detailed five-year plan demonstrating how the funding would advance both their individual scholarly development and the broader field.","t":"每位渴望獲得這一著名獎學金的人都被要求提交一份十五頁的研究提案、三封學術推薦信以及一份詳細的五年計劃，展示資金將如何促進他們個人的學術發展和更廣泛的領域。","as":"For every aspirant to the national orchestra, the audition is a grueling ordeal: candidates must display not only technical virtuosity but also the poise to remain phlegmatic while a panel of exacting judges evaluates every phrase.","at":"對每一位想進入國家樂團的有志者而言，試演都是一場嚴苛的考驗：應試者不僅須展現精湛的技巧，還必須在一群嚴格的評審逐句評估其演奏時保持冷靜沉著。"},{"w":"belligerent","p":"adj.","d":"Hostile, aggressive, eager to fight.","c":"好戰的；好鬥的","s":"The belligerent nation's repeated violations of its neighbours' territorial waters, combined with increasingly inflammatory rhetoric from its leadership, prompted the international community to consider imposing comprehensive economic sanctions as a deterrent to further provocative military actions.","t":"這個好戰國家一再侵犯鄰國領海，加上其領導層越來越煽動性的言辭，促使國際社會考慮實施全面經濟制裁，以阻止進一步的挑釁性軍事行動。","as":"The increasingly belligerent rhetoric of both governments alarmed neutral observers, who feared that a single untoward incident at the border could eventuate in full-scale war unless mediators persuaded the leaders to desist from their provocative military exercises.","at":"兩國政府日益好戰的言論令中立的觀察者憂心忡忡，他們擔心邊境只要發生一起意外事件，就可能演變成全面戰爭，除非調停者能說服雙方領袖停止挑釁性的軍事演習。"},{"w":"belittle","p":"v.","d":"To make seem less important, to dismiss.","c":"貶低；輕視","s":"The manipulative manager would routinely belittle his team members' contributions during client presentations, casually reassigning credit for their most innovative ideas to himself while simultaneously implying that the actual work had been produced under his close and essential supervision.","t":"這位操縱性的經理會在客戶演示中習慣性地貶低他團隊成員的貢獻，隨意將他們最具創新性的想法的功勞歸於自己，同時暗示實際工作是在他密切和重要的監督下完成的。","as":"Nineteenth-century academic critics tended to belittle the Impressionists, dismissing their loose brushwork as rudimentary and unfinished, yet the movement, conceived as the antithesis of rigid academic conventions, would eventually be revered as a paragon of artistic innovation.","at":"十九世紀的學院派評論家往往貶低印象派畫家，認為他們鬆散的筆觸粗淺而未完成；然而這場原本被視為與僵化學院傳統背道而馳的運動，最終卻被尊為藝術創新的典範。"},{"w":"brash","p":"adj.","d":"Impudent, bold, overconfident.","c":"傲慢的；魯莽的","s":"The brash young executive alienated his more experienced colleagues during his first board meeting by dismissing three decades of accumulated institutional knowledge with a casual wave of his hand and proposing radical operational changes that demonstrated a fundamental misunderstanding of the industry's regulatory constraints.","t":"這位魯莽的年輕主管在他的第一次董事會會議上疏遠了更有經驗的同事，輕描淡寫地否定了三十年積累的機構知識，並提出了激進的運營變革，這表明他對行業監管約束存在根本性的誤解。","as":"The brash young entrepreneur boasted to investors that his start-up would revolutionize the industry within a year, but his temerity soon gave way to chagrin when auditors revealed that the company's finances were murky at best.","at":"這位自以為是的年輕創業家向投資人誇口，說他的新創公司一年內就會徹底改變整個產業；但當審計人員揭露公司財務狀況充其量只能說是混沌不明時，他的魯莽隨即轉為懊惱。"},{"w":"castigate","p":"v.","d":"To punish or criticise harshly.","c":"嚴懲；苛評","s":"The editorial board publicly castigate the journalist for fabricating quotes in his award-winning investigation, arguing that his deliberate dishonesty had not only discredited the publication but had undermined public trust in investigative journalism at a moment when that trust was already fragile.","t":"編委會公開嚴厲批評這位記者在其獲獎調查報道中捏造引語，認為他故意的不誠實不僅敗壞了出版物的名譽，而且在公眾對調查性新聞的信任已經脆弱的時刻進一步破壞了這種信任。","as":"In a scathing editorial, the newspaper continued to castigate the city council for its negligent oversight of the chemical plant, arguing that officials' complicity with the company had allowed toxic waste to permeate the region's groundwater with impunity.","at":"在一篇措辭嚴厲的社論中，該報持續痛批市議會對化工廠監督失職，指出官員與企業同流合污，才讓有毒廢料肆無忌憚地滲入該地區的地下水。"},{"w":"disdain","p":"n.","d":"Contempt, scorn for something beneath one.","c":"蔑視；輕蔑","s":"She regarded the popular entertainment industry with barely concealed disdain, finding its commercial priorities antithetical to the artistic integrity she had pursued throughout her career, and consistently declining lucrative offers that would have compromised the uncompromising aesthetic standards she had set for herself.","t":"她對流行娛樂行業幾乎不加掩飾地蔑視，認為其商業優先事項與她在整個職業生涯中追求的藝術誠信相悖，並一貫拒絕那些有損她為自己設定的一絲不苟的美學標準的豐厚邀約。","as":"Many urbane Victorian aristocrats regarded commerce with disdain, viewing trade as unworthy of a gentleman, yet their debt-ridden estates were often rescued only through marriages to the progeny of affluent industrialists.","at":"許多溫文儒雅的維多利亞時代貴族對經商嗤之以鼻，認為從事貿易有失紳士身分；然而他們負債累累的莊園，往往只能靠與富裕實業家的子女聯姻才得以保全。"},{"w":"dregs","p":"n.","d":"The most worthless part, the residue.","c":"渣滓；糟粕","s":"The social reformer dedicated her career to advocating for those society had cast aside as the dregs — the homeless, the addicted, the formerly incarcerated — arguing that a community's true character was revealed not by how it treated its most successful members but by how it treated its most vulnerable.","t":"這位社會改革者致力於為社會所拋棄的那些人倡導——無家可歸者、成癮者、前囚犯——認為一個社區的真實品格不是通過它如何對待最成功的成員來揭示，而是通過它如何對待最脆弱的人來揭示。","as":"Dickens often populated his novels with characters drawn from the dregs of Victorian London, such as pickpockets, destitute orphans, and itinerant peddlers, using their plight to declaim against callous policies that allowed poverty to remain rampant.","at":"狄更斯經常以維多利亞時代倫敦社會底層的人物入書，例如扒手、窮苦孤兒和四處流浪的小販，藉由他們的困境大聲疾呼，抨擊那些放任貧窮蔓延的冷酷政策。"},{"w":"feint","p":"n.","d":"A false attack intended to deceive.","c":"佯攻；假動作","s":"The boxer executed a brilliant feint with his left hand that caused his opponent to drop his guard in anticipation of a body blow, creating precisely the defensive opening needed for the decisive right-hand counterpunch that ended the fight in the seventh round.","t":"拳擊手用左手做出了一個精彩的佯攻，使對手在預期腹部打擊時放低了防守，恰好創造了第七回合結束比賽的決定性右手反擊所需的防守空隙。","as":"The army's conspicuous advance toward the northern port was merely a feint, intended to lure defenders away from the capital while the main force made a surreptitious march through the mountains to harass the enemy's exposed rear, leaving its startled generals to recoil in confusion.","at":"軍隊大張旗鼓地向北方港口挺進，其實只是一記佯攻，目的是把守軍引離首都；與此同時，主力部隊悄悄翻山越嶺，襲擾敵軍暴露在外的後方，讓措手不及的敵方將領在混亂中節節退縮。"},{"w":"frenzy","p":"n.","d":"Wild excitement or uncontrolled activity.","c":"狂熱；狂暴","s":"The announcement of the limited-edition release sent collectors into a frenzy of competitive bidding, with prices escalating to twenty times the retail value within the first three hours as enthusiasts around the world competed simultaneously through multiple online auction platforms.","t":"限量版發行的消息讓收藏家陷入競爭性競標的狂熱中，在最初三小時內，隨著世界各地的愛好者通過多個在線拍賣平台同時競爭，價格升至零售價值的二十倍。","as":"News of the gold discovery in California set off a frenzy of migration, as thousands of men who aspired to instant wealth abandoned their domiciles and endured tortuous journeys westward, though few of them ever struck it rich.","at":"加州發現黃金的消息掀起一股移民狂潮，成千上萬渴望一夜致富的人拋下家園，踏上曲折艱辛的西行之路，然而真正發財的人寥寥無幾。"},{"w":"intimidate","p":"v.","d":"To overawe, frighten into submission.","c":"恐嚇；威嚇","s":"The defence attorney argued that the prosecution had attempted to intimidate the key witness by revealing her home address to the media, creating a climate of fear that had materially affected her willingness to testify freely and had therefore compromised the fundamental fairness of the trial.","t":"辯護律師認為，檢方試圖通過向媒體透露關鍵證人的家庭地址來恐嚇她，製造了一種恐懼氣氛，這實質上影響了她自由作證的意願，因此損害了審判的基本公正性。","as":"Regimes determined to repress dissent often try to intimidate journalists by branding them accomplices of foreign powers, yet such tactics can frustrate their own aims, since the persecution of reporters tends to provoke international condemnation.","at":"執意壓制異議的政權，常把記者扣上外國勢力共犯的帽子來加以恐嚇；然而這類手段可能適得其反，因為迫害記者往往會招致國際譴責。"},{"w":"laceration","p":"n.","d":"A jagged wound or tear.","c":"撕裂傷；裂傷","s":"The emergency surgeon noted a deep laceration along the patient's forearm that had damaged several tendons and required immediate microsurgical repair to restore full mobility, estimating that complete rehabilitation would take between six and nine months of intensive physical therapy.","t":"急診外科醫生注意到患者前臂有一道深深的撕裂傷，損傷了幾條肌腱，需要立即進行顯微外科修復以恢復完全的活動能力，估計完全康復需要六到九個月的密集物理治療。","as":"Although the deep laceration on the wan hiker's leg looked alarming to his squeamish companions, the paramedic calmly cleaned and bandaged the wound, explaining that perhaps a week would elapse before he could walk without pain.","at":"這名登山客臉色蒼白，腿上深深的撕裂傷讓他那些見血就怕的同伴驚慌不已；但醫護人員冷靜地為傷口清潔包紮，並解釋大概要過一個星期，他才能走路不感到疼痛。"},{"w":"octogenarian","p":"n.","d":"A person in their eighties.","c":"八十多歲的人","s":"The remarkable octogenarian completed his first marathon at the age of eighty-four, finishing in just under six hours and attributing his extraordinary physical condition to fifty years of daily walking, a Mediterranean diet, and what he described as a constitutional refusal to acknowledge the limitations others expected of his age.","t":"這位非凡的八十多歲老人在八十四歲時完成了他的第一場馬拉松，用時不到六小時，並將他非凡的身體狀況歸因於五十年的每日步行、地中海飲食以及他所描述的對他人對其年齡期望的局限性的根本性拒絕。","as":"Although friends and family repeatedly importuned her to retire, the octogenarian sculptor continued to produce monumental bronzes whose jaunty, playful forms seemed incongruous with her frail physique and steadily failing eyesight.","at":"儘管親友們一再懇求她退休，這位八旬雕塑家仍持續創作巨型青銅雕像；作品輕快活潑的造型，與她孱弱的身軀和日漸衰退的視力形成強烈反差。"},{"w":"promulgate","p":"v.","d":"To make known officially, to announce.","c":"公布；頒布","s":"The new environmental regulations, carefully drafted over eighteen months of consultation with industry representatives, environmental scientists, and community groups, were formally promulgate by the minister on the first day of the parliamentary session, taking effect immediately upon publication in the official gazette.","t":"新的環境法規在與行業代表、環境科學家和社區團體進行了十八個月的協商後精心起草，由部長在議會會議的第一天正式頒布，在官方公報發布後立即生效。","as":"Shortly after seizing power, the junta hastened to promulgate decrees banning public assemblies and the display of placards, a measure that political scientists construe as symptomatic of the regime's insecurity rather than its strength.","at":"軍政府奪權後不久，便急忙頒布禁止公眾集會和展示標語牌的法令；政治學者將這項措施解讀為該政權缺乏安全感的徵兆，而非其實力的展現。"},{"w":"pugnacious","p":"adj.","d":"Eager to fight, quarrelsome.","c":"好鬥的；爭強好勝的","s":"The pugnacious senator had built her entire political brand around confrontational rhetoric, relishing the opportunity to challenge opponents in televised debates with a barely restrained aggression that her supporters celebrated as fearless advocacy and her critics denounced as theatrical bullying.","t":"這位好鬥的參議員圍繞對抗性言辭建立了她整個政治品牌，享受在電視辯論中以幾乎無法壓抑的攻擊性挑戰對手的機會，她的支持者將此稱讚為無畏的倡導，而她的批評者則譴責這是戲劇性的霸凌。","as":"Known for his pugnacious debating style, the senator relished every chance to interject caustic remarks while opponents spoke, but his asperity eventually alienated even the allies whose votes he needed to pass his own legislation.","at":"這位參議員以好鬥的辯論風格聞名，總愛趁對手發言時插入尖酸刻薄的評論；然而他的嚴苛態度最終連他推動法案所需倚重的盟友也疏遠了。"},{"w":"scoff","p":"v.","d":"To speak with contempt or mock.","c":"嘲笑；嘲弄","s":"The established scientists initially scoff at the young researcher's hypothesis that stress hormones could directly influence genetic expression across generations, dismissing it as theoretically implausible — a reaction that made his subsequent experimental confirmation of the effect all the more professionally satisfying.","t":"既有的科學家最初嘲弄這位年輕研究員關於壓力荷爾蒙可以直接影響跨代基因表達的假設，認為這在理論上是不可能的——這種反應使他隨後對這一效應的實驗確認在職業上更加令人滿足。","as":"Many incredulous nineteenth-century physicians would scoff at Ignaz Semmelweis's claim that doctors' unwashed hands were spreading a virulent fever among new mothers, since the notion that healers could be culpable for their patients' deaths wounded their professional pride.","at":"十九世紀許多半信半疑的醫師，對塞麥爾維斯「醫師未洗淨的雙手正在產婦間散播致命熱病」的說法嗤之以鼻，因為「醫者可能要為病人之死負責」這種觀念，嚴重傷害了他們的專業自尊。"},{"w":"scurrilous","p":"adj.","d":"Coarse, vulgar, abusive.","c":"粗俗的；下流的","s":"The candidate's legal team threatened defamation proceedings against the anonymous blogger who had published a series of scurrilous accusations about his personal conduct, arguing that the allegations were not only entirely fabricated but had been specifically designed to destroy his reputation during the final critical weeks of the campaign.","t":"候選人的法律團隊威脅要對匿名博主提起誹謗訴訟，該博主發布了一系列關於他個人行為的粗俗指控，認為這些指控不僅完全是捏造的，而且是專門設計在競選最後關鍵幾週破壞他的名譽。","as":"During the bitterly contested American presidential election of 1800, partisan newspapers would spew scurrilous attacks with remarkable venom, denouncing Thomas Jefferson and others of his ilk as godless radicals while mocking John Adams as a would-be monarch.","at":"在1800年競爭激烈的美國總統大選中，黨派報紙以驚人的惡毒口吻大肆發表粗鄙的人身攻擊，痛斥湯瑪斯・傑佛遜及其同類是不信神的激進分子，同時嘲諷約翰・亞當斯一心想當君主。"},{"w":"solace","p":"n.","d":"Comfort or consolation in distress.","c":"安慰；慰藉","s":"She found unexpected solace in the discipline of long-distance running during the difficult months following her diagnosis, the rhythmic physicality of the activity providing a temporary but genuine respite from the relentless anxiety that had otherwise come to dominate her waking hours.","t":"在診斷後的困難幾個月裡，她在長跑的紀律中找到了意想不到的安慰，這項活動的有節奏的身體性提供了一個短暫但真實的喘息機會，否則無情的焦慮將主導她的清醒時光。","as":"Confined for years to a dank subterranean cell, the dissident found solace in composing poems on scraps of paper, and those doleful verses, smuggled out by sympathetic guards, eventually inspired the campaign that secured his ultimate release.","at":"這位異議人士被囚禁在陰濕的地下牢房多年，靠著在紙片上寫詩尋求慰藉；這些由同情他的獄卒偷偷帶出的哀傷詩句，最終激發了一場社會運動，讓他終獲自由。"},{"w":"sordid","p":"adj.","d":"Dirty, base, morally degraded.","c":"骯髒的；卑鄙的","s":"The investigative documentary exposed the sordid conditions in which migrant workers were being housed by the construction contractor, revealing overcrowded dormitories without adequate sanitation facilities, unpaid wages withheld through illegal debt arrangements, and systematic violations of basic employment rights.","t":"調查紀錄片揭露了建築承包商為外來工人提供的骯髒生活條件，揭示了沒有足夠衛生設施的過度擁擠宿舍、通過非法債務安排扣押的未付工資以及對基本就業權利的系統性侵犯。","as":"The journalist's exposé revealed the sordid underside of the city's construction boom, a web of extortion in which officials demanded kickbacks from contractors, rewarded those who paid with lucrative deals, and gave their own relatives nominal posts that were, in effect, sinecures.","at":"這名記者的揭發報導，揭露了該市建築熱潮背後骯髒的內幕——那是一張勒索之網：官員向承包商索取回扣，以利潤豐厚的合約回報付錢者，還讓自己的親戚擔任有名無實的職位，實際上就是坐領乾薪的閒差。"},{"w":"tangible","p":"adj.","d":"Having actual form, concrete, real.","c":"有形的；實體的；可感知的","s":"The years of painstaking diplomatic negotiations had finally produced tangible results: a formal treaty signed by all seven regional governments, a joint commission established to oversee implementation, and a binding arbitration mechanism to resolve disputes that inevitably arose during the five-year transition period.","t":"多年艱苦的外交談判終於產生了有形的成果：一份由所有七個地區政府簽署的正式條約、一個成立以監督執行的聯合委員會，以及一個在五年過渡期內不可避免地出現爭議時解決爭端的具有約束力的仲裁機制。","as":"Although investments in basic science rarely yield tangible returns in the short term, economists warn legislators not to terminate such funding, since inquiries that once seemed abortive or irrelevant have repeatedly given rise to transformative inventions.","at":"雖然投資基礎科學在短期內鮮少帶來具體的回報，經濟學家仍警告立法者不要終止這類經費，因為那些一度看似失敗或無關緊要的研究，一再催生出改變世界的發明。"}]},{"unit":5,"cards":[{"w":"acrimonious","p":"adj.","d":"Bitter, sharp, harsh in manner.","c":"嚴厲的；辛辣的","s":"The divorce proceedings became increasingly acrimonious as both parties refused to accept the mediator's compromise proposals, the accumulated grievances of a fifteen-year marriage ultimately expressing themselves in a courtroom battle that dragged on for nearly two years and consumed a substantial portion of the joint estate.","t":"離婚訴訟變得越來越嚴厲，雙方都拒絕接受調解員的妥協提案，十五年婚姻積累的委屈最終在法庭鬥爭中表達出來，這場鬥爭持續了將近兩年，消耗了共同財產的相當大一部分。","as":"Isaac Newton and Gottfried Leibniz became embroiled in an acrimonious dispute over who had first invented calculus, a feud fraught with national pride in which Newton's zealous allies cast Leibniz as an interloper who had stolen ideas, a charge most historians now reject.","at":"艾薩克・牛頓與哥特佛萊德・萊布尼茲為了究竟誰先發明微積分而陷入激烈的爭執；在這場夾雜民族自尊的論戰中，牛頓狂熱的支持者把萊布尼茲描繪成竊取他人構想的闖入者，但如今大多數歷史學家都不接受這項指控。"},{"w":"admonish","p":"v.","d":"To warn or reprove gently but seriously.","c":"警告；勸誡","s":"The judge admonish the attorney for repeatedly interrupting the opposing counsel during cross-examination, making clear that a third violation of courtroom protocol would result in a formal finding of contempt and an immediate adjournment of the proceedings at the attorney's professional expense.","t":"法官警告律師在交叉盤問期間一再打斷對方律師，明確表示第三次違反法庭程序規則將導致正式認定藐視法庭，並立即休庭，費用由律師個人承擔。","as":"Rather than issue a public reprimand to the student who had flouted the honor code, the professor chose to admonish him privately, warning that such a rash shortcut could permanently tarnish his academic reputation.","at":"這位教授並未公開斥責那名違反榮譽守則的學生，而是選擇私下告誡他，提醒他這種輕率的捷徑可能永久玷污他的學術聲譽。"},{"w":"clandestine","p":"adj.","d":"Secret, undercover, kept hidden.","c":"秘密的；暗中的","s":"The clandestine meeting between the foreign minister and opposition leaders had been arranged through a series of intermediaries specifically to prevent any official record of the contact, both sides recognising that public knowledge of the discussions would undermine their respective negotiating positions.","t":"外交部長與反對派領導人之間的秘密會議是通過一系列中間人安排的，專門防止任何關於接觸的官方記錄，雙方都認識到公眾對討論的了解將破壞各自的談判立場。","as":"During the Nazi occupation, members of the French Resistance operated clandestine printing presses in cellars, concealed caches of weapons beneath farmhouses, and risked execution to galvanize a populace that the occupiers hoped would remain supine.","at":"納粹佔領期間，法國抵抗運動成員在地窖裡經營祕密印刷所，在農舍下方藏匿武器，冒著被處決的風險喚醒民眾——而佔領者原本期望這些民眾始終消極順從。"},{"w":"concur","p":"v.","d":"To agree, to act in harmony.","c":"同意；一致","s":"After reviewing the independent geological survey commissioned to verify the initial findings, all three expert consultants concur that the proposed construction site was unsuitable due to unstable subsurface conditions that posed an unacceptable risk of structural failure within the projected building's first decade.","t":"在審查了委託以核實初步調查結果的獨立地質調查後，所有三位專家顧問一致同意，擬建的建築工地由於地下條件不穩定而不適合，在預計建築的頭十年內存在結構失敗的不可接受風險。","as":"Climate scientists overwhelmingly concur that human activity is the paramount cause of recent global warming, yet they caution that its regional consequences remain nebulous, making it imperative that coastal cities prepare for a broad gamut of possible outcomes.","at":"氣候科學家普遍同意，人類活動是近來全球暖化的首要成因；但他們也提醒，暖化在各地區造成的影響仍不明確，因此沿海城市必須為各種可能的後果預作準備。"},{"w":"construe","p":"v.","d":"To make a deduction, to interpret.","c":"解釋；推斷","s":"The ambiguous wording of the contractual clause had been construe in two entirely incompatible ways by the respective legal teams: the plaintiff's lawyers arguing it established an unconditional obligation, while the defendant's counsel maintained it merely created a discretionary option subject to prevailing market conditions.","t":"合同條款的模糊措辭被各自的法律團隊以兩種完全不相容的方式解釋：原告律師認為它確立了無條件義務，而被告律師則堅持認為它僅創建了一個受主流市場條件約束的可選擇選項。","as":"Analysts warned that the neighboring state might construe the joint naval exercises as a hostile provocation, and they urged both governments to communicate their intentions with candor lest a misunderstanding trigger an escalation that neither side desired.","at":"分析人士警告，鄰國可能將這次聯合海上軍演解讀為帶有敵意的挑釁，因此敦促兩國政府坦誠溝通彼此的意圖，以免誤會引發雙方都不樂見的衝突升級。"},{"w":"culprit","p":"n.","d":"The person guilty of an offence.","c":"罪犯；肇事者","s":"After months of investigation, the forensic accountants identified the culprit behind the systematic embezzlement: a mid-level financial controller who had exploited weaknesses in the company's internal audit procedures to divert nearly two million pounds over a four-year period.","t":"經過幾個月的調查，法證會計師確定了系統性侵吞背後的肇事者：一名中層財務控制員，他利用公司內部審計程序的漏洞，在四年內轉移了近兩百萬英鎊。","as":"When cholera swept through London's Soho district in 1854, physician John Snow mapped the deaths with meticulous care and identified the culprit, a contaminated public water pump, challenging the prevalent theory, endorsed by many eminent doctors, that disease spread through foul air.","at":"1854年霍亂席捲倫敦蘇活區時，醫師約翰・斯諾一絲不苟地標出死亡病例的分布，找出了罪魁禍首——一座遭到污染的公共水泵，從而挑戰了當時許多知名醫師所支持、認為疾病經由污濁空氣傳播的主流理論。"},{"w":"distraught","p":"adj.","d":"Confused and upset, deeply distressed.","c":"心煩意亂的；極度苦惱的","s":"The distraught mother arrived at the police station having received no news of her missing daughter for seventy-two hours, her desperation evident in her inability to complete sentences coherently and the way she clutched the photograph she had brought to help officers identify the girl.","t":"這位心煩意亂的母親在七十二小時內沒有收到關於她失蹤女兒的任何消息後來到警察局，她的絕望從她無法連貫地完成句子以及她緊握著帶來幫助警官識別女孩的照片的方式中顯而易見。","as":"Distraught relatives gathered at the edge of the debris, imploring rescue teams to keep searching, and even the most sedate volunteers found it difficult to remain composed amid such palpable anguish.","at":"心急如焚的家屬聚集在瓦礫堆旁，懇求救難隊繼續搜索；面對如此真切的悲痛，即使是最沉穩的志工也難以保持鎮定。"},{"w":"duplicity","p":"n.","d":"Cunning deception, double-dealing.","c":"表裡不一；欺騙","s":"The tribunal concluded that the contractor had engaged in deliberate duplicity, simultaneously assuring the client that construction was proceeding to schedule while knowingly concealing structural defects that would have triggered immediate contract termination and substantial financial penalties.","t":"法庭得出結論，承包商蓄意欺騙，一方面向客戶保證施工正在按計劃進行，同時故意隱瞞本會觸發立即終止合同和大額罰款的結構缺陷。","as":"The double agent's duplicity went undetected for years, as he fed his superiors mendacious reports while passing secrets to the enemy in covert meetings, a betrayal that, once exposed, besmirched the reputation of the entire intelligence service.","at":"這名雙面間諜的欺瞞多年來都未被察覺，他一面向上級呈交不實的報告，一面在祕密會面中把機密交給敵方；這場背叛一經揭發，整個情報機構的名聲都因此蒙羞。"},{"w":"duress","p":"n.","d":"Compulsion by threat, forcible restraint.","c":"脅迫；強制","s":"The defendant's legal team argued that the confession had been obtained under duress, presenting medical evidence of sleep deprivation during the interrogation, testimony from a custody officer who had witnessed coercive questioning techniques, and contemporaneous notes showing that requests for legal representation had been repeatedly denied.","t":"被告的法律團隊認為認罪是在脅迫下獲得的，提供了審訊期間睡眠剝奪的醫學證據、目睹強制性盤問技術的羈押官員的證詞，以及顯示法律代理請求被多次拒絕的同期筆記。","as":"Courts have repeatedly held that a confession extracted under duress cannot be trusted, since vulnerable suspects facing threats may acknowledge crimes they never committed, and judges deem such coercive tactics abhorrent to the principle of due process.","at":"法院一再裁定，在脅迫下取得的自白不可採信，因為面臨威脅的弱勢嫌犯可能會承認自己從未犯下的罪行；法官也認為，這類強迫手段嚴重違背正當法律程序的原則。"},{"w":"egregious","p":"adj.","d":"Remarkably bad, outstandingly offensive.","c":"極壞的；令人震驚的","s":"The independent audit revealed an egregious misallocation of charitable funds: nearly forty percent of donations intended for direct humanitarian relief had been absorbed by administrative costs, consultancy fees, and what the auditors diplomatically described as 'unexplained expenditure of uncertain benefit.'","t":"獨立審計揭示了一個極其嚴重的慈善資金分配不當問題：近百分之四十用於直接人道主義救援的捐款被行政費用、諮詢費用以及審計師外交性地描述為'不確定收益的不明支出'所吸收。","as":"The auditors uncovered egregious accounting fraud at the energy firm, where executives driven by insatiable avarice had hidden enormous debts in shell companies, triggering a collapse that left thousands of employees bereft of their pensions.","at":"審計人員在這家能源公司發現了極其惡劣的會計舞弊：高層受貪得無厭的欲望驅使，把巨額債務藏在空殼公司中，最終導致公司倒閉，讓數千名員工的退休金化為烏有。"},{"w":"elicit","p":"v.","d":"To draw forth or bring out.","c":"引出；引起","s":"The skilled therapist used a combination of open-ended questioning, extended silence, and carefully chosen reflective observations to elicit from her client a full account of the traumatic events that had been suppressed for over two decades, creating a safe environment for memories that had previously been inaccessible.","t":"熟練的治療師使用開放式問題、延長的沉默和精心選擇的反思性觀察的組合，從客戶那裡引出了被壓抑超過二十年的創傷事件的完整陳述，為以前無法訪問的記憶創造了一個安全的環境。","as":"Seasoned anthropologists know that blunt questions seldom elicit honest answers about taboo subjects, so they cultivate congenial relationships with community members over many months before cautiously broaching sensitive topics such as illness or death.","at":"經驗豐富的人類學家深知，直截了當的提問很少能引出關於禁忌話題的真實答案，因此他們會花上好幾個月與社區成員建立融洽的關係，然後才小心翼翼地觸及疾病或死亡等敏感議題。"},{"w":"ethics","p":"n.","d":"The moral principles governing conduct.","c":"道德規範；倫理","s":"The medical school's revised curriculum devoted considerably more attention to clinical ethics than its predecessor, reflecting the faculty's conviction that the ability to navigate complex moral dilemmas was as professionally essential as any technical competency for doctors working within modern healthcare systems.","t":"醫學院修訂後的課程比其前身更加關注臨床道德，反映了教師的信念，即對於在現代醫療保健系統中工作的醫生來說，駕馭複雜道德困境的能力在職業上與任何技術能力一樣重要。","as":"As algorithms increasingly decide who receives loans or parole, scholars of ethics warn that systems trained on historical data may perpetuate inveterate prejudices while cloaking them in an aura of infallible objectivity.","at":"隨著演算法日益左右誰能獲得貸款或假釋，倫理學者警告：以歷史資料訓練出來的系統，可能延續根深柢固的偏見，同時為這些偏見披上一層看似絕對客觀、不容置疑的外衣。"},{"w":"flagrant","p":"adj.","d":"Outrageous, conspicuously bad.","c":"公然的；惡名昭彰的","s":"The referee had no hesitation in dismissing the player following what he characterised as a flagrant violation of the rules of fair play — a deliberate and unprovoked assault on an opponent that had occurred in full view of both officials and the substantial crowd watching from the stands.","t":"裁判毫不猶豫地罰下了這名球員，他將其描述為明目張膽地違反公平競技規則——這是對對手的蓄意和無端的侵犯，在官員和看台上大量觀眾的眼前發生。","as":"The regime's flagrant violation of the ceasefire, which it breached within hours by shelling civilian neighborhoods, drew a sharp rebuke even from its staunchest adherents, who had previously been loath to criticize it in public.","at":"該政權公然違反停火協議，簽約數小時內便砲轟平民社區，此舉甚至招致其最忠實擁護者的嚴厲斥責——而這些擁護者先前一向不願公開批評它。"},{"w":"impunity","p":"n.","d":"Freedom from punishment or consequences.","c":"免受懲罰；不受制裁","s":"Human rights organisations repeatedly condemned the culture of impunity that allowed officials responsible for documented atrocities to continue serving in senior government positions, arguing that the international community's failure to support accountability mechanisms sent a devastating message to future perpetrators.","t":"人權組織一再譴責允許對有記錄的暴行負責的官員繼續擔任政府高級職位的有罪不罰文化，認為國際社會未能支持問責機制向未來的施暴者發出了毀滅性的信息。","as":"For years the warlord's militia plundered villages with impunity, since the fledgling government's jurisdiction over the mountainous provinces was largely theoretical and corrupt officials had little incentive to impede his raids.","at":"多年來，這名軍閥的民兵肆無忌憚地劫掠村莊，因為剛成立的政府對山區各省的管轄權大多只是紙上談兵，而貪腐的官員也沒有什麼動機去阻止他的襲擊。"},{"w":"inane","p":"adj.","d":"Silly, empty of intelligence or meaning.","c":"愚蠢的；無意義的","s":"The editorial board rejected the columnist's piece as too inane for publication, noting that its argument consisted entirely of unsupported generalisations, that every substantive claim had been made more eloquently by previous writers, and that the humorous anecdotes included were neither original nor particularly amusing.","t":"編委會以過於愚蠢為由拒絕刊登這位專欄作家的文章，指出其論點完全由無支撐的概括組成，每一個實質性主張都曾被以前的作家更雄辯地提出，所包含的幽默趣聞既不原創也不特別有趣。","as":"Exasperated by the inane questions about her wardrobe that garrulous reporters kept posing at the press conference, the physicist gave a terse but cogent reply, reminding them that her discovery, not her clothing, was the news.","at":"記者會上，多話的記者不斷追問這位物理學家的穿著打扮，這些愚蠢的問題讓她十分惱火；她簡短而有力地回應，提醒他們真正的新聞是她的發現，而不是她的衣著。"},{"w":"inexorable","p":"adj.","d":"Inflexible, impossible to stop.","c":"無情的；不可阻擋的","s":"The inexorable advance of the glacial melt, accelerating year on year in response to rising atmospheric temperatures, presented the scientific community with increasingly compelling evidence that the tipping points identified in early climate models had already been passed in several critical subsystems.","t":"冰川融化的無情推進，隨著大氣溫度的上升每年加速，向科學界呈現出越來越有力的證據，表明早期氣候模型中確定的臨界點已在幾個關鍵子系統中被超越。","as":"Low-lying island nations face the inexorable advance of rising seas, which threatens to obliterate coastal villages and render ancestral lands uninhabitable, a plight that their leaders have urged wealthier countries to palliate through emissions cuts and adaptation funding.","at":"地勢低窪的島國正面臨海平面無情地步步上升，沿海村落可能因此消失，祖先留下的土地也將無法居住；這些國家的領袖已敦促較富裕的國家透過減排與調適資金來減輕他們的困境。"},{"w":"paucity","p":"n.","d":"Scarcity, a lack or shortage.","c":"缺乏；不足","s":"The medical review identified a troubling paucity of clinical evidence supporting the widespread prescription of the medication for paediatric patients, with only three small-scale studies having been conducted in the relevant age group, none of which had involved a sample size sufficient for statistically reliable conclusions.","t":"醫學審查發現支持向兒科患者廣泛開具這種藥物的臨床證據嚴重不足，只有三項小規模研究在相關年齡組中進行，沒有一項涉及足夠大的樣本量以得出統計上可靠的結論。","as":"Historians of early medieval Europe must contend with a paucity of reliable documents, relying instead on archaeological artifacts and a handful of extant chronicles whose monastic authors freely mingled fact with superstition.","at":"研究中世紀早期歐洲的歷史學家必須面對可靠文獻匱乏的難題，只能轉而依靠考古文物和寥寥幾部現存的編年史，而這些編年史的修士作者往往把史實與迷信混為一談。"},{"w":"pernicious","p":"adj.","d":"Harmful, causing subtle damage.","c":"有害的；致命的","s":"The researcher argued that the most pernicious effect of chronic sleep deprivation was not the obvious impairment of immediate cognitive performance but rather the insidious, cumulative damage to the neural consolidation processes essential for long-term memory formation and emotional regulation.","t":"研究人員認為，慢性睡眠剝奪最有害的影響不是立即認知表現的明顯損害，而是對長期記憶形成和情緒調節必不可少的神經鞏固過程的隱性、累積性損害。","as":"Public health officials regard the pernicious spread of medical misinformation online as a serious detriment to efforts to eradicate measles, since anxious parents are often more susceptible to vivid anecdotes than to statistical evidence.","at":"公共衛生官員認為，網路上醫療錯誤資訊的悄然擴散，對根除麻疹的努力造成嚴重危害，因為焦慮的家長往往比較容易被生動的個人經歷所左右，而非統計證據。"},{"w":"rampant","p":"adj.","d":"Going unchecked, widespread, unrestrained.","c":"猖獗的；盛行的","s":"The charity's annual report documented rampant malnutrition across the drought-affected region, with field researchers recording severe acute malnutrition rates in children under five that exceeded internationally recognised emergency thresholds in seventeen of the twenty-three districts surveyed.","t":"慈善機構的年度報告記錄了受乾旱影響地區猖獗的營養不良問題，實地研究人員記錄的五歲以下兒童嚴重急性營養不良率在調查的二十三個地區中有十七個超過了國際公認的緊急閾值。","as":"During the hyperinflation that afflicted Weimar Germany, price increases became so rampant that workers rushed to spend their wages within hours, and the savings of thrifty households became worthless, a catastrophic loss that fueled political strife.","at":"威瑪德國陷入惡性通貨膨脹期間，物價失控狂飆，工人一領到薪水便在數小時內趕緊花掉，而節儉家庭的積蓄則變得一文不值；這場災難性的損失加劇了政治動盪。"},{"w":"tolerate","p":"v.","d":"To put up with, allow, bear.","c":"容忍；忍受","s":"The headteacher made clear at the beginning of the academic year that the school would no longer tolerate any form of bullying behaviour, whether physical, verbal, or digital, and that all incidents would be investigated systematically and result in sanctions proportionate to their severity and any pattern of repetition.","t":"校長在學年開始時明確表示，學校將不再容忍任何形式的欺凌行為，無論是身體的、言語的還是數字的，所有事件都將系統地調查，並根據其嚴重程度和任何重複模式採取相應的制裁措施。","as":"Despite its puny size, the tardigrade can tolerate extreme temperatures, intense radiation, and even the vacuum of space, a phenomenon scientists attribute to its ability to enter a dormant state in which it remains virtually inert until conditions improve.","at":"水熊蟲雖然體型微小，卻能耐受極端溫度、強烈輻射，甚至太空的真空環境；科學家將這種現象歸因於牠能進入休眠狀態，在此狀態下幾乎完全靜止不動，直到環境好轉為止。"}]},{"unit":6,"cards":[{"w":"affluent","p":"adj.","d":"Rich, having abundant wealth.","c":"富裕的","s":"The affluent suburb had consistently ranked among the top ten most desirable residential areas in the country for the past fifteen years, its property values sustained by excellent schools, low crime rates, and convenient transport links to the city's main financial and commercial districts.","t":"這個富裕的郊區在過去十五年中一直被列為全國最受歡迎的十大住宅區之一，其房產價值由優秀的學校、低犯罪率以及便捷的通往城市主要金融和商業區的交通連接所支撐。","as":"Although the affluent suburb boasted a plethora of private galleries, critics construed its lavish spending on art as a pretext for social climbing rather than a genuine commitment to nurturing local talent.","at":"雖然這個富裕的郊區擁有大量私人畫廊，評論家卻將其在藝術上的揮霍解讀為攀附社會地位的藉口，而非真心致力於培育在地人才。"},{"w":"chagrin","p":"n.","d":"A feeling of disappointment or humiliation.","c":"懊惱；羞愧","s":"Much to her considerable chagrin, the seasoned diplomat discovered that she had memorised entirely the wrong name for the newly appointed foreign minister, addressing him incorrectly throughout the thirty-minute introductory meeting before a junior aide quietly passed her a corrective note.","t":"令她相當懊惱的是，這位資深外交官發現她記錯了新任外交部長的名字，在三十分鐘的介紹性會議中一直錯誤地稱呼他，直到一位初級助手悄悄遞給她一張更正便條。","as":"To the chagrin of the eminent physicist, her rival's simplistic experiment elicited far more public acclaim than her own decades of meticulous research, a paradox she attributed to the media's appetite for easy stories.","at":"令這位傑出物理學家懊惱的是，對手那個過於簡化的實驗所引起的公眾讚譽，遠遠超過她自己數十年嚴謹的研究；她將這種矛盾歸因於媒體對簡單故事的偏好。"},{"w":"confidant","p":"n.","d":"A person trusted with private matters.","c":"知己；心腹","s":"Having served as the prime minister's closest confidant for over a decade, the retired civil servant possessed a uniquely comprehensive understanding of the internal debates that had shaped the most consequential policy decisions of the previous administration's three terms in office.","t":"作為首相十多年來最親密的知己，這位退休公務員對塑造前任政府三個任期最重要政策決定的內部辯論有著獨特而全面的了解。","as":"The diplomat's closest confidant, a reticent aide who had served him for decades, would not disclose the clandestine negotiations even under duress, convinced that loyalty to his mentor outweighed any threat to his own career.","at":"這位外交官最信任的心腹是一位追隨他數十年、沉默寡言的助理；即使在脅迫之下，他也不肯透露那些祕密談判的內容，深信對恩師的忠誠遠比自身前途受到的威脅更重要。"},{"w":"consternation","p":"n.","d":"Dismay, astonishment causing anxiety.","c":"驚愕；震驚","s":"The announcement of the merger caused considerable consternation among the workforce, as employees who had been given repeated assurances about job security found themselves suddenly confronting the possibility of significant redundancies across all three of the organisation's operating divisions.","t":"合並消息在員工中引起了相當大的驚愕，那些曾多次獲得工作保障保證的員工突然發現自己面臨著組織所有三個運營部門大規模裁員的可能性。","as":"The inadvertent release of the confidential report caused widespread consternation among investors, who feared that the company's egregious accounting errors would soon trigger an inexorable decline in its stock price.","at":"這份機密報告意外外流，在投資人之間引起普遍的驚愕，他們擔心公司嚴重的會計錯誤很快就會導致股價無可阻擋地下跌。"},{"w":"deride","p":"v.","d":"To ridicule, scoff at, mock.","c":"嘲笑；嘲弄","s":"The established medical community initially deride the physician's proposal that stomach ulcers were caused by bacterial infection rather than stress, dismissing it as fundamentally contrary to decades of accepted clinical wisdom — a rejection that lasted until his controlled experiments provided incontrovertible proof.","t":"既有的醫學界最初嘲弄醫生提出的胃潰瘍是由細菌感染而非壓力引起的理論，認為這從根本上違背了數十年被接受的臨床智慧——這種拒絕一直持續到他的對照實驗提供了無可辯駁的證明。","as":"Academic critics continued to deride the Impressionists as careless amateurs, scoffing at their loose brushstrokes, yet the painters' attention to every nuance of light eventually won over the very institutions that had once disdained them.","at":"學院派評論家一再嘲笑印象派畫家是草率的業餘者，譏諷他們鬆散的筆觸；然而這些畫家對光線每一絲細微變化的關注，最終贏得了當初輕視他們的那些機構的認可。"},{"w":"discern","p":"v.","d":"To perceive, distinguish, or recognise.","c":"辨別；識別","s":"After years of training, the master sommelier could discern not merely the grape variety and vintage year from a single sip, but the specific vineyard's aspect, the particular growing season's rainfall patterns, and occasionally the individual barrel in which the wine had been aged.","t":"經過多年訓練，這位侍酒大師能夠從一口酒中辨別出不僅是葡萄品種和年份，而且還能識別特定葡萄園的朝向、特定生長季節的降雨模式，有時甚至能識別出葡萄酒陳年所用的特定桶。","as":"After years of vigilant observation, the avid ornithologist learned to discern subtle variations in the songs of neighboring flocks, perceiving regional dialects in what casual listeners would dismiss as mundane chirping.","at":"經過多年警覺細心的觀察，這位熱衷的鳥類學家學會辨別鄰近鳥群歌聲中的細微差異，在一般聽眾視為平凡無奇的鳴叫聲中察覺出地域性的「方言」。"},{"w":"disparage","p":"v.","d":"To discredit or belittle someone.","c":"貶低；詆毀","s":"The biography's publication sparked controversy when it became clear that several of the subject's former colleagues had used their interviews with the author to disparage her professional reputation, making claims about her management style and research methodology that her supporters characterised as motivated by professional jealousy.","t":"傳記的出版引發了爭議，因為很明顯傳主的幾位前同事利用與作者的採訪來詆毀她的職業聲譽，對她的管理風格和研究方法提出了支持者認為出於職業嫉妒的指控。","as":"Rather than disparage her opponent with scurrilous personal attacks, the candidate chose to castigate only his policies, a strategy that many voters found refreshing amid the acrimonious tone of the campaign.","at":"這位候選人沒有用粗鄙的人身攻擊來貶低對手，而是只嚴厲批評他的政策；在選戰充滿火藥味的氛圍中，許多選民覺得這種策略令人耳目一新。"},{"w":"dubious","p":"adj.","d":"Doubtful, uncertain, suspect.","c":"可疑的；不確定的","s":"Environmental scientists remained deeply dubious about the company's claims that its new extraction process would cause negligible ecological damage, pointing to the absence of independent verification, the obvious financial interests involved, and the corporation's consistently poor environmental compliance record.","t":"環境科學家對公司聲稱其新提取工藝將造成可忽略的生態破壞仍然深感懷疑，指出缺乏獨立驗證、明顯的財務利益以及公司一貫糟糕的環境合規記錄。","as":"The curators grew dubious about the origins of the medieval manuscript when chemical analysis revealed a tinge of modern pigment, suggesting that a skilled forger may have fabricated the entire document to dupe wealthy collectors.","at":"化學分析顯示這份中世紀手稿帶有一絲現代顏料的痕跡，策展人因此開始懷疑它的來歷，這意味著可能有技巧高超的偽造者捏造了整份文件，以欺騙富有的收藏家。"},{"w":"eschew","p":"v.","d":"To avoid, abstain from deliberately.","c":"避開；戒除","s":"The celebrated architect had made a conscious decision to eschew the use of synthetic materials in all her residential projects, insisting on locally sourced timber, natural stone, and traditional lime render despite the significant additional expense these choices invariably imposed on her clients.","t":"這位著名建築師做出了有意識的決定，在她所有的住宅項目中避免使用合成材料，堅持使用當地採購的木材、天然石材和傳統石灰粉刷，儘管這些選擇不可避免地給她的客戶帶來了大量的額外費用。","as":"Determined to eschew the ornate prose of earlier Victorian novels, the author cultivated a laconic style, trusting that sparse dialogue could elicit deeper emotion than her predecessors' paragraphs, which were replete with elaborate description.","at":"這位作家決心避開早期維多利亞小說華麗的文風，培養出簡潔精練的風格；她相信，比起前輩們充滿繁複描寫的段落，簡短的對話更能引發讀者深刻的情感。"},{"w":"feasible","p":"adj.","d":"Possible, capable of being done.","c":"可行的；可能的","s":"After reviewing the engineering reports, the project committee concluded that the proposed underground extension of the city's transit network was technically feasible but that the estimated construction cost of approximately four billion dollars would require a dedicated funding stream that current municipal budgets could not accommodate.","t":"在審查了工程報告後，項目委員會得出結論，城市交通網絡擬議的地下延伸在技術上是可行的，但估計約四十億美元的建設成本將需要一個當前市政預算無法容納的專項資金流。","as":"Engineers once judged a tunnel beneath the strait to be technically feasible but financially ruinous, since the paucity of public funds and the rampant inflation of the era threatened to make construction seem interminable.","at":"工程師曾認為在海峽底下開鑿隧道在技術上可行，但在財務上將是災難，因為當時公共資金匱乏、通貨膨脹猖獗，恐怕會讓工程看似永無止境。"},{"w":"fiasco","p":"n.","d":"A complete and humiliating failure.","c":"慘敗；大失敗","s":"The product launch, which the company's marketing department had promoted as a transformative moment for the brand, descended into a spectacular fiasco when the live demonstration system failed repeatedly on stage, the celebrity endorser forgot her scripted remarks, and the press conference was interrupted by protesters.","t":"公司市場部門宣傳為品牌轉型時刻的產品發布演變成了一場慘敗，當時現場演示系統在台上多次失敗，名人代言人忘記了她的劇本台詞，新聞發布會被抗議者打斷。","as":"The product launch became a notorious fiasco after a lackluster demonstration in which the much-hyped device repeatedly malfunctioned, and the company's inane attempt to blame a hapless technician only deepened the embarrassment.","at":"這場產品發表會在一次乏善可陳的展示後成了眾所周知的大失敗：備受吹捧的裝置一再故障，而公司愚蠢地試圖把責任推給一名倒楣的技術人員，只讓難堪雪上加霜。"},{"w":"laudable","p":"adj.","d":"Deserving praise, commendable.","c":"值得讚賞的；可嘉的","s":"While the initiative's objectives were entirely laudable — reducing food waste, supporting local farmers, and providing nutritious meals to vulnerable families — the organisation's implementation left considerable room for improvement in terms of operational efficiency, financial transparency, and equitable distribution across the different community zones.","t":"雖然這項倡議的目標完全值得讚賞——減少食物浪費、支持當地農民、為弱勢家庭提供營養餐食——但該組織的執行在運營效率、財務透明度以及不同社區區域的公平分配方面還有相當大的改進空間。","as":"The charity's goal of ending childhood hunger was laudable, but auditors who scrutinized its finances found a flagrant misuse of donations, prompting regulators to admonish its directors for violating basic ethics.","at":"這個慈善機構終結兒童飢餓的目標值得讚賞，但仔細審查其財務的稽核人員發現捐款遭到公然濫用，促使主管機關告誡其董事違反了基本的道德規範。"},{"w":"masticate","p":"v.","d":"To chew food thoroughly.","c":"咀嚼","s":"The speech therapist advised her patient to masticate each mouthful at least twenty times before swallowing, explaining that thorough chewing would not only reduce the aspiration risk that had caused his recent hospitalisation but would also improve his overall digestive efficiency significantly.","t":"語言治療師建議她的患者在吞嚥前每口至少咀嚼二十次，解釋說徹底咀嚼不僅能降低導致他近期住院的誤吸風險，還能顯著提高他整體的消化效率。","as":"Because many herbivores must masticate tough plant fibers for hours each day, their molars have evolved broad, ridged surfaces, an adaptation that biologists perceive as crucial in enabling these voracious grazers to abound even in arid grasslands.","at":"由於許多草食動物每天必須花好幾個小時咀嚼堅韌的植物纖維，牠們的臼齒演化出寬闊且有稜脊的表面；生物學家認為，正是這項適應讓這些食量驚人的吃草動物即使在乾燥的草原上也能大量繁衍。"},{"w":"obsolescence","p":"n.","d":"The process of becoming outdated.","c":"荒廢；淘汰","s":"The rapid obsolescence of manufacturing skills in the affected communities had created a structural unemployment problem that simple retraining programmes could not adequately address, as the pace of automation was consistently outstripping the capacity of the workforce to acquire economically relevant new competencies.","t":"受影響社區製造技能的快速淘汰造成了簡單的再培訓計劃無法充分解決的結構性失業問題，因為自動化的速度持續超過勞動力獲得經濟上相關的新能力的能力。","as":"Critics argue that planned obsolescence, in which manufacturers deliberately design gadgets to fail, is a pernicious practice that enriches corporations with impunity while consumers tolerate an endless cycle of costly replacements.","at":"批評者認為，「計畫性淘汰」──也就是製造商刻意讓電子產品容易故障──是一種有害的做法，讓企業得以不受懲罰地獲利，而消費者卻只能忍受無止境、代價高昂的汰換循環。"},{"w":"perfunctory","p":"adj.","d":"Done without care, superficially.","c":"敷衍的；馬虎的","s":"The inspection report's conclusions were widely dismissed as perfunctory by independent safety experts who noted that the assessors had spent less than forty minutes on site, had failed to test three of the seven critical safety systems, and had not reviewed any maintenance records dating from before the previous twelve months.","t":"獨立安全專家普遍認為檢查報告的結論是敷衍了事的，他們指出評估人員在現場花費的時間不到四十分鐘，未能測試七個關鍵安全系統中的三個，也未審查前十二個月以前的任何維護記錄。","as":"The inspector's perfunctory review of the aging bridge, little more than a hurried glance, failed to detect incipient cracks in its supports, an ominous lapse for which he was sharply reprimanded once engineers discovered the damage.","at":"檢查員對這座老舊橋樑的檢查十分敷衍，不過是匆匆一瞥，因而沒有發現支柱上初期的裂縫；工程師發現損壞後，這個不祥的疏失讓他受到嚴厲斥責。"},{"w":"perverse","p":"adj.","d":"Contrary, persistent in error, wrongheaded.","c":"固執錯誤的；乖戾的","s":"There was something deeply perverse in the committee's decision to reduce funding for preventive health programmes precisely when epidemiological evidence was demonstrating their cost-effectiveness most clearly, a choice that prioritised short-term budget optics over the long-term financial sustainability of the entire healthcare system.","t":"委員會在流行病學證據最清楚地證明預防保健計劃的成本效益時恰恰減少對這些計劃的資助，這一決定有些極其乖戾，這一選擇將短期預算形象置於整個醫療系統的長期財務可持續性之上。","as":"In a perverse twist, regulations intended to curb pollution encouraged factories to relocate to regions with even laxer standards, a paradox that economists construe as evidence that well-meaning laws can inadvertently exacerbate the very problems they target.","at":"諷刺又違背常理的是，原本為了遏止污染的法規反而促使工廠遷往標準更寬鬆的地區；經濟學家將這種矛盾解讀為證據，說明立意良善的法律可能在無意間讓它們想解決的問題更加惡化。"},{"w":"precocious","p":"adj.","d":"Reaching maturity or development early.","c":"早熟的","s":"The precocious cellist had performed with professional orchestras by the age of eleven, recorded her first internationally distributed album at thirteen, and been appointed as a guest principal with a major European ensemble at sixteen — an ascent through the classical music world of a speed that genuinely had no modern precedent.","t":"這位早熟的大提琴手在十一歲時就與職業管弦樂團演出，十三歲時錄製了她的第一張國際發行專輯，十六歲時被任命為一個主要歐洲樂團的客座首席——在古典音樂界的晉升速度確實沒有現代先例。","as":"A precocious child who could reportedly read music before she could walk, the composer astonished avid concertgoers across Europe, yet she shunned the throngs of admirers who gathered after each recital and found solace only in solitary practice.","at":"這位作曲家是個早熟的孩子，據說還不會走路就能看懂樂譜；她讓歐洲各地熱情的樂迷驚嘆不已，卻刻意避開每場獨奏會後聚集的大批仰慕者，只在獨自練琴中尋得慰藉。"},{"w":"quell","p":"v.","d":"To put an end to, suppress.","c":"平息；鎮壓","s":"Emergency services deployed substantial resources to quell the disturbance that had broken out following the controversial verdict, with police making thirty-seven arrests and establishing a security perimeter around the courthouse that effectively prevented further public access for the remainder of the day.","t":"緊急服務部署了大量資源來平息在爭議性裁決後爆發的騷亂，警察逮捕了三十七人，並在法院周圍建立了安全周界，有效地阻止了當天剩餘時間的進一步公眾進入。","as":"To quell the frenzy that erupted after the disputed election, authorities imposed a curfew and implored community leaders to urge calm, though belligerent protesters continued to jostle police lines for several nights.","at":"為了平息這場具爭議的選舉後爆發的狂亂，當局實施宵禁，並懇求社區領袖呼籲民眾保持冷靜，但好鬥的抗議者仍連續數夜推擠警方的封鎖線。"},{"w":"sally","p":"v.","d":"To suddenly rush out.","c":"突圍；出發","s":"The cavalry regiment would sally forth from the fortified position at first light, exploiting the enemy's confusion during the dawn hours to strike their supply lines and then withdraw rapidly before the main opposing force could organise an effective defensive response.","t":"騎兵團將在黎明時分從設防陣地衝出，利用敵人在黎明時分的混亂攻擊其補給線，然後在主要對立力量能夠組織有效防禦回應之前迅速撤退。","as":"Noticing that the besieging army had grown careless at dawn, the intrepid commander ordered his troops to sally from the fortress, and their sudden feint toward the eastern camp allowed a convoy of supplies to slip through the enemy lines.","at":"這位無畏的指揮官注意到圍城的敵軍在黎明時分變得鬆懈，便下令部隊從要塞突圍而出；他們突然佯攻東側營地，讓一支補給車隊得以趁機穿越敵軍防線。"},{"w":"verbose","p":"adj.","d":"Using too many words, wordy.","c":"囉嗦的；冗長的","s":"The committee rejected the consultant's proposal not because of any substantive weaknesses in the underlying analysis but because the document was so verbose that the key recommendations were effectively buried under eighty pages of contextual background, methodological justification, and qualifying caveats that obscured rather than supported the central argument.","t":"委員會拒絕了顧問的提案，不是因為基礎分析有任何實質性弱點，而是因為文件太囉嗦了，關鍵建議被有效地埋沒在八十頁的背景說明、方法論論證和限定性警告之下，這些內容掩蓋而非支持了核心論點。","as":"The committee's verbose report, replete with jargon and needless digressions, buried its few tangible recommendations, prompting the director to cajole her staff into condensing its essence into a brief summary for busy legislators.","at":"委員會的報告冗長囉嗦，充斥著術語和不必要的離題內容，把少數幾項具體建議都淹沒了；主任因此好說歹說地勸員工將重點濃縮成一份簡短摘要，供忙碌的立法委員閱讀。"}]},{"unit":7,"cards":[{"w":"arbitrary","p":"adj.","d":"Based on random choice or personal whim.","c":"任意的；武斷的","s":"The employees filed a formal grievance against what they described as the manager's arbitrary allocation of shift patterns, arguing that there was no discernible objective criteria governing who received the most desirable schedules and that personal favouritism appeared to be the primary determining factor.","t":"員工提出了正式申訴，反對他們所描述的經理任意分配班次模式，認為沒有可辨別的客觀標準來決定誰能獲得最理想的時間表，個人偏袒似乎是主要決定因素。","as":"Historians disparage the colonial officials who drew arbitrary borders across Africa, ignoring the realms of established kingdoms and ethnic groups, a blunder whose pernicious consequences continue to afflict the region today.","at":"歷史學家貶斥那些在非洲任意劃定邊界的殖民官員，他們無視既有王國與族群的疆域，這項錯誤所造成的有害後果至今仍困擾著該地區。"},{"w":"cognizant","p":"adj.","d":"Aware of, having knowledge of.","c":"認識到的；知曉的","s":"Fully cognizant of the political sensitivities surrounding the proposed legislation, the minister carefully briefed all coalition partners before the formal announcement, ensuring that no government ally would be caught unprepared by media questions about a policy with such significant implications for core electoral constituencies.","t":"充分認識到擬議立法周圍的政治敏感性，部長在正式宣布之前仔細向所有聯合夥伴匯報，確保沒有政府盟友在媒體關於對核心選區有重大影響的政策問題上措手不及。","as":"Fully cognizant of the dubious legality of their methods, the journalists nonetheless posed as buyers to infiltrate the smuggling ring, reasoning that exposing its sordid trade in endangered wildlife justified a measure of duplicity.","at":"記者們完全清楚自己的手法在法律上有疑慮，卻仍假扮成買家滲透這個走私集團，理由是揭發其買賣瀕危野生動物的骯髒勾當，足以合理化些許欺瞞的手段。"},{"w":"effigy","p":"n.","d":"A likeness, usually of a disliked person.","c":"雕像；假人像","s":"Protesters gathered outside the embassy gates carrying placards and a crudely constructed effigy of the foreign president, which they ceremonially burnt at the conclusion of their demonstration as television cameras recorded the scene for broadcast on evening news programmes across the country.","t":"抗議者聚集在大使館大門外，手持標語和一個粗製濫造的外國總統假人像，他們在示威結束時儀式性地燒毀了假人像，電視攝像機記錄了這一場景，在全國各地的晚間新聞節目中播出。","as":"Furious at the new tax, the irate crowd paraded an effigy of the governor through the streets before setting it ablaze in the town square, a brash act of defiance that the authorities struggled to quell.","at":"憤怒的群眾不滿新稅，抬著總督的假人像在街上遊行，最後在城鎮廣場上將它點火焚燒；這種魯莽的反抗行為讓當局難以平息。"},{"w":"exacerbate","p":"v.","d":"To make worse, to irritate.","c":"惡化；激怒","s":"The decision to impose additional austerity measures at precisely the moment when economic data indicated the beginnings of a fragile recovery appeared likely to exacerbate the very structural problems the original policy had been designed to address, creating a self-reinforcing cycle of contraction that alarmed international creditors.","t":"在經濟數據顯示脆弱復甦開始的確切時刻決定實施額外的緊縮措施，似乎可能惡化原始政策本應解決的結構性問題，創造出一個令國際債權人警覺的自我強化的收縮循環。","as":"The decision to subsidize water-hungry crops only served to exacerbate the depletion of groundwater, an outcome that agronomists had prognosticated years earlier, only to see their warnings derided as alarmist by officials who eschewed scientific advice.","at":"補貼高耗水作物的決策只讓地下水枯竭的情況更加惡化；農藝學家早在多年前就預言了這個結果，但他們的警告卻被刻意迴避科學建議的官員嘲笑為危言聳聽。"},{"w":"flout","p":"v.","d":"To disregard openly, to mock.","c":"嘲弄；無視規則","s":"The construction company continued to flout environmental protection regulations despite having received three formal warnings and two substantial financial penalties over the preceding eighteen months, apparently calculating that the cost of compliance significantly exceeded the fines imposed for non-compliance.","t":"儘管在過去十八個月中收到了三次正式警告和兩次大額罰款，建築公司繼續無視環境保護法規，顯然計算出合規成本大大超過了不合規所受的罰款。","as":"Some affluent shipping magnates continue to flout international environmental treaties with seeming impunity, dumping toxic waste in remote waters where enforcement is lax, inspections are rare, and the culprits are seldom identified, let alone prosecuted.","at":"一些富有的航運大亨持續公然無視國際環保條約，似乎從未受到懲罰；他們在執法鬆散、鮮少檢查的偏遠海域傾倒有毒廢棄物，肇事者很少被查出來，更別說遭到起訴了。"},{"w":"forthwith","p":"adv.","d":"Immediately, without delay.","c":"立即；馬上","s":"The arbitration panel ordered the defendant company to cease all contested construction activities forthwith and to restore the affected wetland areas to their pre-development condition within a period not exceeding ninety days, subject to monthly progress inspections by independent environmental assessors.","t":"仲裁小組命令被告公司立即停止所有有爭議的建設活動，並在不超過九十天的期限內將受影響的濕地區域恢復到開發前的狀況，接受獨立環境評估員每月的進度檢查。","as":"Upon learning that a contaminated batch of medicine had already been shipped, the distraught health minister ordered the manufacturer to recall every bottle forthwith and stipulated that no new products be sold until inspectors had scrutinized its facilities.","at":"得知一批受污染的藥品已經出貨後，心急如焚的衛生部長下令藥廠立即回收每一瓶，並明定在檢查人員徹底審查其廠房之前，不得販售任何新產品。"},{"w":"fray","p":"n.","d":"A fight, conflict, or noisy quarrel.","c":"爭吵；打鬥","s":"Several previously neutral nations were gradually drawn into the diplomatic fray as the regional dispute intensified, finding that their economic and strategic interests made complete detachment impossible despite their initial determination to maintain an impartial stance throughout the crisis.","t":"隨著地區爭端的加劇，幾個以前保持中立的國家逐漸被捲入外交糾紛，發現他們的經濟和戰略利益使得完全超然是不可能的，儘管他們最初決心在整個危機過程中保持公正立場。","as":"Although the senator had vowed to remain neutral, she eventually entered the fray over the controversial bill, delivering a caustic speech that belittled her colleagues' compromise as a feeble pretext for continued inaction.","at":"雖然這位參議員曾誓言保持中立，最後她還是加入了這項爭議法案的論戰，發表一場尖酸的演說，貶低同僚的妥協方案不過是繼續無所作為的薄弱藉口。"},{"w":"harass","p":"v.","d":"To trouble, torment, or intimidate repeatedly.","c":"騷擾；煩擾","s":"The human resources investigation found substantial evidence that the manager had systematically harass three junior employees over a period of eighteen months, using his supervisory authority to assign disproportionately burdensome workloads, exclude them from important meetings, and undermine their professional credibility within the department.","t":"人力資源調查發現有大量證據表明，這位經理在十八個月的時間裡系統地騷擾了三名初級員工，利用他的監督職權分配不成比例的繁重工作量，將他們排除在重要會議之外，並在部門內破壞他們的職業信譽。","as":"Investigators found that the landlord had hired thugs to harass and intimidate elderly tenants into abandoning their rent-controlled apartments, a scheme so blatant that even his longtime confidant agreed to testify against him.","at":"調查人員發現，這名房東僱用打手一再騷擾、恐嚇年長房客，逼他們搬離租金管制的公寓；這個計謀明目張膽到連他多年的心腹都同意出庭指證他。"},{"w":"implacable","p":"adj.","d":"Cannot be calmed, relentless.","c":"難以平息的；不屈不撓的","s":"The implacable opposition of the local residents' association to the proposed development proved decisive: despite the developer's repeated attempts to modify the plans in response to specific objections, the association maintained its fundamental objection to any construction on the designated green belt land.","t":"當地居民協會對擬議開發的不屈不撓的反對被證明是決定性的：儘管開發商多次試圖修改計劃以回應具體的反對意見，但協會對綠化帶土地上任何建設的根本反對立場保持不變。","as":"Steeped in ancient myth, Greek tragedies portrayed the Furies as implacable avengers who would hound any culprit guilty of shedding a relative's blood, ignoring even the most tremulous pleas for mercy.","at":"希臘悲劇深受古代神話薰陶，將復仇女神描繪成無法平息的復仇者，她們會窮追任何殺害親人的罪人，即使是最顫抖哀切的求饒也置之不理。"},{"w":"indigent","p":"adj.","d":"Poor, needy, lacking basic necessities.","c":"貧困的；窮困的","s":"The city's emergency housing programme was specifically designed to serve the most indigent residents, prioritising placement for families with dependent children who had been living in temporary accommodation for more than three months and whose combined household income fell below the defined poverty threshold.","t":"城市緊急住房計劃專門為最貧困的居民服務，優先安置在臨時住所生活超過三個月且家庭總收入低於規定貧困線的有被撫養子女的家庭。","as":"The legal clinic offers free counsel to indigent defendants who might otherwise succumb to the inexorable pressure to plead guilty, a laudable initiative that has helped many clients repudiate false confessions extracted under duress.","at":"這間法律扶助中心為貧困的被告提供免費諮詢，否則他們可能會屈服於認罪那股難以抗拒的壓力；這項值得讚揚的計畫已幫助許多當事人推翻在脅迫下被逼出的不實自白。"},{"w":"jurisdiction","p":"n.","d":"The power or range of legal authority.","c":"司法權；管轄範圍","s":"The complex international fraud case raised fundamental questions about jurisdiction that took two years to resolve, as four different national courts each claimed the authority to try the principal defendants, while the accused argued persuasively that none of the claimant states possessed the necessary legal basis for proceeding.","t":"這個複雜的國際詐騙案引發了關於管轄權的根本問題，這個問題花了兩年時間才解決，因為四個不同的國家法院各自聲稱有權審判主要被告，而被告有說服力地辯稱所有主張的國家都不具備繼續程序的必要法律基礎。","as":"Because the alleged fraud spanned several countries, rival prosecutors spent months debating which court had jurisdiction, and the delay allowed the infamous felon, an adroit manipulator of legal loopholes, to move his assets beyond the reach of investigators.","at":"由於這起涉嫌詐欺案橫跨數國，各方檢察官花了好幾個月爭論哪個法院擁有管轄權；這段延誤讓那名惡名昭彰、擅長鑽法律漏洞的重罪犯得以將資產轉移到調查人員無法觸及之處。"},{"w":"monolithic","p":"adj.","d":"Massively solid, uniform, inflexible.","c":"巨大而單一的；整體的","s":"Critics of the educational system argued that its monolithic structure — centralised curriculum, standardised assessment, and uniform pedagogical approaches regardless of student diversity or local context — fundamentally prevented the adaptability needed to serve the genuinely varied learning needs of modern student populations.","t":"教育系統的批評者認為，其整體結構——集中課程、標準化評估以及不考慮學生多樣性或當地背景的統一教學方法——從根本上阻止了服務現代學生群體真正多樣化學習需求所需的適應性。","as":"Political scientists caution against portraying any electorate as a monolithic bloc, since voters within the same demographic often hold incongruous views on issues from taxation to immigration, a diversity that perfunctory analyses fail to discern.","at":"政治學家提醒，不應把任何選民群體描繪成鐵板一塊，因為同一人口族群中的選民，對從稅制到移民等議題往往抱持互相矛盾的看法；而這種多元性正是草率的分析所無法辨識的。"},{"w":"oust","p":"v.","d":"To drive out, eject, or force from power.","c":"驅逐；罷免","s":"The board of directors voted unanimously to oust the chief executive following the publication of an independent report detailing serious governance failures, financial irregularities, and a pattern of behaviour toward employees that the non-executive directors concluded was incompatible with the values the organisation had publicly committed to upholding.","t":"董事會一致投票罷免了首席執行官，此前發布了一份獨立報告，詳細說明了嚴重的治理失敗、財務違規以及對員工的行為模式，非執行董事得出結論認為這與組織公開承諾維護的價值觀不符。","as":"After months of mass demonstrations, reform-minded legislators moved to oust the autocratic president, who had promulgated decrees muzzling the press and whose belligerent rhetoric had alienated even the loyalists in his own entourage.","at":"經過數月的大規模示威後，主張改革的立法者採取行動罷黜這位專制總統；他曾頒布箝制新聞自由的法令，而他好戰的言論甚至疏遠了身邊隨從中的忠誠支持者。"},{"w":"paroxysm","p":"n.","d":"A sudden fit or outburst.","c":"陣發；突發","s":"The revelation that the long-trusted financial adviser had been systematically stealing from his elderly clients' accounts over a period of seven years triggered a paroxysm of public outrage, with calls for immediate legislative changes to the regulations governing the fiduciary responsibilities of investment professionals.","t":"這位長期受信任的財務顧問在七年內系統地從老年客戶賬戶盜竊的揭露引發了公眾憤怒的突然爆發，呼籲立即對管理投資專業人員受托責任的法規進行立法變更。","as":"The announcement of the ceasefire sent the throng gathered outside the palace into a paroxysm of joy, yet seasoned diplomats remained reticent, aware that earlier truces had swiftly collapsed amid a frenzy of mutual recrimination.","at":"停火的宣布讓聚集在宮殿外的群眾爆發一陣狂喜，但經驗老到的外交官仍保持緘默，因為他們知道先前的停戰協議都在雙方瘋狂互相指責中迅速瓦解。"},{"w":"revert","p":"v.","d":"To return to a previous condition.","c":"恢復；重返","s":"Without continued maintenance and community engagement, many urban regeneration projects tend to revert to their pre-intervention condition within five to ten years, as the underlying social and economic factors that produced the original deterioration reassert themselves in the absence of sustained structural support.","t":"沒有持續的維護和社區參與，許多城市更新項目往往在五到十年內恢復到干預前的狀況，因為在沒有持續結構性支持的情況下，導致原始惡化的根本社會和經濟因素重新發揮作用。","as":"Once the novelty wore off, many residents of the eco-village began to revert to their old habits, abandoning with alacrity the drudgery of composting and hand-washing laundry and admitting with some chagrin that convenience had triumphed over ideals.","at":"新鮮感一過，這個生態村的許多居民便開始恢復舊習慣，迫不及待地拋下堆肥和手洗衣物的苦差事，並略帶懊惱地承認便利終究戰勝了理想。"},{"w":"skirmish","p":"n.","d":"A small fight or brief encounter.","c":"小衝突；小規模戰鬥","s":"What began as a minor diplomatic skirmish over fishing rights in the disputed territorial waters escalated rapidly into a full constitutional crisis when the incident was instrumentalised by nationalist politicians in both countries to advance their respective domestic political agendas.","t":"關於爭議領水中捕魚權的最初小衝突迅速升級為全面的憲法危機，當時兩國的民族主義政客將這一事件工具化，以推進各自的國內政治議程。","as":"What began as a minor skirmish between border patrols at a disputed river crossing soon escalated, to the consternation of neighboring states, as pugnacious commanders on both sides ignored diplomats who badgered them to accept mediation.","at":"一開始只是邊境巡邏隊在一處有爭議的渡河點發生的小規模衝突，卻很快升級，令鄰國驚愕不已，因為雙方好鬥的指揮官都無視外交官一再催促他們接受調停。"},{"w":"stymie","p":"v.","d":"To hinder or prevent from proceeding.","c":"阻礙；妨礙","s":"Persistent disagreements between the two largest member states had effectively stymie the organisation's ability to respond coherently to the humanitarian crisis, as every proposed intervention measure required unanimous approval under the founding charter and either nation could exercise an absolute veto over collective action.","t":"兩個最大成員國之間持續的分歧有效地阻礙了組織對人道主義危機作出連貫回應的能力，因為每項擬議的干預措施都需要根據創始章程的一致批准，任何一個國家都可以對集體行動行使絕對否決權。","as":"Arcane permitting rules continue to stymie efforts to modernize the region's antiquated power grid, and blackouts have become such a mundane nuisance that affluent households simply eschew the public system by installing private solar panels.","at":"晦澀難懂的許可規定持續阻礙該地區老舊電網的現代化，停電已成為司空見慣的麻煩，富裕家庭乾脆裝設私人太陽能板，避開公共電網。"},{"w":"terminate","p":"v.","d":"To bring to an end.","c":"終止；結束","s":"The pharmaceutical company announced its decision to terminate the clinical trial following a scheduled interim safety review that identified a statistically significant increase in adverse cardiac events among the treatment group compared to placebo recipients, a finding that the independent data monitoring committee deemed sufficient to halt the study immediately.","t":"製藥公司宣布決定終止臨床試驗，此前定期的中期安全審查發現，與安慰劑接受者相比，治療組中不良心臟事件在統計上顯著增加，獨立數據監測委員會認為這一發現足以立即停止研究。","as":"The board voted to terminate the chief executive's contract after an internal audit uncovered furtive accounting maneuvers that had concealed heavy losses, a breach of ethics that no euphemism in his public apology could disguise.","at":"內部稽核發現執行長以鬼祟的會計手法掩蓋了巨額虧損後，董事會投票終止了他的合約；這種違反職業道德的行為，無論他在公開道歉中用什麼委婉說法都掩飾不了。"},{"w":"turbulent","p":"adj.","d":"Unruly, agitated, causing unrest.","c":"動盪的；混亂的","s":"The turbulentedecades following the colonial withdrawal had been characterised by military coups, contested elections, regional separatist movements, and intermittent armed conflicts that had prevented the sustained institutional development necessary for stable democratic governance and consistent economic growth.","t":"殖民撤退後動盪的幾十年以軍事政變、有爭議的選舉、地區分裂主義運動和間歇性武裝衝突為特徵，阻止了穩定民主治理和持續經濟增長所必需的持續制度發展。","as":"During the turbulent years after the revolution, rival factions repeatedly wrested control of the capital from one another, and the annals of the period describe a weary populace longing for any cessation of violence, regardless of who ruled.","at":"在革命後的動盪歲月裡，敵對派系多次從彼此手中奪取首都的控制權；當時的編年史記載，疲憊的民眾只渴望暴力能夠停止，無論由誰掌權都無所謂。"},{"w":"untoward","p":"adj.","d":"Unfortunate, improper, unfavourable.","c":"不適當的；不幸的","s":"The clinical guidelines specified that any untoward reactions to the new medication should be reported to the prescribing physician within twenty-four hours and documented in the patient's medical record regardless of whether the symptoms were considered clinically significant or likely to require direct medical intervention.","t":"臨床指南規定，對新藥的任何不良反應應在二十四小時內報告給開藥醫生，並記錄在患者的醫療記錄中，無論這些症狀是否被認為具有臨床意義或可能需要直接的醫療干預。","as":"Regulators suspended the clinical trial after several volunteers suffered untoward reactions, which critics blamed on the indiscriminate recruitment of participants, and the company's clumsy denials only compounded the damage to a laboratory once considered eminent in its field.","at":"數名志願者出現不良反應後，主管機關暫停了這項臨床試驗；批評者將問題歸咎於受試者招募過於隨意，而公司笨拙的否認只讓這間曾在業界享有盛名的實驗室所受的傷害雪上加霜。"}]},{"unit":8,"cards":[{"w":"afflict","p":"v.","d":"To trouble greatly, cause distress.","c":"折磨；使痛苦","s":"The degenerative neurological condition that had begun to afflict the composer in his early fifties progressed with devastating speed over the following decade, ultimately depriving him of the fine motor control essential for performance while leaving his compositional imagination entirely and cruelly intact.","t":"從五十歲初開始折磨這位作曲家的退行性神經系統疾病在接下來的十年中以毀滅性的速度發展，最終剝奪了他演奏所必需的精細運動控制，同時讓他的作曲想象力完全且殘忍地保持完好。","as":"For centuries, scurvy would afflict sailors on long voyages, and although a few astute captains discerned a link between citrus fruit and recovery, naval bureaucrats took decades to stipulate that daily rations include lemon juice.","at":"好幾個世紀以來，壞血病一直折磨著長途航行的水手；雖然少數精明的船長察覺到柑橘類水果與康復之間的關聯，海軍官僚卻花了數十年才明文規定每日配給必須包含檸檬汁。"},{"w":"ascend","p":"v.","d":"To rise, climb upward.","c":"上升；攀登","s":"The balloon ascend gradually through the early morning cloud layer, emerging into brilliant sunshine at approximately three thousand metres, the passengers' conversation hushing to collective silence as the spectacular panoramic view of the coastline and the distant mountain range became fully visible.","t":"氣球在清晨緩慢穿越雲層，在大約三千米處升入燦爛的陽光，當海岸線和遠處山脈的壯觀全景完全可見時，乘客們的談話沉寂為集體沉默。","as":"As the expedition began to ascend the final ridge, an ominous bank of clouds appeared, and the vigilant guide gesticulated urgently, warning the brash newcomers that they must turn back forthwith.","at":"當探險隊開始攀登最後一道山脊時，一片不祥的雲層出現了；警覺的嚮導急切地比手畫腳，警告那些莽撞的新手必須立刻折返。"},{"w":"besiege","p":"v.","d":"To surround and hem in.","c":"圍攻；包圍","s":"Following the announcement of the surprise casting decision, the production company's offices were besiege by journalists, photographers, and disappointed fans who had camped outside since the previous evening in hopes of obtaining either a statement from the director or a glimpse of the controversially chosen lead actor.","t":"在宣布出乎意料的選角決定後，製作公司的辦公室被記者、攝影師和從前一天晚上就在外面紮營的失望粉絲所包圍，他們希望獲得導演的聲明或一睹具爭議性選擇的主角。","as":"When rebel forces began to besiege the capital, the king held a clandestine council with his confidants, but their plan to sally forth at night was betrayed by a spy, and the fiasco hastened the city's surrender.","at":"叛軍開始圍攻首都時，國王與心腹們祕密召開會議，但他們夜間突圍的計畫遭間諜出賣，這場慘敗加速了城市的投降。"},{"w":"emaciated","p":"adj.","d":"Abnormally thin, wasted away.","c":"憔悴的；極度消瘦的","s":"The humanitarian workers who reached the isolated village following weeks of blocked road access found a population that was visibly emaciated, the combination of crop failure, disrupted supply routes, and inadequate emergency food distributions having created a nutritional crisis of alarming severity.","t":"在道路封鎖數週後抵達偏遠村莊的人道主義工作者發現，當地居民明顯消瘦，作物歉收、供應路線中斷和緊急食物分配不足的結合製造了一場嚴重程度令人震驚的營養危機。","as":"Photographs of emaciated prisoners released from wartime camps provoked global consternation, and even governments that had long been reticent about the atrocities were compelled to concur that an international tribunal was necessary.","at":"從戰時集中營獲釋、骨瘦如柴的囚犯照片引發全球震驚，就連長期對這些暴行保持沉默的政府，也不得不同意有必要成立國際法庭。"},{"w":"excruciating","p":"adj.","d":"Agonizing, extremely painful.","c":"極痛苦的；難以忍受的","s":"The patient described the post-surgical nerve pain as excruciating, rating it consistently at nine or ten on the standard numerical scale and reporting that it was severe enough to prevent sleep for more than two consecutive hours even with the maximum permitted dose of prescribed analgesic medication.","t":"患者將術後神經痛描述為難以忍受的，在標準數字量表上始終評為九或十分，並報告說即使使用最大允許劑量的處方止痛藥，疼痛也嚴重到阻止超過兩個連續小時的睡眠。","as":"Before anesthesia was introduced, surgeons treating even a deep laceration prized speed above all, since every incision caused excruciating pain, and the annals of early hospitals describe patients who implored doctors to stop midway through operations.","at":"在麻醉發明之前，即使只是處理一道深深的撕裂傷，外科醫生也最重視速度，因為每一刀都會帶來極度的疼痛；早期醫院的紀錄中記載著病人在手術進行到一半時哀求醫生停手。"},{"w":"fretful","p":"adj.","d":"Worrisome, irritable, anxious.","c":"煩躁的；焦躁不安的","s":"The fretful investor checked market indices every twenty minutes throughout the trading day, unable to concentrate on any other task as the portfolio value fluctuated by amounts that, while relatively modest in percentage terms, represented substantial sums that triggered acute anxiety whenever a downward movement occurred.","t":"這位煩躁的投資者在整個交易日每二十分鐘查看一次市場指數，無法集中精力做任何其他任務，因為投資組合價值的波動，雖然在百分比上相對適中，但代表著每次向下波動時都會引發急性焦慮的可觀金額。","as":"Fretful after a week of turbulent markets, many small investors sold their shares in a frenzy, a perverse reaction that economists say merely compounds losses by locking them in at the worst possible moment.","at":"經歷一週動盪的市場後，許多焦躁不安的小額投資人在一陣狂亂中拋售股票；經濟學家表示，這種違反常理的反應只會在最糟的時機鎖定虧損，讓損失雪上加霜。"},{"w":"harbinger","p":"n.","d":"A forerunner or advance sign.","c":"先兆；前兆","s":"Ecologists have identified the irregular migration patterns of certain sensitive species as a reliable harbinger of broader ecosystem disruption, with the early arrival or departure of key species consistently preceding detectable changes in temperature, precipitation, and the availability of critical food sources by several weeks.","t":"生態學家將某些敏感物種的不規律遷徙模式確定為更廣泛生態系統破壞的可靠先兆，關鍵物種的提前到來或離開始終比幾週後才能檢測到的溫度、降水和關鍵食物來源可用性變化早出現。","as":"In many ancient cultures, a comet was construed as a harbinger of calamity, and court astrologers who prognosticated the downfall of kings wielded enormous influence, though their predictions were as dubious as they were ominous.","at":"在許多古代文化中，彗星被解讀為災難的前兆；預言君王覆滅的宮廷占星師握有極大的影響力，儘管他們的預測既不祥又十分可疑。"},{"w":"malignant","p":"adj.","d":"Destructive, deadly, deeply harmful.","c":"惡性的；致命的","s":"The oncologist delivered the difficult news that the tumour, which had initially appeared operable based on the preliminary imaging, had proven on closer examination to be malignant in the most aggressive clinical sense, with metastatic spread already evident in three adjacent lymph node clusters.","t":"腫瘤科醫生傳達了困難的消息：根據初步影像最初看起來可以手術的腫瘤，在更仔細的檢查後被證明在最積極的臨床意義上是惡性的，轉移擴散已在三個相鄰的淋巴結群中明顯可見。","as":"When the biopsy revealed that the tumor was malignant, the oncologist urged surgery forthwith, but the patient, a frail octogenarian, judged such an arduous operation hardly feasible and opted instead for palliative care.","at":"切片檢查顯示腫瘤是惡性的，腫瘤科醫師力勸立即動手術；但這位身體虛弱的八旬病人認為如此艱鉅的手術並不可行，轉而選擇了安寧緩和照護。"},{"w":"malnutrition","p":"n.","d":"Faulty or inadequate diet causing ill-health.","c":"營養不良","s":"The global report documented the paradox that malnutrition in its various forms — both undernutrition in low-income communities and diet-related obesity in high-income settings — had become the leading preventable cause of premature death and disability across every regional income category.","t":"全球報告記錄了一個悖論：各種形式的營養不良——低收入社區的營養不足和高收入環境中與飲食相關的肥胖——已成為每個地區收入類別中可預防的過早死亡和殘疾的主要原因。","as":"Chronic malnutrition remains rampant in drought-stricken regions, where indigent families subsist on a paucity of staple grains, and aid workers warn that such deprivation can permanently stunt children's cognitive development.","at":"在飽受乾旱之苦的地區，長期營養不良的情況依然普遍；貧困家庭只能靠少量主食穀物維生，援助人員警告，這種匱乏可能會永久阻礙孩童的認知發展。"},{"w":"privation","p":"n.","d":"Lack of basic necessities.","c":"匱乏；艱苦","s":"The expedition members had endured six weeks of considerable privation — inadequate food, sleeping in temperatures below minus thirty degrees Celsius, and the complete absence of any communication with the outside world — yet returned with research data of such exceptional scientific value that their sacrifice was unanimously considered worthwhile.","t":"探險隊員們忍受了六週相當大的匱乏——食物不足、在攝氏零下三十度以下的溫度中睡覺，以及與外界完全失去聯繫——但帶回了科學價值如此卓越的研究數據，使他們的犧牲被一致認為是值得的。","as":"Despite the privation of years spent in exile, the poet refused to repudiate his political convictions, and the deceptively laconic verses he composed in his bare abode are now regarded as masterpieces of resistance literature.","at":"儘管流亡多年、生活困頓，這位詩人始終不肯放棄自己的政治信念；他在簡陋居所中寫下那些看似簡短的詩句，如今被視為抵抗文學的傑作。"},{"w":"remote","p":"adj.","d":"Distant, hidden away, unlikely.","c":"遙遠的；偏僻的","s":"The archaeological team spent three seasons excavating the remote site in the high mountain plateau, accessible only by a four-hour helicopter flight from the nearest town, their isolation complete and their supplies dependent on weather conditions that frequently prevented re-provisioning for weeks at a time.","t":"考古隊花了三個季節挖掘高山高原上的偏遠遺址，只能從最近的城鎮乘坐四小時直升機到達，他們的隔離是完全的，補給品依賴於天氣條件，這些條件經常阻止一次長達數週的補給。","as":"Linguists documenting endangered languages often travel to remote villages where the obsolescence of the local tongue seems inexorable, so they work with alacrity to record every nuance of its grammar before the last fluent speakers pass away.","at":"記錄瀕危語言的語言學家經常前往偏遠的村落，那裡的在地語言似乎無可避免地走向消亡，因此他們爭分奪秒地記錄其文法的每一個細微之處，趕在最後一批流利使用者離世之前。"},{"w":"respite","p":"n.","d":"A short period of relief from difficulty.","c":"喘息；暫緩","s":"The unexpected week of mild weather provided a welcome respite for rescue operations that had been suspended for ten days due to severe conditions, allowing recovery teams to reach several previously inaccessible areas and locate survivors whose locations had been identified through aerial thermal imaging.","t":"意外出現的一週溫和天氣為因嚴酷條件暫停了十天的救援行動提供了受歡迎的喘息機會，使救援隊能夠抵達幾個以前無法進入的地區，並找到通過空中熱成像確定位置的倖存者。","as":"The brief ceasefire offered civilians a much-needed respite from the shelling, but within days skirmishes resumed along the front, exacerbating a humanitarian crisis that aid agencies had implored both sides to address.","at":"短暫的停火讓平民在砲擊中獲得急需的喘息，但不出幾天，前線又爆發小規模衝突，使援助機構懇求雙方正視的人道危機更加惡化。"},{"w":"reverberating","p":"adj.","d":"Echoing, resounding persistently.","c":"迴盪的；持續回響的","s":"The reverberating impact of the financial crisis continued to reshape political landscapes across the continent more than a decade after its initial onset, the accumulated resentment of populations who felt they had borne a disproportionate burden of recovery costs expressing itself in sustained support for anti-establishment political movements.","t":"金融危機的持續影響在其最初發生十多年後繼續重塑整個大陸的政治格局，感覺自己承擔了不成比例的復甦成本負擔的民眾積累的怨恨，通過持續支持反建制政治運動來表達。","as":"Long after the final chord, the reverberating tones of the cathedral organ lingered beneath the vaulted ceiling, enhancing the music's solemnity so profoundly that the throng of tourists fell silent and even restless children ceased to jostle one another.","at":"最後一個和弦結束許久之後，大教堂管風琴的迴盪樂音仍在拱頂下縈繞，大大增添了音樂的莊嚴感，讓成群的遊客都安靜下來，就連躁動的孩子也不再互相推擠。"},{"w":"sanctuary","p":"n.","d":"A place of shelter and protection.","c":"避難所；庇護所","s":"The protected nature reserve functioned as a vital sanctuary for several critically endangered migratory species, providing the undisturbed breeding habitat and reliable food sources necessary for population recovery in the face of the dramatic habitat loss occurring in the surrounding agricultural landscape.","t":"保護自然保護區作為幾種極度瀕危遷徙物種的重要避難所，在周圍農業景觀發生的巨大棲息地喪失面前，為種群恢復提供了必要的不受干擾的繁殖棲息地和可靠的食物來源。","as":"During the purges, the mountain monastery served as a sanctuary for dissidents, and the intrepid monks flouted the decrees promulgated by the regime, refusing to surrender anyone who had sought refuge within its walls.","at":"在整肅期間，這座山中修道院成為異議人士的避難所；無畏的修士們公然違抗政權頒布的法令，拒絕交出任何在院牆內尋求庇護的人。"},{"w":"sinister","p":"adj.","d":"Evil, ominous, threatening harm.","c":"邪惡的；不祥的","s":"There was something deeply sinister about the way the anonymous messages had been timed to arrive precisely when the journalist was most vulnerable — late at night, during personal crises, immediately after the publication of sensitive investigations — suggesting a level of surveillance that went far beyond casual monitoring.","t":"匿名消息的到達時間有些深刻的邪惡之處——精確地在記者最脆弱的時候到達——深夜、個人危機期間、敏感調查發布後立即——這表明監視程度遠遠超出了偶爾的監控。","as":"Beneath the philanthropist's genial public persona lay a sinister ambition, and the novel's protagonist, initially duped by his generosity, gradually discerns the nefarious scheme that has enriched him at the expense of an entire town.","at":"在這位慈善家和藹可親的公眾形象之下，隱藏著邪惡的野心；小說主角起初被他的慷慨所矇騙，後來才逐漸識破這個犧牲整座城鎮來讓他致富的罪惡陰謀。"},{"w":"succumb","p":"v.","d":"To give way, yield to a force.","c":"屈服；死於","s":"Despite the initial optimism of the medical team and the patient's own remarkable determination during the first months of treatment, he ultimately succumb to the infection in the fourth week of his second hospital admission, having fought with extraordinary courage against a condition that had proved resistant to every available therapeutic intervention.","t":"儘管醫療團隊最初樂觀，以及患者在治療的前幾個月自身表現出非凡的決心，但他最終在第二次住院的第四週死於感染，以非凡的勇氣對抗了一種被證明對所有可用治療干預都有抵抗力的病情。","as":"Although the empire had withstood centuries of foreign invasions, it eventually began to succumb to internal decay, as rampant corruption, interminable civil wars, and an arbitrary system of taxation eroded the loyalty of its subjects.","at":"雖然這個帝國抵擋了數百年的外族入侵，最終卻逐漸屈服於內部的腐敗，因為猖獗的貪污、沒完沒了的內戰和任意武斷的稅制，侵蝕了子民的忠誠。"},{"w":"surge","p":"v.","d":"To rush suddenly, to increase sharply.","c":"湧動；急增","s":"Demand for the product surge unexpectedly in the fourth quarter, exceeding the most optimistic sales forecasts by a margin of nearly forty percent and creating immediate supply chain pressures that the company's logistics infrastructure was not configured to absorb without significant lead time for capacity expansion.","t":"該產品的需求在第四季度意外激增，超過了最樂觀的銷售預測近百分之四十，產生了公司物流基礎設施沒有配置為在沒有大量産能擴張準備時間的情況下吸收的立即供應鏈壓力。","as":"When the central bank unexpectedly cut interest rates, demand for urban apartments began to surge, as affluent buyers and avid speculators competed for scarce listings, prompting economists to warn of a fiasco reminiscent of earlier housing bubbles.","at":"中央銀行出乎意料地降息後，都市公寓的需求開始急遽攀升，富裕的買家和熱衷的投機客爭搶稀少的物件，促使經濟學家警告，可能會重演過去房市泡沫那樣的慘敗。"},{"w":"thwart","p":"v.","d":"To hinder, prevent, frustrate.","c":"阻撓；妨礙","s":"The security services were able to thwart the attempted cyber intrusion before it reached the critical infrastructure systems it had been targeting, though the sophistication of the attack methodology suggested the involvement of a state-sponsored actor with access to significantly more advanced technical resources than previously observed.","t":"安全部門能夠在網絡入侵嘗試到達其目標的關鍵基礎設施系統之前阻止它，儘管攻擊方法的複雜性表明涉及一個國家支持的行為者，其擁有比以前觀察到的更先進的技術資源。","as":"Alert customs officers managed to thwart an attempt to smuggle rare orchids out of the country after noticing an incongruous tinge of damp soil on a tourist's luggage, and the smuggler's effort to fabricate an alibi quickly unraveled.","at":"機警的海關人員注意到一名遊客的行李上有一絲不尋常的潮濕泥土痕跡，因而成功阻止了一起走私稀有蘭花出境的企圖，而走私者捏造不在場證明的說詞也很快就被拆穿。"},{"w":"tranquil","p":"adj.","d":"Quiet, peaceful, calm.","c":"寧靜的；平靜的","s":"The tranquil surface of the alpine lake in the early morning, perfectly reflecting the surrounding peaks and the slowly brightening sky before the arrival of hikers disturbed its stillness, presented the kind of complete visual serenity that landscape photographers travel considerable distances specifically to capture.","t":"高山湖泊清晨平靜的水面在徒步旅行者到來打擾其靜謐之前，完美地映照著周圍的山峰和緩緩明亮的天空，呈現出那種風景攝影師特地長途跋涉前來捕捉的完整視覺寧靜。","as":"Steeped in centuries of Zen tradition, the tranquil temple gardens of Kyoto, with their raked gravel and mossy stones, offer visitors a solace that contrasts sharply with the mundane bustle of the modern city outside their walls.","at":"京都的寺院庭園浸潤在數百年的禪宗傳統中，耙紋整齊的砂礫與長滿青苔的石頭營造出寧靜的氛圍，帶給遊客一份慰藉，與牆外現代都市平凡忙亂的喧囂形成強烈對比。"},{"w":"ubiquitous","p":"adj.","d":"Present or found everywhere.","c":"無所不在的；普遍的","s":"The technology had become so ubiquitous within less than a decade of its commercial introduction that younger generations could scarcely imagine how work, communication, or entertainment had functioned before its existence, while older users could recall vividly the specific moment when they had first encountered and been transformed by it.","t":"這項技術在商業推出不到十年內就變得無所不在，以至於年輕一代幾乎無法想象在它出現之前工作、通信或娛樂是如何運作的，而老用戶則能清楚地記得他們第一次接觸並被它改變的具體時刻。","as":"Plastic microfibers have become so ubiquitous that scientists have detected them in Arctic ice and deep-sea sediments, and researchers attribute this pernicious pollution partly to the indiscriminate disposal of synthetic textiles, though its precise effects on health remain elusive.","at":"塑膠微纖維已變得無所不在，科學家甚至在北極冰層和深海沉積物中都偵測到它們；研究人員認為，這種有害的污染部分源於合成纖維織品的隨意丟棄，不過它對健康的確切影響仍難以釐清。"}]},{"unit":9,"cards":[{"w":"adverse","p":"adj.","d":"Unfavourable, harmful, contrary.","c":"不利的；有害的","s":"Despite the adverse weather conditions that had caused multiple competing teams to abandon their summit attempts, the experienced expedition retained sufficient supplies and maintained the psychological cohesion necessary to make a final push when a narrow window of improved conditions appeared on the sixth day.","t":"儘管不利的天氣條件導致多個競爭團隊放棄了他們的登頂嘗試，但這支有經驗的探險隊保留了足夠的補給，並在第六天出現了一個短暫的改善條件時機時，保持了進行最後衝刺所必需的心理凝聚力。","as":"Because the pesticide had become ubiquitous on farmland, ecologists warned of its adverse effects on pollinators, citing evidence that exposure left bees more likely to succumb to parasites, findings the manufacturer disparaged as alarmist.","at":"由於這種殺蟲劑在農地上已無所不在，生態學家警告它對授粉昆蟲的不利影響，並引用證據指出，接觸過的蜜蜂更容易死於寄生蟲；然而製造商卻詆毀這些研究結果是危言聳聽。"},{"w":"advocate","p":"v.","d":"To support, speak in favour of.","c":"提倡；支持","s":"The nutritional scientist spent three decades publishing research and giving public lectures to advocate for a fundamental reassessment of official dietary guidelines, arguing that the evidence base underlying several key recommendations had not been updated to reflect the substantial body of contrary clinical evidence accumulated since their initial formulation.","t":"這位營養科學家花了三十年發表研究成果和進行公開演講，提倡對官方飲食指南進行根本性重新評估，認為支撐幾項關鍵建議的證據基礎沒有更新，以反映自最初制定以來積累的大量相反臨床證據。","as":"Many urban planners advocate replacing congested boulevards with tranquil pedestrian zones, arguing that such changes enhance community life, though some shop owners bristle at the prospect of losing customers who arrive by car.","at":"許多都市規劃者提倡把擁擠的林蔭大道改造成寧靜的行人徒步區，認為這樣的改變能提升社區生活品質；不過有些店家一想到可能失去開車前來的顧客就十分惱火。"},{"w":"amicable","p":"adj.","d":"Friendly, done in a peaceable spirit.","c":"友好的；和睦的","s":"After eighteen months of litigation that had generated substantial legal costs for both parties and considerable media attention, the two companies reached an amicable out-of-court settlement that allowed both sides to avoid the unpredictable outcome of a verdict and to preserve the commercial relationship they had maintained for fourteen years.","t":"在產生了雙方大量法律費用和相當大媒體關注的十八個月訴訟之後，兩家公司達成了友好的庭外和解，使雙方能夠避免裁決的不可預測結果，並保留他們維持了十四年的商業關係。","as":"After years of acrimonious litigation, the two technology firms reached an amicable settlement, agreeing to share their patents and terminate all pending lawsuits, much to the relief of investors who had grown fretful about mounting legal costs.","at":"經過多年尖銳激烈的訴訟後，這兩家科技公司達成了友好的和解，同意共享專利並終止所有未決的訴訟，讓原本對節節攀升的法律費用感到焦躁不安的投資人鬆了一口氣。"},{"w":"asset","p":"n.","d":"A valuable or useful thing.","c":"資產；有價值之物","s":"The new employee's multilingual capability — she was fluent in six languages including Mandarin, Arabic, and Portuguese — proved an invaluable asset for the international development organisation, which had been struggling to communicate effectively with partner communities across three distinct regional programmes.","t":"新員工的多語言能力——她能流利地使用六種語言，包括普通話、阿拉伯語和葡萄牙語——被證明是這個國際發展組織的寶貴資產，該組織一直在努力與三個不同地區計劃的合作社區進行有效溝通。","as":"In an age of rapid obsolescence, employers increasingly perceive adaptability as a greater asset than mastery of any single program, and aspirants who cling to one narrow specialty may find their expertise worthless almost overnight.","at":"在事物迅速被淘汰的時代，雇主越來越把適應力視為比精通任何單一軟體更有價值的資產；而那些固守單一狹隘專長、力求晉升的人，可能會發現自己的專業幾乎在一夕之間變得毫無價值。"},{"w":"astute","p":"adj.","d":"Keen, shrewd, clever in practical matters.","c":"機敏的；精明的","s":"The astute investor had recognised early that the apparent volatility in the sector represented a fundamental mispricing rather than a genuine deterioration in the underlying business fundamentals, positioning herself to benefit significantly when the market eventually corrected its error over the following eighteen months.","t":"這位精明的投資者很早就認識到，這個行業的明顯波動性代表了一種根本性的錯誤定價，而不是基本業務基本面的真實惡化，使自己在市場最終在接下來十八個月糾正錯誤時獲益匪淺。","as":"An astute observer of human nature, Jane Austen exposed the duplicity and petty vanities of the English gentry with such subtle irony that many affluent readers failed to discern that they themselves were the targets of her satire.","at":"珍．奧斯汀是洞察人性的敏銳觀察者，她以極其含蓄的反諷揭露英國仕紳階級的虛偽與小小的虛榮，以致許多富裕的讀者根本沒有察覺，自己正是她諷刺的對象。"},{"w":"bigot","p":"n.","d":"A narrow-minded, prejudiced person.","c":"偏執者；頑固者","s":"The documentary examined how a confirmed bigot could gradually have his views moderated through sustained personal contact with members of the group he had previously demonised, a process that researchers described as contact theory in action and which the subject himself found both deeply uncomfortable and ultimately transformative.","t":"這部紀錄片探討了一個確認的偏執者如何通過與他以前妖魔化的群體成員的持續個人接觸逐漸緩和其觀點，研究人員將這一過程描述為接觸理論的實踐，而受試者本人認為這既非常不舒適又最終是變革性的。","as":"The documentary portrays the former mayor as an unrepentant bigot who castigated immigrant families in caustic speeches and stymied every proposal for a multicultural community center, until exasperated residents finally ousted him at the polls.","at":"這部紀錄片將前任市長描繪成一個毫無悔意的偏執者：他在尖刻的演說中嚴厲抨擊移民家庭，並阻撓每一項興建多元文化社區中心的提案，直到忍無可忍的居民終於用選票將他趕下台。"},{"w":"blatant","p":"adj.","d":"Obvious, conspicuously bad.","c":"明目張膽的；公然的","s":"The auditors identified a blatantediscrepancy between the declared income figures and the actual bank deposits during the period under review, a gap of over three hundred thousand dollars that would have been immediately apparent to any competent examiner applying even the most basic forensic accounting procedures.","t":"審計人員確定了審查期間申報的收入數字與實際銀行存款之間的明目張膽差異，超過三十萬美元的差距對任何應用最基本法證會計程序的稱職審查員來說都會立即顯而易見。","as":"The cyclist's blatant violation of anti-doping rules caused consternation among his fans, and his inane claim that the banned substance had been inadvertently added to his breakfast only deepened public skepticism.","at":"這名自行車選手公然違反禁藥規定，令他的支持者驚愕不已；而他荒謬地聲稱禁藥是被人不小心加進早餐裡，只讓大眾更加懷疑。"},{"w":"entourage","p":"n.","d":"A group of attendants or associates.","c":"隨從；隨行人員","s":"The visiting head of state arrived with an entourage of forty-seven officials, advisers, security personnel, and administrative support staff, the logistical requirements of which had consumed three months of coordinating work by protocol officers from both governments before the state visit could be confirmed.","t":"這位到訪的國家元首帶來了四十七名官員、顧問、安全人員和行政支持人員的隨行團隊，在正式訪問得到確認之前，其後勤要求消耗了兩國政府禮賓官員三個月的協調工作。","as":"The visiting monarch traveled with an enormous entourage of courtiers, servants, and guards, an extravagant spectacle that the indigent throngs lining the streets, many of whom could barely afford bread, regarded with silent disdain.","at":"來訪的君主帶著由朝臣、僕役和侍衛組成的龐大隨行人員，這種鋪張的排場，讓沿街圍觀、許多人連麵包都快買不起的貧苦群眾默默投以鄙視的眼光。"},{"w":"extortion","p":"n.","d":"Getting money or favours through threats.","c":"勒索；敲詐","s":"The investigation revealed a systematic extortion operation that had been targeting small business owners in the district for nearly four years, with organised crime figures threatening property damage, regulatory complaints, or physical harm unless monthly protection payments were maintained without interruption or disclosure.","t":"調查揭示了一個系統性的勒索行動，近四年來一直以該地區的小企業主為目標，有組織犯罪人物威脅財產損壞、監管投訴或人身傷害，除非每月的保護費不間斷地支付且不被披露。","as":"The crime syndicate grew rich through extortion, threatening shopkeepers who refused to pay for protection, and its infamous leader enjoyed impunity for years by intimidating any witness willing to testify against him.","at":"這個犯罪集團靠勒索致富，威脅那些不肯繳交保護費的店家；而它惡名昭彰的首腦藉由恐嚇任何願意出庭指證他的證人，多年來都逍遙法外。"},{"w":"impresario","p":"n.","d":"An organiser of entertainment.","c":"演出經紀人；主辦人","s":"The legendary concert impresario had discovered and managed the careers of three of the most commercially successful performers of the preceding three decades, his exceptional ability to identify emerging talent before it was widely recognised having made him one of the most influential figures in the global entertainment industry.","t":"這位傳奇的演出經紀人在過去三十年中發現並管理了三位最具商業成功的表演者的職業生涯，他在廣為人知之前識別新興才能的非凡能力使他成為全球娛樂業最有影響力的人物之一。","as":"The flamboyant impresario behind the touring circus was an adroit showman who could cajole even skeptical investors, though his verbose advertisements often promised spectacles that no troupe could possibly deliver.","at":"這個巡迴馬戲團背後那位浮誇的演出經紀人是個手腕高明的表演家，連心存懷疑的投資人都能被他哄得心動；不過他冗長的廣告經常承諾一些任何劇團都不可能做到的奇觀。"},{"w":"ineffectual","p":"adj.","d":"Unable to accomplish anything, weak.","c":"無效的；軟弱無能的","s":"The government's response to the housing crisis was widely criticised as ineffectual, with analysts pointing out that the modest tax incentives and voluntary developer commitments announced in the policy package were wholly inadequate to address a structural shortfall in affordable housing stock that had been accumulating for over twenty years.","t":"政府對住房危機的回應受到廣泛批評，認為是無效的，分析人士指出，政策包中宣布的適度稅收激勵措施和自願開發商承諾完全不足以解決已積累超過二十年的可負擔住房供應結構性短缺。","as":"Historians generally regard the League of Nations as ineffectual in the years before the Second World War, since it lacked an army of its own and could not thwart belligerent powers that openly flouted its resolutions.","at":"歷史學家普遍認為，國際聯盟在第二次世界大戰前的那些年裡軟弱無能，因為它沒有自己的軍隊，無法阻止那些公然無視其決議的好戰強權。"},{"w":"loath","p":"adj.","d":"Unwilling, reluctant.","c":"不情願的；勉強的","s":"She was deeply loath to accept the promotion, recognising that the additional salary and status came with a level of administrative responsibility and political exposure that would inevitably reduce her time for the laboratory research that had always been both her primary professional motivation and her greatest source of personal satisfaction.","t":"她非常不情願接受晉升，認識到額外的薪水和地位帶來了一定程度的行政責任和政治曝光，這不可避免地會減少她從事實驗室研究的時間，而這一直是她主要的職業動力和個人最大的滿足感來源。","as":"Although the new evidence was compelling, the committee was loath to repudiate the eminent professor's theory, partly out of deference to his reputation and partly because doing so might exacerbate tensions within an already divided department.","at":"雖然新證據很有說服力，委員會卻不願否定這位傑出教授的理論，一方面是出於對他聲望的尊重，另一方面則是因為這樣做可能會讓原本就分裂的系所內部關係更加緊張。"},{"w":"malady","p":"n.","d":"A disease or disorder.","c":"疾病；弊病","s":"The physician cautioned that the apparent improvement in the patient's condition might represent temporary symptomatic relief rather than a genuine resolution of the underlying malady, and that premature discontinuation of the treatment regimen would risk a rapid relapse potentially more severe than the original presentation.","t":"醫生警告說，患者病情的明顯改善可能代表暫時的症狀緩解，而不是根本疾病的真正解決，提前停止治療方案將冒著快速復發的風險，可能比原始表現更為嚴重。","as":"Some sociologists contend that loneliness has become a pervasive malady of modern urban life, one that can afflict even prosperous professionals and is compounded by ubiquitous digital devices that offer connection without genuine intimacy.","at":"有些社會學家主張，孤獨已成為現代都市生活中普遍存在的弊病，就連事業有成的專業人士也可能深受其苦；而無所不在的數位裝置只提供連結、卻沒有真正的親密感，更讓這個問題雪上加霜。"},{"w":"nefarious","p":"adj.","d":"Wicked, villainous, criminal.","c":"邪惡的；罪惡的","s":"The parliamentary inquiry concluded that the regulatory failures had allowed nefarious financial practices to flourish for nearly a decade without detection, enabling a small number of institutional actors to extract extraordinary profits through mechanisms that were clearly designed to obscure their harmful effects from oversight bodies.","t":"議會調查得出結論，監管失敗允許邪惡的金融行為在近十年內不被發現，使少數機構行為者能夠通過明顯旨在向監督機構掩蓋其有害影響的機制獲取巨額利潤。","as":"Detectives uncovered a nefarious plot in which corrupt officials had furtively diverted relief funds intended for drought victims, leaving entire villages in the parched highlands to endure months of privation and widespread malnutrition.","at":"警探揭發了一樁罪惡的陰謀：貪腐官員暗中挪用原本要給旱災災民的救濟金，使得乾旱高地上整座村莊的居民承受數月的匱乏與普遍的營養不良。"},{"w":"scrutinize","p":"v.","d":"To examine closely and critically.","c":"仔細檢查；審查","s":"The independent ethics committee was established specifically to scrutinize the research proposals submitted by investigators who had declared commercial interests, applying a higher level of methodological review and conflict-of-interest assessment than was routinely required for applications without such financial complications.","t":"獨立倫理委員會的建立是專門為了仔細審查聲明有商業利益的研究人員提交的研究提案，對這些申請應用比沒有此類財務複雜情況的申請通常所需更高水平的方法論審查和利益衝突評估。","as":"Before accepting the startling claim, the journal asked independent statisticians to scrutinize the raw data, and their analysis revealed that the authors had fabricated several key results, a fiasco that rendered every earlier study from the laboratory dubious.","at":"在接受這項驚人的主張之前，期刊請獨立的統計學家仔細審查原始數據，結果發現作者捏造了幾項關鍵結果；這場大失敗讓該實驗室先前的每一項研究都變得可疑。"},{"w":"solicit","p":"v.","d":"To beg, seek, or ask for.","c":"懇求；徵求","s":"The charity was legally prohibited from directly solicitedonations from members of the public in a public space without a licence, a restriction that had significantly reduced its traditional street-collection income and forced the organisation to develop alternative digital fundraising strategies to compensate for the shortfall.","t":"該慈善機構在法律上被禁止在沒有許可證的情況下在公共場所直接向公眾徵求捐款，這一限制大大減少了其傳統的街頭募款收入，迫使該組織開發替代性數字籌款策略以彌補短缺。","as":"To fund the restoration of the crumbling cathedral, volunteers began to solicit donations door to door with remarkable alacrity, though a few residents complained of being badgered so persistently that they contributed simply to restore their tranquil evenings.","at":"為了籌措修復這座搖搖欲墜的大教堂所需的經費，志工們以驚人的熱忱挨家挨戶募款；不過也有幾位居民抱怨被糾纏得太頻繁，最後捐錢只是為了換回寧靜的夜晚。"},{"w":"spew","p":"v.","d":"To pour out, eject forcefully.","c":"噴出；大量湧出","s":"The industrial plant continued to spew toxic effluents into the river system despite repeated enforcement notices from the environmental agency, the company's management apparently calculating that the ongoing fines represented a more economically rational response than investing in the remediation systems that proper compliance would require.","t":"儘管環保機構多次發出執法通知，工業廠仍繼續向河流系統噴出有毒廢水，公司管理層顯然認為持續的罰款比投資於適當合規所需的補救系統在經濟上更為合理。","as":"For weeks the volcano continued to spew ash and toxic gases, and the reverberating rumbles beneath the mountain, which seismologists construed as a harbinger of a larger eruption, forced thousands of residents to evacuate.","at":"這座火山連續數週不斷噴出火山灰和有毒氣體，而山底下持續迴盪的隆隆聲被地震學家解讀為更大規模噴發的前兆，迫使數千名居民撤離。"},{"w":"venom","p":"n.","d":"Poison, malice, spite.","c":"毒液；惡意","s":"The political commentator's columns were notable for the concentrated venom they directed at the opposition leadership, employing a register of personal attack that went considerably beyond conventional political criticism and which the targets' legal advisers were monitoring closely for potential defamation claims.","t":"這位政治評論員的專欄因其對反對派領導層集中的惡毒攻擊而引人注目，採用了一種遠遠超出傳統政治批評的人身攻擊語氣，目標方的法律顧問正在密切關注可能的誹謗索賠。","as":"The two rival poets attacked each other with such venom in published pamphlets, each belittling the other's verse as clumsy doggerel, that their scurrilous feud eclipsed their poetry and attracted a voracious readership of its own.","at":"這兩位互相較勁的詩人在出版的小冊子裡以極其惡毒的言辭彼此攻擊，都貶低對方的詩作是拙劣的打油詩；他們這場粗鄙的筆戰甚至蓋過了詩作本身，吸引了一大群如飢似渴的讀者。"},{"w":"vexatious","p":"adj.","d":"Causing annoyance, troublesome.","c":"令人煩惱的；惱人的","s":"The planning department had received numerous complaints about what residents described as vexatious late-night deliveries to the newly opened distribution centre, with residents reporting that the combination of reversing alarms, diesel engines, and radio communications regularly disrupted sleep from two in the morning onwards.","t":"規劃部門收到了大量關於居民描述為令人煩惱的深夜向新開放的配送中心送貨的投訴，居民報告說倒車警報、柴油發動機和無線電通信的組合從凌晨兩點開始定期干擾睡眠。","as":"Judges may dismiss vexatious lawsuits filed merely to harass a rival, and several jurisdictions now penalize plaintiffs who repeatedly file baseless claims in an attempt to intimidate journalists and critics into silence.","at":"法官可以駁回那些純粹為了騷擾對手而提起的惱人訴訟；而且如今已有好幾個司法管轄區會處罰一再提出毫無根據的訴訟、企圖恐嚇記者和批評者噤聲的原告。"},{"w":"virulent","p":"adj.","d":"Full of hatred, extremely harmful.","c":"劇毒的；惡毒的","s":"The newly identified pathogen proved to be exceptionally virulent, spreading with a rapidity that overwhelmed the local healthcare infrastructure within seventy-two hours of the first confirmed cases, necessitating the immediate mobilisation of regional emergency medical reserves and the temporary closure of all educational institutions within the affected zone.","t":"新發現的病原體被證明是非常致命的，在第一批確認病例後七十二小時內以壓倒當地醫療基礎設施的速度傳播，需要立即調動地區緊急醫療儲備，並臨時關閉受影響區域內的所有教育機構。","as":"The virulent strain spread with alarming speed through the crowded refugee camps, where malnutrition and a paucity of clean water had left residents especially vulnerable, and overstretched doctors struggled for weeks to quell the outbreak.","at":"這種劇毒的病株以驚人的速度在擁擠的難民營中蔓延，那裡的居民因營養不良和乾淨用水匱乏而格外容易受到感染，人手不足的醫生們奮鬥了好幾週才勉強控制住疫情。"}]},{"unit":10,"cards":[{"w":"desist","p":"v.","d":"To cease, stop an activity.","c":"停止；終止","s":"The court issued a formal cease and desist order requiring the defendant to immediately discontinue all use of the trademarked brand name, remove all infringing materials from its website within forty-eight hours, and provide a sworn affidavit confirming compliance within ten business days.","t":"法院發布了一項正式的停止令，要求被告立即停止對商標品牌名稱的所有使用，在四十八小時內從其網站上刪除所有侵權材料，並在十個工作日內提供確認合規的宣誓書。","as":"The court ordered the developer to desist from clearing the ancient forest, but he openly flouted the injunction, prompting conservationists, cognizant of how swiftly irreversible damage could occur, to solicit emergency intervention from federal authorities.","at":"法院命令開發商停止砍伐這片古老森林，但他公然無視禁制令；保育人士深知不可逆的破壞可能轉眼發生，於是向聯邦當局請求緊急介入。"},{"w":"doleful","p":"adj.","d":"Sad, melancholy, expressing grief.","c":"悲哀的；憂鬱的","s":"The memorial concert concluded with the choir's performance of a hauntingly doleful lament composed specifically for the occasion, the piece's sustained minor harmonies and the simplicity of its recurring melodic phrase combining to produce an emotional effect that reduced several hundred audience members to tears.","t":"紀念音樂會以合唱團演唱的一首悲哀輓歌結束，這首歌是專門為這個場合創作的，作品持續的小調和聲和其反復旋律片段的簡潔性結合起來產生了使幾百名觀眾淚流滿面的情感效果。","as":"Written shortly after the death of his young daughter, the composer's doleful elegy eschews ornamentation in favor of a sparse, halting melody that conveys a grief so profound that no solace seems possible.","at":"這首哀戚的輓歌是作曲家在年幼女兒過世後不久寫成的，它捨棄繁複的裝飾，改用稀疏而斷續的旋律，傳達出一種深沉到似乎無從慰藉的悲痛。"},{"w":"elusive","p":"adj.","d":"Hard to grasp, pin down, or find.","c":"難以捉摸的；難以獲得的","s":"A definitive scientific consensus on the mechanisms underlying consciousness has proved remarkably elusive, with competing theoretical frameworks — each supported by credible experimental evidence — continuing to generate productive disagreement among neuroscientists, philosophers, and cognitive scientists several decades into systematic investigation.","t":"關於意識基礎機制的明確科學共識被證明極難捉摸，每個由可信實驗證據支持的競爭性理論框架，在系統調查幾十年後，繼續在神經科學家、哲學家和認知科學家之間產生富有成效的分歧。","as":"Despite decades of research, a satisfying explanation of consciousness remains elusive, and even eminent neuroscientists concede that current theories are rudimentary, often crumbling as soon as skeptical colleagues scrutinize their assumptions.","at":"儘管經過數十年的研究，意識仍然難以得到令人滿意的解釋；就連傑出的神經科學家也承認，現有的理論仍屬粗淺，一旦抱持懷疑的同行仔細檢視其前提，往往就站不住腳。"},{"w":"engrossed","p":"adj.","d":"Fully absorbed, completely occupied.","c":"全神貫注的；專心致志的","s":"She became so completely engrossed in the manuscript that she failed to notice the gradual darkening of the afternoon sky, the persistent knocking at her study door, or the fact that she had been sitting in the same position for over four hours without food, water, or any break in her concentration.","t":"她完全沉浸在手稿中，以至於沒有注意到下午天空逐漸變暗、書房門持續的敲門聲，也沒有注意到她已經在同一位置坐了四個多小時，沒有食物、水或任何注意力的中斷。","as":"So engrossed was the historian in the medieval annals that she remained in the archive long after closing time, and a vigilant guard, mistaking her for an intruder, accosted her in the darkened reading room.","at":"這位歷史學家全神貫注地研讀中世紀編年史，在閉館後許久仍留在檔案室裡；一名警覺的警衛誤以為她是闖入者，在昏暗的閱覽室裡上前厲聲盤問她。"},{"w":"frustrate","p":"v.","d":"To foil, prevent from achieving.","c":"挫敗；使沮喪","s":"The persistent bureaucratic delays that had been allowed to frustrate the environmental impact assessment process for over three years were ultimately challenged through judicial review, with the court finding that the responsible authority had acted unreasonably in consistently deferring decisions that the legislation clearly required to be made within specified timeframes.","t":"被允許阻撓環境影響評估過程超過三年的持續官僚延遲最終通過司法審查受到挑戰，法院認定負責機構在一貫推遲立法明確要求在特定時限內做出的決定方面行為不合理。","as":"The opposition used interminable speeches and a barrage of amendments to frustrate the government's reform agenda, and the prime minister, conceding defeat with evident chagrin, eventually reverted to a far more modest plan.","at":"反對黨以冗長不休的演說和接連不斷的修正案來阻撓政府的改革議程；首相最後帶著明顯的懊惱認輸，退回到一個規模小得多的方案。"},{"w":"histrionics","p":"n.","d":"Exaggerated theatrical behaviour.","c":"裝腔作勢；誇張表演","s":"The mediator privately viewed the CEO's display of wounded dignity and barely suppressed tears as calculated histrionicsedesigned to gain negotiating advantage, a performance that might have been convincing to observers unfamiliar with his established pattern of emotional manipulation during previous high-stakes commercial negotiations.","t":"調解員私下認為CEO表現出受傷尊嚴和幾乎壓抑的眼淚是計算好的誇張表演，旨在獲得談判優勢，這種表演對不熟悉他在以前高風險商業談判中建立的情緒操縱模式的觀察者來說可能是令人信服的。","as":"Jurors seemed unmoved by the defense attorney's histrionics, which included weeping and gesticulating wildly throughout her verbose closing argument, and they ultimately concurred that the evidence against the defendant was overwhelming.","at":"陪審員似乎完全不為辯護律師的誇張表演所動──她在冗長的結辯中一邊哭泣、一邊誇張地揮舞手臂──他們最終一致認為，對被告不利的證據確鑿無疑。"},{"w":"imminent","p":"adj.","d":"About to happen, threatening.","c":"迫近的；即將發生的","s":"The seismological monitoring network detected precursors that indicated the imminent eruption of the dormant volcano with sufficient advance warning to allow the evacuation of approximately forty thousand residents from the highest-risk zones before the main eruptive episode began six days later.","t":"地震監測網絡探測到的前兆顯示休眠火山即將噴發，有足夠的提前預警，在六天後主要噴發事件開始之前允許從最高風險區域疏散約四萬名居民。","as":"When satellite images showed that the typhoon's landfall was imminent, officials ordered coastal residents to evacuate forthwith, but a few intrepid fishermen stayed behind, loath to abandon the boats that were their only valuable asset.","at":"衛星影像顯示颱風即將登陸時，官員下令沿海居民立即撤離；但仍有幾位無畏的漁民留了下來，因為他們不願拋下那些是自己唯一值錢資產的漁船。"},{"w":"inclement","p":"adj.","d":"Unfavourable, stormy, harsh.","c":"惡劣的；嚴酷的","s":"The race organisers delayed the start by ninety minutes due to inclement weather conditions, but eventually made the reluctant decision to cancel the event entirely when updated meteorological forecasts confirmed that conditions would deteriorate further throughout the afternoon rather than improving as initially predicted.","t":"比賽組織者因惡劣的天氣條件將開始時間推遲了九十分鐘，但最終做出了取消整個賽事的不情願決定，當時更新的氣象預報確認條件將在整個下午進一步惡化，而不是如最初預測的那樣改善。","as":"Weeks of inclement weather thwarted the expedition's attempt to ascend the summit, and the climbers, emaciated after subsisting on meager rations, reluctantly abandoned their goal and began the long descent.","at":"連續數週的惡劣天氣阻撓了探險隊攻頂的計畫；靠著微薄口糧維生而變得憔悴消瘦的登山者們，只好無奈地放棄目標，開始漫長的下山路程。"},{"w":"inert","p":"adj.","d":"Without power to move, sluggish.","c":"遲鈍的；惰性的","s":"The political opposition had become increasingly inert over the preceding parliamentary term, failing to mount coherent challenges to several significant pieces of legislation that numerous commentators considered constitutionally questionable, a passivity attributed by observers to internal factional divisions and an absence of effective centralised leadership.","t":"政治反對派在上一個議會任期內變得越來越遲鈍，未能對幾項許多評論家認為在憲法上存疑的重要立法提出連貫的挑戰，觀察人士將這種消極性歸因於內部派系分裂和有效中央領導的缺失。","as":"Lying inert on a sun-warmed rock in the tranquil desert morning, the lizard appeared oblivious to its surroundings, yet the instant an insect strayed nearby, it would sally from its perch, revealing its stillness as a feint to lure unwary prey.","at":"在寧靜的沙漠清晨，這隻蜥蜴一動也不動地趴在被太陽曬暖的岩石上，看似對周遭渾然不覺；但只要有昆蟲靠近，牠就會立刻從棲處猛衝而出，顯示牠的靜止不過是引誘粗心獵物的假動作。"},{"w":"interject","p":"v.","d":"To interrupt with a comment.","c":"插嘴；打斷","s":"The chair of the panel discussion had to interject repeatedly throughout the evening to prevent the most vocal participant from monopolising every exchange, a delicate management challenge since the speaker's contributions, while disproportionately lengthy, were also among the most intellectually substantive of the evening.","t":"小組討論的主席在整個晚上不得不多次插嘴，以防止最直言不諱的參與者壟斷每一次交流，這是一個微妙的管理挑戰，因為演講者的貢獻雖然不成比例地冗長，但也是晚上智識上最有實質內容的之一。","as":"When the candidate began to disparage his opponent's record with dubious statistics, the moderator was compelled to interject, admonishing both speakers to support their claims with evidence rather than personal attacks.","at":"當候選人開始用可疑的統計數字貶低對手的政績時，主持人不得不插話，告誡兩位發言者要以證據支持自己的論點，而不是進行人身攻擊。"},{"w":"mastiff","p":"n.","d":"A large, powerful breed of dog.","c":"獒犬；大型猛犬","s":"The estate's pair of mastiff s, while temperamentally gentle with family members and trusted visitors, had been specifically trained to respond to unauthorised entry with a combination of sustained alarm barking and physical presence that had proved an effective deterrent against the series of rural burglaries affecting neighbouring properties.","t":"莊園的一對獒犬雖然對家庭成員和受信任的訪客性情溫和，但被專門訓練為用持續的警報吠叫和身體存在的組合來回應未經授權的進入，這已被證明是對影響鄰近房產的一系列農村入室盜竊的有效威懾。","as":"The affluent recluse's mansion was guarded by an enormous mastiff whose reverberating bark could deter even the most intrepid trespasser, though the dog was, by all accounts, remarkably gentle with children.","at":"這位富有的隱士宅邸由一隻巨大的獒犬看守，牠迴盪不絕的吠叫聲足以嚇退最大膽的闖入者；不過據大家所說，這隻狗對孩子卻出奇地溫和。"},{"w":"obsess","p":"v.","d":"To haunt, preoccupy the mind of.","c":"迷住；使困擾","s":"The unresolved questions surrounding his father's wartime service had begun to obsess him in a way that was affecting his professional effectiveness, and his therapist suggested that pursuing a systematic archival investigation might provide the closure necessary to allow him to disengage from the persistent and intrusive rumination.","t":"圍繞他父親戰時服役的未解決問題開始以影響他職業效率的方式困擾著他，他的治療師建議進行系統性的檔案調查可能提供必要的釋懷，使他能夠從持續的侵入性反芻中解脫出來。","as":"In Melville's novel, the hunt for the white whale comes to obsess Captain Ahab, whose implacable thirst for vengeance and perverse disregard for his crew's safety propel the hapless sailors toward catastrophe.","at":"在梅爾維爾的小說中，追捕白鯨這件事逐漸讓亞哈船長著了魔；他無法平息的復仇渴望，加上對船員安危固執而乖戾的漠視，將那些不幸的水手推向了災難。"},{"w":"pertinent","p":"adj.","d":"Relevant, appropriate to the situation.","c":"相關的；貼切的","s":"The presiding judge interrupted the defence counsel's extended argument to request that subsequent submissions be confined strictly to evidence that was directly pertinent to the specific charges under consideration, noting that several of the points raised in the preceding hour had no bearing on the legal questions the jury would be required to determine.","t":"主審法官打斷了辯護律師的長篇論點，要求後續提交的材料嚴格限於與正在考慮的具體指控直接相關的證據，指出前一小時提出的幾點對陪審團需要裁定的法律問題沒有任何關聯。","as":"The judge sustained the objection, ruling that questions about the witness's private life were not pertinent to the case and could be construed as an attempt to harass and intimidate her into recanting her testimony.","at":"法官裁定異議成立，認為有關證人私生活的問題與本案無關，而且可能被解讀為企圖騷擾、恐嚇她撤回證詞。"},{"w":"peruse","p":"v.","d":"To read carefully and thoroughly.","c":"仔細閱讀；審閱","s":"Board members were expected to have peruse the full four-hundred-page due diligence report before attending the extraordinary general meeting at which the proposed acquisition would be put to a vote, rather than relying solely on the executive summary that the investment bank had circulated as a briefing document.","t":"董事會成員應在出席將對擬議收購進行投票的特別股東大會之前仔細閱讀完整的四百頁盡職調查報告，而不僅僅依賴投資銀行作為簡報文件流通的執行摘要。","as":"Before casting their votes, conscientious legislators should peruse the full text of a bill rather than rely on perfunctory summaries prepared by lobbyists, which often omit untoward provisions buried deep within the verbose legislation.","at":"在投票之前，認真負責的立法委員應該仔細閱讀法案全文，而不是依賴遊說人士準備的草率摘要，因為這些摘要常常略去深埋在冗長條文中的不當條款。"},{"w":"premonition","p":"n.","d":"A forewarning or feeling of what is to come.","c":"預感；預兆","s":"She had experienced a powerful premonition of impending disaster throughout the morning that she was unable to rationalise or dismiss, a persistent sense of unease that she later found impossible to describe coherently to the investigator who interviewed her in the days following the accident she had foreseen.","t":"整個上午她都感受到即將發生災難的強烈預感，她無法理性化或忽視，一種持續的不安感，她後來發現難以連貫地向在她預見的事故發生後幾天採訪她的調查員描述。","as":"Haunted by a premonition of disaster, the fretful explorer filled his journal with ominous entries, yet he pressed onward across the ice, a decision that historians now regard as an egregious miscalculation.","at":"這位焦躁不安的探險家被災難將至的預感所困擾，在日記中寫滿不祥的記載，但他仍執意橫越冰原前進；歷史學家如今認為，這個決定是極其嚴重的誤判。"},{"w":"recoil","p":"v.","d":"To draw back, shrink from in disgust.","c":"退縮；畏縮","s":"She recoil instinctively from the graphic images included in the investigative report, having underestimated the visceral impact of seeing documented evidence of what she had previously understood only through statistical abstractions and second-hand narrative accounts of conditions in the detention facilities.","t":"她本能地從調查報告中包含的圖形圖像中退縮，低估了看到她以前只通過統計抽象和關於拘留設施條件的二手敘述報告所理解的已記錄證據的本能衝擊。","as":"Although some readers recoil from the novel's graphic depictions of trench warfare, the author maintains that softening those scenes would amount to a kind of euphemism, a betrayal of soldiers who endured privation and excruciating wounds.","at":"雖然有些讀者對小說中壕溝戰的血腥描寫感到畏縮，作者卻堅持，淡化那些場景無異於一種委婉粉飾，是對那些忍受匱乏與劇痛傷口的士兵的背叛。"},{"w":"salient","p":"adj.","d":"Most important, prominent, noticeable.","c":"顯著的；突出的","s":"In his closing argument, the defence attorney highlighted the three most salient weaknesses in the prosecution's case: the absence of physical evidence directly linking his client to the scene, the inconsistencies in the key witness's timeline, and the failure to investigate an alternative suspect who had both motive and opportunity.","t":"在結案陳詞中，辯護律師強調了檢方案件中三個最突出的弱點：缺乏直接將他的當事人與現場聯繫起來的實物證據、關鍵證人時間線中的不一致，以及未能調查一個同樣有動機和機會的替代嫌疑人。","as":"The most salient finding of the long-term study was that childhood malnutrition, rather than genetics, accounted for the stunted growth observed in the region, a conclusion that compelled officials to repudiate earlier claims and advocate free school meals.","at":"這項長期研究最顯著的發現是：該地區孩童發育遲緩的原因是兒時營養不良，而非遺傳；這個結論迫使官員推翻先前的說法，轉而提倡學校免費供餐。"},{"w":"squeamish","p":"adj.","d":"Easily nauseated or shocked.","c":"易受驚的；神經質的","s":"Prospective medical students are advised that those who are particularly squeamish about the sight of blood should carefully consider whether the clinical demands of a surgical career are genuinely compatible with their temperamental disposition, as exposure to graphic medical procedures is unavoidable and continuous throughout professional training and practice.","t":"準醫學生被告知，那些對血腥場面特別敏感的人應仔細考慮外科職業的臨床要求是否真正與他們的性情相容，因為在整個職業培訓和實踐中，接觸圖形醫療程序是不可避免的和持續的。","as":"Squeamish viewers may wish to avert their eyes during the documentary's surgical scenes, which show doctors suturing a deep laceration, though the filmmakers insist such candor is essential to convey the relentless drudgery and stress that afflict emergency-room staff.","at":"容易感到噁心的觀眾在這部紀錄片的手術片段時或許會想移開視線，因為畫面呈現醫生縫合一道深長的撕裂傷；不過製作團隊堅持，如此坦率的呈現對於傳達急診室人員所承受的無盡辛勞與壓力是必要的。"},{"w":"symptomatic","p":"adj.","d":"Indicative of something deeper.","c":"有症狀的；象徵性的","s":"Many social commentators argued that the incident was symptomatic of a deeper cultural shift in how younger generations related to institutional authority, and that attempting to address the surface manifestation without understanding and responding to the underlying attitudinal changes would produce only temporary amelioration rather than genuine resolution.","t":"許多社會評論員認為，這一事件是更深層文化轉變的象徵，反映了年輕一代如何與機構權威相處，而不理解和回應潛在的態度變化而試圖解決表面表現，只會產生暫時的改善而非真正的解決。","as":"Economists contend that the way household debt continues to surge is symptomatic of deeper structural problems, such as stagnant wages and an inexorable rise in housing costs fueled by rampant speculation, rather than mere consumer extravagance.","at":"經濟學家主張，家庭債務持續急遽攀升，反映的是更深層的結構性問題，例如薪資停滯，以及猖獗的投機炒作所推動、無法遏止的房價上漲，而不只是消費者揮霍無度。"},{"w":"wan","p":"adj.","d":"Sickly pale, lacking colour or vitality.","c":"蒼白的；無精打采的","s":"The patient's wan complexion and evident physical weakness when she arrived at the outpatient clinic were consistent with the haematological findings that subsequently confirmed a diagnosis of severe anaemia, the condition having gone undetected and untreated for an estimated period of between eight and twelve months.","t":"患者到達門診時蒼白的膚色和明顯的體力虛弱與隨後確認嚴重貧血診斷的血液學發現一致，這種情況在估計八到十二個月的時間內一直未被發現和治療。","as":"After a month battling a virulent infection, the patient looked wan and frail, yet she greeted her visitors with a tremulous smile, assuring them that the worst of her malady had passed.","at":"與一場猛烈的感染搏鬥了一個月之後，病人看起來蒼白而虛弱，但她仍帶著微微顫抖的笑容迎接訪客，向他們保證病情最糟的階段已經過去了。"}]},{"unit":11,"cards":[{"w":"poignant","p":"adj.","d":"Moving, painful to the feelings.","c":"辛酸的；感人的","s":"The documentary's most poignant moment came when the elderly veteran returned to the beach where he had lost his closest friends seventy years earlier, kneeling silently in the sand while his children and grandchildren stood respectfully behind him in the fading afternoon light.","t":"這部紀錄片最感人的時刻，是當這位老兵七十年後重返他失去最親密戰友的那片海灘，在夕陽餘暉中默默跪在沙地上，而他的子孫們恭敬地站在他身後。","as":"The documentary's most poignant scene, in which an indigent widow peruses the faded letters her husband wrote from the front, moved even viewers who usually disdain sentimental films to tears.","at":"這部紀錄片最感人的一幕，是一位貧困的寡婦細細閱讀丈夫從前線寄回、早已褪色的信件，連平常不屑煽情電影的觀眾都為之落淚。"},{"w":"inundate","p":"v.","d":"To flood, overwhelm with a great quantity.","c":"淹沒；泛濫","s":"The customer service department was completely inundate with complaints following the nationwide product recall, receiving more than forty thousand calls and emails within the first twenty-four hours — a volume that exceeded its entire previous month's combined contact total.","t":"客戶服務部門在全國性產品召回後被投訴淹沒，在最初二十四小時內收到超過四萬通電話和電子郵件，這一數量超過了上個月的全部聯繫總量。","as":"After the newspaper exposed the mayor's duplicity, its editors were inundated with irate letters, a surge of correspondence so large that a small team had to scrutinize each one for pertinent tips.","at":"報社揭發市長的兩面手法後，編輯們被大量憤怒的來信淹沒；信件激增到必須由一個小組逐封仔細審閱，從中找出相關的線索。"},{"w":"fruitless","p":"adj.","d":"Producing no result, useless.","c":"徒勞的；無結果的","s":"After three years of fruitless negotiations during which neither party demonstrated any willingness to make the fundamental concessions necessary for a settlement, the international mediators reluctantly concluded that the diplomatic process had reached an impasse that required a fundamentally different approach.","t":"經過三年徒勞的談判，雙方都沒有表現出達成協議所必需的根本性讓步意願，國際調解員不情願地得出結論，外交進程已陷入僵局，需要採取根本上不同的方法。","as":"Despite years of fruitless negotiations, the two rival factions refused to desist from their acrimonious skirmishes, and mediators eventually conceded that no compromise was likely while each side remained implacable.","at":"儘管多年來的談判毫無成果，兩個敵對派系仍不肯停止尖刻激烈的小規模衝突；調停者最終承認，只要雙方都毫不讓步，就不太可能達成任何妥協。"},{"w":"garbled","p":"adj.","d":"Confused, mixed up, distorted.","c":"混淆的；含糊不清的","s":"The rescue coordinator received a garbled message from the stranded hikers whose satellite communicator was failing — the transmission cut in and out repeatedly, conveying only fragments of their location coordinates and none of the critical information about injuries that would determine the appropriate response.","t":"救援協調員收到了一條來自受困徒步者的混淆信息，他們的衛星通訊器正在故障——傳輸反覆中斷，只傳達了他們位置坐標的片段，而沒有傳達確定適當回應所需的關於傷情的關鍵信息。","as":"Because the radio transmission from the hapless expedition arrived so garbled, rescuers could discern only a few words amid the static, forcing them to construe the explorers' location from a paucity of clues.","at":"由於那支不幸的探險隊傳來的無線電訊號嚴重失真，救難人員只能在雜訊中辨認出幾個字，被迫憑著極少的線索來推斷探險者的位置。"},{"w":"sanguine","p":"adj.","d":"Optimistic, confidently hopeful.","c":"樂觀的；充滿希望的","s":"Despite the preliminary results suggesting considerable challenges ahead, the research director remained remarkably sanguine about the project's ultimate prospects, citing three previous instances where similarly discouraging early data had preceded breakthrough discoveries that transformed the entire field.","t":"儘管初步結果顯示前方有相當大的挑戰，研究主任對項目的最終前景仍然非常樂觀，引用了三個先前的例子，在這些例子中，類似令人沮喪的早期數據之後出現了改變整個領域的突破性發現。","as":"Although some economists remained sanguine about the nation's recovery, pointing to tangible gains in exports, others warned that rampant inflation and a shortage of skilled workers could stymie growth for years.","at":"雖然部分經濟學家指出出口已有實際成長，對國家的復甦仍感樂觀，但也有人警告，猖獗的通貨膨脹與技術人力短缺可能會讓經濟成長停滯多年。"},{"w":"phlegmatic","p":"adj.","d":"Calm, hard to rouse to action.","c":"冷靜的；遲鈍的","s":"The veteran emergency room physician maintained a characteristically phlegmaticedemeanour throughout the chaotic multi-casualty incident, his measured instructions and unhurried movements projecting a confidence that visibly steadied the less experienced nurses and paramedics working around him.","t":"這位資深急診室醫生在混亂的多傷亡事故中保持了一貫冷靜的態度，他有條不紊的指示和不慌不忙的動作展現出一種自信，明顯穩定了在他周圍工作的經驗較少的護士和急救人員。","as":"The phlegmatic captain remained composed even as turbulent waves battered the ship during the storm, issuing orders in a calm, measured voice that helped quell the frenzy spreading among the distraught passengers below deck.","at":"暴風雨中，即使洶湧的海浪不斷拍打船身，那位沉著冷靜的船長依然泰然自若，以平穩從容的語氣下達命令，平息了在甲板下心煩意亂的乘客之間蔓延的恐慌。"},{"w":"corroborate","p":"v.","d":"To confirm or support with evidence.","c":"證實；確證","s":"Three independent witnesses were able to corroborate the defendant's account of his whereabouts on the evening in question, each recalling specific details that were consistent with his testimony and impossible to have fabricated without advance knowledge of the events being investigated.","t":"三名獨立證人能夠證實被告關於當晚所在地的陳述，每人都回憶起與他的證詞一致的具體細節，而這些細節若非事先了解所調查的事件是無法捏造的。","as":"Archaeologists were thrilled when newly unearthed tablets corroborated the annals of an ancient dynasty, since historians had long been dubious about whether the chronicles' accounts of an affluent capital were anything more than royal propaganda.","at":"新出土的泥板證實了一個古代王朝的史冊記載，令考古學家振奮不已；因為長久以來，歷史學家一直懷疑編年史中關於富裕都城的描述，是否只是王室的宣傳而已。"},{"w":"comprehensive","p":"adj.","d":"Thorough, covering all aspects.","c":"廣泛的；綜合的","s":"The government commissioned a comprehensive review of the nation's infrastructure, examining roads, bridges, rail networks, energy grids, and digital communications systems simultaneously over eighteen months — the most ambitious assessment of its kind in the country's history.","t":"政府委託對全國基礎設施進行全面審查，在十八個月內同時審查道路、橋樑、鐵路網絡、能源網絡和數字通信系統——這是該國歷史上同類評估中最雄心勃勃的一次。","as":"The commission's comprehensive report did more than name a single culprit for the bridge's collapse; it examined every salient factor, from perfunctory inspections to outdated design codes, that had exacerbated the structure's decline.","at":"調查委員會的全面報告不只是為橋梁倒塌找出單一禍首，更檢視了每一個關鍵因素，從敷衍了事的檢查到過時的設計規範，這些都加劇了結構的劣化。"},{"w":"zealous","p":"adj.","d":"Fervently enthusiastic, intensely devoted.","c":"熱心的；狂熱的","s":"The newly appointed compliance officer was so zealous in his enforcement of internal procedures that he managed to create significant operational disruption within his first month, flagging as violations several long-established informal practices that had actually improved efficiency without contravening any genuine regulatory requirement.","t":"這位新任命的合規官員在執行內部程序方面如此狂熱，以至於在第一個月內就造成了重大的運營干擾，他將幾種長期建立的非正式做法標記為違規，而這些做法實際上提高了效率，並沒有違反任何真正的監管要求。","as":"Zealous advocates of renewable energy implored lawmakers to terminate subsidies for coal-fired power plants, arguing that the pernicious effects of air pollution on public health could no longer be tolerated by any responsible government.","at":"熱情投入的再生能源倡議者懇求立法者終止對燃煤電廠的補貼，他們主張，任何負責任的政府都不能再容忍空氣污染對公共健康造成的有害影響。"},{"w":"coerce","p":"v.","d":"To force or compel by pressure.","c":"強制；脅迫","s":"The labour tribunal found that the company had systematically attempted to coerce employees into signing away their contractual redundancy rights by threatening that those who refused to accept the new terms voluntarily would be placed at the top of any future redundancy selection list.","t":"勞動法庭發現，公司曾系統地試圖通過威脅那些拒絕自願接受新條款的人將被列在任何未來裁員選擇名單的首位，來強迫員工放棄其合同裁員權利。","as":"Investigators found that the syndicate had used extortion and veiled threats to coerce local merchants into paying for protection, a nefarious scheme that flourished because its leaders operated with seeming impunity.","at":"調查人員發現，該犯罪集團以勒索和隱晦的威脅脅迫當地商家繳交保護費；這個邪惡的勾當之所以猖獗，是因為其首腦似乎可以為所欲為而不受懲罰。"},{"w":"elapse","p":"v.","d":"To slip by, pass (of time).","c":"(時間)流逝","s":"Three entire decades had elapse between the commission of the crime and the eventual arrest of the perpetrator, a span of time during which forensic science had advanced sufficiently to extract DNA evidence from materials that had been stored in an evidence locker since the original investigation.","t":"從犯罪到最終逮捕犯罪者之間已經過去了整整三十年，在這段時間裡，法證科學已經進步到足以從自最初調查以來一直存放在證物箱中的材料中提取DNA證據。","as":"By the time several centuries had elapsed, the once monolithic empire had fractured into rival kingdoms, and the grand temples that had served as sanctuaries for pilgrims lay in ruins, their origins elusive even to scholars.","at":"數百年過去之後，這個曾經堅若磐石的帝國已分裂成互相敵對的王國，昔日作為朝聖者庇護所的宏偉神殿也淪為廢墟，連學者都難以考證其起源。"},{"w":"meticulous","p":"adj.","d":"Taking extreme care over details.","c":"一絲不苟的；細心的","s":"The restorer's approach to the damaged painting was painstakingly meticulous, spending fourteen months on a canvas that measured less than half a square metre — documenting every brushstroke under magnification before cleaning, consolidating, and inpainting each damaged area with absolute fidelity to the original.","t":"修復者對這幅受損畫作的處理方式一絲不苟，在一幅不到半平方米的畫布上花了十四個月——在清潔、鞏固和修補每個受損區域之前，在放大鏡下記錄每一筆觸，對原作保持絕對忠實。","as":"The meticulous conservator spent months cleaning the fresco with a scalpel and cotton swabs, careful to avoid any inadvertent damage to the fragile plaster, a painstaking approach that colleagues considered laudable after earlier hasty restorations had become fiascoes.","at":"這位一絲不苟的修復師花了好幾個月，用手術刀和棉花棒清理壁畫，小心避免對脆弱的灰泥造成任何無意的損傷；由於先前草率的修復曾以慘敗收場，同事們都認為她這種費心費力的做法值得讚揚。"},{"w":"domicile","p":"n.","d":"A place of permanent residence.","c":"住所；住宅","s":"For tax purposes, the court was required to determine the billionaire's legal domicile, a question complicated by the fact that he maintained properties in seven countries, spent no more than ninety days per year in any single nation, and had structured his financial affairs specifically to obscure his primary place of residence.","t":"出於稅務目的，法院需要確定這位億萬富翁的法定住所，這個問題因他在七個國家擁有房產、每年在任何單一國家停留不超過九十天、並專門構建了他的財務事務以掩蓋其主要居住地而變得複雜。","as":"Although the reticent author's official domicile was a modest abode in the countryside, she spent most of each year traveling, which made it hard for the tax authorities with jurisdiction over her income to determine where she actually lived.","at":"這位沉默寡言的作家，正式住所是鄉間一棟樸素的房子，但她每年大部分時間都在旅行，使得對她的收入有管轄權的稅務機關難以判定她實際居住在哪裡。"},{"w":"lax","p":"adj.","d":"Careless, not strict or firm.","c":"鬆懈的；馬虎的","s":"The food safety investigation concluded that the contamination outbreak had resulted directly from lax enforcement of hygiene protocols at the processing facility, where supervisors had routinely overlooked violations that should have triggered immediate corrective action and temporary production shutdown.","t":"食品安全調查得出結論，污染爆發直接源於加工設施衛生規程執行的鬆懈，在那裡，主管們習慣性地忽視本應立即觸發糾正措施和臨時停產的違規行為。","as":"Critics charged that lax enforcement of safety regulations had allowed the factory to flout environmental laws for years, a negligence that became flagrant when toxic waste was found spewing into the river.","at":"批評者指控，安全法規執行鬆散，讓這家工廠多年來得以公然藐視環保法令；當有毒廢水被發現直接噴湧排入河中時，這種疏失便昭然若揭。"},{"w":"sporadic","p":"adj.","d":"Occurring occasionally, scattered.","c":"偶爾的；零星的","s":"The archaeologists recorded sporadic evidence of human habitation at the site spanning nearly four thousand years, but the gaps between occupation periods were far longer than the periods of settlement, suggesting that the valley had been used as a seasonal camp rather than a permanent community throughout most of its history.","t":"考古學家記錄了該遺址跨越近四千年的零星人類居住證據，但佔領期之間的間隔遠長於定居期，這表明在其大部分歷史中，這個山谷被用作季節性營地而非永久社區。","as":"Although the treaty brought an uneasy respite from war, sporadic outbreaks of violence continued in the border villages, an ominous sign to diplomats who feared the fragile peace might soon revert to open conflict.","at":"儘管條約帶來了短暫而不安的停戰喘息，邊境村落仍零星爆發暴力事件；這對外交官而言是不祥的徵兆，他們擔心脆弱的和平可能很快又回到公開衝突的局面。"},{"w":"rash","p":"adj.","d":"Too hasty, reckless, impetuous.","c":"魯莽的；輕率的","s":"The board concluded that the chief executive's rashedecision to acquire the struggling competitor without adequate due diligence had exposed the company to liabilities that would take at least five years to unwind, and that the absence of proper consultation with the audit committee represented a serious governance failure.","t":"董事會得出結論，首席執行官在沒有充分盡職調查的情況下收購陷入困境的競爭對手的魯莽決定，使公司面臨至少需要五年才能解決的負債，而沒有與審計委員會進行適當協商代表著嚴重的治理失敗。","as":"The young general's rash decision to besiege the mountain fortress without waiting for reinforcements proved disastrous, as his exhausted troops soon succumbed to disease and privation in the harsh winter that followed.","at":"年輕將軍魯莽地決定不等援軍就圍攻山上的要塞，結果釀成災難：他疲憊不堪的部隊在隨之而來的嚴冬中，很快就不敵疾病與物資匱乏而倒下。"},{"w":"conjecture","p":"n.","d":"A guess or inference without proof.","c":"推測；猜測","s":"The historian was careful to distinguish throughout her analysis between conclusions supported by documentary evidence and those that remained conjecture, acknowledging honestly that the absence of surviving primary sources from the relevant period made definitive claims about the ruler's motivations impossible to substantiate.","t":"這位歷史學家在整個分析過程中小心地區分了有文獻證據支持的結論和那些仍然是推測的結論，誠實地承認，相關時期缺乏現存的原始資料使得對統治者動機的確定性陳述無法得到證實。","as":"Because the ancient manuscript was found without a title page or signature, the identity of its author remains a matter of conjecture, though astute scholars have noted that its verbose style and caustic wit resemble those of a famous satirist.","at":"由於這份古代手稿被發現時既無扉頁也無署名，作者身分至今仍只能推測；不過敏銳的學者指出，其冗長的文風與尖刻的機智，與一位著名的諷刺作家十分相似。"},{"w":"obviate","p":"v.","d":"To do away with or eliminate a difficulty.","c":"消除；排除","s":"The installation of automated temperature monitoring systems throughout the storage facility would effectively obviate the need for the costly overnight security patrols that had previously been required to check conditions manually at two-hourly intervals throughout each twelve-hour shift.","t":"在整個儲存設施安裝自動溫度監測系統將有效消除對昂貴的隔夜安全巡邏的需求，這些巡邏以前需要在每個十二小時班次中每隔兩小時手動檢查一次條件。","as":"The engineers argued that installing automated sensors along the pipeline would obviate the need for manual inspections, sparing vigilant workers the drudgery of walking miles of rugged terrain in inclement weather.","at":"工程師主張，沿著管線裝設自動感測器便可免除人工巡檢的必要，讓警覺的工人不必再在惡劣天候中徒步走過數英里崎嶇地形，從事這種枯燥乏味的苦差事。"},{"w":"lurid","p":"adj.","d":"Sensational, shocking, ghastly.","c":"駭人聽聞的；耀眼的","s":"The tabloid's lurid coverage of the criminal trial — featuring graphic descriptions of the evidence, speculative accounts of the defendant's private life, and photographs of the crime scene published without the victims' families' consent — prompted the judge to issue a formal warning about prejudicial reporting.","t":"小報對刑事審判的聳人聽聞報道——包括對證據的生動描述、對被告私生活的推測性陳述，以及未經受害者家屬同意發布的犯罪現場照片——促使法官發出關於帶有偏見報道的正式警告。","as":"The tabloid's lurid account of the murder, replete with gruesome details and sensational headlines, provoked consternation among readers who felt that such sordid coverage profited from the victims' grief for profit.","at":"這份小報對謀殺案駭人聽聞的報導，充斥著血腥細節與聳動標題，引起讀者驚愕；他們認為這種卑劣的報導是在利用受害者家屬的悲痛來牟利。"},{"w":"quip","p":"v.","d":"To say something clever or amusing.","c":"嘲弄；說俏皮話","s":"The prime minister was renowned for his ability to quip under pressure, deflecting the most aggressive parliamentary questions with a perfectly timed observation that simultaneously entertained the chamber, undermined the questioner's premise, and left journalists struggling to frame a follow-up.","t":"首相以其在壓力下說俏皮話的能力而聞名，用一個時機完美的觀察偏轉了最具攻擊性的議會問題，同時娛樂了議院，削弱了提問者的前提，並讓記者難以擬定後續問題。","as":"When an avid young interviewer asked whether she would ever retire, the octogenarian novelist would quip that writing was the only vice her doctors had not yet forbidden, a witty answer proving that her mind was anything but inert.","at":"每當熱切的年輕訪問者問她是否打算退休，這位八十多歲的小說家總會俏皮地回答，寫作是醫生唯一還沒禁止她的嗜好；這句妙語證明她的頭腦一點也不遲鈍。"}]},{"unit":12,"cards":[{"w":"diatribe","p":"n.","d":"A bitter verbal attack or criticism.","c":"抨擊；誹謗","s":"The senator's forty-minute diatribe against the proposed trade agreement — delivered with increasing intensity to a nearly empty chamber at eleven o'clock on a Tuesday evening — was less intended to persuade colleagues than to create a recorded statement for distribution to his domestic constituency.","t":"參議員對擬議貿易協定的四十分鐘抨擊——在周二晚上十一點向幾乎空無一人的議院以越來越強烈的語氣發表——與其說是為了說服同僚，不如說是為了創建一份向其國內選區分發的書面聲明。","as":"The senator's televised diatribe against journalists, laced with scurrilous accusations and personal insults, failed to win over his opponents and instead seemed to corroborate their claim that he was too belligerent to tolerate legitimate criticism.","at":"這位參議員在電視上對記者發表的猛烈抨擊，夾雜著惡毒的指控與人身攻擊，非但沒有爭取到對手的支持，反而似乎證實了他們的說法：他好鬥成性，容不下正當的批評。"},{"w":"inhibition","p":"n.","d":"A restraint on behaviour or impulse.","c":"抑制；禁忌","s":"The clinical psychologist explained that the patient's social inhibition stemmed not from shyness in the conventional sense but from a deeply rooted fear of negative evaluation that had developed during childhood and which standard cognitive behavioural techniques had thus far proved insufficient to address.","t":"臨床心理學家解釋說，患者的社交抑制不是來自傳統意義上的害羞，而是源於兒童時期形成的對負面評價的根深蒂固的恐懼，而標準認知行為技術迄今已被證明不足以解決這個問題。","as":"Drama coaches often use improvisation games to help shy students overcome their inhibition, encouraging them to gesticulate freely, interject improvised lines, and embrace the bold histrionics that the stage so often demands.","at":"戲劇教練常用即興遊戲幫助害羞的學生克服心理上的拘束，鼓勵他們盡情比手畫腳、隨興插入臺詞，並勇於展現舞臺上經常需要的誇張表演。"},{"w":"fortuitous","p":"adj.","d":"Lucky, happening by fortunate chance.","c":"偶然的；幸運的","s":"The discovery of the manuscript was entirely fortuitous — a researcher investigating a completely unrelated fifteenth-century land dispute happened to notice a familiar handwriting style in a bundle of documents that had been misfiled under an incorrect catalogue number for nearly three centuries.","t":"手稿的發現完全是偶然的——一位調查完全不相關的十五世紀土地糾紛的研究人員碰巧在一捆近三個世紀以來被錯誤歸入錯誤目錄號的文件中注意到了熟悉的筆跡風格。","as":"The discovery of penicillin was famously fortuitous: Alexander Fleming noticed that mold had contaminated a culture dish he had left out, and the astute scientist perceived that this inadvertent mishap had produced a substance that killed the surrounding bacteria.","at":"青黴素的發現是出了名的幸運巧合：弗萊明注意到一個被他擱置的培養皿遭黴菌污染，這位敏銳的科學家察覺到，這個無心的意外竟產生了一種能殺死周圍細菌的物質。"},{"w":"incoherent","p":"adj.","d":"Unable to speak clearly, disjointed.","c":"語無倫次的；不連貫的","s":"The witness's testimony was so incoherent that the judge was forced to adjourn proceedings twice during the afternoon session, noting that the combination of the elderly woman's evident distress and the complexity of the events she was attempting to describe made it impossible for the court to establish a reliable chronology.","t":"證人的證詞如此語無倫次，以至於法官在下午的庭審中被迫兩次休庭，指出這位老婦人明顯的痛苦與她試圖描述的事件的複雜性相結合，使法院無法建立可靠的時間順序。","as":"Suffering from a high fever and severe dehydration, the emaciated hiker was nearly incoherent when rescuers found him, mumbling garbled phrases that offered few pertinent clues about where his missing companions might be.","at":"這名骨瘦如柴的登山客發著高燒且嚴重脫水，被救難人員找到時幾乎語無倫次，只能喃喃說出含糊不清的字句，幾乎提供不了任何關於失蹤同伴下落的相關線索。"},{"w":"ilk","p":"n.","d":"A type, kind, or sort.","c":"種類；同類","s":"The venture capitalist expressed his particular disdain for entrepreneurs of that ilk — those who arrived at funding meetings with polished presentations and rehearsed answers but demonstrated, under any substantive questioning, a fundamental ignorance of the market they claimed to be disrupting.","t":"這位風險資本家表達了他對那種類型的企業家的特別蔑視——那些帶著精心設計的演示文稿和排練好的答案出現在融資會議上，但在任何實質性問題下都表現出對他們聲稱要顛覆的市場的根本性無知的人。","as":"The eminent critic had little patience for celebrity memoirs and other books of that ilk, which she disparaged as mundane exercises in self-promotion rather than literature worthy of serious attention from thoughtful readers.","at":"這位知名評論家對名人回憶錄以及同類書籍毫無耐心，她貶斥這些書只是平庸的自我宣傳，而非值得有思想的讀者認真看待的文學作品。"},{"w":"prestigious","p":"adj.","d":"Having a high reputation, respected.","c":"享有聲望的","s":"Admission to the prestigious research fellowship was more competitive than entry to the country's most selective universities, with fewer than twelve candidates selected annually from a global pool of applicants that typically exceeded three thousand in any given year.","t":"獲得這一享有聲望的研究獎學金的競爭比進入該國最嚴格的大學更為激烈，每年從通常超過三千名申請者的全球候選人中選出不到十二名候選人。","as":"Each year thousands of aspirants apply to the prestigious conservatory, but only a handful are admitted, so even the most avid young musicians must endure months of grueling auditions, and many succumb to the pressure before the final round.","at":"每年都有數千名有志者報考這所享有盛名的音樂學院，但只有寥寥數人獲得錄取；因此，即使是最熱衷的年輕音樂家，也得熬過數個月艱苦的試奏，許多人在決選前就承受不住壓力而放棄。"},{"w":"placard","p":"n.","d":"A notice or sign for public display.","c":"海報；標語牌","s":"The striking workers assembled outside the factory gates carrying placard s bearing slogans that had been professionally printed overnight, a level of organisational sophistication that suggested the labour action had been planned considerably more carefully than the management's public statements implied.","t":"罷工工人聚集在工廠大門外，手持印有口號的標語牌，這些標語牌是連夜專業印製的，這種組織複雜程度表明，勞動行動的計劃比管理層的公開聲明所暗示的要謹慎得多。","as":"A throng of demonstrators marched toward the capitol carrying placards that denounced the government's egregious corruption, while police officers stood vigilant along the route in case the peaceful rally turned turbulent.","at":"一大群示威者手持譴責政府嚴重貪腐的標語牌，朝議會大廈遊行前進；警察則沿途保持警戒，以防這場和平集會演變成騷亂。"},{"w":"integral","p":"adj.","d":"Essential, forming a necessary part.","c":"不可或缺的；整體的","s":"Community consultation has been integral to the urban planning process since the city revised its development charter fifteen years ago, with no significant project now able to proceed to the planning permission stage without documented evidence of meaningful engagement with the affected residential and commercial populations.","t":"自城市十五年前修訂其發展章程以來，社區諮詢一直是城市規劃過程不可或缺的組成部分，現在沒有任何重大項目能夠在沒有與受影響的住宅和商業人口進行有意義接觸的文件記錄的情況下進入規劃許可階段。","as":"Cooperation among rival nations is integral to any feasible plan for combating climate change, since no single country, however powerful, can thwart the adverse effects of rising global temperatures on its own.","at":"敵對國家之間的合作，是任何可行的氣候變遷因應計畫中不可或缺的一環，因為沒有任何一個國家，無論多麼強大，能夠單憑一己之力阻擋全球升溫帶來的不利影響。"},{"w":"remuneration","p":"n.","d":"Payment or compensation for work.","c":"報酬；酬勞","s":"The independent review of executive remuneration at publicly listed companies found a systematic disconnection between pay and performance, with chief executive salaries having increased by an average of three hundred and forty percent over the previous two decades while median employee wages had grown by less than twelve percent in real terms.","t":"對上市公司高管薪酬的獨立審查發現薪酬與業績之間存在系統性脫節，首席執行官薪酬在過去二十年間平均增長了三百四十個百分點，而員工中位數工資的實際增長不到百分之十二。","as":"Union leaders argued that the low remuneration offered to farm workers, who toiled for long hours in excruciating heat, was a flagrant injustice that left many families mired in privation despite their tireless labor.","at":"工會領袖主張，農場工人在酷熱難耐的天氣下長時間辛苦勞動，所得報酬卻如此微薄，這是明目張膽的不公不義，讓許多家庭儘管不辭辛勞，仍深陷貧困之中。"},{"w":"nominal","p":"adj.","d":"In name only, very small.","c":"名義上的；微不足道的","s":"The rent charged for the community arts space was deliberately kept at a nominal level — equivalent to approximately two percent of the prevailing market rate — to ensure that the building's cultural programming could continue without the financial pressures that had forced the closure of similar venues across the city.","t":"社區藝術空間收取的租金被故意保持在象徵性的水平——相當於現行市場利率的約百分之二——以確保建築的文化節目可以繼續進行，而不必承受迫使城市各地類似場所關閉的財務壓力。","as":"Although the elderly monarch remained the nominal head of state, real power had long since been wrested from him by a circle of affluent merchants, whose duplicity he was too feeble to discern.","at":"雖然年邁的君主仍是名義上的國家元首，但實權早已被一群富商奪走，而他年老體衰，根本無法察覺這些人的口是心非。"},{"w":"expunge","p":"v.","d":"To erase or remove completely.","c":"抹去；刪除","s":"The court granted the petition to expunge the conviction from his criminal record on the grounds that he had been seventeen years old at the time of the offence, had completed all required community service without incident, and had maintained an unblemished record in the eighteen years since the original sentencing.","t":"法院批准了從其犯罪記錄中刪除定罪的申請，理由是他犯罪時年僅十七歲，無事故地完成了所有要求的社區服務，並且在原始判決後的十八年裡保持了無可指責的記錄。","as":"After DNA evidence corroborated his alibi, the wrongly convicted man petitioned to have his criminal record expunged so that the stigma of being labeled a felon would no longer stymie his efforts to find steady work.","at":"在DNA證據證實他的不在場證明後，這名遭冤判的男子申請將犯罪紀錄完全刪除，好讓「重罪犯」的污名不再阻礙他尋找穩定工作。"},{"w":"flamboyant","p":"adj.","d":"Showy, extravagant, colourful.","c":"艷麗的；炫耀的","s":"The architect's flamboyantedesign for the new cultural centre — featuring a roof structure modelled on breaking ocean waves rendered in iridescent titanium panels — divided critics sharply between those who celebrated it as an inspired response to the city's maritime heritage and those who condemned it as expensive self-indulgence.","t":"建築師為新文化中心設計的炫麗方案——以虹彩鈦板呈現的仿衝浪浪形屋頂結構為特色——讓批評者截然分開，一方讚揚它是對城市海洋遺產的有靈感的回應，另一方則譴責它是昂貴的自我放縱。","as":"The flamboyant pianist, famous for his sequined costumes and candelabra-topped piano, was often derided by critics as a mere showman, yet his performances were anything but lackluster, and his loyal fans scoffed at such snobbery.","at":"這位浮誇華麗的鋼琴家以綴滿亮片的服裝和擺著燭臺的鋼琴聞名，常被評論家嘲笑只是個表演者；然而他的演出絕不乏味，忠實樂迷對這種勢利的批評也嗤之以鼻。"},{"w":"anathema","p":"n.","d":"Something greatly detested or loathed.","c":"令人厭惡的事物；詛咒","s":"Any suggestion of compromising on press freedom was complete anathema to the editorial board, whose founding charter specifically identified journalistic independence from governmental and commercial influence as the single non-negotiable principle that distinguished the publication from its competitors.","t":"任何妥協新聞自由的建議對編委會來說都是完全令人厭惡的，其創始章程特別將新聞獨立於政府和商業影響力作為使出版物區別於競爭對手的唯一不可談判的原則。","as":"For the pious monks, any display of worldly luxury was anathema, so they eschewed fine clothing, ate only rudimentary meals, and regarded the pursuit of wealth as a pernicious distraction from prayer and contemplation.","at":"對虔誠的僧侶而言，任何世俗奢華的展現都令人深惡痛絕；因此他們避穿華服，只吃最簡單的餐食，並將追求財富視為妨礙祈禱與冥想的有害干擾。"},{"w":"schism","p":"n.","d":"A division or split within a group.","c":"分裂；派系","s":"The theological schism that developed within the congregation over the proposed modernisation of the Sunday liturgy proved impossible to heal through mediation, ultimately resulting in a formal separation that divided the original community of four hundred families into two smaller but internally unified groups.","t":"由於擬議的週日禮儀現代化而在會眾中發展起來的神學分裂被證明無法通過調解來癒合，最終導致了正式的分離，將四百個家庭的原始社區分成兩個較小但內部統一的群體。","as":"The acrimonious dispute over doctrine eventually produced a schism within the denomination, as reformers repudiated the authority of the elders and founded rival congregations that openly castigated their former leaders as corrupt.","at":"這場關於教義的激烈爭論最終導致教派分裂：改革派否認長老的權威，另立互相抗衡的會眾團體，並公開嚴厲譴責他們先前的領袖腐敗。"},{"w":"utopia","p":"n.","d":"An imagined place of perfection.","c":"烏托邦；理想國","s":"The founding documents of the cooperative movement reveal a genuine belief among its nineteenth-century architects that worker-owned enterprises represented not merely a pragmatic economic alternative but the first step toward a genuine social utopia in which exploitation would be structurally impossible.","t":"合作社運動的創始文件揭示了其十九世紀設計者之間的真正信念，即工人擁有的企業不僅代表了一種務實的經濟替代方案，而且是走向真正社會烏托邦的第一步，在那裡剝削在結構上是不可能的。","as":"Many nineteenth-century reformers founded rural communes in hopes of building a utopia free of greed and poverty, but their sanguine visions soon faded as members found the drudgery of farm work and constant quarrels over money hard to tolerate.","at":"許多十九世紀的改革者創立鄉村公社，希望打造一個沒有貪婪與貧窮的烏托邦；但當成員們發現農務的苦差事和永無止境的金錢爭執令人難以忍受時，他們樂觀的願景很快便破滅了。"},{"w":"timorous","p":"adj.","d":"Fearful, easily frightened.","c":"膽怯的；怯懦的","s":"The timorous junior associate's reluctance to question the senior partner's legal strategy — even when she had identified a significant procedural error — ultimately proved costly, as the oversight was not discovered until after the filing deadline had passed and the defect could no longer be remedied.","t":"這位膽怯的初級律師不願質疑高級合夥人的法律策略——即使她已經發現了一個重大程序錯誤——最終被證明是昂貴的，因為這一疏忽直到提交截止日期過後才被發現，缺陷再也無法補救。","as":"The timorous deer recoiled at the faintest rustle in the underbrush and bolted into the forest whenever a hiker ventured near, so vigilant wildlife photographers had to stay motionless for hours to capture even an elusive glimpse of it.","at":"這頭膽小的鹿只要聽見矮樹叢中最輕微的窸窣聲就會退縮，一有登山客靠近便竄入林中；因此警覺的野生動物攝影師得一動不動地守候好幾個小時，才能捕捉到牠難得一見的身影。"},{"w":"truncated","p":"adj.","d":"Shortened, cut off abruptly.","c":"截短的；縮短的","s":"The truncated version of the report released to the public omitted the three chapters containing the most damaging findings about regulatory failures, a selective disclosure that the opposition parties immediately condemned as a deliberate attempt to manage the political fallout before the full document could be independently analysed.","t":"發布給公眾的報告截短版本省略了包含關於監管失敗最具破壞性發現的三個章節，反對黨立即譴責這種選擇性披露是在完整文件能夠被獨立分析之前故意管理政治影響的企圖。","as":"Because the network aired only a truncated version of the interview, the scientist's careful explanation of the study's nuances was lost, and viewers were left with a misleading sound bite that pundits soon began to construe as support for dubious health claims.","at":"由於電視臺只播出經過刪減的訪談版本，科學家對研究細微之處的仔細說明全數遺漏，觀眾只看到一段誤導性的片段，評論員隨即將其解讀為支持可疑健康說法的證據。"},{"w":"jaunty","p":"adj.","d":"Lively, cheerful, self-confident.","c":"輕鬆活潑的","s":"The returning expedition members emerged from the airport arrivals hall with a jaunty air that belied the extreme physical hardships they had endured during three months in one of the world's most hostile environments, their evident high spirits a testament to both the success of their mission and their remarkable resilience.","t":"返回的探險隊員帶著輕鬆活潑的神態走出機場入境大廳，掩蓋了他們在世界上最惡劣環境之一待了三個月所經歷的極端身體艱辛，他們明顯的高昂士氣既是他們任務成功的見證，也是他們非凡韌性的見證。","as":"Whistling a jaunty tune as he pushed his cart, the elderly street vendor greeted every customer with a joke, and his cheerful manner offered solace and a brief respite to neighbors still distraught after the flood.","at":"年邁的街頭小販推著攤車，一邊吹著輕快的口哨，一邊用笑話招呼每位客人；他開朗的態度為洪災過後仍心神不寧的鄰居帶來慰藉，也讓他們得以暫時喘口氣。"},{"w":"fractious","p":"adj.","d":"Quarrelsome, easily irritated.","c":"易怒的；好爭吵的","s":"Managing the fractious coalition government required extraordinary diplomatic skill, as the three constituent parties held fundamentally incompatible positions on at least seven of the twelve major policy areas included in the governing agreement, necessitating constant negotiation to prevent minor disputes from escalating into constitutional crises.","t":"管理這個容易爭吵的聯合政府需要非凡的外交技巧，因為三個組成政黨在執政協議所包含的十二個主要政策領域中至少七個上持有根本上不相容的立場，需要不斷談判以防止小爭端升級為憲法危機。","as":"The fractious coalition, whose members bickered over nearly every bill, proved so ineffectual that even its own supporters grew weary of the vexatious infighting that frustrated every attempt at meaningful reform.","at":"這個爭吵不休的執政聯盟，成員幾乎對每項法案都意見相左，施政毫無成效，連自己的支持者都對那些令人厭煩、使每一次實質改革嘗試都受挫的內鬥感到厭倦。"},{"w":"ostentatious","p":"adj.","d":"Showy, designed to impress.","c":"炫耀的；賣弄的","s":"The billionaire's ostentatiousedisplay of wealth — the private island, the collection of vintage aircraft, the purpose-built yacht equipped with a submarine — generated considerable public resentment during the economic recession, when his company was simultaneously requesting government subsidies for operational losses.","t":"這位億萬富翁炫耀性的財富展示——私人島嶼、古董飛機收藏、配備潛水艇的定制遊艇——在經濟衰退期間引起了相當大的公眾怨恨，當時他的公司同時正在申請政府補貼以彌補運營虧損。","as":"In a neighborhood where most affluent families favored understated homes, the tycoon's ostentatious mansion, with its gold-plated faucets and marble statues of himself, became a target of scorn, and neighbors loathed its blatant vanity.","at":"在一個多數富裕家庭偏好低調住宅的社區裡，這位大亨炫耀浮誇的豪宅擺滿鍍金水龍頭和他本人的大理石雕像，成了眾人嘲諷的對象，鄰居們對這種明目張膽的虛榮深惡痛絕。"}]},{"unit":13,"cards":[{"w":"importune","p":"v.","d":"To ask urgently and persistently.","c":"強求；胡纏","s":"The desperate refugees importuned every official they could reach at the border crossing, presenting their documents repeatedly and explaining their situation with increasing urgency as the afternoon wore on and the crossing point prepared to close for the night without processing their applications.","t":"絕望的難民強求每一個他們能在邊境口岸接觸到的官員，隨著下午時光流逝、過境點準備關閉過夜而不處理他們的申請，他們反覆出示文件並以越來越緊迫的語氣解釋他們的情況。","as":"Reporters continued to importune the reticent scientist for an interview, but she refused to comment on her surprising findings until independent colleagues could corroborate the data, a cautious stance that many in her field considered laudable.","at":"記者們不斷纏著這位沉默寡言的科學家要求專訪，但在獨立研究的同儕證實數據之前，她拒絕對自己出人意料的發現發表任何評論；她這種謹慎的立場，獲得許多同行的讚許。"},{"w":"incontrovertible","p":"adj.","d":"Not able to be denied or disputed.","c":"無可辯駁的；不容置疑的","s":"The prosecution presented what it described as incontrovertible forensic evidence linking the defendant to the scene — DNA recovered from multiple locations, digital records showing his precise movements, and CCTV footage capturing his vehicle at each critical point in the timeline.","t":"檢察官提出了它所描述的將被告與現場聯繫起來的無可辯駁的法証證據——從多個地點採集的DNA、顯示他精確行動的數字記錄，以及捕捉到他的車輛在時間軸上每個關鍵點的閉路電視錄像。","as":"Although the defense raised a plethora of objections and tried to construe the evidence as merely circumstantial, the security footage provided incontrovertible proof that the culprit had been at the scene on the night of the robbery.","at":"雖然辯方提出大量異議，並試圖把證據解釋為僅是間接證據，但監視器畫面提供了無可辯駁的證明：搶案當晚，嫌犯確實就在現場。"},{"w":"surreptitious","p":"adj.","d":"Done secretly, stealthy.","c":"鬼鬼祟祟的；暗中的","s":"The journalist had obtained the internal documents through what management later characterised as surreptitious means — specifically, an employee had photographed them on a personal device during a routine meeting and subsequently forwarded the images through an encrypted messaging application.","t":"這位記者通過管理層後來描述為鬼鬼祟祟的方式獲得了內部文件——具體來說，一名員工在一次例行會議期間用個人設備拍攝了這些文件，並隨後通過加密消息應用程序轉發了圖像。","as":"The spy made surreptitious recordings of the diplomats' private conversations, a clandestine operation that, once exposed by a newspaper, caused a diplomatic fiasco and prompted both governments to oust several embassy officials.","at":"這名間諜暗中錄下外交官的私人談話；這項秘密行動被報社揭發後，演變成一場外交上的大失敗，也迫使兩國政府驅逐了數名使館官員。"},{"w":"haven","p":"n.","d":"A place of safety and shelter.","c":"避難所；港口","s":"The remote island had served as a tax haven for wealthy individuals and corporations for more than four decades, its combination of minimal disclosure requirements, sympathetic judicial interpretation of financial regulations, and geographical remoteness making it particularly attractive to those seeking to minimise their exposure to the tax authorities of their home countries.","t":"這個偏遠島嶼已為富裕個人和企業服務了四十多年的避稅天堂，其最低披露要求、對金融法規的同情性司法解釋和地理偏遠性的結合，使其對那些尋求最大限度地減少在本國稅務機關面前曝光的人特別具有吸引力。","as":"During the war, the mountain monastery became a haven for refugees fleeing persecution, offering them sanctuary, simple food, and solace at a time when privation and fear were ubiquitous throughout the region.","at":"戰爭期間，這座山中修道院成了逃避迫害的難民的避風港；在整個地區到處充斥著匱乏與恐懼的時候，它為難民提供庇護、簡單的食物與心靈慰藉。"},{"w":"subjugate","p":"v.","d":"To conquer and bring under control.","c":"征服；降伏","s":"The imperial expansion policy had successfully subjugated seventeen distinct ethnic groups within forty years, but historical records suggest that the apparent pacification masked deep resentments that would periodically erupt in organised resistance movements whenever the military presence in a region was temporarily reduced.","t":"帝國擴張政策在四十年內成功征服了十七個不同的民族群體，但歷史記錄表明，表面上的平定掩蓋了深深的怨恨，每當一個地區的軍事存在暫時減少時，這些怨恨就會定期爆發為有組織的抵抗運動。","as":"The empire sought to subjugate neighboring tribes not only through military conquest but also by attempting to coerce local leaders into abandoning their languages and customs, a pernicious policy whose legacy historians still scrutinize today.","at":"這個帝國不僅以武力征服來壓制鄰近部落，還企圖脅迫當地領袖放棄自己的語言與傳統；這項有害政策所留下的影響，至今仍是歷史學家仔細探究的對象。"},{"w":"ultimate","p":"adj.","d":"Final, most extreme, fundamental.","c":"最終的；極限的","s":"The committee's ultimate objective was not merely to reform the specific practices under investigation but to establish a durable institutional framework that would prevent similar abuses from occurring in future, even under leadership teams with different values or priorities from those currently in place.","t":"委員會的最終目標不僅僅是改革被調查的具體做法，而是建立一個持久的制度框架，以防止未來發生類似的濫用行為，即使在具有不同價值觀或優先事項的領導團隊下也是如此。","as":"The ultimate goal of the vaccination campaign was to wipe out the virulent disease entirely, but health officials knew that sporadic outbreaks in isolated villages could thwart their efforts for many years to come.","at":"這項疫苗接種計畫的最終目標，是徹底根除這種致命的疾病；但衛生官員也明白，偏僻村落中零星爆發的疫情，可能會讓他們的努力在未來多年內受挫。"},{"w":"eventuate","p":"v.","d":"To result in, to end in.","c":"最終導致；結果是","s":"The series of seemingly minor diplomatic missteps that characterised the early months of the new administration ultimately eventuated in a formal breakdown of relations with the neighbouring country, a deterioration that most international observers had considered unlikely as recently as six months before the rupture occurred.","t":"新政府最初幾個月一系列看似微小的外交失誤最終導致了與鄰國關係的正式破裂，大多數國際觀察員在破裂發生前六個月還認為這種惡化不太可能發生。","as":"Economists warned that lax oversight of the banking sector might eventuate in a financial crisis, but officials, sanguine about continued growth, dismissed such ominous predictions until rampant speculation finally triggered a devastating crash.","at":"經濟學家警告，對銀行業監管鬆散最終可能導致金融危機；但官員們對經濟持續成長過於樂觀，對這些不祥的預測置之不理，直到猖獗的投機炒作終於引發一場毀滅性的崩盤。"},{"w":"emit","p":"v.","d":"To send out, give off.","c":"發出；散發","s":"The volcano had been quietly emit ting sulphur dioxide at elevated levels for approximately three weeks before the main eruption, a warning signal that the monitoring network had detected and flagged but which the local authorities had chosen not to communicate publicly to avoid creating unnecessary panic.","t":"火山在主要噴發前大約三週一直在以較高水平安靜地排放二氧化硫，這是監測網絡已檢測並標記但地方當局選擇不公開傳達以避免製造不必要恐慌的警告信號。","as":"Fireflies emit brief flashes of light to attract mates, each species using a distinctive pattern that meticulous biologists have learned to discern, although some predatory fireflies mimic these signals to dupe unsuspecting males.","at":"螢火蟲會發出短暫的閃光來吸引配偶，每個物種都有獨特的閃光模式，細心的生物學家已學會加以辨識；不過，有些掠食性螢火蟲會模仿這些訊號，誘騙毫無戒心的雄蟲上當。"},{"w":"subterranean","p":"adj.","d":"Existing or occurring underground.","c":"地下的；隱蔽的","s":"The subterranean network of tunnels discovered beneath the ancient city proved far more extensive than the initial surveys had suggested, stretching for nearly four kilometres and incorporating chambers of varying sizes that appeared to have served simultaneously as water cisterns, grain stores, and emergency refuge spaces.","t":"在古城下發現的地下隧道網絡被證明比最初調查所顯示的要廣泛得多，延伸近四公里，包含不同大小的腔室，這些腔室似乎同時充當蓄水池、糧倉和緊急避難空間。","as":"Biologists exploring the subterranean caverns found blind, colorless fish thriving despite a paucity of food, a paradox that made sense only once they understood how the creatures had adapted to a realm without sunlight.","at":"在地下洞穴探勘的生物學家發現，失明、無色的魚類儘管食物匱乏仍能繁衍興盛；這個看似矛盾的現象，直到他們理解這些生物如何適應一個沒有陽光的世界，才終於說得通。"},{"w":"viable","p":"adj.","d":"Practicable, capable of working.","c":"切實可行的；能存活的","s":"The energy consultants concluded that offshore wind power represented the only viable long-term solution to the region's electricity supply challenges, given that the geographic and environmental constraints affecting the area made both nuclear expansion and new hydroelectric development practically impossible within any realistic planning timeframe.","t":"能源顧問得出結論，海上風電代表了解決該地區電力供應挑戰的唯一切實可行的長期解決方案，鑑於影響該地區的地理和環境限制使核電擴展和新的水力發電開發在任何現實規劃時間框架內都實際上不可能。","as":"Engineers concluded that the proposed tunnel was not economically viable, since the porous rock beneath the river would require costly reinforcement, and even the project's most avid supporters had to concur that its benefits were dubious.","at":"工程師的結論是，這條擬議中的隧道在經濟上並不可行，因為河床下多孔的岩層需要昂貴的補強工程；就連這項計畫最熱衷的支持者，也不得不同意其效益令人存疑。"},{"w":"premise","p":"n.","d":"A proposition from which a conclusion is drawn.","c":"前提；假設","s":"The entire policy framework rested on a premise that subsequent research had seriously undermined — specifically, the assumption that increasing home ownership rates would automatically reduce social inequality — and without this foundational belief the justification for three decades of government intervention in the housing market largely dissolved.","t":"整個政策框架建立在一個後來的研究嚴重削弱的前提上——具體來說，是提高住房擁有率將自動減少社會不平等的假設——如果沒有這個基本信念，三十年政府幹預住房市場的理由基本上消失了。","as":"The novel rests on an intriguing premise: an automaton built to perform household drudgery gradually becomes cognizant of its own emotions, compelling readers to consider what it truly means to be human.","at":"這部小說建立在一個引人入勝的前提上：一個被製造來做繁瑣家務的機器人，逐漸意識到自己擁有情感，促使讀者深思「身而為人」的真正意義。"},{"w":"jeopardize","p":"v.","d":"To put in danger, threaten.","c":"危害；使受危險","s":"The whistleblower was acutely aware that coming forward publicly would jeopardize not only her career but also her family's financial security and potentially her physical safety, yet she concluded that the alternative — allowing the systematic fraud to continue undisturbed — was morally indefensible.","t":"舉報人深刻意識到公開站出來不僅會危害她的職業生涯，還會危害她家人的財務安全，甚至可能危及她的人身安全，但她得出結論，另一個選擇——允許系統性欺詐繼續不受干擾——在道德上是站不住腳的。","as":"Scientists warned that the proposed dam could jeopardize several endangered fish species whose rivers were already afflicted by pollution, and they implored officials to scrutinize the project's ecological consequences before construction began.","at":"科學家警告，擬建的水壩可能危及數種棲地早已飽受污染之苦的瀕危魚類，並懇求官員在動工之前，仔細審查這項工程對生態的影響。"},{"w":"incredulous","p":"adj.","d":"Unwilling or unable to believe.","c":"懷疑的；不輕信的","s":"The experienced fraud investigator remained deeply incredulous when the chief financial officer claimed to have had no knowledge of the systematic misappropriation that had occurred under his direct supervision for nearly four years, finding it implausible that such extensive and systematic irregularities could have continued unnoticed by someone in his position.","t":"當首席財務官聲稱對在他直接監督下發生近四年的系統性挪用公款毫不知情時，這位經驗豐富的欺詐調查員仍然深感懷疑，認為如此廣泛和系統性的違規行為能夠在他這個職位的人不注意的情況下持續下去是難以置信的。","as":"When the precocious astronomer announced that she had spotted a new comet, her eminent colleagues were initially incredulous, but their doubts vanished once other observatories confirmed the sighting, and she soon received a prestigious award.","at":"這位早慧的天文學家宣布自己發現了一顆新彗星時，德高望重的同僚們起初都難以置信；但在其他天文臺證實這項觀測後，他們的疑慮隨即消散，她不久便獲頒一項享有盛譽的獎項。"},{"w":"permeate","p":"v.","d":"To spread throughout, penetrate.","c":"彌漫；滲透","s":"A culture of casual dishonesty had gradually permeated every level of the organisation, beginning with minor misrepresentations in marketing materials and eventually extending to falsified safety records, manipulated financial statements, and systematic pressure on employees to misreport performance metrics.","t":"一種隨意不誠實的文化逐漸滲透到組織的每個層面，從市場材料中的輕微虛假陳述開始，最終延伸到偽造的安全記錄、操縱的財務報表，以及對員工虛報業績指標的系統性壓力。","as":"A sense of dread permeated the village as the drought dragged on, and the doleful farmers, watching their wan crops wither under the relentless sun, began to fear that famine was imminent.","at":"隨著乾旱遲遲未解，一股恐懼瀰漫整個村莊；憂愁的農民眼看著無精打采的作物在毒辣的陽光下逐漸枯萎，開始擔心饑荒即將來臨。"},{"w":"propitious","p":"adj.","d":"Giving or indicating a good chance of success.","c":"吉利的；有利的","s":"The timing of the diplomatic initiative proved remarkably propitious, coinciding with a period of unusual domestic political weakness in both countries that made their respective leaders unusually receptive to compromise proposals that they would almost certainly have rejected under more stable political conditions.","t":"外交倡議的時機被證明異常有利，恰逢兩國都出現不尋常國內政治弱點的時期，這使他們各自的領導人對妥協提案出乎意料地接受，而在更穩定的政治條件下，他們幾乎肯定會拒絕這些提案。","as":"With calm seas and steady winds, the explorers judged the moment propitious for setting sail, though veteran sailors cautioned that such tranquil conditions could quickly turn turbulent and that a rash departure might prove deadly.","at":"海面平靜、風勢穩定，探險隊認為這是啟航的大好時機；但經驗豐富的水手提醒，如此平靜的海況可能轉眼就變得波濤洶湧，貿然出發恐怕會招致殺身之禍。"},{"w":"surmise","p":"v.","d":"To guess or infer without firm evidence.","c":"猜測；臆測","s":"From the pattern of purchases visible in the recovered financial records, investigators were able to surmise the approximate location of the suspect's undisclosed secondary residence, even though no direct documentation of the property's existence had yet been found in any of the seized materials.","t":"從已恢復的財務記錄中可見的購買模式，調查人員能夠猜測出嫌疑人未披露的次要住所的大概位置，儘管在任何查獲的材料中都還沒有發現該房產存在的直接文件記錄。","as":"Finding the mountain abode abandoned, with a half-eaten meal still on the table, the detectives could only surmise that its occupant had fled in a frenzy, perhaps seized by a sudden premonition of danger.","at":"偵探們發現這棟山中住所已人去樓空，桌上還留著吃了一半的飯菜，只能推測屋主是在驚慌失措中倉皇逃走，或許是突然預感到危險將至。"},{"w":"curtail","p":"v.","d":"To reduce or impose a restriction on.","c":"縮減；剝奪","s":"The emergency health measures introduced at the height of the outbreak significantly curtail ed civil liberties that citizens of democratic societies had taken for granted for generations — restrictions on movement, assembly, and commercial activity that would have been considered unacceptable in any ordinary peacetime context.","t":"在疫情高峰期間引入的緊急衛生措施大幅縮減了民主社會公民幾代人視為理所當然的公民自由——對移動、集會和商業活動的限制，在任何普通和平時期都會被認為是不可接受的。","as":"Faced with a severe budget shortfall, the city council voted to curtail library hours and arts funding, a decision that elicited a barrage of irate complaints from residents who considered such services integral to the community.","at":"面臨嚴重的預算短缺，市議會投票決定縮減圖書館開放時間和藝文補助；此舉引來居民排山倒海的憤怒投訴，因為他們認為這些服務是社區不可或缺的一部分。"},{"w":"repress","p":"v.","d":"To hold back, suppress forcibly.","c":"壓抑；鎮壓","s":"Decades of research in psychology have consistently demonstrated that attempts to repress traumatic memories are counterproductive, typically intensifying rather than diminishing their psychological impact and creating secondary anxiety about the very fact that the memories continue to surface despite conscious efforts to contain them.","t":"數十年的心理學研究一致表明，試圖壓抑創傷記憶適得其反，通常會加強而不是減弱其心理影響，並對儘管有意識的努力去控制記憶仍繼續浮現這一事實產生繼發性焦慮。","as":"The authoritarian regime used censorship and mass arrests to repress opposition, yet the brutal crackdown only intensified public outrage, and dissidents continued to flout censorship laws, distributing pamphlets that castigated the government for its egregious abuses.","at":"這個獨裁政權以審查制度和大規模逮捕來鎮壓異議，然而殘暴的鎮壓只讓民怨更加沸騰；異議人士依舊公然違抗審查法令，散發嚴厲譴責政府惡劣暴行的傳單。"},{"w":"cryptic","p":"adj.","d":"Having a hidden meaning, puzzling.","c":"神秘的；隱晦的","s":"The director's final film was so deliberately cryptic that critics spent years debating its meaning, with interpretations ranging from a straightforward allegory about political repression to an entirely abstract meditation on memory, time, and the impossibility of communicating authentic personal experience through a commercial art form.","t":"這位導演的最後一部電影如此刻意地隱晦，以至於批評家們花了數年時間爭論其含義，解釋範圍從關於政治壓迫的直接寓言到關於記憶、時間以及通過商業藝術形式傳達真實個人體驗的不可能性的完全抽象冥想。","as":"The poet's final letter contained a cryptic reference to a hidden manuscript, and generations of scholars have scrutinized her diaries in vain, each offering a new conjecture about what the elusive phrase might mean.","at":"這位詩人的最後一封信中，隱晦地提到一份藏起來的手稿；好幾代學者仔細研讀她的日記卻一無所獲，每個人都對這句令人捉摸不透的話提出新的推測。"},{"w":"inchoate","p":"adj.","d":"Just beginning, not fully formed.","c":"早期的；未成形的","s":"The new political movement remained distinctly inchoate, lacking coherent policy positions on most major issues, a stable organisational structure, or sufficient financial resources to mount a credible electoral challenge, though its early grassroots energy suggested it might develop into something more substantial over the following electoral cycle.","t":"這個新政治運動仍然明顯地處於早期階段，在大多數重大問題上缺乏連貫的政策立場、穩定的組織結構或足夠的財務資源來發動可信的選舉挑戰，儘管其早期的草根能量表明它可能在以下選舉週期中發展成更有實質內容的東西。","as":"In its inchoate stage, the reform movement consisted of little more than a few zealous students holding placards outside city hall, but within ten years it had grown into a monolithic force that no politician could ignore.","at":"在剛起步、尚未成形的階段，這場改革運動不過是幾名熱血學生在市政府外舉著標語牌；但不到十年，它已發展成一股任何政治人物都無法忽視的龐大力量。"}]},{"unit":14,"cards":[{"w":"aspire","p":"v.","d":"To strive for something great.","c":"渴望；立志","s":"From childhood she had aspired to conduct at the world's great concert halls, practising piano and studying scores with an intensity that her teachers recognised as exceptional while simultaneously mastering the orchestral repertoire that would ultimately define her career at the highest professional level.","t":"從童年起她就渴望在世界偉大的音樂廳指揮，以她的老師認為非凡的強度練習鋼琴和研究樂譜，同時掌握最終在最高職業水平定義她職業生涯的管弦樂曲目。","as":"Many young athletes aspire to compete at the Olympics, yet few are willing to endure the drudgery of daily training, and fewer still can withstand the inexorable pressure that accompanies a prestigious international career.","at":"許多年輕運動員立志參加奧運，但願意忍受日復一日枯燥訓練的人寥寥無幾，而能承受伴隨顯赫國際生涯而來、無法擺脫之壓力的人更是少之又少。"},{"w":"inveigh","p":"v.","d":"To protest strongly, attack verbally.","c":"猛烈抨擊；痛罵","s":"The columnist had been inveighing against the planning committee's decisions for three years in increasingly intemperate language, but his campaign gained genuine public traction only when his predictions about the traffic consequences of the approved development proved accurate within six months of the project's completion.","t":"這位專欄作家三年來以越來越激烈的語言猛烈抨擊規劃委員會的決定，但只有當他對已批准開發項目交通後果的預測在項目完成後六個月內得到證實時，他的運動才獲得了真正的公眾支持。","as":"In his weekly sermons, the outspoken preacher would inveigh against the greed of affluent merchants, whose nefarious lending practices, he claimed, had plunged countless families in the parish into privation.","at":"這位直言不諱的牧師在每週講道中，總會猛烈抨擊富商的貪婪；他聲稱，這些富商卑劣的放貸手段，讓教區內無數家庭陷入貧困。"},{"w":"nettle","p":"v.","d":"To irritate or annoy.","c":"惹怒；激怒","s":"What particularly nettled the senior scientist was not the criticism itself but the manner in which it had been delivered — publicly, without prior private discussion, and in terms that seemed designed to maximise professional embarrassment rather than to initiate a genuine scholarly exchange.","t":"特別惹怒這位高級科學家的不是批評本身，而是批評的方式——公開地，沒有事先私下討論，而且措辭似乎旨在最大限度地造成職業尷尬，而不是啟動真正的學術交流。","as":"Nothing seemed to nettle the veteran diplomat more than reporters who misquoted her, yet she always hid her chagrin behind a phlegmatic smile, refusing to give them the satisfaction of an irate outburst.","at":"最讓這位資深外交官惱火的，莫過於錯誤引述她話語的記者；但她總是以冷靜的微笑掩飾心中的懊惱，絕不讓對方因她怒氣爆發而稱心如意。"},{"w":"overt","p":"adj.","d":"Done openly, not concealed.","c":"公開的；明顯的","s":"The shift from covert surveillance to overt monitoring of the protest movement represented a significant tactical change by the security services, apparently calculated to create a deterrent effect through the visible presence of observers rather than to gather additional intelligence that was not already available through existing channels.","t":"從秘密監控轉向對抗議運動的公開監控代表了安全部門的重大戰術變化，顯然是通過觀察員的可見存在來製造威懾效果，而不是通過現有渠道已有的途徑收集額外情報。","as":"Whereas earlier generations faced overt discrimination, from segregated schools to placards barring certain groups from restaurants, today's prejudice is often less blatant, surfacing in subtle nuances of language that are difficult to discern.","at":"上一代人面對的是公開的歧視，從種族隔離的學校到禁止特定族群進入餐廳的告示牌皆是；如今的偏見往往不那麼明目張膽，而是隱藏在難以察覺的細微語言差異之中。"},{"w":"relegate","p":"v.","d":"To assign to an inferior position.","c":"降級；貶謫","s":"The former minister, once considered a serious contender for the party leadership, had been effectively relegated to the political backbenches following his handling of the departmental scandal, his influence now confined to occasional interventions in debates where his acknowledged expertise made his contributions difficult to ignore entirely.","t":"這位前部長，曾被認為是嚴肅的黨魁競爭者，在處理部門醜聞後被有效地降到了政治後座，他的影響力現在僅限於在他公認的專業知識使他的貢獻難以完全忽視的辯論中偶爾干預。","as":"After his duplicity was exposed, the once powerful minister was relegated to a minor post in a far-flung province, a humiliating demotion that his rivals derided as a nominal role with no real influence.","at":"這位曾經權傾一時的部長在兩面手法被揭穿後，被降調到偏遠省份擔任一個小職位；他的對手嘲笑這不過是個毫無實權的掛名職務，令他顏面盡失。"},{"w":"supine","p":"adj.","d":"Lying face upward, passive and inactive.","c":"仰臥的；軟弱的","s":"The parliamentary opposition's supine response to successive constitutional reforms — offering only token resistance and ultimately abstaining rather than voting against proposals that fundamentally altered the balance of power — was characterised by commentators as a historic abdication of the democratic responsibility to hold government accountable.","t":"議會反對派對連續憲政改革的軟弱回應——只提供象徵性的抵抗，最終在根本上改變權力平衡的提案上棄權而不是投票反對——被評論員描述為歷史性地放棄了追究政府責任的民主責任。","as":"Critics accused the supine legislature of meekly endorsing every decree the president issued, arguing that its refusal to scrutinize executive power had allowed corruption to become rampant and officials to act with impunity.","at":"批評者指責這個軟弱消極的立法機關對總統頒布的每一項命令都唯唯諾諾地背書，認為正是它拒絕監督行政權力，才讓貪腐猖獗，官員得以為所欲為而不受懲罰。"},{"w":"mammoth","p":"adj.","d":"Huge, of very great size.","c":"巨大的；龐大的","s":"The mammoth infrastructure project — encompassing six new rail lines, forty-three stations, and over two hundred kilometres of tunnelling beneath a densely populated urban environment — was expected to take twenty years to complete and represented the single largest capital investment in the city's history.","t":"這個龐大的基礎設施項目——涵蓋六條新鐵路線、四十三個車站和在密集城市環境下超過兩百公里的隧道——預計需要二十年才能完成，代表著這座城市歷史上最大的單項資本投資。","as":"Building the transcontinental railroad was a mammoth undertaking in which thousands of immigrant laborers endured excruciating toil, inclement weather, and dangerous blasting through solid granite, yet their contributions were long omitted from the official annals.","at":"興建橫貫大陸鐵路是一項極其龐大的工程，數以千計的移民勞工忍受著極度艱苦的勞動、惡劣的天候，以及在堅硬花崗岩中爆破的危險；然而，他們的貢獻長久以來都未被寫入官方史冊。"},{"w":"repulse","p":"v.","d":"To drive back, reject firmly.","c":"擊退；拒絕","s":"The garrison managed to repulse three successive assault attempts before nightfall, each time inflicting casualties sufficient to force the attacking forces to withdraw and regroup, though the defenders were acutely aware that their own ammunition reserves were diminishing at a rate that made their position ultimately untenable.","t":"駐軍在夜幕降臨前設法擊退了三次連續的突擊嘗試，每次都造成足夠的傷亡迫使攻擊部隊撤退和重組，儘管防禦者深刻意識到他們自己的彈藥儲備正在以使他們的陣地最終站不住腳的速度減少。","as":"The outnumbered garrison managed to repulse three successive assaults on the fortress, an intrepid defense that astonished the army besieging it, though the defenders, emaciated from months of privation, could not hold out indefinitely.","at":"寡不敵眾的守軍成功擊退了敵人對要塞的三次連續猛攻，這番英勇的防守令圍城大軍大感震驚；然而，因數月物資匱乏而骨瘦如柴的守軍，終究無法無限期地堅守下去。"},{"w":"havoc","p":"n.","d":"Great damage and disorder.","c":"大破壞；浩劫","s":"The unprecedented storm wrought havoc across the coastal communities, destroying three hundred homes, washing away four kilometres of seafront road, and causing an estimated two billion dollars worth of damage to infrastructure that had been specifically designed to withstand the most severe weather events historically recorded in the region.","t":"這場前所未有的風暴在沿海社區造成了巨大破壞，摧毀了三百所房屋，沖走了四公里的海濱道路，並對專門設計用於承受該地區歷史上記錄的最嚴重天氣事件的基礎設施造成了估計二十億美元的損失。","as":"The hurricane wreaked havoc on the coastal towns, flooding homes and toppling power lines, and in its aftermath residents grew distraught as relief efforts were stymied by impassable roads and a paucity of supplies.","at":"颶風對沿海城鎮造成嚴重破壞，淹沒房屋、吹倒電線桿；災後，由於道路無法通行、物資短缺，救援工作受阻，居民們也越來越憂心如焚。"},{"w":"raze","p":"v.","d":"To completely destroy a building.","c":"夷為平地；破壞","s":"The developers' application to raze the Victorian warehouse and replace it with a twenty-storey apartment complex was unanimously rejected by the heritage committee, which ruled that the building's architectural significance and its contribution to the neighbourhood's historical character outweighed any economic benefit from its redevelopment.","t":"開發商申請夷平維多利亞時代倉庫並以二十層公寓綜合體取而代之的申請被遺產委員會一致否決，委員會裁定，該建築的建築意義及其對鄰里歷史特徵的貢獻超過了其重新開發的任何經濟利益。","as":"The conquerors ordered their troops to raze the ancient city, an egregious act that destroyed priceless libraries and temples and left modern scholars to surmise the customs of that eminent civilization from scattered fragments.","at":"征服者下令軍隊將這座古城夷為平地；這項惡劣的暴行摧毀了無價的圖書館與神殿，使得現代學者只能從零散的殘片中推測那個輝煌文明的風俗習慣。"},{"w":"lethal","p":"adj.","d":"Sufficient to cause death.","c":"致命的；致死的","s":"The toxicologist testified that the concentration of the compound found in the victim's bloodstream was approximately four times the lethaledose for a person of his body weight, a finding that was inconsistent with accidental ingestion and strongly supported the prosecution's contention that deliberate poisoning had occurred.","t":"毒理學家作證說，在受害者血液中發現的化合物濃度大約是他體重的人的致死劑量的四倍，這一發現與意外攝入不符，並強烈支持了檢察官關於蓄意下毒的主張。","as":"Although the venom of many spiders is lethal to insects and other small prey, it rarely poses a serious threat to humans, so experts urge squeamish homeowners not to panic or resort to the indiscriminate use of pesticides.","at":"雖然許多蜘蛛的毒液對昆蟲等小型獵物足以致命，但對人類卻很少構成嚴重威脅；因此專家呼籲容易受驚的屋主不要驚慌，也不要毫無節制地濫用殺蟲劑。"},{"w":"scurry","p":"v.","d":"To move quickly with short steps.","c":"急跑；碎步快跑","s":"The sudden downpour sent the market traders scurrying to cover their displays with protective sheets, the practiced efficiency of their movements suggesting this was a familiar emergency drill executed many times previously during the unpredictable summer weather that characterised the region.","t":"突如其來的大雨讓市場攤販急忙用防護布蓋住他們的展示品，他們動作的熟練效率表明這是一個熟悉的緊急演練，在該地區特有的不可預測的夏季天氣中已多次執行。","as":"When the lights in the abandoned warehouse suddenly flickered on, dozens of rats began to scurry across the floor, an ominous sight that made even the seasoned inspectors recoil and conclude that the building's lax sanitation posed a serious health risk.","at":"廢棄倉庫的燈突然閃爍亮起時，數十隻老鼠開始在地板上四處竄逃；這不祥的景象讓經驗老到的檢查員也不禁退縮，並斷定這棟建築鬆散的衛生管理已構成嚴重的健康風險。"},{"w":"incisive","p":"adj.","d":"Intelligently analytical and clear.","c":"敏銳的；深刻的","s":"Her most incisive observation during the entire seminar — that the theoretical framework being discussed was internally consistent but rested entirely on empirical assumptions that had never been tested — reframed the subsequent debate in a way that exposed fundamental weaknesses the previous three hours of discussion had entirely failed to address.","t":"她在整個研討會中最敏銳的觀察——正在討論的理論框架內部一致，但完全建立在從未經過測試的實證假設上——以一種揭示了前三個小時討論完全未能解決的根本弱點的方式重新框架了隨後的辯論。","as":"The journalist's incisive analysis cut through the government's euphemisms, exposing how officials had described mass layoffs as workforce adjustments and revealing the salient facts that more perfunctory coverage had overlooked.","at":"這位記者鞭辟入裡的分析，戳破了政府的委婉說詞，揭露官員如何把大規模裁員說成「人力調整」，並指出那些敷衍了事的報導所忽略的重要事實。"},{"w":"precipitate","p":"v.","d":"To cause suddenly or prematurely.","c":"促成；使沉澱","s":"The unexpected announcement by the central bank precipitated a sharp sell-off across equity markets, with investors interpreting the change in language as signalling a more aggressive approach to interest rate increases than had previously been anticipated and adjusting their portfolios accordingly within minutes of the statement's release.","t":"央行的意外宣布促成了股票市場的大幅拋售，投資者將語言的變化解讀為比之前預期的更激進的利率上調方式的信號，並在聲明發布後幾分鐘內相應地調整了他們的投資組合。","as":"The assassination of an Austrian archduke helped precipitate the First World War, as rigid alliances and belligerent speeches inexorably transformed a regional dispute into a devastating conflict that few leaders had anticipated and none could quell.","at":"奧地利大公遇刺一事加速引爆了第一次世界大戰；僵化的同盟關係和好戰的演說，無可阻擋地將一場區域爭端演變成一場少有領袖預料得到、也無人能平息的災難性衝突。"},{"w":"stereotype","p":"n.","d":"An oversimplified fixed idea about a group.","c":"刻板印象；成見","s":"The study demonstrated that even highly educated professionals with declared commitments to equality were susceptible to stereotype -driven bias in their recruitment decisions, unconsciously evaluating identical application materials differently depending on whether the applicant's name suggested membership of a minority or majority demographic group.","t":"這項研究表明，即使是具有明確平等承諾的高學歷專業人士也容易在招聘決策中受到刻板印象驅動的偏見，根據申請人的名字是否暗示其屬於少數或多數人口群體，他們無意識地對相同的申請材料進行不同的評估。","as":"The documentary challenged a stereotype, often used by urban pundits to disparage rural farmers, that people in the countryside resist change, showing instead how astute growers have adopted innovative techniques to enhance their yields.","at":"這部紀錄片挑戰了一個常被都市名嘴用來貶低農民的刻板印象，也就是鄉下人抗拒改變；片中反而呈現精明的農民如何採用創新技術來提高收成。"},{"w":"stentorian","p":"adj.","d":"Very loud and powerful.","c":"聲音洪亮的","s":"The lecturer's stentorian voice filled the enormous auditorium without amplification, his deep resonant tones carrying clearly to the back row during a period before modern sound systems existed, a natural gift that had made him a celebrated orator long before his scholarly reputation had been established.","t":"講師那洪亮的聲音在沒有擴音的情況下充滿了巨大的禮堂，在現代音響系統存在之前的時代，他深沉共鳴的聲調清晰地傳到後排，這是一種天賦，使他在他的學術聲譽建立之前很久就成為了著名的演說家。","as":"The drill sergeant's stentorian voice was reverberating across the parade ground, so that even the most fretful recruits snapped to attention, while those who dared to flout his orders faced a swift reprimand.","at":"教育班長洪亮如雷的聲音在閱兵場上迴盪，連最緊張不安的新兵也立刻立正站好；而膽敢違抗命令的人，則會馬上遭到嚴厲斥責。"},{"w":"singular","p":"adj.","d":"Remarkably unusual or extraordinary.","c":"異常的；單一的","s":"Her singular achievement in winning the championship three consecutive years after returning from a career-threatening injury was recognised by the governing body with a special award that had been presented only twice in the sport's ninety-year history, both previous recipients having long since retired.","t":"她在從威脅職業生涯的傷病中恢復後連續三年贏得冠軍的非凡成就，得到了管理機構特別獎的認可，這個獎項在這項運動九十年歷史中只頒發過兩次，之前的兩位獲獎者早已退役。","as":"The precocious violinist displayed a singular gift for interpretation, imbuing even familiar concertos with subtle shadings that eminent critics had never perceived, and her debut recital was hailed as a revelation.","at":"這位早慧的小提琴家展現出非凡的詮釋天賦，即使是耳熟能詳的協奏曲，也能被她注入連知名評論家都未曾察覺的細膩層次；她的首場獨奏會因此被譽為一大驚豔之作。"},{"w":"valor","p":"n.","d":"Courage in the face of danger.","c":"英勇；勇氣","s":"The citation accompanying the posthumous medal described acts of extraordinary valor — specifically the sergeant's decision to remain behind to provide covering fire while his entire unit withdrew from an untenable position, allowing all eleven of his colleagues to reach safety at the cost of his own life.","t":"伴隨著這枚遺孀勳章的引語描述了非凡英勇的行為——具體是這位中士決定留下來提供掩護火力，同時他的整個部隊從一個站不住腳的陣地撤退，以他自己的生命為代價讓他的十一名同僚到達了安全地帶。","as":"The medics who remained in the besieged city to treat the wounded displayed remarkable valor, working without respite amid reverberating explosions and choking dust, and their selfless deeds were later honored by the entire nation.","at":"留在被圍困城市中救治傷患的醫護人員展現了非凡的英勇，他們在迴盪的爆炸聲與令人窒息的塵土中不眠不休地工作；他們無私的事蹟後來獲得全國上下的表揚。"},{"w":"bias","p":"n.","d":"A prejudice in favour of or against something.","c":"偏見；斜紋","s":"The peer review process was designed specifically to minimise conscious bias, but subsequent analysis of publication outcomes suggested that more subtle factors — including the institutional affiliation and nationality of authors — continued to influence editorial decisions in ways that the double-blind submission system had failed to eliminate.","t":"同行評審過程專門設計以最大限度地減少有意識的偏見，但對出版結果的後續分析表明，更微妙的因素——包括作者的機構隸屬和國籍——繼續以雙盲提交系統未能消除的方式影響編輯決策。","as":"Researchers found that the company's hiring algorithm displayed a marked bias against female applicants, an inadvertent flaw inherited from historical data, so executives terminated the program and solicited advice from independent auditors.","at":"研究人員發現，該公司的招聘演算法對女性求職者存在明顯偏見，這是從歷史資料中繼承而來的無心缺陷；因此高層終止了這套程式，並向獨立稽核人員尋求建議。"},{"w":"sinecure","p":"n.","d":"A position requiring little work but giving payment.","c":"掛名差事；閒職","s":"The appointment was widely regarded as a sinecure created to reward a loyal political ally with a comfortable retirement income rather than to fulfil any genuine administrative function, a characterisation supported by the fact that the position had no defined responsibilities, no staff, and no discernible output during its entire three-year existence.","t":"這個任命被廣泛認為是一個為了給一個忠誠的政治盟友提供舒適退休收入而創建的閒職，而不是為了履行任何真正的行政職能，這一描述得到了以下事實的支持：該職位在其整整三年的存在中沒有明確的職責、沒有員工，也沒有可辨別的產出。","as":"The corrupt governor rewarded members of his entourage with sinecures that demanded nothing more than a nominal appearance at the office each month, a flagrant abuse of public funds that infuriated taxpayers across the state.","at":"這位貪腐的州長以閒差肥缺酬庸身邊的親信，這些職位只要求每月到辦公室露個面應付一下；這種明目張膽濫用公帑的行徑，激怒了全州的納稅人。"}]},{"unit":15,"cards":[{"w":"abrogate","p":"v.","d":"To officially abolish or annul.","c":"廢除；取消","s":"The new administration announced its intention to abrogate the treaty within its first hundred days in office, arguing that the agreement had been negotiated under fundamentally different geopolitical conditions that no longer obtained and that continued adherence to its terms was contrary to the national interest.","t":"新政府宣布打算在任職後的前一百天內廢除這項條約，認為該協議是在根本不同的地緣政治條件下談判的，這些條件已不再存在，繼續遵守其條款有違國家利益。","as":"The belligerent new government moved to abrogate the treaty its predecessors had signed, claiming that the agreement had been negotiated under duress and that its terms had relegated the nation to a subordinate role in regional affairs.","at":"好戰的新政府著手廢除前朝簽訂的條約，聲稱該協議是在脅迫下談成的，而且其條款使國家在區域事務中淪為從屬地位。"},{"w":"access","p":"n.","d":"The means or right to approach.","c":"接近；通道","s":"The landmark ruling established that disabled individuals had a fundamental legal right of access to all publicly funded facilities, placing an obligation on local authorities to make reasonable adjustments to physical environments and service delivery systems regardless of the financial costs involved.","t":"這一里程碑式的裁決確立了殘疾人對所有公共資助設施的基本法律接近權，要求地方當局對物理環境和服務提供系統進行合理調整，無論所涉及的財務成本如何。","as":"Advocates argued that reliable access to clean water should be regarded as an integral human right, especially in arid regions where malnutrition and waterborne diseases remain ubiquitous among the poorest families.","at":"倡議者主張，可靠地取得乾淨用水應被視為不可或缺的基本人權，尤其是在乾旱地區，那裡最貧困的家庭仍普遍飽受營養不良與水媒疾病之苦。"},{"w":"accomplice","p":"n.","d":"A person who helps another commit a crime.","c":"共犯；幫兇","s":"The prosecution contended that although the defendant had not been present at the scene during the actual robbery, her role in providing detailed information about the security arrangements, lending her vehicle for the getaway, and disposing of stolen property afterwards made her an accomplice whose culpability was legally equivalent to that of the principal offender.","t":"檢察官主張，儘管被告在實際搶劫期間不在現場，但她提供安全安排詳細信息、借出逃跑車輛以及事後處置贓物的角色，使她成為一名法律上的共犯，其罪責等同於主要罪犯。","as":"The detectives surmised that the elusive thief must have had an accomplice inside the museum, since the alarm system had been disabled with a meticulous precision that no outsider could possibly have achieved.","at":"偵探們推測，這名神出鬼沒的竊賊在博物館內一定有共犯，因為警報系統被解除的手法極為精準細膩，外人絕不可能辦到。"},{"w":"alleged","p":"adj.","d":"Said to have done something but not proven.","c":"涉嫌的；據稱的","s":"The newspaper's decision to name the alleged perpetrator before any charges had been formally filed drew sharp criticism from legal professionals who argued that the publication had effectively denied the suspect the presumption of innocence that remained a cornerstone of the jurisdiction's criminal justice system.","t":"報紙在正式提出任何指控之前就公開點名所謂犯罪者的決定遭到了法律專業人士的強烈批評，他們認為這家媒體實際上剝奪了嫌疑人被推定無罪的權利，而這仍然是該司法管轄區刑事司法體系的基石。","as":"The alleged mastermind of the extortion scheme denied every charge, insisting that the documents cited by prosecutors had been fabricated by former associates seeking revenge, a claim that most jurors found dubious at best.","at":"這起勒索案的涉嫌主謀否認所有指控，堅稱檢方引用的文件是一心報復的前合夥人捏造的；但大多數陪審員認為，這種說法充其量只是令人存疑。"},{"w":"asperity","p":"n.","d":"Harshness of manner or tone.","c":"粗暴；嚴厲","s":"The chairwoman responded to the repeated interruptions with increasing asperity, her initial attempts at measured diplomacy giving way to a crisp directness that made clear she would not tolerate further disruption of proceedings that had already run two hours beyond their scheduled conclusion.","t":"女主席對反覆的打斷以越來越嚴厲的態度回應，她最初的謹慎外交嘗試讓位於一種清晰的直接性，這清楚地表明她不會容忍已經超過預定結束時間兩小時的會議進程被進一步干擾。","as":"The editor responded to the young writer's questions with such asperity that the timorous newcomer nearly abandoned journalism, though years later she conceded that his caustic critiques had helped her develop an incisive style.","at":"主編回答這位年輕作者的問題時態度極為嚴厲，讓這名膽怯的新人幾乎放棄新聞工作；不過多年後她承認，正是他尖刻的批評幫助她培養出犀利的文風。"},{"w":"complicity","p":"n.","d":"Partnership in wrongdoing.","c":"同謀；共犯關係","s":"The historical inquiry concluded that the institution's complicity in the systematic abuse had extended beyond passive failure to act on complaints to active suppression of evidence, reassignment of accused personnel to positions where they retained unsupervised access to vulnerable individuals, and deliberate obstruction of external investigations.","t":"歷史調查得出結論，該機構在系統性虐待中的共謀關係不僅僅是被動地未能對投訴採取行動，還包括積極壓制證據、將被指控人員重新分配到他們保留對脆弱個人無監督接觸的職位，以及蓄意阻撓外部調查。","as":"Investigators uncovered evidence of the bank's complicity in the money-laundering scheme, revealing that senior executives had been cognizant of suspicious transfers for years but had ignored them rather than jeopardize relationships with their most affluent clients.","at":"調查人員發現該銀行參與洗錢計畫的證據，揭露高層主管多年來一直知道有可疑的轉帳，卻選擇視而不見，以免危及與最富有客戶之間的關係。"},{"w":"controversial","p":"adj.","d":"Causing public disagreement.","c":"有爭議的","s":"Few policy decisions in the administration's history had proved as controversial as the proposal to introduce mandatory national identity cards, which simultaneously attracted support from security-focused conservatives and fierce opposition from civil liberties advocates across the entire political spectrum.","t":"在政府歷史上，很少有政策決定像引入強制性國家身份證的提案那樣具有爭議性，它同時吸引了以安全為重點的保守派的支持，並遭到了整個政治光譜中公民自由倡導者的強烈反對。","as":"The museum's decision to display the controversial painting, which portrayed a sacred figure in a lurid and irreverent manner, provoked a diatribe from conservative critics and an equally zealous defense from advocates of artistic freedom.","at":"博物館決定展出這幅備受爭議的畫作，畫中以聳動且不敬的方式描繪一位神聖人物，此舉引來保守派評論家的猛烈抨擊，也激起藝術自由倡議者同樣熱烈的辯護。"},{"w":"culpable","p":"adj.","d":"Deserving blame for a fault.","c":"有罪的；該受譴責的","s":"The independent inquiry found all three senior executives culpable for the disaster, concluding that the incident had been caused not by a single catastrophic failure but by a cumulative series of decisions in which each had chosen operational convenience over the safety procedures that the regulatory framework specifically required.","t":"獨立調查發現三位高級主管都對這場災難負有責任，得出結論認為，這一事件不是由單一災難性失敗造成的，而是由一系列累積的決定造成的，在這些決定中，每個人都選擇了操作便利而非監管框架特別要求的安全程序。","as":"Although the driver who caused the crash was clearly culpable, investigators argued that the city shared the blame, since officials had ignored a plethora of complaints about the defective signal and conducted only perfunctory inspections, negligence that exacerbated the danger.","at":"雖然肇事駕駛顯然難辭其咎，但調查人員認為市政府也應分擔責任，因為官員無視大量關於號誌故障的投訴，只做了敷衍了事的檢查，這種疏失加劇了路口的危險。"},{"w":"declaim","p":"v.","d":"To speak or recite pompously.","c":"慷慨陳詞；演說","s":"The young politician declaimed his manifesto commitments with an intensity that the audience found initially impressive but ultimately exhausting, his rhetorical style offering no modulation between emphatic declaration and emphatic declaration, a monotony of passion that paradoxically drained rather than amplified his message.","t":"這位年輕政治家以一種觀眾最初覺得令人印象深刻但最終感到疲憊的強度慷慨陳詞，他的修辭風格在強調聲明和強調聲明之間沒有任何調節，一種激情的單調反而削弱而非放大了他的信息。","as":"Standing on the courthouse steps, the candidate began to declaim about justice and liberty in such a pompous, verbose manner that the throng of onlookers soon grew restless, and several hecklers would interject sarcastic remarks.","at":"這位候選人站在法院臺階上，開始慷慨激昂地大談正義與自由，但他的語氣浮誇、長篇大論，圍觀群眾很快就不耐煩起來，還有幾個起鬨的人不時插嘴冷嘲熱諷。"},{"w":"epithet","p":"n.","d":"A descriptive word or phrase, often derogatory.","c":"綽號；貶稱","s":"The epithet that had attached itself to the politician early in her career — initially intended as mockery by her opponents — had been so thoroughly reclaimed and redeployed by her supporters that it had become a badge of honour that she herself now used in campaign materials and public speeches.","t":"在她職業生涯早期附著在這位政治家身上的綽號——最初是她的對手用來嘲弄的——已被她的支持者如此徹底地重新奪回和重新部署，以至於它已成為一個榮譽徽章，她現在在競選材料和公開演講中也在使用。","as":"Enemies of the reformer coined a series of insulting epithets to belittle her, yet the scurrilous nicknames only increased her popularity among voters who admired her intrepid campaign against corruption.","at":"改革者的敵人編造了一連串侮辱性的綽號來貶低她，然而這些惡毒的外號反而讓她在選民之間更受歡迎，因為選民欽佩她無畏地對抗貪腐。"},{"w":"extrinsic","p":"adj.","d":"Coming from outside, not essential.","c":"外在的；非固有的","s":"The philosopher argued that the value assigned to artworks by the market represented entirely extrinsic worth — a function of scarcity, fashion, and investment speculation — rather than any intrinsic aesthetic quality, and that conflating economic value with artistic merit had been one of the defining intellectual confusions of the preceding century.","t":"這位哲學家認為，市場賦予藝術品的價值代表了完全外在的價值——是稀缺性、時尚和投機性投資的函數——而不是任何內在的美學品質，將經濟價值與藝術价值混為一談是前一個世紀決定性的智識混亂之一。","as":"Psychologists have found that extrinsic rewards such as money or prizes can sometimes diminish children's natural curiosity, an apparent paradox that has prompted astute educators to eschew excessive incentives and instead cultivate students' love of learning.","at":"心理學家發現，金錢或獎品等外在獎勵有時反而會削弱孩子天生的好奇心；這個看似矛盾的現象，促使有見識的教育者避免過度使用獎勵，轉而培養學生對學習的熱愛。"},{"w":"fetter","p":"v.","d":"To restrict or restrain.","c":"束縛；羈絆","s":"The excessively rigid regulatory framework had fetter ed the sector's capacity for innovation, imposing compliance requirements so onerous that smaller companies — which typically drove the most significant technological advances — were systematically disadvantaged relative to larger competitors with dedicated regulatory affairs departments.","t":"過於僵化的監管框架束縛了該行業的創新能力，施加了如此繁重的合規要求，以至於通常推動最重要技術進步的小公司相對於擁有專門監管事務部門的大型競爭對手而言，系統性地處於不利地位。","as":"Some economists contend that burdensome regulations fetter small enterprises and stifle innovation, but skeptics counter that lax oversight could precipitate the sort of reckless speculation that triggered past crises, so they advocate a more balanced approach.","at":"有些經濟學家主張，繁瑣的法規束縛了小型企業並扼殺創新；但持懷疑態度的人反駁說，監管鬆散可能促成過去引發危機的那種魯莽投機，因此他們提倡採取更平衡的做法。"},{"w":"invalidate","p":"v.","d":"To make legally void or cancel.","c":"使無效；使作廢","s":"The discovery that several key witnesses had been interviewed by investigators before the formal inquiry commenced, in sessions that were neither recorded nor disclosed to the defence, was sufficient to invalidate the entire conviction and require a retrial before a differently constituted panel.","t":"發現幾名關鍵證人在正式調查開始之前已接受調查員的非正式訪談——這些訪談既未記錄也未向辯護方披露——足以使整個定罪無效，並要求在不同組成的小組面前重新審判。","as":"The judge decided to invalidate the contract after learning that the elderly widower had been coerced into signing it while still distraught over his wife's death, and she castigated the developers for such flagrant exploitation.","at":"法官得知這位年邁的鰥夫是在喪妻之痛中仍心神大亂時被脅迫簽約後，決定判定該合約無效，並嚴厲譴責建商如此明目張膽地占人便宜。"},{"w":"landmark","p":"adj.","d":"Historically significant, a turning point.","c":"里程碑；劃時代的","s":"The landmark ruling represented the most significant expansion of constitutional rights in the country's history, establishing for the first time that the protections previously extended only to citizens applied equally to all persons present within the national territory regardless of their immigration status.","t":"這一里程碑式的裁決代表了該國歷史上憲法權利最重大的擴展，首次確立了以前只適用於公民的保護同樣適用於無論移民身份如何在全國領土上的所有人。","as":"The landmark ruling that declared school segregation unconstitutional was a harbinger of sweeping social change, yet many districts flouted it for years, and federal intervention was eventually required to quell the turmoil that ensued.","at":"宣告學校種族隔離違憲的這項劃時代判決，預示著全面的社會變革即將到來；然而許多學區多年來公然無視這項判決，最終還得靠聯邦介入，才平息了隨之而來的動盪。"},{"w":"liquidation","p":"n.","d":"The disposal or destruction of something.","c":"清算；肅清","s":"The company entered voluntary liquidation after it became clear that its liabilities exceeded its assets by a margin that made any rescue plan economically irrational, with the administrator's primary responsibility shifting from preserving the business as a going concern to maximising returns for the hierarchy of creditors.","t":"在公司債務超過資產的幅度使任何救援計劃在經濟上都不合理之後，公司進入了自願清算，管理人的主要責任從維持業務作為持續經營轉移到為債權人層次最大化回報。","as":"After years of mounting debt, the company was forced into liquidation, its assets sold at auction to repay creditors, a fate that dubious accounting had long concealed and that left hundreds of loyal employees doleful and anxious.","at":"在債務多年不斷累積之後，這家公司被迫進行清算，資產拍賣以償還債權人；這個下場長期被可疑的帳目所掩蓋，也讓數百名忠心的員工憂愁又焦慮。"},{"w":"nomadic","p":"adj.","d":"Roaming from place to place.","c":"遊牧的；流浪的","s":"The nomadic lifestyle that technology had made possible — working remotely from different countries for weeks or months at a time — created novel complications for tax authorities, social security systems, and pension administrators, none of which had been designed with the assumption that significant numbers of working-age adults would have no fixed country of residence.","t":"技術使之成為可能的遊牧式生活方式——每次在不同國家遠程工作數週或數月——為稅務機關、社會保障體系和養老金管理機構帶來了新的複雜性，這些機構都沒有基於大量工作年齡成年人沒有固定居住國的假設而設計。","as":"The nomadic herders of the Mongolian steppe move with the seasons, a way of life that demands resilience against inclement winters and that outsiders have often disparaged as rudimentary, though scholars perceive it as an astute adaptation to a harsh environment.","at":"蒙古草原上的遊牧民族隨季節遷徙，這種生活方式需要能抵禦嚴酷寒冬的韌性；外人常貶低它為原始落後，但學者則認為，這是對嚴苛環境的一種精明適應。"},{"w":"paragon","p":"n.","d":"A person regarded as perfect.","c":"模範；典範","s":"She had been presented throughout her career as a paragon of professional integrity, which made the revelation of her involvement in the pricing cartel doubly devastating — not merely damaging to her personally but deeply corrosive to public trust in the profession she had come to represent.","t":"她在整個職業生涯中一直被塑造為職業誠信的典範，這使得她參與定價卡特爾的揭露更加具有雙重毀滅性——不僅對她個人有損害，而且對她所代表的職業的公眾信任具有深深的腐蝕作用。","as":"The nurse came to be regarded as a paragon of mercy, tending to soldiers afflicted by disease with tireless dedication and offering solace to the dying despite the sordid conditions of the overcrowded military hospital.","at":"這位護理師被視為仁慈的典範，儘管人滿為患的軍醫院環境骯髒不堪，她仍不辭辛勞地照顧身染疾病的士兵，並為臨終者帶來慰藉。"},{"w":"persevere","p":"v.","d":"To continue despite difficulty.","c":"堅持不懈；不屈不撓","s":"The researcher persevered through seven years of largely negative experimental results, sustained by a theoretical conviction that the mechanism she was investigating existed even when the evidence consistently failed to confirm it, a persistence that was eventually vindicated by a series of breakthrough findings in the eighth year.","t":"這位研究人員在七年主要是負面的實驗結果中堅持不懈，靠著即使在證據一致未能確認時她所研究的機制仍然存在的理論信念支撐，這種堅持最終在第八年的一系列突破性發現中得到了驗證。","as":"Although her early experiments proved fruitless and skeptical colleagues scoffed at her hypothesis, the biochemist chose to persevere, and her research eventually yielded a viable method for producing the vaccine on a large scale.","at":"雖然她早期的實驗徒勞無功，抱持懷疑的同事也對她的假說嗤之以鼻，這位生化學家仍選擇堅持不懈，她的研究最終找到了一種可大規模生產疫苗的可行方法。"},{"w":"preclude","p":"v.","d":"To prevent or make impossible.","c":"排除；防止","s":"The existence of a prior contractual agreement between the two parties did not preclude the possibility of additional tort claims arising from the same set of circumstances, the judge ruled, as the damages sought under each legal theory were distinct in nature and non-duplicative in their practical effect.","t":"法官裁定，兩方之間先前存在的合同協議並不排除基於相同情況的額外侵權索賠的可能性，因為每種法律理論下尋求的損害賠償在性質上是不同的，在實際效果上是非重複的。","as":"The charred, fragile condition of the ancient scrolls seemed to preclude any attempt to read them, but scientists devised an ingenious imaging technique that let them peruse the text without unrolling the papyrus, a feat that eminent classicists had long considered anything but feasible.","at":"這些古代卷軸已經碳化且極為脆弱，看似不可能有人讀得了；但科學家設計出一種巧妙的影像技術，無須展開莎草紙就能細讀內容，知名古典學者長久以來都認為這是不可能辦到的壯舉。"},{"w":"recant","p":"v.","d":"To withdraw a previous statement.","c":"撤回(聲明)；放棄(信仰)","s":"Under sustained pressure from the ecclesiastical authorities, the astronomer was forced to publicly recant his heliocentric theory, acknowledging in a formal statement that the Earth was stationary at the centre of the universe — a humiliation that, according to contemporary accounts, he privately described as the most degrading experience of his scientific life.","t":"在教會當局的持續壓力下，這位天文學家被迫公開撤回他的日心說，在一份正式聲明中承認地球靜止地位於宇宙中心——根據同時代的記述，他私下描述這是他科學生涯中最具羞辱性的經歷。","as":"Faced with incontrovertible evidence that his data had been fabricated by a dishonest assistant, the eminent physicist chose to recant his celebrated findings, a frank admission that ultimately preserved his reputation for integrity.","at":"面對無可辯駁的證據，顯示他的數據遭一名不誠實的助理捏造，這位著名的物理學家選擇公開撤回自己備受讚譽的研究成果；這番坦率的認錯，最終保住了他正直的名聲。"}]},{"unit":16,"cards":[{"w":"altruistic","p":"adj.","d":"Showing unselfish concern for others.","c":"利他的；無私的","s":"Her decision to donate her entire research prize fund to the charitable foundation struck her colleagues as genuinely altruistic, though a few cynics privately argued that the accompanying publicity generated sufficient reputational benefit to qualify the gesture as a sophisticated form of enlightened self-interest rather than pure generosity.","t":"她決定將全部研究獎金捐給慈善基金會，讓她的同事覺得是真正無私的，儘管一些憤世嫉俗者私下認為，隨之而來的宣傳所產生的聲譽利益足以使這個姿態成為一種複雜形式的開明自利，而不是純粹的慷慨。","as":"Although skeptics often deride such gestures as mere pretexts for publicity, the altruistic surgeon spent her weekends treating indigent patients in a rural clinic, asking for no remuneration beyond the solace of knowing she had eased their suffering.","at":"雖然憤世嫉俗的人常譏諷這類舉動只是博取名聲的藉口，這位無私的外科醫師仍利用週末在鄉間診所為貧困病患看診，不求任何報酬，只求知道自己減輕了他們的痛苦所帶來的慰藉。"},{"w":"amorous","p":"adj.","d":"Showing sexual desire, relating to love.","c":"多情的；戀愛的","s":"The biographer approached the subject's amorous correspondence with considerable sensitivity, aware that several of the individuals involved were still living and that the letters contained disclosures that were both historically significant and potentially distressing to families who had not previously been aware of the relationships described.","t":"傳記作家以相當的敏感性處理傳主的情愛書信，意識到幾個相關人物仍然健在，這些信件包含了歷史上重要的披露，對於那些以前不知道所描述關係的家庭來說可能令人痛苦。","as":"The novel's early chapters chronicle the hero's amorous pursuit of a reticent young widow, but his flamboyant declarations of love only elicit her disdain, and the courtship becomes a poignant study of two mismatched temperaments.","at":"小說的前幾章描述男主角對一位沉默寡言的年輕寡婦展開熱烈追求，但他浮誇的示愛只換來她的鄙視，這段追求於是成為兩種格格不入性情的動人寫照。"},{"w":"antithesis","p":"n.","d":"The exact opposite of something.","c":"對立面；對照","s":"Everything about his leadership style was the antithesis of his predecessor's — where she had been consultative, he was directive; where she had valued consensus, he preferred unilateral decision-making; where she had been transparent about uncertainty, he projected an unwavering confidence that colleagues privately found unsettling.","t":"他的領導風格的一切都是他前任的對立面——她善於諮詢，他善於指導；她重視共識，他更喜歡單邊決策；她對不確定性保持透明，他則表現出一種同事私下覺得令人不安的堅定信心。","as":"To the meticulous scholars of the old academy, the brash, improvisational style of the young painters seemed the very antithesis of art, a flagrant rejection of the rudimentary rules of perspective that every aspirant had once been required to master.","at":"在老派學院一絲不苟的學者眼中，年輕畫家們莽撞即興的風格簡直是藝術的對立面，公然拋棄了每位有志習畫者過去都必須掌握的透視基本法則。"},{"w":"bulwark","p":"n.","d":"A defensive wall or protection.","c":"堡壘；保障","s":"The independent judiciary had historically served as the primary bulwark against executive overreach, but the systematic appointment of ideologically sympathetic judges to senior positions over the preceding decade had gradually eroded the institutional independence that gave that protective function its legitimacy and effectiveness.","t":"獨立的司法機構歷來是抵禦行政越權的主要堡壘，但在過去十年中對高級職位系統性地任命意識形態上有同情心的法官，逐漸侵蝕了賦予這一保護功能合法性和有效性的制度獨立性。","as":"For centuries the coastal wetlands served as a natural bulwark against inclement weather, absorbing storm surges that would otherwise inundate inland villages, but unchecked development has steadily curtailed their capacity to protect the communities behind them.","at":"數百年來，沿海濕地一直是抵禦惡劣天候的天然屏障，吸收原本會淹沒內陸村莊的暴潮；然而毫無節制的開發已逐漸削弱它們保護後方社區的能力。"},{"w":"cache","p":"n.","d":"A secret hiding place for storing things.","c":"隱藏處；儲藏物","s":"Investigators discovered a substantial cache of documents hidden beneath a false floor in the abandoned warehouse — correspondence, financial records, and internal memoranda spanning nearly a decade that provided comprehensive evidence of the conspiracy the prosecution had previously been able to establish only circumstantially.","t":"調查人員在廢棄倉庫的假地板下發現了大量文件——跨越近十年的書信、財務記錄和內部備忘錄，為檢察官以前只能間接建立的陰謀提供了全面的證據。","as":"While excavating a collapsed farmhouse, archaeologists discovered a cache of silver coins buried beneath the floor, a find that corroborates the conjecture that the family had surreptitiously hidden its wealth during a turbulent period of civil war.","at":"考古學家在挖掘一座倒塌的農舍時，於地板下發現一批埋藏的銀幣；這項發現證實了先前的推測：這戶人家曾在動盪的內戰時期偷偷藏匿財產。"},{"w":"coterie","p":"n.","d":"A small group sharing a common interest.","c":"小圈子；同夥","s":"The artistic movement had begun as an intimate coterie of perhaps twelve individuals meeting in a basement café, but its ideas had spread with extraordinary speed through a network of little magazines, public readings, and personal correspondence that connected sympathetic writers across three continents within a decade.","t":"這個藝術運動起初是一個大約十二人在地下室咖啡館聚會的親密小圈子，但它的思想通過小雜誌、公開朗誦和個人通信的網絡以非凡的速度傳播，在十年內將三大洲的志同道合的作家聯繫在一起。","as":"The poet shared her drafts only with a small coterie of trusted confidants, whose incisive yet amicable critiques helped her refine the verses that would later win her the most prestigious literary prize in the country.","at":"這位詩人只把草稿分享給一小群信任的知己；他們犀利卻友善的評論幫助她修飾詩句，而這些作品後來為她贏得了國內最具聲望的文學獎。"},{"w":"cupidity","p":"n.","d":"Greed for money or possessions.","c":"貪婪；貪財","s":"The financial regulator's report characterised the behaviour of the bank's senior management as driven primarily by cupidity, documenting a systematic pattern of prioritising short-term bonus structures over sound risk management, customer interests, and long-term institutional sustainability.","t":"金融監管機構的報告將銀行高管的行為描述為主要由貪婪驅動，記錄了一種系統性的模式，即將短期獎金結構置於健全的風險管理、客戶利益和長期機構可持續性之上。","as":"Investigators concluded that the bank's collapse stemmed not from misfortune but from the cupidity of its executives, whose voracious appetite for bonuses led them to approve egregious loans and conceal the resulting losses through elaborate duplicity.","at":"調查人員認定，這家銀行的倒閉並非出於不幸，而是源於高層主管的貪婪：他們對獎金貪得無厭，因而核准了離譜的貸款，再用精心設計的欺瞞手段掩蓋隨之而來的虧損。"},{"w":"cursory","p":"adj.","d":"Hasty and superficial.","c":"粗略的；草率的","s":"A cursory reading of the contract might suggest that the indemnification clause was standard boilerplate, but careful analysis revealed that its scope had been subtly modified in a way that transferred a significant portion of the commercial risk from the vendor to the purchaser without this shift being reflected elsewhere in the pricing structure.","t":"粗略地閱讀合同可能會讓人認為賠償條款是標準樣板，但仔細分析揭示，其範圍已被微妙地修改，以一種沒有在定價結構的其他地方反映這種轉變的方式，將很大一部分商業風險從賣方轉移到了買方。","as":"A cursory glance at the data might suggest that the new drug is effective, but a comprehensive analysis reveals that its alleged benefits are dubious and that the most salient side effects were quietly omitted from the published summary.","at":"粗略瀏覽數據，或許會以為這種新藥有效；但全面分析後會發現，它所宣稱的療效十分可疑，而且最顯著的副作用竟被悄悄地從公開的摘要中刪去。"},{"w":"embellish","p":"v.","d":"To make more attractive by decoration.","c":"裝飾；潤飾","s":"The memoir had clearly been embellished to enhance its dramatic appeal, with the author inserting himself into several historically documented events at which he could not possibly have been present and attributing to senior political figures statements that bore no relationship to any recorded utterance.","t":"這本回憶錄顯然被潤飾以增強其戲劇吸引力，作者將自己插入了幾個他不可能出現的有歷史記錄的事件中，並向高層政治人物歸因了與任何記錄的言論毫無關係的陳述。","as":"Medieval chroniclers often embellished the annals of their kings with invented miracles and heroic battles, so modern historians must scrutinize such accounts with care in order to discern which details are factual and which are mere flattery.","at":"中世紀的編年史家常以虛構的神蹟與英勇戰役來潤飾國王的史冊，因此現代史學家必須仔細審視這些記載，才能分辨哪些細節屬實、哪些只是阿諛奉承。"},{"w":"frugal","p":"adj.","d":"Sparing with money or food, thrifty.","c":"節儉的；樸素的","s":"Despite accumulating considerable wealth over a forty-year career, she remained notably frugal in her personal lifestyle, driving an unremarkable ten-year-old vehicle, living in the modest house she had purchased decades before her financial success, and consistently declining the premium service upgrades her assistant automatically booked for her.","t":"儘管在四十年的職業生涯中積累了相當的財富，她的個人生活方式仍然明顯節儉，開著一輛普通的十年舊車，住在她在財務成功幾十年前購買的樸素房子裡，並一貫拒絕她的助理自動為她預訂的高級服務升級。","as":"Having grown up in an era of severe privation, the frugal grandmother saved every scrap of fabric and string, a habit her affluent grandchildren found puzzling but one that had allowed her to amass a modest fortune by the time she became an octogenarian.","at":"在物資極度匱乏的年代長大，這位節儉的祖母連一小塊布、一段繩子都捨不得丟；她富裕的孫輩對這個習慣感到不解，但正是這份節儉讓她在八十多歲時已累積了一筆可觀的積蓄。"},{"w":"gregarious","p":"adj.","d":"Fond of company, sociable.","c":"群居的；社交的","s":"Her gregarious nature made her exceptionally effective as a fundraiser, her genuine interest in people from all backgrounds enabling her to establish authentic connections at events ranging from intimate donor dinners to large public galas with equal ease and equally convincing warmth.","t":"她的社交天性使她在募款方面非常有效，她對各種背景人士的真誠興趣使她能夠在從親密的捐助者晚宴到大型公開晚會等各種活動中，以同樣的輕鬆和同樣令人信服的熱情建立真實的聯繫。","as":"Unlike their solitary relatives, gregarious birds such as starlings gather in vast throngs whose synchronized movements, scientists surmise, help the flock remain vigilant against predators that would otherwise single out a weak or isolated individual.","at":"與習性孤僻的近親不同，椋鳥等群居鳥類會聚集成龐大的鳥群；科學家推測，牠們同步的飛行動作有助於整個鳥群對掠食者保持警覺，否則掠食者便會鎖定落單或虛弱的個體下手。"},{"w":"habitat","p":"n.","d":"The natural environment of an organism.","c":"棲息地；產地","s":"The conservation report concluded that the fragmentation of previously continuous forest into isolated patches had proved more damaging to biodiversity than the total area of habitat lost, because many species required unbroken connectivity between territories to maintain the gene flow essential for long-term population viability.","t":"保護報告得出結論，以前連續的森林碎片化成孤立的地塊，對生物多樣性的損害比失去的棲息地總面積更大，因為許多物種需要領地之間不間斷的連通性，以維持對長期種群生存能力至關重要的基因流動。","as":"As logging and mining continue to raze vast stretches of rainforest, the habitat of countless species is shrinking at an alarming rate, and conservationists warn that the havoc wrought by such development may soon jeopardize creatures found nowhere else on Earth.","at":"隨著伐木與採礦持續夷平大片雨林，無數物種的棲息地正以驚人的速度縮減；保育人士警告，這類開發所造成的浩劫，可能很快就會危及地球上其他地方都找不到的生物。"},{"w":"indigenous","p":"adj.","d":"Originating naturally in a region.","c":"本土的；土生土長的","s":"The legal framework protecting indigenous land rights had been systematically weakened over four decades of legislative amendments, each individually characterised as minor administrative adjustments but cumulatively constituting a fundamental erosion of the original treaty obligations that had been entered into with considerably more generous intent.","t":"保護本土土地權利的法律框架在四十年的立法修正案中被系統性地削弱，每一個單獨被描述為輕微的行政調整，但累積起來構成了對原始條約義務的根本侵蝕，而這些義務最初是以更為慷慨的意圖締結的。","as":"Colonial administrators sought to subjugate the indigenous peoples of the region by outlawing their languages, yet these communities persevered, preserving their songs and rituals in clandestine gatherings that the authorities never managed to suppress.","at":"殖民官員企圖透過禁止當地原住民族使用母語來征服他們，然而這些族群堅持不懈，在當局始終無法壓制的祕密聚會中保存了自己的歌謠與儀式。"},{"w":"interloper","p":"n.","d":"A person who intrudes without permission.","c":"闖入者；干涉者","s":"The established gallery network initially treated the new online auction platforms as interloper s threatening to disrupt an ecosystem they had carefully cultivated over decades, before gradually recognising that the digital channels were expanding the collector base rather than simply redirecting existing demand through alternative channels.","t":"老牌畫廊網絡最初將新的在線拍賣平台視為威脅破壞他們數十年精心培育的生態系統的闖入者，然後逐漸認識到數字渠道正在擴大收藏家基礎，而不僅僅是通過替代渠道重新引導現有需求。","as":"The established merchants regarded the foreign trader as an interloper in their profitable market and sought to oust him, spreading scurrilous rumors about the quality of his goods and badgering local officials to revoke his license.","at":"老字號商人將這名外國商人視為闖入他們有利可圖之市場的不速之客，處心積慮想把他趕走：他們散布有關其貨品品質的惡毒謠言，並不斷糾纏地方官員撤銷他的執照。"},{"w":"progeny","p":"n.","d":"A person's descendants or offspring.","c":"後代；子孫","s":"The geneticist's research traced the progeny of the original colony through seventeen generations, documenting the progressive divergence of physiological characteristics that had occurred as different sub-populations adapted to the distinct micro-environments within the archipelago over a period spanning approximately four hundred years.","t":"遺傳學家的研究通過十七代追蹤了原始群落的後代，記錄了生理特徵的漸進分化，這些分化是在大約四百年間，不同子種群適應群島內不同微環境時發生的。","as":"The aging emperor, obsessed with securing his dynasty, showered his progeny with titles and estates, but the fractious rivalry among his many sons precipitated a schism that tore the empire apart soon after his death.","at":"年邁的皇帝一心想鞏固王朝，便將頭銜與領地大量賞賜給子孫；然而眾多皇子之間爭執不休的明爭暗鬥，卻在他死後不久引發分裂，使帝國四分五裂。"},{"w":"prolific","p":"adj.","d":"Producing many works or offspring.","c":"多產的；高產的","s":"The prolific novelist published an average of three books per year for nearly four decades, a rate of output that her critics attributed to a willingness to sacrifice depth for productivity but which her supporters argued reflected an extraordinary creative discipline and an inexhaustible imaginative reservoir.","t":"這位多產的小說家在近四十年間平均每年出版三本書，這種產出速度被她的批評者歸因於願意犧牲深度換取生產力，但她的支持者認為這反映了非凡的創作紀律和取之不盡的想象力儲備。","as":"Despite being remarkably prolific, the composer was never indiscriminate about what he released, discarding any piece he found lackluster and laboring over each symphony with a devotion that astonished even his most eminent contemporaries.","at":"這位作曲家雖然創作量驚人，對發表的作品卻從不隨便：凡是他覺得平淡無奇的曲子一律捨棄，並對每一首交響曲投注心血，那份執著連同時代最傑出的音樂家都為之驚嘆。"},{"w":"saturate","p":"v.","d":"To fill completely, soak thoroughly.","c":"浸透；使飽和","s":"The market had become so saturated with streaming services that subscriber acquisition costs had risen to levels that made profitability essentially impossible for any new entrant, effectively creating the conditions for a consolidation phase that industry analysts had been predicting for several years.","t":"市場已被流媒體服務如此飽和，以至於訂戶獲取成本已上升到使任何新進入者基本上不可能盈利的水平，有效地為行業分析師預測了幾年的整合階段創造了條件。","as":"Weeks of heavy rain had so thoroughly saturated the hillside that the soil could absorb no more water, and after an ominous rumbling was heard one night, geologists warned that a landslide was imminent and urged residents below to evacuate forthwith.","at":"連續數週的豪雨使山坡完全浸透，土壤再也吸不了任何水分；某天夜裡傳出不祥的隆隆聲後，地質學家警告山崩迫在眉睫，並敦促山下居民立即撤離。"},{"w":"sedentary","p":"adj.","d":"Tending to sit or remain inactive.","c":"久坐的；定棲的","s":"Public health research consistently demonstrated a direct correlation between sedentary occupations and elevated rates of cardiovascular disease, metabolic disorders, and musculoskeletal conditions, findings that had prompted numerous employers to introduce standing desk programmes and mandatory movement breaks into the working day.","t":"公共衛生研究一致表明久坐職業與心血管疾病、代謝紊亂和肌肉骨骼疾病率升高之間存在直接相關性，這些發現促使眾多雇主在工作日引入站立辦公桌計劃和強制性活動休息。","as":"Because a sedentary lifestyle can exacerbate heart disease and a host of other maladies, physicians now admonish office workers to interrupt long hours at their desks with brief walks, a simple habit that may obviate the need for medication later in life.","at":"由於久坐不動的生活型態會加重心臟病及其他多種疾病，醫師如今告誡上班族要在長時間伏案工作之間穿插短暫散步；這個簡單的習慣，或許能讓人日後免於服藥。"},{"w":"temerity","p":"n.","d":"Excessive confidence, reckless boldness.","c":"魯莽；冒失","s":"He had the temerity to challenge the methodology of the Nobel laureate's foundational paper during the open question session of the conference, a moment of astonishing intellectual confidence that the assembled researchers found simultaneously admirable and mortifying depending on whether they considered his critique valid.","t":"他有魯莽地在會議的公開問答環節挑戰這位諾貝爾獎得主的基礎論文的方法論，這一令人驚嘆的智識自信時刻讓在場的研究人員根據他們是否認為他的批評有效而同時感到欽佩和難堪。","as":"The junior officer had the temerity to castigate the general in front of his entire entourage, an act of insubordination so blatant that the onlookers fell silent and the young man nearly lost his commission.","at":"這名資淺軍官竟膽敢當著將軍所有隨從的面嚴厲斥責他，如此明目張膽的抗命行為令在場眾人鴉雀無聲，這位年輕人也險些因此丟了官職。"},{"w":"virtuosity","p":"n.","d":"Technical skill of the highest level.","c":"精湛技藝","s":"The conductor's virtuosity extended far beyond his celebrated ability to communicate interpretative nuance to orchestras — he possessed an equally formidable technical memory, able to conduct all the major symphonic and operatic repertoire entirely from memory without a single score in front of him.","t":"指揮家的精湛技藝遠不止他向管弦樂團傳達詮釋細微之處的著名能力——他還擁有同樣令人生畏的技術記憶，能夠完全從記憶中指揮所有主要的交響樂和歌劇曲目，面前沒有一份樂譜。","as":"The pianist's virtuosity transformed études that most students regard as tedious drudgery into richly nuanced performances, her fingers scurrying across the keys with such adroit precision that even the most incredulous critics were won over.","at":"這位鋼琴家精湛的技藝，將多數學生視為枯燥苦差事的練習曲化為細膩豐富的演出；她的手指以靈巧精準的動作在琴鍵上飛奔，連最抱持懷疑的樂評家都被折服。"}]},{"unit":17,"cards":[{"w":"assiduous","p":"adj.","d":"Showing great care and effort.","c":"勤勉的；刻苦的","s":"The assiduous researcher spent twelve years in the archives, working through seventeen thousand documents in three languages to establish a historical narrative that could withstand the most rigorous scholarly scrutiny — a commitment to thoroughness that reviewers universally acknowledged when the resulting monograph was published.","t":"這位勤勉的研究人員在檔案館度過了十二年，用三種語言研究了一萬七千份文件，以建立一個能夠承受最嚴格學術審查的歷史敘述——當由此產生的專著出版時，評審員普遍承認了這種對徹底性的承諾。","as":"Through assiduous study of faded manuscripts, the young scholar managed to decipher the cryptic notes of a medieval astronomer, whose incontrovertible observations of planetary motion had been overlooked for centuries by historians who gave the documents only a cursory reading.","at":"這位年輕學者孜孜不倦地研讀褪色的手稿，終於解讀出一位中世紀天文學家晦澀難懂的筆記；這些關於行星運行、無可辯駁的觀測紀錄，數百年來一直被只草草翻閱文件的史學家所忽略。"},{"w":"attest","p":"v.","d":"To declare or certify as true.","c":"證明；證實","s":"The independent auditors attest ed to the accuracy of the financial statements, but their sign-off was subsequently revealed to have been based on documentation that the company's management had knowingly falsified — a revelation that triggered both criminal proceedings and a fundamental review of audit independence standards.","t":"獨立審計師證明了財務報表的準確性，但他們的簽字後來被披露是基於公司管理層明知是偽造的文件——這一揭露觸發了刑事訴訟和對審計獨立標準的根本審查。","as":"Dozens of letters written by ordinary soldiers attest to the excruciating hardships of the winter campaign, describing emaciated men who froze in their tents while a fretful commander waited in vain for supplies that never arrived.","at":"數十封由普通士兵寫下的家書，證實了那場冬季戰役中令人痛苦不堪的艱辛：信中描述骨瘦如柴的士兵在帳篷裡受凍，而焦躁不安的指揮官則徒然等待著始終沒有送達的補給。"},{"w":"component","p":"n.","d":"A part or element of a larger whole.","c":"零件；成分","s":"Each component of the complex rehabilitation programme had been designed to address a specific aspect of recovery — physical therapy for mobility restoration, occupational therapy for daily living skills, neuropsychological support for cognitive sequelae, and social work intervention for reintegration into community and employment.","t":"這個複雜康復計劃的每個組成部分都被設計來解決康復的特定方面——用於恢復活動能力的物理治療、用於日常生活技能的職業治療、用於認知後遺症的神經心理支持，以及用於重新融入社區和就業的社會工作干預。","as":"Every component of a coral reef ecosystem is integral to its survival, so when rising ocean temperatures cause even sporadic die-offs of a single species of algae, the effects can permeate the entire food web with startling speed.","at":"珊瑚礁生態系的每一個組成部分對其存續都不可或缺；因此，當海水升溫導致即使只是某一種藻類零星死亡時，其影響也可能以驚人的速度擴散到整個食物網。"},{"w":"concoct","p":"v.","d":"To devise or invent a story.","c":"捏造；調製","s":"The elaborate alibi that the suspect had concoct ed over several days of interrogation unravelled completely when investigators established that the restaurant he claimed to have visited on the relevant evening had been closed for renovation since the previous month.","t":"嫌疑人在幾天審訊中精心捏造的不在場證明，在調查人員確認他聲稱在相關當晚光顧的餐廳自上個月以來一直因裝修而關閉時，完全崩潰了。","as":"Hoping to evade punishment, the culprit concocted an elaborate alibi involving a fictitious business trip, but astute detectives soon noticed inconsistencies in his story and located witnesses whose testimony he could not repudiate.","at":"為了逃避懲罰，犯人捏造了一套精心設計的不在場證明，聲稱自己正在進行一趟子虛烏有的出差；但精明的警探很快就察覺他說詞前後矛盾，並找到了他無法否認其證詞的目擊者。"},{"w":"consummate","p":"adj.","d":"Showing great skill, complete.","c":"圓滿的；技藝高超的","s":"The negotiation was handled with consummate skill by the mediator, who managed to guide both parties from entrenched positions to a mutually acceptable settlement in less than three days — an achievement that all participants described as remarkable given the depth of the animosity that had existed between the organisations.","t":"這次談判由調解員以精湛的技巧處理，他設法在不到三天的時間內引導雙方從頑固立場走向相互接受的解決方案——考慮到組織之間存在的深刻敵意，所有參與者都認為這一成就非凡。","as":"A consummate diplomat, the ambassador managed to quell the acrimonious dispute between the two neighboring nations, patiently cajoling leaders who had long loathed one another into signing a treaty that brought lasting peace to the region.","at":"這位大使是技巧純熟的外交家，他成功平息了兩個鄰國之間激烈尖刻的爭端，耐心地哄勸彼此長期厭惡的領袖簽下條約，為該地區帶來數十年的和平。"},{"w":"deploy","p":"v.","d":"To position strategically for use.","c":"部署；展開","s":"The emergency management agency deploy ed specialised search and rescue teams to three separate locations simultaneously, coordinating their activities through a central operations room that maintained continuous radio contact and directed resources dynamically in response to developing information about survivor locations.","t":"緊急管理局同時在三個不同地點部署了專業搜救隊，通過一個中央作戰室協調他們的活動，該作戰室保持持續的無線電聯繫，並根據關於倖存者位置的不斷發展的信息動態指導資源。","as":"When the volcano began to spew ash and toxic gases, the government deployed troops to evacuate nearby towns, though many residents were loath to abandon their homes until soldiers convinced them that the volcano posed a lethal threat.","at":"當火山開始噴出火山灰與有毒氣體時，政府部署軍隊疏散附近城鎮；然而許多居民不願離開家園，直到士兵說服他們這次噴發會帶來致命威脅，他們才肯撤離。"},{"w":"enigma","p":"n.","d":"A puzzling or mysterious person or thing.","c":"謎；難以理解的事物","s":"The composer remained an enigma to those closest to her throughout her life — deliberately cultivating uncertainty about her personal history, consistently refusing biographical interviews, and choosing to communicate almost exclusively through music in a way that made her private self permanently inaccessible to even her most dedicated admirers.","t":"這位作曲家在她的一生中對最親近她的人來說仍然是個謎——故意對她的個人歷史製造不確定性，一貫拒絕傳記採訪，並選擇幾乎完全通過音樂交流，以一種使她的私人自我對即使是她最忠誠的崇拜者也永久無法接近的方式。","as":"For generations the purpose of the massive stone circle remained an enigma, and scholars proposed wildly incongruous theories, some calling it an astronomical calendar and others a sanctuary where priests sought to link the earthly realm with the heavens.","at":"好幾個世代以來，這座巨大石圈的用途始終是個謎；學者們提出了南轅北轍的理論，有人認為它是天文曆法，也有人認為它是祭司試圖連結人間與天界的聖所。"},{"w":"evaluate","p":"v.","d":"To assess the value or importance of.","c":"評估；評價","s":"The committee was asked to evaluate the competing proposals against six weighted criteria — technical feasibility, cost-effectiveness, environmental impact, implementation timeline, community benefit, and alignment with long-term strategic objectives — and to present a ranked recommendation with supporting rationale within sixty days.","t":"委員會被要求根據六個加權標準——技術可行性、成本效益、環境影響、實施時間表、社區效益和與長期戰略目標的一致性——評估競爭性提案，並在六十天內提交帶有支持理由的排名建議。","as":"Before approving a new vaccine, regulators must carefully evaluate whether its benefits outweigh its risks, a process that requires them to peruse thousands of pages of trial data and weigh every pertinent finding against the possibility of adverse reactions.","at":"在核准新疫苗之前，主管機關必須審慎評估其效益是否大於風險；這個過程需要他們詳讀數千頁的試驗數據，並將每一項相關發現與可能產生的不良反應仔細權衡。"},{"w":"exult","p":"v.","d":"To be joyfully triumphant.","c":"歡欣鼓舞；狂喜","s":"The team exult ed with undisguised emotion when the final result was confirmed — players embracing, staff weeping openly, and supporters in the stands creating the kind of collective noise that those present would recall as one of the most viscerally powerful moments of their sporting lives.","t":"當最終結果確認時，球隊毫不掩飾地狂喜慶祝——球員互相擁抱，工作人員公開哭泣，看台上的支持者製造出那種在場者將其回憶為他們體育生涯中最發自內心的強大時刻之一的集體噪音。","as":"Reporters exulted when parliament finally abrogated the law that had fettered the press for generations, though veteran editors cautioned that the government could still find subtler ways to harass journalists who criticized its policies.","at":"國會終於廢除了箝制新聞界數十年的法律，記者們為此歡欣鼓舞；不過資深編輯提醒，政府仍可能找到更隱晦的方式，騷擾批評其政策的記者。"},{"w":"fallacious","p":"adj.","d":"Based on a false belief, misleading.","c":"謬誤的；欺騙性的","s":"The committee's report identified several fallacious assumptions underlying the original policy design — most significantly the belief that market forces alone would generate sufficient affordable housing in high-demand urban areas — and recommended a fundamental rethinking of the regulatory framework rather than incremental adjustments to a fundamentally flawed model.","t":"委員會的報告確定了原始政策設計背後的幾個謬誤假設——最重要的是相信市場力量單獨就能在高需求城市地區產生足夠的可負擔住房——並建議對監管框架進行根本性的重新思考，而不是對根本上有缺陷的模型進行漸進式調整。","as":"The candidate's argument was fallacious, resting on the unfounded premise that recent immigrants were culpable for rising crime, a stereotype that the city's own statistics consistently failed to support in any meaningful way.","at":"這位候選人的論點是錯誤的，因為它建立在一個毫無根據的前提上：認為新移民應為犯罪率上升負責；然而這種刻板印象，始終無法從該市自身的統計數據中得到任何實質支持。"},{"w":"fraught","p":"adj.","d":"Filled with, causing anxiety.","c":"充滿的；令人憂慮的","s":"The discovery phase of the litigation proved particularly fraught for the defendant corporation, as the compelled disclosure of internal communications revealed a pattern of deliberate concealment that was substantially more damaging than the original allegations and prompted the company's legal team to recommend an immediate settlement.","t":"訴訟的發現階段對被告公司來說特別令人憂慮，因為被迫披露的內部通信揭示了一種蓄意隱瞞的模式，這比最初的指控實質上更具破壞性，並促使公司的法律團隊建議立即和解。","as":"The journey across the frozen plateau was fraught with peril, and the intrepid explorers, besieged by blizzards and afflicted with frostbite, found no respite until a rescue party finally reached their battered tents.","at":"橫越冰封高原的旅程危機四伏；這群無畏的探險家被暴風雪重重圍困，又飽受凍傷之苦，直到救援隊終於抵達他們殘破的帳篷，才得以喘息。"},{"w":"gullible","p":"adj.","d":"Easily persuaded to believe something.","c":"易受騙的；輕信的","s":"The fraud had specifically targeted elderly individuals whom the perpetrators had characterised internally as gullible — not because they were mentally diminished but because their generation had been socialised to trust authority figures and to extend goodwill to people who presented themselves as helpful professionals.","t":"這種欺詐專門針對犯罪者內部描述為容易受騙的老年人——不是因為他們在智力上有所降低，而是因為他們那一代人被社會化為信任權威人物，並向那些以有幫助的專業人士身份出現的人伸出善意之手。","as":"Online swindlers deliberately seek out gullible users, sending urgent messages that importune them to share their passwords under some plausible pretext, and the hapless victims who comply often lose their savings before realizing they have been duped.","at":"網路詐騙集團專門鎖定容易受騙的使用者，發送緊急訊息、以看似合理的藉口一再要求他們提供密碼；那些照做的不幸受害者，往往在發現自己被騙之前就已失去積蓄。"},{"w":"hoax","p":"n.","d":"A deceptive trick or false story.","c":"騙局；惡作劇","s":"The elaborate hoax had fooled experts for eleven years before a combination of improved analytical techniques and a chance examination of previously unavailable archival records established beyond reasonable doubt that the document was a skilled forgery produced in the early twentieth century rather than the medieval manuscript it purported to be.","t":"這個精心設計的騙局在十一年內欺騙了專家，直到改進的分析技術與對以前無法獲得的檔案記錄的偶然檢查相結合，在合理懷疑之外確認了該文件是二十世紀初製作的熟練偽造品，而不是它聲稱的中世紀手稿。","as":"The famous photograph of the lake monster was finally exposed as a hoax when an elderly man recanted his long-standing denials and confessed his complicity in the scheme, admitting that the elusive creature was merely a toy submarine fitted with a carved wooden head.","at":"那張著名的湖怪照片最終被揭穿是一場騙局：一位老人推翻了自己長年的否認，坦承參與了這項計謀，並承認那隻難以捉摸的怪物其實只是一艘裝上木雕頭部的玩具潛水艇。"},{"w":"impeccable","p":"adj.","d":"In accordance with the highest standards.","c":"無懈可擊的；無缺點的","s":"Her impeccable professional reputation made the allegations doubly shocking — not merely because they were serious in themselves but because they seemed so fundamentally inconsistent with every aspect of the character that forty years of colleagues, students, and institutional partners had directly observed and consistently praised.","t":"她無懈可擊的職業聲譽使這些指控更加令人震驚——不僅因為它們本身嚴重，而且因為它們似乎與四十年來同事、學生和機構合作夥伴直接觀察到並一貫讚揚的性格的每個方面根本上不一致。","as":"Although the forger's technique was impeccable, chemical analysis revealed that the pigments in the alleged Renaissance masterpiece were modern, a discovery that invalidated the painting's attribution, much to the chagrin of the collector who had bought it.","at":"儘管偽造者的技法無懈可擊，化學分析卻顯示這幅號稱文藝復興傑作的畫中所用顏料是現代產物；這項發現推翻了該畫的作者歸屬，令買下它的收藏家懊惱不已。"},{"w":"labyrinth","p":"n.","d":"A complicated network of paths.","c":"迷宮；錯綜複雜的事物","s":"Navigating the regulatory labyrinth required by the approval process had consumed nearly two years and several hundred thousand dollars in legal and consulting fees before the company could begin actual product development — a barrier to entry that effectively advantaged established players with dedicated regulatory affairs departments over innovative newcomers.","t":"獲得批准過程所需的監管迷宮讓公司消耗了近兩年時間和幾十萬美元的法律和諮詢費用，然後才能開始實際的產品開發——這一進入壁壘有效地使擁有專門監管事務部門的老牌企業相對於創新新來者佔有優勢。","as":"Beneath the old city lies a subterranean labyrinth of tunnels so convoluted that early explorers who rashly entered without maps often lost their way, and local legends abound with tales of hapless travelers who never emerged.","at":"古城地底下有一座地下隧道迷宮，錯綜複雜到早期貿然不帶地圖便進入的探險者經常迷路；當地流傳著許多倒楣旅人一去不返的傳說。"},{"w":"manifold","p":"adj.","d":"Many and various, multiple.","c":"多種多樣的；繁多的","s":"The manifold consequences of the policy change extended far beyond the direct economic impact on affected workers, encompassing effects on local tax revenues, social service demand, housing markets, mental health outcomes, and community cohesion that collectively represented a transformation in the social fabric of the affected regions.","t":"政策變化的多種多樣的後果遠遠超出了對受影響工人的直接經濟影響，涵蓋了對地方稅收、社會服務需求、住房市場、心理健康結果和社區凝聚力的影響，這些共同代表了受影響地區社會結構的轉變。","as":"The advantages of bilingual education are manifold: research suggests that students who master two languages not only enhance their cognitive flexibility but also become more cognizant of cultural nuances that their monolingual peers may overlook.","at":"雙語教育的好處多不勝數：研究顯示，精通兩種語言的學生不僅能提升思維的靈活度，也會更能察覺單語同儕可能忽略的文化細微差異。"},{"w":"murky","p":"adj.","d":"Dark and gloomy, not clear.","c":"昏暗的；陰晦的","s":"The provenance of the artwork remained deeply murkyedespite extensive research, with gaps in the documented ownership chain corresponding precisely to the years of the Nazi occupation — an absence of records that, according to the restitution claims committee, was itself sufficient to create a rebuttable presumption of unlawful appropriation.","t":"儘管進行了廣泛的研究，這件藝術品的來源仍然非常不清楚，有記錄的所有權鏈中的空白恰好對應於納粹佔領的年份——根據歸還索賠委員會的說法，這種記錄缺失本身就足以產生可反駁的非法侵吞推定。","as":"Divers searching for the sunken galleon could barely see through the murky water of the estuary, where pernicious industrial runoff had settled into the silt, and they were forced to curtail each dive before sinister currents could sweep them out to sea.","at":"搜尋沉沒大帆船的潛水員在河口混濁的水中幾乎什麼也看不見，那裡有害的工業廢水早已沉積在淤泥中；他們每次下潛都不得不縮短時間，以免被險惡的暗流捲入大海。"},{"w":"perpetrate","p":"v.","d":"To commit a harmful act.","c":"犯(罪)；做(壞事)","s":"Those who perpetrated financial crimes against elderly victims were subject to enhanced sentencing guidelines under the revised legislation, reflecting the legislature's determination that the deliberate exploitation of vulnerable populations warranted more severe punishment than equivalent offences committed against individuals not in protected categories.","t":"根據修訂後的法律，對老年受害者實施金融犯罪的人受到加強量刑指南的約束，這反映了立法機構的決心，即故意剝削弱勢群體比針對不在保護類別中的個人的同等犯罪行為應受到更嚴重的懲罰。","as":"Undeterred by repeated attempts to intimidate their sources, zealous reporters spent years gathering evidence against the officials who had perpetrated the fraud, finally ending the impunity those officials had enjoyed for so long.","at":"儘管消息來源一再遭到恐嚇，熱忱的記者仍不為所動，花了數年蒐集證據揭發犯下這起詐欺案的官員，終於終結了這些官員長久以來逍遙法外的局面。"},{"w":"resourceful","p":"adj.","d":"Having the ability to find solutions.","c":"足智多謀的；機智的","s":"The expedition's survival over seventy-two days in one of the world's most hostile environments testified less to physical endurance than to the resourceful leadership of the team's most experienced member, whose ability to improvise solutions to successive crises using only the materials available became the subject of a celebrated survival manual.","t":"探險隊在世界上最惡劣的環境之一中生存了七十二天，與其說是體力耐力，不如說是團隊最有經驗的成員的足智多謀的領導力，他只利用現有材料即興解決連續危機的能力成為一本著名的生存手冊的主題。","as":"Stranded on a barren island after their ship ran aground, the resourceful crew salvaged canvas and timber from the wreck, built a shelter sturdy enough to repulse the fierce winds, and rationed their food so carefully that no one succumbed to malnutrition.","at":"船隻擱淺後受困於荒島，足智多謀的船員們從殘骸中搶救出帆布與木材，搭建出足以抵擋強風的庇護所，並謹慎地分配糧食，使得沒有任何人因營養不良而倒下。"},{"w":"subterfuge","p":"n.","d":"Deception to achieve a goal.","c":"詭計；遁詞","s":"The corporate espionage operation had relied on subterfuge rather than technical intrusion — specifically, the systematic placement of individuals in junior administrative roles within target organisations, where they had legitimate access to documents whose significance they could not individually assess but which, collectively, constituted a comprehensive picture of competitive strategy.","t":"企業間諜活動依賴於詭計而非技術入侵——具體來說，是系統性地在目標組織的初級行政崗位安插個人，在那裡他們有合法的文件訪問權限，這些文件他們無法單獨評估其重要性，但集體構成了競爭策略的全面圖景。","as":"Stymied by the embassy's tight security, the spy resorted to subterfuge, posing as a cleaner so that she could furtively photograph classified files while guards, lulled by the mundane rhythm of her nightly routine, paid her no attention.","at":"受阻於大使館的嚴密保全，這名間諜只好使出詭計，假扮成清潔工，以便偷偷拍攝機密文件；而警衛們早已被她每晚平凡單調的例行工作麻痺，完全沒有注意她。"}]},{"unit":18,"cards":[{"w":"abortive","p":"adj.","d":"Failing to produce the intended result.","c":"失敗的；夭折的","s":"Three abortive attempts to negotiate a ceasefire had preceded the current initiative, each collapsing within weeks of announcement as one or both parties withdrew from commitments they had made under conditions that subsequent events had rendered politically untenable in their respective domestic contexts.","t":"在當前的倡議之前，三次談判停火的失敗嘗試已經發生，每次都在宣布後幾週內崩潰，因為一方或雙方撤回了他們在條件下做出的承諾，隨後的事件使這些條件在各自的國內環境中在政治上站不住腳。","as":"The rebels' abortive attempt to seize the capital ended in a fiasco after an accomplice betrayed their plans to the palace, and the government then used the failed uprising as a pretext to repress all political opposition for years.","at":"叛軍企圖奪取首都的行動以失敗告終，成了一場鬧劇，原因是一名共犯向王宮洩漏了他們的計畫；政府隨後便以這次失敗的起事為藉口，多年來壓制一切政治異議。"},{"w":"accommodate","p":"v.","d":"To make fit, to provide for.","c":"容納；適應","s":"The venue had been specifically redesigned to accommodate the needs of performers and audiences with disabilities, incorporating accessible backstage facilities, hearing loop systems throughout the auditorium, tactile programming guides, and reserved seating areas positioned to provide optimal sightlines for wheelchair users.","t":"場地已被專門重新設計以容納殘疾表演者和觀眾的需求，在整個禮堂內置入無障礙後台設施、聽力環路系統、觸覺節目指南，以及為輪椅使用者提供最佳視線的預留座位區。","as":"To accommodate the refugees fleeing the besieged city, the small town converted its schools and churches into temporary shelters, an altruistic gesture that won national acclaim even as the strain on local resources began to nettle some residents.","at":"為了收容從被圍困城市逃出的難民，這座小鎮把學校與教堂改建為臨時收容所；這項無私之舉贏得全國讚譽，儘管當地資源吃緊也開始讓部分居民感到不滿。"},{"w":"barometer","p":"n.","d":"An instrument or indicator of change.","c":"晴雨表；氣壓計","s":"Consumer confidence surveys have traditionally served as a reliable barometer of economic conditions, but recent research suggests that the relationship between reported sentiment and actual spending behaviour has weakened considerably, possibly because respondents have learned to provide politically influenced answers rather than honest assessments of their personal financial situations.","t":"消費者信心調查傳統上作為經濟狀況的可靠晴雨表，但最近的研究表明，報告的情緒與實際支出行為之間的關係已大大削弱，可能是因為受訪者已學會提供受政治影響的答案，而不是對他們個人財務狀況的誠實評估。","as":"Economists often treat consumer spending as a barometer of public confidence, since households of nearly every income level tend to curtail their purchases as soon as they perceive ominous signs of an economic downturn.","at":"經濟學家常把消費支出視為民眾信心的晴雨表，因為幾乎各種收入階層的家庭，一察覺到經濟衰退的不祥徵兆，往往就會減少消費。"},{"w":"buff","p":"n.","d":"An enthusiastic fan or expert.","c":"愛好者；迷","s":"The symposium attracted an eclectic mix of academic historians, professional archivists, and dedicated buff s whose extensive personal research had in several cases surpassed the depth of specialist scholarship — a phenomenon that the conference organiser described as the democratisation of historical knowledge enabled by digital archive access.","t":"這次研討會吸引了一群學術歷史學家、專業檔案管理員和熱心愛好者的混合，他們廣泛的個人研究在幾個案例中已經超過了專業學術研究的深度——這一現象是會議組織者描述為數字檔案訪問所實現的歷史知識民主化。","as":"A devoted history buff, the retired engineer spent his weekends combing through dusty county archives, and his assiduous research eventually produced a comprehensive account of the local railway that even eminent historians praised as definitive.","at":"這位退休工程師是個熱衷歷史的愛好者，他利用週末翻遍縣府積滿灰塵的檔案；他孜孜不倦的研究最終寫成一部關於當地鐵路的完整紀錄，連知名的歷史學家都讚譽為權威之作。"},{"w":"conjugal","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to marriage or the relationship between married people.","c":"婚姻的；夫妻的","s":"The prison policy regarding conjugal visits had been revised three times in the preceding decade, each revision reflecting a different theory about whether maintaining family bonds reduced recidivism rates sufficiently to justify the security complications and administrative costs associated with supervising such arrangements.","t":"關於婚姻探視的監獄政策在過去十年中已修訂了三次，每次修訂都反映了不同的理論，即維持家庭聯繫是否能充分降低累犯率，以證明與監督此類安排相關的安全複雜性和行政成本是合理的。","as":"In many traditional societies, conjugal duties were stipulated by custom rather than by law, and a wife who dared to flout these expectations risked being castigated by her in-laws and shunned by the entire village.","at":"在許多傳統社會中，夫妻之間的義務是由習俗而非法律所規定；膽敢違背這些期待的妻子，可能會遭到公婆嚴厲責罵，並被全村的人排斥。"},{"w":"crave","p":"v.","d":"To desire urgently, to long for.","c":"渴望；懇求","s":"After eighteen months of enforced separation from family and colleagues during the pandemic lockdown, many individuals found they craved social interaction with an intensity that revealed how fundamentally human beings were wired for community and how inadequately digital communication substituted for physical presence.","t":"在疫情封鎖期間被迫與家人和同事分離十八個月後，許多人發現他們以一種強度渴望社交互動，這揭示了人類在根本上是如何為社區而生的，以及數字通信如何不足以替代實體存在。","as":"After months of isolation at the polar research station, the scientists began to crave fresh vegetables and unfamiliar faces, and even the most mundane letters from home could elicit a paroxysm of joy among the weary crew.","at":"在極地研究站與世隔絕數月後，科學家們開始渴望新鮮蔬菜和陌生的面孔；即使是家鄉寄來最平凡無奇的信件，也能讓疲憊的隊員們欣喜若狂。"},{"w":"deem","p":"v.","d":"To regard or consider in a particular way.","c":"認為；視為","s":"The committee deem ed it appropriate to commission an independent review before making any final decision, recognising that the complexity of the issues involved and the diversity of stakeholder interests made any unilateral determination susceptible to challenge on both procedural and substantive grounds.","t":"委員會認為在做出任何最終決定之前委托獨立審查是適當的，認識到所涉及問題的複雜性和利益相關者利益的多樣性，使任何單方面決定在程序和實質基礎上都容易受到挑戰。","as":"Although critics initially deemed her experimental novel incoherent, later generations of readers discerned in its fragmented structure a laudable attempt to convey the chaos and confusion of wartime memory for a generation of survivors.","at":"雖然評論家起初認為她的實驗性小說語無倫次，後世讀者卻從其支離破碎的結構中看出，這是試圖為一整代倖存者呈現戰時記憶之混亂與迷惘的可貴嘗試。"},{"w":"inherent","p":"adj.","d":"Existing naturally as a permanent quality.","c":"固有的；與生俱來的","s":"The risk assessors concluded that the dangers were not merely operational but inherent to the technology itself — built into its fundamental design in ways that could not be adequately managed through procedural safeguards alone, making the case for a more fundamental engineering redesign.","t":"風險評估員得出結論，危險不僅僅是操作性的，而且是技術本身固有的——以無法僅通過程序保障措施充分管理的方式構建到其基本設計中，這為更根本的工程重新設計提供了理由。","as":"Every financial investment carries inherent risks, and even the most astute advisers cannot prognosticate with certainty how markets will behave, which is why sensible investors spread their assets across many different sectors.","at":"任何金融投資都有其固有的風險，即使是最精明的顧問也無法準確預測市場走向；正因如此，明智的投資人會把資產分散到許多不同的產業。"},{"w":"innate","p":"adj.","d":"Inborn, possessed from birth.","c":"天生的；先天的","s":"The developmental psychologist's research challenged the longstanding assumption that numerical reasoning was purely a learned capacity, providing evidence that infants as young as five months demonstrated responses suggesting innate sensitivity to quantity that preceded any possible instruction or cultural influence.","t":"這位發展心理學家的研究挑戰了長期以來數字推理純粹是後天習得能力的假設，提供了五個月大的嬰兒表現出先於任何可能的指導或文化影響的對數量的天生敏感性的反應的證據。","as":"Linguists have long debated whether humans possess an innate capacity for language, since young children master complex grammar with remarkable alacrity despite hearing only garbled fragments of speech, a paradox that imitation alone seems unable to explain.","at":"語言學家長期爭論人類是否天生具備語言能力，因為幼童儘管只聽到殘缺混亂的話語片段，卻能以驚人的速度掌握複雜的文法；這個矛盾現象似乎無法單靠模仿來解釋。"},{"w":"irrelevant","p":"adj.","d":"Not connected with the matter in hand.","c":"不相關的；不切題的","s":"The judge sustained the objection and instructed the jury to disregard the testimony, ruling that the witness's account of events occurring six years after the relevant period was entirely irrelevant to the specific charges before the court and could only serve to prejudice the defendant's right to a fair trial.","t":"法官維持了異議，指示陪審團忽略這一證詞，裁定證人關於在相關時期六年後發生事件的陳述對法院面前的具體指控完全不相關，只能損害被告獲得公平審判的權利。","as":"The defense attorney objected that the prosecutor's questions about the defendant's flamboyant lifestyle were irrelevant to the charges, arguing that such lurid details served only to bias the jury rather than to prove that he was culpable.","at":"辯護律師提出異議，指出檢察官針對被告奢華浮誇生活方式的提問與指控毫不相關，並主張這些聳人聽聞的細節只會讓陪審團產生偏見，而無法證明他有罪。"},{"w":"itinerant","p":"adj.","d":"Travelling from place to place.","c":"巡迴的；流動的","s":"The itinerant agricultural workers who moved seasonally between harvests in different regions occupied a peculiarly vulnerable position in the labour market — too mobile to benefit from local union representation, too temporary to qualify for most statutory employment protections, and too dispersed to organise collectively with any effectiveness.","t":"在不同地區收穫之間季節性移動的巡迴農業工人在勞動市場上占據了一個特別脆弱的位置——太過流動以至於無法從地方工會代表中受益，太臨時以至於無法獲得大多數法定就業保護，太分散以至於無法有效地集體組織。","as":"In medieval Europe, itinerant minstrels traveled from one village to the next, performing ballads that embellished local legends, and in an age when news arrived only sporadically, their visit was often the most salient event of the season.","at":"在中世紀的歐洲，巡迴的吟遊詩人從一個村莊走到下一個村莊，演唱為地方傳說增添色彩的歌謠；在消息往來零零星星的年代，他們的到訪往往是當季最引人注目的大事。"},{"w":"latent","p":"adj.","d":"Existing but not yet developed.","c":"潛在的；隱伏的","s":"The researchers identified a latent capacity in the virus to evolve resistance to the primary antiviral compounds currently in clinical use, a finding that significantly complicated the treatment planning for long-term management and underscored the urgent need for the development of second-generation therapeutic options.","t":"研究人員確定了病毒進化出對目前在臨床使用的主要抗病毒化合物的耐藥性的潛在能力，這一發現使長期管理的治療計劃複雜化，並強調了迫切需要開發第二代治療選項。","as":"Because the virus can remain latent in nerve cells for years, a patient who appears fully recovered may suddenly suffer a painful outbreak, a pernicious pattern that frustrates doctors and makes the malady exceptionally difficult to cure.","at":"由於這種病毒能在神經細胞中潛伏多年，看似完全康復的病人可能突然再次發作、疼痛不堪；這種有害的模式令醫師束手無策，也使這種疾病極難治癒。"},{"w":"modify","p":"v.","d":"To change partially.","c":"修改；修飾","s":"The architects were asked to modify the original design to address the heritage committee's concerns about visual impact on the protected streetscape, a process that required six iterations over fourteen months before a version was produced that satisfied both the developer's commercial requirements and the conservation authority's aesthetic standards.","t":"建築師被要求修改原始設計，以解決遺產委員會對受保護街景視覺影響的關切，這一過程在十四個月內經歷了六次迭代，才產生了一個既滿足開發商的商業要求又符合保護機構美學標準的版本。","as":"Engineers had to modify the bridge's original design after wind-tunnel tests corroborated an ominous suspicion that its slender deck would sway dangerously in turbulent winds, a flaw that could have precipitated a disastrous collapse.","at":"風洞測試證實了一個令人不安的疑慮：橋梁細長的橋面在強烈亂流中會危險地擺動；這個缺陷可能導致災難性的坍塌，因此工程師不得不修改原本的設計。"},{"w":"myriad","p":"adj.","d":"Countless in number.","c":"無數的；極大量的","s":"The digital revolution had created myriad new opportunities for creative expression, but had simultaneously generated conditions in which the economic viability of individual creative careers had become substantially more precarious, as the expansion of supply dramatically outpaced any corresponding growth in the total financial resources available to support creative work.","t":"數字革命創造了無數新的創意表達機會，但同時產生了使個人創意職業的經濟可行性變得更加不穩定的條件，因為供應的擴大大大超過了支持創意工作的總財務資源的任何相應增長。","as":"Entomologists exploring the rainforest canopy encounter myriad insects, many of them never formally described, and they often become so engrossed in pursuing elusive specimens that they barely notice the ubiquitous mosquitoes feasting on their arms.","at":"探索雨林樹冠層的昆蟲學家會遇到無數種昆蟲，其中許多從未被正式描述過；他們常常專注於追捕難以捉摸的標本，以至於幾乎沒注意到無所不在的蚊子正在叮咬自己的手臂。"},{"w":"peregrination","p":"n.","d":"A journey, especially a long one.","c":"旅程；遊歷","s":"Her literary peregrination s through the lesser-known regions of the continent produced three volumes of travel writing that combined precise observation, historical research, and personal reflection in a way that was compared favourably by reviewers to the finest traditions of the genre.","t":"她對大陸鮮為人知地區的文學遊歷產生了三卷旅行文學，以一種被評論家與該流派最優秀傳統相提並論的方式結合了精確的觀察、歷史研究和個人反思。","as":"During his long peregrination through the northern provinces of Japan, the poet Basho composed haiku of laconic beauty, verses steeped in Buddhist reflection that transformed a journey fraught with hardship into a masterpiece of travel literature.","at":"詩人松尾芭蕉在日本北方諸國的漫長旅途中，寫下簡潔優美的俳句；這些浸透佛教省思的詩句，將一段充滿艱辛的旅程化為遊記文學的傑作。"},{"w":"romp","p":"v.","d":"To move in a lively, boisterous way.","c":"嬉鬧；喧鬧地玩耍","s":"The documentary's footage of young orangutans romping through the forest canopy under the watchful eyes of their mothers provided an unexpectedly joyful counterpoint to the sombre conservation narrative that surrounded it, reminding audiences of the individual personalities that statistics about species decline could never adequately convey.","t":"紀錄片中幼年猩猩在母親注視下在森林樹冠中嬉鬧的畫面，為圍繞它的嚴肅保護敘述提供了出乎意料的歡樂對位，讓觀眾想起了關於物種數量下降的統計數據永遠無法充分傳達的個體個性。","as":"Released at last from their cramped kennel, the young dogs began to romp across the meadow, their jaunty leaps and mock skirmishes a striking contrast to the inert, listless behavior they had displayed while confined indoors.","at":"終於從狹窄的狗舍被放出來，小狗們在草地上嬉戲奔跑；牠們輕快的跳躍與假裝打鬥的模樣，與被關在室內時那種了無生氣、無精打采的樣子形成鮮明對比。"},{"w":"spontaneous","p":"adj.","d":"Done without being planned.","c":"自發的；自然的","s":"The spontaneousedemonstration that erupted outside the courthouse following the verdict drew tens of thousands of participants within hours, a gathering that no organisation claimed to have coordinated and which the authorities ultimately chose to facilitate rather than disperse, recognising that any attempt at suppression would likely intensify rather than reduce the public reaction.","t":"裁決後在法院外爆發的自發示威在幾小時內吸引了數萬名參與者，這是一個沒有任何組織聲稱已協調的集會，當局最終選擇促進而不是驅散，認識到任何鎮壓嘗試可能會加劇而不是減少公眾反應。","as":"The march was not organized by any political party but arose as a spontaneous outpouring of grief and anger after the egregious verdict, and the authorities, cognizant of the public mood, wisely chose not to quell it.","at":"這場遊行並非由任何政黨發起，而是在那項離譜的判決之後，民眾自發地宣洩悲傷與憤怒；當局察覺到民心向背，明智地選擇不加以鎮壓。"},{"w":"tortuous","p":"adj.","d":"Full of twists and turns.","c":"彎曲的；曲折的","s":"The tortuous path to regulatory approval had consumed seven years, required the submission of documentation exceeding forty thousand pages, involved responses to three separate rounds of queries from four different regulatory bodies, and ultimately necessitated a complete reformulation of the product's active ingredient delivery system.","t":"獲得監管批准的曲折之路消耗了七年，需要提交超過四萬頁的文件，涉及對四個不同監管機構的三輪獨立查詢的回應，最終需要對產品活性成分遞送系統進行完全重新配製。","as":"The tortuous path to the mountain monastery winds along sheer cliffs, and pilgrims who ascend it must endure dizzying heights and inclement weather, yet many describe the arduous climb as a source of deep spiritual solace.","at":"通往山中修道院的小徑蜿蜒曲折，沿著陡峭的懸崖盤旋而上；攀登的朝聖者必須忍受令人暈眩的高度與惡劣的天氣，但許多人形容這段艱辛的攀爬是深刻的心靈慰藉。"},{"w":"urbane","p":"adj.","d":"Suave, confident and sophisticated.","c":"溫文爾雅的；都市化的","s":"His urbane manner concealed a steely determination that occasionally surprised those who had mistaken his surface courtesy for passivity — a misreading he had consistently turned to his advantage in negotiations where opponents had underestimated both his intellectual depth and his willingness to pursue confrontation when circumstances required it.","t":"他溫文爾雅的舉止掩蓋了一種鋼鐵般的決心，這偶爾會讓那些把他表面的禮貌誤認為被動的人感到驚訝——這是一種誤讀，他在談判中一貫將其轉化為優勢，在那些對手低估了他的智識深度和在情況需要時追求對抗的意願的談判中。","as":"An urbane host who moved effortlessly between languages, the diplomat could disarm even the most fractious guests with a well-timed quip, and his dinner parties became a haven where rival politicians could converse amicably.","at":"這位外交官是溫文儒雅的主人，能在多種語言之間自在切換，即使面對最難纏好鬥的賓客，也能以一句恰到好處的妙語化解；他的晚宴因此成了敵對政治人物能夠和睦交談的避風港。"},{"w":"veneer","p":"n.","d":"A thin covering to hide what is underneath.","c":"飾面；虛飾","s":"The apparent civility that characterised public discourse in the organisation was, as the internal review documented extensively, a thin veneer concealing substantial tensions, unresolved conflicts, and deeply entrenched patterns of preferential treatment that had never been addressed through the formal mechanisms supposedly designed for that purpose.","t":"表徵組織公開討論的表面文明，正如內部審查廣泛記錄的那樣，是一層薄薄的虛飾，掩蓋著大量緊張關係、未解決的衝突以及從未通過據說為此目的設計的正式機制解決的根深蒂固的優惠待遇模式。","as":"Beneath the veneer of civility that the royal court displayed to foreign visitors lurked a world of intrigue and duplicity, where ambitious courtiers would disparage their rivals in whispers and scheme to oust anyone who threatened their influence.","at":"在王室宮廷向外國訪客展現的彬彬有禮的表象之下，潛藏著充滿陰謀與欺詐的世界：野心勃勃的朝臣會私下低聲詆毀對手，並設計排擠任何威脅到自身權勢的人。"}]},{"unit":19,"cards":[{"w":"amnesty","p":"n.","d":"A general pardon for offences.","c":"大赦；特赦","s":"The peace agreement included a conditional amnesty for combatants who had not been directly involved in documented atrocities, with the specific crimes excluded from its scope having been negotiated extensively between the parties and subject to independent verification by an international tribunal.","t":"和平協議包括對沒有直接參與有記錄暴行的戰鬥人員的有條件大赦，被排除在其範圍之外的具體罪行已由各方廣泛談判，並受到國際法庭的獨立核實。","as":"Hoping to end years of fighting, the new government offered amnesty to the belligerent factions that agreed to lay down their arms, a conciliatory policy that skeptics deemed overly lenient but that eventually helped quell the insurgency.","at":"為了結束多年的戰火，新政府向同意放下武器的交戰派系提供特赦；這項和解政策雖被懷疑者認為過於寬容，最終卻幫助平息了叛亂。"},{"w":"balk","p":"v.","d":"To be unwilling to proceed.","c":"畏縮；猶豫","s":"The committee members balk ed at the proposal's financial implications once the full cost modelling was presented — a reaction that the project's advocates had anticipated and attempted to pre-empt by structuring the presentation to emphasise long-term returns before disclosing the substantial upfront investment that those returns required.","t":"一旦提出完整的成本模型，委員會成員對提案的財務影響感到猶豫——項目倡導者已預料到這一反應，並試圖通過在披露那些回報所需的大量前期投資之前強調長期回報來結構演示，以搶先阻止這一反應。","as":"Although the plan's goals were laudable, investors began to balk at funding a project so fraught with technical uncertainty, especially after an earlier abortive attempt to build a similar tidal power plant had cost them dearly.","at":"雖然這項計畫的目標值得稱許，投資人卻開始對資助一個充滿技術不確定性的計畫裹足不前，尤其先前興建類似潮汐發電廠的嘗試失敗，已讓他們付出慘痛代價。"},{"w":"blunt","p":"adj.","d":"Plainspoken, lacking in subtlety.","c":"直率的；遲鈍的","s":"Her assessment of the manuscript was characteristically blunt, identifying with precision the three structural weaknesses that had caused the previous three reviewers to reject it while simultaneously acknowledging the genuine intellectual ambition that distinguished the work from the competent but uninspired submissions that comprised the majority of the journal's submissions.","t":"她對手稿的評估具有典型的直率，精確地識別了導致前三位評審員拒絕它的三個結構性弱點，同時承認使該作品區別於構成期刊提交大多數的有能力但缺乏靈感的提交的真正智識抱負。","as":"Known for her blunt assessments, the editor told the aspiring novelist that his manuscript was verbose and lackluster, a frank critique that stung at first but ultimately spurred him to rewrite the book with far greater economy.","at":"這位編輯以直言不諱的評論聞名，她直接告訴這位有志成為小說家的年輕人，他的手稿冗長又平淡乏味；這番坦率的批評起初令他刺痛，最終卻促使他以更精簡的筆法重寫全書。"},{"w":"coup","p":"n.","d":"A sudden successful seizure of power.","c":"政變；出乎意料的成功","s":"The constitutional coup had been executed with remarkable precision — all key institutions secured, communication infrastructure controlled, and the interim administration announced within a six-hour window that gave the international community insufficient time to coordinate a preventive response before the transition of power was effectively complete.","t":"憲法政變以非凡的精確度執行——所有關鍵機構得到保障，通信基礎設施受到控制，臨時政府在六小時窗口內宣布，這使國際社會沒有足夠的時間在權力轉移有效完成之前協調預防性回應。","as":"The military coup was swift and nearly bloodless: within hours the generals had ousted the elected president, seized the state broadcaster, and promulgated a nationwide curfew, leaving incredulous citizens to wonder whether democracy would ever be restored.","at":"這場軍事政變迅速且幾乎未見流血：短短數小時內，將領們便推翻了民選總統、接管國營電視台，並頒布全國宵禁，讓難以置信的民眾不禁懷疑民主是否還有恢復的一天。"},{"w":"dismantle","p":"v.","d":"To take apart piece by piece.","c":"拆除；解散","s":"The new administration had pledged to dismantle the previous government's flagship regulatory framework within its first term, but the practical complexity of replacing interconnected legislation affecting multiple industries simultaneously had significantly moderated the pace of reform compared with the sweeping changes that had been promised during the campaign.","t":"新政府承諾在第一個任期內拆除前政府的旗艦監管框架，但同時替換影響多個行業的相互關聯立法的實際複雜性，與競選期間承諾的全面改革相比，顯著減緩了改革步伐。","as":"Under the terms of the treaty, international inspectors oversaw efforts to dismantle the enrichment plant, scrutinizing every warehouse to ensure that no essential component was surreptitiously hidden away for use in a future weapons program.","at":"根據條約規定，國際檢查人員監督拆除濃縮廠的工作，並仔細檢查每一座倉庫，確保沒有任何關鍵零件被暗中藏匿、留待日後的武器計畫使用。"},{"w":"exonerate","p":"v.","d":"To officially absolve from blame.","c":"免除責任；宣佈無罪","s":"The investigation's conclusion that the officer had acted in accordance with established protocols fully exonerated her from the allegations of misconduct, but the formal clearance did little to repair the reputational damage caused by the months of intense media coverage that had preceded the inquiry's findings.","t":"調查得出結論，該官員按照既定規程行事，完全免除了她的不當行為指控，但正式平反幾乎沒有修復調查發現之前數月強烈媒體報道所造成的聲譽損害。","as":"After newly analyzed DNA evidence exonerated a man who had spent half his life in prison, advocates for reform argued that the case exposed an inherent flaw in a justice system that relied far too heavily on dubious eyewitness testimony.","at":"一名在獄中度過半生的男子，因重新分析的DNA證據而獲判無罪；倡議改革的人士指出，此案暴露了司法制度的固有缺陷：過度依賴可疑的目擊證詞。"},{"w":"expatriate","p":"n.","d":"A person living outside their native country.","c":"移居國外者；流放者","s":"The survey of expatriate professionals revealed a complex mixture of motivations for remaining abroad — career opportunities unavailable in their home countries, lifestyle preferences, family circumstances, and in some cases explicit reluctance to return to political or social environments they found uncongenial.","t":"對移居國外專業人員的調查揭示了留在國外的複雜動機組合——在本國無法獲得的職業機會、生活方式偏好、家庭情況，以及在某些情況下，明確不願意回到他們認為不合適的政治或社會環境中。","as":"Drawn by low rents and a vibrant artistic scene, many American writers lived as expatriates in Paris after the First World War, forming a gregarious coterie whose letters, while celebrating European freedom, often disparage the puritanical culture they had left behind.","at":"受到低廉房租與蓬勃藝術氛圍的吸引，許多美國作家在第一次世界大戰後旅居巴黎，形成一個喜好交際的小圈子；他們的書信在讚頌歐洲自由風氣的同時，也常貶抑他們所拋下的清教徒式文化。"},{"w":"fiat","p":"n.","d":"An official order or decree.","c":"命令；法令","s":"The regulation had been introduced by executive fiat rather than through normal legislative procedures, a decision that gave it immediate effect but left it vulnerable to legal challenge on procedural grounds and dependent on the continued support of an administration that might itself be subject to electoral change within the near term.","t":"這一法規是通過行政命令而非正常立法程序引入的，這一決定使其立即生效，但使其容易受到程序基礎上的法律挑戰，並依賴於可能在近期本身就面臨選舉變化的行政機構的持續支持。","as":"Rather than consulting the public, the governor imposed the new zoning rules by fiat, an arbitrary decision that provoked an acrimonious backlash and prompted several towns to challenge the extent of her jurisdiction in court.","at":"州長未徵詢民意，便以命令強行實施新的分區規定；這項專斷的決定引發激烈的反彈，並促使數個城鎮向法院挑戰她的管轄權範圍。"},{"w":"legion","p":"adj.","d":"Vast in number.","c":"眾多的；軍團","s":"The challenges facing the incoming administration were legion: a depleted treasury, deteriorating infrastructure, a healthcare system near collapse, a diplomatic reputation requiring substantial rehabilitation, and a civil service demoralised by years of politically motivated interference in its professional functions.","t":"新任政府面臨的挑戰眾多：耗盡的財政、惡化的基礎設施、瀕臨崩潰的醫療體系、需要大量修復的外交聲譽，以及因多年出於政治動機的干預其專業職能而士氣低落的公務員隊伍。","as":"The obstacles facing the newly independent nation were legion: its treasury was empty, its roads and bridges had been ravaged by war, and fractious regional leaders repeatedly thwarted every attempt to form a viable central government.","at":"這個新獨立國家所面臨的障礙多不勝數：國庫空虛，道路與橋梁遭戰火摧殘，而且彼此爭執不休的地方領袖一再阻撓每一次建立可行中央政府的嘗試。"},{"w":"megalomania","p":"n.","d":"An obsessive desire for power or wealth.","c":"狂妄自大；自大狂","s":"Historians have debated whether the emperor's increasingly irrational military campaigns represented a genuine clinical condition akin to megalomania or simply the unchecked expression of ambitions that had never been subject to meaningful constraint from any institutional check or personal adviser willing to deliver unwelcome counsel.","t":"歷史學家一直在爭論，這位皇帝日益非理性的軍事征伐是否代表了一種類似於狂妄自大的真正臨床狀況，還是僅僅是從未受到任何制度制衡或願意提供不受歡迎建議的個人顧問的有意義約束的野心的不受控制的表達。","as":"The dictator's megalomania was evident in the mammoth statues of himself that he erected in every city, monuments so ostentatious that even his most loyal confidants privately scoffed at them.","at":"這位獨裁者的自大狂從他在每座城市豎立的巨型自身雕像便可見一斑；這些紀念碑浮誇至極，連他最忠心的心腹都私下嗤之以鼻。"},{"w":"mendacious","p":"adj.","d":"Not telling the truth, lying.","c":"虛假的；撒謊的","s":"The inquiry characterised the company's public communications during the critical period as systematically mendacious, finding that executives had made statements about product safety that they had known to be false at the time of making them, based on internal research to which they had direct access.","t":"調查將公司在關鍵時期的公開傳播定性為系統性虛假，發現高管們根據他們直接訪問的內部研究，對產品安全性做出了他們在發表時就知道是假的陳述。","as":"Journalists eventually exposed the mendacious tobacco executives who had concocted misleading studies and insisted, seemingly with impunity, that their products posed no lethal danger to the millions of people who used them every day.","at":"記者最終揭發了那些滿口謊言的菸草公司高層：他們捏造誤導人的研究，並在似乎不必承擔後果的情況下堅稱，自家產品對每天使用的數百萬人不構成任何致命危險。"},{"w":"nostalgia","p":"n.","d":"A longing for the past.","c":"懷舊；思鄉病","s":"The political movement's remarkable electoral success was attributed by analysts to its ability to exploit a widespread nostalgia for an idealised past — one that had never quite existed as remembered but which nonetheless represented, for significant portions of the electorate, a more reassuring narrative than any vision of an uncertain future could provide.","t":"這個政治運動非凡的選舉成功被分析人士歸因於其利用對理想化過去的普遍懷舊情緒的能力——這個過去從未完全如記憶中那樣存在，但對選民的很大一部分來說，它代表著比任何不確定未來的願景都更令人安心的敘述。","as":"Older residents often speak with nostalgia of the tranquil fishing village that once occupied the bay, but younger people, who crave the jobs that tourism brings, tend to deride such longing as a rosy memory that ignores the privations of the past.","at":"年長的居民常懷念昔日坐落在海灣旁那座寧靜的漁村，但渴望觀光業帶來工作機會的年輕人，往往嘲笑這種嚮往只是美化過的回憶，忽略了過去物資匱乏的困苦。"},{"w":"parsimonious","p":"adj.","d":"Very unwilling to spend money.","c":"吝嗇的；極度節儉的","s":"The foundation's parsimonious approach to administrative overhead — limiting staff costs to a percentage so low that it prevented the hiring of personnel with sufficient expertise to manage the programmes effectively — was ultimately counterproductive, as the resulting inefficiencies caused more waste than the savings in overhead could possibly justify.","t":"基金會對行政管理費用的吝嗇做法——將人員成本限制在低到阻止雇用足夠有能力有效管理計劃的人員的百分比——最終適得其反，因為由此產生的低效率造成的浪費比節省的管理費用所能合理解釋的要多。","as":"The parsimonious landlord refused to spend anything on repairs, and tenants who implored him to fix the broken heating were met with caustic dismissals, leaving families to endure the bitter winter in sordid, freezing apartments.","at":"這名吝嗇的房東不肯花一毛錢修繕，房客懇求他修理故障的暖氣時，只換來他尖酸刻薄的回絕，讓一戶戶家庭只能在骯髒又冰冷的公寓裡熬過嚴冬。"},{"w":"pecuniary","p":"adj.","d":"Relating to or involving money.","c":"金錢的；金錢上的","s":"The committee found that the official's failure to declare his pecuniary interest in the company that received the contract constituted a serious breach of the code of conduct, regardless of whether the undisclosed interest had actually influenced his decision to support the relevant procurement award.","t":"委員會發現，該官員未能申報他在獲得合同的公司中的金錢利益構成了對行為準則的嚴重違反，無論未披露的利益是否實際上影響了他支持相關採購決定。","as":"Investigators discovered that the senator held a pecuniary interest in the very firm that had won the highway contract, a flagrant breach of ethics that, critics argued, should preclude him from voting on any related legislation.","at":"調查人員發現，這位參議員在得標公路合約的那家公司中擁有金錢上的利益；批評者認為，這是公然違反倫理的行為，應該禁止他對任何相關法案進行表決。"},{"w":"profligate","p":"adj.","d":"Recklessly extravagant or wasteful.","c":"揮霍的；放蕩的","s":"The audit revealed a profligate approach to public procurement that had resulted in expenditure nearly three times the budgeted amount on a project of questionable necessity — a pattern of waste that the comptroller general described as symptomatic of a broader failure of financial governance within the department.","t":"審計揭示了一種對公共採購揮霍的做法，導致一個需要性可疑的項目的支出幾乎是預算金額的三倍——審計長將這種浪費模式描述為部門內更廣泛的財務治理失敗的症狀。","as":"The profligate young heir squandered his father's fortune on rash wagers and extravagant parties, and within a few years the once affluent family had to sell its estate, a downfall that the boy's frugal grandfather could never have imagined.","at":"這位揮霍無度的年輕繼承人把父親的財產浪擲在魯莽的賭注與奢侈的派對上；短短幾年內，這個曾經富裕的家族便不得不變賣莊園，這樣的沒落是他那節儉的祖父做夢也想不到的。"},{"w":"restrictive","p":"adj.","d":"Imposing limitations.","c":"限制性的；約束的","s":"The competition authority concluded that the covenant's restrictive provisions effectively prevented meaningful market entry by potential competitors, creating conditions of market dominance that were not the outcome of superior commercial performance but of contractual arrangements specifically designed to exclude competition.","t":"競爭監管機構得出結論，該契約的限制性條款有效地阻止了潛在競爭者的有意義的市場進入，創造了市場主導地位的條件，這不是優越商業表現的結果，而是專門設計用來排除競爭的合同安排。","as":"Critics argue that the city's restrictive zoning laws, which prohibit apartment buildings in most neighborhoods, have exacerbated the housing shortage and inadvertently pushed indigent families into overcrowded districts far from their jobs.","at":"批評者認為，該市嚴格的分區法規禁止在多數社區興建公寓大樓，不僅加劇了住宅短缺，也在無意間把貧困家庭推往遠離工作地點、過度擁擠的地區。"},{"w":"rife","p":"adj.","d":"Widespread, full of.","c":"普遍的；盛傳的","s":"Corruption was so rife throughout the procurement system that even officials who wished to act honestly found themselves confronting a network of expectations, informal obligations, and career consequences that made resistance to corrupt practices personally costly in ways that the formal anti-corruption framework was entirely insufficient to counteract.","t":"腐敗在整個採購體系中如此普遍，以至於即使是希望誠實行事的官員也發現自己面臨著一個期望、非正式義務和職業後果的網絡，使抵制腐敗行為對個人而言代價高昂，而正式的反腐框架完全不足以抵消。","as":"In the final years of the dynasty, the imperial bureaucracy was rife with corruption, as officials routinely solicited bribes, engaged in extortion, and treated the law with such disdain that a peasant uprising became all but inexorable.","at":"在王朝的最後幾年，帝國官僚體系貪腐橫行：官員經常索賄、敲詐勒索，並對法律如此輕蔑，以致農民起義幾乎成了無法阻擋的結果。"},{"w":"strife","p":"n.","d":"Angry or violent disagreement.","c":"衝突；爭吵","s":"The internal strife that had paralysed the coalition for the preceding eighteen months finally reached a resolution when both factions agreed to an independent arbitration process that neither had initially been willing to accept, their eventual concurrence reflecting a shared recognition that continued deadlock was more damaging to both parties than compromise.","t":"在過去十八個月癱瘓了聯盟的內部衝突最終達到了解決，當時兩個派系同意了一個最初都不願意接受的獨立仲裁過程，他們最終的一致反映了一種共同的認識，即繼續陷入僵局對雙方的損害都大於妥協。","as":"Years of sectarian strife had left the city deeply scarred, and although an amicable truce now holds, community leaders fear that the latent hostility between the two groups could be rekindled by a single inflammatory epithet.","at":"多年的宗派衝突在這座城市留下深刻的傷痕；雖然目前維持著和睦的停戰，社區領袖仍擔心，兩個群體之間潛藏的敵意可能因一句煽動性的侮辱稱呼而再度點燃。"},{"w":"sumptuous","p":"adj.","d":"Splendid and expensive-looking.","c":"奢華的；豪華的","s":"The sumptuous banquet held in honour of the visiting delegation — featuring seventeen courses, wines from five different countries, and a floral arrangement that alone cost more than most of the guests' monthly salaries — attracted considerable public criticism given the austerity measures that the government had simultaneously been imposing on ordinary citizens.","t":"為訪問代表團舉辦的奢華宴會——包括十七道菜、來自五個不同國家的葡萄酒，以及僅花卉佈置的費用就超過大多數客人月薪的插花——鑒於政府同時對普通公民實施的緊縮措施，引發了相當大的公眾批評。","as":"Guests at the palace were served a sumptuous banquet of roasted game and imported wines, an incongruous display of luxury at a time when emaciated peasants just beyond the walls were dying of malnutrition.","at":"宮中賓客享用著野味與進口美酒的奢華盛宴；而就在宮牆之外，骨瘦如柴的農民正因營養不良而死去，這場奢靡的排場顯得極不相稱。"},{"w":"underwrite","p":"v.","d":"To provide financial support for.","c":"承保；提供資金","s":"The government's decision to underwrite the infrastructure bonds reduced the borrowing cost substantially — reflecting the lower risk premium that markets attached to government-backed securities compared with purely commercial paper — but also transferred the ultimate credit risk to the public balance sheet in ways that opposition economists characterised as irresponsible.","t":"政府決定為基礎設施債券提供擔保，大幅降低了借貸成本——反映了市場對政府支持的證券與純商業票據相比所附加的較低風險溢價——但也以反對派經濟學家描述為不負責任的方式，將最終信貸風險轉移到了公共資產負債表上。","as":"Several private foundations agreed to underwrite the excavation after government agencies, citing the paucity of preliminary evidence, declined to fund it, and their gamble paid off when the team unearthed a subterranean tomb replete with ancient treasures.","at":"由於政府機關以初步證據不足為由拒絕撥款，數個私人基金會同意資助這項挖掘工作；而當團隊挖出一座滿是古代珍寶的地下墓穴時，他們的冒險終於得到了回報。"}]},{"unit":20,"cards":[{"w":"abstemious","p":"adj.","d":"Restrained in eating and drinking.","c":"飲食有節制的","s":"His abstemious habits at the celebratory dinner — choosing water over wine, declining the dessert course, and departing well before midnight — contrasted sharply with the behaviour of most other guests and reminded newer colleagues that his extraordinary physical conditioning at fifty-eight was not accidental.","t":"他在慶祝晚宴上飲食節制的習慣——選擇水而非酒，拒絕甜點，在午夜前很早就離開——與大多數其他客人的行為形成了鮮明對比，並提醒了新同事，他五十八歲時非凡的身體狀況並非偶然。","as":"Renowned for his abstemious habits, the philosopher ate a single frugal meal each day and eschewed wine entirely, a regimen that his profligate contemporaries derided as needless self-denial even as they envied his robust health.","at":"這位哲學家以飲食節制聞名，每天只吃一頓簡樸的餐點，並且滴酒不沾；他那些揮霍無度的同代人嘲笑這種作息是不必要的自我克制，卻又羨慕他強健的體魄。"},{"w":"derogatory","p":"adj.","d":"Showing a critical or disrespectful attitude.","c":"貶低的；誹謗的","s":"The employment tribunal found that the manager's use of derogatory language about an employee's national background in performance reviews constituted direct discrimination, ruling that the characterisation of cultural communication styles as professional deficiencies served no legitimate management function and was objectively offensive.","t":"就業法庭認定，管理者在績效評估中對員工的民族背景使用貶低性語言構成了直接歧視，裁定將文化溝通風格描述為職業缺陷沒有合法的管理功能，客觀上是冒犯性的。","as":"After the commentator made derogatory remarks about immigrant workers on live television, the network faced a frenzy of criticism, and he was compelled to recant his statements, though many viewers deemed his perfunctory apology insincere.","at":"這名評論員在直播節目中發表貶低移工的言論後，電視台遭到排山倒海的抨擊，他也被迫收回自己的說法；不過許多觀眾認為他那敷衍了事的道歉毫無誠意。"},{"w":"disparate","p":"adj.","d":"Essentially different in kind.","c":"迥然不同的；無法比較的","s":"The coalition brought together disparate interest groups that would under normal political circumstances never have found common cause — environmental activists, rural farmers, urban property owners, and technology entrepreneurs — united solely by their shared opposition to the proposed infrastructure development corridor.","t":"聯盟匯聚了在正常政治環境下永遠不會找到共同事業的迥然不同的利益群體——環保活動人士、農村農民、城市業主和技術企業家——僅僅通過他們對擬議基礎設施開發走廊的共同反對而團結在一起。","as":"The research team brought together experts from disparate fields such as linguistics, genetics, and archaeology, and by combining these seemingly incongruous methods, they developed a viable theory of human migration that later fossil discoveries corroborated.","at":"這個研究團隊集結了語言學、遺傳學與考古學等迥然不同領域的專家；藉由結合這些看似格格不入的研究方法，他們提出了一套可行的人類遷徙理論，並在後來的化石發現中得到證實。"},{"w":"edifice","p":"n.","d":"A large imposing building.","c":"宏偉的建築；大廈","s":"The edifice that had housed the colonial administration for nearly a century stood empty now, its grandeur intact but its purpose dissolved, the ambiguity of its future reflecting a broader national conversation about how a society should relate to the physical remnants of a historical period it had definitively rejected.","t":"曾容納殖民地行政機構近一個世紀的宏偉建築現在空置著，其壯觀完好無損但其目的已消失，其未來的模糊性反映了一個社會應如何與一個它明確拒絕的歷史時期的物質遺跡相關聯的更廣泛的國家對話。","as":"Generations of masons labored to complete the towering Gothic edifice, whose spires remain the city's most famous landmark, but acid rain has gradually permeated its limestone carvings, and conservators warn that unchecked decay could jeopardize the entire structure.","at":"一代又一代的石匠辛勤勞動，才完成這座高聳的哥德式宏偉建築，其尖塔至今仍是全市最著名的地標；然而酸雨已逐漸滲入其石灰岩雕刻，修復人員警告，若任由侵蝕持續，整座建築都可能岌岌可危。"},{"w":"extant","p":"adj.","d":"Still in existence.","c":"現存的；尚存的","s":"Of the forty-seven letters that the biographer had documented as having been written during the composer's final decade, only eleven were currently extant, the remainder having been destroyed by the composer's own instruction before his death, an act that continued to frustrate scholars seeking a complete understanding of his late creative period.","t":"在傳記作家記錄的作曲家最後十年所寫的四十七封信中，目前只有十一封現存，其餘的已按照作曲家在去世前的親自指示被銷毀，這一行為繼續讓試圖全面了解他晚期創作時期的學者感到沮喪。","as":"Although the prolific Greek dramatist Sophocles is said to have written more than one hundred plays, only seven are extant today, so scholars must rely on garbled fragments and secondhand summaries to surmise what the lost works contained.","at":"據說多產的希臘劇作家索福克勒斯寫過一百多部劇本，但今天只有七部留存下來；因此學者們只能依靠殘缺不全的片段和二手摘要，來推測那些失傳作品的內容。"},{"w":"indict","p":"v.","d":"To formally accuse of a crime.","c":"控告；起訴","s":"The grand jury voted to indict all four defendants on multiple counts of conspiracy and financial fraud, a decision that the defendants' legal team immediately characterised as politically motivated and pledged to challenge through both pre-trial motions and, if necessary, a full evidentiary hearing before a different panel.","t":"大陪審團投票決定對所有四名被告提出多項共謀和金融欺詐罪指控，被告的法律團隊立即將這一決定定性為出於政治動機，並承諾通過審前動議以及在必要時通過在不同小組面前的完整證據聽證來提出挑戰。","as":"A grand jury voted to indict the former mayor on charges of fraud, alleging that he had fabricated invoices to conceal his complicity in a kickback scheme that had operated with apparent impunity throughout his time in office.","at":"大陪審團投票決定起訴前市長詐欺罪，指控他偽造發票，以掩飾自己參與一項回扣計畫；而這項計畫在他整個任期內似乎一直逍遙法外地運作著。"},{"w":"levity","p":"n.","d":"Treating something seriously with humour.","c":"輕浮；輕率","s":"The chief constable's attempt to inject some levity into what had been an unexpectedly tense press conference — with an ill-judged comment about the weather — was met with stony silence from journalists who regarded the remark as indicative of a fundamental failure to appreciate the gravity of the situation being discussed.","t":"警察局長試圖在一場出乎意料地緊張的新聞發布會中注入一些輕浮——用一個判斷失當的關於天氣的評論——遭到了記者們冷漠的沉默，他們認為這句話表明根本未能意識到正在討論的情況的嚴重性。","as":"Although some mourners welcomed the brief respite that the speaker's levity offered, others, still distraught over the sudden death, admonished him afterward for telling jokes during such a solemn ceremony.","at":"雖然有些弔唁者樂於藉著致詞者的幽默得到片刻喘息，但另一些仍因這場猝逝而心煩意亂的人，事後卻責備他竟在如此莊嚴的儀式上說笑話。"},{"w":"lugubrious","p":"adj.","d":"Looking or sounding sad and dismal.","c":"悲哀的；令人傷心的","s":"The detective's characteristically lugubrious expression made it impossible to read his reaction to the evidence that had just been presented, a studied neutrality that his colleagues had learned over decades of partnership meant nothing in particular — he wore the same funereal look when examining a parking ticket complaint as when confronting a major crime scene.","t":"偵探一貫悲哀的表情使人無法讀出他對剛才呈現的證據的反應，這種經過研究的中立性是他的同事在幾十年的合作中學到的——他在審查停車罰款投訴時和面對重大犯罪現場時都帶著同樣的喪葬般的表情。","as":"The film's lugubrious soundtrack, dominated by slow cellos and doleful choral chants, suits its tragic subject, yet several critics found the relentless gloom so interminable that they struggled to remain engrossed in the story.","at":"這部電影的配樂陰鬱哀戚，以緩慢的大提琴和悲傷的合唱詠唱為主，與其悲劇題材相當契合；然而好幾位影評人認為，這種無止盡的陰沉冗長乏味，讓他們很難持續投入劇情。"},{"w":"maudlin","p":"adj.","d":"Sentimental in a foolish or weak way.","c":"傷感流淚的；感情脆弱的","s":"The anniversary broadcast degenerated from a dignified commemoration into a maudlin spectacle of competitive grief that, in the view of many survivors, trivialised the actual complexity of the historical events being remembered by reducing them to a series of emotionally manipulative narrative vignettes.","t":"週年紀念廣播從一個有尊嚴的紀念活動退化為一場競爭性悲傷的傷感場面，在許多倖存者看來，通過將歷史事件減縮為一系列情感操縱性的敘述短片，使被紀念的實際複雜的歷史事件變得微不足道。","as":"Although the novel's early chapters portray grief with understated nuance, its final scene lapses into maudlin sentimentality, piling up tearful reunions and deathbed confessions that seem designed to elicit tears rather than offer any poignant insight.","at":"雖然這部小說的前幾章以含蓄細膩的筆法描寫悲傷，結尾卻流於濫情，堆砌淚眼相擁的重逢與臨終告白；這些情節似乎只為了賺人熱淚，而非提供任何真正動人的洞見。"},{"w":"nebulous","p":"adj.","d":"Not clear, hazy, vague.","c":"朦朧的；模糊的","s":"The policy paper's proposals were so nebulous that it was impossible to determine what specific operational changes they would require, a vagueness that sceptical commentators attributed less to genuine conceptual complexity than to a deliberate desire to avoid committing to anything that could be specifically criticised or held against the authors.","t":"政策文件的提案如此模糊，以至於無法確定它們需要什麼具體的操作性變化，持懷疑態度的評論員將這種模糊性歸因於不是真正的概念複雜性，而是刻意希望避免承諾任何可能被特別批評或對作者不利的事情。","as":"Voters grew frustrated with the candidate's nebulous promises of change, which offered no tangible details about how she would reduce unemployment or pay for the comprehensive reforms she claimed the country so urgently needed.","at":"選民對這位候選人含糊不清的改革承諾越來越感到失望，因為她始終沒有提出任何具體細節，說明她將如何降低失業率，或如何支付她聲稱國家迫切需要的全面改革。"},{"w":"omnivorous","p":"adj.","d":"Eating both plants and animals.","c":"雜食的；無所不吃的","s":"Her omnivorous intellectual appetite — encompassing medieval theology, contemporary neuroscience, architectural history, and competitive mathematics with apparently equal enthusiasm — made her both the most stimulating colleague in the faculty and the most difficult to schedule, as she invariably found every departmental meeting relevant to her current thinking.","t":"她對中世紀神學、當代神經科學、建築歷史和競技數學顯然具有同等熱情的無所不食的智識胃口，使她既是教職員工中最具啟發性的同事，也是最難安排的同事，因為她總是發現每個部門會議都與她當前的思考相關。","as":"Because raccoons are omnivorous, eating everything from fruit and insects to discarded leftovers, they have adapted with remarkable alacrity to urban life, and these voracious scavengers now thrive wherever garbage bins abound and natural predators are scarce.","at":"由於浣熊是雜食性動物，從水果、昆蟲到丟棄的剩菜無所不吃，牠們以驚人的速度適應了都市生活；如今，這些貪吃的拾荒者在垃圾桶林立、天敵稀少的地方都能繁衍興盛。"},{"w":"pesky","p":"adj.","d":"Causing irritation.","c":"討厭的；煩人的","s":"The software update had been intended to improve security but had introduced a series of pesky bugs that prevented the document management system from saving files correctly — a malfunction that, while not catastrophic, had generated hundreds of support tickets and significant user frustration across the organisation.","t":"軟件更新本是為了改善安全性，但引入了一系列討厭的漏洞，阻止文檔管理系統正確保存文件——這一故障雖然不是災難性的，但已在整個組織中產生了數百個支持票和大量用戶沮喪。","as":"Rather than relying on pernicious chemical sprays, many organic farmers now release ladybugs to control pesky aphids, a feasible strategy that obviates the need for pesticides while sparing the bees that pollinate their crops.","at":"許多有機農民不再依賴有害的化學噴劑，而是釋放瓢蟲來對付惱人的蚜蟲；這種可行的策略不但免除了使用殺蟲劑的必要，也保護了為作物授粉的蜜蜂。"},{"w":"puissant","p":"adj.","d":"Having great power or influence.","c":"強大的；有權力的","s":"The treaty was negotiated between three puissant regional powers whose combined economic and military capacity exceeded that of all other signatories combined, a disparity that critics argued fundamentally compromised the agreement's legitimacy as an instrument of collective governance rather than great-power management.","t":"該條約在三個強大的地區大國之間談判，其綜合經濟和軍事能力超過所有其他簽署國的總和，批評者認為這種差距從根本上損害了協議作為集體治理工具而非大國管理工具的合法性。","as":"Once a puissant empire whose fleets dominated distant oceans, the kingdom gradually lost its colonies through a series of abortive wars and profligate spending at court, until its decline seemed inexorable even to its most loyal subjects.","at":"這個王國曾是艦隊稱霸遠洋的強大帝國，卻因一連串失敗的戰爭與宮廷的揮霍無度而逐漸失去殖民地，最後連最忠誠的子民都認為它的衰落已無法挽回。"},{"w":"redolent","p":"adj.","d":"Strongly suggestive of, fragrant.","c":"芬芳的；使人想起...的","s":"The old harbour district remained deeply redolent of its maritime past — in the salt smell of the air, the texture of the cobblestones worn smooth by generations of fishermen's boots, and the particular quality of morning light falling on facades that had been painted the same colours for two hundred years.","t":"古老的港區仍然深深地讓人想起它的海洋過去——在空氣的鹹味中，在幾代漁民靴子磨光的鵝卵石的質感中，以及在照射到兩百年來始終如一地塗著相同顏色的外牆上的晨光的特殊質量中。","as":"The narrow alleys of the old spice market, redolent of cinnamon and cloves, still awaken intense nostalgia in expatriates who return after years abroad, for whom the fragrance offers solace and a link to a childhood that has otherwise vanished.","at":"老香料市場狹窄的巷弄裡飄散著肉桂與丁香的芬芳，仍會在旅居海外多年後歸來的遊子心中喚起強烈的懷舊之情；對他們而言，這股香氣帶來慰藉，也是通往那段早已消逝之童年的唯一連結。"},{"w":"repose","p":"n.","d":"A state of rest or tranquillity.","c":"休息；睡眠","s":"The formal portrait showed the statesman in an attitude of studied repose, but those who knew him well recognised the controlled tension in his posture — the slight forward lean, the clasped hands — as the characteristic bearing of a man who had never in his adult life found genuine relaxation entirely natural or comfortable.","t":"正式肖像展示了這位政治家處於一種刻意的休息姿態，但了解他的人從他的姿勢中認出了受控制的緊張——略微前傾、交握的雙手——這是一個在成年生活中從未真正發現真正放鬆完全自然或舒適的男人的典型儀態。","as":"After a grueling campaign marked by acrimonious debates, the exhausted senator retreated to a secluded mountain haven, seeking a few weeks of repose far from the reporters who had harassed her relentlessly for months.","at":"經歷了一場充滿激烈辯論、令人筋疲力盡的選戰後，疲憊的參議員退隱到一處僻靜的山間避風港，希望能遠離數月來不斷糾纏她的記者，好好休養幾個星期。"},{"w":"reviled","p":"adj.","d":"Hated and criticised.","c":"辱罵；斥責","s":"Once reviled as a collaborator and opportunist by the resistance movement, the historian's nuanced reassessment of the official's wartime record — drawing on newly available archival sources from three countries — suggested a far more complex and morally ambiguous picture than the binary narrative of heroism and betrayal that had dominated public memory.","t":"歷史學家對官員戰時記錄的細緻重新評估——借助來自三個國家新獲得的檔案資料——曾經被抵抗運動斥責為合作者和機會主義者，提出了一個比主導公眾記憶的英雄主義和背叛的二元敘述複雜得多、道德上更加模糊的圖景。","as":"Reviled by many fellow physicians for insisting that doctors wash their hands before delivering babies, Ignaz Semmelweis died in obscurity, yet his once controversial claim is now deemed an incontrovertible pillar of modern medicine.","at":"塞麥爾維斯因堅持醫師在接生前必須洗手，而遭到許多同行醫師的唾棄，最終默默無聞地離世；然而他當年備受爭議的主張，如今已被視為現代醫學中無可辯駁的基石。"},{"w":"sultry","p":"adj.","d":"Oppressively hot and humid.","c":"悶熱的；風騷的","s":"The sultry August heat had transformed the normally energetic city into a languorous landscape of shade-seekers and slow-moving crowds, the usual urgency of the financial district replaced by a collective torpor that lasted from mid-morning until the brief respite of a late afternoon thunderstorm.","t":"悶熱的八月熱浪將通常充滿活力的城市轉變為一個尋找陰涼的人和緩慢移動的人群組成的倦怠景觀，金融區通常的緊迫感被一種從上午中段持續到短暫的傍晚雷陣雨片刻喘息的集體遲鈍所取代。","as":"During the sultry monsoon season, laborers in the rice paddies endure the drudgery of transplanting seedlings under oppressive humidity, and some succumb to heat exhaustion despite taking frequent respites in the shade of nearby trees.","at":"在悶熱的季風季節裡，稻田裡的工人得在令人窒息的濕氣中從事插秧的苦差事；儘管他們經常到附近樹蔭下歇息，仍有些人因熱衰竭而倒下。"},{"w":"trenchant","p":"adj.","d":"Vigorous or incisive in expression.","c":"銳利的；一針見血的","s":"Her most trenchant observation was that the proposed solution addressed the symptom rather than the cause — an insight delivered with such clarity and economy of language that it immediately reframed the entire discussion and rendered most of the preceding two hours of deliberation irrelevant.","t":"她最一針見血的觀察是，擬議的解決方案解決的是症狀而不是原因——這一見解以如此清晰和簡潔的語言表達，立即重新框架了整個討論，並使前兩個小時的大部分審議變得無關緊要。","as":"George Orwell's trenchant essays exposed how politicians use euphemism to disguise brutal policies, and his incisive analysis of political language remains strikingly salient in an age of slogans and spin.","at":"喬治．歐威爾一針見血的文章揭露了政客如何用委婉說法掩飾殘酷的政策；在這個充斥口號與操弄話術的時代，他對政治語言的犀利分析依然格外切中要害。"},{"w":"unabated","p":"adj.","d":"Without any reduction in intensity.","c":"不減退的；未減弱的","s":"Despite three years of intensive international pressure, the government's crackdown on civil society organisations continued unabated, with new arrests reported in each successive month and the legislative framework governing civil liberties progressively tightened in ways that effectively placed organised dissent outside the boundaries of legal activity.","t":"儘管三年來受到國際社會的強烈壓力，政府對民間社會組織的打壓仍未減退，每個連續月份都有新的逮捕報告，管理公民自由的立法框架逐步收緊，有效地將有組織的異見置於合法活動的邊界之外。","as":"Despite years of international pledges to curtail emissions, the rise in atmospheric carbon dioxide has continued largely unabated, and many climate scientists regard each new record as an ominous harbinger of more extreme weather to come.","at":"儘管國際間多年來一再承諾減少排放，大氣中二氧化碳濃度的上升卻大致有增無減；許多氣候科學家將每一次創下的新紀錄，都視為更多極端天氣即將來臨的不祥預兆。"},{"w":"vicissitudes","p":"n.","d":"Changes in circumstances, especially difficulties.","c":"變遷；興衰","s":"The memoir traced the vicissitudes of a remarkable career that had encompassed extraordinary success and near-total professional ruin within the space of a decade, the author's retrospective analysis revealing how contingent both extremes had been on factors entirely beyond his control rather than any consistent quality of his own judgment.","t":"回憶錄追蹤了一個非凡職業生涯的變遷，在十年間包含了非凡的成功和幾乎完全的職業毀滅，作者的回顧性分析揭示了這兩個極端如何取決於完全超出他控制的因素，而不是他自己判斷的任何一貫品質。","as":"Through all the vicissitudes of war, exile, and poverty, the poet persevered in her craft, composing verses under the duress of censorship that nonetheless retained a remarkably sanguine faith in human decency.","at":"歷經戰爭、流亡與貧困種種的人生起伏，這位詩人始終堅持創作；即使在審查制度的壓迫下寫詩，她的作品仍對人性的善良保有驚人的樂觀信念。"}]},{"unit":21,"cards":[{"w":"scion","p":"n.","d":"A young member of a noble family; a descendant.","c":"子孫；後代","s":"The scion of the once-eminent banking dynasty arrived at the prestigious auction with characteristic alacrity, determined to reclaim the ancestral portrait that had been sold during the turbulent years of the family's financial collapse in the previous century.","t":"這位曾經傑出銀行世家的後代充滿活力地來到享有聲望的拍賣會，決心收回上世紀家族金融崩潰動盪歲月中被出售的祖先肖像。","as":"As the scion of an affluent banking dynasty, the young heir surprised his family by eschewing the prestigious positions they offered him and instead devoting his inheritance to clinics for indigent farmers in remote villages.","at":"身為富裕銀行世家的後代，這位年輕繼承人出乎家人意料，拒絕了他們提供的顯赫職位，反而將遺產投入為偏遠村落貧困農民設立的診所。"},{"w":"indoctrinate","p":"v.","d":"To teach a person to accept a set of beliefs.","c":"灌輸；教導","s":"The regime systematically attempted to indoctrinate every generation of citizens with the same nebulous ideology, its mendacious propaganda so permeating daily life that even critical thinkers found it excruciating to separate genuine belief from conditioned response.","t":"政權系統地試圖向每一代公民灌輸同樣模糊的意識形態，其虛假宣傳如此滲透日常生活，以至於即使是批判性思考者也發現很難區分真正的信仰和條件反射。","as":"Totalitarian regimes of the twentieth century often sought to indoctrinate children through school textbooks that disparaged opposition and praised the leader as a paragon of virtue, a strategy designed to repress critical thinking before it could become overt.","at":"二十世紀的極權政權常透過學校教科書灌輸兒童思想；這些教科書貶低異議，並把領袖讚頌為美德的典範，目的是在批判性思考公開萌芽之前就加以壓制。"},{"w":"opulence","p":"n.","d":"Great wealth and luxuriousness.","c":"財富；富裕","s":"The opulence of the new estate contrasted grotesquely with the destitution that flourished just beyond its ornate gates, the mammoth mansion's sumptuous interiors visible from the cramped dwellings where emaciated workers sheltered after their exhausting daily labour.","t":"新莊園的財富與其華麗大門外盛行的赤貧形成了怪誕的對比，龐大豪宅奢華的內部從疲憊的日常勞動後筋疲力盡工人棲身的狹窄住所中清晰可見。","as":"Visitors to the palace of Versailles are often astonished by the opulence of its gilded halls, yet historians note that such ostentatious display was financed by heavy taxes that exacerbated the privation of ordinary French peasants.","at":"參觀凡爾賽宮的遊客常驚嘆於其金碧輝煌大廳的奢華富麗，但歷史學家指出，這種炫耀式的排場是靠沉重賦稅支撐的，加劇了法國一般農民的貧困。"},{"w":"obsequious","p":"adj.","d":"Excessively eager to please or obey.","c":"諂媚的；奉承的","s":"The obsequious assistant shadowed the visiting dignitary with a vigilance that many observers found more suffocating than helpful, his fulsome compliments and profligate attentiveness generating visible chagrin in the guest who had explicitly requested a less ceremonial reception.","t":"這位諂媚的助手以許多觀察者認為更令人窒息而非有益的警覺性跟隨訪問官員，他過分誇張的讚美和揮霍的殷勤在明確要求較不正式接待的客人身上引起了明顯的懊惱。","as":"The courtier's obsequious manner, which included bowing low and praising every inane remark the king made, earned him a comfortable sinecure but also the disdain of rivals who construed his flattery as a form of duplicity.","at":"這名朝臣卑躬屈膝的態度——包括深深鞠躬、稱讚國王每一句空洞的話——為他換來一份輕鬆的閒差，卻也招來對手的鄙視，他們把他的奉承視為一種表裡不一的手段。"},{"w":"fulsome","p":"adj.","d":"Excessively complimentary, insincere.","c":"過度誇張的；令人作嘔的","s":"The fulsome praise heaped upon the mediocre novel by its publisher's marketing department struck every incisive critic as blatant promotional hyperbole, the verbose campaign further disparaging the author's modest genuine achievement by surrounding it with claims no serious reader could credit.","t":"出版商市場部門對這部平庸小說堆砌的過度讚美，在每位敏銳的批評家看來都是明目張膽的促銷誇大其詞，冗長的宣傳活動通過將作者適度的真實成就與任何嚴肅讀者都無法相信的說法相伴而行，進一步貶低了它。","as":"The critic dismissed the publisher's fulsome praise of the debut novel as a mere pretext for boosting sales, noting that the book's verbose prose and lackluster characters hardly merited such exaggerated acclaim.","at":"評論家認為出版社對這部處女作的過度吹捧只是促銷的藉口，並指出這本書文字冗長、角色乏味，根本配不上如此誇張的讚譽。"},{"w":"lush","p":"adj.","d":"Luxuriously rich, elaborate, or profuse.","c":"茂盛的；奢華的","s":"The lush rainforest canopy that had once formed a sanctuary for innumerable indigenous species was being inexorably reduced by rampant commercial logging, each cleared hectare representing a compound loss of biodiversity whose full consequences scientists struggled to prognosticate with confidence.","t":"曾經為無數本土物種提供庇護的茂盛雨林樹冠正在被猖獗的商業伐木不可阻擋地減少，每一公頃被清除的土地代表著生物多樣性的複合損失，科學家們難以自信地預測其全部後果。","as":"The lush rainforests of the Amazon serve as a habitat for a myriad of species, but ecologists warn that rampant logging could turn these regions into barren scrubland within just a few generations.","at":"亞馬遜茂密的雨林是無數物種的棲息地，但生態學家警告，猖獗的伐木可能在短短幾個世代內，就把這些地區變成貧瘠的灌木荒地。"},{"w":"destitution","p":"n.","d":"The state of extreme poverty.","c":"貧困；赤貧","s":"Widespread destitution had become the most ominous harbinger of the regime's ultimate collapse, the emaciated faces of children and the wan expressions of parents too exhausted to implore passing officials for help conveying a human catastrophe that no euphemism could adequately conceal.","t":"廣泛的赤貧已成為政權最終崩潰最不祥的先兆，孩子們消瘦的臉龐和太過疲憊以至於無法懇求路過官員幫助的父母蒼白的表情，傳達出任何委婉語都無法充分掩蓋的人道主義災難。","as":"During the Great Depression, the sudden liquidation of thousands of banks plunged many once-prosperous families into destitution, forcing them to seek solace in soup kitchens and makeshift shelters that offered only a brief respite from hunger.","at":"經濟大蕭條期間，數千家銀行突然倒閉清算，使許多原本富裕的家庭陷入赤貧，只能在施粥所和臨時收容所中尋求慰藉，而那裡只能讓他們短暫擺脫飢餓。"},{"w":"ponder","p":"v.","d":"To think carefully and seriously.","c":"仔細考慮","s":"She sat in the garden for over an hour, pondering the cryptic message that had arrived that morning — its elusive meaning resisting every analytical approach she tried, the more she scrutinised each word the more labyrinthine the possible interpretations became.","t":"她在花園裡坐了超過一個小時，仔細考慮那天早上收到的神秘信息——它難以捉摸的含義抵制著她嘗試的每一種分析方法，她越仔細審查每個詞，可能的解釋就越像迷宮般複雜。","as":"Before signing the treaty, the president paused to ponder whether its restrictive clauses might jeopardize the nation's sovereignty or whether rejecting it would precipitate an even more turbulent conflict with neighboring states.","at":"簽署條約之前，總統停下來仔細思考：其中的限制性條款是否會危及國家主權，或者拒絕簽署是否會引發與鄰國更動盪的衝突。"},{"w":"supplication","p":"n.","d":"An earnest request or prayer.","c":"懇求；祈求","s":"The delegation arrived not with demands but with supplication, their forlorn expressions and careful choice of conciliatory language making clear that they came as petitioners rather than adversaries, imploring the committee to reconsider the landmark ruling before its consequences became irreversible.","t":"代表團不是帶著要求而是帶著懇求而來，他們孤苦的表情和謹慎選擇的和解性語言清楚地表明他們是作為請願者而非對手而來，懇求委員會在其後果變得不可逆轉之前重新考慮這一里程碑式的裁決。","as":"Kneeling before the statue, the pilgrims offered an earnest supplication for rain, for the drought had become so severe that crops withered, malnutrition was ubiquitous, and the villagers' doleful faces betrayed an ominous sense of despair.","at":"朝聖者跪在神像前，誠心祈求降雨；因為旱災嚴重到農作物枯萎、營養不良隨處可見，村民憂傷的面容流露出一種不祥的絕望。"},{"w":"decadence","p":"n.","d":"Moral or cultural decline and self-indulgence.","c":"墮落；衰退","s":"Historians continue to debate whether the empire's decadence was an inherent consequence of its opulence or a symptom of the pernicious political fragmentation that had gradually subjugated every institution designed to maintain civic virtue and prevent the profligate consumption of public resources.","t":"歷史學家繼續爭論帝國的墮落是其財富固有的後果，還是逐漸征服了每一個旨在維護公民美德並防止揮霍公共資源的制度的有害政治分裂的症狀。","as":"Some Roman writers blamed the empire's decline on the decadence of its elite, who indulged in sumptuous banquets and profligate spending while the frontier garrisons, poorly paid and increasingly fractious, struggled to repulse invaders.","at":"一些羅馬作家將帝國的衰落歸咎於菁英階層的墮落：他們沉溺於奢華的宴席、揮霍無度，而邊境軍團卻薪餉微薄、日益難以駕馭，苦苦抵擋入侵者。"},{"w":"penance","p":"n.","d":"Voluntary self-punishment to atone for a fault.","c":"懺悔；贖罪","s":"He performed years of quiet penance for the egregious wrong he had committed, not through any dramatic public gesture but through the assiduous and largely anonymous donation of his considerable wealth to institutions serving the community he had once so gravely harmed.","t":"他通過多年安靜的贖罪來彌補他所犯的極端錯誤，不是通過任何戲劇性的公開姿態，而是通過勤勉且在很大程度上匿名地將他可觀的財富捐贈給服務他曾經嚴重傷害過的社區的機構。","as":"In medieval Europe, a nobleman who had committed an egregious sin might perform penance by walking barefoot to a distant shrine, a grueling peregrination meant to demonstrate his remorse and elicit forgiveness from the church.","at":"在中世紀歐洲，犯下嚴重罪過的貴族可能會以赤腳步行前往遙遠聖地的方式來贖罪；這段艱苦的朝聖旅程意在表明他的悔悟，並求得教會的寬恕。"},{"w":"ascetic","p":"n.","d":"A person who practises severe self-discipline.","c":"苦行的；禁慾者","s":"The ascetic philosopher's frugal lifestyle drew admiration from some and bewilderment from others — his deliberate rejection of opulence, his indifference to comfort, and his laconic dismissal of material acquisition as inherently inimical to genuine wisdom were all integral to a coherent philosophical position.","t":"這位苦行哲學家的節儉生活方式引起了一些人的欽佩和其他人的困惑——他有意識地拒絕財富、對舒適的漠視，以及他簡潔地將物質積累視為真正智慧的固有對立的態度，都是連貫哲學立場不可或缺的組成部分。","as":"The ascetic renounced all worldly comforts, living in a mountain cave on a frugal diet of bread and water, yet pilgrims who came to importune him for advice found him surprisingly gregarious and quick to quip.","at":"這位苦行者捨棄一切世俗享受，住在山洞裡，只靠麵包和水的簡樸飲食度日；然而前來懇求他指點的朝聖者卻發現，他出奇地健談，而且妙語連珠。"},{"w":"desultory","p":"adj.","d":"Lacking purpose, disconnected, random.","c":"散漫的；斷斷續續的","s":"The negotiations had proceeded in a characteristically desultory fashion for three frustrating months — sporadic meetings producing no substantive progress, each session more perfunctory than the last, until a fortuitous change in the political landscape suddenly galvanised both parties into genuine engagement.","t":"談判以典型的散漫方式進行了令人沮喪的三個月——零星的會議沒有產生實質性進展，每次會議都比上一次更敷衍，直到政治格局的偶然變化突然激勵雙方真正投入。","as":"After months of desultory negotiations in which delegates traded perfunctory remarks and seldom addressed the salient issues, both sides finally concurred that a more structured agenda was necessary if any agreement was to be reached.","at":"經過數月散漫的談判，代表們只交換敷衍的言辭、很少觸及關鍵問題，雙方終於一致認為，若想達成任何協議，就必須訂出更有條理的議程。"},{"w":"disciple","p":"n.","d":"A follower of a teacher or leader.","c":"門徒；信徒","s":"The philosopher's most devoted disciple proved more adroit at popularising his mentor's ideas than the original thinker had ever been, translating abstruse theoretical concepts into accessible language with a virtuosity that expanded the movement's influence far beyond the academic community where it had originated.","t":"這位哲學家最忠誠的門徒被證明比原來的思想家更善於推廣導師的思想，以精湛的技藝將深奧的理論概念翻譯成易懂的語言，將運動的影響力擴展到遠超其起源的學術社區之外。","as":"Plato, the most celebrated disciple of Socrates, recorded his teacher's dialogues with meticulous care, and scholars still scrutinize these texts to discern which ideas belonged to the master and which were Plato's own embellishments.","at":"蘇格拉底最著名的門徒柏拉圖一絲不苟地記錄了老師的對話，學者至今仍仔細研究這些文本，試圖分辨哪些思想屬於老師，哪些是柏拉圖自己的潤飾。"},{"w":"metamorphosis","p":"n.","d":"A dramatic change in form or nature.","c":"變態；蛻變","s":"The city's metamorphosis from an industrial wasteland into a vibrant cultural quarter had been neither swift nor seamless — a turbulent process spanning two decades, punctuated by acrimonious disputes between developers and conservationists that had at various points threatened to preclude any meaningful regeneration.","t":"這座城市從工業廢墟到充滿活力的文化區的蛻變既不迅速也不無縫——一個跨越二十年的動盪過程，中間穿插著開發商和保護主義者之間嚴厲的爭論，這些爭論在不同時間點威脅要阻止任何有意義的重建。","as":"The caterpillar's metamorphosis into a butterfly, a process encoded in genes inherent to the species, radically modifies the insect's body as larval tissues dissolve inside the chrysalis and reorganize into wings, antennae, and other delicate components.","at":"毛毛蟲蛻變成蝴蝶的過程，是由該物種本身固有的基因所編碼；在這個過程中，幼蟲組織在蛹內溶解，再重組成翅膀、觸角和其他精細的構造，徹底改變了昆蟲的身體。"},{"w":"bona fide","p":"adj.","d":"Genuine, real, done in good faith.","c":"真實的；真誠的","s":"The auction house insisted that every lot in the forthcoming sale represented a bona fide historical artefact with incontrovertible provenance documentation, having scrutinised each item's ownership history with meticulous care following a series of controversies involving forgeries that had tainted the institution's prestigious reputation.","t":"拍賣行堅稱即將舉行的拍賣會中的每件拍品都是具有無可辯駁出處文件的真實歷史文物，在一系列涉及偽造品污損該機構享有聲望聲譽的爭議後，仔細審查了每件物品的所有權歷史。","as":"Art experts spent years trying to corroborate that the newly discovered sketch was a bona fide work by Leonardo, since the market had recently been inundated with skillful forgeries designed to dupe gullible collectors.","at":"藝術專家花了數年時間，試圖證實這幅新發現的素描確實是達文西的真跡，因為市場上最近充斥著專門用來欺騙輕信收藏家的高明贗品。"},{"w":"salvation","p":"n.","d":"Deliverance from danger or ruin.","c":"拯救；救贖","s":"For the beleaguered community, the unexpected funding represented nothing short of salvation, arriving at precisely the moment when the most pessimistic members had begun to accept that the inevitable closure of all local services would compound their existing hardships beyond any prospect of recovery.","t":"對於被圍困的社區來說，意外的資金不亞於救贖，恰好在最悲觀的成員開始接受所有當地服務不可避免關閉將使他們現有的困難複雜化到任何復甦前景之外的時刻到來。","as":"For the declining fishing town, the new marine research institute proved to be its economic salvation, providing stable remuneration to residents who had endured years of financial vicissitudes and reviving a community many had deemed doomed to obsolescence.","at":"對這座日漸沒落的漁村而言，新成立的海洋研究所成了經濟上的救星，不僅為歷經多年經濟起伏的居民提供穩定的收入，也讓這個許多人認定註定要被淘汰的社區重獲生機。"},{"w":"materialism","p":"n.","d":"A tendency to consider material things more important than spiritual values.","c":"物質主義","s":"The philosopher argued that rampant materialism had created a paradox at the heart of affluent societies — unprecedented abundance generating unprecedented anxiety, the incessant acquisition of tangible goods failing to provide the enduring satisfaction that its proponents had always promised but never delivered.","t":"哲學家認為，猖獗的物質主義在富裕社會的核心創造了一個悖論——前所未有的豐富產生了前所未有的焦慮，對有形商品的持續獲取未能提供其支持者始終承諾但從未兌現的持久滿足感。","as":"Critics of modern consumer culture contend that materialism fosters a relentless cupidity, leading people to crave a plethora of possessions even as studies suggest that such acquisitions provide only a fleeting and shallow sense of contentment.","at":"現代消費文化的批評者主張，物質主義助長了永不滿足的貪婪，使人們渴望擁有過多的物品，即使研究顯示這些購買只能帶來短暫而膚淺的滿足感。"},{"w":"nurture","p":"v.","d":"To care for and encourage growth.","c":"養育；培育","s":"The nurture of genuine scientific curiosity in young people required something more profound than the mundane transmission of factual knowledge — it demanded teachers who could perceive latent talent, cultivate intrinsic motivation, and create conditions where intellectual risk-taking was celebrated rather than penalised.","t":"在年輕人中培育真正的科學好奇心需要比日常傳遞事實知識更深刻的東西——它需要能夠察覺潛在才能、培養內在動力，並創造出智識冒險受到讚揚而非懲罰的環境的教師。","as":"Montessori educators believe that teachers should nurture a child's innate curiosity rather than stifle it with rigid drills, arguing that even a precocious student will become timorous and withdrawn if every spontaneous question is met with a reprimand.","at":"蒙特梭利教育者認為，教師應該培育孩子與生俱來的好奇心，而不是用死板的練習扼殺它；他們主張，如果每個自發的提問都換來斥責，即使是早慧的學生也會變得膽怯退縮。"},{"w":"nirvana","p":"n.","d":"A state of perfect peace and happiness.","c":"涅槃；解脫","s":"For the exhausted researcher, the moment of finally comprehending the elusive theoretical connection she had been pursuing for seven years felt like intellectual nirvana — a sudden cessation of the chronic anxiety that had accompanied her through every frustrating dead end and every desultory false start.","t":"對於這位精疲力竭的研究人員來說，終於理解她七年來一直追求的難以捉摸的理論聯繫的那一刻，感覺就像智識上的涅槃——伴隨她走過每一個令人沮喪的死胡同和每一個散漫的錯誤開始的慢性焦慮的突然停止。","as":"In Buddhist teaching, nirvana is the ultimate goal of spiritual practice, a tranquil state that, according to the Buddha, can be attained only after the cessation of the desires and illusions that afflict ordinary human existence.","at":"在佛教教義中，涅槃是修行的終極目標，依佛陀所言，這是一種唯有在欲望與幻象止息之後才能達到的寧靜境界，而這些欲望與幻象正困擾著凡人的日常存在。"}]},{"unit":22,"cards":[{"w":"juxtapose","p":"v.","d":"To place side by side for contrast.","c":"並列","s":"The curator deliberately juxtaposed the scion's extravagant portrait against an emaciated figure from the same era, the bona fide contrast between opulence and destitution creating a visceral impact that no amount of verbose explanatory text could have achieved as effectively.","t":"策展人故意將這位後代奢華的肖像與同一時代消瘦的人物並列，真實的財富與貧困之間的對比創造了任何冗長的解釋性文字都無法如此有效地實現的直觀衝擊。","as":"The museum curator chose to juxtapose ancient indigenous pottery with contemporary ceramic sculptures, a provocative arrangement that compelled even cursory visitors to ponder how ancestral techniques have been both preserved and reinvented over the centuries.","at":"策展人刻意將古老的原住民陶器與當代陶瓷雕塑並列展出，這種發人深省的安排，讓即使只是匆匆瀏覽的參觀者也不禁思考：祖傳技藝如何在數百年間既被保存，又被重新詮釋。"},{"w":"plight","p":"n.","d":"A dangerous or difficult situation.","c":"困境；苦境","s":"The plight of the displaced farming communities had become so ominous that even the most phlegmatic government officials could no longer maintain their desultory engagement with the crisis, the mounting evidence of systemic failure finally compelling a comprehensive policy review.","t":"流離失所農業社區的困境已變得如此不祥，即使是最冷靜的政府官員也無法再維持他們對危機漫不經心的參與，越來越多的系統性失敗證據最終迫使進行全面的政策審查。","as":"The documentary drew global attention to the plight of refugees stranded at the border, whose emaciated children and makeshift shelters posed a poignant challenge to the governments that had relegated the crisis to a mere footnote.","at":"這部紀錄片讓全世界關注滯留在邊境的難民的困境：他們骨瘦如柴的孩子與臨時搭建的棲身之所，對那些把這場危機當成無關緊要小事的政府，構成了令人心酸的質問。"},{"w":"covert","p":"adj.","d":"Not openly acknowledged, hidden.","c":"隱蔽的；秘密的","s":"The covert surveillance operation had proceeded with such adroit subterfuge that even the most vigilant members of the target organisation remained entirely unaware for eleven months that their internal communications were being systematically intercepted and analysed.","t":"這次隱蔽的監視行動以如此熟練的詭計進行，以至於目標組織中最警覺的成員在十一個月內完全沒有意識到他們的內部通信正在被系統地攔截和分析。","as":"During the Cold War, intelligence agencies conducted covert operations to oust unfriendly governments, and many of these clandestine schemes, once exposed, became a source of lasting chagrin for the nations that had orchestrated them.","at":"冷戰期間，各國情報機構進行隱密行動以推翻不友好的政府；這些祕密計畫一旦曝光，往往成為主導國家長久的難堪。"},{"w":"cope","p":"v.","d":"To deal effectively with something difficult.","c":"應付；處理","s":"Many survivors found they could cope with the immediate aftermath of the disaster, but struggled profoundly with the protracted psychological plight that followed — the myriad latent anxieties that only emerged months later, when the initial solidarity of the crisis period had dissolved into ordinary solitude.","t":"許多倖存者發現他們能夠應付災難的直接後果，但卻深深地掙扎於隨之而來的長期心理困境——無數潛在的焦慮只在幾個月後才出現，當危機時期最初的團結已溶解為普通的孤獨。","as":"Psychologists have found that resilient individuals cope with hardship not by ignoring their distress but by seeking solace from confidants and reframing even an excruciating setback as a reason to persevere.","at":"心理學家發現，韌性強的人面對困境時並非忽視自己的痛苦，而是向知己尋求慰藉，甚至把極其痛苦的挫折重新看作堅持下去的理由。"},{"w":"incompatibility","p":"n.","d":"A state of being unable to work together harmoniously.","c":"不相容；不協調","s":"The fundamental incompatibility between the two partners' approaches to financial management — one parsimonious and methodical, the other profligate and spontaneous — had created a strife that no amount of altruistic goodwill on either side proved sufficient to overcome without structural changes to their arrangement.","t":"兩位合夥人財務管理方式之間的根本不相容——一位吝嗇而有條理，另一位揮霍而自發——創造了一種衝突，任何一方無論多少無私的善意都不足以克服，而不對他們的安排進行結構性改變。","as":"The merger collapsed within two years because of a fundamental incompatibility between the startup's spontaneous, informal culture and the parent company's rigid hierarchy, a schism that acrimonious board meetings only exacerbated.","at":"這樁合併案在兩年內便告破局，原因在於新創公司自由隨性的文化與母公司僵化的層級制度根本不相容，而充滿火藥味的董事會議只讓這道裂痕更加擴大。"},{"w":"incapacitated","p":"adj.","d":"Deprived of the ability to function.","c":"失去能力的","s":"The organisation was effectively incapacitatededuring the critical transition period by the simultaneous resignation of three integral members of its leadership team — a fortuitous alignment of personal circumstances that its adversaries had done nothing to engineer but were quick to exploit.","t":"該組織在關鍵過渡時期因其領導團隊三名不可或缺的成員同時辭職而實際上失去了能力——這是其對手沒有做任何安排但卻迅速加以利用的一種偶然的個人情況巧合。","as":"When a sudden stroke left the aging monarch incapacitated, belligerent factions within the court began to jostle for power, each claiming that its rivals had concocted the royal decrees issued in his name.","at":"年邁的君主因突發中風而失去行事能力後，宮廷中好鬥的各派勢力開始爭權奪利，每一派都聲稱對手捏造了以國王名義頒布的詔令。"},{"w":"fabricate","p":"v.","d":"To invent or construct something false.","c":"捏造；偽造","s":"The fabricated alibi had been assembled with such painstaking ingenuity that investigators initially struggled to identify the precise points at which the mendacious narrative diverged from verifiable reality — only the cumulative weight of corroborated contradictions eventually rendering its fundamental dishonesty incontrovertible.","t":"這個捏造的不在場證明是以如此費力的巧思組裝的，以至於調查員最初難以確定虛假敘述偏離可驗證現實的確切點——只有被証實的矛盾的累積重量最終使其根本的不誠實無可辯駁。","as":"The disgraced scientist was found to have fabricated data in dozens of published studies, a flagrant breach of research ethics that invalidated years of work and led colleagues to repudiate any findings bearing his name.","at":"這位身敗名裂的科學家被發現在數十篇已發表的研究中捏造數據；這種公然違反研究倫理的行為使多年的成果失效，也讓同事們否認任何掛有他名字的研究結果。"},{"w":"connubial","p":"adj.","d":"Of or relating to marriage.","c":"婚姻的","s":"The biographer handled the subject's troubled connubial history with considerable sensitivity, aware that the acrimonious disputes documented in private correspondence had already caused sufficient strife for surviving family members without requiring additional public exposure.","t":"傳記作者以相當的敏感性處理了傳主動盪的婚姻歷史，意識到私人信件中記錄的嚴厲爭議已經給在世的家庭成員造成了足夠的衝突，而不需要額外的公開曝光。","as":"Victorian novelists frequently portrayed connubial harmony as a mere veneer, beneath which husbands and wives endured years of domestic strife, financial duress, and the stifling expectations imposed by a rigid social code.","at":"維多利亞時代的小說家常把婚姻和諧描寫成一層表象，其下是夫妻多年忍受的家庭紛爭、經濟壓力，以及僵化社會規範所強加的令人窒息的期望。"},{"w":"demur","p":"v.","d":"To raise objections, hesitate.","c":"反對；抗議","s":"She demur ed politely but firmly when asked to endorse the initiative without adequate time to scrutinise its implications, her incisive questioning revealing nebulous assumptions that the proposal's advocates had hoped would go unexamined beneath the fulsome enthusiasm of the launch event.","t":"當被要求在沒有足夠時間仔細審查其影響的情況下認可該倡議時，她有禮貌但堅定地反對，她敏銳的質疑揭示了提案支持者希望在發佈活動過度熱情的掩護下不被審查的模糊假設。","as":"When the board proposed slashing the research budget, the chief scientist did not merely demur; she presented incontrovertible evidence that such cuts would stymie ongoing projects and jeopardize the firm's most viable products.","at":"董事會提議大幅削減研究預算時，首席科學家不只是提出異議；她拿出無可辯駁的證據，證明這樣的削減會阻礙進行中的計畫，並危及公司最具發展前景的產品。"},{"w":"appellation","p":"n.","d":"A name or title.","c":"名稱；稱呼","s":"The appellation bestowed on the eminent scientist by her colleagues — 'the architect of modern immunology' — was neither fulsome flattery nor desultory hyperbole, but a bona fide recognition that her assiduous decades of research had genuinely transformed the discipline.","t":"同事們授予這位傑出科學家的稱號——'現代免疫學的建築師'——既不是過度的奉承，也不是散漫的誇大，而是對她幾十年勤勉研究確實改變了這門學科的真實認可。","as":"The appellation Iron Lady, originally coined as a mocking epithet by a Soviet newspaper, was soon embraced by Margaret Thatcher herself, who construed it as a tribute to her valor rather than as an insult.","at":"「鐵娘子」這個稱號原本是蘇聯一家報紙創造的嘲諷綽號，卻很快被柴契爾夫人本人欣然接受，她將其解讀為對自己勇氣的讚揚，而非侮辱。"},{"w":"escalation","p":"n.","d":"A rapid increase in intensity.","c":"逐步升級","s":"The diplomatic escalation had proceeded with such rapidity that even the most cogent analytical frameworks could not adequately account for the speed of deterioration — each provocative act generating a belligerent response that compounded the original grievance and made de-escalation progressively more difficult.","t":"外交升級的進展如此迅速，以至於即使是最有說服力的分析框架也無法充分解釋惡化的速度——每一個挑釁行為都產生了好戰的回應，這加重了最初的委屈，使降級變得越來越困難。","as":"Diplomats feared that the border skirmish could trigger a rapid escalation into full-scale war, so they worked tirelessly to broker a ceasefire before either belligerent government could deploy additional troops to the region.","at":"外交官擔心這場邊境小衝突可能迅速升級為全面戰爭，因此不眠不休地斡旋停火，以免任何一個好戰的政府向該地區增派部隊。"},{"w":"indifference","p":"n.","d":"A lack of interest or concern.","c":"漠不關心","s":"The bureaucratic indifference that greeted the community's repeated requests for assistance reflected not the individual malice of any single official but a systemic inertia — a collective failure of empathy that had permeated every level of the administrative structure over decades of institutional atrophy.","t":"官僚機構對社區反覆提出援助請求的漠不關心，反映的不是任何單個官員的個人惡意，而是系統性的惰性——一種在數十年機構萎縮過程中滲透到行政結構每個層面的集體同理心失敗。","as":"The novelist's portrayal of the town's indifference to the hapless orphan's suffering serves as a caustic critique of a society that, engrossed in its own mundane concerns, ignored the destitution at its very doorstep.","at":"小說家描寫小鎮對那名不幸孤兒的苦難漠不關心，尖銳地批判了一個沉迷於自身瑣事、對家門口的赤貧視而不見的社會。"},{"w":"potential","p":"adj.","d":"Possible, having latent capability.","c":"潛在的","s":"Every potential investor the development team approached expressed dubious interest at best, the project's ambitious scope and the team's inchoate business plan failing to instil the confidence that would have translated cautious curiosity into tangible financial commitment.","t":"開發團隊接觸的每一位潛在投資者頂多表示了可疑的興趣，項目雄心勃勃的範圍和團隊不成熟的商業計劃未能灌輸將謹慎好奇心轉化為切實財務承諾所需的信心。","as":"Engineers must scrutinize every potential flaw in a bridge's design, since even a seemingly minor defect, if left unchecked, could precipitate a collapse with lethal consequences for the thousands of commuters who cross it daily.","at":"工程師必須仔細檢查橋梁設計中每一個潛在的缺陷，因為即使是看似微不足道的瑕疵，若置之不理，也可能導致坍塌，對每天通行的數千名通勤者造成致命的後果。"},{"w":"cumulative","p":"adj.","d":"Increasing by successive additions.","c":"累積的","s":"The cumulative effect of years of sporadic but persistent environmental violations had proven far more catastrophic than any single incident — a pernicious pattern of neglect whose compound consequences only became fully apparent when the watershed ecosystem finally collapsed beyond the possibility of restoration.","t":"多年零星但持續環境違規的累積影響被證明比任何單一事件都更具災難性——一種忽視的有害模式，其複合後果只有在分水嶺生態系統最終崩潰到無法恢復的可能性時才完全顯現。","as":"Although each individual exposure to the pesticide was nominal, researchers discovered that its cumulative effect on farmworkers was pernicious, gradually damaging their nervous systems in ways that remained latent for years.","at":"雖然每一次接觸農藥的劑量都微乎其微，研究人員卻發現，其對農場工人的累積影響極為有害，會逐漸損害他們的神經系統，而這些傷害可能潛伏多年才顯現。"},{"w":"recondite","p":"adj.","d":"Not known by many, obscure, hidden.","c":"深奧的；隱蔽的","s":"Her recondite knowledge of medieval manuscript traditions allowed her to perceive immediately that the document was fraudulent — a subterfuge invisible to generalist scholars but transparent to anyone with her highly specialised expertise in the particular scribal conventions of the relevant period.","t":"她對中世紀手稿傳統的深奧知識使她能夠立即察覺文件是假的——對通才學者來說不可見的詭計，但對任何具有她在相關時期特定書記慣例方面高度專業知識的人來說都是透明的。","as":"The professor's lectures on medieval theology were so recondite that even avid graduate students found them cryptic, though a few diligent listeners eventually perceived the elegant logic underlying his seemingly incoherent arguments.","at":"這位教授講授中世紀神學的課程極為深奧，連熱衷求知的研究生都覺得晦澀難懂；不過仍有幾位勤奮的聽眾最終領會到，他那看似語無倫次的論證背後其實有著嚴謹優雅的邏輯。"},{"w":"palliate","p":"v.","d":"To alleviate without curing, to excuse.","c":"減輕；掩飾","s":"The committee's elaborate public relations campaign served only to palliate the damage rather than address its root causes — a perfunctory exercise in reputation management that astute observers immediately recognised as an attempt to deflect scrutiny from the egregious governance failures the report had documented.","t":"委員會精心設計的公關活動只是減輕了損害，而非解決其根本原因——一種敷衍的聲譽管理活動，精明的觀察者立即認識到這是試圖轉移對報告所記錄的嚴重治理失敗的審查。","as":"The physicians could only palliate the patient's virulent malady, easing her paroxysms of coughing with medication, since no treatment then available could halt the inexorable progress of a disease that would claim countless lives before antibiotics were discovered.","at":"醫師們只能減輕這名病患猛烈病症的痛苦，以藥物緩解她陣發性的劇咳，因為當時沒有任何療法能阻止這種疾病無可避免的惡化，而在抗生素問世之前，它奪走了無數人的性命。"},{"w":"delude","p":"v.","d":"To cause to believe something false.","c":"欺騙；蠱惑","s":"She had deluded herself for years into believing that the superficial veneer of professional success adequately compensated for the profound destitution of her personal life — a fallacious equation that therapy eventually helped her to identify and dismantle.","t":"她多年來一直欺騙自己，認為職業成功的表面虛飾足以補償她個人生活的深刻貧困——一個治療最終幫助她識別和拆解的謬誤等式。","as":"Charismatic swindlers often delude unwary investors with promises of extraordinary returns, cajoling them into surrendering their savings to a nefarious hoax that collapses as soon as new deposits stop flowing in.","at":"富有魅力的詐騙者常以驚人報酬的承諾蒙騙不設防的投資人，哄騙他們交出積蓄，投入一場一旦新資金停止流入就會崩潰的邪惡騙局。"},{"w":"prelude","p":"n.","d":"An introduction or preliminary action.","c":"序幕；前奏","s":"The minor diplomatic incident proved to be merely the prelude to a far more serious confrontation — an inchoate conflict whose latent tensions had been accumulating for decades and which required only this fortuitous spark to escalate with the turbulent rapidity that subsequently surprised even those who had prognosticated its eventual emergence.","t":"這一小外交事件被證明只是一場更嚴重對抗的序幕——一場潛在緊張局勢已積累數十年的不成形衝突，只需要這個偶然的火花就能以隨後甚至讓那些曾預測其最終出現的人都感到驚訝的動盪速度升級。","as":"Historians regard the assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand as the prelude to the First World War, yet they caution that the war's true causes were manifold, including rampant nationalism, an inherently unstable web of alliances, and an arms race that grew more turbulent each year.","at":"歷史學家認為斐迪南大公遇刺是第一次世界大戰的序幕，但他們提醒，戰爭的真正原因是多方面的，包括猖獗的民族主義、本身就不穩定的同盟體系，以及逐年愈演愈烈的軍備競賽。"},{"w":"chimerical","p":"adj.","d":"Imaginary, fantastically improbable.","c":"荒唐的；空想的","s":"The project's business case rested on chimerical assumptions about market growth that even a cursory examination of the available data would have revealed as fallacious — projections so disconnected from empirical reality that the institutional investors who had funded previous ventures declined to participate.","t":"該項目的商業案例建立在對市場增長的空想假設上，即使對可用數據進行粗略審查也會揭示這些假設是謬誤的——與實證現實如此脫節的預測，以至於資助過以前風險投資的機構投資者拒絕參與。","as":"Early alchemists pursued the chimerical dream of transforming lead into gold, and although their quest proved fruitless, their assiduous experiments laid a rudimentary foundation for the modern science of chemistry.","at":"早期煉金術士追逐把鉛變成金子的空想美夢，雖然他們的追尋徒勞無功，但他們孜孜不倦的實驗為現代化學奠定了初步的基礎。"},{"w":"acknowledge","p":"v.","d":"To admit or accept the truth of.","c":"承認；答謝","s":"She was too cogent a thinker to refuse to acknowledge the salient weaknesses in her own argument — a rare intellectual honesty that her colleagues found disarming and that lent her positions far greater credibility than the impeccable logic of those who never conceded a single point.","t":"她是一位太有說服力的思考者，無法拒絕承認自己論點中突出的弱點——這種罕見的智識誠實讓她的同事感到解除武裝，這讓她的立場比那些從不讓步一點的人的無懈可擊的邏輯更具可信度。","as":"The company finally acknowledged that its factory had emitted toxic waste into the river, but only after independent laboratories attested to the villagers' complaints and the once-clear water had turned murky and lifeless.","at":"這家公司終於承認其工廠曾將有毒廢棄物排入河中，但那是在獨立實驗室證實了村民的投訴、原本清澈的河水已變得混濁而毫無生機之後。"}]},{"unit":23,"cards":[{"w":"analogous","p":"adj.","d":"Comparable in certain respects.","c":"類似的；可類比的","s":"The situation proved analogous to the financial crises documented in the annals of previous centuries — a pattern of rampant speculation, perfunctory oversight, and cumulative institutional complacency that historians found depressingly familiar despite the ostensibly modern context.","t":"這個情況被證明與史冊中記載的歷代金融危機相似——猖獗的投機、敷衍的監管，以及日積月累的制度自滿，儘管背景看似現代，歷史學家卻覺得這種模式熟悉得令人沮喪。","as":"Some economists argue that the recent housing bubble was analogous to the tulip mania of the seventeenth century, since in both cases a frenzy of speculation eclipsed rational judgment and investors deluded themselves that prices would surge indefinitely.","at":"一些經濟學家認為，近年的房市泡沫與十七世紀的鬱金香狂熱相似，因為兩者都是投機狂潮壓過理性判斷，投資人自欺欺人地相信價格會無限飆漲。"},{"w":"catastrophic","p":"adj.","d":"Involving or causing sudden disaster.","c":"災難性的","s":"The catastrophic collapse of the infrastructure had been preceded by years of sporadic warnings that the relevant authorities had consistently relegated to lower-priority status — a desultory response to imminent structural failure that the subsequent inquiry characterised as an egregious abdication of institutional responsibility.","t":"基礎設施發生災難性崩塌之前，多年來早有零星警告，但相關當局一再把它們列為次要事項——面對迫在眉睫的結構失效卻反應散漫，事後的調查形容這是嚴重的失職。","as":"The catastrophic failure of New Orleans' levees during Hurricane Katrina exposed years of lax oversight and sporadic inspections, and the resulting floods left thousands of residents in a desperate plight, stranded on rooftops awaiting rescue.","at":"卡崔娜颶風期間紐奧良堤防的災難性潰決，暴露出多年來監督鬆散、檢查斷斷續續的問題，隨之而來的洪水使數以千計的居民陷入絕境，只能困在屋頂上等待救援。"},{"w":"compensatory","p":"adj.","d":"Intended to make amends for a loss.","c":"補償的","s":"The court awarded compensatoryedamages calculated to reflect not merely the tangible financial losses the plaintiff had sustained but the plight of prolonged professional uncertainty that had compounded her distress during the three years the litigation had remained unresolved.","t":"法院判給補償性賠償，金額不僅反映原告所蒙受的實際財務損失，也考量訴訟懸而未決的三年間，長期職業前途未卜的困境對她造成的加倍痛苦。","as":"After the factory explosion, the court ordered the corporation to pay compensatory damages to the victims' families, ruling that its managers were culpable for flouting safety regulations and ignoring ominous warnings from their own engineers.","at":"工廠爆炸後，法院判決該公司須向罹難者家屬支付補償性賠償，認定其管理階層無視安全法規、忽略自家工程師發出的不祥警訊，應負罪責。"},{"w":"decade","p":"n.","d":"A period of ten years.","c":"十年","s":"Over the course of the preceding decade, the once-nondescript neighbourhood had undergone a metamorphosis so complete that even long-term residents occasionally failed to recognise landmarks that had defined the area throughout their formative years, the changes accumulating with a rapidity that urban historians found remarkable.","t":"在過去十年間，這個原本毫不起眼的街區經歷了徹底的蛻變，就連老住戶有時也認不出伴隨他們成長的地標；變化累積之快，令都市歷史學家嘖嘖稱奇。","as":"Over the past decade, the ubiquitous presence of smartphones has transformed how adolescents socialize, and some psychologists contend that constant online comparison has exacerbated teenage anxiety, though others caution that such conjecture rests on dubious data.","at":"過去十年間，智慧型手機無所不在，改變了青少年的社交方式；一些心理學家主張，網路上無止境的比較加劇了青少年的焦慮，但也有人提醒，這種推測所依據的數據令人存疑。"},{"w":"enunciate","p":"v.","d":"To express or state precisely; to articulate clearly.","c":"闡明；清晰發音","s":"The professor could enunciate even the most recondite theoretical concepts with remarkable clarity, his natural virtuosity as a communicator allowing complex ideas to become accessible without losing the nuance that distinguished sophisticated analysis from superficial simplification.","t":"這位教授即使是最深奧的理論概念也能闡述得極為清晰，他天生的表達功力讓複雜的觀念變得易懂，卻又不失區分精闢分析與膚淺簡化的細膩之處。","as":"In her inaugural address, the new president took care to enunciate her policy priorities in clear and incisive language, avoiding the verbose euphemisms that her predecessors had used to disguise unpopular decisions.","at":"新任總統在就職演說中，用清晰而犀利的語言明確闡述她的政策重點，避開前任們用來掩飾不受歡迎決策的冗長委婉說法。"},{"w":"gamut","p":"n.","d":"The complete range of something.","c":"全音階；全部範圍","s":"The investigation examined the full gamut of the organisation's activities, from its most mundane administrative procedures to its most covert operational decisions, ultimately corroborating what critics had long alleged and rendering incontrovertible what the management had consistently sought to palliate with euphemistic explanations.","t":"調查檢視了該組織活動的全部範圍，從最平凡的行政程序到最隱密的營運決策，最終證實了批評者長久以來的指控，讓管理階層一直試圖用委婉說法掩飾的事實變得無可辯駁。","as":"The pianist's recital ran the gamut from delicate Baroque preludes to turbulent modern compositions, showcasing a virtuosity that won over even the skeptical critics who had questioned whether she was ready for such a prestigious stage.","at":"這位鋼琴家的獨奏會涵蓋了從細膩的巴洛克前奏曲到激烈的現代作品等各種曲風，所展現的精湛技藝，連原本懷疑她是否準備好登上如此重要舞台的評論家都為之折服。"},{"w":"heterogeneous","p":"adj.","d":"Diverse in character or content.","c":"異質的","s":"The heterogeneous coalition that had assembled to oppose the development was as remarkable for its internal diversity as for its shared purpose — indigenous landowners, affluent suburban residents, environmental scientists, and urban poverty advocates all heterogeneous in their opposition despite their profoundly disparate perspectives.","t":"集結起來反對這項開發案的異質聯盟，其內部的多元與共同目標同樣引人注目——原住民地主、富裕的郊區居民、環境科學家與都市貧窮倡議者，儘管觀點天差地別，卻在反對立場上團結一致。","as":"Ecologists have found that heterogeneous forests, composed of many disparate tree species, are more resilient than monocultures, since a blight that afflicts one species is unlikely to raze the entire woodland.","at":"生態學家發現，由許多不同樹種組成的異質性森林比單一樹種林更具韌性，因為侵襲某一樹種的病害不太可能摧毀整片林地。"},{"w":"inordinate","p":"adj.","d":"Exceeding reasonable limits, excessive.","c":"過度的；無節制的","s":"The inordinate attention devoted to relatively minor procedural violations while the most egregious substantive failures went unaddressed reflected a fallacious institutional priority that had persisted for years — preferring the comfort of enforcing manageable rules to the discomfort of confronting systemic problems.","t":"對相對輕微的程序違規投以過度的關注，最嚴重的實質缺失卻無人處理，這反映出一種存在多年的錯誤制度優先順序——寧可安於執行容易管理的規則，也不願面對系統性問題帶來的不適。","as":"The chief executive's inordinate salary, which dwarfed the remuneration of ordinary employees by several hundred times, provoked acrimonious debate among shareholders, who argued that such generosity was unjustified given the firm's lackluster performance.","at":"這位執行長過高的薪資比一般員工的報酬高出數百倍，引發股東之間激烈的爭論，他們認為公司表現平平，如此慷慨的待遇毫無道理。"},{"w":"introspective","p":"adj.","d":"Examining one's own thoughts and feelings.","c":"內省的；反省的","s":"The introspective quality of her late novels distinguished them sharply from her earlier, more extroverted work — each character rendered with an empathetic nuance that suggested a writer who had spent considerable time scrutinising her own emotional landscape before attempting to portray others.","t":"她晚期小說的內省特質，使其與早期較外向的作品截然不同——每個角色都被刻畫得富有同理心且細膩，顯示作者在試圖描寫他人之前，已花了大量時間審視自己的內心世界。","as":"The poet's later work became increasingly introspective as she withdrew from public life to scrutinize her own memories, and critics noted that these reticent, contemplative verses possessed a depth absent from her earlier, more flamboyant poems.","at":"這位詩人退出公眾生活、細細審視自己的回憶，她的後期作品也因此越來越內省；評論家指出，這些含蓄沉靜的詩句有著她早期較華麗張揚的詩作所缺少的深度。"},{"w":"irascible","p":"adj.","d":"Having a tendency to become angry easily.","c":"易怒的","s":"The irascible general had become so notorious for badgering subordinates with fractious outbursts that even the most capable officers requested transfers rather than endure another tour under his command — a pattern of behaviour that had cost the army some of its most promising talent.","t":"這位易怒的將軍以暴躁發作、不斷刁難部屬而惡名昭彰，就連最能幹的軍官也寧願申請調職，也不願再於他麾下服役——這種行為模式讓軍隊失去了一些最有潛力的人才。","as":"The irascible conductor was infamous for his outbursts during rehearsals, castigating musicians for the slightest error, yet many endured his diatribes because his exacting standards produced performances of unrivaled brilliance.","at":"這位脾氣暴躁的指揮家以排練時大發雷霆而惡名昭彰，常因最微小的錯誤就嚴厲斥責樂手；然而許多人仍忍受他的痛罵，因為他嚴苛的標準造就了無與倫比的精彩演出。"},{"w":"maladjusted","p":"adj.","d":"Failing to cope with the demands of a normal social environment.","c":"適應不良的","s":"The children most vulnerable to becoming maladjusted were not, the research suggested, those from the most destitute backgrounds, but those experiencing the pernicious instability of unpredictable environments — homes where the absence of nurture was compounded by the arbitrary withdrawal of the affection that was occasionally present.","t":"研究指出，最容易出現適應不良的孩子，並非來自最貧困家庭的孩子，而是經歷難以預測的環境所帶來之有害不穩定的孩子——這些家庭不但缺乏照顧，偶爾出現的關愛還會被任意收回。","as":"Child psychologists caution that labeling a shy or unconventional pupil as maladjusted can become a self-fulfilling prophecy, since the stereotype may elicit mockery from classmates and relegate the child to the margins of school life.","at":"兒童心理學家提醒，將害羞或特立獨行的學生貼上適應不良的標籤，可能變成自我應驗的預言，因為這種刻板印象可能招來同學的嘲笑，並把孩子排擠到校園生活的邊緣。"},{"w":"mandate","p":"n.","d":"An authoritative command or instruction.","c":"命令；授權","s":"The new administration's claimed mandate for radical reform was dubious at best, given that it had been elected with the slimmest possible majority — a result that even its most ardent supporters acknowledged was more a rejection of its predecessor than an endorsement of its own ambitious programme.","t":"新政府聲稱擁有推動激進改革的授權，這說法充其量令人存疑，因為它僅以極微弱的多數當選——連最熱烈的支持者也承認，這個結果與其說是認同其雄心勃勃的施政計畫，不如說是對前任政府的否定。","as":"Following a landslide victory, the new government claimed a clear mandate to curtail carbon emissions, yet it soon faced belligerent opposition from industries that deemed such restrictive policies a threat to their survival.","at":"新政府在壓倒性勝選後宣稱獲得明確授權去削減碳排放，卻很快遭到產業界的強烈反對，這些產業認為這類限制性政策威脅到它們的生存。"},{"w":"mortality","p":"n.","d":"The state of being subject to death; death rate.","c":"死亡率；必死性","s":"The mortality statistics for the disease revealed starkly that outcomes were not randomly distributed but strongly correlated with socioeconomic status — an incontrovertible finding that rendered the government's claim of providing universal healthcare access deeply nebulous and politically untenable.","t":"這種疾病的死亡率統計鮮明地顯示，結果並非隨機分布，而是與社經地位高度相關——這項無可辯駁的發現，使政府宣稱提供全民醫療照護的說法顯得十分空泛，在政治上也站不住腳。","as":"Historians cite the sharp decline in infant mortality during the twentieth century as a salient example of how vaccines and clean drinking water could curb maladies that had once been rampant in crowded cities.","at":"歷史學家以二十世紀嬰兒死亡率大幅下降為顯著例證，說明疫苗與乾淨的飲用水如何遏止曾在擁擠城市中猖獗的疾病。"},{"w":"neurotic","p":"adj.","d":"Affected by neurosis, abnormally anxious.","c":"神經質的","s":"His neurotic preoccupation with professional failure had become so engrossing that it was paradoxically impairing the very performance it feared — a self-fulfilling prophecy that his therapist described as the most pernicious cognitive pattern she encountered in high-achieving individuals.","t":"他對職場失敗神經質般的執著已嚴重到讓他無法自拔，反而矛盾地損害了他所擔心的表現——他的治療師形容這種自我應驗的預言，是她在高成就者身上遇過最有害的認知模式。","as":"The protagonist of the novel is a neurotic clerk who obsesses over petty details, repeatedly checking whether his door is locked, and his fretful monologues reveal an inhibition so deep that he can scarcely converse with his colleagues.","at":"這部小說的主角是一名神經質的職員，他執著於瑣碎細節，一再檢查門是否上鎖；他焦躁不安的獨白，揭露了一種深刻到使他幾乎無法與同事交談的壓抑。"},{"w":"neutralize","p":"v.","d":"To make ineffective by countering with equal force.","c":"抵銷；中和","s":"The defence team's most effective strategy was to neutralize the prosecution's most cogent evidence not by disputing it directly but by introducing contextual information that, while not exonerating the defendant, rendered the inferences the prosecution wished to draw from it sufficiently ambiguous to preclude conviction.","t":"辯護團隊最有效的策略，是抵銷檢方最有力的證據——不是直接反駁，而是提出背景資訊，雖然無法證明被告清白，卻讓檢方想從證據中得出的推論變得足夠模稜兩可，因而無法定罪。","as":"Antacids neutralize excess stomach acid and provide a temporary respite from heartburn, but doctors caution that chronic discomfort may be symptomatic of a more serious disorder whose underlying cause such remedies cannot obviate.","at":"制酸劑能中和過多的胃酸，暫時緩解胃灼熱，但醫師提醒，長期不適可能是更嚴重疾病的徵兆，而這類藥物無法消除其根本原因。"},{"w":"pedagogue","p":"n.","d":"A teacher, especially a strict one.","c":"教師；教育者","s":"The celebrated pedagogue had trained three generations of musicians, his methods considered excessively demanding by some and indispensably rigorous by those whose virtuosity could be traced directly to the disciplined foundations he had insisted on establishing before allowing any creative exploration.","t":"這位知名的教育家培育了三代音樂家；有些人認為他的方法過於嚴苛，但那些精湛技藝可直接追溯到他堅持先打好紮實基礎、才允許任何創意探索的學生，則認為這種嚴格不可或缺。","as":"The old-fashioned pedagogue insisted that his students memorize interminable lists of Latin verbs, and he would admonish anyone whose recitation stumbled, a regimen that many pupils regarded as sheer drudgery.","at":"這位老派的嚴師堅持學生背誦冗長無盡的拉丁文動詞表，只要有人背誦結巴就會被他訓誡，許多學生都覺得這種訓練純粹是苦差事。"},{"w":"perpetuate","p":"v.","d":"To make something continue indefinitely.","c":"使不朽；使持續","s":"Every institution that failed to confront its historical complicity in discriminatory practices risked perpetuateing the systemic inequalities it professed to oppose — a paradox at the heart of reform movements that the most perspicacious critics consistently identified and that the most resistant institutions consistently denied.","t":"每個未能正視自身在歧視行為中歷史共謀的機構，都有可能使它聲稱反對的系統性不平等延續下去——這是改革運動核心的矛盾，最有洞察力的批評者一再指出，而最抗拒改變的機構則一再否認。","as":"Critics argue that textbooks which omit the integral contributions of women and minorities perpetuate a narrow view of history, subtly fostering bias in young readers who are not yet cognizant of what has been left out.","at":"批評者主張，忽略女性和少數族群重要貢獻的教科書，會延續一種狹隘的歷史觀，在尚未察覺哪些內容被刪去的年輕讀者心中悄悄培養偏見。"},{"w":"perspicacious","p":"adj.","d":"Having a ready insight, shrewd.","c":"有洞察力的","s":"The perspicacious analyst had identified the chimerical assumptions underlying the investment thesis several months before the collapse became apparent to other market participants — a demonstration of the incisive pattern recognition that distinguished genuinely skilled assessment from the superficial consensus that had misled the majority.","t":"這位有洞察力的分析師早在崩盤被其他市場參與者察覺的數個月前，就看出這套投資論點背後不切實際的假設——展現出敏銳的模式辨識能力，這正是真正專業的評估與誤導多數人的膚淺共識之間的差別。","as":"A perspicacious investor, she discerned the promise of renewable energy long before her peers, quietly acquiring stakes in small, unproven solar companies while skeptics scoffed at the entire venture as chimerical.","at":"她是位眼光敏銳的投資人，早在同儕之前就看出再生能源的前景，悄悄買進尚未經過考驗的小型太陽能公司的股份，而當時懷疑者還嘲笑這項投資是異想天開。"},{"w":"phenomenon","p":"n.","d":"A fact or event observed to occur.","c":"現象","s":"The social phenomenon of voluntary simplicity — affluent individuals choosing destitution-adjacent lifestyles in deliberate rejection of materialism — had become sufficiently widespread to merit serious academic attention, its causes and consequences proving more heterogeneous than either its advocates or critics had initially assumed.","t":"「自願簡樸」這種社會現象——富裕的人刻意拒絕物質主義，選擇近乎貧困的生活方式——已普遍到值得學術界認真關注，其成因與影響也比擁護者或批評者最初所想的更加多元。","as":"The aurora borealis, a dazzling phenomenon caused by charged solar particles colliding with gases in the upper atmosphere, inspired a plethora of myths among indigenous peoples of the Arctic, many of whom construed the shimmering lights as harbingers of war or as the spirits of ancestors.","at":"北極光是太陽帶電粒子與高層大氣氣體碰撞所產生的絢麗現象，在北極地區的原住民之間催生了大量神話，其中許多人曾將這些閃爍的光芒解讀為戰爭的預兆或祖先的靈魂。"},{"w":"susceptible","p":"adj.","d":"Likely to be influenced or affected.","c":"易受影響的","s":"Individuals with susceptible temperaments who had been exposed to indoctrination during their most formative years were, the research suggested, significantly more likely to maintain their acquired beliefs even when subsequently confronted with incontrovertible evidence that those beliefs rested on fallacious foundations.","t":"研究指出，性格容易受影響、又在人格形成的關鍵時期接受過灌輸的人，即使之後面對無可辯駁的證據，證明這些信念建立在錯誤的基礎上，仍明顯更可能堅守他們所習得的信念。","as":"Elderly patients with weakened immune systems are especially susceptible to influenza, so public health officials advocate annual vaccination and urge caregivers to remain vigilant for early symptoms that could signal a lethal complication.","at":"免疫力較弱的年長病患特別容易感染流感，因此公共衛生官員提倡每年接種疫苗，並呼籲照顧者對可能預示致命併發症的早期症狀保持警覺。"}]},{"unit":24,"cards":[{"w":"abhorrent","p":"adj.","d":"Inspiring disgust and loathing.","c":"令人厭惡的","s":"The practice was considered so abhorrent by the indigenous population that even decades of colonial indoctrination had failed to normalise it — an incontrovertible demonstration that some cultural values possess a tenacity that external mandate and institutional pressure cannot simply override.","t":"原住民認為這種做法令人極度厭惡，以至於數十年的殖民灌輸都無法使其成為常態——這無可辯駁地證明，某些文化價值具有強韌的生命力，不是外來命令與制度壓力就能輕易推翻的。","as":"Most modern societies regard slavery as abhorrent, yet for centuries the practice was tolerated, and even defended, by eminent thinkers who justified it with fallacious arguments about a supposedly natural hierarchy among human beings.","at":"大多數現代社會認為奴隸制度令人憎惡，然而數百年來，它卻被容忍、甚至被一些傑出思想家辯護，他們以人類之間存在所謂天生階級的謬誤論點為其找理由。"},{"w":"absurd","p":"adj.","d":"Wildly unreasonable, illogical.","c":"荒謬的","s":"It struck the more perspicacious analysts as frankly absurd that the regime's mendacious propaganda was being accepted as bona fide information by so significant a proportion of the population — a phenomenon that social psychologists attributed to decades of systematic indoctrination rather than any deficiency of critical intelligence.","t":"在較有洞察力的分析師看來，這個政權的虛假宣傳竟被如此大比例的民眾當成真實資訊接受，實在荒謬——社會心理學家將此現象歸因於數十年有系統的灌輸，而非民眾缺乏批判思考能力。","as":"Although the claim that the Earth is flat seems absurd to most people today, a surprising number of online communities perpetuate the notion, dismissing incontrovertible photographic evidence as an elaborate hoax concocted by governments.","at":"雖然地球是平的這種說法在今天大多數人看來荒謬可笑，卻有數量驚人的網路社群延續這個觀念，把無可辯駁的照片證據斥為政府捏造的精心騙局。"},{"w":"anthropologist","p":"n.","d":"An expert in the study of human societies.","c":"人類學家","s":"The anthropologist observed that the taboo surrounding discussion of mortality in this particular culture was not a desultory cultural artefact but an integral component of an elaborate cosmological framework that structured every aspect of social life from birth rituals to funeral practices.","t":"這位人類學家觀察到，在這個文化中，談論死亡的禁忌並非可有可無的文化遺留，而是一套精密宇宙觀不可或缺的一部分，從出生儀式到喪葬習俗，這套框架構築了社會生活的每個面向。","as":"The anthropologist spent several years living among a nomadic people of the Sahara, meticulously documenting kinship rituals that she argued were integral to the group's survival in such a harsh and unforgiving environment.","at":"這位人類學家花了數年時間與撒哈拉的一支游牧民族共同生活，一絲不苟地記錄他們的親屬儀式，並主張這些儀式對該族群在如此嚴酷無情的環境中生存不可或缺。"},{"w":"artifact","p":"n.","d":"An object made by human craft.","c":"人工製品","s":"Each artifact recovered from the excavation site was treated with the meticulous care appropriate to its bona fide historical significance — documented, photographed, and catalogued before removal, a process whose assiduous thoroughness reflected the lead archaeologist's conviction that context was as informative as the objects themselves.","t":"從挖掘現場出土的每件文物，都依其真正的歷史價值受到審慎對待——在移出前先記錄、拍照並編目，這個過程的一絲不苟反映出首席考古學家的信念：出土脈絡與文物本身同樣富含資訊。","as":"Archaeologists unearthed a cache of bronze artifacts in a subterranean chamber, and the remarkable condition of these objects led scholars to surmise that the tomb had escaped the attention of looters for thousands of years.","at":"考古學家在一處地下墓室中挖出一批青銅器物，這些器物保存得極為完好，使學者推測該墓穴數千年來都未曾遭到盜墓者覬覦。"},{"w":"bizarre","p":"adj.","d":"Very strange or unusual.","c":"奇異的","s":"The most bizarre aspect of the whole affair was not the deception itself but the chimerical confidence with which it had been perpetrated — the charlatan apparently bizarre in the belief that his transparent fabrications could indefinitely palliate the scrutiny of investigators who had already corroborated the contradictions in his account.","t":"整起事件最離奇的不是騙局本身，而是行騙者那份不切實際的自信——這個騙子顯然深信，他漏洞百出的捏造能無限期地應付調查人員的審查，而調查人員早已證實他說詞中的矛盾。","as":"The deep-sea anglerfish, with its bizarre glowing lure dangling above a mouth full of needle-like teeth, has adapted to the murky depths of its habitat by using this appendage to dupe unwary prey.","at":"深海鮟鱇魚頭上懸著一個怪異的發光誘餌，下方是一張布滿針狀利齒的大嘴；牠適應了棲息地幽暗的深海環境，利用這個構造誘騙毫無戒心的獵物。"},{"w":"contemptuous","p":"adj.","d":"Showing contempt, scornful.","c":"蔑視的","s":"Her contemptuousedismissal of the committee's concerns struck observers as counterproductive — the disdain she directed at the most perspicacious questioners generating precisely the antagonism that a more urbane and diplomatically adroit response might have defused.","t":"她以輕蔑的態度駁回委員會的疑慮，旁觀者認為這只會適得其反——她對最具洞察力的提問者所表現的鄙視，正好引發了一個較圓融、較有外交手腕的回應原本可以化解的敵意。","as":"The aristocrat was openly contemptuous of newly wealthy industrialists, deriding their ostentatious mansions and lavish parties as vulgar displays of new money, even as his own family's fortune steadily dwindled through years of profligate spending.","at":"這位貴族公開輕蔑那些新近致富的實業家，嘲笑他們炫耀的豪宅與奢華派對是暴發戶的俗氣排場，然而他自家的財富卻正因多年揮霍無度而逐漸縮水。"},{"w":"entreaty","p":"n.","d":"An earnest or humble request.","c":"懇求；乞求","s":"Every entreaty from the displaced community had been met with bureaucratic indifference — a desultory acknowledgement of receipt followed by months of silence that compounded the original destitution with the additional burden of administrative abandonment.","t":"流離失所的社區每一次懇求，都只換來官僚的冷漠——敷衍地確認收件後便是數月的沉默，使原本的貧困之外，又多了一層被行政體系拋棄的負擔。","as":"Ignoring the tearful entreaty of her parents, the young physician resolved to volunteer in a region besieged by famine, where malnutrition and cholera were rife and the few local clinics lacked even rudimentary supplies.","at":"這位年輕醫師不顧父母含淚的懇求，決心前往一個飽受饑荒圍困的地區當志工，那裡營養不良與霍亂肆虐，少數幾間當地診所連最基本的物資都缺乏。"},{"w":"fetish","p":"n.","d":"An object believed to have magical powers; an obsessive fixation.","c":"迷信物；戀物","s":"The anthropologist documented how the community's fetish objects had evolved over generations from genuine sacred artefacts with specific ritual functions into more diffuse cultural symbols whose precise meaning had become so recondite that even most community members could offer only a desultory account of their original significance.","t":"這位人類學家記錄了該社區的崇拜物如何在數代之間演變：從具有特定儀式功能的真正聖物，轉變為意義較模糊的文化象徵，其確切含義已變得如此深奧，連多數社區成員對其原始意義也只能說出零星片段。","as":"Some economists warn that policymakers have made a fetish of economic growth, pursuing ever-higher output with zealous intensity while ignoring the havoc that unchecked expansion can wreak on fragile ecosystems and the cumulative toll it takes on workers.","at":"一些經濟學家警告，政策制定者已把經濟成長當成盲目崇拜的對象，以狂熱的態度追求不斷提高的產出，卻忽視了無節制的擴張對脆弱生態系造成的破壞，以及對勞工造成的累積代價。"},{"w":"imperative","p":"adj.","d":"Of vital importance, essential.","c":"必要的；命令的","s":"It was imperative that the team receive the incontrovertible forensic results before any public statement was issued, since premature disclosure of uncertain findings would palliate neither the community's anxiety nor the institution's credibility, and might instead compound the reputational damage the investigation had been commissioned to repair.","t":"在發布任何公開聲明之前，團隊務必先取得無可辯駁的鑑識結果，因為過早公布不確定的發現，既無法緩解社區的焦慮，也無法維護機構的公信力，反而可能加深這次調查原本要修補的聲譽損害。","as":"With sea levels rising steadily, scientists insist it is imperative that coastal cities strengthen their bulwarks against storm surges, warning that further delay could precipitate catastrophic flooding in low-lying neighborhoods.","at":"隨著海平面持續上升，科學家堅稱沿海城市必須強化抵禦暴潮的屏障，並警告再拖延下去可能在低窪社區引發災難性洪水。"},{"w":"imprudent","p":"adj.","d":"Not showing care, unwise.","c":"輕率的；不智的","s":"The imprudent acquisition of the struggling competitor without adequate scrutiny of its latent liabilities proved catastrophic — a desultory due diligence process that the board's subsequent post-mortem characterised as the single most egregious governance failure in the company's history.","t":"在未充分審查潛在負債的情況下輕率收購這家陷入困境的競爭對手，結果證明是一場災難——董事會事後檢討時，把這次敷衍的盡職調查形容為公司史上最嚴重的治理失敗。","as":"It would be imprudent for a novice investor to stake her entire savings on an unstable cryptocurrency, especially when its alleged returns are attested only by anonymous testimonials of dubious credibility.","at":"對新手投資人來說，把全部積蓄押在一種極不穩定的加密貨幣上是不明智的，尤其當其所謂的報酬只有來路可疑的匿名見證可以佐證時。"},{"w":"inanimate","p":"adj.","d":"Not alive, lacking consciousness.","c":"無生命的","s":"The forensic anthropologist explained that even inanimate materials could preserve biological signatures for millennia under the right conditions — a phenomenon that had rendered several previously insoluble historical mysteries susceptible to resolution through the application of modern analytical techniques.","t":"這位法醫人類學家解釋，在適當條件下，即使是無生命的物質也能保存生物跡證長達數千年——這個現象使得幾個原本無解的歷史謎團，得以透過現代分析技術找到答案。","as":"Young children often attribute feelings to inanimate objects, scolding a table they have bumped into, a phenomenon that developmental psychologists construe as an innate stage of cognitive growth rather than a sign of confusion.","at":"年幼的孩子常把情感投射到無生命的物體上，例如責罵自己撞到的桌子；發展心理學家將這種現象解讀為認知發展中與生俱來的一個階段，而非思緒混亂的徵兆。"},{"w":"inviolable","p":"adj.","d":"Never to be broken or dishonoured.","c":"不可侵犯的","s":"The treaty's inviolable provisions had been treated as such for over a century before a newly elected administration chose to abrogate them unilaterally, the belligerent act generating international condemnation and precipitating the acrimonious diplomatic crisis that dominated the subsequent decade.","t":"這份條約中不可侵犯的條款被如此看待了一個多世紀，直到新當選的政府選擇單方面予以廢除；這項好戰之舉招致國際譴責，並引發了主導其後十年的激烈外交危機。","as":"In many democracies, freedom of the press is regarded as an inviolable principle, and any government attempt to curtail it, however nominal, tends to elicit fierce protests from journalists and civic organizations alike.","at":"在許多民主國家，新聞自由被視為不可侵犯的原則，政府任何削弱它的企圖，不論多麼微小，往往都會招致記者與公民團體的強烈抗議。"},{"w":"originate","p":"v.","d":"To have a beginning, arise from.","c":"發源；創立","s":"The tradition was believed to originate in a spontaneous communal celebration following an unexpected deliverance from disaster — a bona fide historical event whose precise details had become so enveloped in mythology over successive generations that the anthropologist found it difficult to separate the verifiable core from accumulated legend.","t":"這項傳統據信起源於一場自發的集體慶祝，慶祝人們意外逃過一場災難——這是一個真實的歷史事件，但其確切細節歷經世代已被神話層層包覆，讓人類學家難以將可查證的核心與累積的傳說分開。","as":"Many linguists believe that the Austronesian languages originated in Taiwan, from which intrepid seafarers ventured across the Pacific over thousands of years, carrying their crops, customs, and words to islands as remote as Hawaii and New Zealand, a feat of navigation that scholars deem remarkable.","at":"許多語言學家認為南島語系起源於台灣，數千年來，無畏的航海者從這裡出發橫渡太平洋，將他們的作物、習俗和詞彙帶到遠至夏威夷和紐西蘭的島嶼，學者認為這是了不起的航海壯舉。"},{"w":"prohibition","p":"n.","d":"The act of forbidding something.","c":"禁止","s":"The prohibition of certain traditional practices by the colonial administration had been framed as a civilising measure but was experienced by indigenous communities as a pernicious assault on the cultural foundations of their collective identity — an abhorrent suppression whose legacies continued to reverberate generations later.","t":"殖民政府對某些傳統習俗的禁止，被包裝成一項教化措施，但原住民社區卻感受到這是對其集體認同文化根基的有害攻擊——這種令人憎惡的壓迫，其影響在數代之後仍持續迴盪。","as":"The prohibition of alcohol in the United States during the 1920s proved largely ineffectual, as clandestine bars flourished in nearly every city and bootleggers amassed enormous fortunes with apparent impunity.","at":"美國在一九二〇年代實施的禁酒令大致上成效不彰，因為祕密酒吧幾乎在每座城市大行其道，私酒販子更是看似肆無忌憚地累積龐大財富。"},{"w":"superstition","p":"n.","d":"A belief not based on reason or knowledge.","c":"迷信","s":"The community's elaborate system of superstition around the eclipse was not, the anthropologist argued, mere irrationality — it represented a coherent cosmological framework through which phenomena that could not otherwise be explained were rendered comprehensible and robbed of their capacity to induce paralysing anxiety.","t":"這位人類學家認為，該社區圍繞日食所發展出的一整套迷信並非單純的不理性——它代表一個連貫的宇宙觀框架，讓原本無法解釋的現象變得可以理解，也使這些現象不再能引發令人癱瘓的焦慮。","as":"Despite advances in science, the superstition that the number four brings misfortune still permeates East Asian culture, so many buildings omit a fourth floor, a practice that practical-minded architects find vexatious yet are loath to abandon.","at":"儘管科學進步，數字四會帶來厄運的迷信仍深植於東亞文化，許多建築因此省略四樓；務實的建築師雖覺得這種做法令人困擾，卻也不願放棄。"},{"w":"taboo","p":"n.","d":"A social or religious custom prohibiting action.","c":"禁忌","s":"Discussing financial failure remained the last real taboo in the otherwise candid startup culture — a superstition born of the well-founded conviction that admitting vulnerability would precipitate the very outcome it feared, jeopardising funding relationships that continued investment required.","t":"在原本坦率直言的新創文化中，談論財務失敗仍是最後一個真正的禁忌——這種迷信源自一個有根據的信念：承認自己的弱點會招致所擔心的結果，危及持續投資所需的資金關係。","as":"In many cultures, discussing mental illness remains a taboo, so sufferers often repress their symptoms rather than risk the disdain of neighbors, a silence that can turn a treatable malady into a lifelong burden.","at":"在許多文化中，談論精神疾病仍是一種禁忌，因此患者往往壓抑自己的症狀，而不願冒著遭鄰居鄙視的風險；這種沉默可能使原本可治療的疾病變成終身的負擔。"},{"w":"taint","p":"n.","d":"A trace of a bad quality or substance.","c":"污點；感染","s":"The taint of historical association with the disgraced institution proved surprisingly persistent — long after the original abhorrent practices had been abolished and personnel entirely replaced, the organisation's reputation continued to carry a reputational blemish that no amount of subsequent exemplary conduct entirely erased.","t":"與這個聲名狼藉的機構有過歷史關聯的污點，持續得出人意料——即使原本令人憎惡的做法早已廢除、人員也全部更換，這個組織的名聲仍背負著污名，後來再多的模範表現都無法完全抹去。","as":"Although the senator was eventually exonerated, the taint of the bribery scandal lingered, and his opponents continued to disparage him as a culprit who had escaped justice through legal subterfuge.","at":"儘管這位參議員最終獲判無罪，賄賂醜聞留下的污點卻揮之不去，對手仍持續貶低他，說他是靠法律伎倆逃過制裁的罪魁禍首。"},{"w":"tradition","p":"n.","d":"A long-established custom or belief.","c":"傳統","s":"The tradition of passing the skill from master to disciple through direct apprenticeship rather than formal instruction was so integral to the craft that practitioners who had trained through institutional programmes were considered, however unfairly, as somewhat less bona fide than those who had learned through the established lineage.","t":"透過直接拜師學藝、而非正式教學將技藝由師父傳給徒弟的傳統，對這門手藝來說是如此不可或缺，以至於透過機構課程受訓的從業者，無論多麼不公平，都被認為不如出身正統師承者來得道地。","as":"The annual Mazu pilgrimage, a tradition that draws throngs of devotees through central Taiwan each spring, has endured for generations, adapting to the vicissitudes of modern life while still offering participants solace and a sense of community.","at":"每年春天的媽祖遶境是吸引大批信眾走過台灣中部的傳統，已延續好幾代人；它隨著現代生活的變遷而調整，卻依然為參與者帶來慰藉與歸屬感。"},{"w":"universal","p":"adj.","d":"Applicable to all cases, general.","c":"普遍的；宇宙的","s":"Whether altruism was a universal human capacity or a culturally specific phenomenon remained an open and genuinely fascinating question — one that the most perspicacious evolutionary psychologists approached with a nuance that resisted the simplistic certainties that had dominated earlier theoretical frameworks.","t":"利他精神究竟是人類普遍具有的能力，還是特定文化的現象，仍是一個懸而未決且引人入勝的問題——最有洞察力的演化心理學家以細膩的態度探討它，拒絕接受早期理論框架中那些過於簡化的定論。","as":"Although cross-cultural studies corroborate that facial expressions of joy and fear are nearly universal, researchers caution that the norms dictating when such emotions may be displayed are far from monolithic, varying markedly among heterogeneous societies.","at":"雖然跨文化研究證實，喜悅與恐懼的臉部表情幾乎是普世共通的，研究人員仍提醒，規範何時可以表露這些情緒的準則絕非一成不變，而是在各種不同的社會之間差異顯著。"},{"w":"vulnerable","p":"adj.","d":"Susceptible to physical or emotional attack.","c":"脆弱的；易受傷的","s":"The most vulnerable populations were invariably those caught at the intersection of multiple simultaneous adversities — economic destitution, political marginalisation, and social isolation compounding each other's effects in ways that made the sum of their plight considerably greater than its individual components would suggest.","t":"最脆弱的族群總是那些同時陷入多重困境交會處的人——經濟貧困、政治邊緣化與社會孤立彼此加乘，使他們所受的困苦遠比各個因素單獨相加還要嚴重得多。","as":"Coral reefs are particularly vulnerable to rising ocean temperatures, which cause corals to expel the algae on which they depend, and scientists fear that if such bleaching recurs too often, entire reefs could succumb, leaving the myriad species that inhabit them without sanctuary.","at":"珊瑚礁特別容易受到海水溫度上升的影響，高溫會使珊瑚排出賴以維生的藻類；科學家擔心，若這種白化現象太常發生，整片珊瑚礁可能死亡，使棲息其中的無數物種失去庇護所。"}]},{"unit":25,"cards":[{"w":"aegis","p":"n.","d":"Protection or support from a powerful source.","c":"庇護；贊助","s":"The research programme operated under the aegis of a prestigious international foundation whose patronage lent the project both the financial security and the institutional credibility needed to attract the most eminent scientists in the field to participate in its ambitious agenda.","t":"這項研究計畫在一個聲譽卓著的國際基金會贊助下運作，其支持為計畫帶來財務保障與機構公信力，使其得以吸引該領域最傑出的科學家參與這項雄心勃勃的研究議程。","as":"Under the aegis of the World Health Organization, a global vaccination campaign eventually wiped out smallpox, a virulent disease that had afflicted humanity for thousands of years and whose mortality rate was once appallingly high.","at":"在世界衛生組織的支持與主導下，一場全球疫苗接種運動最終根除了天花——這種猛烈的疾病已折磨人類數千年，死亡率一度高得驚人。"},{"w":"awesome","p":"adj.","d":"Inspiring great admiration or fear.","c":"令人敬畏的","s":"The awesome scale of the natural catastrophe — entire towns obliterated, the gamut of critical infrastructure destroyed, and the cumulative displacement of nearly a million people — rendered even the most cogent policy responses inadequate to the immediate humanitarian imperative.","t":"這場天災令人震懾的規模——整座城鎮被夷為平地、各類關鍵基礎設施盡遭摧毀，累計近百萬人流離失所——讓即使是最有說服力的政策回應，也不足以應付迫在眉睫的人道需求。","as":"Astronauts often describe the sight of Earth from orbit as awesome, and many report that this vista induces an introspective mood, prompting them to ponder how petty the skirmishes between nations appear against the vastness of space.","at":"太空人常形容從軌道上俯瞰地球的景象令人震撼敬畏，許多人表示，這番景致使他們變得內省，思索在浩瀚宇宙的映襯下，國與國之間的衝突顯得多麼微不足道。"},{"w":"conflagration","p":"n.","d":"An extensive destructive fire.","c":"大火災","s":"The conflagration that consumed the historic library had been preceded by sporadic warnings about inadequate fire suppression systems that the building's management had treated with precisely the lax indifference that the subsequent inquiry characterised as the proximate cause of an entirely preventable catastrophe.","t":"吞噬這座歷史圖書館的大火發生之前，曾有零星警告指出消防系統不足，但大樓管理單位卻以極度鬆懈的態度漠然處之，事後調查認定這正是這場完全可以避免的災難之直接原因。","as":"The Great Fire of London in 1666 was a conflagration that razed thousands of houses and the medieval edifice of St Paul's Cathedral, yet it spurred officials to promulgate stricter building codes requiring brick and stone.","at":"一六六六年的倫敦大火是一場燒毀數千棟房屋及中世紀聖保羅大教堂建築的大火災，然而它也促使官員頒布更嚴格的建築規範，規定房屋須以磚石建造。"},{"w":"congenial","p":"adj.","d":"Pleasant because suited to one's character.","c":"意氣相投的","s":"The collaborative atmosphere at the research station proved deeply congenial to her particular style of working — the absence of hierarchical inhibitions allowing the sort of spontaneous intellectual cross-pollination between disciplines that the more sedentary academic environment of her previous institution had consistently prevented.","t":"研究站的合作氛圍與她獨特的工作風格十分相投——沒有階級束縛，讓各學科之間得以自然地激盪出知識火花，而這正是她先前任職機構那種較停滯的學術環境一直阻礙的。","as":"The novelist found the quiet seaside village a congenial place to write, because its unhurried pace and gregarious neighbors offered a welcome respite from the frantic literary circles of the capital, where she had felt besieged by critics and publishers.","at":"這位小說家發現那座寧靜的海邊村莊是個很適合她寫作的地方，因為那裡悠閒的步調和熱情友善的鄰居，讓她得以暫時擺脫首都那個忙亂的文壇——在那裡，她曾覺得飽受評論家和出版商的圍攻。"},{"w":"debris","p":"n.","d":"Scattered pieces of rubbish or remains.","c":"碎片；殘骸","s":"The investigative team painstakingly catalogued the debris from the collapsed structure, each fragment potentially an artifact that could corroborate or refute the competing theories about whether the failure had been catastrophic and sudden or the cumulative result of years of neglect.","t":"調查小組費盡心力將倒塌建築的殘骸逐一編目，每塊碎片都可能是一件證物，可以證實或推翻相互競爭的理論：這次倒塌究竟是突發性的災難，還是多年疏於維護累積的結果。","as":"Orbital debris, composed of defunct satellites and fragments from earlier collisions, now abounds in low Earth orbit, and engineers warn that even a tiny shard traveling at tremendous speed could inflict lethal damage on astronauts or thwart an entire mission.","at":"太空碎片由失效的衛星和過往碰撞產生的碎片組成，如今在近地軌道上大量存在；工程師警告，即使是一片以極高速度飛行的微小碎片，也可能對太空人造成致命傷害，或使整個任務功虧一簣。"},{"w":"deplorable","p":"adj.","d":"Deserving strong condemnation.","c":"可悲的；應受譴責的","s":"The deplorable conditions in which migrant workers were being housed represented not merely a humanitarian failure but a blatant violation of the legal standards that every employer in the sector was inviolably obligated to maintain — a finding the inspectors characterised as among the most egregious they had documented.","t":"移工被安置的居住環境惡劣得令人痛心，這不僅是人道上的失敗，更公然違反了該產業每位雇主都必須嚴格遵守的法定標準——檢查人員形容這是他們記錄過最嚴重的案例之一。","as":"Charles Dickens's novels exposed the deplorable conditions of Victorian workhouses, where indigent children endured malnutrition and harsh reprimands, and his poignant portrayals helped spur advocates of social reform to demand better treatment for the poor.","at":"狄更斯的小說揭露了維多利亞時代濟貧院令人痛心的惡劣環境——貧困的孩子在那裡忍受營養不良和嚴厲斥責，而他動人的描寫也激勵了社會改革的倡議者，要求改善窮人的待遇。"},{"w":"detriment","p":"n.","d":"A cause of harm or damage.","c":"損害；危害","s":"The policy change was implemented without any rigorous assessment of its potential detriment to the most vulnerable populations — an imprudent omission that the subsequent independent review characterised as symptomatic of the fallacious assumption that economic efficiency and social equity were invariably complementary rather than potentially competing objectives.","t":"這項政策變更在實施前，完全沒有嚴謹評估它可能對最弱勢族群造成的損害——事後的獨立審查指出，這種輕率的疏忽反映出一個錯誤的假設：經濟效率與社會公平總是相輔相成，而非可能彼此衝突的目標。","as":"Nutritionists warn that a diet replete with processed sugar is a serious detriment to long-term health, noting that obesity and diabetes have become rife even among children, partly because of the ubiquitous marketing of sugary drinks.","at":"營養學家警告，充斥加工糖的飲食會嚴重損害長期健康，並指出肥胖和糖尿病如今甚至在兒童中也十分普遍，部分原因在於含糖飲料的廣告無所不在。"},{"w":"dispersed","p":"adj.","d":"Scattered over a wide area.","c":"被驅散的","s":"The previously cohesive community had become dispersed over two decades of economic migration, its members now dispersed across seventeen countries yet maintaining a remarkable cultural coherence through the digital channels that had become the primary medium for transmitting the traditions and language of the homeland.","t":"這個原本凝聚的社群，在二十年的經濟移民潮中四散各地，成員如今分散於十七個國家，卻透過已成為傳承家鄉傳統與語言主要媒介的數位管道，維持著驚人的文化凝聚力。","as":"Because the indigenous community's members are dispersed across remote mountain villages, efforts to preserve their endangered language have been sporadic, and elders worry that their oral tradition may not survive another generation.","at":"由於這個原住民族群的成員散居在偏遠的山村，保存其瀕危語言的努力一直斷斷續續，長者們擔心他們的口傳傳統可能無法延續到下一代。"},{"w":"doddering","p":"adj.","d":"Trembling or tottering due to old age.","c":"蹣跚的；老態龍鍾的","s":"The doddering emeritus professor confounded those who had dismissed him as intellectually diminished by delivering one of the most incisive analyses of the decade — a reminder that the superficial veneer of physical frailty could be profoundly misleading as an indicator of cognitive capability.","t":"這位步履蹣跚的榮譽教授，讓那些認為他智力已衰退的人大感意外，因為他發表了十年來最犀利的分析之一——這提醒世人，身體虛弱的表象作為判斷認知能力的指標，可能極具誤導性。","as":"The doddering old monarch, who could scarcely ascend the palace stairs without assistance, remained the nominal ruler of the kingdom, but real power had long since passed to his ambitious entourage of advisers.","at":"這位步履蹣跚的老國王沒人攙扶幾乎爬不上宮殿的階梯，他雖仍是王國名義上的統治者，實權卻早已落入他身邊那群野心勃勃的謀臣手中。"},{"w":"eruption","p":"n.","d":"A sudden violent outburst.","c":"爆發","s":"The political eruption that followed the revelation of the nefarious financial scheme had been neither unpredictable nor unforewarned — it was the inevitable consequence of years of accumulated grievances that even the most phlegmatic observers had recognised as primed for precisely this kind of turbulent catalysis.","t":"揭露那起邪惡的金融陰謀之後所爆發的政治風暴，既非無法預料，也並非毫無預警——這是多年積怨的必然結果，就連最冷靜的觀察者也看得出，局勢早已一觸即發，只待這樣的動盪催化。","as":"The eruption of Mount Vesuvius in 79 CE buried Pompeii beneath a thick layer of ash, which, though deadly to many of the town's inhabitants, created an extant record of Roman daily life that archaeologists still scrutinize with meticulous care.","at":"西元七九年維蘇威火山爆發，以厚厚的火山灰掩埋了龐貝城；這些火山灰雖奪去了許多居民的性命，卻留下一份留存至今的羅馬日常生活紀錄，考古學家至今仍一絲不苟地仔細研究。"},{"w":"hoard","p":"v.","d":"To accumulate and store secretly.","c":"囤積；貯藏","s":"The investigation revealed that several officials had been hoarding public funds in undisclosed accounts — a nefarious scheme whose cumulative scale proved awesome, the total amount eventually identified exceeding what the entire department had legitimately spent on its core public mandate during the same period.","t":"調查發現，數名官員一直把公款私藏在未申報的帳戶中——這起邪惡陰謀的累積規模令人咋舌，最終查出的總額，竟超過整個部門在同期間用於其核心公共職責的合法支出。","as":"During periods of hyperinflation, frightened citizens often hoard food and fuel, a reaction that, while understandable, can exacerbate shortages and precipitate a frenzy of panic buying that leaves the poorest families with nothing.","at":"在惡性通膨時期，驚恐的民眾常會囤積食物和燃料；這種反應雖可理解，卻可能加劇物資短缺，並引發一陣搶購狂潮，使最貧困的家庭一無所有。"},{"w":"imbibe","p":"v.","d":"To drink or absorb.","c":"飲；吸收","s":"Young scholars who imbibed the intellectual traditions of their discipline through extended apprenticeship with a distinguished mentor tended, studies suggested, to develop a more nuanced mastery than those who had acquired the same factual knowledge through purely formal academic instruction.","t":"研究顯示，透過長期追隨傑出導師學習、吸收本學科知識傳統的年輕學者，往往比只透過正規學術教學獲得同樣知識的人，發展出更細膩的專精。","as":"As an apprentice in Verrocchio's Florentine workshop, the young Leonardo imbibed a gamut of skills ranging from sculpture to painting, and his precocious talent soon rivaled that of his eminent teacher.","at":"年輕的達文西在佛羅倫斯維洛及奧的工作坊當學徒時，吸收了從雕塑到繪畫的各種技藝，他早慧的天分很快便足以與他那位聲名卓著的老師匹敵。"},{"w":"initiate","p":"v.","d":"To cause something to begin.","c":"開始；發起","s":"The decision to initiate formal proceedings was not taken lightly — the legal team had scrutinised the available evidence with meticulous care over several months before concluding that the incontrovertible nature of the documentary record justified the reputational and financial risks that litigation inevitably entailed.","t":"啟動正式訴訟程序的決定並非草率做出——法律團隊花了數個月仔細審查現有證據，最後才認定書面紀錄無可辯駁，足以承擔訴訟必然帶來的聲譽與財務風險。","as":"To revive the sluggish economy, the new administration initiated sweeping reforms to dismantle state monopolies, yet entrenched bureaucrats, fearing the loss of their comfortable sinecures, sought to stymie every proposal.","at":"為了振興停滯的經濟，新政府推動了全面改革以拆解國營壟斷事業，然而根深蒂固的官僚因害怕失去他們輕鬆的閒差，試圖阻撓每一項提案。"},{"w":"longevity","p":"n.","d":"Long life; the fact of lasting for a long time.","c":"長壽","s":"The longevity of the institution's reputation rested not on the flamboyant achievements of any single decade but on the cumulative credibility built through a century of assiduous, methodical, and largely unheralded scholarly work that had gradually made its imprimatur a reliable indicator of genuine quality.","t":"這個機構的聲譽之所以歷久不衰，靠的不是任何單一年代的耀眼成就，而是一個世紀以來勤懇、有條理且大多默默無聞的學術工作所累積的公信力，使其認可逐漸成為真正品質的可靠指標。","as":"Researchers studying the remarkable longevity of residents on the Japanese island of Okinawa attribute it to a combination of factors, including a frugal diet rich in vegetables, an active rather than sedentary lifestyle, and close coteries of lifelong friends.","at":"研究沖繩居民驚人長壽現象的學者，將其歸因於多種因素的結合，包括富含蔬菜的簡樸飲食、活躍而非久坐的生活方式，以及由終身好友組成的緊密小圈子。"},{"w":"obliterate","p":"v.","d":"To destroy utterly, wipe out.","c":"抹去；清除","s":"The conflagration had effectively obliterated three decades of accumulated archival material in a matter of hours — an awesome destruction that rendered many historical questions permanently insoluble and deprived future generations of evidence whose significance the previous generation had not fully appreciated.","t":"這場大火在短短幾小時內，就徹底摧毀了三十年來累積的檔案資料——如此驚人的毀滅，使許多歷史問題永遠無解，也讓後代失去了上一代未能充分體認其重要性的證據。","as":"The asteroid that struck the Yucatán Peninsula some sixty-six million years ago is widely believed to have obliterated most dinosaur species, plunging the planet into a prolonged darkness so inclement that only small, omnivorous creatures could survive the ensuing privation.","at":"大約六千六百萬年前撞擊猶加敦半島的小行星，一般認為消滅了大多數恐龍物種，使地球陷入漫長而嚴酷的黑暗，只有體型小、雜食性的生物才熬得過隨之而來的匱乏。"},{"w":"puny","p":"adj.","d":"Small and weak.","c":"微小的；弱小的","s":"The puny protest that gathered outside the ministry seemed to confirm the government's dismissive assessment — until a fortuitous convergence of media attention and a spontaneous surge in public outrage transformed what had begun as a desultory gathering of fewer than fifty into a nationwide movement within a single week.","t":"聚集在部會外那場人數寥寥的抗議，似乎印證了政府輕蔑的判斷——直到媒體關注與民眾怒火自發高漲意外地同時出現，原本不到五十人的零散集會，在短短一週內便發展成一場全國性運動。","as":"The puny defenses of the medieval village, consisting of a shallow ditch and a flimsy wooden fence, were no match for the mammoth siege engines the invaders deployed, and despite the valor of its defenders the settlement fell within hours.","at":"這座中世紀村莊的防禦工事十分薄弱，只有一道淺溝和一圈脆弱的木柵，根本抵擋不了入侵者部署的龐大攻城器械；儘管守軍英勇奮戰，村莊仍在數小時內淪陷。"},{"w":"rue","p":"v.","d":"To bitterly regret.","c":"後悔；悲傷","s":"She would rue the imprudent decision for years — not primarily for its direct consequences, which had been manageable, but for the precedent it had set, establishing in her own mind and in the minds of colleagues a template for the kind of desultory risk assessment she had previously prided herself on never committing.","t":"她將為那個輕率的決定後悔多年——主要不是因為其直接後果，那些尚可應付，而是因為它開了先例，在她自己和同事心中樹立了一種敷衍的風險評估模式，而她過去一向以從不犯這種錯為傲。","as":"The general would later rue his decision to ignore the scouts' ominous warnings, for his rash advance into the narrow mountain pass allowed the enemy to encircle his troops, resulting in a fiasco that ended his once illustrious career.","at":"這位將軍日後對自己忽視斥候不祥警告的決定悔恨不已，因為他草率地挺進狹窄的山隘，讓敵軍得以包圍他的部隊，釀成一場終結他昔日輝煌生涯的慘敗。"},{"w":"sage","p":"adj.","d":"Having profound wisdom.","c":"睿智的；聖人","s":"The sage counsel offered by the retiring director — to prioritise the long-term credibility of the institution over any short-term reputational management — proved prophetic, as the organisations that had heeded her advice consistently weathered the subsequent crises more effectively than those that had not.","t":"即將退休的主任所給予的睿智建議——將機構的長期公信力置於任何短期的聲譽管理之上——結果證明極具先見之明，因為聽從她建議的組織，在後來的危機中一貫比沒有聽從的組織應對得更好。","as":"Seeking sage advice on how to end the famine ravaging his provinces, the young emperor summoned the elderly philosopher, whose laconic yet incisive observations about governance had earned him renown throughout the realm.","at":"為了尋求如何終結肆虐各省之饑荒的睿智建言，年輕的皇帝召見了那位年邁的哲學家；他對治國之道的見解言簡意賅卻一針見血，因而名聞全國。"},{"w":"senile","p":"adj.","d":"Having or showing the weakness of old age.","c":"衰老的；老態龍鍾的","s":"His opponents' whisper campaign suggesting he had become senile was comprehensively refuted by the trenchant precision of his parliamentary interventions — each contribution demonstrating an acuity of analysis and a command of detail that put younger colleagues to shame.","t":"他的對手私下散布他已年老昏聵的耳語，但他在議會中發言時的犀利精準，徹底駁斥了這種說法——每一次發言都展現出敏銳的分析能力與對細節的掌握，讓年輕的同僚自嘆不如。","as":"As the aging tycoon became increasingly senile, his relatives began to jostle over his fortune, and a protracted, acrimonious legal battle ensued when one heir claimed that the others had coerced the confused old man into rewriting his will.","at":"隨著這位年邁的大亨日益衰老糊塗，他的親屬開始爭奪他的財產；其中一名繼承人聲稱其他人脅迫這位神智不清的老人改寫遺囑，一場曠日持久、劍拔弩張的官司隨之展開。"},{"w":"virile","p":"adj.","d":"Having strength and energy, manly.","c":"有男子氣概的","s":"The virile energy with which the young conductor approached the most demanding orchestral repertoire — his physical commitment to the music and his ability to sustain intense concentration across four-hour rehearsals — made an immediate impression on musicians accustomed to the more sedentary podium manner of his predecessors.","t":"這位年輕指揮家以充滿陽剛活力的方式詮釋最艱難的管弦樂曲目——他全身心投入音樂，並能在長達四小時的排練中保持高度專注——讓習慣了前任指揮較靜態台風的樂手們立刻留下深刻印象。","as":"Classical Greek sculptors often portrayed Heracles as a virile, muscular hero whose intrepid spirit was the antithesis of cowardice, and these statues became a paragon of physical perfection that Renaissance artists later strove to imitate.","at":"古典希臘雕塑家常把海克力斯塑造成一位雄健壯碩的英雄，其無畏的精神正是怯懦的對立面；這些雕像成為體態完美的典範，後來文藝復興時期的藝術家也努力仿效。"}]},{"unit":26,"cards":[{"w":"acute","p":"adj.","d":"Present or experienced to a severe degree.","c":"敏銳的；急性的","s":"The organisation's most acute problem was not the detriment caused by individual failures but the systemic indifference that permeated every level of management — a diffuse reluctance to initiate difficult conversations that had allowed minor dysfunctions to accumulate into a deplorable institutional culture.","t":"該組織最迫切的問題不是個別失敗造成的損害，而是滲透到管理每個層面的系統性漠不關心——一種使輕微功能失調積累成可悲制度文化的對啟動困難對話的彌漫性不情願。","as":"During the drought, the acute shortage of clean water exacerbated the spread of waterborne maladies, and relief workers struggled to accommodate the throng of hapless villagers who had walked for days to reach the makeshift camp.","at":"乾旱期間，乾淨用水嚴重短缺，使經由水傳播的疾病更加猖獗；救援人員疲於安置那一大群走了好幾天才抵達臨時營地的不幸村民。"},{"w":"aversion","p":"n.","d":"A strong dislike or disinclination.","c":"厭惡；反感","s":"Her deep aversion to the ostentatious display of wealth was both aesthetic and philosophical — she regarded the indiscriminate accumulation of luxury goods as not merely aesthetically deplorable but as a symptom of the materialism she considered antithetical to any serious engagement with what actually mattered.","t":"她對炫耀性財富展示的深度厭惡既是審美上的也是哲學上的——她認為對奢侈品的不加選擇的積累不僅在審美上可悲，而且是她認為與真正重要的事物認真接觸的對立面——物質主義的症狀。","as":"Her lifelong aversion to public speaking seemed incongruous with her reputation as an incisive critic, yet colleagues who scrutinized her essays understood that she preferred to wield her trenchant arguments on the printed page.","at":"她終生厭惡公開演說，這似乎與她身為犀利評論家的名聲格格不入；然而仔細研讀過她文章的同事都明白，她寧可在紙上施展那些一針見血的論點。"},{"w":"cogent","p":"adj.","d":"Clear, logical, and convincing.","c":"令人信服的","s":"The report presented the most cogent case that had yet been assembled for fundamental structural reform — a careful marshalling of incontrovertible empirical evidence that made continued resistance to change appear not merely imprudent but fundamentally incompatible with the institution's own stated objectives.","t":"該報告提出了迄今為止為根本性結構改革組裝的最有說服力的案例——對無可辯駁的實證證據的謹慎整理，使繼續抵制變革顯得不僅輕率，而且從根本上與機構自身聲明的目標不相容。","as":"The lawyer presented such a cogent argument, supported by meticulously organized documents that corroborated every key claim, that even the most incredulous jurors were compelled to concede that the alleged fraud could not have occurred as the prosecution described.","at":"這位律師提出了極具說服力的論證，並以條理分明、足以證實每項關鍵主張的文件作為佐證，就連最心存懷疑的陪審員也不得不承認，所指控的詐欺不可能如檢方所描述的那樣發生。"},{"w":"evince","p":"v.","d":"To show or reveal a quality.","c":"表明；顯示","s":"The candidate evinced a cognitive flexibility during the interview that immediately distinguished her from the other applicants — a spontaneous ability to imbibe new information rapidly, integrate it with existing knowledge, and produce nuanced assessments that the panel found genuinely impressive.","t":"候選人在面試中展示了一種認知靈活性，立即使她從其他申請者中脫穎而出——一種快速吸收新信息、將其與現有知識整合並產生小組認為真正令人印象深刻的細緻評估的自發能力。","as":"Although the young diplomat tried to appear phlegmatic during the tense negotiations, his tremulous voice and furtive glances at the clock evinced an anxiety that his astute counterparts were quick to discern.","at":"儘管這位年輕外交官在緊張的談判中努力表現得沉著冷靜，他顫抖的聲音和不時偷瞄時鐘的眼神，卻透露出內心的焦慮，而精明的談判對手很快就察覺到了。"},{"w":"gist","p":"n.","d":"The substance or main point.","c":"主旨；要點","s":"The gist of the committee's lengthy and verbose report could be distilled into three incisive sentences, a fact that the chair acknowledged privately while defending publicly the necessity of documenting every nuance of a process whose complexity the abbreviated version could not adequately convey.","t":"委員會冗長且囉嗦報告的主旨可以提煉成三句簡練的話，這一事實主席私下承認，同時公開捍衛記錄過程每個細微之處的必要性，這些細微之處是縮寫版本無法充分傳達的。","as":"Rather than peruse every page of the interminable government report, the busy journalist asked an analyst to summarize its gist, which was that years of lax regulation had allowed pernicious pollutants to permeate the city's groundwater.","at":"這位忙碌的記者沒有逐頁細讀那份冗長不堪的政府報告，而是請一位分析師概述其要點：多年來寬鬆的監管，使有害污染物滲入了該市的地下水。"},{"w":"hostile","p":"adj.","d":"Opposed and aggressive.","c":"敵對的","s":"The hostile reception that greeted the reform proposals reflected not genuine substantive disagreement but the fractious institutional defensiveness of an organisation that had grown so sedentary in its practices that any challenge to established procedure was experienced as an existential threat.","t":"對改革提案的敵對接待反映的不是真正的實質性分歧，而是一個在其實踐中已變得如此久坐以至於任何對既定程序的挑戰都被視為生存威脅的組織的好爭吵的制度防禦性。","as":"When the expatriate scientist returned home, she encountered a hostile press that derided her controversial research on genetic engineering and disparaged her as a mere puppet of the foreign corporations that had funded her laboratory.","at":"這位旅居海外的科學家返國時，遭遇了充滿敵意的媒體，他們嘲笑她關於基因工程的爭議性研究，並貶低她不過是資助其實驗室的外國企業的傀儡。"},{"w":"inevitable","p":"adj.","d":"Certain to happen, unavoidable.","c":"不可避免的","s":"The inevitable consequence of decades of cumulative neglect was a catastrophic infrastructure failure that, while awesome in its scale and deplorable in its human cost, surprised none of the engineers who had been sporadic but persistent in warning about the accelerating deterioration of the underlying systems.","t":"數十年累積忽視的不可避免後果是一場災難性的基礎設施失敗，雖然其規模令人敬畏且其人員代價令人痛惜，但這並不讓那些零散但持續地警告基礎系統加速惡化的工程師感到驚訝。","as":"Once the empire's profligate rulers had squandered its wealth on sumptuous palaces while the indigent masses starved, many historians argue, rebellion was inevitable, though few at the time could foresee the havoc it would wreak.","at":"許多歷史學家認為，當帝國揮霍無度的統治者把財富浪費在奢華宮殿上、而貧困的百姓卻在挨餓時，叛亂就已無可避免，儘管當時鮮少有人能預見它將造成多大的浩劫。"},{"w":"intrinsic","p":"adj.","d":"Belonging naturally, essential.","c":"固有的；內在的","s":"The intrinsic value of the collection was not its market worth, which fluctuated with the arbitrary preferences of successive generations of collectors, but the irreplaceable historical information embodied in each artifact — a significance that its philistine new owner appeared entirely incapable of perceiving.","t":"這批藏品的固有價值不是其市場價值（隨著歷代收藏家的任意偏好而波動），而是每件文物所包含的不可替代的歷史信息——其庸俗的新主人似乎完全無法感知的重要性。","as":"Critics who dismiss comic books as mundane entertainment overlook their intrinsic artistic value, for the most accomplished illustrators combine visual virtuosity with narratives as complex and nuanced as those found in prestigious literary novels.","at":"把漫畫斥為平凡娛樂的評論者，忽略了它們內在的藝術價值；因為最有成就的插畫家，能將精湛的視覺技藝與不輸給知名文學小說那般複雜而細膩的敘事結合在一起。"},{"w":"jettison","p":"v.","d":"To throw or drop from an aircraft or ship.","c":"拋棄；丟棄","s":"The pragmatic decision to jettison several flagship policies within the first year in office caused considerable chagrin among the party's most ardent supporters, who had sacrificed considerable effort and resources to achieve the electoral outcome that was now being so casually abandoned.","t":"在任職第一年內拋棄幾項旗艦政策的務實決定，在黨內最熱烈支持者中引起了相當大的懊惱，他們為實現現在被如此隨意拋棄的選舉結果犧牲了相當多的努力和資源。","as":"As the storm intensified and the crippled cargo ship began to list dangerously, the captain ordered his crew to jettison the heavy containers, a drastic but feasible measure to avert an imminent and catastrophic sinking in the turbulent waters.","at":"隨著暴風雨加劇、受損的貨輪開始危險地傾斜，船長下令船員將沉重的貨櫃拋入海中；這是個激烈但可行的措施，以避免船隻在洶湧的海浪中即將發生的災難性沉沒。"},{"w":"lethargic","p":"adj.","d":"Affected by lethargy, sluggish.","c":"昏睡的；遲鈍的","s":"The organisation had grown so lethargic over years of guaranteed institutional support that the sudden withdrawal of its aegis produced a genuinely catalytic crisis — the acute shock of financial vulnerability galvanising a leadership team that had become effectively inert under conditions of chronic comfort.","t":"該組織在多年有保障的機構支持下已變得如此遲鈍，以至於其庇護的突然撤除產生了真正的催化危機——財務脆弱性的急性衝擊激勵了在長期舒適條件下已有效變得惰性的領導團隊。","as":"Patients recovering from the virulent infection often remain lethargic for weeks, and physicians caution that such persistent sluggishness may be symptomatic of a latent complication or even a harbinger of relapse.","at":"從這種猛烈感染中康復的病人，往往會連續數週昏沉無力；醫師提醒，這種持續的倦怠可能是潛在併發症的症狀，甚至是復發的前兆。"},{"w":"lucrative","p":"adj.","d":"Producing a great deal of profit.","c":"有利可圖的","s":"The contract proved extraordinarily lucrative in the short term but catastrophically damaging in the long term — a pattern that the most perspicacious financial analysts had identified from the outset as inherently unsustainable, their cogent warnings consistently jettisoned in favour of the compelling appeal of immediate returns.","t":"合同在短期內被證明非常有利可圖，但在長期卻具有災難性破壞性——最有洞察力的財務分析師從一開始就確定的固有不可持續的模式，他們有說服力的警告不斷被拋棄，以支持立即回報的強烈吸引力。","as":"The spice trade proved so lucrative for European merchants that belligerent rival nations fought numerous skirmishes to wrest control of key ports, and the immense profits fueled the opulence of courts from Lisbon to Amsterdam.","at":"香料貿易為歐洲商人帶來極為豐厚的利潤，以致好戰的敵對國家為了奪取重要港口的控制權而爆發多次小規模衝突，而巨額利潤也支撐起從里斯本到阿姆斯特丹各地宮廷的奢華。"},{"w":"paramount","p":"adj.","d":"More important than anything else.","c":"首要的；至高無上的","s":"The preservation of institutional integrity was paramount in the board's deliberations — more salient even than short-term financial considerations, more acute than reputational concerns, because without that foundational credibility every other objective the organisation aspired to achieve became essentially chimerical.","t":"在董事會的審議中，維護機構誠信是首要的——甚至比短期財務考量更突出，比聲譽關切更迫切，因為沒有那個基礎可信度，組織渴望實現的其他每個目標基本上都變成了空想。","as":"For engineers designing bridges in earthquake-prone regions, safety is paramount, so they deem it imprudent to curtail spending on reinforcements that help an edifice withstand tremors capable of razing less sturdy structures.","at":"對於在地震頻繁地區設計橋梁的工程師而言，安全至上，因此他們認為削減補強工程的經費是不智之舉，因為這些補強能讓建築承受足以摧毀較不堅固結構的震動。"},{"w":"prevalent","p":"adj.","d":"Widespread, common in a particular area.","c":"普遍的；盛行的","s":"Corruption had become so prevalent within the procurement system that even the most altruistic officials found themselves navigating a labyrinth of informal expectations whose cumulative pressure made ethical neutrality practically impossible without accepting the professional detriment that resistance invariably entailed.","t":"腐敗在採購系統中變得如此普遍，以至於即使是最無私的官員也發現自己在一個非正式期望的迷宮中行走，其累積壓力使倫理中立在實踐中幾乎不可能，除非接受抵制不可避免地帶來的職業損害。","as":"Superstitions about unlucky numbers remain prevalent across East Asia, and anthropologists observe that even urbane, highly educated residents of Taipei may avoid the number four, a taboo steeped in the fact that it sounds like the word for death.","at":"對不吉利數字的迷信在東亞依然普遍，人類學家觀察到，即使是溫文儒雅、受過高等教育的台北居民，也可能避開數字四；這個禁忌源於「四」的發音與「死」相近。"},{"w":"rebuke","p":"v.","d":"To express sharp disapproval.","c":"斥責；指責","s":"The judge rebuked the attorney with unusual sharpness for the third time that afternoon, the lethargic pace of the proceedings and the attorney's remiss preparation having compounded the court's frustration to a point where the characteristic judicial restraint could no longer be maintained.","t":"法官在那天下午第三次以不尋常的犀利斥責了律師，訴訟的遲鈍步伐和律師怠忽的準備使法院的挫敗感積累到特有的司法克制無法再維持的地步。","as":"The senator publicly rebuked her colleague for his flagrant breach of ethics, declaring that handing sinecures to relatives was a form of favoritism that undermined public trust and should no longer be tolerated.","at":"這位參議員公開斥責她的同僚公然違反倫理規範，並宣稱把閒差肥缺分派給親戚是一種裙帶關係，會損害公眾信任，不應再被容忍。"},{"w":"remiss","p":"adj.","d":"Lacking care or attention to duty.","c":"怠忽職守的","s":"It would have been gravely remiss not to acknowledge the acute detriment caused by the policy — the incontrovertible evidence of harm was too prevalent and the vulnerability of those affected too manifest for any responsible authority to maintain the lethargic indifference that had characterised the previous administration's response.","t":"不承認政策造成的嚴重損害將是嚴重的失職——傷害的無可辯駁的證據太普遍了，受影響者的脆弱性太明顯，任何負責任的當局都無法維持前任政府回應所特有的遲鈍漠不關心。","as":"Investigators concluded that the factory's inspectors had been remiss in their duties, conducting only perfunctory checks of the aging boilers and dismissing the ominous noises reverberating through the pipes, and were therefore partly culpable for the deadly explosion.","at":"調查人員斷定，該工廠的檢查員怠忽職守，只對老舊鍋爐進行敷衍了事的檢查，並對在管線中迴盪的不祥聲響置之不理，因此必須為這場致命爆炸負起部分責任。"},{"w":"superficial","p":"adj.","d":"Appearing to be true only until examined.","c":"表面的；膚淺的","s":"The superficial resemblance between the two approaches concealed a fundamental incompatibility that only became apparent under acute scrutiny — a cogent demonstration of why rigorous analysis was invariably more valuable than the kind of cursory pattern-matching that generated false confidence in misleading analogies.","t":"這兩種方法之間表面的相似性掩蓋了只有在嚴格審查下才變得明顯的根本不相容性——這是一個有說服力的證明，說明為什麼嚴格的分析總是比產生對誤導性類比的虛假信心的那種粗略模式匹配更有價值。","as":"Although the two economic theories bear a superficial resemblance, when scrutinized closely they rest on disparate premises and arrive at conclusions that are, in many crucial respects, the very antithesis of each other.","at":"雖然這兩套經濟理論表面上相似，但仔細檢視就會發現，它們建立在截然不同的前提上，得出的結論在許多關鍵方面也恰恰完全相反。"},{"w":"terse","p":"adj.","d":"Sparing in the use of words, brief.","c":"簡潔的；扼要的","s":"Her terse response to the parliamentary committee — a single sentence that simultaneously acknowledged the gist of the criticism, conceded the salient factual points, and outlined the remedial measures already underway — was regarded by observers as a masterclass in the art of lucid accountability under pressure.","t":"她對議會委員會的簡短回應——一個同時承認批評要點、承認突出事實要點並概述已在進行的補救措施的單句話——被觀察者視為在壓力下清晰問責藝術的大師課。","as":"Known for her terse replies, the reticent novelist answered the interviewer's verbose questions with a single word or a shrug, a habit that some critics construed as arrogance but admirers regarded as a laudable refusal to indulge in empty chatter.","at":"這位沉默寡言的小說家以回答簡短扼要聞名，面對訪問者冗長的提問，她只用一個字或聳聳肩回應；有些評論家將此解讀為傲慢，但欣賞她的人卻認為，這是拒絕沉溺於空洞閒聊、值得稱許的態度。"},{"w":"transient","p":"adj.","d":"Lasting only for a short time.","c":"短暫的；瞬息的","s":"The transient nature of political popularity was nowhere more apparent than in the remarkable vicissitudes of this particular leader's career — the same policies that had generated awesome public approval in one decade generating acute hostility in the next as circumstances and expectations changed.","t":"政治受歡迎程度的短暫性質在這位特定領導人職業生涯的顯著興衰中表現得最為明顯——同樣的政策在一個十年中產生了令人敬畏的公眾認可，在下一個十年中隨著情況和期望的變化產生了急性敵意。","as":"The desert bloom is a transient phenomenon: after a rare downpour, seemingly inert seeds burst into flower and saturate the barren landscape with color, but within weeks the blossoms wither and the arid plains revert to their usual drab hues.","at":"沙漠花海是短暫的現象：一場難得的大雨過後，看似毫無生機的種子迸發成花，為荒蕪的大地染滿色彩；然而短短數週之內，花朵便會凋謝，乾旱的平原又恢復往常單調的色調。"},{"w":"tussle","p":"n.","d":"A vigorous struggle or scuffle.","c":"扭打；爭執","s":"The prolonged tussle between the two factions within the coalition had been so depleting of institutional energy and public credibility that both sides eventually acknowledged the acute detriment it was causing — a rare moment of shared perspicacity that allowed negotiators to initiate the compromise process.","t":"聯盟兩個派系之間的長期爭執對機構活力和公信力的消耗如此之大，以至於雙方最終承認了它造成的嚴重損害——一個罕見的共同洞察力時刻，使談判者得以啟動妥協進程。","as":"What began as a minor tussle between two irate fans over a souvenir ball quickly escalated into a melee, prompting vigilant security guards to quell the disturbance before the frenzy spread through the stadium.","at":"起初只是兩名憤怒的球迷為了一顆紀念球而發生的小扭打，很快便演變成一場混戰，促使警覺的保全人員在騷動蔓延至整座球場之前迅速平息這場混亂。"},{"w":"vogue","p":"n.","d":"The prevailing fashion at a particular time.","c":"流行；時尚","s":"The vogue for minimalist architectural aesthetics had so thoroughly permeated institutional design that buildings of genuine distinction had become as rare as they were salient — their virtuosity of form and material all the more striking against the backdrop of the prevailing homogeneity.","t":"極簡主義建築美學的流行如此徹底地滲透到機構設計中，以至於真正卓越的建築變得像它們突出一樣稀少——其形式和材料的精湛技藝在普遍同質性的背景下更加引人注目。","as":"Minimalist interior design has been in vogue for years, as affluent urban residents eschew ornate furniture in favor of clean lines, though some critics contend that the fashion is merely a veneer of simplicity masking costly materialism.","at":"極簡主義室內設計已流行多年，富裕的都市居民捨棄華麗的家具，偏好簡潔的線條；不過有些評論家認為，這股潮流不過是披著簡約的外衣，掩飾其背後昂貴的物質主義。"}]},{"unit":27,"cards":[{"w":"adamant","p":"adj.","d":"Refusing to be persuaded or to change.","c":"固執的；堅定不移的","s":"She remained adamant in her refusal to jettison the core principles of the reform package despite the vogue for pragmatic compromise that had taken hold among her colleagues — a terse defiance that her adversaries found exasperating and her supporters celebrated as the paramount virtue of genuine leadership.","t":"儘管同事間流行務實妥協，她在拒絕拋棄改革方案核心原則方面仍然堅定不移——這種簡潔的抗拒讓她的對手感到惱怒，讓她的支持者慶賀為真正領導力的首要美德。","as":"Despite mounting evidence that the policy was ineffectual, the minister remained adamant that it would eventually succeed, refusing to recant his position even when his own advisers presented incontrovertible data showing that unemployment had surged.","at":"儘管越來越多證據顯示該政策成效不彰，部長仍堅持它終將成功；即使他自己的顧問提出無可辯駁的數據，顯示失業率已急遽攀升，他仍拒絕收回自己的立場。"},{"w":"ardent","p":"adj.","d":"Very enthusiastic or passionate.","c":"熱烈的；激情的","s":"The ardent support of the organisation's most prominent patron had transformed what might have remained an inchoate research initiative into a well-funded programme with both the aegis of institutional credibility and the resources to initiate genuinely ambitious experimental work.","t":"該組織最著名贊助人的熱烈支持，將可能一直保持不成熟研究倡議的東西，轉變為擁有機構可信度庇護和資源以啟動真正雄心勃勃實驗工作的資金充足計劃。","as":"An ardent advocate of wildlife conservation, the biologist spent years in the rainforests of Borneo documenting indigenous species, and her zealous campaigns eventually persuaded the government to protect their dwindling habitat.","at":"這位生物學家熱切擁護野生動物保育，在婆羅洲的雨林中度過多年，記錄當地原生物種；她滿腔熱忱的倡議行動，最終說服政府保護這些物種日益縮減的棲息地。"},{"w":"array","p":"n.","d":"An impressive display or collection.","c":"陣列；打扮","s":"The array of cogent arguments assembled by the defence team was impressive in its breadth — encompassing technical forensic evidence, procedural objections, character testimony, and constitutional challenges that collectively presented the prosecution with a formidable and multi-layered response to address.","t":"辯護團隊匯集的有說服力論點的陣列在廣度上令人印象深刻——涵蓋技術法証證據、程序異議、品格證詞和憲法挑戰，這些共同為檢察官提出了一個需要回應的強大且多層次的挑戰。","as":"Curated by an eminent archaeologist, the museum's new exhibition features a dazzling array of ancient artifacts, from ornate jade carvings to rudimentary bronze tools, allowing visitors to perceive how craftsmanship evolved over many dynasties.","at":"博物館這次的新展覽由一位知名考古學家策畫，展出琳瑯滿目的古代文物，從精雕細琢的玉器到簡樸的青銅工具應有盡有，讓參觀者得以看出工藝技術如何歷經多個朝代而演進。"},{"w":"bereft","p":"adj.","d":"Lacking something or feeling a great loss.","c":"喪失的；被剝奪的","s":"bereft of both the institutional aegis that had previously protected it and the lucrative funding streams that had sustained its research programme, the laboratory faced an acute crisis that tested the resilience and resourcefulness of every remaining member with a severity none had previously encountered.","t":"失去了以前保護它的制度庇護和維持其研究計劃的有利可圖的資金流，這個實驗室面臨著一場嚴峻的危機，以前所未有的嚴重程度考驗著每個剩餘成員的韌性和足智多謀。","as":"Bereft of the government subsidies that had once sustained them, many small farmers endured severe privation, and some succumbed to destitution as young villagers migrated to cities in search of better remuneration.","at":"失去了曾經賴以維生的政府補助，許多小農飽受困頓之苦，有些人更陷入赤貧，因為村裡的年輕人紛紛遷往城市，尋求更好的報酬。"},{"w":"besmirch","p":"v.","d":"To damage or tarnish a reputation.","c":"玷污；毀謗","s":"His adversaries had systematically attempted to besmirch his reputation through a carefully orchestrated campaign of innuendo and selective disclosure — a nefarious strategy that the most sagacious observers recognised as evidence of the weakness of their substantive case rather than the strength of their ethical concerns.","t":"他的對手通過精心策劃的影射和選擇性披露運動，系統地試圖玷污他的名聲——最睿智的觀察者認識到這是他們實質性案例薄弱的證據，而不是其倫理關切強度的惡意策略。","as":"The anonymous pamphlets, filled with scurrilous rumors and fabricated quotations, were designed to besmirch the reformist candidate, but voters quickly recognized them as a crude subterfuge orchestrated by her nefarious rivals.","at":"這些匿名小冊子充斥著惡毒的謠言和捏造的引言，目的是要抹黑那位改革派候選人；然而選民很快便看穿，這不過是她那些居心不良的對手所策劃的拙劣詭計。"},{"w":"constrict","p":"v.","d":"To make or become narrow or tight.","c":"壓縮；束緊","s":"The increasingly hostile regulatory environment had begun to constrict the sector's capacity for innovation — the cumulative weight of compliance requirements becoming so paramount in operational planning that it left insufficient resources for the experimental initiatives that had historically generated the most valuable advances.","t":"日益敵對的監管環境已開始壓縮該行業的創新能力——合規要求的累積重量在運營規劃中變得如此首要，以至於留給歷史上產生最有價值進步的實驗性倡議的資源不足。","as":"During an asthma attack, which afflicts millions of children worldwide, inflamed airways constrict so tightly that each breath becomes excruciating, and without prompt treatment the episode can precipitate a potentially lethal shortage of oxygen.","at":"氣喘侵擾著全世界數以百萬計的兒童；發作時，發炎的呼吸道會緊縮到每次呼吸都痛苦萬分，若不及時治療，可能會引發足以致命的缺氧。"},{"w":"culminate","p":"v.","d":"To reach a climax or point of highest development.","c":"達到頂點","s":"Three decades of ardent research and countless setbacks culminated in a discovery that the scientific community immediately recognised as a landmark advance — the kind of paradigm-shifting finding that justified not merely the researcher's own sacrifice but the entire institutional investment in basic science.","t":"三十年熱烈的研究和無數的挫折達到頂點，產生了科學界立即認可為里程碑式進步的發現——這種改變範式的發現不僅證明了研究人員自身的犧牲，還證明了整個機構在基礎科學投資的合理性。","as":"Years of clandestine meetings and acrimonious negotiations between the implacable rival factions culminated in a historic peace accord, though skeptics warned that a schism so deeply rooted could not be healed by a single document.","at":"互不相讓的敵對派系之間多年的祕密會談與激烈談判，最終促成了一項歷史性的和平協定；不過懷疑論者警告，如此根深蒂固的分裂，不可能靠一紙文件就彌合。"},{"w":"egotist","p":"n.","d":"A person excessively absorbed in themselves.","c":"利己主義者；自大狂","s":"The celebrated director was widely regarded as an incorrigible egotist whose notorious disregard for his collaborators' contributions had besmirched several otherwise distinguished professional relationships — yet his virtuosity was so unambiguous that the industry continued, with considerable ambivalence, to celebrate his work.","t":"這位著名導演被廣泛認為是一個無可救藥的自大狂，他對合作者貢獻的臭名昭著的漠視，玷污了幾段本來傑出的職業關係——然而他的精湛技藝如此明確，以至於業界繼續以相當大的矛盾心理讚揚他的作品。","as":"An unabashed egotist, the celebrity chef constantly embellished stories of his own accomplishments and belittled his staff, so few were surprised when his obsequious entourage abandoned him after his restaurant failed.","at":"這位名廚是個毫不掩飾的自大狂，總愛誇大自己的成就並貶低員工；因此當他的餐廳倒閉後，那群阿諛奉承的隨從棄他而去，幾乎沒有人感到意外。"},{"w":"exultation","p":"n.","d":"A feeling of triumphant joy.","c":"狂喜；歡躍","s":"The team's exultation at achieving the breakthrough was entirely understandable given the arduous years of cumulative setbacks that had preceded it — the years of bereft resources, hostile institutional environments, and sporadic encouragement that had tested the resolve of every member.","t":"團隊在取得突破後的狂喜完全可以理解，考慮到之前艱苦的多年累積挫折——資源匱乏、敵對的制度環境和零散鼓勵的歲月，這些考驗了每個成員的決心。","as":"The exultation of the rescue workers was palpable when the last trapped miner emerged from the subterranean tunnel, having survived the collapse because a fortuitous pocket of air had shielded him from the falling debris.","at":"當最後一名受困礦工從地底坑道中走出時，救援人員的狂喜溢於言表；他之所以能在坍塌中倖存，是因為一個幸運形成的空氣空間替他擋住了掉落的碎石。"},{"w":"falter","p":"v.","d":"To lose strength or momentum.","c":"蹣跚；動搖","s":"Despite the acute pressure of the hostile questioning, she never falter ed in her testimony — delivering each response with a terse precision that demonstrated a command of detail and an equanimity under scrutiny that only intensified the committee's conviction that she had prepared her account with exceptional thoroughness.","t":"儘管受到敵對質疑的強烈壓力，她在證詞中從未動搖——以一種簡潔的精確性提供每個回應，展示了對細節的掌握和在審查下的平靜，這只加強了委員會的信念，認為她以非凡的徹底性準備了她的陳述。","as":"The economy began to falter after the central bank raised interest rates too abruptly, and as sporadic layoffs gave way to rampant unemployment, the pundits who had prognosticated a swift recovery were forced to revise their forecasts.","at":"中央銀行升息過於倉促之後，經濟開始走弱；隨著零星的裁員演變成猖獗的失業潮，那些曾預言經濟將迅速復甦的專家也不得不修正他們的預測。"},{"w":"humility","p":"n.","d":"A modest view of one's own importance.","c":"謙卑；謙遜","s":"The sage advisor was notable as much for her humility as for her perspicacity — always careful to acknowledge the provisional nature of her most cogent conclusions, and genuinely receptive to evidence that challenged her existing frameworks in ways that her more egotistical colleagues rarely managed.","t":"這位睿智的顧問以她的謙卑和洞察力同樣著名——總是小心地承認她最有說服力的結論的暫時性，並真正接受以她更加自大的同事很少能做到的方式挑戰她現有框架的證據。","as":"Despite receiving the Nobel Prize, the physicist spoke with genuine humility, attributing her breakthrough to the assiduous work of her students and declining the ostentatious celebrations that her avid admirers had planned.","at":"儘管榮獲諾貝爾獎，這位物理學家仍然真誠謙遜，將自己的突破歸功於學生們勤奮不懈的努力，並婉拒了熱情的仰慕者為她籌劃的鋪張慶祝活動。"},{"w":"invective","p":"n.","d":"Insulting, abusive, or highly critical language.","c":"辱罵；猛烈抨擊","s":"The memo's extraordinary invective — language so vitriolic that several recipients questioned whether it had been intended for internal circulation at all — besmirched the author's reputation as effectively as any of his adversaries might have hoped, demonstrating the paramount importance of emotional regulation in professional communications.","t":"備忘錄非同尋常的辱罵——措辭如此刻薄，以至於幾位收件人質疑它是否根本打算供內部流通——如他的任何對手所希望的那樣有效地玷污了作者的聲譽，展示了情緒調節在職業溝通中的首要重要性。","as":"The televised debate quickly degenerated into a torrent of invective, with both candidates hurling derogatory epithets at each other instead of addressing the pertinent issues that voters actually cared about.","at":"這場電視辯論很快便淪為一連串的謾罵，兩位候選人互相拋出貶損的稱號，卻不去處理選民真正關心的相關議題。"},{"w":"inveterate","p":"adj.","d":"Having a particular habit or activity for a long time.","c":"根深蒂固的；積習的","s":"The inveterate pessimism of the organisation's most senior strategist had become so prevalent in the institutional culture that even genuinely propitious developments were routinely greeted with scepticism rather than the ardent enthusiasm they deserved — a pattern of cognitive distortion that impeded effective decision-making.","t":"該組織最高級戰略家根深蒂固的悲觀主義已在制度文化中變得如此普遍，以至於即使是真正吉利的發展也常常以懷疑而非它們應得的熱烈熱情被迎接——一種阻礙有效決策的認知扭曲模式。","as":"An inveterate procrastinator, the novelist would ponder a single paragraph for weeks, yet his editor accepted these delays because his prose, once completed, was invariably impeccable and replete with vivid imagery.","at":"這位小說家積習難改、老愛拖延，常常為了一個段落苦思數週；然而編輯仍包容這些延誤，因為他的文字一旦完成，總是無懈可擊，而且充滿生動的意象。"},{"w":"obscure","p":"adj.","d":"Not well known or hard to understand.","c":"模糊的；默默無聞的","s":"The citation's obscure reference to an inveterate tradition of the region proved to be the pivotal clue — a recondite allusion that only a specialist in the particular sub-field could perceive, yet once recognised, rendered the entire document's previously cryptic meaning immediately transparent.","t":"引文中對該地區根深蒂固傳統的模糊引用被證明是關鍵線索——一個只有特定子領域專家才能感知的深奧暗示，但一旦被識別，立即使整個文件以前神秘的含義變得清晰透明。","as":"Once an obscure painter who sold almost nothing despite his prolific output, Vincent van Gogh is now hailed as a paragon of artistic innovation, and his canvases command prices that would have seemed chimerical to the impoverished artist.","at":"梵谷生前雖然創作量驚人，卻幾乎賣不出任何作品，是個沒沒無聞的畫家；如今他被譽為藝術創新的典範，其畫作的售價，對當年窮困潦倒的他而言簡直是天方夜譚。"},{"w":"pinnacle","p":"n.","d":"The most successful point, the peak.","c":"頂點；巔峰","s":"Reaching the pinnacle of the discipline required not merely assiduous technical preparation but a particular quality of creative audacity that could not be taught — the willingness to initiate experiments whose failure probability was high precisely because their potential contribution was so transformative.","t":"達到學科的頂點不僅需要勤勉的技術準備，還需要一種無法教授的特殊創造性膽識——願意啟動失敗概率高的實驗，恰恰是因為它們的潛在貢獻如此具有變革性。","as":"At the pinnacle of its power, the Roman Empire seemed monolithic and invincible, yet historians detect in that era the incipient decadence and civil strife that would gradually erode its foundations.","at":"羅馬帝國在權力巔峰時期看似堅如磐石、無可匹敵，但歷史學家從那個時代中察覺到初露端倪的腐化與內部紛爭，而正是這些因素逐漸侵蝕了帝國的根基。"},{"w":"prodigy","p":"n.","d":"A person with exceptional talents.","c":"神童；奇蹟","s":"The young prodigy had accumulated an array of prestigious accolades by the age of sixteen that most practitioners in the field would consider remarkable at any age — yet those who knew her best cautioned against the chimerical assumption that early promise invariably culminated in enduring achievement.","t":"這位年輕的神童在十六歲時已積累了一批享有聲望的榮譽，大多數該領域的從業者在任何年齡都會認為這是非凡的——然而最了解她的人對早期承諾不變地最終達到持久成就的空想假設提出了警告。","as":"A musical prodigy who composed his first symphony as a child, Mozart displayed a precocious mastery that astonished the royal courts of Europe, though his later years were marred by pecuniary troubles and the indifference of fickle patrons.","at":"莫札特是位音樂神童，年幼時便創作了第一首交響曲，他早熟的才華令歐洲各國宮廷驚嘆不已；然而他晚年卻深受財務困境所苦，也飽嘗反覆無常的贊助者的冷漠。"},{"w":"pungent","p":"adj.","d":"Having a sharply strong taste or smell.","c":"辛辣的；刺鼻的","s":"The critic's prose style was as pungent as his wit was acute — his vitriolic assessments of mediocre work delivering their invective with a precision that made them impossible to dismiss even by those most ardently committed to defending the targets of his considerable scorn.","t":"這位評論家的文章風格和他的機智一樣辛辣——他對平庸作品的刻薄評估以一種精確性傳達其辱罵，使那些最熱烈致力於為其相當蔑視的目標辯護的人都無法置之不理。","as":"The pungent odor of durian is so infamous that many hotels and subways in Southeast Asia have imposed a prohibition on the fruit, yet its devoted fans insist that anyone who overcomes an initial squeamish reaction will find its creamy flesh redolent of almonds and caramel.","at":"榴槤刺鼻的氣味惡名昭彰，東南亞許多飯店和地鐵都明令禁止攜帶這種水果；然而它的忠實愛好者堅稱，只要克服起初的反胃感，就會發現它綿密的果肉散發著杏仁與焦糖的香氣。"},{"w":"retrospect","p":"n.","d":"A survey of past time or events.","c":"回顧；追溯","s":"In retrospect, the series of imprudent decisions that had precipitated the crisis appeared so obviously avoidable that the investigators found it difficult to evince any sympathetic understanding of how rational actors had failed to perceive the paramount risk they represented — a paradox that the psychology of collective overconfidence helped partially explain.","t":"回顧起來，促成危機的一系列輕率決定看起來如此明顯可以避免，以至於調查員發現很難對理性行為者如何未能察覺其所代表的首要風險表現出任何同情的理解——集體過度自信的心理學幫助部分解釋了這個悖論。","as":"In retrospect, the decision to dismantle the city's tram network in the mid-twentieth century seems remarkably shortsighted, since planners now struggle to cope with the very traffic congestion that a comprehensive transit network might have obviated.","at":"回顧過去，二十世紀中葉拆除市內電車路網的決定，如今看來實在短視近利，因為都市規劃者現在正疲於應付交通壅塞，而一套完善的大眾運輸網路原本或許可以避免這個問題。"},{"w":"vitriolic","p":"adj.","d":"Filled with bitter criticism.","c":"刻薄的；惡意的","s":"The vitriolic response to the publication was as disproportionate as it was revealing — the invective deployed against a relatively measured argument suggesting that the critic had been provoked less by substantive disagreement than by the pungent challenge the argument posed to a position she had long considered inviolable.","t":"對出版物的刻薄回應與其揭示性一樣不成比例——針對相對有節制論點部署的辱罵，暗示批評者受到刺激的原因與其說是實質性分歧，不如說是論點對她長期認為不可侵犯的立場提出的辛辣挑戰。","as":"The playwright's vitriolic review of his rival's new drama, which castigated the actors as wooden and the dialogue as inane, provoked such consternation in the theater community that the newspaper eventually issued an apology.","at":"這位劇作家對競爭對手的新劇發表了尖酸刻薄的評論，痛斥演員表演呆板、台詞空洞無聊，在戲劇界引起極大的驚愕，最後報社不得不出面道歉。"},{"w":"voluminous","p":"adj.","d":"Occupying or containing much space.","c":"卷帙浩繁的；龐大的","s":"The voluminousedocumentation assembled for the judicial review — spanning forty years of institutional records, thousands of internal communications, and the retrospective accounts of over two hundred former employees — represented an array of evidence whose sheer scale made complete analytical processing within the allocated timeframe practically impossible.","t":"為司法審查匯集的大量文件——涵蓋四十年的機構記錄、數千份內部通信和兩百多名前僱員的回顧性陳述——代表了一批證據，其規模之大使在分配的時間框架內完整的分析處理實際上不可能。","as":"The scholar spent years sifting through the voluminous annals of the imperial court, hoping to unearth cryptic references that might confirm her conjecture that an emperor's death had been concealed for weeks.","at":"這位學者花了數年時間爬梳卷帙浩繁的宮廷史料，希望找到隱晦的記載，以證實她的推測：某位皇帝駕崩的消息曾被隱瞞了好幾個星期。"}]},{"unit":28,"cards":[{"w":"avarice","p":"n.","d":"Extreme greed for wealth.","c":"貪婪","s":"The avarice that had driven the scheme's architects was, the tribunal found, of a particularly egregious variety — not the mundane accumulation of modest advantages but a voluminous extraction of public resources motivated by an insatiable appetite that no amount of accumulated wealth had shown any capacity to diminish.","t":"法庭發現，推動這個計劃設計者的貪婪屬於特別嚴重的類型——不是適度優勢的平凡積累，而是由任何積累財富都未顯示任何能力減少的貪得無厭的食欲驅動的大量公共資源提取。","as":"In Dickens's A Christmas Carol, Ebenezer Scrooge embodies avarice, hoarding his wealth with parsimonious zeal until a series of increasingly sinister ghostly visions compels him to mend his ways and embrace altruistic generosity.","at":"在狄更斯的《小氣財神》中，史古基是貪婪的化身，他以吝嗇的狂熱囤積財富，直到一連串越來越陰森的鬼魂幻象迫使他悔改，轉而擁抱無私的慷慨。"},{"w":"bedlam","p":"n.","d":"A scene of uproar and confusion.","c":"混亂；喧鬧","s":"The announcement precipitated absolute bedlam in the chamber — delegates abandoning their assigned seats, simultaneous eruptions of ardent advocacy and vitriolic counter-argument in multiple languages, and a cacophony of procedural objections that the presiding officer's increasingly terse calls for order proved entirely inadequate to address.","t":"這一宣布在會場引發了絕對的混亂——代表們放棄了他們指定的座位，多種語言同時爆發出熱烈的倡議和刻薄的反駁，以及主持官員日益簡潔的秩序呼籲被證明完全無法解決的程序性反對的嘈雜聲。","as":"When the stock market crashed, the trading floor descended into bedlam, as frantic brokers jostled one another and shouted orders amid a paroxysm of panic selling that the exchange's officials were powerless to stymie.","at":"股市崩盤時，交易大廳陷入一片混亂，驚慌失措的交易員互相推擠、高聲喊單，陷入一陣恐慌性拋售的狂潮，連交易所官員也無力遏止。"},{"w":"cacophony","p":"n.","d":"A harsh mixture of sounds.","c":"刺耳的聲音","s":"The urban cacophony that assaulted the researcher's senses upon arrival — the eruption of construction noise, vehicular traffic, and the voluminous competing audio systems of adjacent retail establishments — made sustained concentration effectively impossible and vindicated her adamant preference for the tranquil research environment she had left behind.","t":"研究員到達時衝擊她感官的城市嘈雜聲——建築噪音、車輛交通和相鄰零售機構爭相競音的大量音頻系統的爆發——使持續集中注意力實際上不可能，並證明了她對她所離開的寧靜研究環境的堅定偏好是正確的。","as":"Residents of the once-tranquil neighborhood complained that a cacophony of jackhammers, car horns, and blaring music harassed them day and night, and they implored the city council to stipulate stricter limits on construction hours.","at":"這個曾經寧靜的社區居民抱怨，手提鑽、汽車喇叭和震耳欲聾的音樂所交織成的刺耳噪音日夜騷擾著他們，因此他們懇求市議會明文規定更嚴格的施工時間限制。"},{"w":"compatible","p":"adj.","d":"Able to exist or work together.","c":"相容的；和諧的","s":"The two systems had been developed in parallel under the aegis of different institutional priorities and proved fundamentally incompatible when integration was eventually attempted — a costly oversight that an ardent proponent of unified standards had been warning about with prophetic accuracy for nearly a decade.","t":"這兩個系統在不同機構優先事項的庇護下並行開發，當最終嘗試整合時被證明根本上不相容——一個統一標準的熱烈支持者以幾乎十年的先知精確性一直在警告的代價高昂的疏忽。","as":"Before an organ transplant, doctors must confirm that the donor's tissue is compatible with the recipient's, because the body's immune system will otherwise repulse the foreign organ, a reaction that, if not palliated with powerful drugs, renders the surgery abortive.","at":"進行器官移植前，醫師必須確認捐贈者的組織與受贈者相容，否則人體的免疫系統會排斥這個外來器官；而這種反應若未能以強效藥物加以緩解，手術便會以失敗告終。"},{"w":"disgruntled","p":"adj.","d":"Angry or dissatisfied.","c":"不滿的","s":"The disgruntled former employees who had filed the complaint were, the investigation found, motivated less by avarice than by a genuine sense of grievance about working conditions — bereft of the institutional support and professional recognition that their voluminous contributions to the organisation's success arguably warranted.","t":"提出投訴的心懷不滿的前僱員，調查發現，其動機與其說是貪婪，不如說是對工作條件的真實不滿感——失去了機構支持和職業認可，這是他們對組織成功的大量貢獻可以說值得獲得的。","as":"Disgruntled by years of frozen wages and arbitrary dismissals, the factory workers staged a strike, and their cause soon won the support of a coterie of journalists who exposed the sordid conditions in the company dormitories.","at":"多年來工資停滯不前、又遭到任意解僱，心懷不滿的工廠工人發動罷工；他們的訴求很快就獲得一群記者的支持，這些記者揭露了公司宿舍骯髒惡劣的環境。"},{"w":"equanimity","p":"n.","d":"Mental calmness in difficult situations.","c":"平靜；鎮定","s":"She faced the invective with a remarkable equanimity that her adversaries found more frustrating than any vitriolic counter-attack could have been — her measured, terse responses and manifest refusal to be provoked into bedlam depriving them of the emotional escalation their strategy required.","t":"她以非凡的平靜面對辱罵，這讓她的對手比任何刻薄的反擊都更感到沮喪——她有節制的、簡短的回應和明顯拒絕被激怒進入混亂的態度，剝奪了他們的策略所需的情感升級。","as":"Even when hostile reporters bombarded her with accusatory questions, the spokeswoman maintained her equanimity, answering each query with a calm, cogent explanation that left her critics unable to elicit the flustered reaction they had hoped for.","at":"即使充滿敵意的記者連番丟出指控性的問題，這位發言人依然保持鎮定，以冷靜而有說服力的說明回答每一個提問，讓批評者無法引出他們所期待的慌亂反應。"},{"w":"eradicate","p":"v.","d":"To destroy completely, put an end to.","c":"根除；消滅","s":"The programme's ambition to eradicate the inveterate corruption that had permeated the procurement system for decades was laudable in its scope but chimerical in its timeline — the ardent reformers underestimating the resilience of networks whose lucrative operation had generated decades of entrenched beneficiaries.","t":"該計劃根除在採購系統中滲透了幾十年根深蒂固腐敗的雄心在範圍上值得讚揚，但在時間表上是空想的——熱烈的改革者低估了那些有利可圖的運作已產生幾十年根深蒂固受益者的網絡的韌性。","as":"Smallpox, once a ubiquitous scourge that killed millions, was eradicated through a global vaccination campaign whose success remains a landmark in public health and a powerful rebuttal to the fatalism that regards such diseases as inexorable.","at":"天花曾是無所不在、奪走數百萬人性命的禍害，最終透過全球疫苗接種運動而被根除；這項成就至今仍是公共衛生史上的里程碑，也有力地駁斥了那種認為這類疾病無法阻擋的宿命論。"},{"w":"exploit","p":"v.","d":"To make use of, utilise fully.","c":"開發；剝削","s":"The most perspicacious entrepreneurs in the sector were those who could exploit the opportunities created by regulatory change before their competitors had even perceived that the landscape had shifted — an acuity of market sensing that the most successful consistently described as the paramount competitive advantage.","t":"該行業最有洞察力的企業家是那些能夠在競爭對手甚至察覺到格局已改變之前利用監管變化創造的機會的人——最成功的人一致描述為首要競爭優勢的市場感知敏銳度。","as":"To exploit the immense geothermal energy beneath their island, Icelandic engineers built power plants that harness volcanic heat, a resourceful strategy proving that renewable energy can be economically viable even in a land prone to eruptions.","at":"為了充分利用島嶼底下蘊藏的豐沛地熱能源，冰島工程師興建了利用火山熱能的發電廠；這項足智多謀的策略證明，即使在火山頻繁爆發的土地上，再生能源也能具備經濟上的可行性。"},{"w":"impede","p":"v.","d":"To delay or prevent by obstructing.","c":"阻礙；妨礙","s":"The voluminous bureaucratic requirements that impeded access to the research funding were not, critics argued, incidental features of the system but its paramount structural characteristic — a labyrinth of compliance designed less to ensure accountability than to constrict the pool of eligible applicants to those with dedicated administrative support.","t":"阻礙獲得研究資金的大量官僚要求，批評者認為，不是系統的附帶特徵，而是其首要結構特徵——一個合規迷宮，其設計與其說是為了確保問責制，不如說是將合格申請者的範圍縮小到那些擁有專門行政支持的人。","as":"Convoluted bureaucratic procedures continue to impede the delivery of humanitarian aid, and relief agencies warn that each delay deepens the plight of refugees who are already emaciated from malnutrition and disease.","at":"繁瑣的官僚程序持續阻礙人道援助的運送，救援機構警告，每一次延誤都會使難民的困境更加惡化，而這些難民早已因營養不良和疾病而骨瘦如柴。"},{"w":"infallible","p":"adj.","d":"Incapable of making mistakes or being wrong.","c":"絕對正確的","s":"No analytical method, however rigorous, was infallible — a fundamental epistemological humility that the most perspicacious researchers consistently practised by building uncertainty quantification into every conclusion and maintaining an ardent commitment to revising their positions when incontrovertible new evidence warranted it.","t":"無論多麼嚴格的分析方法都不是絕對正確的——這是最有洞察力的研究人員通過在每個結論中構建不確定性量化並在無可辯駁的新證據需要時維持熱烈的修正立場承諾，一貫實踐的基本認識論謙遜。","as":"Though many jurors regard eyewitness testimony as infallible, psychologists have shown that memory is highly susceptible to suggestion, so even confident witnesses may inadvertently offer fallacious accounts of events they genuinely believe they saw.","at":"雖然許多陪審員認為目擊者證詞絕對可靠，但心理學家已證明記憶極易受到暗示影響，因此即使是自信滿滿的證人，也可能在不經意間，對自己真心相信親眼目睹的事件作出錯誤的陳述。"},{"w":"insatiable","p":"adj.","d":"Impossible to satisfy.","c":"貪得無厭的","s":"Her insatiable intellectual curiosity — which drove her to imbibe voluminous literature from disciplines seemingly remote from her primary research focus — proved to be her most distinctive scientific asset, the cross-disciplinary perspectives it generated consistently yielding the most innovative approaches to intractable problems.","t":"她貪得無厭的求知欲——驅使她大量吸收看似遠離她主要研究重點的學科文獻——被證明是她最獨特的科學資產，它產生的跨學科視角不斷為棘手問題產生最具創新性的方法。","as":"Consumers' insatiable appetite for cheap clothing has spawned a lucrative global industry, yet critics contend that its factories spew toxic dyes into rivers and perpetuate a system that relies on the drudgery of underpaid workers.","at":"消費者對廉價服飾永無止境的需求，催生出一個利潤豐厚的全球產業；然而批評者認為，這些工廠把有毒染料排入河川，並延續了一套仰賴低薪工人從事苦差事的體制。"},{"w":"irrational","p":"adj.","d":"Not logical or reasonable.","c":"不理智的","s":"The irrational avarice that had driven the scheme was evident from the outset to those who scrutinised the underlying economics — the projected returns were so disconnected from any realistic assessment of the viable market that only wilful self-deception could have sustained the architects' apparent conviction in its feasibility.","t":"推動這個計劃的非理性貪婪對那些仔細審查基礎經濟學的人來說從一開始就很明顯——預計回報與可行市場的任何現實評估如此脫節，只有故意的自我欺騙才能維持設計者對其可行性的表面信念。","as":"Although he readily conceded that his aversion to flying was irrational, since statistics show air travel to be safer than driving, the otherwise intrepid explorer could not repress the dread that engulfed him whenever the aircraft shuddered.","at":"雖然他坦然承認自己對搭飛機的排斥毫無道理，畢竟統計數據顯示搭飛機比開車更安全，但這位平日無所畏懼的探險家，每當飛機晃動時，仍無法壓抑那股將他吞沒的恐懼。"},{"w":"moribund","p":"adj.","d":"At the point of death; lacking vitality.","c":"垂死的","s":"The moribund institution's annual report — voluminous in its retrospective detail but conspicuously bereft of any cogent vision for future development — confirmed what most observers had suspected for several years: that its leadership had effectively ceased to initiate and was merely presiding over a protracted and undignified decline.","t":"這個垂死機構的年度報告——在回顧性細節上大量，但明顯缺乏任何有說服力的未來發展願景——證實了大多數觀察者幾年來所懷疑的：其領導層實際上已停止啟動，只是在主持一場漫長而不體面的衰落。","as":"As coal mining slid into obsolescence, many Appalachian towns became moribund, their populations shrinking and their storefronts vacant, yet some have staged a modest revival by turning abandoned mines into museums that chronicle the vicissitudes and valor of generations of miners.","at":"隨著煤礦業逐漸被淘汰，許多阿帕拉契山區的小鎮變得奄奄一息，人口日益減少、店面空無一人；不過有些小鎮把廢棄礦坑改建成博物館，記錄一代又一代礦工的興衰起伏與英勇事蹟，因而稍稍重獲生機。"},{"w":"nadir","p":"n.","d":"The lowest or most unsuccessful point.","c":"最低點","s":"The financial scandal represented the nadir of the institution's public reputation — a bereft moment from which recovery would require not merely the eradication of the specific practices that had generated the crisis but a fundamental reconstruction of the governance culture that had permitted them to flourish.","t":"金融醜聞代表了該機構公眾聲譽的最低點——一個被剝奪的時刻，從中恢復不僅需要根除產生危機的具體做法，還需要從根本上重建允許它們蓬勃發展的治理文化。","as":"The nadir of the campaign came during the brutal winter, when the besieged garrison, bereft of food and fuel and pounded by constant shelling, saw its morale collapse so completely that mutiny seemed inevitable.","at":"這場戰役的最低谷出現在嚴酷的冬季：遭到圍困的守軍既缺糧又缺燃料，還承受著持續不斷的砲轟，士氣徹底崩潰，叛變似乎已無可避免。"},{"w":"panacea","p":"n.","d":"A solution to all problems.","c":"萬靈藥","s":"Technology was not the panacea its most ardent advocates claimed — a cogent reality that became increasingly prevalent as organisations discovered that digitalisation could impede as readily as facilitate the human judgements and institutional processes on which genuine effectiveness depended.","t":"技術不是其最熱烈倡導者所聲稱的萬靈藥——這一有說服力的現實隨著組織發現數字化可以像促進一樣容易地阻礙真正效力所依賴的人類判斷和制度流程而變得越來越普遍。","as":"Although some reformers tout standardized testing as a panacea for educational inequality, skeptics argue that such a simplistic remedy ignores the myriad factors that hamper learning and treats a single score as a reliable barometer of a child's intrinsic abilities.","at":"雖然有些改革者把標準化測驗吹捧成解決教育不平等的萬靈丹，但懷疑者認為，這種過於簡化的對策忽略了阻礙學習的種種因素，還把單一分數當作衡量孩子內在能力的可靠指標。"},{"w":"propinquity","p":"n.","d":"Nearness in place, time, or relationship.","c":"接近；鄰近","s":"The propinquity of the two research centres — separated by merely a corridor yet operating in near-total institutional isolation — exemplified the irrational fragmentation that impeded collaborative innovation across the organisation, a deplorable waste of the synergistic potential that physical adjacency might otherwise have catalysed.","t":"這兩個研究中心的鄰近——僅隔一條走廊卻在幾乎完全的制度隔離中運作——例示了阻礙整個組織協作創新的非理性碎片化，這是物理鄰近性本可以催化的協同潛力的可悲浪費。","as":"Social psychologists have found that propinquity is a surprisingly powerful predictor of friendship, since students assigned to neighboring dormitory rooms often become close confidants, whether they are gregarious or timorous, even in a highly heterogeneous student body.","at":"社會心理學家發現，空間上的鄰近是預測友誼的一個出乎意料的有力指標：即使在背景極為多元的學生群體中，被分配到相鄰宿舍房間的學生，無論個性外向或膽怯，往往都會成為親密的知己。"},{"w":"revere","p":"v.","d":"To feel deep respect or admiration for.","c":"尊崇；敬畏","s":"The community continued to revere the founder's memory long after the institution she had established had drifted from the principles she had considered paramount — a paradox that the more perspicacious members recognised as indicating the depth of affection for the person rather than consistent endorsement of the organisation's current direction.","t":"社區繼續尊崇創始人的記憶，即使在她建立的機構已偏離她認為首要的原則之後很久——更有洞察力的成員認識到這個悖論表明對這個人的深厚感情，而不是對組織當前方向的一致認可。","as":"Across East Asia, Confucius is still revered as a sage whose teachings on filial piety and moral conduct shape everything from family customs to educational traditions, an influence his original disciples could scarcely have imagined.","at":"在整個東亞地區，孔子至今仍被尊崇為聖賢，他關於孝道與道德操守的教誨，影響著從家庭習俗到教育傳統的方方面面，其影響之深遠，恐怕是他最初的弟子們難以想像的。"},{"w":"sedate","p":"adj.","d":"Calm, dignified, unhurried.","c":"安詳的；莊重的","s":"The sedate pace of the village's daily life stood in acute contrast to the bedlam of the capital from which the researcher had recently escaped — the propinquity of genuine tranquillity to her field site proving an unexpected benefit that facilitated the equanimity her extended analytical work required.","t":"村莊日常生活的安詳步伐與研究員最近逃離的首都喧鬧形成了鮮明對比——真實寧靜與她的實地調查點的鄰近被證明是一個意想不到的好處，這有助於她延長的分析工作所需的平靜。","as":"Unlike his flamboyant predecessor, who gesticulated wildly and relished histrionics, the new conductor projected a sedate dignity on the podium, guiding the orchestra with restrained gestures that some critics initially found lackluster.","at":"不同於前任那位作風浮誇、總是誇張比手畫腳又熱衷於做戲的指揮，新任指揮在指揮台上展現出沉穩莊重的氣度，以內斂的手勢引導樂團，有些評論家起初還覺得這種風格平淡無奇。"},{"w":"serenity","p":"n.","d":"The state of being calm and peaceful.","c":"寧靜；平靜","s":"The serenity with which she approached even the most turbulent professional crises was not the product of indifference but of an ardent commitment to the equanimity she had cultivated over decades — a disciplined inner composure that those who revered her most recognised as her paramount professional quality.","t":"她以平靜面對即使是最動盪的職業危機，不是冷漠的產物，而是她幾十年來培養的對平靜的熱烈承諾——那些最尊崇她的人認識到的、她首要的職業品質的紀律性內在沉著。","as":"Weary of the relentless pace of city life, many professionals seek serenity in secluded mountain sanctuaries, where an ascetic routine of silent meditation and simple meals offers a welcome respite from the incessant buzz of their phones.","at":"厭倦了城市生活的緊湊步調，許多上班族前往幽靜的山中靜修處尋求心靈的平靜；在那裡，靜默冥想與粗茶淡飯的簡樸作息，讓他們得以暫時擺脫手機不停響起的通知聲。"},{"w":"vulnerable","p":"adj.","d":"Susceptible to attack or harm.","c":"易受傷的；脆弱的","s":"The most vulnerable point in any negotiation was, the seasoned mediator observed, precisely the moment of greatest apparent progress — when parties relaxed the vigilance that had previously protected them and became susceptible to the avarice or short-sightedness that had historically sabotaged so many agreements at the final stage.","t":"最有經驗的調解員觀察到，任何談判中最脆弱的時刻，恰恰是表面上進展最大的時刻——當各方放鬆了以前保護他們的警覺性，並容易受到貪婪或短視的影響，這些在歷史上在最後階段破壞了如此多協議。","as":"Coral reefs are especially vulnerable to rising ocean temperatures, and marine biologists warn that repeated bleaching could obliterate these fragile ecosystems, which shelter a plethora of species, to the lasting detriment of coastal fishing communities.","at":"珊瑚礁對海水溫度上升格外脆弱，海洋生物學家警告，反覆發生的白化現象可能徹底摧毀這些庇護著大量物種的脆弱生態系，對沿海漁業社群造成長遠的損害。"}]},{"unit":29,"cards":[{"w":"adherent","p":"n.","d":"A person who supports a cause.","c":"擁護者；信徒","s":"The movement's most ardent adherent s had remained loyal through years of nadir and adversity — a serenity in the face of setback that the most disgruntled critics could not credibly attribute to irrationality, since the depth of commitment clearly rested on cogent philosophical foundations rather than mere avarice or self-interest.","t":"這個運動最熱烈的擁護者在多年的最低點和逆境中保持了忠誠——面對挫折的平靜，最心懷不滿的批評者無法可信地歸因於非理性，因為承諾的深度顯然建立在有說服力的哲學基礎上，而不僅僅是貪婪或自我利益。","as":"As an ardent adherent of Stoic philosophy, the Roman emperor Marcus Aurelius cultivated equanimity amid war and plague, recording his reflections in a private journal that is still revered by readers seeking guidance on how to live.","at":"羅馬皇帝馬可．奧理略是斯多噶哲學的熱忱信徒，他在戰爭與瘟疫中始終保持泰然自若，並把自己的省思寫在一本私人日記裡；這本書至今仍受到尋求人生指引的讀者推崇。"},{"w":"adversary","p":"n.","d":"A person's opponent in a contest.","c":"對手；敵手","s":"The most effective adversary is not one who merely opposes but one who forces genuine intellectual engagement — a vitriolic critic whose pungent objections are sufficiently cogent to compel the refinement of arguments that might otherwise remain unexamined, serving paradoxically as an agent of intellectual improvement.","t":"最有效的對手不是僅僅反對的人，而是迫使真正智識接觸的人——一位刻薄批評者，其辛辣的反對意見足夠有說服力，迫使論點的精煉，這些論點否則可能保持未被審查，弔詭地作為智識進步的推動者。","as":"Cognizant that her adversary excelled at deception, the veteran chess champion spent weeks analyzing his previous games, enabling her to anticipate the subtle feint that had thwarted so many of his earlier opponents.","at":"這位資深西洋棋冠軍深知她的對手擅長虛張聲勢，於是花了數週時間分析他過去的棋局，因而能預料到那記曾讓許多早先對手吃盡苦頭的巧妙佯攻。"},{"w":"apathy","p":"n.","d":"Lack of interest or enthusiasm.","c":"冷漠；無興趣","s":"The apathy that had come to characterise public engagement with the political process was not, the political scientist argued, an inherent feature of democratic societies but the predictable consequence of years of mendacious political communication — a rational disengagement from institutions that had demonstrably failed to evince the candour that trust required.","t":"政治學家認為，公眾對政治進程的參與中出現的冷漠，不是民主社會的固有特徵，而是多年虛假政治傳播的可預測後果——從顯然未能顯示信任所需坦率的機構中理性地脫離。","as":"Political scientists attribute the low voter turnout to prevalent apathy among young citizens, many of whom have grown so disillusioned with mendacious politicians and hollow campaign promises that they regard voting as a fruitless exercise.","at":"政治學者將投票率低落歸因於年輕公民之間普遍存在的冷漠，他們當中許多人對滿口謊言的政客和空洞的競選承諾感到幻滅，以至於認為投票是徒勞無功的事。"},{"w":"atypical","p":"adj.","d":"Not representative of a type.","c":"非典型的","s":"The case was atypical in so many respects that the precedents typically cited by adherents of the conventional approach were essentially inapplicable — a recondite set of circumstances that required not the inveterate application of established doctrine but a genuinely creative legal analysis.","t":"這個案例在如此多方面都是非典型的，以至於傳統方法支持者通常引用的先例基本上不適用——一套深奧的情況，需要的不是對既定學說的根深蒂固的應用，而是真正有創意的法律分析。","as":"Because the patient's symptoms were atypical of the disease, several cursory examinations failed to identify it, and only a perspicacious specialist recognized that her lethargic manner and aching joints signaled a rare autoimmune disorder.","at":"由於這名病患的症狀與該疾病的典型表現不同，幾次草率的檢查都沒能診斷出來，直到一位眼光敏銳的專科醫師才看出，她無精打采的模樣和關節疼痛，其實是一種罕見自體免疫疾病的徵兆。"},{"w":"banal","p":"adj.","d":"Lacking originality, obvious and dull.","c":"平庸的；陳腐的","s":"The critique was not wrong in its substance but so banal in its formulation that it failed to make any impression on an audience that had heard identical objections articulated with greater force and originality on numerous previous occasions — a pedagogical failure that the most perspicacious students immediately recognised.","t":"這個批評在實質上並沒有錯，但在表述上如此平庸，以至於它未能給在許多以前場合以更大力量和獨創性聽到相同反對意見的聽眾留下任何印象——最有洞察力的學生立即認識到的教學失敗。","as":"Critics complained that the blockbuster's dazzling special effects could not disguise its banal dialogue and superficial characters, which seemed to have been concocted by a marketing committee rather than by an artist with a singular vision.","at":"評論家抱怨，這部賣座大片炫目的特效掩飾不了平庸的對白和膚淺的角色，這些看起來像是行銷委員會拼湊出來的，而非出自一位眼光獨到的藝術家之手。"},{"w":"bliss","p":"n.","d":"Perfect happiness, great joy.","c":"極樂；狂喜","s":"The bliss of the discovery's first moment — that pure exultation of incontrovertible confirmation after years of ardent pursuit — was, she later reflected, entirely incompatible with equanimity, the serenity she normally prized dissolving instantly into an ecstatic cacophony of relief, vindication, and wonder.","t":"發現第一刻的極樂——在多年熱烈追求後無可辯駁確認的純粹狂喜——她後來反思，完全與平靜不相容，她通常珍視的寧靜瞬間溶解進一種充滿解脫、平反和驚奇的狂喜嘈雜聲中。","as":"After hours of ascending a rugged trail under the scorching sun, the weary hikers found pure bliss in plunging into the cool alpine lake, their exultation at reaching the summit giving way to a deep serenity.","at":"在烈日下沿著崎嶇的山路攀登了好幾個小時後，疲憊的登山客跳進清涼的高山湖泊，感受到純粹的極樂；登頂時的狂喜，也隨之化為深沉的寧靜。"},{"w":"burly","p":"adj.","d":"Large and strong, heavily built.","c":"魁梧的","s":"The burly security officer's imposing physique proved far less relevant to his effectiveness than his remarkable equanimity in difficult situations — his sedate demeanour under the most acute provocation consistently defusing bedlam that his more reactive colleagues would have inadvertently escalated.","t":"這位魁梧的安保官員令人生畏的體格對其有效性的相關性，遠不如他在困難情況下非凡的平靜——他在最強烈挑釁下安詳的舉止，不斷化解了他更容易反應的同事可能無意中升級的混亂。","as":"Despite his burly frame and intimidating scowl, the nightclub's bouncer was known among regulars for his gentle temperament, preferring to calm pugnacious patrons with a well-timed quip rather than with his fists.","at":"儘管這位夜店保鑣身材魁梧、表情兇狠嚇人，常客們卻都知道他性情溫和；比起動用拳頭，他更喜歡用一句恰到好處的俏皮話，讓好鬥的客人冷靜下來。"},{"w":"dilettante","p":"n.","d":"A person with a superficial interest.","c":"業餘愛好者；半吊子","s":"The dilettante 's superficial engagement with the subject — evident in the banal observations he offered and the inveterate avoidance of any recondite detail that might reveal the limits of his preparation — stood in acute contrast to the genuine mastery that the programme's most assiduous participants had clearly cultivated.","t":"業餘愛好者對這個主題的膚淺參與——從他提供的平庸觀察和對任何可能揭示其準備限制的深奧細節的根深蒂固的迴避中顯而易見——與節目中最勤勉參與者顯然培養的真正掌握形成了鮮明對比。","as":"Although rival scholars scoffed at him as a dilettante who dabbled in a gamut of disciplines, the self-taught naturalist filled voluminous notebooks with observations of insect behavior that later proved invaluable to entomologists.","at":"雖然對立的學者們嘲笑他是個涉獵各種學科卻樣樣淺嘗即止的半吊子，這位自學出身的博物學家卻在大量筆記本中寫滿了昆蟲行為的觀察紀錄，後來對昆蟲學家而言極具價值。"},{"w":"exhort","p":"v.","d":"To strongly encourage or urge.","c":"敦促；告誡","s":"The celebrated mentor would exhort her students to embrace the most intimidating intellectual challenges rather than retreating to the familiar — not through vitriolic criticism of caution but through the ardent and congenial modelling of intellectual courage that had characterised her own distinguished career.","t":"這位著名導師會敦促她的學生擁抱最令人生畏的智識挑戰，而不是退回到熟悉的環境——不是通過對謹慎的刻薄批評，而是通過她自己傑出職業生涯所特有的智識勇氣的熱烈且令人愉快的示範。","as":"During the darkest months of the war, Winston Churchill exhorted the British people to persevere despite relentless bombing, and his defiant oratory helped transform a vulnerable island into a resolute bulwark against Nazi aggression.","at":"在戰爭最黑暗的那幾個月裡，邱吉爾敦促英國人民在無情的轟炸下堅持下去，他那不屈不撓的演說，幫助這座脆弱的島國成為抵禦納粹侵略的堅定堡壘。"},{"w":"forlorn","p":"adj.","d":"Pitifully sad and abandoned.","c":"孤苦伶仃的；絕望的","s":"The forlorn figure of the exhorted but ultimately ignored whistleblower — bereft of institutional protection, abandoned by erstwhile colleagues, and facing the acute detriment of professional isolation — represented precisely the kind of vulnerability that robust legal safeguards were specifically designed to prevent.","t":"被敦促但最終被忽視的舉報人那孤苦伶仃的身影——缺乏機構保護、被昔日同事拋棄，並面臨職業孤立的嚴重損害——恰恰代表了強有力的法律保障專門設計以防止的那種脆弱性。","as":"Standing alone on the deserted platform long after the last train had departed, the forlorn traveler wore a doleful expression as he reread a crumpled letter whose terse message had dashed his hopes of an amicable reconciliation.","at":"末班車早已駛離，那位孤苦無依的旅人獨自站在空蕩蕩的月台上，神情哀戚地重讀一封皺巴巴的信；信中簡短的幾句話，粉碎了他期盼和平和解的希望。"},{"w":"fracas","p":"n.","d":"A noisy disturbance or quarrel.","c":"喧鬧的打鬥","s":"The fracas that erupted outside the committee room — two fracas groups of adherents from opposed factions engaged in progressively more vitriolic exchanges — was swiftly fracased by security personnel before it could escalate into the kind of bedlam that the media presence would have amplified into a reputational catastrophe.","t":"在委員會室外爆發的喧鬧打鬥——兩組來自對立派系的擁護者進行越來越刻薄的交流——在它升級成媒體存在會將其放大為聲譽災難的那種混亂之前，被安保人員迅速平息。","as":"A fracas broke out in the legislature when opposition lawmakers, brandishing placards and inveighing against the bill as an egregious abuse of power, stormed the podium and grappled with security guards in front of astonished television crews.","at":"反對黨議員高舉標語牌，痛斥這項法案是極其惡劣的濫權行為，並衝上主席台與警衛扭打成一團，議會因此爆發一場混戰，現場的電視台工作人員看得目瞪口呆。"},{"w":"garrulous","p":"adj.","d":"Excessively talkative about trivial matters.","c":"喋喋不休的","s":"The contrast between the garrulous sociability she displayed at public events and the taciturn focus of her private working hours reflected not duplicity but a genuine compartmentalisation — the ardent engagement with ideas that her voluminous published output attested requiring an equivalent degree of protected solitude.","t":"她在公共活動中展示的喋喋不休的社交性與私人工作時間的沉默專注之間的對比，反映的不是表裡不一，而是真正的隔間化——她大量出版作品所證明的對思想的熱烈參與，需要同等程度的受保護的孤獨。","as":"Seated beside a garrulous passenger on a long overnight flight, the novelist, eager for repose, endured a monologue that lurched desultorily from his pets to his golf scores, and even her most laconic replies did nothing to stem the torrent of words.","at":"在一趟漫長的夜間航班上，渴望休息的小說家坐在一名喋喋不休的乘客旁，只能忍受他東拉西扯、從寵物聊到高爾夫成績的長篇大論；就連她最簡短的回應，也絲毫擋不住對方滔滔不絕的話語。"},{"w":"gusto","p":"n.","d":"Enthusiasm and energy in doing something.","c":"熱情；津津有味","s":"She approached even the most labyrinthine administrative challenges with a gusto that her more lethargic colleagues found both enviable and faintly exasperating — the same ardent energy she brought to intellectual work apparently extending, apparently inexhaustibly, into every dimension of her professional activity.","t":"她以一種讓她更懶散的同事既羨慕又略感惱火的熱情，甚至處理最複雜的行政挑戰——她帶給智識工作的同樣熱烈能量，顯然無窮無盡地延伸到她職業活動的每個維度。","as":"Although he was an octogenarian, the retired professor still tackled new subjects with remarkable gusto, rejecting a sedentary retirement in favor of language courses and lively debates and proving that longevity need not dull one's intellect.","at":"這位退休教授雖已八十多歲，卻仍以驚人的熱情投入新學科，他拒絕過著久坐不動的退休生活，轉而參加語言課程與熱烈的辯論，證明了長壽並不一定會使人的智力變得遲鈍。"},{"w":"indolent","p":"adj.","d":"Wanting to avoid activity or effort.","c":"懶惰的","s":"The indolent management style that had prevailed during the organisation's most comfortable years had produced a workforce so accustomed to minimal challenge that the demands of genuine crisis management proved acutely disorienting — the sudden imperative for ardent effort exposing the atrophy that decades of comfortable stagnation had generated.","t":"在組織最舒適年份盛行的懶惰管理風格，產生了一支如此習慣於最低限度挑戰的員工隊伍，以至於真正的危機管理要求被證明令人迷失方向——對熱烈努力的突然迫切需求暴露了數十年舒適停滯所產生的萎縮。","as":"The indolent scion of a shipping dynasty spent his days lounging on yachts rather than learning the trade, and, much to his family's chagrin, the company he neglected eventually slid into liquidation.","at":"這位航運世家的懶散繼承人整天在遊艇上閒晃，不肯學習經營之道；令家族懊惱不已的是，被他荒廢的公司最終走上了清算一途。"},{"w":"inebriated","p":"adj.","d":"Drunk, intoxicated.","c":"醉酒的","s":"The banal explanation that the incident had been precipitated by an inebriated participant failed to satisfy investigators who had corroborated through multiple independent sources that the sequence of events reflected a pattern of inveterate institutional dysfunction rather than the aberrant behaviour of a single individual on a single occasion.","t":"事件是由一個醉酒的參與者引發的平庸解釋，未能讓通過多個獨立來源證實了事件序列反映了根深蒂固的制度功能失調模式而非單個人在單一場合異常行為的調查員滿意。","as":"The inebriated driver who caused the collision tried to cajole the officers into releasing him with a feeble pretext about a medical condition, but the breathalyzer results rendered his excuse absurd.","at":"那名造成車禍的醉酒駕駛，試圖以身體不適這種站不住腳的藉口哄騙警察放他走，但酒測結果讓他的說詞顯得荒謬可笑。"},{"w":"lithe","p":"adj.","d":"Thin, supple, and graceful.","c":"柔軟的；輕盈的","s":"The lithe precision with which she navigated the most complex procedural terrain — moving through institutional constraints with a fluency that suggested deep familiarity with both the explicit rules and the recondite informal conventions that governed them — marked her as an adroit operator of exceptional calibre.","t":"她處理最複雜程序地形的輕盈精確性——以流暢性穿越制度限制，暗示對明確規則和管理它們的深奧非正式慣例的深度熟悉——使她成為一位卓越的熟練操作者。","as":"Lithe and remarkably elusive, the snow leopard moves silently across the rugged cliffs of its Central Asian habitat, an ability that has long frustrated scientists who aspire to document its behavior in the wild.","at":"雪豹身形輕盈柔軟，而且極為難以捉摸，牠能在中亞棲息地崎嶇的懸崖間悄無聲息地移動；長久以來，這種本領讓渴望記錄牠野外行為的科學家們屢屢受挫。"},{"w":"nondescript","p":"adj.","d":"Lacking distinctive or interesting features.","c":"難以形容的；普通的","s":"The nondescript exterior of the building gave no indication of the extraordinary intellectual activity it contained — a deliberate architectural choice that the institute's founders had considered paramount in an era when the organisation's most inveterate adversaries were actively seeking to identify and impede its operations.","t":"建築的普通外觀沒有給出它所包含的非凡智識活動的任何指示——這是研究所創始人在組織最根深蒂固的對手積極尋求識別和阻礙其運作的時代認為首要的故意建築選擇。","as":"Behind the nondescript facade of a suburban warehouse, investigators discovered a covert factory that had been churning out counterfeit medicines and selling them to gullible customers, jeopardizing the health of thousands.","at":"在郊區一座毫不起眼的倉庫外觀背後，調查人員發現了一間祕密工廠，它不斷大量製造假藥並賣給輕信的顧客，危害了數千人的健康。"},{"w":"pique","p":"n.","d":"A feeling of irritation at being slighted.","c":"生氣；怨恨","s":"The pique she felt at being excluded from the key deliberation was understandable — she was, by any cogent assessment, the most qualified person in the organisation to contribute to the discussion, and the slight was sufficiently overt to constitute a blatant disregard for both her expertise and her institutional standing.","t":"她對被排除在關鍵審議之外的怨恨是可以理解的——按任何有說服力的評估，她是組織中最有資格為討論做出貢獻的人，這種輕視足夠公開，構成對她的專業知識和機構地位的公然漠視。","as":"In a fit of pique after the board repudiated his proposal, the senior engineer abruptly resigned, a rash decision he came to rue when his successor quietly implemented nearly identical ideas a year later.","at":"董事會否決了他的提案後，這位資深工程師一氣之下憤而辭職；然而一年後，他的繼任者悄悄推行了幾乎一模一樣的構想，讓他對當初那個衝動的決定懊悔不已。"},{"w":"platitude","p":"n.","d":"A remark that is overused and unoriginal.","c":"陳腔濫調","s":"The response was so replete with platitude s that even the most indolent observer could perceive the absence of any genuine analytical engagement — the verbal equivalent of the nondescript facade that some institutions deploy to obscure the inertia that has replaced the ardent purposefulness of their founding years.","t":"回應充斥著如此多的陳腔濫調，以至於即使是最懶惰的觀察者也能察覺到任何真正分析參與的缺失——一些機構用來掩蓋已取代其創立年代熱烈目標性的惰性的普通外觀的語言等價物。","as":"Instead of proposing tangible solutions to the housing crisis, the candidate offered only platitudes about hope and unity, a speech that critics dismissed as nebulous language designed to delude voters into believing that change was at hand.","at":"這位候選人沒有針對住房危機提出具體的解決方案，只說了一些關於希望與團結的陳腔濫調；評論者認為，這場演講不過是含糊空泛的言辭，目的在於讓選民誤以為改變即將到來。"},{"w":"wane","p":"n.","d":"A gradual decrease.","c":"衰退；減弱","s":"The wane of public confidence in the institution had proceeded with the same inexorable momentum as its rise — a gradual erosion over years of banal communication, platitudinous leadership responses to genuine crises, and the indolent failure to initiate the reforms that more perspicacious observers had been exhorting for the better part of a decade.","t":"機構公眾信心的衰退以與其上升相同的不可阻擋的勢頭進行——多年平庸的溝通、對真正危機的陳腔濫調領導層回應，以及未能啟動更有洞察力的觀察者在近十年中一直在敦促的改革的懶惰失敗所帶來的逐漸侵蝕。","as":"By the late nineteenth century, the power of the Ottoman Empire was clearly on the wane, as Balkan nationalist movements exploited its fiscal weakness and a court rife with intrigue proved unable to neutralize growing demands for independence.","at":"到了十九世紀末，鄂圖曼帝國的國力明顯日漸衰退，巴爾幹半島的民族主義運動趁其財政疲弱之際乘勢而起，而陰謀叢生的朝廷則無力化解日益高漲的獨立訴求。"}]},{"unit":30,"cards":[{"w":"candor","p":"n.","d":"The quality of being open and honest.","c":"坦率；真誠","s":"The candor with which she addressed the most uncomfortable questions distinguished her press conference from the platitude-laden performances that had characterised her predecessors — each response delivered with a terse directness that the assembled journalists found both refreshing and slightly disorienting after years of accustomed evasion.","t":"她以坦率回答最令人不舒服問題的方式，使她的新聞發布會有別於前任充斥陳腔濫調表演——每個回應以一種簡潔的直接性傳達，在多年習慣的迴避之後，聚集的記者發現既令人耳目一新又略感迷失方向。","as":"The retired general's memoir surprised readers with its candor, for instead of glorifying his victories, he acknowledged, in retrospect, the tactical blunders that had cost many lives, displaying a humility seldom found in military autobiographies.","at":"這位退役將軍的回憶錄以坦率令讀者驚訝，他沒有美化自己的勝利，反而在回顧時坦承那些造成許多人喪命的戰術失誤，展現出軍事自傳中罕見的謙遜。"},{"w":"charlatan","p":"n.","d":"A person who falsely claims to have skill.","c":"江湖郎中；騙子","s":"The celebrated physician was eventually exposed as a charlatan whose mendacious credentials had been assembled with remarkable ingenuity — a bona fide medical degree from a non-existent institution, fabricated research publications that cited each other in an intricate web of mutual corroboration, and patient testimonials of dubious provenance.","t":"這位著名醫生最終被揭露為一個騙子，其虛假資歷以非凡的聰明才智組裝而成——一個不存在機構的真實醫學學位、相互引用形成複雜相互佐證網絡的捏造研究出版物，以及來源可疑的病人證言。","as":"In the nineteenth century, itinerant charlatans hawked bottles of flavored alcohol as a panacea for every ailment, duping desperate customers who could not afford genuine medical care and had little reason to doubt such confident claims.","at":"十九世紀時，四處遊走的江湖郎中把一瓶瓶調味過的酒當成包治百病的萬靈丹兜售，矇騙那些負擔不起正規醫療、也沒有理由懷疑這些自信說詞的絕望顧客。"},{"w":"condescend","p":"v.","d":"To act as if one is superior.","c":"屈尊；俯就","s":"The tendency to condescend to younger colleagues — to offer their contributions a superficial acknowledgement before redirecting the conversation toward one's own more established perspective — was, the senior professor recognised belatedly, one of the most pernicious habits she had acquired during decades of unquestioned institutional authority.","t":"對年輕同事屈尊俯就的傾向——給予他們的貢獻表面上的承認，然後將對話重新引導到自己更確立的觀點——資深教授事後認識到，這是她在幾十年不受質疑的制度權威期間養成的最有害習慣之一。","as":"The consultant from the capital condescended to the village farmers, lecturing them on irrigation with thinly veiled disdain, an attitude that nettled the elders, whose ancestral techniques had nurtured the terraced fields for centuries.","at":"這位從首都來的顧問以居高臨下的姿態對待村裡的農民，帶著幾乎不加掩飾的輕蔑向他們講授灌溉知識；這種態度激怒了村中長老，因為正是他們祖傳的技術，數百年來一直滋養著這片梯田。"},{"w":"decorum","p":"n.","d":"Behaviour in keeping with good taste.","c":"端莊；得體","s":"The decorum with which the senior official conducted himself throughout the tussle — maintaining an urbane composure while his adversaries resorted to invective and his allies to garrulous over-explanation — was subsequently cited as exemplary evidence that equanimity under pressure was a learnable professional skill.","t":"這位高級官員在爭執中始終以端莊的方式行事——保持溫文爾雅的鎮定，而他的對手訴諸辱罵，他的盟友則喋喋不休地過度解釋——隨後被引用為壓力下平靜是一種可習得的職業技能的典範證據。","as":"Although parliamentary rules demand strict decorum, the budget debate degenerated into a fracas as lawmakers hurled invective across the chamber, and the exasperated speaker was forced to admonish several members before order was restored.","at":"雖然議會規則要求議員嚴守禮節，這場預算辯論卻淪為一場混戰，議員們在議場內互相叫罵，忍無可忍的議長不得不告誡數名議員，秩序才得以恢復。"},{"w":"encumbrance","p":"n.","d":"A burden or impediment.","c":"累贅；妨礙","s":"The voluminous compliance requirements had become such a substantial encumbrance on the organisation's operational capacity that its leadership was spending more time managing regulatory obligations than initiating the creative work that constituted its core purpose — a deplorable inversion of institutional priorities.","t":"大量的合規要求已成為對組織運營能力的如此實質性的累贅，以至於其領導層花費更多時間管理監管義務而非啟動構成其核心目的的創造性工作——一種可悲的制度優先事項倒置。","as":"For many young graduates, student debt has become a heavy encumbrance that fetters their career choices, compelling them to abandon aspirations of public service in favor of lucrative corporate jobs.","at":"對許多年輕畢業生而言，學貸已成為沉重的負擔，束縛了他們的職涯選擇，迫使他們放棄從事公共服務的抱負，轉而投身待遇優渥的企業工作。"},{"w":"extinct","p":"adj.","d":"No longer in existence.","c":"滅絕的","s":"The social convention had not so much become extinct as been displaced by a new etiquette that its advocates considered more appropriate to contemporary conditions — a metamorphosis whose cultural significance the most perspicacious anthropologists found as worthy of serious study as the traditions it had supplanted.","t":"這種社會習俗與其說是消失了，不如說是被其倡導者認為更適合當代條件的新禮儀所取代——一種蛻變，最有洞察力的人類學家認為其文化意義與它所取代的傳統一樣值得認真研究。","as":"Although the dodo has been extinct for centuries, it endures as a poignant symbol of human folly, since the flightless bird, having evolved without predators, was utterly vulnerable to the human interlopers and invasive animals that arrived on Mauritius.","at":"雖然渡渡鳥早在數百年前就已滅絕，牠至今仍是人類愚行的一個令人心酸的象徵：這種不會飛的鳥類在沒有天敵的環境下演化，因此面對抵達模里西斯的人類入侵者及外來動物時，完全不堪一擊。"},{"w":"fledgling","p":"n.","d":"A person or organisation that is new and inexperienced.","c":"無經驗的人；幼鳥","s":"The fledgling organisation had demonstrated an array of qualities — candor in its public communications, gusto in its operational energy, and a sagacious clarity of institutional purpose — that made its rapid rise less surprising than it appeared to the established incumbents who had assumed its inexperience would condemn it to irrelevance.","t":"這個新興組織展示了一系列品質——在其公開溝通中的坦率、在其運營能量中的熱情，以及睿智的機構目標清晰性——這使其迅速崛起比認為其缺乏經驗將使其無關緊要的老牌現任者看起來的更不令人驚訝。","as":"As a fledgling in the cutthroat world of investment banking, she was initially daunted by her brash colleagues, but she soon proved adroit at navigating the labyrinth of financial regulations that bewildered even veteran traders.","at":"身為競爭激烈的投資銀行界新手，她起初被那些自以為是的同事嚇住了，但她很快就證明自己能熟練地穿梭於錯綜複雜的金融法規之中，而那些法規連資深交易員都會感到困惑。"},{"w":"galvanize","p":"v.","d":"To shock or excite into taking action.","c":"激勵；刺激","s":"The unprecedented catastrophe galvanized a political class that had been moribund on the issue for years — the acute visibility of the crisis making continued indolence politically untenable and generating the ardent cross-party cooperation that more gradual developments had consistently failed to initiate.","t":"這場前所未有的災難激勵了在這個問題上多年垂死的政治階層——危機的急性可見性使繼續懶惰在政治上站不住腳，並產生了更漸進的發展一直未能啟動的熱烈跨黨合作。","as":"Rachel Carson's Silent Spring galvanized a generation of activists by revealing how the indiscriminate use of pesticides was killing birds, and despite vitriolic attacks from chemical companies, the book helped initiate stricter federal regulation.","at":"瑞秋．卡森的《寂靜的春天》揭露了濫用殺蟲劑如何導致鳥類大量死亡，激勵了一整代的社會運動人士；儘管遭到化學公司惡毒的抨擊，這本書仍促成了更嚴格的聯邦法規。"},{"w":"gaudy","p":"adj.","d":"Extravagantly bright or showy.","c":"俗麗的","s":"The gaudy opulence of the reception — the flamboyant floral arrangements, the ostentatious tableware, and the conspicuously lucrative wine list — struck several guests as profoundly incongruous with the charitable purpose the event was ostensibly serving, the dissonance between stated and revealed values generating considerable private discomfort.","t":"招待會俗麗的豪華——浮誇的花卉裝飾、炫耀的餐具和顯眼的高端酒單——在幾位客人看來與活動表面上服務的慈善目的極度不協調，陳述的和顯示的價值觀之間的不和諧產生了相當大的私人不舒適感。","as":"The tycoon's mansion, crammed with gaudy gold-plated fixtures and neon chandeliers, was meant to evince refined taste, but contemptuous visitors regarded it as a garish monument to his insatiable vanity.","at":"這位大亨的豪宅裡塞滿了俗麗的鍍金裝潢和霓虹吊燈，本意是要彰顯高雅的品味，但心存輕蔑的訪客卻把它視為他永不滿足的虛榮心所打造出的一座怪誕紀念碑。"},{"w":"idyllic","p":"adj.","d":"Like an idyll, peaceful and happy.","c":"田園詩般的","s":"The idyllic setting of the research station — a converted farmhouse in a landscape of remarkable natural serenity — had been selected not for aesthetic reasons but for the practical conviction that the tranquillity of the environment would enhance the quality of sustained analytical work.","t":"研究站田園詩般的環境——在一片非凡自然寧靜景觀中的一座改建農舍——被選擇不是出於審美原因，而是出於對環境寧靜將提升持續分析工作質量的實際信念。","as":"Lured by brochures showing an idyllic island paradise, many tourists are dismayed to find beaches inundated with plastic and a ceaseless cacophony of jet skis, while older islanders recall with nostalgia the quiet shores of their childhood.","at":"許多遊客被宣傳手冊上田園詩般的海島天堂所吸引，抵達後卻失望地發現海灘上滿是塑膠垃圾、水上摩托車的噪音不絕於耳；而年長的島民則懷念起童年時那片寧靜的海岸。"},{"w":"jocose","p":"adj.","d":"Fond of or characterised by joking.","c":"詼諧的；開玩笑的","s":"His jocose manner concealed a perspicacious analytical intelligence that adversaries frequently underestimated — the gusto with which he deployed wit in social settings leading them to mistake the affable surface for the totality of the person, a recurrent error that proved costly in every direct intellectual encounter.","t":"他詼諧的舉止掩蓋了對手頻繁低估的有洞察力的分析智識——他在社交環境中以熱情部署機智，導致他們將親切的外表誤認為是整個人的全部，這在每次直接的智識交鋒中都被證明是代價高昂的反覆錯誤。","as":"Despite the gravity of the subject, the historian's jocose lecturing style, full of playful puns and witty asides, kept even the most indolent students engrossed, though his levity never trivialized the suffering he described.","at":"儘管主題相當沉重，這位歷史學家詼諧風趣的講課風格，充滿俏皮的雙關語和機智的題外話，讓即使是最懶散的學生也聽得津津有味，而他的輕鬆幽默從未淡化他所描述的苦難。"},{"w":"jubilant","p":"adj.","d":"Feeling or expressing great happiness.","c":"歡呼的；喜悅的","s":"The jubilant reception that greeted the landmark ruling reflected not merely satisfaction at the specific outcome but a cathartic release of years of accumulated frustration — the ardent campaigners' exultation tinged with a candid acknowledgement that the victory had arrived far later than the urgency of the underlying injustice had warranted.","t":"對里程碑式裁決的歡呼迎接，不僅反映了對具體結果的滿意，還反映了多年積累挫敗感的宣洩性釋放——熱烈活動人士的狂喜帶著坦率的承認，即勝利來得比潛在不公正的緊迫性所保證的要晚得多。","as":"Jubilant crowds poured into the streets of Berlin when the wall was finally breached, and strangers embraced in scenes of bliss that seemed incongruous beside the grim barrier, long an anathema to the divided city's residents.","at":"柏林圍牆終於被打開時，歡欣鼓舞的人群湧上街頭，素不相識的人們彼此相擁；那份狂喜的景象與那道陰森的高牆顯得格格不入，而這道牆長久以來一直為這座分裂城市的居民所深惡痛絕。"},{"w":"malign","p":"v.","d":"To speak about in an unfairly critical way.","c":"誹謗；中傷","s":"The tendency of each successive leadership to malign its predecessor's record — attributing to deliberate malice what was more plausibly the consequence of genuine constraint — had created an institutional culture so corrosive of candor that even objectively accurate criticism was reflexively dismissed as partisan invective.","t":"每一任領導層誹謗其前任記錄的傾向——將更可能是真實約束的後果歸因於蓄意惡意——創造了一種對坦率如此腐蝕的制度文化，以至於即使是客觀準確的批評也被條件反射地作為黨派辱罵而被駁回。","as":"Although many contemporaries maligned the physician Ignaz Semmelweis for insisting that doctors wash their hands, his seemingly bizarre advice was ultimately proven correct, as hospitals that heeded it saw maternal mortality plummet, a salient lesson in the perils of dogma.","at":"雖然許多同時代的人詆毀醫師塞麥爾維斯，只因他堅持醫生必須洗手，但他這看似怪異的建議最終獲得平反：採納此建議的醫院，產婦死亡率大幅下降，這是一個關於教條危害的鮮明教訓。"},{"w":"mortify","p":"v.","d":"To cause great embarrassment.","c":"使屈辱；使窘迫","s":"She was mortifyed less by the error itself — which was, in retrospect, entirely understandable — than by the discovery that colleagues had been aware of it for weeks and had discussed it with characteristic garrulousness among themselves without according her the candor of direct notification.","t":"她感到窘迫的，與其說是錯誤本身——回顧起來完全可以理解——不如說是發現同事幾週前就已知道，並以典型的喋喋不休在彼此之間討論，而沒有給予她直接通知的坦率。","as":"The young pianist was mortified when her memory faltered midway through the concerto, but the audience's warm applause offered her solace, and she returned to the practice room with renewed alacrity the very next morning.","at":"這位年輕鋼琴家在協奏曲演奏到一半時突然忘譜，羞愧得無地自容；但觀眾溫暖的掌聲給了她安慰，隔天一早，她便重新振作、迫不及待地回到練琴室。"},{"w":"omnipotent","p":"adj.","d":"Having unlimited power.","c":"全能的","s":"No institution, however omnipotent it might appear during its zenith, was immune to the wane of influence that followed the loss of the legitimacy on which its authority ultimately depended — a historical pattern so prevalent across civilisations that the most sagacious political theorists had elevated it to the status of an empirical law.","t":"沒有任何機構，無論在其頂峰時看起來多麼全能，都能免受隨著其權威最終依賴的合法性喪失而來的影響力衰退——一個在文明中如此普遍的歷史模式，以至於最睿智的政治理論家將其提升到實證規律的地位。","as":"Dictators gripped by megalomania often cultivate the illusion that they are omnipotent, yet history shows that even entrenched autocrats can be swiftly ousted by a popular uprising or a military coup.","at":"深陷自大妄想的獨裁者往往營造自己無所不能的假象，然而歷史證明，即使是根基穩固的獨裁者，也可能因一場民眾起義或軍事政變而迅速垮台。"},{"w":"peremptory","p":"adj.","d":"Insisting on immediate obedience.","c":"專橫的；不容反抗的","s":"The peremptory tone of the directive — brooking neither demurral nor modification — galvanised the compliance team into immediate action but simultaneously generated considerable resentment among those whose professional expertise had been entirely ignored in the formulation of requirements they were now being ordered to implement without consultation.","t":"指令的專橫語氣——不容反對或修改——激勵合規團隊立即採取行動，但同時在那些在制定要求時其專業知識完全被忽視、現在被命令不經諮詢執行的人中產生了相當大的怨恨。","as":"The new principal's peremptory memos, which demanded immediate compliance and brooked no objection, alienated a faculty accustomed to congenial collaboration, and several veteran teachers balked at what they regarded as one unilateral fiat after another.","at":"新任校長那些專橫的備忘錄要求老師立即服從、容不得任何異議，疏遠了習慣於融洽合作的教師群；好幾位資深教師對這一道又一道單方面下達的命令強烈抗拒。"},{"w":"precedent","p":"n.","d":"An earlier event used as a guide.","c":"先例；前例","s":"The ruling established a precedent whose ramifications extended far beyond the immediate case — the cogent reasoning of the majority opinion providing adherents of the reform movement with an authoritative foundation from which to initiate the broader challenges they had been ardently preparing for the better part of a decade.","t":"這一裁決確立了一個先例，其影響遠遠超出了直接案例——多數意見的有說服力的推理為改革運動的擁護者提供了一個權威基礎，從中啟動他們近十年來一直熱烈準備的更廣泛挑戰。","as":"When the court ruled that the tribe's ancestral claim to the forest, attested by centuries of oral history, outweighed the logging company's permit, it set a precedent that could invalidate similar permits and that disgruntled industry lobbyists vowed to contest.","at":"法院裁定，這個部落有數百年口述歷史為證的祖傳森林權利，優先於伐木公司的許可證；此一判決樹立了先例，可能使類似的許可證失效，而心懷不滿的業界遊說團體則誓言提出抗告。"},{"w":"rustic","p":"adj.","d":"Having a simple and unsophisticated character.","c":"鄉村的；質樸的","s":"The rustic simplicity of the retreat's accommodation proved congenial to the kind of uninterrupted reflection that the participants had come seeking — the absence of the gaudy distractions of urban life facilitating a quality of sustained concentration that the most voluminous productivity manuals had advocated but rarely successfully prescribed.","t":"靜修住宿的質樸簡單，被證明與參與者來尋求的那種不間斷反思的特質相契合——沒有城市生活俗麗的干擾，促進了最大量的生產力手冊所倡導但很少成功規定的那種持續集中注意力的質量。","as":"Many city dwellers romanticize the rustic simplicity of mountain villages, yet residents point out that such charm often masks a dire paucity of medical services and the inexorable wane of crafts that had flourished for generations.","at":"許多城市居民把山村質樸簡單的生活浪漫化，但當地居民指出，這種魅力往往掩蓋了醫療資源嚴重匱乏的事實，以及曾經興盛數代的傳統手工藝無可挽回的衰落。"},{"w":"wheedle","p":"v.","d":"To use flattery or coaxing to persuade.","c":"哄騙；誘騙","s":"His method of wheedleing concessions from initially resistant negotiating partners — combining jocose informality with the occasional flash of perspicacious insight that reminded them of his genuine acuity — was a more subtle variant of the obsequious flattery that less sophisticated operators typically deployed.","t":"他從最初抗拒的談判夥伴身上哄騙讓步的方法——將詼諧的非正式與偶爾閃現的有洞察力見解相結合，提醒他們他真正的敏銳——是不那麼精通的操作者通常部署的諂媚奉承的更微妙變體。","as":"The con artist wheedled large sums out of lonely retirees by exploiting their isolation and showering them with fulsome compliments, and prosecutors struggled to indict him because his victims had surrendered the money willingly.","at":"這名騙子利用孤獨退休人士的寂寞，對他們大灌迷湯，從他們身上哄騙走大筆金錢；由於受害者都是心甘情願交出錢財，檢察官很難將他起訴。"},{"w":"zenith","p":"n.","d":"The time at which something is most powerful.","c":"頂點；鼎盛時期","s":"At the zenith of its influence, the institution had wielded an omnipotent authority over the field that made its subsequent decline all the more instructive — the rapidity of the wane, once the underlying legitimacy had been compromised, suggesting how precarious even the most apparently impregnable positions ultimately remained.","t":"在其影響力的頂點，該機構對該領域擁有全能的權威，這使其後來的衰落更具啟示性——一旦潛在的合法性受到損害，衰退的速度之快，表明即使是最顯然固若金湯的地位最終仍然多麼不穩固。","as":"At the zenith of its power, the Mongol Empire, which had grown from a confederation of nomadic tribes, stretched from East Asia to Eastern Europe, yet its vast realm soon fragmented into rival khanates whose rulers seldom concurred.","at":"蒙古帝國由游牧部落聯盟發展而來，在國力鼎盛時期，疆域從東亞一路延伸到東歐；然而這片遼闊的領土不久便分裂成數個彼此對立的汗國，各汗國的統治者鮮少意見一致。"}]},{"unit":31,"cards":[{"w":"heresy","p":"n.","d":"a belief that goes against accepted doctrine.","c":"異端；邪說","s":"In the seventeenth century, Galileo's claim that the Earth revolved around the Sun was condemned as heresy by church authorities, who regarded any challenge to established doctrine as a grave offense. Forced to recant publicly, the elderly astronomer spent his final years under house arrest. Today, historians cite his trial as a sobering reminder that ideas once denounced as dangerous deviations from orthodoxy may later be recognized as fundamental scientific truths.","t":"十七世紀時，伽利略主張地球繞太陽運行，被教會當局譴責為異端邪說，他們將任何挑戰既定教義的行為視為嚴重罪行。這位年邁的天文學家被迫公開撤回主張，晚年在軟禁中度過。如今，歷史學家以他的審判作為警世案例：曾被斥為危險背離正統的思想，日後可能被公認為基本的科學真理。","as":"In the seventeenth century, Galileo's claim that the Earth orbits the sun was deemed heresy by church authorities, who were loath to tolerate any premise that seemed to undermine the inviolable doctrines they had promulgated for centuries.","at":"十七世紀時，伽利略主張地球繞著太陽運行，卻被教會當局視為異端；他們不願容忍任何可能動搖其數百年來所頒布、不容侵犯之教義的前提。"},{"w":"prudent","p":"adj.","d":"wise, cautious.","c":"謹慎的；明智的","s":"Facing an uncertain economic outlook, the board of directors made the prudentedecision to postpone its ambitious expansion plans and build up substantial cash reserves instead. Several competitors that had borrowed heavily to finance rapid growth soon struggled to repay their debts when interest rates rose sharply. Analysts later praised the company's cautious, far-sighted strategy, noting that careful planning had allowed it to survive the downturn without laying off a single employee.","t":"面對不確定的經濟前景，董事會做出了謹慎明智的決定，推遲雄心勃勃的擴張計畫，轉而累積大量現金儲備。數家為了快速成長而大舉借貸的競爭對手，在利率急遽上升後很快便難以償還債務。分析師事後稱讚該公司謹慎且具遠見的策略，指出周詳的規劃使公司得以度過經濟衰退，且未裁撤任何一名員工。","as":"Faced with a plethora of volatile investment schemes, the frugal retiree made the prudent decision to eschew speculative stocks and keep most of her savings in assets that would not jeopardize her financial security.","at":"面對五花八門、變幻莫測的投資方案，這位節儉的退休人士做出明智的決定：避開投機性股票，把大部分積蓄放在不會危及自身財務安全的資產上。"},{"w":"ostensible","p":"adj.","d":"outward, seeming.","c":"表面的；假裝的","s":"The ostensible purpose of the new surveillance program was to improve public safety by reducing street crime in the downtown area. However, investigative journalists soon uncovered internal documents revealing that the cameras were also being used to monitor peaceful protesters and collect data on their movements. Critics argued that officials had deliberately concealed the program's true objectives behind a reassuring justification designed to minimize public opposition. Public trust in the city council declined sharply afterward.","t":"這項新監控計畫表面上的目的，是透過減少市中心的街頭犯罪來提升公共安全。然而，調查記者很快便發現內部文件，顯示這些攝影機也被用來監視和平抗議者並蒐集其行動資料。批評者認為，官員刻意以一個令人安心的理由掩蓋計畫的真正目標，藉此將民眾的反對降到最低。此後，民眾對市議會的信任急遽下降。","as":"Although the ostensible purpose of the expedition was scientific research, historians who peruse the captain's clandestine letters have discerned that its real goal was to exploit the region's lucrative mineral deposits.","at":"雖然這次探險表面上的目的是科學研究，但仔細研讀船長祕密信件的歷史學家已察覺，其真正目標是開採該地區利潤豐厚的礦藏。"},{"w":"fervid","p":"adj.","d":"intense, enthusiastic, passionate.","c":"熱情的；熱烈的","s":"The candidate delivered a fervid speech that electrified the enormous crowd gathered in the town square. Speaking with intense passion about economic justice and educational opportunity, she repeatedly raised her fist as supporters cheered and waved banners. Even skeptical journalists admitted that her emotional energy was remarkably contagious. Political observers predicted that such enthusiastic public appearances would significantly boost her popularity among young voters who had previously felt ignored. Her campaign office reported record donations.","t":"這位候選人發表了一場熱情洋溢的演說，令聚集在城鎮廣場的廣大群眾情緒沸騰。她以強烈的熱忱談論經濟正義與教育機會，在支持者歡呼、揮舞旗幟之際一再高舉拳頭。就連抱持懷疑態度的記者也承認，她的情感能量極具感染力。政治觀察家預測，如此熱烈的公開露面將大幅提升她在過去一直覺得被忽視的年輕選民中的聲望。她的競選辦公室回報捐款創下新高。","as":"The young poet's fervid speeches against colonial rule galvanized a throng of students, yet his ardent supporters were soon dispersed when the government, fearing further strife, imposed a strict curfew.","at":"這位年輕詩人反對殖民統治的激昂演說，激勵了一大群學生；然而政府擔心衝突擴大而實施嚴格宵禁後，他那些熱情的支持者很快就被驅散了。"},{"w":"spurious","p":"adj.","d":"false, counterfeit.","c":"虛假的；偽造的","s":"The museum curator quickly recognized that the so-called ancient manuscript was spurious. Chemical analysis revealed that the ink contained synthetic compounds invented only in the twentieth century, and the paper showed no signs of genuine aging. Although the seller had provided an elaborate certificate of authenticity, experts confirmed that the document was a skillful forgery. The discovery prompted the institution to adopt far stricter verification procedures for all future acquisitions.","t":"博物館策展人很快便看出，這份所謂的古代手稿是偽造的。化學分析顯示，墨水含有二十世紀才發明的合成化合物，而紙張也沒有任何真正老化的跡象。儘管賣家提供了一份精心製作的真品證書，專家仍確認這份文件是一件高明的贗品。此一發現促使該機構對未來所有收購品採取更嚴格的鑑定程序。","as":"Curators concluded that the so-called ancient artifact was spurious after a meticulous chemical analysis revealed modern pigments, exposing an elaborate hoax that had deceived gullible collectors and even several eminent scholars.","at":"一項縝密的化學分析驗出現代顏料後，策展人斷定這件所謂的古代文物是偽造的，揭穿了一場不僅騙倒輕信的收藏家、甚至騙過數位知名學者的精心騙局。"},{"w":"propagate","p":"v.","d":"to multiply, spread.","c":"傳播；繁殖","s":"Social media platforms have made it alarmingly easy to propagate misinformation across the globe within a matter of hours. A single misleading post, shared by thousands of users who never verify its accuracy, can reach millions of readers before fact-checkers have an opportunity to respond. Researchers warn that false claims often spread faster than corrections because they provoke stronger emotional reactions, particularly fear, outrage, and surprise. Slowing this cycle requires both technology and education.","t":"社群媒體平台讓錯誤資訊能在短短幾小時內傳播到全球，其容易程度令人憂心。一則誤導性的貼文，經由數千名從不查證其正確性的使用者分享，可能在事實查核人員有機會回應之前就觸及數百萬名讀者。研究人員警告，虛假說法往往比更正消息傳得更快，因為它們會激起更強烈的情緒反應，尤其是恐懼、憤怒和驚訝。要減緩這種循環，科技與教育兩者缺一不可。","as":"Botanists warn that invasive vines propagate so rapidly in sultry climates that they can saturate an entire forest canopy within a few years, choking indigenous trees and destroying the habitat of countless birds.","at":"植物學家警告，入侵性藤蔓在濕熱的氣候中繁殖極快，幾年內就能布滿整片森林樹冠，使原生樹木窒息，並摧毀無數鳥類的棲息地。"},{"w":"anomaly","p":"n.","d":"irregularity, abnormality.","c":"異常；反常","s":"While analyzing years of climate records, the research team noticed a striking anomaly: one remote mountain station had reported temperatures consistently five degrees higher than every surrounding location. Initially suspecting a natural phenomenon, the scientists launched a thorough investigation. They eventually discovered that the irregular readings were caused by a malfunctioning sensor installed beside a heating vent, which had been distorting the station's measurements for nearly a decade. Replacing it solved the mystery.","t":"在分析多年的氣候紀錄時，研究團隊注意到一個明顯的異常現象：一座偏遠的山區測站所回報的氣溫，始終比周遭所有地點高出五度。科學家起初懷疑這是某種自然現象，於是展開徹底調查。他們最終發現，這些不規則的讀數是由一個安裝在暖氣出風口旁的故障感測器所造成，它扭曲了該測站的測量數據將近十年。更換感測器後，謎團隨之解開。","as":"When a sensor on the research vessel recorded an anomaly in ocean temperatures, the astute oceanographer refused to dismiss it as a mere glitch and instead began to scrutinize the data for signs of a latent subterranean volcano.","at":"研究船上的感測器記錄到海水溫度異常時，這位精明的海洋學家沒有把它當成小故障而置之不理，反而開始仔細審視數據，尋找一座潛伏地底火山的跡象。"},{"w":"innocuous","p":"adj.","d":"harmless, mild, innocent.","c":"無害的","s":"At first, the email appeared completely innocuous, containing only a friendly greeting and a link to what seemed to be a holiday card. However, when several employees clicked the link, malicious software was secretly installed on the company's network, allowing hackers to steal confidential financial records. Cybersecurity experts emphasize that the most dangerous attacks often disguise themselves as ordinary, trustworthy messages to lower their victims' natural defenses. Regular training helps staff recognize such traps.","t":"起初，這封電子郵件看起來完全無害，只有一句友善的問候和一個看似節日賀卡的連結。然而，當幾名員工點擊該連結後，惡意軟體便被秘密安裝到公司網路中，使駭客得以竊取機密財務紀錄。資安專家強調，最危險的攻擊往往偽裝成普通、可信的訊息，以降低受害者的天然戒心。定期訓練能幫助員工識破這類陷阱。","as":"What appeared to be an innocuous remark about the mayor's wardrobe was construed by his irascible aides as a deliberate insult, precipitating an acrimonious exchange that dominated the evening news.","at":"一句看似無傷大雅、關於市長穿著的評論，卻被他那些脾氣暴躁的助理解讀為蓄意侮辱，引發一場言詞尖刻的口角，成了當晚新聞的焦點。"},{"w":"surfeit","p":"n.","d":"excess, superabundance.","c":"過量；飲食過度","s":"Many modern consumers suffer not from a lack of information but from a surfeit of it. Every day, they are bombarded with countless notifications, advertisements, news updates, and messages competing relentlessly for their limited attention. Psychologists observe that this overwhelming excess can impair concentration, increase anxiety, and make thoughtful decision-making considerably more difficult. Consequently, some people deliberately schedule periods of digital silence to restore their mental clarity. Less, they find, is often more.","t":"許多現代消費者所苦的並非資訊不足，而是資訊過量。每天，他們被無數的通知、廣告、新聞更新和訊息轟炸，這些內容不停地爭奪他們有限的注意力。心理學家觀察到，這種壓倒性的過剩會損害專注力、加劇焦慮，並使深思熟慮的決策變得困難許多。因此，有些人刻意安排「數位靜默」時段，以恢復思緒的清晰。他們發現，少往往就是多。","as":"Nutritionists note that while malnutrition once afflicted much of the population, many affluent societies now suffer from a surfeit of sugar and fat, a dietary excess that greatly exacerbates heart disease.","at":"營養學家指出，營養不良雖曾困擾大多數人口，如今許多富裕社會卻苦於糖分與脂肪攝取過量，而這種飲食過度大大加劇了心臟疾病。"},{"w":"milieu","p":"n.","d":"environment, setting.","c":"環境；社會背景","s":"Growing up in the vibrant artistic milieu of 1920s Paris, the young painter was constantly surrounded by writers, musicians, and philosophers who challenged conventional ideas. Evenings spent in crowded cafés debating politics and aesthetics profoundly shaped his creative vision. Art historians argue that his innovative style cannot be fully understood without considering the intellectual environment and social setting that nurtured his remarkable talent during those formative years. His early sketches clearly reflect this lively atmosphere.","t":"這位年輕畫家成長於1920年代巴黎充滿活力的藝術環境中，身邊不斷圍繞著挑戰傳統觀念的作家、音樂家與哲學家。在擁擠的咖啡館中辯論政治與美學的夜晚，深刻地塑造了他的創作視野。藝術史學家認為，若不考慮在那些關鍵成長歲月中培育他非凡才華的知識氛圍與社會背景，便無法完全理解他的創新風格。他早期的素描清楚反映了這種活潑的氛圍。","as":"Raised in the cosmopolitan milieu of nineteenth-century Vienna, the composer absorbed a heterogeneous gamut of musical traditions, an upbringing that helps explain the singular virtuosity of his early symphonies.","at":"這位作曲家在十九世紀維也納兼容並蓄的環境中長大，吸收了各式各樣的音樂傳統；這樣的成長背景，正說明了他早期交響曲何以展現出非凡的精湛技藝。"},{"w":"strident","p":"adj.","d":"shrill, harsh, rough.","c":"刺耳的；尖銳的","s":"The neighbors complained repeatedly about the strident alarm that sounded from the abandoned warehouse every night at midnight. Its harsh, piercing tone echoed through the quiet residential streets, waking sleeping children and disturbing elderly residents. Local officials initially ignored the complaints, but after a petition gathered hundreds of signatures, they finally dispatched technicians to disconnect the faulty system. Residents celebrated the restored peace with a small community gathering. Silence, they agreed, had never sounded sweeter.","t":"鄰居們一再抱怨那座廢棄倉庫每晚午夜響起的刺耳警報聲。那尖銳、穿透性的聲響在寧靜的住宅街道間迴盪，吵醒熟睡的孩童，也打擾年長的居民。地方官員起初對這些投訴置之不理，但在一份請願書蒐集到數百人連署後，他們終於派遣技術人員切斷這套故障的系統。居民們舉辦了一場小型社區聚會，慶祝恢復寧靜。他們一致認為，寂靜從未如此美好。","as":"The activists' strident chants reverberating through the plaza were meant to elicit attention from lawmakers, but the cacophony only nettled residents who craved a respite from months of protest.","at":"激進人士刺耳的口號在廣場上迴盪，本意是要引起立法者的注意，但這片嘈雜聲只惹惱了渴望從數月抗議中喘口氣的居民。"},{"w":"concomitant","p":"adj.","d":"accompanying, attending.","c":"伴隨的","s":"Rapid urbanization has brought substantial economic benefits to many developing nations, but it has also produced several concomitant problems. As millions of rural workers migrate to cities in search of employment, overcrowded housing, traffic congestion, and air pollution inevitably accompany this population growth. Urban planners argue that governments must address these related challenges simultaneously rather than treating them as separate issues, since each one tends to intensify the others. Integrated planning is therefore essential.","t":"快速都市化為許多開發中國家帶來可觀的經濟利益，但也產生了若干伴隨而來的問題。隨著數百萬名農村勞工為了就業而遷往城市，住宅過度擁擠、交通壅塞與空氣污染無可避免地伴隨著人口成長而出現。都市規劃者主張，政府必須同時處理這些相關挑戰，而非將其視為各自獨立的問題，因為每一個問題往往會加劇其他問題。因此，整合性的規劃至關重要。","as":"The rapid industrialization of nineteenth-century Britain brought unprecedented wealth to affluent factory owners, but its concomitant pollution and overcrowding left indigent workers susceptible to cholera and other virulent diseases.","at":"十九世紀英國的快速工業化為富裕的工廠主帶來空前的財富，但隨之而來的污染與過度擁擠，卻使貧困的工人容易感染霍亂及其他致命疾病。"},{"w":"lassitude","p":"n.","d":"weariness, fatigue.","c":"疲倦；無精打采","s":"After weeks of working double shifts at the understaffed hospital, the nurse was overcome by a profound lassitude that no amount of coffee could relieve. Her limbs felt heavy, her concentration faded, and even simple tasks required enormous effort. Medical researchers warn that such chronic exhaustion among healthcare workers not only damages their own wellbeing but also significantly increases the likelihood of errors that could endanger patients' lives. Adequate staffing remains the most effective remedy.","t":"在人手不足的醫院連續數週值雙班後，這名護理師被一股深沉的疲倦所淹沒，再多的咖啡也無法緩解。她四肢沉重、注意力渙散，就連簡單的工作都需要付出極大的努力。醫學研究人員警告，醫護人員這種長期的疲憊不僅損害他們自身的健康，也大幅增加了可能危及病患生命的失誤機率。充足的人力配置仍是最有效的解決之道。","as":"After weeks of interminable drudgery on the night shift, the nurses complained of a lassitude so persistent that even routine tasks felt excruciating, a fatigue that hospital administrators could no longer ignore.","at":"在夜班熬了好幾週沒完沒了的苦差事後，護理師們抱怨倦怠感揮之不去，連例行工作都變得苦不堪言，醫院管理階層再也無法忽視這種疲憊。"},{"w":"deleterious","p":"adj.","d":"bad, harmful.","c":"有害的；造成傷害的","s":"Numerous scientific studies have documented the deleterious effects of prolonged screen exposure on adolescents' sleep patterns. Blue light emitted by phones and tablets suppresses the production of melatonin, a hormone that regulates the body's natural sleep cycle. As a result, teenagers who use devices late at night frequently experience reduced sleep quality, impaired memory, and declining academic performance. Pediatricians therefore recommend removing electronic devices from bedrooms entirely. Many families now enforce a strict nighttime curfew.","t":"許多科學研究已記錄了長時間使用螢幕對青少年睡眠模式的有害影響。手機與平板電腦所發出的藍光會抑制褪黑激素的分泌，而這種荷爾蒙負責調節人體的自然睡眠週期。因此，深夜使用電子裝置的青少年經常出現睡眠品質下降、記憶力受損以及學業表現退步的情況。小兒科醫師因此建議將電子裝置完全移出臥室。許多家庭現在實施嚴格的夜間使用禁令。","as":"Researchers have corroborated earlier studies showing that a sedentary lifestyle has deleterious effects on cardiovascular health, and they exhort office workers to stand or walk at least once every hour.","at":"研究人員證實了先前的研究結果：久坐不動的生活方式對心血管健康有害，因此他們敦促上班族至少每小時起身站立或走動一次。"},{"w":"efficacy","p":"n.","d":"power to produce an effect.","c":"功效；效力","s":"Before any new medication can be approved for public use, researchers must conduct rigorous clinical trials to demonstrate its efficacy and safety. Thousands of volunteers are randomly assigned to receive either the experimental drug or a placebo, allowing scientists to measure whether the treatment genuinely produces the intended results. Only when the data consistently confirm the drug's effectiveness without serious side effects will regulatory agencies grant final approval. This process often takes nearly a decade.","t":"任何新藥在獲准供大眾使用之前，研究人員都必須進行嚴謹的臨床試驗，以證明其功效與安全性。數千名志願者被隨機分配服用實驗藥物或安慰劑，讓科學家能夠衡量該療法是否確實產生預期的效果。唯有當數據一致證實藥物有效且無嚴重副作用時，主管機關才會給予最終核准。這個過程往往需要將近十年。","as":"Before the vaccine could be deployed nationwide, regulators insisted on a comprehensive trial to evaluate its efficacy, since anecdotal reports were too dubious to prove that it actually neutralized the virus.","at":"在這款疫苗於全國施打之前，主管機關堅持進行全面試驗以評估其效力，因為零星的個案報告太不可靠，無法證明它真能中和病毒。"},{"w":"dissent","p":"v.","d":"to differ, disagree, protest.","c":"持異議；不同意","s":"Although the majority of the Supreme Court justices supported the controversial ruling, two members chose to dissent, publishing a lengthy opinion that explained their objections in considerable detail. They argued that the decision contradicted established legal precedent and threatened fundamental civil liberties. Legal scholars note that such disagreements, though they carry no immediate legal force, often influence future judges and occasionally lay the groundwork for overturning flawed decisions. History has vindicated many such opinions.","t":"雖然大多數最高法院大法官支持這項具爭議性的判決，但有兩位成員選擇提出異議，並發表了一份冗長的意見書，相當詳盡地說明他們反對的理由。他們主張，該判決違背既有的法律判例，並威脅到基本的公民自由。法律學者指出，這類不同意見雖然不具即時的法律效力，卻常常影響後世的法官，有時更為推翻有缺陷的判決奠定基礎。歷史已證明許多這類意見是正確的。","as":"Although the majority of the court upheld the restrictive law, two justices chose to dissent, arguing in a trenchant opinion that the statute flouted constitutional protections and set a dangerous precedent.","at":"雖然法院多數維持這項限制性法律，但有兩位大法官選擇提出異議，在一份措辭犀利的意見書中主張，該法公然漠視憲法保障，並開創了危險的先例。"},{"w":"ferment","p":"n.","d":"uproar, agitation, turmoil.","c":"騷動；動亂（亦指發酵）","s":"The sudden announcement of massive tuition increases threw the entire university campus into a state of ferment. Within hours, students organized protests, occupied administrative buildings, and circulated petitions demanding the immediate resignation of the president. Faculty members were sharply divided, with some supporting the demonstrators and others urging calm negotiation. The turmoil lasted several weeks before administrators finally agreed to reconsider their controversial financial decision. Tuition was eventually frozen for two full years.","t":"學費大幅調漲的突然宣布，使整個大學校園陷入一片騷動。短短數小時內，學生們便組織抗議、佔領行政大樓，並傳閱請願書要求校長立即辭職。教職員的意見嚴重分歧，有人支持示威者，也有人呼籲冷靜協商。這場動亂持續了數週，校方才終於同意重新考慮這項具爭議性的財務決定。學費最終凍漲了整整兩年。","as":"The political ferment that swept Paris in 1848 was symptomatic of deeper economic grievances, as disgruntled laborers and idealistic students alike rose against a monarchy they regarded as callous and ineffectual.","at":"1848年席捲巴黎的政治動盪，反映出更深層的經濟不滿：心懷怨氣的勞工與滿懷理想的學生紛紛起身，反抗他們眼中冷漠又無能的君主政體。"},{"w":"attenuated","p":"adj.","d":"weakened, thinned, decreased.","c":"減弱的；變薄的","s":"By the time the powerful hurricane reached the mountainous inland region, its strength had been considerably attenuated. The rugged terrain and cooler air had gradually weakened its winds from devastating speeds to moderate gusts, sparing most villages from serious destruction. Meteorologists explained that storms typically lose energy once they move away from warm ocean waters, which supply the heat and moisture necessary to sustain their intensity. Heavy rainfall, however, still caused minor flooding in several valleys.","t":"當這場強烈颶風抵達內陸山區時，其威力已大幅減弱。崎嶇的地形與較涼的空氣，逐漸將其風速從毀滅性的強度削弱為中等陣風，使大部分村莊免於嚴重破壞。氣象學家解釋，暴風一旦遠離溫暖的海水便通常會失去能量，因為溫暖海水提供了維持其強度所需的熱量與水氣。然而，豪雨仍在數個山谷造成輕微淹水。","as":"By the time the radio signal reached Earth, it had grown so attenuated during its voyage across interstellar space that astronomers needed a mammoth array of antennas to capture the elusive whisper amid the cosmic static.","at":"這道無線電訊號抵達地球時，已在穿越星際空間的旅途中衰減得極為微弱，天文學家必須動用龐大的天線陣列，才能在宇宙雜訊中捕捉到這縷難以捉摸的微音。"},{"w":"arbiter","p":"n.","d":"judge.","c":"仲裁者；權威","s":"When the two technology companies could not resolve their bitter patent dispute through negotiation, they agreed to appoint an independent arbiter to settle the matter. The retired judge carefully examined thousands of pages of technical documents, interviewed engineers from both firms, and listened to lengthy arguments from each legal team. Both parties had promised in advance to accept her final judgment, avoiding years of expensive and unpredictable litigation. Her ruling was widely respected as fair.","t":"當兩家科技公司無法透過協商解決激烈的專利糾紛時，他們同意指派一位獨立的仲裁者來裁決此事。這位退休法官仔細審閱了數千頁技術文件，訪談兩家公司的工程師，並聆聽雙方律師團隊冗長的論述。雙方事先都承諾接受她的最終裁決，藉此避免了多年昂貴且結果難料的訴訟。她的裁決被普遍認為公正而備受尊重。","as":"Throughout the 1950s, the influential critic served as the ultimate arbiter of literary taste in New York, and any young aspirant who incurred his disdain could expect to see a debut novel relegated to the bargain bins.","at":"整個1950年代，這位極具影響力的評論家是紐約文學品味的最終裁判；任何招致他鄙夷的年輕新秀，都可能眼睜睜看著自己的處女作被打入特價書堆。"},{"w":"incumbent","p":"adj.","d":"morally required.","c":"負有責任的；現任的","s":"When a serious error is discovered in published research, it is incumbent upon the authors to issue a prompt and transparent correction. Other scientists may have already relied on the flawed findings to design their own experiments, so any delay could waste valuable time and resources. Most academic institutions regard this obligation as a fundamental ethical responsibility, and researchers who deliberately conceal mistakes may face severe professional consequences. Honesty, in short, is non-negotiable in science.","t":"當已發表的研究被發現有嚴重錯誤時，作者有責任迅速且透明地發布更正。其他科學家可能已經依據這些有缺陷的研究結果來設計自己的實驗，因此任何延誤都可能浪費寶貴的時間與資源。大多數學術機構將此義務視為基本的倫理責任，而刻意隱瞞錯誤的研究人員可能面臨嚴重的職業後果。簡而言之，在科學中誠實是不容妥協的。","as":"Because the factory had knowingly perpetrated years of pollution, the judge ruled that it was incumbent upon its owners to underwrite the cleanup and offer compensatory payments to families whose wells had been tainted.","at":"由於這家工廠明知故犯，造成多年污染，法官裁定業主有責任出資進行清理，並向水井遭到污染的家庭支付賠償金。"}]},{"unit":32,"cards":[{"w":"profound","p":"adj.","d":"deep, intense.","c":"深奧的；深刻的","s":"Reading the letters her grandfather had written during the war had a profound effect on the young historian, permanently changing how she understood her family's past. His quiet descriptions of hunger, loss, and unexpected kindness revealed emotional depths she had never suspected. The experience inspired her to devote her career to collecting ordinary soldiers' personal correspondence, convinced that such intimate documents offered insights that official records could never capture. Her first book became a bestseller.","t":"閱讀祖父在戰時寫下的信件，對這位年輕的歷史學家產生了深刻的影響，永遠改變了她對家族歷史的理解。他對飢餓、失去與意外善意的平靜描述，揭露了她從未察覺的情感深度。這段經歷激勵她將職業生涯投入於蒐集普通士兵的私人書信，她深信這類私密文件能提供官方紀錄永遠無法捕捉的洞見。她的第一本書成了暢銷書。","as":"The publication of Darwin's theory had a profound impact on Victorian society, compelling devout readers to ponder whether humanity's origins were as sacred as tradition had taught and opening a lasting schism between scientists and clergy.","at":"達爾文理論的出版對維多利亞時代社會產生了深遠的影響，迫使虔誠的讀者思考人類的起源是否真如傳統所教導的那般神聖，也在科學家與神職人員之間造成長久的分裂。"},{"w":"alleviate","p":"v.","d":"to make easier, lighten.","c":"減輕；緩解","s":"To alleviate severe traffic congestion in the capital, city planners introduced a network of dedicated bus lanes and expanded the underground railway system. Within two years, average commuting times had fallen significantly, and air quality in the downtown district had noticeably improved. Officials acknowledged, however, that these measures only eased the problem rather than solving it completely, since the city's population continued to grow at a remarkable rate. Further expansion is already being planned.","t":"為了緩解首都嚴重的交通壅塞，都市規劃者引進了公車專用道網絡，並擴建地下鐵路系統。兩年內，平均通勤時間大幅縮短，市中心的空氣品質也明顯改善。然而，官員承認這些措施只是減輕了問題，而非徹底解決，因為該市人口仍以驚人的速度持續成長。進一步的擴建計畫已在規劃中。","as":"To alleviate the acute food shortages caused by the drought, relief agencies distributed grain to families facing destitution, though officials conceded that such aid could only palliate the crisis rather than eradicate its root causes.","at":"為了緩解乾旱造成的嚴重糧荒，救援機構向瀕臨赤貧的家庭發放穀物，但官員也坦承，這類援助只能暫時減輕危機，無法根除問題的根源。"},{"w":"prodigious","p":"adj.","d":"extraordinary, enormous.","c":"巨大的；驚人的","s":"Even as a child, the composer displayed a prodigious talent that astonished everyone around him. By the age of six, he could perform complex piano sonatas from memory, and by twelve he had written several symphonies. Music critics throughout Europe described his abilities as nearly miraculous. Historians still debate how such an extraordinary gift emerged so early, though most agree that intensive training from his father played a crucial role.","t":"這位作曲家從小就展現出驚人的天賦，令身邊所有人大為驚奇。六歲時，他便能憑記憶彈奏複雜的鋼琴奏鳴曲；十二歲時，他已寫出數部交響曲。歐洲各地的樂評家形容他的能力近乎奇蹟。歷史學家至今仍在爭論如此非凡的天賦為何能這麼早出現，不過多數人同意，父親的密集訓練扮演了關鍵角色。","as":"Mozart displayed a prodigious talent from early childhood, composing intricate sonatas at an age when most children are still mastering rudimentary skills, which is why biographers often cite him as the paragon of a musical prodigy.","at":"莫札特從幼年起就展現驚人的天賦，在大多數孩子還在學習基本技能的年紀，他已能譜寫精巧的奏鳴曲，這也是傳記作家常把他奉為音樂神童典範的原因。"},{"w":"celerity","p":"n.","d":"speed, rapidity.","c":"迅速；敏捷","s":"The emergency response team acted with remarkable celerity after the earthquake struck, reaching the most severely damaged neighborhoods within twenty minutes. Rescuers immediately began searching collapsed buildings for survivors, while medical staff established temporary clinics in nearby schools. Disaster experts later concluded that this swift, well-coordinated reaction had saved dozens of lives, since trapped victims' chances of survival decline dramatically with every hour that passes. Their training had clearly paid off.","t":"地震發生後，緊急應變小組以驚人的迅速行動，在二十分鐘內便抵達受損最嚴重的社區。救援人員立刻開始在倒塌的建築物中搜尋生還者，醫護人員則在附近的學校設立臨時診所。災害專家事後斷定，這種迅速且協調良好的反應拯救了數十條人命，因為受困者的生存機率會隨著每一小時的流逝而急劇下降。他們的訓練顯然收到了成效。","as":"The firefighters responded with remarkable celerity, arriving within minutes of the alarm and containing the conflagration before it could raze the historic edifice that had anchored the town square for two centuries.","at":"消防員以驚人的速度出動，在警報響起後數分鐘內抵達，趕在大火將這座矗立於鎮廣場兩百年的歷史建築夷為平地之前控制住火勢。"},{"w":"expedite","p":"v.","d":"to carry out promptly.","c":"加速；促進","s":"To expedite the approval process for urgently needed medicines, the health ministry created a special fast-track program during the public health crisis. Applications that would normally require two years of review were evaluated within several months, without lowering essential safety standards. Pharmaceutical companies welcomed the streamlined procedures, while patient advocacy groups praised the government for recognizing that bureaucratic delays could have fatal consequences for seriously ill people. Thousands of patients benefited almost immediately.","t":"為了加速急需藥品的審核流程，衛生部在公共衛生危機期間設立了特別的快速審查計畫。通常需要兩年審查的申請案，在數個月內便完成評估，且未降低必要的安全標準。製藥公司對這些簡化的程序表示歡迎，病患權益團體也讚揚政府體認到官僚延誤可能對重症患者造成致命後果。數千名病患幾乎立即受惠。","as":"Hoping to expedite the reconstruction of the earthquake-ravaged city, the governor issued a fiat that waived restrictive permit requirements, a move critics feared would allow unscrupulous contractors to cut corners with impunity.","at":"為了加速這座遭地震重創城市的重建，州長發布一道命令，免除了繁瑣的許可規定；批評者擔心，此舉會讓不肖承包商偷工減料卻不必受罰。"},{"w":"bizarre","p":"adj.","d":"fantastic, odd.","c":"奇異的；古怪的","s":"Visitors to the small coastal museum are often puzzled by its bizarre collection, which includes a stuffed two-headed calf, a violin made entirely of matchsticks, and hundreds of antique false teeth. The eccentric founder spent fifty years acquiring unusual objects from flea markets around the world. Although some critics dismiss the exhibits as strange curiosities, the museum attracts thousands of tourists who enjoy its peculiar and unpredictable charm. Few leave without taking photographs.","t":"參觀這座小型海濱博物館的遊客，常對其古怪的收藏感到困惑，其中包括一隻雙頭小牛標本、一把完全用火柴棒製成的小提琴，以及數百副古董假牙。這位古怪的創辦人花了五十年從世界各地的跳蚤市場蒐集奇特物品。雖然有些評論家認為這些展品只是奇怪的珍奇玩意，這座博物館仍吸引數千名喜愛其獨特且難以預料魅力的遊客。很少有人離開時不拍照留念。","as":"Early naturalists considered the platypus so bizarre, a furry mammal with a duck's bill that lays eggs, that many suspected the specimen had been fabricated by a mischievous taxidermist, a conjecture later shown to be absurd.","at":"早期的博物學家覺得鴨嘴獸實在太奇特——一種長著鴨嘴、會下蛋的毛茸茸哺乳動物——許多人懷疑這件標本是某個愛惡作劇的標本師拼湊捏造的，這種猜測後來被證明十分荒謬。"},{"w":"usurp","p":"v.","d":"to seize, annex, grab.","c":"篡奪；奪取","s":"In 1399, Henry Bolingbroke returned from exile, raised an army, and managed to usurp the English throne from his cousin, King Richard II. Although Henry claimed he was merely reclaiming his inheritance, many nobles regarded the seizure of power as illegitimate. The controversy surrounding his reign contributed to decades of political instability, eventually helping to trigger the bloody series of civil conflicts known as the Wars of the Roses. His dynasty never fully escaped this shadow.","t":"1399年，亨利．博林布魯克結束流亡返國，召集軍隊，成功從堂兄理查二世手中篡奪了英格蘭王位。雖然亨利聲稱他只是收回自己的繼承權，許多貴族仍認為這種奪權行為並不正當。圍繞其統治的爭議導致了數十年的政治動盪，最終促成了被稱為玫瑰戰爭的一連串血腥內戰。他的王朝始終未能完全擺脫這個陰影。","as":"After the ambitious general staged a coup to usurp the throne, he moved swiftly to oust loyal ministers and subjugate rebellious provinces, determined to consolidate power he had seized by force.","at":"這位野心勃勃的將軍發動政變篡奪王位後，迅速罷黜忠心的大臣、鎮壓叛亂的省分，決心鞏固他以武力奪來的政權。"},{"w":"paltry","p":"adj.","d":"petty, worthless.","c":"微不足道的；少得可憐的","s":"After working overtime for six consecutive months, the factory employees were outraged to receive a paltry bonus of only twenty dollars each. Meanwhile, company executives awarded themselves substantial raises and luxurious holiday trips. The workers' union argued that such a meager reward was an insult to the staff's dedication and sacrifice. Following widespread protests and negative media coverage, management reluctantly agreed to renegotiate the compensation package. The final agreement satisfied most workers.","t":"在連續加班六個月後，工廠員工收到每人僅二十美元、少得可憐的獎金，感到十分憤怒。與此同時，公司高層卻為自己大幅加薪並安排奢華的假期旅遊。工會主張，如此微薄的獎勵是對員工奉獻與犧牲的侮辱。在大規模抗議與負面媒體報導之後，管理階層勉強同意重新協商薪酬方案。最終協議讓大多數員工感到滿意。","as":"Even as executive salaries continued to surge, the company offered its warehouse workers a paltry raise of a few cents an hour, a gesture that irate employees derided as an insult rather than a genuine reward for their labor.","at":"在高階主管薪資持續飆漲之際，公司卻只給倉庫員工每小時區區幾分錢的加薪，憤怒的員工嘲諷這根本是一種侮辱，而非對他們辛勞的真心回報。"},{"w":"trivial","p":"adj.","d":"of little importance, insignificant.","c":"瑣碎的；微不足道的","s":"The committee wasted nearly three hours arguing about trivial matters, such as the color of the conference brochures and the brand of coffee to serve during breaks. Meanwhile, genuinely important issues, including the organization's serious budget deficit, were postponed until the next meeting. Frustrated members complained that the chairperson consistently allowed minor details to dominate discussions, preventing the group from making urgent decisions about its future. Several members eventually resigned in protest.","t":"委員會浪費了將近三個小時爭論瑣碎的事情，例如會議手冊的顏色和休息時間要供應哪個牌子的咖啡。與此同時，真正重要的議題，包括該組織嚴重的預算赤字，卻被延到下次會議。沮喪的成員抱怨主席總是讓細枝末節主導討論，使團體無法就其未來做出緊急決策。數名成員最終憤而辭職以示抗議。","as":"The editor urged the young journalist to omit trivial details about the senator's wardrobe and focus instead on the salient facts of the bribery scandal she had been assiduously investigating, which were far more pertinent to readers.","at":"編輯要求這位年輕記者刪去參議員穿著打扮的瑣碎細節，轉而聚焦於她一直孜孜不倦調查的賄賂醜聞中的關鍵事實，因為這些對讀者而言切題得多。"},{"w":"condone","p":"v.","d":"to excuse, pardon.","c":"寬恕；縱容","s":"The school principal made it clear that she would not condone cheating under any circumstances, regardless of the pressure students faced during examination season. Anyone caught copying answers or using unauthorized devices would automatically receive a failing grade. Some parents argued that the policy was excessively harsh, but the principal insisted that overlooking dishonesty, even occasionally, would send a dangerous message and undermine the value of every student's achievements. Cheating incidents declined sharply the following year.","t":"校長明確表示，無論學生在考試季面臨多大的壓力，她在任何情況下都不會縱容作弊。任何被抓到抄襲答案或使用未經許可裝置的人，都將自動得到不及格的成績。有些家長認為這項政策過於嚴苛，但校長堅持，即使偶爾對不誠實行為視而不見，也會傳達危險的訊息，並削弱每位學生成就的價值。隔年作弊事件大幅減少。","as":"Although the principal sympathized with the students' plight, she refused to condone their vandalism, insisting that even a laudable cause could not exonerate those who had damaged school property.","at":"雖然校長同情學生們的處境，但她拒絕縱容他們的破壞行為，堅稱即使出發點值得讚揚，也不能為損壞學校財產的人開脫罪責。"},{"w":"venerable","p":"adj.","d":"respected, worshiped.","c":"值得尊敬的；莊嚴的","s":"The venerable professor had taught philosophy at the university for more than fifty years, and generations of former students still traveled great distances to attend his annual lecture. Colleagues admired not only his extraordinary knowledge but also his humility and patience. When he finally retired at the age of eighty-five, the university honored his remarkable contributions by naming its newly renovated library after him. Hundreds attended the moving dedication ceremony.","t":"這位德高望重的教授在大學教授哲學超過五十年，一代又一代的校友至今仍遠道而來參加他的年度講座。同事們不僅欽佩他非凡的學識，也敬重他的謙遜與耐心。當他終於在八十五歲退休時，大學以他的名字為新整修的圖書館命名，以表彰他卓越的貢獻。數百人出席了這場感人的啟用典禮。","as":"Villagers revere the venerable oak in the town square, which has endured three centuries of inclement weather and the countless vicissitudes of local history, from wars and famines to floods.","at":"村民們崇敬鎮廣場上那棵古老的橡樹，它挺過了三個世紀的惡劣天氣，也見證了戰爭、饑荒與洪水等地方歷史上無數的興衰變遷。"},{"w":"menial","p":"adj.","d":"humble, degrading.","c":"卑微的；（工作）低下的","s":"Although she held a university degree, the recent immigrant initially had to accept menial jobs such as washing dishes and cleaning offices at night. These humble positions paid very little and offered almost no opportunity for advancement. Nevertheless, she used every spare moment to study the local language and professional certification requirements. Within five years, she had become a licensed accountant running her own successful business. Her story now inspires many newcomers.","t":"雖然擁有大學學位，這位新移民起初不得不接受洗碗和夜間清潔辦公室等卑微的工作。這些低下的職位薪資微薄，幾乎沒有升遷機會。儘管如此，她利用每一刻空閒時間學習當地語言並研究專業證照的要求。五年內，她已成為一名持有執照的會計師，經營著自己成功的事業。她的故事如今激勵著許多新移民。","as":"Many highly educated expatriates discover that their foreign credentials are not acknowledged, forcing them to accept menial jobs that offer meager remuneration and little opportunity to use their professional expertise.","at":"許多受過高等教育的旅外人士發現自己的外國學歷不被承認，只得接受報酬微薄、又幾乎無法發揮專業的低下工作。"},{"w":"succinct","p":"adj.","d":"brief, concise.","c":"簡明的；簡潔的","s":"Busy executives generally prefer succinct reports that summarize essential information in a single page rather than lengthy documents filled with unnecessary detail. Consultants are therefore trained to present their key findings clearly and briefly, eliminating repetition and technical jargon whenever possible. A concise summary allows decision-makers to grasp complex situations quickly, although supporting data should always remain available for anyone who wishes to examine the analysis more closely. Clarity, after all, respects the reader's time.","t":"忙碌的高階主管通常偏好將重要資訊濃縮在一頁內的簡明報告，而非充斥不必要細節的冗長文件。因此，顧問們受訓以清楚、簡短的方式呈現主要發現，盡可能刪除重複內容與技術術語。簡潔的摘要能讓決策者迅速掌握複雜的情況，不過佐證資料應隨時備妥，供希望更仔細檢視分析的人查閱。畢竟，清晰是對讀者時間的尊重。","as":"Unlike his verbose predecessor, the new president favored succinct addresses, conveying the gist of complex policies in a few cogent sentences that even skeptical voters could easily follow.","at":"不同於他那位冗長囉嗦的前任，新總統偏好簡潔的演說，只用寥寥幾句條理分明的話就傳達出複雜政策的要旨，連抱持懷疑的選民也能輕鬆理解。"},{"w":"ambiguous","p":"adj.","d":"vague, undefined, not specific.","c":"模稜兩可的","s":"The contract contained an ambiguous clause stating that payment would be made 'upon completion,' without specifying whether this referred to the construction work itself or the final safety inspection. When a dispute arose, each company interpreted the phrase differently to support its own financial interests. Lawyers eventually spent months arguing over the unclear wording, a costly lesson demonstrating why legal documents must be drafted with absolute precision. Both firms have since revised their contracts.","t":"這份合約中有一項模稜兩可的條款，寫明款項將於「完成時」支付，卻未具體說明這是指施工本身還是最終的安全檢查。發生糾紛時，雙方公司各自以不同方式解讀這句話，以維護自身的財務利益。律師們最終花了數月爭論這段不明確的文字，這個代價高昂的教訓說明了法律文件為何必須以絕對精確的方式擬定。兩家公司此後都修訂了各自的合約。","as":"Because the treaty's wording was ambiguous, each nation interpreted the boundary clauses in its own favor, and minor border skirmishes soon gave way to a hostile standoff that no international mandate could resolve.","at":"由於條約的措辭模稜兩可，兩國各自對邊界條款作出有利於己的解讀，小規模的邊境衝突很快演變成敵對僵局，任何國際授權都無法化解。"},{"w":"extraneous","p":"adj.","d":"foreign, not belonging.","c":"無關的；外來的","s":"When writing a research paper, students should remove any extraneous information that does not directly support their central argument. Interesting but unrelated anecdotes, lengthy background descriptions, and repetitive examples can distract readers and weaken the overall clarity of the essay. Experienced editors recommend asking a simple question about every paragraph: does this material genuinely advance the thesis? If not, it probably belongs in a different piece of writing. Less is often more.","t":"撰寫研究報告時，學生應刪除任何不直接支持其核心論點的無關資訊。有趣但不相干的軼事、冗長的背景描述以及重複的例子，都可能分散讀者的注意力，並削弱整篇文章的清晰度。經驗豐富的編輯建議針對每一段落問一個簡單的問題：這些內容是否真正推進了論點？如果沒有，它可能屬於另一篇文章。少往往就是多。","as":"To keep the documentary focused, the director decided to expunge every extraneous scene, including a lush sequence of the rainforest that, however beautiful, was irrelevant to the film's central argument.","at":"為了讓紀錄片保持焦點，導演決定刪除所有無關的場景，包括一段蒼翠繁茂的雨林畫面——無論多美，它都與影片的核心論點無關。"},{"w":"archaic","p":"adj.","d":"out-of-date.","c":"古老的；過時的","s":"Many government offices still rely on archaic computer systems installed in the 1980s, which frequently crash and cannot communicate with modern software. Employees must often print documents and manually enter the same information into several different databases. Technology experts estimate that replacing these outdated systems would cost billions of dollars, yet continuing to maintain them wastes enormous amounts of time and creates serious security vulnerabilities. Several upgrade projects are finally underway.","t":"許多政府機關至今仍依賴1980年代安裝的老舊電腦系統，這些系統經常當機，也無法與現代軟體相容。員工常常必須列印文件，並將相同的資訊手動輸入數個不同的資料庫。科技專家估計，汰換這些過時的系統將耗資數十億美元，然而繼續維護它們卻浪費大量時間，並造成嚴重的資安漏洞。數項系統升級計畫終於開始進行。","as":"Linguists visiting the isolated mountain village were astonished to hear elders still using archaic expressions that had long since become extinct elsewhere, making the village a sanctuary for words otherwise found only in obscure medieval manuscripts.","at":"前往這座偏僻山村的語言學家驚訝地發現，當地長者仍在使用早已在別處絕跡的古老說法，使這座村莊成了一處庇護所，保存著那些原本只見於冷僻中世紀手稿的詞彙。"},{"w":"rabid","p":"adj.","d":"fanatical, furious, mad.","c":"狂熱的；瘋狂的","s":"The football club's most rabid supporters travel to every match regardless of distance, paint their faces in team colors, and chant loudly for the full ninety minutes. Some have even tattooed the club's crest on their arms. While their fanatical devotion creates an electric atmosphere in the stadium, police occasionally worry that such extreme passion could escalate into violent confrontations with rival fans after particularly important games. Extra officers are therefore deployed.","t":"這支足球俱樂部最狂熱的支持者不論距離多遠都會前往每一場比賽，他們在臉上塗上球隊的顏色，並在整整九十分鐘內大聲吶喊。有些人甚至將俱樂部的隊徽刺在手臂上。雖然他們狂熱的忠誠為球場營造出熱烈的氣氛，警方有時仍擔心，在特別重要的比賽後，這種極端的熱情可能升級為與對手球迷的暴力衝突。因此警方會加派警力。","as":"Fueled by rabid nationalism, the newspaper published vitriolic editorials that maligned foreign merchants and stirred up a frenzy of violence that the police were powerless to quell.","at":"在狂熱民族主義的推波助瀾下，這家報紙刊出一篇篇惡毒的社論，詆毀外國商人，掀起一波警方無力平息的暴力狂潮。"},{"w":"emulate","p":"v.","d":"to strive to equal or surpass.","c":"效仿；努力趕上","s":"Many young entrepreneurs attempt to emulate the success of famous technology founders by adopting their daily routines, reading the same books, and even wearing similar clothing. However, business researchers caution that simply imitating someone else's habits rarely produces comparable results. Genuine achievement, they argue, depends on understanding one's own strengths, identifying unmet needs in the market, and developing original solutions rather than copying established models. Authenticity, in short, matters more than imitation.","t":"許多年輕創業家試圖仿效知名科技創辦人的成功，採用他們的日常作息、閱讀相同的書籍，甚至穿著類似的服裝。然而，商業研究人員提醒，單純模仿他人的習慣很少能帶來相當的成果。他們主張，真正的成就取決於了解自身的長處、找出市場中未被滿足的需求，並發展原創的解決方案，而非複製既有的模式。簡而言之，真誠比模仿更重要。","as":"Aspiring chefs from around the world flock to Kyoto hoping to emulate the impeccable knife work of its master cooks, yet few have the humility to persevere through years of grueling apprenticeship.","at":"世界各地有志成為廚師的人紛紛湧向京都，希望效法當地名廚無可挑剔的刀工，但很少有人具備足夠的謙遜，能熬過多年艱苦的學徒生涯。"},{"w":"facetious","p":"adj.","d":"sarcastic, comical, humorous.","c":"愛開玩笑的；不正經的","s":"During the serious board meeting about potential layoffs, the manager made a facetious remark suggesting that the company could save money by replacing all employees with robots. Although he intended the comment as a joke, many staff members found it deeply offensive given the circumstances. The human resources director later reminded him that humor, however lighthearted, must always be appropriate to the situation and sensitive to people's genuine anxieties. He apologized the next morning.","t":"在討論可能裁員的嚴肅董事會議上，這位經理開了一句不正經的玩笑，說公司可以把所有員工換成機器人來省錢。雖然他的本意只是開玩笑，但在當時的情況下，許多員工覺得這句話極具冒犯性。人資主管事後提醒他，幽默無論多麼輕鬆，都必須合乎場合，並顧及人們真實的焦慮。他隔天早上便道歉了。","as":"When the senator made a facetious remark about solving the budget crisis by selling the national parks, some listeners missed the levity and reacted with consternation, while others were incredulous that he would joke about so grave a matter.","at":"參議員開玩笑說要賣掉國家公園來解決預算危機時，有些聽眾沒聽出其中的戲謔而大感驚慌，另一些人則不敢相信他竟會拿如此嚴肅的事情說笑。"},{"w":"salubrious","p":"adj.","d":"healthful, wholesome.","c":"有益健康的","s":"In the nineteenth century, wealthy city residents suffering from respiratory illnesses often traveled to mountain resorts, believing the salubrious climate would restore their health. Doctors prescribed fresh air, clean water, and gentle exercise as treatments for conditions ranging from tuberculosis to nervous exhaustion. Although modern medicine has replaced many of these remedies, researchers acknowledge that clean environments genuinely contribute to physical and psychological wellbeing. Mountain towns still market themselves this way.","t":"十九世紀時，罹患呼吸道疾病的富裕城市居民常前往山區度假勝地，相信當地有益健康的氣候能讓他們恢復健康。醫生開出新鮮空氣、潔淨的水和溫和運動的處方，用來治療從肺結核到神經衰竭等各種病症。雖然現代醫學已取代了其中許多療法，研究人員仍承認，乾淨的環境確實有助於身心健康。山區小鎮至今仍以此作為宣傳賣點。","as":"Victorian physicians often sent patients with tuberculosis to breathe the salubrious mountain air of Switzerland, believing that tranquil surroundings would nurture recovery from a malady that sooty industrial cities only aggravated.","at":"維多利亞時代的醫生常讓結核病患到瑞士山區呼吸有益健康的空氣，相信寧靜的環境有助於病體復原，而煤煙瀰漫的工業城市只會使這種疾病惡化。"}]},{"unit":33,"cards":[{"w":"complacent","p":"adj.","d":"self-satisfied.","c":"自滿的；得意自滿的","s":"After winning the championship three years in a row, the team became complacent, skipping extra training sessions and assuming that victory was guaranteed. Their coach repeatedly warned them that rival clubs were improving rapidly, but the players ignored his advice. When a young, determined opponent defeated them decisively in the opening round of the tournament, the shocked athletes finally realized that their smug overconfidence had cost them everything they had worked for.","t":"在連續三年贏得冠軍後，這支球隊變得自滿，不再參加額外的訓練，並認定勝利是理所當然的。教練一再警告他們，對手球隊正在迅速進步，但球員們對他的建議置若罔聞。當一支年輕、充滿決心的對手在錦標賽首輪以懸殊比分擊敗他們時，震驚的球員們才終於明白，他們自以為是的過度自信讓他們失去了所有努力的成果。","as":"Having dominated the smartphone market for years, the company grew complacent, belittling its fledgling rivals until their innovative designs triggered a catastrophic slump in its sales.","at":"這家公司稱霸智慧型手機市場多年後變得自滿，一再輕視羽翼未豐的競爭對手，直到對方的創新設計讓它的銷量出現災難性的暴跌。"},{"w":"somber","p":"adj.","d":"gloomy, sad.","c":"憂鬱的；昏暗的","s":"The mood inside the courtroom was somber as the jury announced its verdict in the tragic case. Family members of the victims sat silently, some quietly weeping, while others stared at the floor in grief. Even the lawyers, usually animated and confident, spoke in hushed, serious tones. Outside, dark clouds gathered over the city, and many reporters later remarked that the gloomy weather seemed to mirror the heavy atmosphere of that unforgettable afternoon.","t":"陪審團宣布這起悲劇案件的判決時，法庭內的氣氛十分沉重。受害者的家屬靜靜地坐著，有些人低聲啜泣，有些人則悲痛地盯著地板。就連平常神采奕奕、充滿自信的律師們，也以低沉、嚴肅的語調說話。法院外，烏雲籠罩著城市，許多記者事後表示，陰沉的天氣彷彿映照出那個難忘午後的沉重氛圍。","as":"The mood at the memorial ceremony was somber, as mourners offered condolences to the bereft families and a lone trumpeter played a doleful melody beneath the overcast sky.","at":"追悼儀式的氣氛肅穆哀傷，弔唁者向痛失至親的家屬致上慰問，一名號手獨自在陰沉的天空下吹奏一曲悲淒的旋律。"},{"w":"debilitate","p":"v.","d":"to weaken.","c":"使衰弱","s":"Chronic sleep deprivation can gradually debilitate even the healthiest individuals, reducing their physical strength, mental sharpness, and resistance to infection. Medical studies show that adults who regularly sleep fewer than six hours per night experience impaired memory, slower reaction times, and a significantly weakened immune system. Over time, this persistent exhaustion may contribute to serious conditions such as heart disease and depression, which is why doctors increasingly treat adequate rest as essential.","t":"長期睡眠不足會逐漸使最健康的人變得虛弱，降低他們的體力、思緒的敏銳度以及對感染的抵抗力。醫學研究顯示，經常每晚睡眠不足六小時的成年人，會出現記憶力受損、反應變慢，以及免疫系統明顯減弱的情況。久而久之，這種持續的疲憊可能導致心臟病與憂鬱症等嚴重疾病，這也是醫生越來越將充足休息視為必要條件的原因。","as":"Months of privation during the siege began to debilitate the garrison, leaving many soldiers so emaciated and lethargic that they could barely lift their rifles when the enemy launched its final assault.","at":"圍城期間長達數月的物資匱乏逐漸拖垮了守軍，許多士兵骨瘦如柴、萎靡不振，當敵軍發動最後攻擊時，他們幾乎連步槍都舉不起來。"},{"w":"impetuous","p":"adj.","d":"impulsive.","c":"衝動的；魯莽的","s":"In an impetuous moment, the young investor withdrew his entire savings and bought shares in a company he had heard about only that morning on social media. He did not research its finances, consult an advisor, or consider the risks involved. Within a week, the stock had collapsed, and he had lost nearly everything. The painful experience taught him that impulsive financial decisions, however exciting they may feel, rarely lead to lasting success.","t":"在一時衝動之下，這位年輕投資人提領了全部積蓄，買進一家他當天早上才在社群媒體上聽說的公司股票。他既沒有研究該公司的財務狀況、諮詢理財顧問，也沒有考慮其中的風險。不到一週，股價便崩盤，他幾乎血本無歸。這次慘痛的經驗讓他明白，衝動的理財決定無論感覺多麼刺激，都很少能帶來長久的成功。","as":"Ignoring his mentor's efforts to admonish him, the impetuous young investor poured his entire inheritance into a dubious start-up, a decision he would rue when the company collapsed within months.","at":"這位衝動的年輕投資人無視導師的再三告誡，把全部遺產投入一家前景可疑的新創公司；幾個月後公司倒閉，他才為這個決定懊悔不已。"},{"w":"occult","p":"adj.","d":"mysterious, supernatural.","c":"神秘的；超自然的","s":"During the Middle Ages, many people believed that certain scholars possessed occult powers, allowing them to predict the future, communicate with spirits, or transform ordinary metals into gold. Alchemists and astrologers often guarded their mysterious knowledge carefully, recording their experiments in secret codes and symbols. Although modern science has rejected most of these supernatural claims, historians recognize that some alchemical research eventually contributed to the development of chemistry as a legitimate discipline.","t":"在中世紀，許多人相信某些學者擁有神秘的超自然力量，能夠預測未來、與靈魂溝通，或將普通金屬變成黃金。煉金術士與占星師往往小心守護他們神秘的知識，以秘密的密碼和符號記錄實驗。雖然現代科學已否定了大多數這類超自然的說法，歷史學家仍承認，部分煉金術研究最終促成了化學發展成為一門正式的學科。","as":"In medieval Europe, comets were widely regarded as harbingers of disaster, and astrologers claimed occult powers to interpret them, feeding a popular superstition that even sage scholars rarely dared to challenge.","at":"在中世紀歐洲，彗星普遍被視為災禍的前兆，占星師自稱擁有解讀彗星的神祕力量，助長了一種連睿智學者都鮮少敢挑戰的民間迷信。"},{"w":"discreet","p":"adj.","d":"careful, cautious, prudent.","c":"謹慎的；言行慎重的","s":"Personal assistants to celebrities must be extremely discreet, since they regularly encounter private information about their employers' health, finances, and relationships. Revealing such details to journalists or posting them online could destroy both their employer's reputation and their own careers. Most assistants sign strict confidentiality agreements before starting work. Experienced professionals in this field emphasize that trust, tact, and careful silence are far more valuable than any technical skill they possess.","t":"名人的私人助理必須極為謹慎，因為他們經常接觸到雇主關於健康、財務與感情的私人資訊。若將這些細節透露給記者或發布到網路上，可能會同時毀掉雇主的名聲與自己的職業生涯。大多數助理在開始工作前都會簽署嚴格的保密協議。這個領域經驗豐富的專業人士強調，信任、圓融與謹慎的沉默，遠比他們擁有的任何技術能力都更有價值。","as":"Because the negotiations were fraught with tension, the ambassador remained discreet, refusing to comment on rumors so as not to jeopardize a fragile truce that both adversaries had only reluctantly accepted.","at":"由於談判氣氛緊繃，大使始終言行謹慎，拒絕對任何傳聞發表評論，以免危及這份雙方敵手都只是勉強接受的脆弱停戰協議。"},{"w":"foment","p":"v.","d":"to stir up, instigate.","c":"煽動；挑起","s":"Government officials accused foreign agents of using fake social media accounts to foment unrest among the country's citizens before the national election. The anonymous accounts spread inflammatory rumors, exaggerated existing tensions between different communities, and encouraged people to join violent demonstrations. Cybersecurity investigators eventually traced hundreds of these profiles to a single organization overseas. The discovery prompted urgent debates about how democracies can protect themselves from deliberate efforts to provoke division.","t":"政府官員指控外國特工在全國大選前利用假的社群媒體帳號，在國內民眾之間煽動動亂。這些匿名帳號散布煽動性的謠言、誇大不同族群間既有的緊張關係，並鼓吹民眾參加暴力示威。資安調查人員最終將數百個這類帳號追查到海外的單一組織。這項發現引發了緊迫的辯論：民主國家該如何保護自己，免於遭受刻意挑起分裂的行動。","as":"Historians argue that covert pamphlets circulated in London coffeehouses helped foment rebellion, spreading invective against the king among a populace already rife with resentment over heavy taxes.","at":"歷史學家認為，在倫敦咖啡館中暗中流傳的小冊子助長了叛亂，在早已因重稅而怨聲載道的民眾之間散播對國王的辱罵與抨擊。"},{"w":"glean","p":"v.","d":"to gather, collect.","c":"收集；點滴蒐集","s":"By carefully examining thousands of ancient pottery fragments, archaeologists were able to glean valuable information about the daily lives of people who lived in the region three thousand years ago. Food residues revealed what they ate, while decorative patterns suggested trading relationships with distant cultures. Although no written records survived, these small clues, gathered piece by piece, allowed researchers to reconstruct a surprisingly detailed picture of an otherwise forgotten civilization.","t":"透過仔細檢驗數千片古代陶器碎片，考古學家得以蒐集到關於三千年前居住在該地區人們日常生活的寶貴資訊。食物殘留物揭示了他們吃些什麼，裝飾圖案則暗示了與遙遠文化之間的貿易關係。雖然沒有任何文字紀錄留存下來，但這些一點一滴蒐集而來的小線索，讓研究人員得以重建出一幅關於這個原本已被遺忘的文明、細節驚人豐富的圖像。","as":"By analyzing pollen grains still extant in ancient lake sediments, paleoclimatologists can glean surprising insights into prehistoric climates, inferring when forests flourished, when they began to wane, and which species became extinct.","at":"透過分析至今仍保存在古老湖泊沉積物中的花粉粒，古氣候學家能從中蒐集到關於史前氣候的驚人線索，推斷森林何時繁盛、何時開始衰退，以及哪些物種已經滅絕。"},{"w":"quarry","p":"n.","d":"something hunted or pursued.","c":"獵物；追捕目標","s":"The hungry wolf pack tracked its quarry through the snowy forest for nearly six hours, following the deer's footprints and scent with remarkable patience. The wolves worked together strategically, with some members circling ahead to block potential escape routes while others maintained steady pressure from behind. Wildlife biologists who observed the hunt noted that such cooperative behavior dramatically increases the pack's chances of success, particularly during harsh winters when food becomes scarce.","t":"飢餓的狼群在雪林中追蹤牠們的獵物將近六個小時，以驚人的耐心循著鹿的足跡與氣味前進。狼群有策略地合作，部分成員繞到前方封鎖可能的逃脫路線，其餘成員則從後方持續施壓。觀察這場狩獵的野生動物生物學家指出，這種合作行為能大幅提高狼群的成功機率，尤其是在食物匱乏的嚴冬。","as":"The lithe cheetah stalks its quarry through the tall grass with furtive patience, then surges forward at speeds that leave even the swiftest gazelle vulnerable.","at":"身形矯健的獵豹在高草叢中悄悄地、耐心地跟蹤獵物，接著猛然衝刺，速度之快，連最敏捷的瞪羚也難以招架。"},{"w":"slovenly","p":"adj.","d":"disorderly, careless.","c":"邋遢的；馬虎的","s":"The restaurant failed its health inspection because of its slovenly kitchen, where inspectors found dirty dishes piled in the sink, spoiled food left uncovered on counters, and grease coating nearly every surface. Employees admitted that cleaning routines had been ignored for weeks due to staff shortages. The owner was ordered to close the business temporarily until the premises met basic hygiene standards. Local residents were shocked by the news. Many vowed never to return.","t":"這家餐廳未通過衛生檢查，原因是廚房髒亂不堪：檢查人員發現水槽裡堆滿髒碗盤、壞掉的食物未加蓋地放在流理台上，而且幾乎每個表面都覆蓋著油垢。員工承認，由於人手不足，清潔程序已被忽視好幾週。業主被勒令暫時停業，直到場所符合基本衛生標準為止。當地居民對這則新聞感到十分震驚。許多人發誓再也不會光顧。","as":"The inspector's report castigated the restaurant for its slovenly kitchen, citing grease-stained counters and rotting produce as flagrant violations of health codes that the owner had blatantly ignored.","at":"檢查員的報告嚴厲譴責這家餐廳廚房髒亂邋遢，指出沾滿油垢的流理台和腐爛的蔬果明顯違反衛生法規，而業主卻公然置之不理。"},{"w":"abjure","p":"v.","d":"to renounce, abstain from.","c":"發誓放棄；棄絕","s":"After years of struggling with his health, the famous novelist publicly vowed to abjure alcohol and tobacco for the rest of his life. He explained in a heartfelt interview that his doctors had warned him about serious liver damage and breathing problems. Friends were initially skeptical, since he had made similar promises before. This time, however, he kept his word, and his later novels were widely praised as his finest work.","t":"在與健康問題搏鬥多年之後，這位知名小說家公開發誓，餘生將戒絕菸酒。他在一次真誠的訪談中解釋，醫生曾警告他有嚴重的肝臟損傷與呼吸問題。朋友們起初抱持懷疑，因為他以前也做過類似的承諾。然而這一次，他信守了諾言，而他後期的小說被普遍讚譽為其最出色的作品。","as":"After witnessing the havoc that alcohol had wreaked on his family, the novelist vowed to abjure drinking entirely, adopting an abstemious lifestyle that his more profligate friends found baffling.","at":"目睹酒精對家人造成的浩劫後，這位小說家發誓徹底戒酒，從此過著節制的生活，令他那些揮霍無度的朋友們大惑不解。"},{"w":"reproach","p":"v.","d":"to rebuke, reprimand.","c":"責備；斥責","s":"The manager did not reproach the new employee harshly for the costly mistake; instead, she calmly explained what had gone wrong and how to prevent similar errors in the future. She believed that constant criticism only made workers anxious and afraid to take initiative. Her supportive approach proved effective, as the employee quickly regained confidence and eventually became one of the most reliable and innovative members of the entire department.","t":"經理並沒有為這位新員工造成的昂貴失誤而嚴厲責備他；相反地，她冷靜地解釋哪裡出了錯，以及未來如何避免類似的錯誤。她相信不斷的批評只會讓員工焦慮，不敢主動做事。她支持性的做法被證明十分有效，這位員工很快便重拾信心，最終成為整個部門中最可靠、最具創新力的成員之一。","as":"Rather than reproach the timorous young pianist for the mistakes in her recital, her teacher praised her courage, knowing that harsh criticism would only reinforce the inhibitions that impeded her progress.","at":"老師沒有責備這位膽怯的年輕鋼琴手在獨奏會上的失誤，反而稱讚她的勇氣，因為老師明白，嚴厲的批評只會加深阻礙她進步的心理拘束。"},{"w":"penitent","p":"adj.","d":"regretful, confessing guilt.","c":"懺悔的；悔過的","s":"Standing before the judge, the penitent young man admitted that he had stolen money from the elderly neighbor who had once helped his family. With tears in his eyes, he apologized sincerely and promised to repay every dollar through community service and part-time work. Moved by his genuine remorse and clean record, the judge sentenced him to probation rather than prison, hoping the experience would encourage him to rebuild his life responsibly.","t":"站在法官面前，這位懺悔的年輕人承認自己偷了曾經幫助過他家人的年長鄰居的錢。他含著眼淚真誠地道歉，並承諾會透過社區服務與打工償還每一塊錢。法官被他真誠的悔意與清白的紀錄所打動，判處他緩刑而非入獄，希望這次經驗能激勵他負責任地重建人生。","as":"Appearing penitent before the judge, the former mayor acknowledged his complicity in the bribery scheme and implored the court for leniency, though many observers doubted that his remorse was sincere.","at":"前市長在法官面前一副悔悟的模樣，承認自己參與了這起賄賂案，並懇求法庭從輕發落，但許多旁觀者懷疑他的悔意是否真誠。"},{"w":"evanescent","p":"adj.","d":"fleeting, passing, momentary.","c":"瞬息即逝的","s":"Photographers who specialize in capturing rainbows must work quickly, since these evanescentedisplays of color often vanish within minutes as sunlight shifts and rain clouds move. Experienced professionals study weather patterns carefully, positioning themselves in advance where conditions are most favorable. Even so, many spend entire days waiting for a single perfect moment. They insist that the fleeting nature of rainbows is precisely what makes a successful photograph so rewarding and emotionally powerful.","t":"專門捕捉彩虹的攝影師必須動作迅速，因為隨著陽光變化與雨雲移動，這些瞬息即逝的色彩往往在幾分鐘內就消失了。經驗豐富的專業人士會仔細研究天氣型態，事先在條件最有利的地點就位。即便如此，許多人仍花上一整天等待一個完美的瞬間。他們堅稱，正是彩虹短暫易逝的特性，才讓一張成功的照片如此令人滿足且動人心弦。","as":"Intrepid photographers who chase the aurora must stay vigilant through frigid nights, since its evanescent ribbons of color may last only minutes, and a single cloudy sky can render the entire peregrination fruitless.","at":"追逐極光的無畏攝影師必須在嚴寒的夜裡時刻保持警覺，因為那轉瞬即逝的彩色光帶可能只持續幾分鐘，而只要碰上一個陰天，整趟長途跋涉就可能徒勞無功。"},{"w":"tantamount","p":"adj.","d":"equivalent, identical.","c":"同等的；等於","s":"Environmental activists argued that the government's decision to approve oil drilling in the protected wilderness was tantamount to abandoning its climate commitments entirely. They pointed out that the project would release millions of tons of carbon dioxide and destroy habitats for several endangered species. Officials insisted that the development was necessary for economic growth, but critics maintained that the choice was essentially equivalent to breaking promises made to future generations.","t":"環保人士主張，政府批准在保護區荒野鑽探石油的決定，等同於完全放棄其氣候承諾。他們指出，該計畫將釋放數百萬噸二氧化碳，並摧毀數種瀕危物種的棲息地。官員堅稱這項開發對經濟成長而言是必要的，但批評者仍認為，這個選擇實質上等於違背了對後代子孫的承諾。","as":"Environmental groups argued that lifting the prohibition on logging would be tantamount to signing a death warrant for the region's orangutans, whose habitat was already being obliterated at an inexorable pace.","at":"環保團體主張，解除伐木禁令無異於對該地區的紅毛猩猩宣判死刑，因為牠們的棲息地早已以無法遏止的速度遭到摧毀。"},{"w":"propensity","p":"n.","d":"disposition, inclination, bent.","c":"傾向；習性","s":"Psychologists have long studied why some people have a greater propensity for taking risks than others. Research suggests that genetic factors, childhood experiences, and even brain chemistry all influence this natural inclination. Individuals with a strong tendency toward risk-taking are more likely to become entrepreneurs, extreme athletes, or explorers, but they also face higher rates of accidents and financial losses. Understanding these patterns can help people make wiser decisions about their futures.","t":"心理學家長期研究為何有些人比其他人更傾向於冒險。研究顯示，遺傳因素、童年經歷，甚至大腦化學作用，都會影響這種天生的傾向。具有強烈冒險傾向的人更可能成為創業家、極限運動員或探險家，但他們也面臨較高的事故與財務損失機率。了解這些模式能幫助人們對自己的未來做出更明智的決定。","as":"Psychologists have found that adolescents show a greater propensity for risk-taking than adults do, a phenomenon that some researchers attribute to innate neurological factors rather than to the extrinsic influence of peers.","at":"心理學家發現，青少年比成年人更傾向於冒險，有些研究者將這種現象歸因於與生俱來的神經因素，而非來自同儕的外在影響。"},{"w":"wary","p":"adj.","d":"watchful, shrewd.","c":"機警的；謹慎的","s":"After losing money in an online scam last year, the retired teacher became extremely wary of unfamiliar emails and phone calls requesting personal information. She now carefully verifies every message with her bank before responding and refuses to click on any suspicious links. Her grandchildren helped her install security software and taught her to recognize common warning signs. Consumer protection agencies encourage all older adults to adopt similar cautious habits online.","t":"去年在網路詐騙中損失金錢後，這位退休教師對要求提供個人資料的陌生電子郵件與電話變得極為警惕。她現在在回應任何訊息之前，都會先仔細向銀行查證，並拒絕點擊任何可疑的連結。孫子女幫她安裝了防毒軟體，並教她辨識常見的警訊。消費者保護機構鼓勵所有年長者在網路上養成類似的謹慎習慣。","as":"Having once been the dupe of a charlatan who sold him a counterfeit painting, the collector became wary of dealers offering bargains that seemed too good to be true, and he now insists that experts attest to the provenance of every canvas he buys.","at":"這位收藏家曾經上過一名江湖騙子的當，買到一幅贗品，從此對那些好得令人難以置信的便宜貨保持警惕，如今堅持每幅購入的畫作都要由專家證明其來源。"},{"w":"allay","p":"v.","d":"to calm, soothe.","c":"減輕；平息","s":"To allay public fears about the safety of the new nuclear power plant, the energy company invited journalists, scientists, and local residents to tour the facility. Engineers explained the multiple backup systems designed to prevent accidents and answered every question patiently. Independent experts also published a detailed report confirming that radiation levels remained well below international safety limits. These transparent efforts gradually reassured the community, and opposition to the project declined significantly.","t":"為了平息民眾對新核電廠安全性的疑慮，能源公司邀請記者、科學家與當地居民參觀廠區。工程師說明了為防止事故而設計的多重備援系統，並耐心回答每一個問題。獨立專家也發表了一份詳細報告，確認輻射量遠低於國際安全標準。這些透明的做法逐漸讓社區安心，對該計畫的反對聲浪也大幅減少。","as":"To allay the fears of fretful residents after the chemical spill, officials released the results of independent water tests, which showed that no lethal contaminants had permeated the town's underground aquifer.","at":"化學物質外洩事件後，為了平息焦慮居民的恐懼，官員公布了獨立水質檢測的結果，顯示並沒有致命的污染物滲入鎮上的地下含水層。"},{"w":"deter","p":"v.","d":"to hinder, discourage.","c":"威懾；阻止","s":"City officials installed bright lighting and security cameras throughout the park to deter criminals from targeting evening joggers and dog walkers. Before the improvements, several robberies had occurred along poorly lit paths, and many residents had stopped visiting after sunset. Within months, reported crimes dropped by more than half. Criminologists explain that visible security measures discourage offenders because they significantly increase the likelihood of being identified and arrested. Residents now enjoy evening walks again.","t":"市府官員在整座公園裝設明亮的照明與監視器，以嚇阻罪犯鎖定傍晚慢跑和遛狗的民眾。在改善之前，照明不佳的小徑曾發生數起搶案，許多居民在日落後便不再前往公園。短短幾個月內，通報的犯罪案件減少了一半以上。犯罪學家解釋，顯眼的安全措施之所以能嚇阻犯罪者，是因為它們大幅提高了被辨識與逮捕的可能性。居民們如今又能享受傍晚散步了。","as":"City planners hoped that installing brighter streetlights would deter vandals, but the measure proved ineffectual because graffiti remained rampant in the murky alleys that the new lights could not reach.","at":"都市規畫者原本希望加裝更明亮的路燈能嚇阻破壞者，但這項措施成效不彰，因為在新路燈照不到的陰暗小巷裡，塗鴉依然猖獗。"},{"w":"connoisseur","p":"n.","d":"expert.","c":"鑑賞家；行家","s":"A true connoisseur of Taiwanese tea can identify the region, altitude, and even the harvest season of a leaf simply by tasting a single cup. Such experts spend decades visiting mountain plantations, learning traditional processing techniques, and comparing thousands of samples. Their refined palates allow them to detect subtle differences in aroma, sweetness, and texture that ordinary drinkers would never notice. Tea farmers greatly value their expert opinions when pricing premium harvests.","t":"真正的台灣茶鑑賞家只要品嚐一杯茶，就能辨識出茶葉的產區、海拔，甚至採收季節。這類專家花費數十年造訪山區茶園、學習傳統製茶技術，並比較數千種茶樣。他們敏銳的味覺能察覺香氣、甜度與口感上的細微差異，而這些都是一般飲茶者永遠不會注意到的。茶農在為高級茶定價時，非常重視他們的專業意見。","as":"A true connoisseur of tea can discern subtle nuances of aroma and flavor that a casual drinker would never perceive, readily distinguishing a rare high-mountain oolong from a nondescript supermarket blend.","at":"真正的品茶行家能辨別香氣與風味中一般飲茶者永遠察覺不到的細微差異，輕易分辨出珍稀的高山烏龍茶與超市裡平淡無奇的混合茶。"}]},{"unit":34,"cards":[{"w":"site","p":"n.","d":"location.","c":"地點；遺址","s":"Archaeologists announced that construction workers had accidentally discovered an ancient burial site while digging the foundations for a new shopping mall. The location contained dozens of well-preserved skeletons, pottery, and bronze tools dating back nearly two thousand years. Construction was immediately suspended so that experts could excavate the area carefully. City officials are now debating whether to relocate the mall entirely and transform the historic location into a public museum.","t":"考古學家宣布，建築工人在為一座新購物中心挖掘地基時，意外發現了一處古代墓葬遺址。該地點埋有數十具保存良好的骸骨、陶器與青銅工具，年代可追溯至將近兩千年前。工程隨即暫停，讓專家能仔細挖掘該區域。市府官員目前正在討論是否將購物中心整個遷址，並把這處歷史地點改建為公共博物館。","as":"Archaeologists excavating the site of a Bronze Age settlement unearthed a hidden cache of tools and other artifacts, suggesting that its once nomadic inhabitants had gradually adopted a settled agricultural life.","at":"考古學家在一處青銅時代聚落遺址進行挖掘時，發現了一批藏匿的工具與其他文物，顯示原本逐水草而居的居民逐漸轉向定居的農耕生活。"},{"w":"vigil","p":"n.","d":"wakeful watching.","c":"守夜；監視","s":"When the young climber failed to return from the mountain, his parents kept a lonely vigil at the base camp, refusing to sleep while rescue teams searched through the freezing night. They sat beside a small fire, watching the dark slopes for any sign of flashlights. Shortly before dawn, radio messages confirmed that he had been found alive, sheltered in a small cave. His exhausted parents finally wept with relief.","t":"當年輕的登山者未能從山上歸來時，他的父母在基地營孤單地守夜，在救難隊於冰冷夜裡搜尋時拒絕入睡。他們坐在一小堆營火旁，望著漆黑的山坡，尋找任何手電筒的光影。黎明前不久，無線電訊息證實他被找到時仍然活著，躲在一個小山洞裡。精疲力竭的父母終於如釋重負地哭了出來。","as":"Hundreds of relatives kept a tearful vigil at the mouth of the collapsed mine throughout the night, a poignant scene of families who refused to succumb to despair even as the rescue effort began to falter.","at":"數百名家屬徹夜守在坍塌礦坑的入口，含淚守候；即使救援行動開始受挫，這些家庭仍不肯向絕望低頭，場面令人心酸。"},{"w":"cumbersome","p":"adj.","d":"unwieldy, burdensome.","c":"笨重的；累贅的","s":"Early mobile phones were so cumbersome that users often carried them in special bags rather than in their pockets. Weighing nearly a kilogram, these bulky devices required large batteries that lasted only about thirty minutes of conversation. Despite their awkward size, they were considered symbols of wealth and status during the 1980s. Today, engineers marvel at how dramatically technology has shrunk, allowing far more powerful devices to fit comfortably in our hands.","t":"早期的行動電話非常笨重，使用者常常必須用特製的袋子攜帶，而不是放在口袋裡。這些龐大的裝置重達將近一公斤，需要大型電池，而且通話時間只有大約三十分鐘。儘管體積笨拙，它們在1980年代仍被視為財富與地位的象徵。如今，工程師驚嘆科技縮小的幅度之大，讓功能更強大的裝置能輕鬆地握在我們手中。","as":"The first electronic computers were so cumbersome that a single mammoth machine filled an entire room, yet steady refinements to each component eventually allowed engineers to modify the design into devices that fit on a desk.","at":"最早的電子計算機極其笨重，一台龐然大物就塞滿整個房間，但工程師持續改良每一個元件，最終得以修改設計，把它變成能放在桌上的裝置。"},{"w":"interrogate","p":"v.","d":"to question.","c":"審問；質問","s":"Detectives spent nearly eight hours attempting to interrogate the suspect about his whereabouts on the night of the burglary. They asked detailed questions about his movements, his companions, and the stolen jewelry discovered in his car. The man repeatedly changed his story, contradicting earlier statements and growing increasingly nervous. Eventually, when investigators presented fingerprint evidence from the crime scene, he admitted his involvement and agreed to identify his accomplices. The trial began two months later.","t":"警探花了將近八個小時審問嫌犯，追問他在竊案當晚的行蹤。他們詳細詢問他的行動、同伴，以及在他車上發現的失竊珠寶。這名男子一再改變說詞，與先前的陳述自相矛盾，也變得越來越緊張。最終，當調查人員出示犯罪現場的指紋證據時，他承認涉案，並同意指認共犯。審判於兩個月後開始。","as":"Detectives continued to interrogate the alleged accomplice for hours, hoping he would reveal where the stolen paintings were hidden, but the reticent suspect offered only terse, evasive answers.","at":"警探們連續數小時審問這名涉嫌的共犯，希望他供出失竊畫作的藏匿地點，但這名沉默寡言的嫌犯只給出簡短而閃爍其詞的回答。"},{"w":"divulge","p":"v.","d":"to disclose, reveal.","c":"洩露；透露","s":"The journalist refused to divulge the identity of her confidential source, even when a judge threatened her with imprisonment. She argued that revealing the name would endanger the whistleblower's life and discourage future informants from exposing corruption. Press freedom organizations around the world supported her decision, describing it as a courageous defense of democratic principles. After three weeks in jail, she was released when prosecutors finally dropped their demands. Her book became a bestseller.","t":"這位記者拒絕透露其機密消息來源的身分，即使法官威脅要將她監禁也不改變心意。她主張，公開這個名字將危及吹哨者的生命，並使未來的線人不敢揭發貪腐。世界各地的新聞自由組織都支持她的決定，稱之為捍衛民主原則的勇敢之舉。入獄三週後，檢察官終於撤回要求，她隨即獲釋。她的書成了暢銷書。","as":"The whistle-blower agreed to divulge details of the company's surreptitious payments to regulators only after prosecutors promised her amnesty, since her own minor role in the scheme might otherwise have made her culpable as well.","at":"這名吹哨者直到檢察官承諾給予她特赦，才同意透露公司暗中付款給監管人員的細節，因為若非如此，她在這起計畫中扮演的小角色也可能讓她難辭其咎。"},{"w":"fluctuate","p":"v.","d":"to shift, alternate.","c":"波動；起伏","s":"Temperatures in desert regions can fluctuatedramatically within a single day, rising above forty degrees Celsius at noon and falling close to freezing after sunset. The dry air and lack of cloud cover allow heat to escape rapidly once the sun disappears. Travelers who underestimate these extreme variations often suffer from dehydration during the day and hypothermia at night. Experienced guides therefore recommend packing both lightweight clothing and heavy blankets.","t":"沙漠地區的氣溫在一天之內可能劇烈波動，中午時升到攝氏四十度以上，日落後又降到接近冰點。乾燥的空氣與缺乏雲層覆蓋，使熱量在太陽消失後迅速散失。低估這種極端變化的旅人，常在白天脫水、夜間失溫。因此，經驗豐富的嚮導建議同時攜帶輕便衣物與厚重毛毯。","as":"Because global coffee prices fluctuate sharply whenever adverse weather strikes Brazil, small growers in Central America who depend on a single crop remain perpetually susceptible to financial ruin, a plight that local cooperatives are trying to ease.","at":"由於每當巴西遭遇惡劣天氣，全球咖啡價格就會劇烈波動，中美洲仰賴單一作物維生的小農始終容易陷入財務困境，而當地合作社正努力改善這種處境。"},{"w":"unmitigated","p":"adj.","d":"unrelieved, as bad as can be.","c":"十足的；未減輕的","s":"Critics described the expensive film as an unmitigatededisaster, pointing to its confusing plot, wooden acting, and embarrassing special effects. Despite a budget exceeding two hundred million dollars, the movie earned only a small fraction of its costs at the box office. Not a single reviewer found anything positive to say about it. Studio executives later admitted that the project had been a complete failure from its earliest stages of production.","t":"評論家形容這部昂貴的電影是一場徹頭徹尾的災難，指出其劇情混亂、演技呆板，特效更是令人尷尬。儘管預算超過兩億美元，這部電影的票房收入只有成本的一小部分。沒有任何一位影評人說得出它的優點。片廠高層事後承認，這個計畫從製作初期就是一次徹底的失敗。","as":"Critics called the city's new stadium an unmitigated fiasco, noting that the profligate project had cost triple the original estimate and left behind a gaudy monument that now stands empty most of the year.","at":"批評者稱這座城市的新體育場是一場徹頭徹尾的慘敗，指出這項揮霍無度的工程花費高達原先預估的三倍，最後只留下一座一年中大半時間都空無一人的俗麗建築。"},{"w":"commodious","p":"adj.","d":"large, spacious.","c":"寬敞的","s":"After years of living in a cramped studio apartment, the young couple finally moved into a commodious house with four bedrooms, a large kitchen, and a garden. For the first time, each of their children had a private room, and the family could invite relatives for holiday dinners without feeling crowded. Friends who visited were impressed by the spacious living room, which easily accommodated twenty guests during their housewarming party.","t":"在狹小的套房公寓住了多年後，這對年輕夫婦終於搬進一棟寬敞的房子，有四間臥室、一間大廚房和一座花園。他們的每個孩子第一次擁有自己的房間，全家人也能邀請親戚來吃節日晚餐而不覺得擁擠。來訪的朋友對寬敞的客廳印象深刻，在喬遷派對上輕鬆容納了二十位賓客。","as":"The tycoon's commodious mansion, with its forty bedrooms and sumptuous ballroom, was a monument to the opulence of the Gilded Age, an era when ostentatious displays of wealth were in vogue among the elite.","at":"這位大亨的宅邸寬敞氣派，擁有四十間臥室和富麗堂皇的舞廳，堪稱鍍金時代奢華風氣的象徵；在那個年代，炫耀財富正是上流社會的流行風尚。"},{"w":"antiquated","p":"adj.","d":"out-of-date, obsolete.","c":"過時的；陳舊的","s":"The hospital's antiquated equipment, much of which had been purchased forty years earlier, frequently broke down and produced unreliable test results. Doctors complained that the old machines slowed diagnoses and endangered patients who needed urgent treatment. After a local newspaper published a series of reports about the problem, generous donors contributed millions of dollars to replace the obsolete devices with modern technology, dramatically improving the quality of medical care. Patients noticed the difference immediately.","t":"這家醫院陳舊的設備大多是四十年前購入的，經常故障，也產生不可靠的檢驗結果。醫生抱怨這些老舊機器拖慢了診斷速度，也危及需要緊急治療的病患。在一家地方報紙針對此問題發表一系列報導後，熱心的捐款人捐出數百萬美元，以現代科技取代這些過時的設備，大幅提升了醫療品質。病患立刻感受到了其中的差異。","as":"Inspectors warned that the hospital's antiquated electrical system, installed nearly a century ago, posed an imminent fire hazard, yet the parsimonious board, citing a paucity of funds, kept postponing the renovation.","at":"檢查人員警告，這家醫院將近百年前裝設的老舊電力系統隨時可能引發火災，然而吝嗇的董事會卻以資金短缺為由，一再延後翻修工程。"},{"w":"disheveled","p":"adj.","d":"disorderly in appearance.","c":"蓬亂的；衣冠不整的","s":"The student arrived at the examination hall looking completely disheveled, with his shirt untucked, his hair sticking out in every direction, and one shoe untied. He explained breathlessly that his alarm had failed and he had run nearly two kilometers to reach the school on time. Although his appearance amused his classmates, he managed to calm down, focus on the questions, and eventually earn one of the highest scores. His teacher was deeply impressed.","t":"這名學生抵達考場時，看起來衣冠不整：襯衫沒塞好、頭髮四處亂翹，還有一隻鞋帶沒綁。他上氣不接下氣地解釋，他的鬧鐘沒響，他跑了將近兩公里才準時趕到學校。雖然他的模樣逗樂了同學們，他仍設法冷靜下來，專心作答，最終拿到了最高分之一。他的老師對此印象深刻。","as":"The scientist emerged from the laboratory disheveled and unshaven after three sleepless nights, but he was jubilant, because his persistent experiments had finally culminated in a landmark discovery.","at":"熬了三個不眠之夜後，這位科學家頭髮蓬亂、鬍子未刮地走出實驗室，但他欣喜若狂，因為他鍥而不捨的實驗終於促成了一項劃時代的發現。"},{"w":"tenacious","p":"adj.","d":"tough, stubborn.","c":"頑強的；堅持不懈的","s":"The tenacious lawyer spent eleven years fighting to prove the innocence of a man who had been wrongly convicted of murder. Despite repeated rejections from appeals courts and threats from powerful officials, she refused to abandon the case. She tracked down forgotten witnesses and demanded new forensic tests. Her persistence finally succeeded when DNA evidence identified the real criminal, and her client walked free after spending two decades in prison.","t":"這位堅持不懈的律師花了十一年奮戰，證明一名被誤判謀殺罪的男子是清白的。儘管一再遭上訴法院駁回，並受到有權勢官員的威脅，她仍拒絕放棄此案。她找出被遺忘的證人，並要求進行新的鑑識檢驗。當DNA證據指認出真正的罪犯時，她的堅持終於獲得成功，她的委託人在獄中度過二十年後重獲自由。","as":"The tenacious journalist spent seven years investigating the pharmaceutical company, refusing to be intimidated by its lawyers' threats until she had gathered incontrovertible evidence that it had concealed the drug's pernicious side effects.","at":"這位頑強的記者花了七年調查這家製藥公司，始終不受其律師的威脅所恫嚇，直到蒐集到無可辯駁的證據，證明該公司隱瞞了藥物的有害副作用。"},{"w":"façade","p":"n.","d":"front, superficial appearance.","c":"正面；假象","s":"Behind the cheerful façade she displayed at work, the talented designer was struggling with loneliness and exhaustion. She smiled during meetings, joked with colleagues, and never missed a deadline, so no one suspected anything was wrong. Only when she took an unexpected leave of absence did her coworkers realize how much she had been hiding. The experience encouraged the company to introduce programs supporting employees' emotional wellbeing. Honest conversations about stress are now encouraged.","t":"在工作中展現的開朗表象背後，這位才華洋溢的設計師其實正承受著孤獨與疲憊。她在會議中面帶微笑、與同事說笑，也從不錯過任何截止期限，因此沒有人察覺任何異狀。直到她突然請假，同事們才意識到她隱藏了多少心事。這次經驗促使公司推出支持員工情緒健康的方案。如今公司鼓勵員工坦誠談論壓力。","as":"Behind the façade of amicable cooperation that the two executives presented to reporters lay a rivalry steeped in mutual suspicion, a feud that insiders feared would eventually dismantle the entire partnership.","at":"兩位主管在記者面前展現出友好合作的表象，背後卻是一段充滿相互猜忌的較勁關係，知情人士擔心這場明爭暗鬥終將瓦解整個合作夥伴關係。"},{"w":"asinine","p":"adj.","d":"stupid, silly.","c":"愚蠢的","s":"The committee rejected the proposal to paint every school building bright pink, calling the suggestion asinine and a complete waste of public money. Parents complained that the idea had no educational value and would make the schools look ridiculous. The council member who proposed it later admitted that he had not consulted teachers or students beforehand. Local newspapers mocked the foolish plan for weeks, and it quickly became a popular joke.","t":"委員會否決了將每棟校舍都漆成亮粉紅色的提案，稱此建議愚蠢至極，完全是浪費公帑。家長們抱怨這個點子毫無教育價值，只會讓學校看起來很可笑。提出此案的市議員事後承認，他事先並未諮詢老師或學生的意見。地方報紙連續數週嘲諷這個愚蠢的計畫，它很快便成了眾人茶餘飯後的笑話。","as":"Engineers scoffed at the asinine proposal to end the city's traffic jams by banning all left turns, arguing that such an arbitrary rule would merely shift the gridlock onto side streets and compound the problem.","at":"工程師們嘲笑那項以全面禁止左轉來解決市區塞車的荒唐提案，認為如此武斷的規定只會把車潮轉移到小街巷，讓問題雪上加霜。"},{"w":"grimace","p":"n.","d":"facial expression of disgust or pain.","c":"鬼臉；痛苦的表情","s":"When the child tasted the bitter medicine, her face twisted into a dramatic grimace, and she immediately reached for a glass of juice. Her mother laughed but insisted that she finish the entire spoonful. Pharmaceutical companies have long struggled with this problem, since many effective medicines have unpleasant flavors. Researchers are now developing new coatings and sweeteners that disguise bitterness, hoping to make treatment less unpleasant for young patients. Children everywhere will surely be grateful.","t":"當小女孩嚐到苦藥時，她的臉扭成一個誇張的痛苦表情，並立刻伸手去拿一杯果汁。她的母親笑了，但堅持要她把一整匙吃完。製藥公司長期以來一直為這個問題所困，因為許多有效的藥物味道都令人不快。研究人員目前正在開發能掩蓋苦味的新型包衣與甜味劑，希望讓年幼病患的治療不再那麼難受。各地的孩子們想必都會心存感激。","as":"The runner's grimace as she limped across the finish line revealed the acute pain in her injured knee, but her valor in completing the race despite a deep laceration on her leg won the admiration of every spectator.","at":"這名跑者一跛一跛地越過終點線時，臉上痛苦扭曲的表情透露出膝傷的劇痛，但她不顧腿上一道深深的撕裂傷仍堅持跑完全程，這份勇氣贏得了每位觀眾的敬佩。"},{"w":"calumny","p":"n.","d":"false accusation, slander.","c":"誹謗；中傷","s":"The politician's opponents spread vicious calumny about him during the election campaign, falsely claiming that he had accepted bribes and abandoned his family. Although none of the accusations were true, many voters believed the rumors, and his support declined sharply. After losing the election, he sued several newspapers for defamation. The courts eventually ruled in his favor, but he said the damage to his reputation could never be fully repaired.","t":"在選舉期間，這位政治人物的對手散布惡毒的誹謗，誣指他收受賄賂並拋棄家庭。雖然這些指控沒有一項屬實，許多選民仍相信了謠言，他的支持度也急遽下滑。敗選後，他控告數家報社誹謗。法院最終判他勝訴，但他表示，自己名譽所受的損害永遠無法完全修復。","as":"The candidate's campaign collapsed after rivals spread calumny accusing him of embezzlement, and although investigators later proved the charges mendacious, the scurrilous rumors had already besmirched his reputation beyond repair.","at":"對手散布誹謗、指控他盜用公款後，這位候選人的競選活動便土崩瓦解；雖然調查人員後來證實那些指控純屬捏造，但這些惡毒的流言早已讓他的名譽蒙受無法挽回的汙損。"},{"w":"pittance","p":"n.","d":"small amount.","c":"少量；微薄的薪水","s":"In the nineteenth century, children working in textile factories earned a mere pittance for fourteen hours of dangerous labor each day. Their tiny wages were barely enough to buy bread, yet many families depended on this income to survive. Reformers who visited the factories were horrified by the exhausted, malnourished young workers. Their reports eventually persuaded lawmakers to pass legislation limiting working hours and requiring children to attend school. Such reforms transformed countless young lives.","t":"在十九世紀，於紡織工廠工作的童工每天從事十四小時的危險勞動，卻只賺得微薄的薪水。他們少得可憐的工資勉強夠買麵包，但許多家庭仍仰賴這份收入維生。參訪工廠的改革人士對這些疲憊不堪、營養不良的年幼勞工感到震驚。他們的報告最終說服立法者通過法律，限制工時並規定兒童必須上學。這些改革改變了無數年輕人的生命。","as":"In nineteenth-century textile mills, children toiled through twelve-hour shifts for a mere pittance, a deplorable practice that persisted until reformers advocated for laws that sharply curtailed child labor.","at":"在十九世紀的紡織廠裡，童工每天工作十二小時卻只換得微薄工資，這種令人痛心的做法一直持續到改革者大力倡議立法、大幅限制童工為止。"},{"w":"fastidious","p":"adj.","d":"particular, choosy.","c":"挑剔的；一絲不苟的","s":"The fastidious chef insisted on inspecting every ingredient personally before it entered her kitchen, rejecting vegetables with the slightest blemish and fish that was not caught that morning. She measured spices with scientific precision and demanded that each plate be arranged exactly according to her sketches. Although her demanding standards exhausted some employees, critics agreed that her particular attention to detail had earned the restaurant its international reputation. Reservations are booked months in advance.","t":"這位挑剔的主廚堅持在每樣食材進入廚房前親自檢查，退回任何有一點瑕疵的蔬菜，以及不是當天早上捕撈的魚。她以科學般的精準度測量香料，並要求每道菜都必須完全按照她的草圖擺盤。雖然她嚴苛的標準讓部分員工疲憊不堪，評論家一致認為，正是她對細節的講究，為餐廳贏得了國際聲譽。訂位總是在幾個月前就額滿。","as":"A fastidious collector of rare books, the professor rejected any volume bearing even a faint taint of mildew, and his insatiable appetite for flawless first editions gradually drained his pecuniary resources.","at":"這位教授是個挑剔的珍本書收藏家，只要書上帶有一絲霉斑就拒絕收藏，而他對完美初版書永不滿足的渴求，也漸漸耗盡了他的財力。"},{"w":"au courant","p":"adj.","d":"up-to-date.","c":"趕上時代的；熟知最新情況的","s":"To remain au courant with rapid developments in artificial intelligence, the software engineer reads new research papers every morning and attends international conferences twice a year. She believes that professionals who stop learning quickly fall behind in such a fast-moving industry. Her colleagues often ask her to explain the latest tools and techniques. Thanks to her up-to-date knowledge, her team consistently adopts innovations months before their competitors. Her managers consider her an invaluable asset.","t":"為了跟上人工智慧的快速發展，這位軟體工程師每天早上閱讀新的研究論文，每年兩次參加國際研討會。她相信，在這樣一個瞬息萬變的產業中，停止學習的專業人士很快就會落後。同事們常請她解說最新的工具與技術。多虧她與時俱進的知識，她的團隊總能比競爭對手早好幾個月採用新技術。她的主管們視她為無價的資產。","as":"To stay au courant in a field where breakthroughs swiftly lead to the obsolescence of textbooks, the geneticist peruses dozens of journals each week, a habit her less ardent colleagues find daunting.","at":"在新突破很快就讓教科書過時的領域裡，這位遺傳學家為了掌握最新動態，每週仔細研讀數十份期刊，這個習慣讓較不熱衷的同事們望而生畏。"},{"w":"noisome","p":"adj.","d":"foul, unwholesome.","c":"惡臭的；令人厭惡的","s":"Residents living near the landfill complained for years about the noisome odor that drifted into their homes whenever the wind blew from the east. The foul smell made it impossible to open windows or hang laundry outside during summer. Some families reported headaches and nausea. After a long campaign, environmental authorities finally ordered the facility to install modern ventilation systems and cover its waste daily to reduce the unpleasant stench.","t":"住在垃圾掩埋場附近的居民多年來一直抱怨，每當吹東風時，令人作嘔的惡臭便飄進家中。這股臭味讓他們在夏天根本無法開窗或在戶外晾衣服。有些家庭反映出現頭痛與噁心的症狀。經過長期抗爭，環保主管機關終於命令該設施安裝現代化的通風系統，並每天覆蓋廢棄物，以減少令人不快的臭味。","as":"The noisome waste that the tannery would spew into the river each night became so pungent during the summer that nearby residents, long reluctant to complain, finally petitioned the city to terminate its license.","at":"製革廠每晚排入河中的惡臭廢水，到了夏天變得極其刺鼻，連長久以來不願抱怨的附近居民也終於聯名請願，要求市政府吊銷其營業執照。"},{"w":"unkempt","p":"adj.","d":"untidy, neglected.","c":"蓬亂的；未經整理的","s":"The abandoned mansion's unkempt garden had become a wilderness of overgrown weeds, tangled vines, and fallen branches. Rosebushes that had once been carefully trimmed now sprawled across broken pathways, and the fountain was filled with muddy water. When a young couple purchased the property, they spent two years restoring the neglected grounds. Today, the beautifully maintained garden attracts visitors from across the region every spring. Their dedication inspired many neighbors to garden.","t":"這座廢棄豪宅中荒廢的花園，已變成雜草叢生、藤蔓糾結、枯枝遍地的荒野。曾經被精心修剪的玫瑰叢，如今蔓延在破損的步道上，噴水池裡也滿是泥水。一對年輕夫婦買下這處房產後，花了兩年時間修復這片荒廢的庭園。如今，這座照料得美輪美奐的花園每年春天都吸引了來自整個地區的遊客。他們的用心激勵了許多鄰居開始從事園藝。","as":"Once a showpiece of the city, the botanical garden became unkempt after years of lax management, its paths overgrown with weeds and its fountains clogged with debris, until a coterie of volunteers began restoring it.","at":"這座植物園曾是城市的門面，卻在多年管理鬆散之後變得雜亂荒蕪，步道雜草叢生、噴泉被碎屑堵塞，直到一小群志同道合的志工著手整修。"}]},{"unit":35,"cards":[{"w":"parable","p":"n.","d":"moralistic story.","c":"寓言；比喻","s":"The grandmother loved to teach her grandchildren important values through a simple parable rather than direct lectures. One evening, she told the story of a farmer who shared his last bag of rice with a starving stranger, only to discover that the traveler was a wealthy merchant who later repaid him generously. The children understood immediately that kindness is often rewarded, and they remembered the moral tale for decades afterward.","t":"這位祖母喜歡透過簡單的寓言，而非直接說教，來教導孫子女重要的價值觀。某天晚上，她講了一個農夫的故事：他把最後一袋米分給一位飢餓的陌生人，後來才發現這位旅人是一名富商，之後慷慨地回報了他。孩子們立刻明白，善良往往會得到回報，並在之後的數十年裡一直記得這個富含寓意的故事。","as":"Rather than delivering a perfunctory lecture on ethics, the sage philosopher told a brief parable about a merchant whose insatiable avarice eventually left him bereft of both his friends and his fortune.","at":"這位睿智的哲學家沒有敷衍地講授倫理學，而是說了一則簡短的寓言：一位商人貪得無厭，最後落得朋友與財富兩頭空。"},{"w":"whimsical","p":"adj.","d":"humorous, fanciful.","c":"古怪的；異想天開的","s":"The children's author is famous for her whimsical illustrations, which feature cats wearing top hats, elephants riding bicycles, and teapots that sing lullabies. Her playful imagination delights young readers, while parents appreciate the gentle humor hidden in every page. Critics have praised her fanciful style for encouraging creativity rather than strict realism. Her latest picture book, about a moon that decides to take a vacation, has already become an international bestseller.","t":"這位童書作家以她異想天開的插畫聞名，畫中有戴著高帽的貓、騎腳踏車的大象，以及會唱搖籃曲的茶壺。她充滿玩心的想像力讓小讀者們著迷，家長們也欣賞每一頁中隱藏的溫和幽默。評論家讚揚她奇幻的風格鼓勵創造力，而非嚴格的寫實。她的最新繪本講述一個決定去度假的月亮，已經成為國際暢銷書。","as":"Critics who expected mundane holiday illustrations were delighted by the artist's whimsical drawings, in which jaunty foxes ride bicycles through a labyrinth of floating teacups, a flamboyant departure from her earlier, more sedate work.","at":"原本以為會看到平淡節慶插畫的評論家，對這位畫家奇思妙想的作品大感驚喜：畫中神氣活現的狐狸騎著腳踏車，穿梭在漂浮茶杯構成的迷宮裡，與她早期較沉穩的作品相比，風格大膽張揚得多。"},{"w":"lampoon","p":"v.","d":"to ridicule.","c":"諷刺；嘲弄","s":"Late-night comedy programs frequently lampoon powerful politicians, exaggerating their mannerisms and mocking their controversial statements. Comedians argue that such satire serves an important democratic function, since humor can expose hypocrisy more effectively than serious criticism. Some politicians respond with good humor, even appearing on the shows themselves, while others complain that the ridicule is unfair. Historians note that the tradition of mocking rulers dates back to ancient Greek theater. The genre remains enormously popular.","t":"深夜喜劇節目經常諷刺有權勢的政治人物，誇大他們的言行舉止，並嘲弄他們具爭議性的發言。喜劇演員主張，這種諷刺具有重要的民主功能，因為幽默比嚴肅的批評更能有效揭露偽善。有些政治人物以幽默回應，甚至親自上節目，其他人則抱怨這種嘲弄並不公平。歷史學家指出，嘲諷統治者的傳統可追溯至古希臘戲劇。這類節目至今仍大受歡迎。","as":"Eighteenth-century satirists such as Jonathan Swift would lampoon the pompous politicians of their day, using caustic wit and absurd exaggeration to expose the duplicity that more timorous writers were loath to criticize openly.","at":"像綏夫特這樣的十八世紀諷刺作家，常以尖酸的機智和荒謬的誇張手法嘲諷當時自命不凡的政客，揭露那些較膽小的作家不願公開批評的兩面手法。"},{"w":"countenance","p":"v.","d":"to tolerate, approve.","c":"容許；贊同（名詞：面容）","s":"The strict headmaster refused to countenance any form of bullying at his school, no matter how minor it might seem to others. When he discovered that several older students had been teasing a new classmate, he immediately contacted their parents and required the offenders to attend counseling sessions. Teachers supported his firm position, explaining that tolerating small acts of cruelty often allows more serious harassment to develop over time. Incidents declined dramatically afterward.","t":"這位嚴格的校長拒絕容許學校裡出現任何形式的霸凌，無論在他人看來多麼輕微。當他發現幾名高年級學生一直在戲弄一位新同學時，他立刻聯絡他們的家長，並要求這些學生參加輔導課程。老師們支持他堅定的立場，並解釋說，容忍小小的惡意行為，往往會讓更嚴重的騷擾隨著時間滋長。此後霸凌事件大幅減少。","as":"Although the school board was willing to tolerate minor dress-code violations, it refused to countenance the flagrant cheating scandal, insisting that such egregious breaches of academic ethics be punished forthwith.","at":"儘管校務委員會願意容忍輕微的服裝違規，卻絕不姑息這起明目張膽的作弊醜聞，並堅持如此惡劣違反學術倫理的行為必須立即懲處。"},{"w":"sanctimonious","p":"adj.","d":"hypocritical, claiming moral superiority.","c":"假裝神聖的；偽善的","s":"The celebrity's sanctimonious speech about protecting the environment angered many listeners, who knew that he regularly flew around the world in a private jet. He lectured ordinary citizens about reducing their carbon footprints while living in three enormous mansions. Critics called his preachy attitude deeply hypocritical, arguing that moral lectures lose all credibility when the speaker refuses to follow his own advice. His popularity declined sharply after the controversy. Few fans ever forgave him.","t":"這位名人關於保護環境的偽善演說激怒了許多聽眾，因為大家都知道他經常搭乘私人飛機環遊世界。他一邊教訓普通民眾要減少碳足跡，一邊卻住在三棟豪宅裡。批評者稱他說教的態度極為虛偽，認為當演講者自己拒絕遵循自己的建議時，道德說教就完全失去了可信度。爭議發生後，他的人氣急遽下滑。很少有粉絲原諒過他。","as":"The senator's sanctimonious speeches about frugal government spending rang hollow once journalists revealed that he had used public funds to finance a sumptuous vacation, a blatant example of the hypocrisy voters had long surmised.","at":"記者揭露這位參議員曾挪用公款支付奢華假期後，他那些大談政府應節儉開支、自以為清高的演說便顯得空洞無比——這正是選民早已猜到的虛偽，如今昭然若揭。"},{"w":"equanimity","p":"n.","d":"calmness, self-control.","c":"平靜；鎮定","s":"The experienced airline captain handled the engine failure with remarkable equanimity, calmly informing passengers of the situation and guiding the damaged plane to a safe emergency landing. Throughout the crisis, her voice remained steady and reassuring, and she never showed any sign of panic. Aviation experts later praised her composure, noting that emotional self-control under extreme pressure is one of the most important qualities any pilot can possess. Every passenger survived without injury.","t":"這位經驗豐富的機長以驚人的鎮定處理引擎故障，冷靜地向乘客說明狀況，並引導受損的飛機安全緊急降落。在整個危機過程中，她的聲音始終平穩而令人安心，從未顯露任何驚慌的跡象。航空專家事後讚揚她的沉著，指出在極端壓力下的情緒自制力，是任何飛行員所能具備的最重要特質之一。所有乘客都毫髮無傷地生還。","as":"Even as turbulent markets plunged and disgruntled investors flooded her office with irate calls, the veteran fund manager maintained remarkable equanimity, calmly reminding clients that such transient downturns were inevitable.","at":"即使市場動盪暴跌、不滿的投資人怒氣沖沖地打爆她辦公室的電話，這位資深基金經理人仍保持驚人的沉著，冷靜地提醒客戶，這類短暫的下跌在所難免。"},{"w":"effrontery","p":"n.","d":"shameless boldness.","c":"厚顏無恥","s":"After arriving two hours late to the important meeting, the consultant had the effrontery to complain that the coffee was cold and the room was too small. His colleagues stared at him in disbelief, astonished by his shameless behavior. He never apologized for delaying the entire team or for missing the client's presentation. Not surprisingly, the company decided not to renew his contract, citing his arrogance and lack of professional respect.","t":"這位顧問在重要會議遲到兩小時後，竟然還厚著臉皮抱怨咖啡冷了、會議室太小。同事們難以置信地盯著他，對他無恥的行為感到震驚。他從未為耽誤整個團隊或錯過客戶的簡報道歉。不出所料，公司決定不再與他續約，理由是他傲慢自大、缺乏專業上的尊重。","as":"With astonishing effrontery, the alleged culprit appeared at his trial wearing the very jewels he was accused of stealing, a brash gesture that elicited gasps from the courtroom and nettled the presiding judge.","at":"這名涉嫌犯案者厚顏無恥到令人咋舌，竟戴著他被控竊取的珠寶出庭；如此囂張的舉動讓法庭內一片譁然，也激怒了主審法官。"},{"w":"nonentity","p":"n.","d":"one of no importance.","c":"無足輕重的人","s":"Before winning the national singing competition, the young performer was a complete nonentity in the music industry, unknown to producers and ignored by record companies. She had spent years performing in small cafés for tiny audiences who barely noticed her. Overnight, however, her powerful performance on television transformed her into a celebrity. Today, the woman once dismissed as a nobody sells out concert halls across Asia. Her story now inspires countless young singers.","t":"在贏得全國歌唱比賽之前，這位年輕歌手在音樂界是個完全無足輕重的人，製作人不認識她，唱片公司也忽視她。她多年來一直在小咖啡館裡為寥寥無幾、幾乎沒注意到她的觀眾表演。然而一夕之間，她在電視上震撼的演出讓她成為名人。如今，這位曾被視為無名小卒的女子，在亞洲各地的音樂廳演出場場爆滿。她的故事如今激勵著無數年輕歌手。","as":"Dismissed during his lifetime as a literary nonentity whose obscure poems were relegated to the back pages of minor journals, the writer is now revered as a prodigy whose voice was decades ahead of its time.","at":"這位作家生前被視為文壇無名小卒，他鮮為人知的詩作只能被擠到小型期刊的末頁；如今他卻被奉為天才，其文學聲音領先時代數十年。"},{"w":"flabbergasted","p":"adj.","d":"astounded.","c":"大吃一驚的","s":"The retired teacher was absolutely flabbergasted when she learned that a former student had left her two million dollars in his will. She had not heard from him in over thirty years and could barely remember his face. According to his lawyer, the man had credited her encouragement with inspiring his successful career. Still stunned by the news, she announced that she would donate most of the money to scholarships.","t":"當這位退休教師得知一名以前的學生在遺囑中留給她兩百萬美元時，她完全驚呆了。她已經三十多年沒有他的消息，幾乎記不得他的長相。根據他的律師所說，這名男子認為是她的鼓勵啟發了他成功的事業。仍對這則消息感到震驚的她宣布，將把大部分的錢捐作獎學金。","as":"Astronomers were flabbergasted when the supposedly inert asteroid suddenly began to emit jets of gas, a phenomenon so atypical that it forced them to repudiate several long-held premises about such objects.","at":"原以為毫無活動的小行星突然開始噴出氣流，令天文學家目瞪口呆；這種現象極不尋常，迫使他們推翻了好幾個對這類天體長期抱持的前提。"},{"w":"debacle","p":"n.","d":"fiasco, catastrophe.","c":"慘敗；崩潰","s":"The product launch turned into a complete debacle when the company's new smartphone began overheating during the live demonstration. Smoke rose from the device as horrified executives watched, and the embarrassing video spread across social media within minutes. Investors panicked, and the company's stock price fell by thirty percent the following day. Analysts described the disastrous event as one of the worst public relations failures in the history of consumer technology.","t":"當該公司的新款智慧型手機在現場展示中開始過熱時，這場產品發表會變成了一場徹底的慘敗。在驚恐的高層注視下，裝置冒出煙霧，這段令人難堪的影片在幾分鐘內便傳遍社群媒體。投資人陷入恐慌，隔天公司股價下跌了百分之三十。分析師形容這起災難性的事件是消費科技史上最糟糕的公關失敗之一。","as":"The product launch turned into a debacle when the company's servers, inundated by millions of eager customers, crashed within minutes, and the ensuing bedlam on social media jeopardized the firm's once impeccable reputation.","at":"公司伺服器被數百萬名心急的顧客湧入淹沒，幾分鐘內就當機，產品發表會因此一敗塗地；隨後社群媒體上的一片混亂，更危及這家公司原本無可挑剔的聲譽。"},{"w":"vivacious","p":"adj.","d":"lively.","c":"活潑的；快活的","s":"The new tour guide's vivacious personality made the long bus journey through the mountains unexpectedly enjoyable. She told amusing stories, led the passengers in cheerful songs, and answered every question with enthusiasm and energy. Even the tired elderly travelers who had planned to sleep found themselves laughing and participating. At the end of the trip, several passengers wrote letters to the company praising her lively spirit and warm sense of humor.","t":"新導遊活潑的個性，讓這趟穿越山區的漫長巴士旅程出乎意料地愉快。她講述有趣的故事、帶領乘客唱歡樂的歌，並以熱情與活力回答每一個問題。就連原本打算睡覺的疲倦年長旅客，也跟著一起歡笑參與。旅程結束時，好幾位乘客寫信給旅行社，稱讚她充滿活力的精神與溫暖的幽默感。","as":"Unlike her introspective older sister, the vivacious young dancer was gregarious and quick to quip, bringing gusto to every grueling rehearsal and a welcome levity that kept her exhausted colleagues from despair.","at":"與內省的姊姊不同，這位活潑的年輕舞者生性外向、妙語如珠，在每次艱苦的排練中都充滿幹勁，她帶來的輕鬆幽默也讓疲憊的同伴們不致灰心喪志。"},{"w":"gaunt","p":"adj.","d":"thin, haggard.","c":"憔悴的；瘦削的","s":"After three months lost in the Amazon rainforest, the explorer returned home looking gaunt and exhausted. He had lost nearly twenty kilograms, his cheeks were hollow, and his eyes appeared sunken and tired. Surviving mainly on wild fruit and occasional fish, he had struggled daily to find enough food. Doctors admitted him to hospital immediately, and it took several months of careful nutrition before he regained his normal strength. He later wrote a bestselling survival guide.","t":"在亞馬遜雨林迷失三個月後，這位探險家回到家時顯得憔悴又疲憊。他瘦了將近二十公斤，雙頰凹陷，眼窩深陷且滿是倦容。他主要靠野生水果和偶爾捕到的魚維生，每天都在為找到足夠的食物而掙扎。醫生立刻讓他住院，經過數個月細心的營養調理，他才恢復正常的體力。他後來寫了一本暢銷的求生指南。","as":"After months of privation in the besieged city, the survivors who finally emerged were gaunt and wan, their hollow cheeks bearing silent witness to the malnutrition that had afflicted nearly every household.","at":"在被圍困的城市裡熬過數月的匱乏後，最後走出來的倖存者個個憔悴消瘦、面色蒼白，凹陷的雙頰無聲地見證了幾乎侵襲每個家庭的營養不良。"},{"w":"mien","p":"n.","d":"appearance, bearing.","c":"儀態；風度","s":"The ambassador's dignified mien impressed everyone at the international conference. She walked with calm confidence, spoke in measured tones, and listened attentively to every delegate, regardless of their country's size or influence. Even during tense negotiations, her composed bearing never changed. Colleagues remarked that her graceful manner commanded respect before she had spoken a single word, making her one of the most effective diplomats of her generation. Many young diplomats now study her example.","t":"這位大使端莊的儀態讓國際會議上的每個人都印象深刻。她步伐沉穩自信，說話語調從容，並專注聆聽每一位代表的發言，無論其國家大小或影響力如何。即使在緊張的談判中，她沉著的舉止也從未改變。同事們表示，她優雅的風度在她開口之前就已贏得尊重，使她成為同世代中最具影響力的外交官之一。許多年輕外交官如今以她為學習榜樣。","as":"Despite his humble origins, the diplomat carried himself with such an urbane and dignified mien that even astute foreign observers often assumed he was the scion of an affluent aristocratic family.","at":"儘管出身寒微，這位外交官舉止溫文儒雅、氣度莊重，連精明的外國觀察家都常以為他是富裕貴族世家的子弟。"},{"w":"hirsute","p":"adj.","d":"hairy.","c":"多毛的","s":"The hirsute mountain man had not shaved or cut his hair in nearly ten years, and his thick beard reached almost to his waist. Visitors to his remote cabin often mistook him for a bear when they first glimpsed him through the trees. Despite his wild, shaggy appearance, he was a gentle and well-educated person who had once worked as a university professor before choosing a simpler life. His story fascinated local journalists.","t":"這位毛髮濃密的山中隱士將近十年沒有刮鬍子或剪頭髮，他濃密的鬍鬚幾乎長到腰際。前往他偏遠小屋的訪客，第一次從樹林間瞥見他時，常誤以為他是一頭熊。儘管外表狂野蓬亂，他其實是一位溫和且受過良好教育的人，在選擇更簡樸的生活之前，曾擔任大學教授。他的故事讓當地記者深感著迷。","as":"Paleontologists believe that the now-extinct woolly rhinoceros was hirsute not by chance but as an innate adaptation to the inclement Ice Age climate, its dense hair serving as a bulwark against the bitter cold of its frozen habitat.","at":"古生物學家認為，現已滅絕的長毛犀牛渾身長毛並非偶然，而是對冰河時期嚴酷氣候的先天適應；濃密的毛髮就像一道屏障，抵擋冰封棲地的刺骨寒冷。"},{"w":"refute","p":"v.","d":"to prove wrong or false.","c":"駁斥；反駁","s":"The young scientist carefully designed a series of experiments to refute the widely accepted theory that the ancient forest had been destroyed by fire. Her soil samples contained no evidence of burning, but they revealed chemical traces of a prolonged drought. When she published her findings, many established researchers initially resisted her conclusions. However, additional studies soon confirmed her data, and the old explanation was finally proven wrong. Textbooks were revised the following year.","t":"這位年輕科學家精心設計了一系列實驗，以駁斥廣為接受的理論，即這片古老森林是被大火摧毀的。她的土壤樣本中沒有任何燃燒的證據，卻顯示出長期乾旱的化學痕跡。當她發表研究結果時，許多資深研究人員起初抗拒她的結論。然而，更多研究很快證實了她的數據，舊的解釋終於被證明是錯誤的。教科書在隔年隨之修訂。","as":"Using incontrovertible data from thousands of fossil samples, the young researcher was able to refute the eminent professor's dubious conjecture that the species had vanished because of a single catastrophic flood.","at":"這位年輕研究者利用來自數千件化石樣本、無可辯駁的數據，駁倒了那位知名教授的可疑推測——即該物種是因一場災難性洪水而滅絕。"},{"w":"pensive","p":"adj.","d":"thoughtful, reflective.","c":"沉思的；憂思的","s":"Sitting alone by the window on the last evening of summer vacation, the teenager grew pensive, reflecting on the friendships she had formed and the challenges awaiting her in high school. She watched the sunset quietly, thinking about how quickly the months had passed. Her mother noticed her thoughtful mood and joined her without speaking. Together they shared a peaceful silence, understanding that some moments are best experienced without words.","t":"在暑假的最後一個傍晚，這名青少女獨自坐在窗邊，變得若有所思，回想著這段時間結交的友誼，以及在高中等待著她的挑戰。她靜靜地看著夕陽，想著這幾個月過得多麼快。她的母親注意到她沉思的心情，便默默地陪在她身旁。兩人一起分享著寧靜的沉默，明白有些時刻最好不用言語來體會。","as":"Sitting alone by the tranquil lake after her mentor's funeral, the novelist grew pensive, pondering the poignant letters he had written her and the myriad ways his quiet humility had shaped her own career.","at":"在恩師的葬禮後，這位小說家獨坐於寧靜的湖畔，陷入沉思，回想他寫給她那些令人動容的信，以及他默默的謙遜以無數方式影響了她的寫作生涯。"},{"w":"whet","p":"v.","d":"to stimulate, stir up.","c":"刺激；激起（食慾、興趣）","s":"The museum's short introductory film was designed to whet visitors' curiosity about ancient Egypt before they entered the main exhibition halls. It showed brief glimpses of golden masks, mysterious hieroglyphics, and hidden tombs without revealing too many details. By stimulating their interest early, curators hoped visitors would explore the galleries more attentively. The strategy worked remarkably well, as surveys showed that guests spent twice as long examining the artifacts afterward.","t":"博物館的簡短介紹影片，旨在參觀者進入主要展廳之前，激起他們對古埃及的好奇心。影片簡短呈現了黃金面具、神秘的象形文字與隱密的陵墓，卻不透露過多細節。策展人希望透過及早激發參觀者的興趣，讓他們更專注地探索展廳。這個策略的效果出奇地好，調查顯示，參觀者之後觀賞文物的時間增加了一倍。","as":"The museum's free introductory lecture on ancient Egyptian artifacts was designed to whet visitors' curiosity, and many who arrived as mere dilettantes left as ardent buffs eager to peruse the scholarly catalog.","at":"博物館關於古埃及文物的免費入門講座，旨在激發參觀者的好奇心；許多人來時只是一知半解的外行，離開時卻成了熱情的愛好者，迫不及待想細讀那本學術圖錄。"},{"w":"stupor","p":"n.","d":"daze, insensible condition.","c":"昏迷；恍惚","s":"After working thirty-six hours without sleep during the emergency, the young doctor stumbled home in a stupor, barely able to remember how she had driven there. She dropped onto the sofa without removing her coat and immediately fell into a deep, dreamless sleep. When she finally awoke fourteen hours later, she felt confused and disoriented. Hospital administrators later introduced strict limits on shift lengths to prevent such dangerous exhaustion. Her colleagues strongly welcomed the change.","t":"在緊急事件中連續工作三十六小時沒有睡覺後，這位年輕醫生恍恍惚惚地跌跌撞撞回到家，幾乎記不得自己是怎麼開車回來的。她連外套都沒脫就倒在沙發上，立刻陷入沒有夢境的沉睡。當她終於在十四小時後醒來時，感到困惑且迷迷糊糊。醫院管理階層事後對輪班時數實施嚴格限制，以防止這種危險的過度疲勞。她的同事們非常歡迎這項改變。","as":"Inebriated after hours of feasting, the lethargic guests slumped in a collective stupor, so unresponsive that not even the stentorian voice of the host, announcing the imminent fireworks display, could rouse them.","at":"經過數小時的大吃大喝，賓客們酩酊大醉、昏昏沉沉地癱坐在椅子上，毫無反應；就連主人用洪亮的嗓音宣布煙火即將開始，也無法把他們喚醒。"},{"w":"wince","p":"v.","d":"to draw back, flinch.","c":"畏縮；（因痛苦）皺眉","s":"The football player tried to hide his injury, but he could not help but wince each time he put weight on his swollen ankle. The coach noticed the painful expression and immediately removed him from the game. Medical staff examined the injury on the sidelines and discovered a small fracture. Although disappointed, the athlete later admitted that continuing to play despite obvious pain would have been extremely foolish and risky.","t":"這名足球員試圖隱瞞傷勢，但每當他腫脹的腳踝承受重量時，他都忍不住痛得皺眉畏縮。教練注意到他痛苦的表情，立刻將他換下場。醫護人員在場邊檢查傷勢，發現了一處輕微骨折。雖然感到失望，這名運動員事後承認，在明顯疼痛的情況下繼續比賽會是極為愚蠢且危險的。","as":"Even surgeons who are far from squeamish wince when they recall the excruciating procedures of the era before anesthesia, when patients endured acute pain while fully conscious and the mortality rate from infection was appallingly high.","at":"即使是一點也不怕見血的外科醫師，回想起麻醉發明前那些令人痛不欲生的手術時也會不禁皺眉退縮——當時病人得在完全清醒下忍受劇痛，而感染造成的死亡率更是高得驚人。"},{"w":"cliché","p":"n.","d":"commonplace, overused phrase.","c":"陳詞濫調","s":"Writing instructors encourage students to avoid every tired cliché, such as 'as brave as a lion' or 'at the end of the day,' because overused expressions make essays sound predictable and unoriginal. Instead, they recommend creating fresh comparisons that reflect the writer's unique perspective. Although inventing original phrases requires more effort, examiners consistently reward creative language. Students who replace familiar phrases with vivid, personal images often achieve significantly higher scores.","t":"寫作老師鼓勵學生避免使用任何陳腐的陳詞濫調，例如「勇猛如獅」或「說到底」，因為過度使用的表達會讓文章顯得老套且缺乏原創性。相反地，他們建議學生創造能反映自身獨特觀點的新鮮比喻。雖然發明原創的詞句需要更多努力，閱卷者總是會給予富創意的語言較高的評價。以生動、個人化的意象取代熟悉說法的學生，往往能得到明顯較高的分數。","as":"The editor admonished the aspiring novelist to eschew every tired cliché, arguing that banal phrases such as 'a dark and stormy night' would only convince prestigious publishers that her manuscript lacked originality.","at":"編輯告誡這位有志成為小說家的作者，要避開所有老掉牙的陳腔濫調，並指出像「一個漆黑的暴風雨夜」這類平庸的句子，只會讓知名出版社認為她的稿子缺乏原創性。"}]},{"unit":36,"cards":[{"w":"genre","p":"n.","d":"a certain form or style in art or literature.","c":"類型；流派","s":"Science fiction was once dismissed as a minor genre suitable only for teenagers, but it has gained enormous respect among literary critics over the past fifty years. Authors such as Ursula Le Guin and Ted Chiang have used futuristic settings to explore profound questions about identity, technology, and morality. Today, universities offer entire courses on this category of literature, and science fiction novels regularly win prestigious awards that once ignored them completely.","t":"科幻小說曾被視為只適合青少年閱讀的次要文類，但在過去五十年間，它在文學評論家之間贏得了極大的尊重。娥蘇拉．勒瑰恩與姜峯楠等作家，利用未來的場景探討關於身分、科技與道德的深刻問題。如今，大學開設整門探討這類文學的課程，而科幻小說也經常贏得那些過去完全忽視它們的重要獎項。","as":"Once disparaged by critics as a lowbrow genre fit only for adolescents, science fiction has gradually ascended to literary respectability, and its most eminent authors are now deemed serious chroniclers of social and scientific change.","at":"科幻小說曾被評論家貶為只適合青少年的低俗文類，如今卻逐漸登上文學殿堂，其最傑出的作家更被視為記錄社會與科學變遷的嚴肅史家。"},{"w":"candid","p":"adj.","d":"frank, open, honest.","c":"坦白的；直率的","s":"In a remarkably candid interview, the famous actress admitted that she had struggled with self-doubt throughout her career and had nearly quit acting several times. Instead of presenting a polished image, she spoke honestly about her failures, rejections, and fears. Many fans found her openness refreshing and inspiring, especially young performers facing similar challenges. Journalists noted that such frank conversations are rare in an industry that usually values carefully managed reputations.","t":"在一次極為坦率的訪談中，這位知名女演員承認自己在整個演藝生涯中一直與自我懷疑搏鬥，還曾好幾次差點放棄演戲。她沒有呈現精心修飾的形象，而是誠實地談論自己的失敗、被拒絕的經歷與恐懼。許多粉絲認為她的坦誠令人耳目一新且深受鼓舞，尤其是面臨類似挑戰的年輕演員。記者們指出，在一個通常重視精心經營形象的產業裡，如此坦白的對話實屬罕見。","as":"In a refreshingly candid interview, the retired general acknowledged that the military campaign had been a fiasco, conceding that his own rash decisions had exacerbated the plight of the civilians caught in the fray.","at":"在一次坦率得令人耳目一新的訪談中，這位退役將軍承認那場軍事行動徹底失敗，也坦言自己的輕率決策加重了捲入戰火的平民的苦難。"},{"w":"unsavory","p":"adj.","d":"disagreeable, offensive, morally bad.","c":"令人討厭的；道德敗壞的","s":"The businessman's reputation suffered when reporters discovered his unsavory connections to organized crime groups and corrupt officials. Leaked documents showed that he had accepted money from suspicious sources and arranged secret meetings with people under criminal investigation. Although he denied any wrongdoing, several major companies immediately canceled their partnerships with him. Ethics experts warned that associating with disreputable individuals can destroy trust, even when no crime has been proven. His company never fully recovered.","t":"當記者發現這位商人與組織犯罪集團及貪腐官員之間不光彩的關係時，他的名聲一落千丈。外洩的文件顯示，他曾收受來源可疑的金錢，並與正受刑事調查的人安排秘密會面。儘管他否認有任何不法行為，數家大公司仍立即終止與他的合作。倫理專家警告，與名聲不佳的人往來可能摧毀信任，即使並未證實有任何犯罪行為。他的公司從未完全恢復元氣。","as":"The investigative report exposed the unsavory alliance between the mayor and several infamous loan sharks, revealing a sordid network of extortion and bribery that had flourished with seeming impunity for years.","at":"這份調查報導揭露了市長與數名惡名昭彰的高利貸業者之間見不得光的勾結，攤開一張多年來看似逍遙法外、充斥勒索與賄賂的骯髒網絡。"},{"w":"degrade","p":"v.","d":"to make contemptible, lower.","c":"貶低；使降級","s":"Human rights organizations criticized the reality television program for encouraging participants to degrade themselves in exchange for fame and prize money. Contestants were pressured to eat disgusting insects, insult one another, and reveal embarrassing personal secrets on camera. Psychologists warned that such humiliating experiences could cause lasting emotional harm. After widespread public complaints, the broadcasting network finally canceled the show and introduced stricter guidelines protecting the dignity of future participants.","t":"人權組織批評這個實境節目鼓勵參賽者為了名氣與獎金而自貶身價。參賽者被迫吃下噁心的昆蟲、互相辱罵，並在鏡頭前揭露令人難堪的個人秘密。心理學家警告，這類羞辱性的經歷可能造成長久的情緒傷害。在民眾大規模投訴後，電視台終於停播該節目，並推出更嚴格的規範，以保護未來參賽者的尊嚴。","as":"Critics who advocate prison reform argue that prolonged solitary confinement does not merely punish inmates but degrades them, inflicting psychological damage that is often more pernicious and enduring than any physical laceration.","at":"主張監獄改革的批評者認為，長期單獨監禁不只是懲罰受刑人，更是在貶低他們的人格，所造成的心理創傷往往比任何皮肉之傷更具破壞性、也更持久。"},{"w":"venial","p":"adj.","d":"pardonable, forgivable.","c":"可寬恕的；輕微的","s":"The teacher considered the student's late homework a venial offense, since the boy had been caring for his sick grandmother all week. She reminded the class that forgetting an assignment occasionally is a minor mistake compared with cheating or lying. Instead of punishing him, she simply extended the deadline by two days. The student was deeply grateful for her understanding and submitted an excellent essay before the new due date.","t":"老師認為這名學生遲交作業是可以原諒的小過錯，因為這男孩整個星期都在照顧生病的祖母。她提醒全班，偶爾忘記一項作業，與作弊或說謊相比只是小錯誤。她沒有處罰他，而是將截止日期延後兩天。這名學生深深感激她的體諒，並在新的截止日前交出一篇出色的文章。","as":"Though hardly lax about discipline, the abbot regarded the novice's occasional tardiness as a venial fault deserving only a gentle admonishment, but he considered deliberate duplicity a grave sin that demanded rigorous penance.","at":"這位修道院院長雖然對紀律毫不鬆懈，卻把見習修士偶爾遲到視為情有可原的小過，只需溫和告誡；但他認為蓄意欺瞞是嚴重的罪過，必須嚴格懺悔補贖。"},{"w":"epitome","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that represents the best.","c":"縮影；典範","s":"For many travelers, the small Japanese inn represented the epitome of traditional hospitality. Staff members greeted every guest by name, prepared elaborate seasonal meals, and anticipated needs before visitors even expressed them. The rooms were simple yet elegant, with sliding paper doors opening onto peaceful gardens. Guidebooks consistently described the inn as the perfect example of Japanese service culture, and reservations were often booked more than a year in advance.","t":"對許多旅人而言，這間日本小旅館是傳統待客之道的典範。工作人員會叫出每位客人的名字迎接他們，準備精緻的季節料理，並在客人開口之前就預先想到他們的需求。房間簡樸卻優雅，紙拉門外便是寧靜的庭園。旅遊指南一再形容這間旅館是日本服務文化的完美範例，訂房經常在一年多前就已額滿。","as":"With her meticulous research, incisive prose, and impeccable command of primary sources, the historian was widely regarded as the epitome of scholarly rigor, a paragon whom younger researchers aspired to emulate.","at":"憑藉一絲不苟的研究、精闢犀利的文筆，以及對第一手史料無懈可擊的掌握，這位歷史學家被公認為學術嚴謹的典範，是年輕研究者努力仿效的楷模。"},{"w":"dexterity","p":"n.","d":"mental or physical skill.","c":"靈巧；敏捷","s":"The young pianist performed the extremely difficult concerto with astonishing dexterity, her fingers racing across the keys without a single mistake. Audience members watched in amazement as she executed rapid passages that challenge even experienced professionals. Her teacher explained that such remarkable skill developed through years of disciplined practice, often beginning before dawn. Critics predicted that her nimble technique and emotional sensitivity would make her one of the most celebrated musicians of her generation.","t":"這位年輕鋼琴家以驚人的靈巧演奏這首極為艱難的協奏曲，她的手指在琴鍵上飛馳，沒有一絲失誤。觀眾驚嘆地看著她彈奏出連經驗豐富的專業人士都覺得具挑戰性的快速樂段。她的老師解釋，如此非凡的技巧是經年累月、常在黎明前就開始的自律練習所培養出來的。評論家預測，她靈活的技巧與細膩的情感，將使她成為同世代最受讚譽的音樂家之一。","as":"The watchmaker's astonishing dexterity allowed her to assemble hundreds of minuscule components with tweezers, a feat of virtuosity that even the most adroit robotic automatons in the factory could not replicate.","at":"這位製錶師的手指靈巧得驚人，能用鑷子組裝數百個微小零件；如此高超的技藝，連工廠裡最靈活的機器人也無法複製。"},{"w":"grotesque","p":"adj.","d":"strange, bizarre, misshapen.","c":"奇形怪狀的；荒誕的","s":"The medieval cathedral is decorated with hundreds of grotesque stone figures, including twisted demons, monsters with enormous mouths, and animals with human faces. These strange, distorted sculptures, often called gargoyles, served a practical purpose by directing rainwater away from the walls. Historians also believe they were meant to frighten evil spirits and remind worshippers of the dangers of sin. Today, tourists photograph the bizarre creatures from every possible angle. Children especially love spotting them.","t":"這座中世紀大教堂裝飾著數百尊奇形怪狀的石雕，包括扭曲的惡魔、張著巨口的怪物，以及長著人臉的動物。這些奇異扭曲的雕像通常被稱為滴水嘴獸，具有將雨水導離牆面的實際用途。歷史學家也認為，它們是用來嚇退邪靈，並提醒信徒罪惡的危險。如今，遊客們從各種角度拍攝這些古怪的生物。孩子們尤其喜歡尋找它們。","as":"The gargoyles that adorn medieval cathedrals were carved with an array of grotesque features, such as bulging eyes, gaping mouths, and twisted limbs, which, according to one conjecture, were intended to repulse evil spirits from the sacred edifice.","at":"裝飾中世紀大教堂的滴水嘴獸被雕刻出各式各樣怪誕的模樣，如凸出的眼睛、大張的嘴巴和扭曲的四肢；有一種推測認為，這些造型是為了把邪靈擋在神聖的建築之外。"},{"w":"compassion","p":"n.","d":"sympathetic feeling, kindness.","c":"同情；憐憫","s":"The nurse was known throughout the hospital for her deep compassion toward elderly patients who had no visiting relatives. She spent her lunch breaks reading newspapers aloud to them, holding their hands during painful treatments, and celebrating their birthdays with small cakes. Her kindness made lonely patients feel valued and remembered. When she retired after thirty-five years, dozens of former patients and their families gathered to thank her for her extraordinary sympathy.","t":"這位護理師以她對沒有親人探望的年長病患所懷抱的深切同情而聞名全院。她利用午休時間為他們朗讀報紙，在痛苦的治療過程中握著他們的手，並用小蛋糕為他們慶祝生日。她的善良讓孤單的病患感到被重視、被記得。當她在服務三十五年後退休時，數十位昔日病患及其家屬齊聚一堂，感謝她非凡的關懷。","as":"Moved by compassion for the indigent families who had lost their homes in the conflagration, the affluent philanthropist agreed to underwrite a comprehensive relief program providing temporary shelter, food, and medical care.","at":"出於對大火中失去家園的貧困家庭的憐憫，這位富有的慈善家同意出資支持一項全面的救助計畫，提供臨時住所、食物與醫療照護。"},{"w":"repugnant","p":"adj.","d":"distasteful, repulsive.","c":"令人反感的","s":"Most people find the idea of profiting from other people's suffering deeply repugnant. When investigators revealed that a charity director had spent donations intended for earthquake victims on luxury cars and expensive vacations, public outrage was immediate. Citizens described his behavior as morally disgusting and demanded severe punishment. The scandal also damaged trust in legitimate charities, which reported sharp declines in donations during the following months. He was eventually sentenced to eight years in prison.","t":"大多數人都認為從他人的苦難中牟利是極其令人反感的。當調查人員揭露一名慈善機構主管將捐給地震災民的善款揮霍在豪華汽車與昂貴旅遊上時，民眾立刻群情激憤。市民形容他的行為在道德上令人作嘔，並要求嚴懲。這起醜聞也損害了民眾對正當慈善機構的信任，這些機構在接下來幾個月中回報捐款大幅減少。他最終被判處八年徒刑。","as":"Many nineteenth-century reformers found child labor morally repugnant, and they inveighed against factory owners whose avarice subjected children as young as six to interminable shifts of exhausting drudgery in dark, poorly ventilated mills.","at":"許多十九世紀的改革者認為童工在道德上令人厭惡，他們強烈抨擊那些因貪婪而讓年僅六歲的孩童在昏暗、通風不良的工廠裡，輪班做著永無止境、累人苦差的工廠老闆。"},{"w":"acme","p":"n.","d":"peak, pinnacle, zenith.","c":"頂點；極點","s":"The Tang dynasty is often regarded as the acme of classical Chinese civilization, a period when poetry, painting, and international trade flourished as never before. Poets such as Li Bai and Du Fu produced works that are still memorized by students today. The capital, Chang'an, became one of the largest and most cosmopolitan cities in the world. Historians describe this era as the highest point of Chinese cultural achievement. Its influence spread across Asia.","t":"唐朝常被視為中國古典文明的巔峰，這個時期的詩歌、繪畫與國際貿易空前繁榮。李白與杜甫等詩人所創作的作品，至今仍為學生們背誦。首都長安成為當時世界上最大、最具國際色彩的城市之一。歷史學家將這個時代形容為中華文化成就的最高點。其影響力遍及整個亞洲。","as":"Many art historians consider the Sistine Chapel ceiling the acme of Renaissance painting, a work whose myriad figures and awesome scale represent the culmination of Michelangelo's singular genius and continue to draw throngs of visitors every year.","at":"許多藝術史學家認為西斯汀禮拜堂的天頂畫是文藝復興繪畫的巔峰之作，其中無數的人物與令人讚嘆的規模，正是米開朗基羅非凡天才的極致展現，至今每年仍吸引大批遊客前往。"},{"w":"copious","p":"adj.","d":"ample, abundant, plentiful.","c":"豐富的；大量的","s":"The diligent student took copious notes during every lecture, filling several notebooks with detailed explanations, diagrams, and questions to research later. While her classmates relied on the professor's brief slides, she recorded examples and insights that were never included in the official materials. Before the final examination, she shared her abundant notes with friends, who were amazed by how thoroughly she had documented the entire semester's content. Everyone passed the exam comfortably.","t":"這位勤奮的學生在每堂課都做大量筆記，寫滿了好幾本筆記本，內容包括詳細的解說、圖表，以及日後要查的問題。當同學們依賴教授簡短的投影片時，她記錄下從未出現在正式教材中的例子與見解。期末考前，她把豐富的筆記分享給朋友們，大家都驚訝於她將整學期的內容記錄得如此完整。大家都輕鬆通過了考試。","as":"During her two-year stay in the Amazon, the anthropologist took copious notes on the indigenous tribe's rituals, recording every nuance of their ceremonies before such traditions could succumb to the pressures of modernization.","at":"這位人類學家在亞馬遜停留的兩年間，對當地原住民部落的儀式做了大量筆記，記錄下典禮的每個細微差異，以免這些傳統在現代化的壓力下消失。"},{"w":"vehemently","p":"adv.","d":"violently, eagerly, passionately.","c":"激烈地；強烈地","s":"Local residents vehemently opposed the plan to build a chemical factory beside the river, organizing protests, filling public hearings, and writing hundreds of angry letters to the city council. They argued passionately that pollution would poison their drinking water and destroy the fishing industry that supported many families. Their fierce resistance eventually persuaded officials to reject the proposal. Environmental groups praised the community for defending their natural resources so forcefully.","t":"當地居民強烈反對在河邊興建化學工廠的計畫，他們組織抗議、擠滿公聽會，並寫了數百封憤怒的信給市議會。他們激動地主張，污染將毒害他們的飲用水，並摧毀許多家庭賴以維生的漁業。他們激烈的抵抗最終說服官員否決了該提案。環保團體讚揚這個社區如此強而有力地捍衛自己的自然資源。","as":"Environmental groups vehemently opposed the proposal to raze the ancient forest, arguing that its destruction would obliterate the habitat of several vulnerable species and precipitate irreversible soil erosion in the valleys below.","at":"環保團體強烈反對剷平這片古老森林的提案，主張此舉將徹底摧毀數種易危物種的棲地，並在下方的山谷引發無法逆轉的土壤侵蝕。"},{"w":"depict","p":"v.","d":"to describe clearly, picture, portray.","c":"描繪；描述","s":"The new documentary attempts to depictedaily life in rural Taiwan during the 1960s, using rare photographs, interviews with elderly farmers, and carefully restored film footage. Viewers see families harvesting rice by hand, children walking kilometers to school, and villages celebrating temple festivals. Critics praised the film for portraying the period honestly, showing both the hardships and the strong sense of community that characterized that era. Many elderly viewers were moved to tears by it.","t":"這部新紀錄片試圖描繪1960年代台灣農村的日常生活，運用了珍貴的照片、年長農民的訪談，以及精心修復的影片畫面。觀眾可以看到家家戶戶以手工收割稻米、孩子們走好幾公里路上學，以及村莊慶祝廟會的情景。評論家稱讚這部影片忠實地呈現了那個時期，既展現了艱辛，也呈現了那個年代特有的強烈社群凝聚力。許多年長觀眾看得感動落淚。","as":"The novel vividly depicts the vicissitudes of an itinerant family wandering the drought-stricken plains of the 1930s, juxtaposing their grinding poverty with the opulence of the bankers who had seized their farm.","at":"這部小說生動描繪了一個流浪家庭在1930年代乾旱平原上顛沛流離的人生起伏，並將他們的赤貧與奪走他們農場的銀行家的富裕奢華並列對照。"},{"w":"naive","p":"adj.","d":"unworldly, unsophisticated.","c":"天真的；幼稚的","s":"The naive college freshman believed every advertisement promising easy money, and within his first semester he had lost his savings to three different online schemes. Having grown up in a small, trusting community, he had little experience with dishonest people. His older sister eventually sat him down and explained how to recognize common scams. He admitted that his innocent assumption that everyone told the truth had cost him dearly. He is much wiser now.","t":"這位天真的大一新生相信每一則承諾輕鬆賺錢的廣告，才第一個學期，他就在三個不同的網路騙局中賠光了積蓄。由於在一個彼此信任的小社區長大，他幾乎沒有與不誠實的人打交道的經驗。他的姊姊最後找他坐下來談，教他如何辨識常見的詐騙手法。他承認，自己天真地以為每個人都說實話，這讓他付出了慘痛的代價。如今他明智多了。","as":"Investigators later concluded that the naive retirees had been the dupes of a charismatic charlatan, whose fallacious promises of guaranteed returns had cajoled them into surrendering their life savings within a matter of weeks.","at":"調查人員後來斷定，這些涉世未深的退休人士是被一名極具魅力的騙子所愚弄；他以保證獲利的虛假承諾，在短短幾週內就哄騙他們交出了畢生積蓄。"},{"w":"perfidious","p":"adj.","d":"treacherous, false.","c":"背信棄義的","s":"In the famous play, the king's most trusted advisor turns out to be a perfidious traitor who secretly plots with enemy forces to seize the throne. He pretends to be loyal, offering wise counsel and flattering the king, while sending coded messages to foreign armies. When his treachery is finally exposed in the final act, audiences gasp at the depth of his betrayal. Critics consider him one of literature's greatest villains.","t":"在這齣著名的戲劇中，國王最信任的謀士竟是一名背信棄義的叛徒，暗中與敵軍密謀篡奪王位。他假裝忠心耿耿，提供明智的建言並奉承國王，同時卻向外國軍隊傳送密碼訊息。當他的背叛在最後一幕終於被揭穿時，觀眾對他背叛之深感到震驚。評論家認為他是文學史上最偉大的反派角色之一。","as":"The perfidious general, having forged a clandestine pact with the enemy, opened the city gates under the pretext of negotiating a truce, allowing the invaders to subjugate the very population he had sworn to protect.","at":"這名背信棄義的將軍與敵人暗中結盟，藉口要談判停戰而打開城門，讓入侵者征服了他曾誓言保護的百姓。"},{"w":"covet","p":"v.","d":"to want, envy, wish for.","c":"垂涎；貪求","s":"Many young athletes covet the championship trophy displayed in the school's entrance hall, imagining the day they might lift it above their heads. The gleaming silver cup has been awarded only five times in the school's century-long history. Coaches use the players' intense desire for the prize as motivation during exhausting training sessions. This year, the determined basketball team believes it finally has a realistic chance of winning it. The entire school will be watching.","t":"許多年輕運動員都渴望得到陳列在學校大廳的冠軍獎盃，想像著有朝一日能將它高舉過頭。這座閃亮的銀盃在學校百年歷史中只頒發過五次。教練們利用球員們對這項榮譽的強烈渴望，作為激勵他們熬過艱苦訓練的動力。今年，這支意志堅定的籃球隊相信，他們終於有了贏得獎盃的真正機會。全校都會關注這場比賽。","as":"In Victorian England, wealthy collectors would covet rare orchids so intensely that they hired intrepid plant hunters to scour remote jungles for elusive specimens, a frenzy historians later dubbed 'orchidelirium.'","at":"在維多利亞時代的英國，富有的收藏家極度渴望得到稀有蘭花，甚至僱用無畏的植物獵人深入偏遠叢林搜尋難得一見的品種；歷史學家後來把這股狂熱稱為「蘭花狂熱症」。"},{"w":"ingratiate","p":"v.","d":"to win confidence, charm.","c":"討好；迎合","s":"The new employee tried to ingratiate himself with the manager by bringing her coffee every morning, praising her ideas loudly during meetings, and volunteering for every task she mentioned. His colleagues quickly recognized these obvious attempts to win favor and found them uncomfortable. The manager, however, was more impressed by quiet, competent workers than by flattery. She eventually advised him to focus on improving his performance rather than seeking approval.","t":"這名新進員工試圖討好經理，每天早上幫她帶咖啡，在會議上大聲稱讚她的點子，並自願承接她提到的每一項任務。同事們很快便看穿這些明顯想博取好感的舉動，並感到不自在。然而，經理更欣賞安靜又能幹的員工，而非奉承之舉。她最後建議他專注於提升工作表現，而不是一味尋求認可。","as":"Hoping to ingratiate himself with the irascible CEO, the ambitious junior executive offered fulsome praise at every meeting, but his obsequious flattery merely elicited the older man's disdain and the quiet amusement of his colleagues.","at":"為了討好那位脾氣暴躁的執行長，這位野心勃勃的年輕主管在每次會議上都大肆吹捧，但他那奉承巴結的態度只換來對方的輕蔑，以及同事們暗自的訕笑。"},{"w":"penury","p":"n.","d":"poverty.","c":"貧困；拮据","s":"The famous painter Vincent van Gogh lived much of his life in penury, depending on his brother's financial support to buy food, paint, and canvases. He sold only one painting during his lifetime and often went hungry to afford art supplies. Despite such extreme poverty, he produced more than two thousand works. Ironically, his paintings now sell for tens of millions of dollars at international auctions. His story remains deeply moving.","t":"知名畫家梵谷一生大多數時間都過著貧困的生活，靠弟弟的經濟支援購買食物、顏料與畫布。他生前只賣出一幅畫，而且常常為了買得起繪畫用品而挨餓。儘管身處如此極端的貧窮，他仍創作了兩千多件作品。諷刺的是，他的畫作如今在國際拍賣會上以數千萬美元成交。他的故事至今仍令人深深動容。","as":"Although the composer spent his final years in penury, unable even to afford fuel for his drafty attic, he persevered with ardent devotion, composing works whose intrinsic beauty went unrecognized until decades after his death.","at":"這位作曲家晚年窮困潦倒，連為透風的閣樓買燃料都負擔不起，卻仍滿懷熱忱、堅持不懈地創作；他作品本身的美，直到他去世數十年後才獲得肯定。"},{"w":"ignominious","p":"adj.","d":"humiliating, disgraceful.","c":"可恥的；不光彩的","s":"The once-powerful corporation suffered an ignominious collapse when auditors discovered that executives had falsified financial records for nearly a decade. Its shares became worthless within days, thousands of employees lost their jobs, and several top managers were sentenced to prison. The humiliating downfall shocked investors who had considered the company one of the most reliable in the nation. Business schools now use the scandal as a warning about corporate dishonesty.","t":"這家曾經權勢顯赫的企業，在稽核人員發現高層將近十年來一直偽造財務紀錄後，經歷了一場不光彩的崩垮。其股票在幾天內變得一文不值，數千名員工失業，數名高階主管被判入獄。這場羞辱性的垮台震驚了原本認為該公司是全國最可靠企業之一的投資人。商學院如今以這起醜聞作為企業不誠實的警世案例。","as":"The once-puissant dictator's reign came to an ignominious end when a bloodless coup ousted him from power, and he fled the capital disguised as a peasant, bereft of his former entourage.","at":"這位曾經權傾一時的獨裁者，在一場不流血政變將他趕下台後，統治以屈辱的方式告終；他喬裝成農民逃離首都，身邊昔日的隨從早已一個不剩。"}]},{"unit":37,"cards":[{"w":"confront","p":"v.","d":"to come face-to-face with.","c":"面對；遭遇","s":"After years of avoiding the problem, the city council finally decided to confront the growing housing crisis directly. Rents had doubled in a decade, and thousands of young workers could no longer afford to live near their jobs. Council members held public hearings, studied solutions from other countries, and approved an ambitious plan to build affordable apartments. Residents welcomed the decision to face the issue openly rather than ignoring it any longer.","t":"在逃避這個問題多年之後，市議會終於決定直接面對日益嚴重的住房危機。十年間房租翻了一倍，數千名年輕上班族再也負擔不起住在工作地點附近的費用。議員們舉辦公聽會、研究其他國家的解決方案，並通過了一項興建平價公寓的宏大計畫。居民們歡迎市議會決定公開面對這個問題，而不再繼續忽視它。","as":"Public health officials must eventually confront the paradox that the very antibiotics designed to eradicate bacteria have, through decades of indiscriminate overuse, fostered virulent strains that no longer respond to treatment.","at":"公共衛生官員終究必須正視一個矛盾：原本用來消滅細菌的抗生素，卻因數十年來不加節制的濫用，反而培養出對治療不再有反應的強毒菌株。"},{"w":"antipathy","p":"n.","d":"dislike, distaste, hate.","c":"反感；厭惡","s":"The two neighboring farmers had felt a deep antipathy toward each other for decades, ever since a bitter argument over the boundary between their fields. They refused to speak, avoided the same shops, and even attended different temples. When a flood suddenly threatened both farms, however, they were forced to work together to build sandbag walls. The shared crisis gradually transformed their long hostility into an unexpected and lasting friendship.","t":"這兩位相鄰的農夫幾十年來一直對彼此懷有深深的反感，起因於一場關於兩家田地界線的激烈爭執。他們拒絕交談、避開同樣的商店，甚至去不同的廟宇參拜。然而，當一場洪水突然威脅到兩家農田時，他們被迫一起合作堆砌沙包牆。這場共同的危機逐漸將他們長久的敵意，轉變為一段出乎意料且長久的友誼。","as":"The long-standing antipathy between the two rival clans, fueled by generations of acrimonious land disputes and petty acts of revenge, made any amicable settlement seem chimerical, despite the mediator's assiduous efforts to bring the elders together.","at":"兩個敵對宗族因世代激烈的土地糾紛與瑣碎的報復行為而積怨已久，儘管調解人孜孜不倦地努力促成雙方長老會面，任何和平解決的方案仍顯得遙不可及。"},{"w":"servile","p":"adj.","d":"slavish, submissive.","c":"奴性的；卑屈的","s":"The dictator surrounded himself with servile advisors who praised every decision he made and never dared to express disagreement. They laughed at his jokes, repeated his opinions, and bowed deeply whenever he entered the room. Historians argue that this submissive atmosphere prevented him from receiving honest information about the country's worsening economy. Without anyone willing to challenge his mistakes, his disastrous policies eventually led to widespread poverty and rebellion. His regime collapsed within a decade.","t":"這名獨裁者身邊圍繞著卑躬屈膝的顧問，他們讚揚他做的每一個決定，從不敢表達異議。他們對他的笑話大笑、重複他的意見，每當他走進房間時便深深鞠躬。歷史學家認為，這種順從的氛圍使他無法得到關於國家經濟惡化的真實資訊。由於沒有人願意指出他的錯誤，他災難性的政策最終導致了普遍的貧窮與叛亂。他的政權在十年內便垮台了。","as":"Critics of the regime noted that the state-run newspapers had become servile mouthpieces, dutifully praising every fiat issued by the president while repressing any article that might evince even a tinge of dissent.","at":"政權的批評者指出，官方報紙已淪為卑躬屈膝的傳聲筒，對總統頒布的每道命令都盡責地歌功頌德，同時壓下任何可能流露一絲異議的文章。"},{"w":"volition","p":"n.","d":"willpower, choice.","c":"意志；自願","s":"No one forced the young engineer to leave her comfortable job in Taipei; she moved to the remote mountain village entirely of her own volition. She wanted to design clean water systems for communities that lacked safe drinking water. Friends questioned her decision, but she insisted that the choice reflected her deepest values. Five years later, her projects have provided reliable water to more than three thousand residents across the region.","t":"沒有人強迫這位年輕工程師離開她在台北安穩的工作；她完全是出於自願搬到偏遠的山村。她希望為缺乏安全飲用水的社區設計淨水系統。朋友們質疑她的決定，但她堅持這個選擇反映了她最深層的價值觀。五年後，她的計畫已為該地區三千多位居民提供了穩定的供水。","as":"Although the defendant initially claimed he had acted under duress, the prosecution presented cogent evidence that he had joined the nefarious scheme of his own volition, eager to share in its lucrative profits.","at":"儘管被告起初聲稱自己是受到脅迫才犯案，檢方卻提出有力的證據，證明他是出於自己的意願加入這項邪惡的陰謀，只為分一杯豐厚的利潤。"},{"w":"sojourn","p":"n.","d":"temporary stay.","c":"逗留；旅居","s":"During his brief sojourn in Kyoto, the American writer spent every morning wandering through ancient temples and quiet bamboo forests. Although he stayed only three weeks, the visit profoundly influenced his later work. He filled several notebooks with observations about Japanese gardens, tea ceremonies, and seasonal festivals. Critics believe that this short stay inspired the calm, reflective tone that characterizes the novels he wrote during the following decade. He returned to Kyoto every spring afterward.","t":"在京都短暫逗留期間，這位美國作家每天早上都漫步於古老的寺廟與寧靜的竹林之間。雖然他只停留了三週，這趟旅程卻深深影響了他後來的作品。他寫滿了好幾本筆記本，記錄對日本庭園、茶道與季節祭典的觀察。評論家認為，這段短暫的旅居啟發了他在接下來十年所寫小說中那種平靜而內省的基調。此後他每年春天都會重返京都。","as":"During a brief sojourn in Provence, the expatriate painter was so captivated by the region's lush lavender fields and luminous light that his previously lackluster palette underwent a remarkable metamorphosis.","at":"在普羅旺斯短暫旅居期間，這位旅居海外的畫家深深著迷於當地繁茂的薰衣草田與明亮的光線，使他原本黯淡無光的用色產生了驚人的蛻變。"},{"w":"austere","p":"adj.","d":"simple, unadorned, harsh.","c":"嚴峻的；簡樸的","s":"The monks live in an austere monastery high in the mountains, where each small room contains only a narrow bed, a wooden desk, and a single candle. They wake before dawn, eat simple meals of rice and vegetables, and spend most of the day in silent prayer or physical labor. Visitors are often surprised by the plain surroundings, yet many describe feeling unexpectedly peaceful in such a disciplined environment. Some even return every year.","t":"僧侶們住在高山上一座簡樸的修道院裡，每個小房間只有一張窄床、一張木桌和一根蠟燭。他們在黎明前起床，吃米飯和蔬菜等簡單的餐點，一天中大部分時間都在靜默祈禱或勞動中度過。訪客們常對這樣樸素的環境感到驚訝，但許多人表示，在如此自律的環境中，竟意外地感到平靜。有些人甚至每年都會回來。","as":"The monks lived in austere cells furnished with only a narrow cot and a wooden stool, for, like every ascetic in their order, they eschewed worldly comforts and kept an abstemious diet in pursuit of spiritual salvation.","at":"修士們住在簡樸的小室裡，只有一張窄床和一張木凳；就像修會中每位苦行者一樣，他們摒棄世俗享受、節制飲食，以追求靈魂的救贖。"},{"w":"felicitous","p":"adj.","d":"well-suited, pleasing, happy.","c":"恰當的；令人愉悅的","s":"The translator was praised for her felicitous choice of words, which captured both the meaning and the musical rhythm of the original Japanese poems. Instead of translating each line literally, she searched for English expressions that conveyed the same emotions and imagery. Readers who compared the two versions admired how naturally the translations flowed. Critics described her work as a perfect example of how well-chosen language can bridge different cultures.","t":"這位譯者因用字恰到好處而備受讚譽，她的譯文同時捕捉了日文原詩的意涵與音樂般的節奏。她並非逐行直譯，而是尋找能傳達相同情感與意象的英文表達。比較兩個版本的讀者，都讚嘆譯文讀來如此自然流暢。評論家形容她的作品是精挑細選的語言如何跨越文化隔閡的完美範例。","as":"The translator's felicitous choice of words preserved both the humor and the subtle nuances of the original poem, an achievement that even the most contemptuous critics were compelled to deem laudable.","at":"譯者用字貼切得宜，保留了原詩的幽默與細膩的言外之意；這項成就連最不屑一顧的評論家都不得不承認值得稱讚。"},{"w":"halcyon","p":"adj.","d":"idyllically peaceful, calm.","c":"寧靜的；太平的","s":"The elderly man often spoke fondly of the halcyonedays of his childhood, when he spent long summers swimming in the river, climbing fruit trees, and listening to his grandfather's stories under the stars. There were no televisions or smartphones, and time seemed to pass slowly and peacefully. Although he acknowledged that life had also contained hardships, he treasured those serene memories as the happiest period of his entire life.","t":"這位老先生常深情地談起他童年那段寧靜美好的日子，那時他整個漫長的夏天都在河裡游泳、爬果樹，並在星空下聽祖父講故事。當時沒有電視或智慧型手機，時間似乎過得緩慢而平和。雖然他承認那時的生活也有艱辛，他仍將那些平靜的回憶視為一生中最快樂的時光而珍藏著。","as":"Writing her memoir as an octogenarian, the novelist recalled the halcyon summers of her childhood in a rustic fishing village with a nostalgia so poignant that it permeated nearly every chapter.","at":"這位小說家年逾八旬時撰寫回憶錄，憶起童年在純樸漁村度過的那些寧靜美好的夏天，字裡行間滿是令人動容的懷舊之情，幾乎滲透每個章節。"},{"w":"tenable","p":"adj.","d":"supportable, defendable.","c":"站得住腳的；可防守的","s":"The theory that dinosaurs were slow, cold-blooded reptiles is no longer tenable in light of recent fossil discoveries. Scientists have found evidence of feathers, rapid growth rates, and complex nesting behaviors that suggest many species were active and warm-blooded. As new data accumulated, the old explanation became impossible to defend. Most paleontologists now accept that birds are the living descendants of certain dinosaurs, a view once considered extremely controversial. Museums have since updated their displays.","t":"根據近年的化石發現，恐龍是行動緩慢的冷血爬蟲類這一理論已站不住腳。科學家發現了羽毛、快速成長速度以及複雜築巢行為的證據，顯示許多物種是活躍的溫血動物。隨著新資料不斷累積，舊的解釋已無法再自圓其說。大多數古生物學家如今都接受鳥類是某些恐龍現存的後代，而這個觀點過去曾被認為極具爭議。各博物館此後也更新了展示內容。","as":"Once new satellite measurements corroborated the rapid melting of polar ice, the skeptics' claim that global warming was a hoax was no longer tenable, and even some of their most zealous adherents began to recant.","at":"新的衛星測量數據證實了極地冰層正快速融化後，懷疑論者聲稱全球暖化是騙局的說法再也站不住腳，就連他們一些最狂熱的支持者也開始改口。"},{"w":"superfluous","p":"adj.","d":"excessive, surplus, unnecessary.","c":"多餘的；過剩的","s":"The editor removed nearly a third of the manuscript, explaining that many paragraphs contained superfluousedetails that slowed the story without adding meaning. Lengthy descriptions of furniture, repetitive dialogue, and unnecessary background information distracted readers from the central conflict. Although the author initially resisted the cuts, she later admitted that the shorter version was far more powerful. The novel went on to win a major literary prize the following year.","t":"編輯刪除了將近三分之一的書稿，解釋說許多段落包含多餘的細節，拖慢了故事節奏卻沒有增添意義。冗長的家具描寫、重複的對話與不必要的背景資訊，分散了讀者對核心衝突的注意力。雖然作者起初抗拒這些刪減，她後來承認較短的版本更具力量。這部小說隔年便贏得了一項重要的文學獎。","as":"The editor ruthlessly truncated the verbose manuscript, cutting superfluous adjectives and tortuous digressions until only the salient arguments remained, a process the author initially resisted but later conceded had made the book far more trenchant.","at":"編輯毫不留情地刪減這份冗長的書稿，砍掉多餘的形容詞和迂迴曲折的離題段落，只留下最重要的論點；作者起初抗拒，後來卻承認這讓全書犀利得多。"},{"w":"motivate","p":"v.","d":"to inspire, stimulate, provoke.","c":"激發；促動","s":"The basketball coach knew exactly how to motivate his struggling team before the championship game. Instead of criticizing their recent losses, he showed them videos of their best performances and reminded them how far they had come together. He also invited former players to share stories of overcoming difficult challenges. Inspired and confident, the team played with renewed energy that evening and won the title by eleven points. Fans celebrated late into the night.","t":"這位籃球教練非常清楚如何在冠軍賽前激勵陷入低潮的球隊。他沒有批評他們最近的敗績，而是播放他們表現最好的比賽影片，並提醒他們一起走了多遠的路。他還邀請昔日球員分享克服艱難挑戰的故事。受到鼓舞、充滿自信的球隊當晚以全新的活力出賽，並以十一分之差奪得冠軍。球迷們慶祝到深夜。","as":"To motivate the students in her remedial class, who seemed mired in apathy, the resourceful teacher replaced mundane drills with spontaneous debates on controversial issues, and attendance surged within a single semester.","at":"為了激勵補救班上那些看似意興闌珊的學生，這位足智多謀的老師以即興辯論爭議性議題取代枯燥的練習，結果出席率在一學期內大幅攀升。"},{"w":"rationalize","p":"v.","d":"to give a reason other than the real one.","c":"合理化；為…找藉口","s":"People often rationalize unhealthy habits by inventing convenient excuses. A smoker might claim that one cigarette helps him relax, while a student who skips studying might argue that she works better under pressure. Psychologists explain that these explanations protect our self-image by hiding the real reasons behind our choices. Recognizing when we make excuses, they suggest, is the first step toward changing behavior and making more honest decisions. Honesty with ourselves is essential.","t":"人們常常編造方便的藉口，將不健康的習慣合理化。抽菸的人可能聲稱一根菸能幫助他放鬆，而不念書的學生可能辯稱她在壓力下表現更好。心理學家解釋，這些說法透過掩蓋我們選擇背後的真正原因，來保護我們的自我形象。他們建議，察覺自己何時在找藉口，是改變行為、做出更誠實決定的第一步。對自己誠實是不可或缺的。","as":"Smokers often rationalize their habit by claiming that it relieves stress, a convenient pretext that conceals the real reason, an addiction so powerful that many are loath to acknowledge it even to themselves.","at":"吸菸者常以紓解壓力為由替自己的習慣找藉口，這個方便的說詞掩蓋了真正的原因——一種強烈到許多人連對自己都不願承認的成癮。"},{"w":"therapy","p":"n.","d":"healing or curing process.","c":"治療；療法","s":"After the serious car accident, the young athlete needed months of physical therapy to regain the ability to walk normally. Three times a week, specialists guided her through exercises designed to strengthen damaged muscles and restore balance. Progress was slow and often painful, but she never missed a session. Eventually, the treatment succeeded beyond expectations, and within two years she was competing again in national track and field events. She now volunteers helping other injured athletes.","t":"在一場嚴重車禍後，這位年輕運動員需要數個月的物理治療，才能恢復正常行走的能力。每週三次，專業人員指導她進行旨在強化受損肌肉與恢復平衡的運動。進展緩慢且常伴隨疼痛，但她從未缺席任何一次療程。最終，治療的成效超乎預期，兩年內她便重返全國田徑賽場。她如今擔任志工，幫助其他受傷的運動員。","as":"For veterans afflicted with post-traumatic stress, a combination of group therapy and medication can palliate the most acute symptoms, though clinicians caution that no single treatment is a panacea for such complex wounds.","at":"對於飽受創傷後壓力所苦的退伍軍人而言，團體治療加上藥物可以緩解最嚴重的症狀，但臨床醫師提醒，面對如此複雜的創傷，沒有任何單一療法是萬靈丹。"},{"w":"nascent","p":"adj.","d":"beginning to exist or develop.","c":"初生的；新興的","s":"In the early 1990s, the internet was still a nascent technology used mainly by universities and government researchers. Few ordinary people owned computers, and websites consisted mostly of simple text. Visionary entrepreneurs, however, recognized the enormous potential of this emerging network. Within two decades, the developing technology had transformed communication, commerce, and education worldwide, creating industries that nobody could have imagined when it first appeared. Its growth continues to accelerate today.","t":"在1990年代初期，網際網路仍是一項新興技術，主要由大學與政府研究人員使用。當時很少一般民眾擁有電腦，網站大多只有簡單的文字。然而，具遠見的創業家看出了這個新興網路的巨大潛力。二十年內，這項發展中的技術徹底改變了全球的通訊、商業與教育，創造出在它剛出現時沒有人能想像的產業。它的成長至今仍在加速。","as":"In the early 1980s, the nascent personal computer industry was dominated by tiny start-ups run from garages, few of which seemed viable at the time, and few analysts would have dared to prognosticate that several would grow into mammoth global corporations.","at":"在1980年代初期，剛起步的個人電腦產業由一群在車庫裡經營的小型新創公司主導；當時看來能存活的寥寥無幾，也很少有分析師敢預言其中幾家會成長為龐大的跨國企業。"},{"w":"iconoclast","p":"n.","d":"image-breaker, attacker of traditional beliefs.","c":"反傳統者；打破舊習者","s":"The architect was considered an iconoclast because she rejected the traditional rules that had governed building design for centuries. Instead of symmetrical structures with decorative columns, she created twisted towers of glass and steel that seemed to defy gravity. Established critics initially attacked her work as ugly and impractical. Over time, however, her rebellious approach inspired a new generation of designers, and her buildings are now celebrated worldwide. Architecture students study her designs closely.","t":"這位建築師被視為一名反傳統者，因為她拒絕遵循主導建築設計數百年的傳統規則。她沒有設計帶有裝飾柱的對稱建築，而是創造出彷彿違抗重力、由玻璃與鋼材構成的扭曲高塔。資深評論家起初抨擊她的作品醜陋又不實用。然而隨著時間推移，她叛逆的手法啟發了新一代的設計師，她的建築如今享譽全球。建築系學生仔細研究她的設計。","as":"A lifelong iconoclast, the architect flouted the conventions of classical design and scoffed at revered traditions, insisting that the ornate columns his peers adored were nothing but relics of a decadent past.","at":"這位建築師一生都是挑戰傳統的反叛者，他公然違抗古典設計的規範，嘲笑備受推崇的傳統，堅稱同儕所鍾愛的華麗柱子不過是頹廢過去的遺物。"},{"w":"erudite","p":"adj.","d":"very scholarly, learned.","c":"博學的","s":"The erudite professor could discuss ancient Greek philosophy, Renaissance painting, and modern physics with equal expertise. He spoke seven languages fluently and had published more than twenty books on subjects ranging from medieval history to linguistics. Students crowded into his lectures, amazed by his vast knowledge and ability to connect ideas across different fields. Colleagues often joked that consulting him was faster than searching an entire library. His retirement left an enormous gap in the department.","t":"這位博學的教授能以同等的專業談論古希臘哲學、文藝復興繪畫與現代物理學。他能流利地說七種語言，並出版了二十多本著作，主題涵蓋中世紀歷史到語言學。學生們擠滿他的課堂，驚嘆於他淵博的知識，以及貫通不同領域思想的能力。同事們常開玩笑說，請教他比搜尋整座圖書館還快。他的退休在系上留下了巨大的空缺。","as":"The erudite professor could discourse with equal ease on medieval annals, recondite theories of linguistics, and obscure Renaissance poets, yet her lectures were never pedantic or condescending, which made her a favorite among even first-year students.","at":"這位學識淵博的教授無論談中世紀編年史、深奧的語言學理論，或是冷門的文藝復興詩人，都能侃侃而談，而她的講課從不賣弄學問，也不居高臨下，因此連大一新生都很喜歡她。"},{"w":"phobia","p":"n.","d":"persistent fear, strong dislike.","c":"恐懼症","s":"Although she loved traveling, the businesswoman had a severe phobia of flying that made every international trip an ordeal. Her heart raced whenever she boarded an airplane, and she often trembled throughout the entire flight. Determined to overcome this intense fear, she enrolled in a special course run by pilots and psychologists. After several sessions explaining how aircraft work, she finally completed a long-haul flight without panic. She now travels regularly without hesitation.","t":"雖然她熱愛旅行，這位女企業家卻有嚴重的飛行恐懼症，讓每一趟國際旅程都成了一場折磨。每當她登上飛機，心跳便加速，整趟飛行中常常顫抖不已。她下定決心克服這種強烈的恐懼，報名參加了由機師與心理學家開設的特別課程。在幾堂說明飛機如何運作的課程之後，她終於在毫無恐慌的情況下完成了一趟長途飛行。她如今經常旅行，毫不猶豫。","as":"Psychologists believe that a phobia often originates in a single traumatic experience; a child bitten by a mastiff, for example, may develop an irrational fear of all dogs that persists for decades.","at":"心理學家認為，恐懼症往往源自單一的創傷經驗；例如，被獒犬咬過的孩子，可能會對所有狗產生不理性的恐懼，而且持續數十年之久。"},{"w":"germane","p":"adj.","d":"appropriate, relevant.","c":"密切相關的；切題的","s":"During the debate, the moderator repeatedly reminded participants to keep their comments germane to the topic of public transportation. Several speakers had begun discussing unrelated issues such as taxes and foreign policy, wasting valuable time. The moderator insisted that only relevant arguments supported by evidence would be allowed. As a result, the second half of the debate became far more focused and productive, and audiences praised its clarity. Organizers adopted the rule permanently.","t":"辯論期間，主持人一再提醒參與者，發言內容必須與大眾運輸的主題密切相關。有幾位講者已開始談論稅務與外交政策等無關的議題，浪費了寶貴的時間。主持人堅持，只允許有證據支持且切題的論點。結果，辯論的後半段變得更加聚焦且有成效，觀眾們也稱讚其條理清晰。主辦單位將此規則永久採用。","as":"During the hearing, the judge repeatedly admonished the garrulous witness to confine his testimony to facts germane to the case, as his desultory anecdotes about his neighbors were wholly irrelevant.","at":"聽證會上，法官一再告誡那位喋喋不休的證人，證詞只能限於與本案相關的事實，因為他那些東拉西扯的鄰居軼事與案情毫不相干。"},{"w":"vertigo","p":"n.","d":"dizziness.","c":"眩暈","s":"As she stood on the glass floor of the observation deck, more than four hundred meters above the city, the tourist was suddenly overcome by vertigo. The buildings below seemed to spin, her legs weakened, and she grabbed the railing to avoid falling. A staff member quickly guided her to a bench away from the edge. After a few minutes of rest and deep breathing, her dizziness gradually disappeared. She later visited the deck again calmly.","t":"當這名遊客站在離城市四百多公尺高的觀景台玻璃地板上時，突然感到一陣眩暈。下方的建築物似乎在旋轉，她雙腿發軟，趕緊抓住欄杆以免跌倒。一名工作人員迅速引導她到遠離邊緣的長椅上。休息幾分鐘並深呼吸後，她的暈眩感逐漸消失了。她後來再度從容地造訪了觀景台。","as":"Climbers ascending the sheer granite face often experience sudden vertigo when they glance down at the ominous drop below, and even intrepid veterans admit that the dizzying sensation can leave their limbs tremulous.","at":"攀登陡峭花崗岩壁的登山者，往下瞥見腳下那令人不安的深淵時，常會突然一陣暈眩；即使是無畏的老手也承認，那種天旋地轉的感覺會讓他們四肢發抖。"},{"w":"conducive","p":"adj.","d":"leading, helpful.","c":"有助於…的","s":"Research shows that a quiet, well-lit room with comfortable furniture is highly conducive to effective studying. Students who work in noisy or cluttered spaces often struggle to concentrate and retain information. Educational psychologists therefore recommend creating a dedicated study area free from distractions such as televisions and smartphones. Even small improvements, such as adding plants or natural light, can create a more favorable environment for learning. Such changes are inexpensive and highly effective.","t":"研究顯示，一個安靜、光線充足且有舒適家具的房間，非常有助於有效學習。在吵雜或雜亂空間中讀書的學生，往往難以專心並記住資訊。因此，教育心理學家建議規劃一個專屬的讀書區，遠離電視與智慧型手機等干擾。即使是小小的改善，例如擺放植物或引進自然光，也能營造更有利於學習的環境。這類改變花費不多，卻極為有效。","as":"Researchers have found that a tranquil setting, free from the cacophony of traffic, is far more conducive to deep concentration than the bedlam of a typical open-plan office, where few workers can remain engrossed in a task for long.","at":"研究人員發現，遠離車流嘈雜聲的寧靜環境，遠比典型開放式辦公室的喧鬧混亂更有助於深度專注；在後者中，很少有員工能長時間全神貫注於一項工作。"}]},{"unit":38,"cards":[{"w":"glib","p":"adj.","d":"smooth of speech, fluent but insincere.","c":"口齒伶俐的；油嘴滑舌的","s":"The salesman gave glib answers to every question about the used car, assuring customers that it had never been in an accident and needed no repairs. His smooth, confident manner convinced many buyers to sign contracts without inspecting the vehicle carefully. Only later did they discover hidden damage and expensive mechanical problems. Consumer advocates warn that slick, effortless explanations are often designed to discourage people from asking deeper questions before making important purchases.","t":"這名推銷員對於這輛二手車的每個問題都給出油嘴滑舌的回答，向顧客保證它從未發生過事故，也不需要任何維修。他圓滑自信的態度說服了許多買家，在沒有仔細檢查車輛的情況下就簽下合約。直到後來，他們才發現隱藏的損傷與昂貴的機械問題。消費者權益倡議者警告，圓滑、輕鬆的解釋往往是為了讓人們在做出重要購買決定前，不再深入追問。","as":"The salesman's glib assurances that the used car was in impeccable condition failed to deceive the astute buyer, who looked past its glossy veneer and scrutinized the engine, discovering extensive and carefully concealed damage.","at":"推銷員油嘴滑舌地保證這輛二手車車況完美無瑕，卻騙不了精明的買家；他看穿光鮮的外表，仔細檢查引擎，發現了大面積且被刻意掩飾的損傷。"},{"w":"homogeneous","p":"adj.","d":"same, uniform.","c":"同質的；均勻的","s":"For centuries, the remote island had a remarkably homogeneous population, with nearly all residents sharing the same language, religion, and cultural traditions. Few outsiders ever visited, and families rarely moved away. In recent decades, however, tourism and international trade have brought newcomers from many different countries. Sociologists studying the island note that its once uniform society is gradually becoming more diverse, creating both exciting opportunities and new challenges for local communities.","t":"數百年來，這座偏遠島嶼的人口組成極為同質，幾乎所有居民都說同一種語言、信仰相同的宗教，並擁有相同的文化傳統。外人很少造訪，家家戶戶也很少遷出。然而近幾十年來，觀光業與國際貿易帶來了許多來自不同國家的新住民。研究這座島嶼的社會學家指出，這個曾經單一的社會正逐漸變得更加多元，為當地社區帶來了令人期待的機會與新的挑戰。","as":"Contrary to the stereotype of the region as culturally homogeneous, anthropologists have documented a heterogeneous array of languages, cuisines, and religious traditions among its indigenous communities, some of which differ sharply from villages only a few miles away.","at":"與外界認為該地區文化單一的刻板印象相反，人類學家在當地原住民社群中記錄到各式各樣、豐富多元的語言、飲食與宗教傳統，有些甚至與僅數英里外的村落截然不同。"},{"w":"malleable","p":"adj.","d":"capable of being shaped or formed.","c":"可塑的；易受影響的","s":"Gold is one of the most malleable metals on Earth; a single gram can be hammered into a sheet so thin that light passes through it. Ancient craftsmen took advantage of this property to create delicate jewelry, decorative masks, and thin gold leaf for temples. Because the metal can be shaped without breaking, artisans could produce intricate designs using simple tools. Modern electronics manufacturers also value its flexible, adaptable qualities.","t":"黃金是地球上延展性最好的金屬之一，僅僅一公克就能被捶打成薄到可以透光的金箔。古代工匠利用這項特性，製作出精緻的珠寶、裝飾面具，以及寺廟用的薄金箔。由於這種金屬能被塑形而不會斷裂，工匠們只需簡單的工具就能打造出繁複的設計。現代電子製造商也看重它柔韌、可塑的特性。","as":"Because gold is extraordinarily malleable, ancient artisans could hammer it into sheets thinner than paper, and many such artifacts are still extant today, their luster unabated after thousands of years.","at":"由於黃金的延展性極佳，古代工匠能把它捶打成比紙還薄的金箔；許多這類工藝品至今仍保存完好，歷經數千年光澤依舊不減。"},{"w":"legerdemain","p":"n.","d":"sleight of hand, deceptive cleverness.","c":"戲法；騙術","s":"The magician amazed the audience with his legerdemain, making coins disappear from his palm and reappear inside sealed envelopes held by volunteers. Even people sitting in the front row could not detect how he performed the tricks. His hands moved so quickly and smoothly that every illusion seemed genuinely impossible. After the show, he explained that mastering such sleight of hand had required twenty years of practice for several hours every single day.","t":"這位魔術師以他的戲法讓觀眾驚嘆不已，讓硬幣從他的掌心消失，再出現在志願者手中密封的信封裡。即使坐在第一排的人也看不出他是如何變出這些把戲的。他的雙手動作又快又流暢，讓每個幻術看起來都真的不可能辦到。表演結束後，他解釋說，要練就如此純熟的手法，需要二十年每天數小時的練習。","as":"Through a feat of financial legerdemain, the firm's executives hid billions in debt from auditors, a subterfuge so elaborate that regulators needed years to unravel the labyrinth of fictitious accounts and expose their complicity.","at":"公司高層靠著一套財務障眼法，向稽核人員隱瞞了數十億的債務；這場騙局精密複雜，監管單位花了好幾年才理清那迷宮般的假帳，揭發他們的共謀。"},{"w":"trend","p":"n.","d":"general direction, fashion.","c":"趨勢；傾向","s":"Economists have observed a clear trend toward remote work since the global pandemic, with millions of employees now performing their jobs from home at least part of the week. Companies have discovered that flexible arrangements can reduce office costs and improve employee satisfaction. At the same time, city centers have experienced declining foot traffic in restaurants and shops. Analysts predict that this general direction will continue reshaping urban economies for many years to come.","t":"經濟學家觀察到，自全球疫情以來，遠距工作已成為明顯的趨勢，數百萬名員工如今每週至少有部分時間在家工作。企業發現，彈性的工作安排能降低辦公室成本，並提高員工滿意度。與此同時，市中心的餐廳與商店人潮則逐漸減少。分析師預測，這個整體走向將在未來多年持續重塑都市經濟。","as":"Economists have observed a troubling trend in which affluent neighborhoods grow ever more prosperous while nearby indigent communities sink into destitution, a widening gap that threatens to perpetuate inequality for generations.","at":"經濟學家觀察到一個令人憂心的趨勢：富裕社區越來越興旺，鄰近的貧困社區卻陷入赤貧；這道日益擴大的鴻溝，恐將使不平等延續好幾代。"},{"w":"stagnant","p":"adj.","d":"motionless, dull, inactive.","c":"停滯的；不流動的","s":"Mosquitoes breed rapidly in stagnant water, laying their eggs in abandoned tires, blocked gutters, and flower pots that collect rain. Because the water does not flow, larvae can develop undisturbed within a week. Health officials in Taiwan regularly remind residents to empty containers around their homes, especially during the rainy season, to prevent outbreaks of dengue fever. Removing still water is one of the simplest and most effective methods of disease prevention.","t":"蚊子會在不流動的死水中迅速繁殖，把卵產在廢棄輪胎、堵塞的排水溝和積了雨水的花盆裡。由於水不流動，幼蟲可以在一週內不受干擾地發育。台灣的衛生官員經常提醒民眾清空住家周圍的容器，尤其是在雨季，以防止登革熱爆發。清除積水是最簡單也最有效的疾病預防方法之一。","as":"After a decade of stagnant wages and dwindling job prospects, the once-bustling mill town seemed moribund, its disgruntled residents increasingly susceptible to the promises of politicians who blamed outsiders for their plight.","at":"經過十年薪資停滯、工作機會日益減少，這座曾經熱鬧的工廠小鎮顯得奄奄一息；心懷不滿的居民越來越容易聽信那些把他們的困境歸咎於外人的政客所做的承諾。"},{"w":"fatal","p":"adj.","d":"deadly, disastrous.","c":"致命的；毀滅性的","s":"The mountain climber made a fatal error when he ignored the weather forecast and continued toward the summit despite warnings of an approaching storm. Heavy snow soon covered the trail, and temperatures fell far below freezing. Rescue teams searched for three days but could not reach him in time. His tragic death led to new regulations requiring climbers to register their routes and follow the instructions of experienced local guides.","t":"這名登山者犯下了致命的錯誤，他無視天氣預報，不顧暴風雪即將來臨的警告，繼續朝山頂前進。大雪很快覆蓋了步道，氣溫也降到遠低於冰點。搜救隊搜尋了三天，卻未能及時找到他。他的悲劇性死亡促成了新規定的實施，要求登山者登記路線，並遵從經驗豐富的當地嚮導指示。","as":"Historians argue that the emperor's fatal miscalculation was to underestimate the inclement Russian winter, which decimated his ill-equipped army and precipitated the collapse of an empire that had once seemed omnipotent.","at":"歷史學家認為，這位皇帝致命的失算在於低估了俄國嚴酷的冬天；寒冬重創他裝備不足的軍隊，並加速了一個曾看似無所不能的帝國的崩潰。"},{"w":"passé","p":"adj.","d":"outmoded, old-fashioned.","c":"過時的","s":"Teenagers today often consider email completely passé, preferring instant messaging apps and social media platforms to communicate with friends. Many young people check their inboxes only when schools or companies require it. Communication researchers note that technologies which once seemed revolutionary can become outdated remarkably quickly. Just twenty years ago, email was considered the most modern way to stay in touch, while handwritten letters were viewed as old-fashioned relics of the past.","t":"如今的青少年常認為電子郵件完全過時了，他們更喜歡用即時通訊軟體和社群媒體與朋友聯絡。許多年輕人只有在學校或公司要求時才會查看收件匣。傳播研究人員指出，曾經看似革命性的科技，可能會以驚人的速度變得過時。就在二十年前，電子郵件還被視為最現代的聯絡方式，而手寫信則被看作老派的過往遺物。","as":"Styles that seemed daringly avant-garde only a few years ago are now considered passé, and the flamboyant designer who once set the vogue has watched with chagrin as her influence steadily declined, a sobering reminder of how transient fame can be.","at":"幾年前還顯得大膽前衛的風格，如今已被視為過時；那位曾引領潮流、作風浮誇的設計師，懊惱地看著自己的影響力逐漸下滑——這清楚提醒世人，名聲是多麼短暫。"},{"w":"procrastinate","p":"v.","d":"to delay, put off.","c":"拖延；耽擱","s":"Many university students procrastinate until the night before a major deadline, spending weeks watching videos and chatting online instead of working on their assignments. They then stay awake until dawn, rushing to finish essays that deserve far more careful attention. Psychologists explain that people often delay unpleasant tasks because they fear failure or feel overwhelmed. Breaking large projects into smaller steps, they suggest, can help students stop postponing and start working steadily.","t":"許多大學生總是拖到重大截止日期的前一晚，花好幾週看影片、上網聊天，而不是完成作業。接著他們熬夜到天亮，匆忙趕完那些本該更用心對待的報告。心理學家解釋，人們往往會拖延不愉快的任務，因為他們害怕失敗或感到不堪負荷。他們建議，將大型專案拆解成較小的步驟，能幫助學生停止拖延，開始穩定地工作。","as":"Students who habitually procrastinate tend to underestimate the cumulative stress of looming deadlines, and the frantic, perfunctory work they produce at the last minute seldom reflects their latent ability or the knowledge they have actually acquired.","at":"習慣拖延的學生往往低估了截止日期逼近時不斷累積的壓力，而他們在最後一刻匆忙趕出的草率作品，很少能展現他們潛藏的能力，或他們真正學到的知識。"},{"w":"facet","p":"n.","d":"one side or view of a person or situation.","c":"方面；（寶石的）刻面","s":"Climate change affects nearly every facet of modern life, from agriculture and public health to international migration and economic stability. Rising temperatures reduce crop yields, while extreme weather damages homes and infrastructure. Scientists emphasize that addressing such a complex problem requires cooperation among engineers, economists, doctors, and policymakers. Focusing on only one aspect, they warn, would fail to capture the interconnected challenges that communities around the world are already experiencing.","t":"氣候變遷幾乎影響現代生活的每一個層面，從農業、公共衛生到國際移民與經濟穩定皆然。氣溫上升使農作物減產，極端天氣則破壞房屋與基礎建設。科學家強調，要解決這樣一個複雜的問題，需要工程師、經濟學家、醫生與政策制定者通力合作。他們警告，只關注單一面向，將無法掌握世界各地社區早已面臨的環環相扣的挑戰。","as":"The documentary illuminates a little-known facet of the eminent scientist's life: during the war, she carried out clandestine work forging passports to help persecuted families find sanctuary abroad, risking execution had she been caught.","at":"這部紀錄片揭示了這位傑出科學家鮮為人知的一面：戰爭期間，她冒著被捕即遭處決的風險，秘密偽造護照，幫助遭受迫害的家庭到海外尋求庇護。"},{"w":"foist","p":"v.","d":"to force upon, pass off slyly.","c":"強加；以欺騙手段推銷","s":"The dishonest shopkeeper tried to foistedamaged electronics on unsuspecting tourists, hiding scratches under stickers and claiming the products were brand new. Visitors who could not read the local language were especially easy targets. After several travelers posted angry reviews online, police investigated and discovered hundreds of defective items in the storeroom. The shop was closed, and consumer groups urged tourists to inspect purchases carefully before paying. Business at nearby shops improved afterward.","t":"這名不誠實的店主企圖把受損的電子產品硬塞給毫無戒心的觀光客，他用貼紙遮住刮痕，並聲稱這些產品是全新的。看不懂當地語言的遊客尤其容易成為目標。在幾名旅客於網路上發表憤怒的評論後，警方展開調查，在倉庫中發現了數百件瑕疵品。這家店被勒令歇業，消費者團體也呼籲遊客在付款前仔細檢查所購商品。之後附近商店的生意也隨之好轉。","as":"The antiques dealer tried to foist a fabricated 'Ming dynasty' vase on the gullible tourist, but a perspicacious appraiser quickly discerned the subtle flaws in its glaze and brushwork that betrayed the counterfeit.","at":"古董商企圖把一只偽造的「明代」花瓶硬塞給那名容易上當的觀光客，但一位眼光敏銳的鑑定師很快就從釉色與筆法的細微瑕疵中看出這是贗品。"},{"w":"stigmatize","p":"v.","d":"to mark with disgrace.","c":"污名化；使蒙羞","s":"Public health experts warn that societies should not stigmatize people who seek help for mental health problems. When individuals fear being labeled as weak or unstable, they often hide their struggles and avoid treatment. Campaigns featuring celebrities who speak openly about anxiety and depression have helped reduce this sense of shame. Researchers report that when communities stop attaching disgrace to such conditions, far more people are willing to ask for support.","t":"公共衛生專家警告，社會不應該污名化那些因心理健康問題而尋求協助的人。當人們害怕被貼上軟弱或不穩定的標籤時，他們往往會隱藏自己的困境並逃避治療。由名人公開談論焦慮與憂鬱的宣導活動，已幫助減少了這種羞恥感。研究人員指出，當社區不再將這些狀況與恥辱連結時，願意尋求支持的人便會大幅增加。","as":"For centuries, societies tended to stigmatize mental illness as a moral failing rather than a treatable malady, a pernicious bias that discouraged sufferers from seeking help and compounded their isolation from family and friends.","at":"數百年來，社會往往把精神疾病污名化為道德缺陷，而非可治療的疾病；這種有害的偏見使患者不敢求助，也讓他們與家人朋友更加疏離。"},{"w":"capitulate","p":"v.","d":"to surrender, make terms.","c":"投降；屈服","s":"After weeks of strikes that shut down the city's public transportation, the government finally decided to capitulate and accept the union's demands for higher wages and safer working conditions. Officials had initially refused to negotiate, insisting that the requests were unreasonable. However, growing public frustration and severe economic losses forced them to give in. Union leaders celebrated the agreement as a significant victory for workers throughout the country. Commuters were relieved when service resumed.","t":"在罷工讓全市大眾運輸停擺數週後，政府終於決定讓步，接受工會提高薪資與改善工作安全的要求。官員們起初拒絕談判，堅稱這些要求並不合理。然而，民眾日益高漲的不滿與嚴重的經濟損失，迫使他們不得不屈服。工會領袖慶祝這項協議是全國勞工的一大勝利。通勤族在服務恢復後都鬆了一口氣。","as":"After a forty-day siege left the garrison bereft of food and ammunition, the commander was finally forced to capitulate, though he stipulated that his soldiers be granted amnesty and safe passage home.","at":"在長達四十天的圍城使守軍糧盡彈絕後，指揮官最終被迫投降，但他提出條件：他的士兵必須獲得赦免，並能安全返鄉。"},{"w":"audacity","p":"n.","d":"boldness, daring.","c":"大膽；厚顏無恥","s":"The young entrepreneur had the audacity to present her business plan directly to the world's richest investor after sneaking into a private conference. Security guards tried to escort her out, but the investor, amused by her boldness, agreed to listen for five minutes. Her daring approach paid off spectacularly: he invested ten million dollars in her company that same afternoon. Business magazines later featured her story as an example of fearless ambition.","t":"這位年輕創業家竟有膽量溜進一場私人會議，直接向世界首富推銷她的商業計畫。保全人員試圖將她請出去，但這位投資人被她的大膽逗樂了，同意聽她說五分鐘。她大膽的做法獲得了驚人的回報：他當天下午就投資了一千萬美元到她的公司。商業雜誌後來將她的故事作為無畏雄心的範例加以報導。","as":"The young climber's audacity in attempting the treacherous summit alone and without supplemental oxygen astonished veteran mountaineers, some of whom castigated her as rash while others praised the intrepid spirit that had driven her to the top.","at":"這位年輕登山者竟敢在不帶氧氣瓶的情況下獨自挑戰險峻的山峰，其大膽令資深登山家震驚；有些人嚴厲批評她魯莽，也有人讚揚那股帶她登頂的無畏精神。"},{"w":"tantalize","p":"v.","d":"to tease or torment by offering something good but withholding it.","c":"逗弄；使可望而不可即","s":"The bakery's window displays seemed designed to tantalize hungry students walking home from school, featuring warm croissants, chocolate cakes, and colorful pastries arranged beautifully behind the glass. The delicious smells drifted into the street, tempting everyone who passed. Unfortunately, the prices were far beyond most students' pocket money. Many would pause outside for several minutes, staring longingly at treats they knew they could not afford to buy. A few saved for weeks to buy one.","t":"這家麵包店的櫥窗陳列彷彿是專門用來逗弄放學回家的飢餓學生，玻璃後面擺放著溫熱的可頌、巧克力蛋糕和五顏六色的糕點，排列得十分精美。香甜的氣味飄散到街上，誘惑著每個經過的人。可惜的是，價格遠遠超出大多數學生的零用錢。許多人會在店外駐足好幾分鐘，渴望地盯著那些他們明知買不起的點心。有幾個人存了好幾週的錢才買到一個。","as":"Through ubiquitous advertisements, marketers tantalize consumers with glimpses of luxurious lifestyles that remain forever out of reach, and critics contend that this strategy fosters an insatiable materialism that leaves people chronically discontented.","at":"行銷人員透過無所不在的廣告，讓消費者看見永遠遙不可及的奢華生活，吊足他們的胃口；批評者認為，這種手法助長了永不滿足的物質主義，使人們長期感到不滿。"},{"w":"retort","p":"v.","d":"to answer, reply sharply.","c":"反駁；回嘴","s":"When a reporter suggested that the elderly candidate was too old to govern effectively, she paused and then retort that experience and wisdom were exactly what the country needed during difficult times. The audience burst into applause at her quick, sharp reply. Political commentators agreed that her confident response had turned a potential weakness into a strength. Her poll numbers rose significantly in the days following the widely shared exchange.","t":"當一名記者暗示這位年長的候選人年紀太大、無法有效治理時，她停頓了一下，隨即反駁說，經驗與智慧正是國家在艱難時期所需要的。觀眾對她機敏犀利的回應報以熱烈掌聲。政治評論員一致認為，她自信的回答將潛在的弱點轉化為優勢。在這段廣為流傳的交鋒之後幾天，她的民調支持率大幅上升。","as":"When a heckler derided her proposal as absurd, the candidate retorted with a terse, caustic remark about his own record that drew applause from the throng and left her adversary momentarily speechless.","at":"當一名起鬨者嘲笑她的提案荒謬可笑時，這位候選人以一句簡短而辛辣、直指對方過往紀錄的話犀利回擊，贏得群眾的掌聲，也讓她的對手一時語塞。"},{"w":"reticent","p":"adj.","d":"silent, reserved.","c":"沉默寡言的；有保留的","s":"The famous novelist was notoriously reticent about her private life, refusing to discuss her family, relationships, or personal history in interviews. She believed that readers should focus on her books rather than on her biography. Journalists who asked personal questions received only polite smiles and brief, unrevealing answers. Even her closest friends respected her reserved nature, and her biography remained largely a mystery until letters were discovered after her death.","t":"這位知名小說家出了名地對私生活絕口不提，在訪談中拒絕談論她的家庭、感情或個人經歷。她認為讀者應該關注她的作品，而非她的生平。問起私人問題的記者，只會得到禮貌的微笑和簡短、不透露任何資訊的回答。就連她最親近的朋友也尊重她內斂的個性，直到她過世後書信被發現，她的生平在很大程度上仍是個謎。","as":"Though normally reticent about her private life, the Nobel laureate spoke with unusual candor in her final interview, describing the doleful circumstances of her childhood and the solace she had found in mathematics.","at":"這位諾貝爾獎得主平常對私生活總是三緘其口，但在最後一次訪談中卻罕見地坦誠，談起她童年的悲慘處境，以及她在數學中找到的慰藉。"},{"w":"tacit","p":"adj.","d":"understood, implied, not stated.","c":"心照不宣的；默許的","s":"The two roommates never discussed household chores, but they had a tacit agreement that whoever cooked dinner would not have to wash the dishes. Over three years, this unspoken arrangement worked perfectly, and neither ever complained. Psychologists note that many successful relationships depend on such implicit understandings, which develop naturally through shared experience. However, they caution that assumptions left unstated can also lead to misunderstandings when circumstances change unexpectedly. Clear communication remains important.","t":"這兩位室友從未討論過家務分配，卻有一個心照不宣的默契：負責煮晚餐的人就不必洗碗。三年來，這個不言而喻的安排運作得十分完美，雙方都沒有抱怨過。心理學家指出，許多成功的關係都仰賴這類隱含的默契，它們是透過共同的經歷自然形成的。然而他們也提醒，未說出口的假設在情況意外改變時，也可能導致誤會。清楚的溝通仍然很重要。","as":"Although no formal treaty was ever signed, the two hostile nations maintained a tacit agreement not to provoke each other for decades, until a minor border skirmish set off an inexorable escalation into full-scale war.","at":"雖然從未簽訂正式條約，這兩個敵對國家數十年來一直維持著互不挑釁的默契，直到一場小規模的邊境衝突引發無法遏止的情勢升級，演變成全面戰爭。"},{"w":"chicanery","p":"n.","d":"trickery, underhandedness.","c":"詭計；欺騙","s":"The election was marred by widespread chicanery, including forged ballots, bribed officials, and voters who were illegally turned away from polling stations. International observers documented hundreds of irregularities and concluded that the official results could not be trusted. Opposition parties organized massive protests demanding a new election. Eventually, the country's highest court ordered a recount, confirming that deliberate trickery had changed the outcome in several important districts. Several officials were later imprisoned.","t":"這場選舉因廣泛的詭計而蒙上陰影，包括偽造選票、賄賂官員，以及選民在投票所被非法拒於門外。國際觀察員記錄了數百起違規情事，並斷定官方結果不可信。反對黨組織大規模抗議，要求重新選舉。最終，該國最高法院下令重新計票，證實了刻意的欺騙手段改變了數個重要選區的結果。數名官員後來被判入獄。","as":"Investigators uncovered rampant chicanery in the disputed election, from surreptitious ballot tampering to the intimidation of voters at polling stations, and a court eventually moved to invalidate the results in three districts.","at":"調查人員發現這場備受爭議的選舉中詭計橫行，從暗中竄改選票到在投票所恐嚇選民無所不有，法院最終宣告三個選區的選舉結果無效。"},{"w":"obliging","p":"adj.","d":"accommodating, helpful.","c":"樂於助人的；親切的","s":"The hotel receptionist was remarkably obliging, arranging a late checkout, recommending local restaurants, and even lending an umbrella to guests caught in the sudden rain. When a family's luggage was lost by the airline, she personally called the airport several times until the suitcases were located. Online reviews consistently praised her helpful attitude, and the hotel's management eventually promoted her to guest relations manager in recognition of her exceptional service.","t":"這位飯店櫃檯人員非常樂於助人，她為客人安排延後退房、推薦當地餐廳，甚至把雨傘借給遇上突如其來大雨的房客。當一家人的行李被航空公司遺失時，她親自打了好幾通電話到機場，直到找到行李箱為止。網路評論一致讚揚她熱心助人的態度，飯店管理階層最終將她升為賓客關係經理，以表彰她卓越的服務。","as":"The obliging innkeeper went out of his way to accommodate the weary travelers, offering them a congenial room by the fire, a sumptuous late-night meal, and a welcome respite from the storm raging outside.","at":"這位熱心周到的旅店老闆特地盡力照顧疲憊的旅客，為他們安排爐火旁舒適宜人的房間、一頓豐盛的宵夜，讓他們得以暫時躲避屋外肆虐的暴風雨。"}]},{"unit":39,"cards":[{"w":"saga","p":"n.","d":"long heroic story.","c":"傳奇；長篇故事","s":"The novel tells the saga of three generations of a Taiwanese family, beginning with a young farmer who arrived from Fujian in the nineteenth century. Over nearly six hundred pages, readers follow his descendants through wars, economic hardship, political change, and eventual prosperity. Critics praised the author for weaving personal struggles into major historical events. Many readers described the sweeping family chronicle as one of the most moving books they had ever read.","t":"這部小說講述一個台灣家族三代人的傳奇，從十九世紀一位從福建渡海而來的年輕農夫開始。在將近六百頁的篇幅中，讀者跟隨他的子孫歷經戰爭、經濟困頓、政治變遷，最終走向富足。評論家讚揚作者將個人的奮鬥融入重大歷史事件之中。許多讀者形容這部波瀾壯闊的家族史詩，是他們讀過最感人的書籍之一。","as":"Drawing on annals kept by itinerant monks, the historian reconstructed the saga of a nomadic clan whose valor in repulsing invaders was later embellished by generations of storytellers into near-mythic legend.","at":"歷史學家根據四處遊歷的僧侶所留下的編年史，重建了一個游牧部族的英雄史詩；該部族擊退入侵者的英勇事蹟，後來被一代又一代的說書人加油添醋，幾乎成了神話傳說。"},{"w":"belated","p":"adj.","d":"late, delayed.","c":"遲來的","s":"Two weeks after forgetting his best friend's birthday, the embarrassed teenager finally delivered a belated gift along with a handwritten apology. He had been so busy preparing for examinations that the date had completely slipped his mind. His friend laughed and accepted the present graciously, saying that the thoughtful note mattered more than the timing. The two later joked that the overdue celebration had actually lasted longer than a normal birthday.","t":"在忘記最好朋友的生日兩週後，這名尷尬的青少年終於送上一份遲來的禮物，並附上一張手寫的道歉卡。他一直忙著準備考試，完全忘了這個日子。他的朋友笑著大方地收下禮物，說這張用心的卡片比時間更重要。兩人後來開玩笑說，這場遲來的慶祝其實比一般的生日持續得更久。","as":"The ministry's belated admission that the water supply was contaminated did little to quell public consternation, since residents had already endured months of malady and sporadic shortages before any official acknowledged the problem.","at":"部會遲遲才承認供水遭到汙染，這幾乎無法平息民眾的驚恐，因為在任何官員承認問題之前，居民早已忍受了好幾個月的疾病與斷斷續續的缺水。"},{"w":"decrepit","p":"adj.","d":"broken down, worn out.","c":"衰老的；破舊的","s":"The decrepit farmhouse had been abandoned for nearly forty years, and its roof had partially collapsed after countless typhoons. Broken windows let rain pour into the rooms, and wild plants grew through cracks in the wooden floors. When a young architect purchased the property, neighbors assumed she would demolish it. Instead, she spent three years carefully restoring the crumbling structure, transforming it into a beautiful guesthouse that preserved its historic character.","t":"這棟破舊的農舍已荒廢將近四十年，屋頂在無數次颱風後部分坍塌。破掉的窗戶讓雨水灌進屋內，野生植物從木地板的裂縫中長了出來。當一位年輕建築師買下這處房產時，鄰居們以為她會把它拆掉。然而她卻花了三年時間細心修復這座搖搖欲墜的建築，將它改造成一間保留歷史特色的美麗民宿。","as":"Once a prestigious opera house, the decrepit edifice had been relegated to use as a warehouse, its gilded balconies crumbling and its murky corridors permeated by the pungent odor of mildew.","at":"這座破敗的建築曾是聲譽卓著的歌劇院，如今卻淪為倉庫：鍍金的包廂逐漸崩落，昏暗的走廊瀰漫著刺鼻的霉味。"},{"w":"imperturbable","p":"adj.","d":"calm, steady, serene.","c":"鎮定的；泰然自若的","s":"Throughout the chaotic press conference, the spokesperson remained completely imperturbable, answering hostile questions in a calm, steady voice while reporters shouted over one another. Even when one journalist accused her of lying, she simply smiled and repeated the facts patiently. Her colleagues marveled at her composure under such intense pressure. Communication experts later used video of the event to teach young professionals how to handle aggressive questioning without losing control.","t":"在整場混亂的記者會中，這位發言人始終泰然自若，在記者們七嘴八舌大喊時，以平靜穩定的語氣回答充滿敵意的問題。即使一名記者指控她說謊，她也只是微笑，耐心地重申事實。同事們對她在如此巨大壓力下的沉著感到驚嘆。溝通專家後來用這場記者會的影片，教導年輕專業人士如何在不失控的情況下應對咄咄逼人的提問。","as":"Even as the televised debate devolved into bedlam, the veteran moderator remained imperturbable, responding to each caustic remark with such equanimity that the most belligerent panelists eventually desisted and returned to the questions at hand.","at":"即使電視辯論已陷入一片混亂，資深主持人依然泰然自若，以極其沉著的態度回應每一句尖酸刻薄的發言，最終連最好鬥的與談人也停止攻擊，回到眼前的議題上。"},{"w":"vacillate","p":"v.","d":"to hesitate, fluctuate.","c":"猶豫不決；搖擺","s":"For months, the high school senior continued to vacillate between studying medicine and pursuing a career in music. One week she felt certain that becoming a doctor was the practical choice; the next week she dreamed of performing on international stages. Her parents grew frustrated by her constant hesitation. Finally, a conversation with a doctor who also played in an orchestra convinced her that she might combine both passions. She is now studying medicine happily.","t":"好幾個月來，這名高三學生一直在學醫與追求音樂事業之間猶豫不決。這一週她確信成為醫生是務實的選擇；下一週她又夢想著站上國際舞台演出。她的父母對她不斷的搖擺感到沮喪。最後，與一位同時在管弦樂團演奏的醫生的一席話，讓她相信自己或許能兼顧這兩項熱情。她如今快樂地攻讀醫學。","as":"Legislators continued to vacillate between curtailing fossil-fuel subsidies and appeasing powerful industrial donors, a pattern of indecision that critics deemed symptomatic of a government too timorous to confront an imminent environmental crisis.","at":"立法者在削減化石燃料補貼與安撫有權勢的產業捐款者之間猶豫不決；批評者認為，這種優柔寡斷正顯示出政府過於膽怯，不敢正視迫在眉睫的環境危機。"},{"w":"staunch","p":"adj.","d":"strong, trusty, firm.","c":"堅定的；忠誠的","s":"The elderly woman has been a staunch supporter of the local baseball team for more than sixty years, attending nearly every home game regardless of weather or the team's performance. Even during seasons when the players lost repeatedly, she remained loyal, cheering loudly from her usual seat behind third base. The club eventually honored her steadfast devotion by naming a section of the stadium after her. Fans often ask for her autograph.","t":"這位老太太六十多年來一直是當地棒球隊的忠實球迷，無論天氣如何或球隊表現好壞，她幾乎每場主場比賽都到場。即使在球員屢戰屢敗的球季，她依然忠心不二，從她三壘後方的老位子上大聲加油。球團最終以她的名字為球場的一個區域命名，以表彰她堅定不移的熱愛。球迷們常向她索取簽名。","as":"A staunch defender of public education, the senator adamantly refused to tolerate any budget that slashed funding for indigent districts, insisting that schooling was an inviolable right of every child rather than a privilege.","at":"這位參議員是公共教育的堅定捍衛者，她堅決拒絕容忍任何削減貧困學區經費的預算，並堅持受教育是每個孩子不可侵犯的權利，而非特權。"},{"w":"opprobrium","p":"n.","d":"scorn, insult, public disgrace.","c":"恥辱；公開的譴責","s":"The company faced international opprobrium after journalists revealed that its factories had been dumping toxic waste into rivers used by thousands of villagers. Environmental organizations condemned the company, consumers organized boycotts, and several countries banned its products. Executives who had once been celebrated as business leaders were suddenly treated with public scorn. The disgrace eventually forced the chief executive to resign and the company to fund an expensive cleanup program.","t":"在記者揭露該公司工廠一直將有毒廢棄物排入數千名村民使用的河川後，這家公司遭受國際社會的強烈譴責。環保組織對其大加撻伐，消費者發起抵制，數個國家也禁止其產品進口。曾被譽為商界領袖的高層主管，突然成為眾人鄙視的對象。這場恥辱最終迫使執行長辭職，公司也不得不出資推動一項昂貴的清理計畫。","as":"The chemical firm incurred international opprobrium when journalists revealed that it had surreptitiously dumped lethal waste into a river, a flagrant breach of ethics that its executives initially tried to palliate with euphemisms.","at":"記者揭露這家化學公司偷偷將致命廢棄物傾倒入河中後，該公司遭到國際輿論的強烈譴責；這是明目張膽違反道德的行為，而高層起初還試圖用委婉說法來替自己開脫。"},{"w":"Machiavellian","p":"adj.","d":"cunning, governed by opportunity rather than principle.","c":"不擇手段的；權謀的","s":"In the popular television drama, the Machiavellian prime minister manipulates allies, betrays friends, and spreads false rumors about rivals in order to stay in power. He treats every relationship as a tool for achieving his ambitions and never hesitates to deceive anyone who stands in his way. Viewers find his cunning schemes both fascinating and disturbing. Critics describe the character as a brilliant portrait of unscrupulous political ambition. The show has won numerous awards.","t":"在這部熱門電視劇中，這位不擇手段的首相為了保住權力，操弄盟友、背叛朋友，並散布關於對手的不實謠言。他把每一段關係都視為實現野心的工具，毫不猶豫地欺騙任何擋路的人。觀眾覺得他狡猾的陰謀既引人入勝又令人不安。評論家形容這個角色是對毫無原則的政治野心的精彩刻畫。這部劇已贏得無數獎項。","as":"The chancellor's Machiavellian strategy—feigning friendship with rival factions while clandestinely fomenting discord between them—allowed him to oust his adversaries one by one without ever appearing culpable in the eyes of the public.","at":"這位首相採取權謀詭詐的策略：表面上與敵對派系假意交好，暗中卻挑撥他們彼此不和，因此得以把對手一一趕下台，而在大眾眼中自己卻從未顯得有任何過失。"},{"w":"unconscionable","p":"adj.","d":"unreasonable, unjust, shocking to the conscience.","c":"沒良心的；不合理的","s":"Consumer groups described the pharmacy's decision to triple the price of a life-saving medicine during a health emergency as completely unconscionable. Patients who depended on the drug suddenly could not afford their treatment, and some were forced to skip doses. Lawmakers condemned the price increase as morally indefensible and introduced legislation to prevent similar exploitation. Under intense public pressure, the pharmacy eventually reduced its prices and apologized to affected customers.","t":"消費者團體形容這家藥局在衛生緊急狀況期間將救命藥物的價格提高三倍，是完全沒有良心的決定。依賴這種藥物的病患突然負擔不起治療費用，有些人被迫減少服藥次數。立法者譴責這次漲價在道德上站不住腳，並提出法案以防止類似的剝削行為。在強大的輿論壓力下，這家藥局最終調降價格，並向受影響的顧客道歉。","as":"Investigators deemed it unconscionable that the landlord had raised rents on emaciated tenants during a famine, an act of avarice so egregious that even his former confidants publicly repudiated him.","at":"調查人員認為，房東在饑荒期間對骨瘦如柴的房客調漲租金，實在天理難容；這種貪婪行徑惡劣至極，連他昔日的心腹都公開與他劃清界線。"},{"w":"pandemonium","p":"n.","d":"disorder, uproar.","c":"大混亂；喧囂","s":"pandemonium broke out in the stadium when the home team scored the winning goal in the final seconds of the championship match. Fans leaped over barriers, strangers hugged each other, and firecrackers exploded throughout the stands. Security guards struggled to control the celebrating crowd that rushed onto the field. The joyful chaos continued in the streets for hours, as drivers honked their horns and residents danced outside their homes. Nobody slept much that night.","t":"當地主隊在冠軍賽最後幾秒踢進致勝一球時，體育場內頓時陷入一片狂亂。球迷們跳過護欄，陌生人互相擁抱，看台上鞭炮四處炸響。保全人員難以控制衝進場內慶祝的人群。這場歡樂的混亂在街頭持續了好幾個小時，駕駛們猛按喇叭，居民們在家門外跳起舞來。那天晚上幾乎沒有人睡得著。","as":"When the stadium's lights failed during the championship, pandemonium erupted: a throng of fans jostled toward the exits, and the stentorian warnings of security officers were drowned out by a cacophony of panicked voices.","at":"冠軍賽進行中球場燈光突然熄滅，現場頓時陷入一片混亂：大批球迷推擠著湧向出口，保全人員宏亮的警告聲也被驚慌失措的嘈雜人聲所淹沒。"},{"w":"flay","p":"v.","d":"to strip off the skin; to scold harshly.","c":"剝皮；嚴厲批評","s":"Theater critics did not hesitate to flay the expensive new musical, describing its songs as forgettable, its plot as confusing, and its lead performances as painfully stiff. One reviewer called it the worst production he had seen in thirty years. The harsh criticism spread quickly online, and ticket sales collapsed within a week. The producers closed the show early, admitting that the brutal reviews had made recovery impossible. The composer vowed to try again.","t":"劇評家毫不留情地嚴厲抨擊這部昂貴的新音樂劇，形容其歌曲毫無記憶點、劇情混亂不清，主角的表演更是僵硬得令人難受。一位評論家稱它是他三十年來看過最糟糕的製作。這些嚴厲的批評迅速在網路上傳開，票房在一週內崩盤。製作人提前結束演出，並承認這些無情的評論讓該劇無法挽回。作曲家誓言要捲土重來。","as":"In a vitriolic review published on opening night, the critic flayed the director's latest film, deriding its banal dialogue and lackluster performances as proof that the once-prolific filmmaker had squandered his virtuosity.","at":"這位影評人在首映當晚發表一篇尖酸刻薄的評論，嚴厲痛批導演的新片，嘲笑其對白陳腐、演出平淡乏味，認為這證明了這位曾經多產的導演已經揮霍掉自己的精湛才華。"},{"w":"demeanor","p":"n.","d":"conduct, bearing, outward manner.","c":"舉止；風度","s":"The new teacher's friendly demeanor put nervous students at ease on the first day of school. She greeted each child with a warm smile, spoke gently, and listened patiently when they described their summer vacations. Parents noticed that even shy children seemed eager to attend her class. Her calm, cheerful behavior created a welcoming atmosphere that encouraged students to ask questions and participate actively throughout the year. She was later named teacher of the year.","t":"新老師親切的舉止讓緊張的學生們在開學第一天就放鬆下來。她以溫暖的微笑迎接每個孩子，說話溫柔，並耐心聆聽他們描述自己的暑假。家長們注意到，即使是害羞的孩子也似乎很期待上她的課。她沉穩開朗的態度營造出友善的氛圍，鼓勵學生整年都積極提問與參與。她後來獲選為年度最佳教師。","as":"Despite her urbane demeanor at diplomatic receptions, the ambassador was known among her coterie of aides as an astute and occasionally irascible negotiator who rarely let a salient detail escape her notice.","at":"雖然這位大使在外交酒會上舉止溫文儒雅，但在她身邊的幕僚圈中，她是出了名精明、偶爾脾氣火爆的談判者，任何重要細節幾乎都逃不過她的眼睛。"},{"w":"delineation","p":"n.","d":"sketch, description in words or lines.","c":"描繪；描述；輪廓","s":"The novelist's careful delineation of the main character's inner thoughts allowed readers to understand her motivations deeply. Through detailed descriptions of her memories, fears, and hopes, the author created a portrait so vivid that many readers felt they personally knew her. Literature professors frequently use the book to demonstrate how skillful character description can transform a simple plot into a powerful and emotionally complex story. It has been translated into twenty languages.","t":"這位小說家對主角內心想法的細膩描繪，讓讀者能深入理解她的動機。透過對她的回憶、恐懼與希望的詳盡描述，作者塑造出一個如此鮮活的形象，讓許多讀者覺得自己彷彿真的認識她。文學教授經常以這本書來說明，高明的人物描寫如何能將簡單的情節轉化為一個強而有力、情感複雜的故事。這本書已被翻譯成二十種語言。","as":"The cartographer's meticulous delineation of the subterranean cave system, which marked every tortuous passage and hidden cache of artifacts, proved integral to the archaeologists' later excavations, sparing them months of dangerous exploration.","at":"製圖師對這座地下洞穴系統做了一絲不苟的描繪，標出了每一條蜿蜒曲折的通道與每一處藏有古文物的隱密地點，這對考古學家日後的挖掘工作至關重要，替他們省下了好幾個月的危險探勘。"},{"w":"vindicate","p":"v.","d":"to clear of blame, justify.","c":"證明清白；證明…正確","s":"The scientist's controversial prediction was mocked by colleagues for years, but new satellite data finally helped vindicate her theory about melting glaciers. Measurements showed that ice sheets were disappearing exactly as she had calculated decades earlier. Researchers who had once dismissed her work publicly acknowledged their mistake. She was later awarded a prestigious international prize, and her once-rejected ideas now form the foundation of modern climate models. Her story now inspires young scientists everywhere.","t":"這位科學家具爭議性的預測多年來一直遭同行嘲笑，但新的衛星資料終於證實了她關於冰河融化的理論。測量結果顯示，冰層正如她數十年前所計算的那樣在消失。曾經否定她研究的學者們公開承認了自己的錯誤。她後來獲頒一項享有盛譽的國際大獎，而她曾被否定的想法，如今已成為現代氣候模型的基礎。她的故事如今激勵著各地的年輕科學家。","as":"New DNA evidence finally vindicated the octogenarian, who had spent forty years branded a felon for a crime he did not commit; the state formally exonerated him and offered remuneration, though no sum could restore his lost youth.","at":"新的DNA證據終於還給這位八旬老翁清白；他為了一樁自己沒犯下的罪，被冠上重罪犯之名長達四十年。州政府正式宣告他無罪並給予補償，但再多的金錢也換不回他失去的青春。"},{"w":"heinous","p":"adj.","d":"hatefully evil, shockingly wicked.","c":"十惡不赦的；極其可憎的","s":"The judge described the defendant's crimes as truly heinous, noting that he had deliberately defrauded hundreds of elderly retirees of their life savings while pretending to be their trusted financial advisor. Many victims had lost their homes and could no longer afford medical care. The judge imposed the maximum sentence, explaining that such shockingly wicked behavior, targeting the most vulnerable members of society, deserved the strongest possible punishment. Victims applauded the decision.","t":"法官形容被告的罪行實在是十惡不赦，並指出他假扮成值得信賴的理財顧問，蓄意詐騙了數百名年長退休人士的畢生積蓄。許多受害者失去了房子，再也負擔不起醫療費用。法官判處最重的刑罰，並解釋說，這種鎖定社會中最弱勢族群、令人震驚的邪惡行為，理應受到最嚴厲的懲罰。受害者們對此判決報以掌聲。","as":"The tribunal described the massacre of unarmed villagers as a heinous atrocity, rejecting the general's pretext that his troops had acted under duress and insisting that those who perpetrated it must not enjoy impunity.","at":"法庭將屠殺手無寸鐵村民的行為定調為令人髮指的暴行，駁回將軍所謂部隊是在脅迫下行事的藉口，並堅持犯下此罪的人絕不能逍遙法外。"},{"w":"turpitude","p":"n.","d":"vileness, wickedness.","c":"卑鄙；墮落","s":"The university dismissed the professor for moral turpitude after investigators discovered that he had sold stolen examination papers to wealthy students for years. His actions betrayed the trust of colleagues, damaged the institution's reputation, and cheated honest students out of fair evaluation. Legal experts explained that employment contracts often allow immediate termination for such serious wickedness, since it undermines the fundamental values an organization is supposed to represent. Several students were also expelled.","t":"在調查人員發現這名教授多年來一直將偷來的考卷賣給富有的學生後，大學以道德敗壞為由將他解聘。他的行為辜負了同事的信任，損害了學校的聲譽，也剝奪了誠實學生接受公平評量的權利。法律專家解釋，僱傭契約通常允許因這類嚴重的惡行而立即解僱，因為它破壞了一個組織應該代表的基本價值。數名學生也遭到退學。","as":"The scandal exposed the moral turpitude of the city's elite: officials had colluded in an extortion scheme that preyed on the plight of vulnerable immigrants, and their accomplices had fabricated records to conceal it.","at":"這起醜聞揭露了該市權貴的道德敗壞：官員們串通進行勒索，利用弱勢移民的困境牟利，而他們的共犯還偽造紀錄來掩蓋真相。"},{"w":"infraction","p":"n.","d":"violation of a rule or law.","c":"違規；違法","s":"The referee stopped the match after the player committed his third infraction of the game, deliberately tripping an opponent who was about to score. Under tournament rules, repeated violations result in automatic suspension. Although the player argued that the contact was accidental, video replay clearly showed otherwise. The league later fined him heavily and warned all teams that intentional breaches of the rules would be punished more severely in future.","t":"在這名球員犯下本場比賽第三次犯規、蓄意絆倒一名即將得分的對手後，裁判中止了比賽。依照錦標賽規則，屢次違規將自動遭到禁賽。雖然這名球員辯稱接觸是意外，但影片重播清楚顯示並非如此。聯盟後來對他處以重罰，並警告所有球隊，未來蓄意違反規則將受到更嚴厲的懲處。","as":"Under the new mandate, even a minor infraction—such as filing a safety report one day late—could result in heavy fines, a restrictive policy that critics argued would stymie innovation and jeopardize small businesses.","at":"根據新的命令，即使是輕微的違規，例如晚一天提交安全報告，也可能招致高額罰款；批評者認為，這項嚴苛的政策將阻礙創新，並危及小型企業的生存。"},{"w":"callous","p":"adj.","d":"unfeeling, insensitive.","c":"冷酷無情的","s":"The landlord's callous response shocked the tenants who had lost everything in the apartment fire. Instead of offering sympathy or temporary housing, he immediately demanded that they pay the remaining rent and remove their damaged belongings within two days. Neighbors who witnessed the conversation were horrified by his lack of compassion. Local newspapers reported the story, and community members quickly organized donations to help the families he had treated so heartlessly.","t":"房東冷酷無情的反應讓在公寓火災中失去一切的房客們大為震驚。他非但沒有表示同情或提供臨時住所，反而立刻要求他們付清剩餘的房租，並在兩天內搬走受損的物品。目睹這段對話的鄰居們對他毫無同情心感到震驚。地方報紙報導了這則消息，社區居民迅速發起捐款，幫助這些遭他無情對待的家庭。","as":"The CEO's callous remark that laid-off workers should simply 'cope with change' provoked public outrage, and shareholders soon castigated the board for its contemptuous indifference to the hardship of employees who had served the company loyally.","at":"執行長冷血地表示被裁員的員工只要「適應變化」就好，這番話引發眾怒，股東們隨即嚴厲譴責董事會，對那些忠心為公司效力的員工所面臨的困境，表現出輕蔑與漠不關心。"},{"w":"redress","p":"v.","d":"to right a wrong, remedy.","c":"糾正；補償","s":"The government established a special commission to redress injustices suffered by families whose land had been seized illegally during the martial law period. Officials reviewed thousands of documents, interviewed elderly survivors, and calculated appropriate compensation for each case. Although money could never fully repair the damage, many families welcomed the official apology and financial settlements. Historians described the process as an important step toward correcting past wrongs. The commission's work continues today.","t":"政府成立了一個特別委員會，以彌補在戒嚴時期土地遭非法徵收的家庭所蒙受的不公。官員們審閱了數千份文件、訪談年長的倖存者，並為每個案件計算適當的賠償金額。雖然金錢永遠無法完全彌補傷害，許多家庭仍對官方的道歉與財務補償表示歡迎。歷史學家形容這個過程是糾正過去錯誤的重要一步。委員會的工作至今仍在持續。","as":"To redress the historical injustices inflicted on indigenous communities, the government pledged to return ancestral lands, though skeptics doubted that returning a nominal fraction of the territory could expunge the memory of centuries of privation.","at":"為了彌補原住民族群所遭受的歷史不公，政府承諾歸還祖傳土地；但懷疑者認為，只歸還象徵性的一小部分土地，無法抹去數百年來貧困匱乏的記憶。"},{"w":"vituperation","p":"n.","d":"harsh blame, verbal abuse.","c":"謾罵；辱罵","s":"The online forum became so filled with vituperation that the moderators finally decided to shut it down. Users who disagreed about politics had begun attacking each other with vicious insults, threats, and personal accusations rather than reasonable arguments. Many thoughtful members left the community entirely. The administrators explained that constructive discussion had become impossible in an atmosphere of constant abuse, and they introduced strict rules for a new, carefully monitored platform.","t":"這個網路論壇充斥著大量謾罵，版主們最終決定將其關閉。政治立場不同的使用者開始以惡毒的侮辱、威脅與人身攻擊互相攻訐，而非提出合理的論點。許多理性的成員完全離開了這個社群。管理員解釋，在不斷的辱罵氛圍中，建設性的討論已不可能進行，於是他們為一個受到嚴格監管的新平台制定了嚴格的規則。","as":"As the race tightened, the candidate's campaign speeches descended into vituperation: each rally became a diatribe of scurrilous epithets hurled at opponents, alienating moderate voters and eclipsing any pertinent discussion of policy.","at":"隨著選情趨於緊繃，這位候選人的競選演說淪為一連串的謾罵：每場造勢活動都變成對對手的激烈抨擊，充斥著粗鄙下流的綽號，不僅讓中間選民反感，也使任何切題的政策討論黯然失色。"}]},{"unit":40,"cards":[{"w":"rhetoric","p":"n.","d":"use (sometimes exaggerated) of language.","c":"修辭；浮誇的言語","s":"The candidate's speech was full of powerful rhetoric, promising a golden age of prosperity, perfect schools, and an end to poverty within four years. His dramatic language and emotional appeals excited the enormous crowd, who cheered after nearly every sentence. However, economists who examined his proposals found few concrete details about funding or implementation. They warned voters that inspiring words, however persuasive, cannot replace realistic policies supported by careful planning and evidence.","t":"這位候選人的演說充滿了強而有力的修辭，承諾在四年內迎來繁榮的黃金時代、打造完美的學校，並終結貧窮。他戲劇性的言詞與情感訴求讓廣大群眾熱血沸騰，幾乎每說一句話就響起歡呼。然而，研究他政見的經濟學家卻發現，其中關於經費來源與執行方式的具體細節寥寥無幾。他們提醒選民，激勵人心的言語無論多麼有說服力，都無法取代有周詳規劃與證據支持的務實政策。","as":"Though the populist's soaring rhetoric promised a utopia of shared prosperity, astute economists perceived that his proposals were fallacious, relying on emotional appeals to frustrated voters rather than on cogent evidence or careful analysis.","at":"儘管這位民粹政客慷慨激昂的言詞許諾了一個人人共享繁榮的烏托邦，精明的經濟學家卻看出他的提案謬誤百出，靠的是訴諸失意選民的情緒，而非有說服力的證據或審慎的分析。"},{"w":"clique","p":"n.","d":"small, exclusive group of people.","c":"小圈子；派系","s":"During her first month at the new school, the transfer student felt lonely because the popular clique in her class refused to let newcomers sit at their lunch table. The small group of friends shared private jokes, wore similar clothes, and ignored anyone outside their circle. Eventually, she joined the school orchestra, where she found welcoming classmates who shared her interests. By the end of the year, she had formed genuine, lasting friendships.","t":"在新學校的第一個月，這名轉學生感到很孤單，因為班上那個受歡迎的小圈子拒絕讓新同學坐在他們的午餐桌。這一小群朋友分享只有自己懂的笑話、穿著相似的衣服，並忽視任何圈外的人。最後，她加入了學校管弦樂團，在那裡找到了友善且興趣相投的同學。到了學年結束時，她已結交了真誠而長久的友誼。","as":"At the elite boarding school, a clique of wealthy heirs wielded inordinate influence over student life, perpetuating a culture of disdain toward scholarship recipients and relegating them to the margins of every social event.","at":"在這所菁英寄宿學校裡，一小群富家子弟組成的小圈子對校園生活擁有過大的影響力，延續著輕視獎學金學生的風氣，並把這些學生排擠到每個社交活動的邊緣。"},{"w":"extol","p":"v.","d":"to praise highly.","c":"讚美；頌揚","s":"Food critics from around the world continue to extol the small family restaurant in Tainan, describing its beef soup as the finest breakfast they have ever tasted. Magazines have published enthusiastic articles praising the fresh ingredients, the rich broth, and the owner's decades of dedication. Despite such glowing reviews, the elderly owner refuses to raise prices or open additional branches. She insists that serving her neighbors well matters more than international fame or profit.","t":"世界各地的美食評論家不斷盛讚台南這間小小的家庭餐館，形容它的牛肉湯是他們吃過最棒的早餐。雜誌紛紛刊出熱情洋溢的文章，稱讚新鮮的食材、濃郁的湯頭，以及老闆數十年如一日的用心。儘管獲得如此高的評價，年邁的老闆娘仍拒絕漲價或開設分店。她堅持，好好服務鄰居比國際名氣或利潤更重要。","as":"Biographers have long extolled Marie Curie's assiduous research, noting that she persevered through poverty and gender bias to make discoveries about radioactivity that remain a pinnacle of early twentieth-century physics.","at":"傳記作家長久以來盛讚居禮夫人孜孜不倦的研究，指出她在貧困與性別偏見中堅持不懈，在放射性方面的發現至今仍是二十世紀初物理學的巔峰之一。"},{"w":"mentor","p":"n.","d":"counselor, coach, tutor.","c":"導師；良師益友","s":"When the young engineer joined the technology company, a senior colleague volunteered to serve as her mentor, meeting with her weekly to discuss challenges, review her projects, and offer career advice. He introduced her to important contacts and encouraged her to present her ideas confidently at meetings. Years later, after becoming a department director herself, she followed his example by guiding several new employees through their first difficult years in the industry.","t":"當這位年輕工程師加入這家科技公司時，一位資深同事自願擔任她的導師，每週與她見面討論遇到的挑戰、檢視她的專案，並提供職涯建議。他介紹她認識重要的人脈，並鼓勵她在會議中自信地發表想法。多年後，在自己也當上部門主管之後，她效法他的榜樣，指導好幾位新進員工度過他們在業界最艱難的頭幾年。","as":"Under the guidance of a sage mentor who had performed in Vienna for decades, the precocious violinist refined her rudimentary technique into polished artistry, eventually earning acclaim as a prodigy at international competitions.","at":"在一位曾於維也納演出數十年的睿智導師指導下，這位早慧的小提琴手將原本粗淺的技巧磨練成純熟的藝術，最終在國際比賽中以神童之姿贏得讚譽。"},{"w":"facile","p":"adj.","d":"easily accomplished; superficial.","c":"容易的；膚淺的","s":"The professor criticized the student's essay for offering facile solutions to the complex problem of urban poverty. The paper suggested that simply building more shopping malls would create enough jobs to end unemployment, ignoring issues such as education, housing, and discrimination. She explained that serious academic writing must acknowledge complexity rather than presenting simplistic answers. The student revised the essay carefully, eventually producing a thoughtful analysis that earned high marks.","t":"教授批評這名學生的報告，對都市貧窮這個複雜問題提出了膚淺的解決方案。報告主張只要多蓋購物中心，就能創造足夠的工作機會來終結失業，卻忽略了教育、住房與歧視等問題。她解釋，嚴謹的學術寫作必須承認問題的複雜性，而不是提出過於簡化的答案。這名學生仔細修改了報告，最終完成了一篇深思熟慮、獲得高分的分析。","as":"The essay offered a facile explanation for the Roman Empire's collapse, attributing it solely to decadence while ignoring the myriad economic and military factors that more perspicacious historians deem paramount.","at":"這篇文章對羅馬帝國的崩潰提出了膚淺的解釋，將其完全歸咎於道德墮落，卻忽略了無數經濟與軍事因素，而這些正是更具洞察力的歷史學家認為最關鍵的。"},{"w":"cant","p":"n.","d":"insincere or almost meaningless talk.","c":"偽善之言；空話","s":"Employees grew tired of the manager's corporate cant about teamwork, family values, and caring for staff, especially after he announced massive layoffs just weeks later. His speeches were filled with fashionable phrases that sounded inspiring but meant nothing in practice. Workers noticed that his actions consistently contradicted his words. Eventually, the staff stopped attending his motivational meetings altogether, preferring honest communication to empty slogans repeated without genuine commitment. Many eventually found jobs elsewhere.","t":"員工們對經理那套關於團隊合作、家庭價值與關懷員工的企業空話感到厭倦，尤其是在他幾週後就宣布大規模裁員之後。他的演講充斥著聽起來激勵人心、實際上卻毫無意義的流行詞彙。員工們注意到，他的行為總是與他的言語相互矛盾。最後，員工們完全不再參加他的激勵會議，他們寧願要誠實的溝通，也不要沒有真誠承諾、一再重複的空洞口號。許多人最終在別處找到了工作。","as":"By the end of the long campaign, voters had grown weary of the politicians' cant about 'family values,' recognizing these platitudes as a veneer that concealed the officials' own duplicity and sordid backroom deals.","at":"漫長的選戰接近尾聲時，選民早已厭倦了政客們關於「家庭價值」的虛偽空話，他們看穿這些陳腔濫調只是一層掩飾，底下藏著官員們自己的表裡不一與骯髒的私下交易。"},{"w":"umbrage","p":"n.","d":"resentment, offense.","c":"不快；怨恨","s":"The senior chef took umbrage when the restaurant owner hired a young celebrity cook to redesign the entire menu without consulting him first. After twenty years of loyal service, he felt insulted and ignored. He expressed his resentment by refusing to attend planning meetings and eventually submitted his resignation. The owner later admitted that she should have involved him in the decision, recognizing how deeply her actions had offended him.","t":"當餐廳老闆沒有事先詢問就聘請一位年輕的名人廚師重新設計整份菜單時，這位資深主廚感到十分不快。在忠心服務二十年之後，他覺得自己受到侮辱與忽視。他以拒絕參加規劃會議來表達不滿，最終遞出了辭呈。老闆後來承認，她應該讓他參與這項決定，也體認到自己的行為深深冒犯了他。","as":"The veteran actress took umbrage at the director's request that she audition for the role, construing it as a derogatory hint that her career was on the wane and an attempt to belittle her illustrious past.","at":"這位資深女演員對導演要求她試鏡一事感到不悅，她認為這是在貶損地暗示她的演藝生涯正在走下坡，也是企圖貶低她輝煌的過去。"},{"w":"magnanimous","p":"adj.","d":"noble, generous, forgiving.","c":"寬宏大量的","s":"After winning the bitter election, the new president gave a magnanimous victory speech, praising her opponent's dedication and inviting his supporters to help build a better future together. Instead of celebrating her rival's defeat, she appointed several members of the opposing party to important government positions. Political commentators admired her generous, forgiving approach, noting that it helped heal divisions that had deeply troubled the nation throughout the long campaign. Her approval ratings rose steadily.","t":"在贏得這場激烈的選舉後，新任總統發表了一場寬宏大量的勝選演說，讚揚對手的奉獻，並邀請他的支持者一起幫忙打造更好的未來。她沒有為對手的落敗慶祝，反而任命了數名反對黨成員擔任重要的政府職位。政治評論員欣賞她慷慨寬容的做法，指出這有助於彌合在漫長選戰中深深困擾國家的分裂。她的支持率穩定上升。","as":"In a magnanimous gesture after the bitter civil war, the victorious president granted amnesty even to his most implacable adversaries, hoping that clemency rather than vengeance would end the strife that had divided the nation.","at":"在慘烈的內戰結束後，獲勝的總統展現寬宏大量的氣度，甚至特赦了最不肯妥協的敵人，希望以寬恕而非報復，終結撕裂國家的紛爭。"},{"w":"vilify","p":"v.","d":"to slander, speak ill of.","c":"誹謗；詆毀","s":"Some tabloid newspapers began to vilify the young actress after she criticized their invasive photographers, publishing false stories claiming she was arrogant, unkind to fans, and difficult to work with. Anonymous sources made shocking accusations that were never supported by evidence. Her friends and colleagues publicly defended her character, insisting that the slanderous reports were entirely fabricated. She eventually sued two publications and won substantial damages for defamation. Tabloids have treated her more carefully since.","t":"在這位年輕女演員批評某些八卦報紙具侵擾性的攝影師之後，這些報紙開始詆毀她，刊登不實報導，聲稱她傲慢、對粉絲不友善，而且很難共事。匿名消息來源提出了從未有證據支持的驚人指控。她的朋友與同事公開為她的人格辯護，堅稱這些誹謗性的報導完全是捏造的。她最終控告了兩家媒體，並因誹謗獲得了可觀的賠償。此後八卦報紙對她的報導謹慎多了。","as":"During the plague, frightened townspeople began to vilify the city's expatriates as the culprits who had spread the contagion, a baseless conjecture rooted in superstition rather than in any tangible evidence.","at":"瘟疫期間，驚恐的鎮民開始詆毀城裡的外籍居民，把他們說成散播疫病的罪魁禍首；這種毫無根據的臆測源自迷信，而非任何具體證據。"},{"w":"elucidate","p":"v.","d":"to make clear, explain.","c":"闡明；說明","s":"Students struggling with calculus appreciated the tutor's ability to elucidatedifficult concepts using simple examples from everyday life. She explained rates of change by describing how a car accelerates, and she illustrated integration by calculating the amount of water filling a swimming pool. Her clear explanations helped students understand ideas that had previously seemed impossibly abstract. Many of them later said her lessons transformed mathematics from a frightening subject into an enjoyable challenge.","t":"正為微積分所苦的學生們，很感謝這位家教能用日常生活中簡單的例子來闡明困難的概念。她用汽車加速的方式來解釋變化率，並以計算注滿游泳池的水量來說明積分。她清楚的講解，幫助學生理解了過去似乎抽象到難以理解的觀念。許多學生後來表示，她的課讓數學從一門令人害怕的科目，變成了一項有趣的挑戰。","as":"In her lucid lecture, the physicist sought to elucidate the paradox of light, a phenomenon that behaves as both particle and wave, using analogous examples from everyday life to make a recondite concept accessible to novices.","at":"這位物理學家在條理清晰的演講中，試圖闡明光的矛盾特性──一種既像粒子又像波的現象；她以日常生活中類似的例子，讓初學者也能理解這個深奧的概念。"},{"w":"vapid","p":"adj.","d":"uninteresting, dull, lacking liveliness.","c":"乏味的；無趣的","s":"Critics dismissed the new television talk show as vapid, complaining that the host asked shallow questions and allowed celebrity guests to promote their products without any meaningful conversation. Episodes consisted mainly of forced laughter, predictable jokes, and repetitive discussions about fashion and diets. Viewers quickly lost interest, and ratings declined every week. After only two months, the network canceled the dull program and replaced it with a popular documentary series about wildlife.","t":"評論家認為這個新的電視談話節目枯燥乏味，抱怨主持人只問膚淺的問題，還讓名人來賓在毫無實質對話的情況下宣傳自己的產品。每集節目主要都是勉強的笑聲、老套的笑話，以及關於時尚與節食的重複討論。觀眾很快便失去興趣，收視率每週下滑。僅僅兩個月後，電視台便停播了這個無趣的節目，改播一個受歡迎的野生動物紀錄片系列。","as":"Critics who scrutinized the much-hyped debut novel dismissed it as vapid, complaining that its mundane plot and inane dialogue could not be redeemed even by the author's flamboyant, image-laden prose.","at":"仔細審視這本被大肆炒作的處女作後，評論家認為它空洞乏味，抱怨其情節平凡、對白愚蠢，即使作者以華麗、充滿意象的文筆寫作也無法挽救。"},{"w":"unwieldy","p":"adj.","d":"bulky, difficult to handle.","c":"笨重的；難處理的","s":"The delivery workers struggled for nearly an hour to carry the unwieldy antique wardrobe up four flights of narrow stairs. The massive wooden furniture was too wide to turn corners easily, and its heavy doors kept swinging open. Eventually, they removed the doors and legs to make it lighter and easier to maneuver. Exhausted but successful, they finally placed the bulky piece in the owner's bedroom without scratching the walls.","t":"送貨員們花了將近一個小時，才把這座笨重的古董衣櫃搬上四層狹窄的樓梯。這件巨大的木製家具太寬，很難順利轉過轉角，沉重的櫃門也一直打開。最後，他們拆下櫃門和櫃腳，讓它變得較輕、較容易搬動。雖然筋疲力盡，他們終於成功地把這件龐大的家具放進屋主的臥室，而且沒有刮傷牆壁。","as":"The mammoth plate armor of medieval knights, though a formidable bulwark against arrows, proved unwieldy on the muddy battlefield at Agincourt, leaving its wearers lethargic and vulnerable to lithe, lightly armed foot soldiers.","at":"中世紀騎士那套龐大的板甲雖然是抵擋箭矢的堅固屏障，在阿金庫爾泥濘的戰場上卻顯得笨重難行，使穿戴者行動遲緩，容易被身手矯健、輕裝上陣的步兵擊倒。"},{"w":"proximity","p":"n.","d":"nearness.","c":"接近；鄰近","s":"Many families choose apartments based on their proximity to good schools, parks, and public transportation. Living near a subway station can save commuters hours every week, while having a hospital nearby provides peace of mind for elderly residents. Real estate agents report that homes close to popular elementary schools often sell for significantly higher prices. Urban planners therefore consider convenient access to essential services a key factor in designing livable neighborhoods.","t":"許多家庭在選擇公寓時，會考量它們與好學校、公園和大眾運輸的距離遠近。住在捷運站附近每週能為通勤族省下好幾個小時，而附近有醫院則讓年長居民感到安心。房仲業者表示，靠近熱門小學的房子，售價往往明顯較高。因此，都市規劃者將便利取得基本服務視為設計宜居社區的關鍵因素。","as":"Because of the village's proximity to an active volcano, residents lived with the ominous possibility of an eruption, yet many were loath to abandon the fertile soil that had nurtured their crops for generations.","at":"由於村莊鄰近一座活火山，居民始終生活在火山可能爆發的不祥陰影下；然而許多人仍不願離開這片世世代代滋養他們作物的肥沃土地。"},{"w":"lassitude","p":"n.","d":"weariness, weakness, lack of energy.","c":"疲倦；無精打采","s":"During the long, humid summer afternoons, a heavy lassitude often settles over students in classrooms without air conditioning. Heads droop, eyelids grow heavy, and even enthusiastic learners struggle to concentrate on their teachers' explanations. Educational researchers have found that high temperatures significantly reduce students' energy and academic performance. As a result, many schools in Taiwan have installed air conditioners and adjusted timetables to place demanding subjects during cooler morning hours.","t":"在漫長潮濕的夏日午後，沒有冷氣的教室裡，學生們常常被一股沉重的倦怠感籠罩。大家頭低垂、眼皮沉重，即使是熱衷學習的學生，也難以專心聽老師講解。教育研究人員發現，高溫會顯著降低學生的精力與學業表現。因此，台灣許多學校已裝設冷氣，並調整課表，將較吃重的科目安排在較涼爽的早晨時段。","as":"Prolonged malnutrition left the refugees in a state of profound lassitude; afflicted by fever and privation, many found even the brief walk to the village well an excruciating ordeal that drained what little strength remained.","at":"長期營養不良使難民們陷入極度的疲憊無力；在發燒與匱乏的折磨下，許多人連走到村中水井的短短路程，都成了耗盡僅存體力的痛苦考驗。"},{"w":"vitiate","p":"v.","d":"to destroy the use or value of, weaken.","c":"損害；使無效","s":"A single mistake in collecting samples can vitiate the results of an entire scientific study, making months of careful work worthless. If researchers accidentally contaminate a test tube or record data incorrectly, their conclusions may no longer be reliable. For this reason, laboratories follow strict procedures, double-check measurements, and repeat experiments whenever possible. Scientists emphasize that protecting the accuracy of data is essential to preventing errors from undermining important discoveries.","t":"採集樣本時的一個小錯誤，就可能使整項科學研究的結果失去效力，讓數個月的心血白費。如果研究人員不小心污染了試管或記錄錯誤的數據，他們的結論可能就不再可靠。因此，實驗室遵循嚴格的程序、反覆核對測量結果，並盡可能重複實驗。科學家強調，保護數據的準確性，對於防止錯誤損害重要的發現至關重要。","as":"The study's conclusions were vitiated by a fundamental flaw in its premise: after only a cursory pilot test, the researchers surveyed wealthy suburban families and then extrapolated their findings to a vastly heterogeneous population, rendering the results dubious.","at":"這項研究的結論因其前提有根本缺陷而失去價值：研究人員只做了草率的前導測試，便調查富裕的郊區家庭，再將結果推論到組成極為多元的整體人口，使得研究結果令人存疑。"},{"w":"augment","p":"v.","d":"to enlarge, increase.","c":"增加；擴大","s":"Many university students take part-time jobs to augment their limited incomes, working in cafés, tutoring younger students, or delivering food in the evenings. The additional money helps pay for textbooks, transportation, and rising living costs. However, advisors caution that working too many hours can damage academic performance. They recommend finding flexible positions that increase earnings without sacrificing the time students need for studying, sleep, and meaningful social activities. Balance, they insist, is essential.","t":"許多大學生打工來增加有限的收入，他們在咖啡館工作、為年紀較小的學生當家教，或在晚上外送餐點。這些額外的收入有助於支付教科書、交通費與不斷上漲的生活開銷。然而，輔導老師提醒，工作時數過長可能會影響學業表現。他們建議找彈性的工作，在增加收入的同時，不犧牲學生讀書、睡眠與參與有意義社交活動所需的時間。他們堅持，平衡是不可或缺的。","as":"To augment its meager income from tourism, the small island nation began to exploit its offshore fisheries, a lucrative venture that environmentalists warned could ultimately obliterate the coral reef's fragile ecosystem.","at":"為了增加微薄的觀光收入，這個小島國開始開發近海漁業；這項事業雖然獲利豐厚，環保人士卻警告，最終可能徹底摧毀珊瑚礁脆弱的生態系。"},{"w":"fatuous","p":"adj.","d":"foolish, silly, inane.","c":"愚蠢的；昏庸的","s":"The celebrity's fatuous comments about science during the interview, including his claim that the moon produces its own light, embarrassed his fans and amused experts. He spoke with complete confidence despite having obviously never studied the subject. Teachers shared the video with students as an example of why people should verify information rather than trusting famous personalities. Within days, the foolish remarks had become a popular joke on social media platforms.","t":"這位名人在訪談中對科學發表的愚蠢言論，包括他聲稱月亮會自己發光，讓他的粉絲尷尬不已，也讓專家們覺得好笑。儘管他顯然從未研究過這門學科，說起話來卻充滿自信。老師們把這段影片分享給學生，作為人們應該查證資訊、而非盲目相信名人的例子。短短幾天內，這些愚蠢的言論就成了社群媒體上流行的笑話。","as":"The courtier's fatuous flattery, delivered with obsequious bows and fulsome praise for every royal decree, fooled no one except the vain monarch, whose megalomania made him gullible to any compliment.","at":"這名朝臣愚蠢的奉承，伴隨著卑躬屈膝的鞠躬，以及對每一道王令浮誇虛偽的讚美，除了虛榮的君主之外誰也騙不了；而君主的自大狂妄，使他對任何恭維都照單全收。"},{"w":"contort","p":"v.","d":"to twist violently.","c":"扭曲；歪曲","s":"Acrobats in the famous circus can contort their bodies into positions that seem physically impossible, bending backward until their heads touch their heels or folding themselves into tiny glass boxes. Audiences gasp in amazement as the performers twist their limbs with graceful control. Such extraordinary flexibility requires years of daily training, beginning in early childhood. Physical therapists warn untrained people never to attempt these movements, since serious injuries can easily result.","t":"這個著名馬戲團的特技演員能將身體扭曲成看似不可能的姿勢，向後彎到頭碰到腳跟，或將自己摺進小小的玻璃箱裡。觀眾們看著表演者以優雅的控制力扭轉四肢，無不驚嘆連連。這種非凡的柔軟度需要從幼年開始、多年的每日訓練。物理治療師警告，未經訓練的人千萬不要嘗試這些動作，因為很容易造成嚴重的傷害。","as":"In the earthquake's aftermath, engineers surveyed the havoc: steel girders contorted by catastrophic tremors, debris strewn across avenues, and bridges rendered impassable—a scene that underscored why rigorous building codes are imperative.","at":"地震過後，工程師勘查滿目瘡痍的災情：鋼樑在劇烈震動中嚴重扭曲，瓦礫散落街道，橋梁也無法通行──這幅景象凸顯出嚴格的建築規範為何不可或缺。"},{"w":"repertoire","p":"n.","d":"the works an artist is prepared to perform.","c":"全部節目；曲目","s":"The young violinist's repertoire already includes more than forty concertos, sonatas, and chamber pieces, ranging from classical Baroque works to contemporary compositions. She can perform any of them with only a few days' notice, a remarkable achievement for a musician of just nineteen. Orchestra directors value her extensive range, since it allows them to invite her for diverse programs. She plans to add several Taiwanese folk arrangements to her collection next year.","t":"這位年輕小提琴家的演奏曲目已包含四十多首協奏曲、奏鳴曲與室內樂作品，涵蓋古典巴洛克作品到當代創作。只要幾天的準備，她就能演奏其中任何一首，對一位年僅十九歲的音樂家而言，這是非凡的成就。樂團指揮們都很看重她廣泛的曲目範圍，因為這讓他們能邀請她參與多元的演出節目。她計畫明年在她的曲目中加入幾首台灣民謠的改編曲。","as":"The prolific pianist's repertoire was remarkably eclectic, spanning a gamut from Baroque fugues to avant-garde jazz, and critics praised the virtuosity with which she moved between such disparate styles within a single concert.","at":"這位多產鋼琴家的演奏曲目極為多元，從巴洛克賦格到前衛爵士應有盡有；評論家讚賞她能在同一場音樂會中，以精湛技藝在如此迥異的風格之間自如切換。"},{"w":"imperceptible","p":"adj.","d":"extremely slight or gradual, not noticeable.","c":"難以察覺的；極細微的","s":"The movement of the continents is almost imperceptible, occurring at roughly the same speed that human fingernails grow. Nobody can feel the land shifting beneath their feet, yet over millions of years these tiny changes have completely rearranged the planet's geography. Scientists use satellites and precise instruments to measure the slight motion. Their data confirm that the Atlantic Ocean widens by a few centimeters every year, gradually separating Europe from North America.","t":"大陸的移動幾乎難以察覺，其速度大約和人類指甲生長的速度相同。沒有人能感覺到腳下的土地在移動，然而經過數百萬年，這些微小的變化已徹底重塑了地球的地理面貌。科學家利用衛星與精密儀器來測量這種細微的移動。他們的數據證實，大西洋每年會變寬幾公分，逐漸將歐洲與北美洲分開。","as":"The erosion of the coastline was nearly imperceptible from year to year, yet its cumulative effect over a century proved inexorable, eventually forcing the once tranquil fishing village to relocate its domiciles farther inland.","at":"海岸線的侵蝕年年幾乎難以察覺，但百年來累積的影響卻勢不可擋，最終迫使這座昔日寧靜的漁村將住所遷往更內陸的地方。"}]},{"unit":41,"cards":[{"w":"curry","p":"v.","d":"to seek favor by flattery (usually 'curry favor').","c":"拍馬屁；討好","s":"Some employees tried to curry favor with the new director by praising her every idea, laughing loudly at her jokes, and offering to run personal errands for her. She quickly recognized these flattering gestures and found them uncomfortable rather than impressive. Instead, she promoted a quiet analyst whose honest reports had helped the department avoid costly mistakes. Her decision sent a clear message that results mattered far more than compliments or attention-seeking behavior.","t":"有些員工試圖討好新任主管，稱讚她的每一個想法、對她的笑話大聲發笑，還主動替她跑私人雜務。她很快便看穿這些奉承的舉動，覺得不自在，而非印象深刻。相反地，她拔擢了一位安靜的分析師，他誠實的報告曾幫助部門避免代價高昂的錯誤。她的決定傳達了一個明確的訊息：成果遠比恭維或博取關注的行為重要。","as":"In eighteenth-century France, ambitious aspirants to the royal court would curry favor with the king's entourage, lavishing its members with sumptuous gifts in the hope of securing a lucrative sinecure.","at":"在十八世紀的法國，懷抱野心、想進入宮廷的人會極力討好國王的隨從，送上奢華的厚禮，希望能換得一個薪水優渥又清閒的閒差。"},{"w":"pall","p":"v.","d":"to cease to please, become dull.","c":"失去吸引力；令人生厭","s":"At first, the children loved their new video game, playing it every afternoon and discussing strategies at dinner. After several weeks, however, the novelty began to pall, and the same levels and characters no longer excited them. They gradually returned to reading books, building models, and playing outside with neighbors. Their parents observed that even the most thrilling entertainment eventually loses its appeal when experienced repeatedly without variety or challenge.","t":"一開始，孩子們非常喜歡他們的新電玩，每天下午都在玩，吃晚餐時還在討論攻略。然而幾週之後，新鮮感開始消退，同樣的關卡與角色再也無法讓他們興奮。他們逐漸回到看書、做模型，以及和鄰居在外面玩耍。他們的父母發現，即使是最刺激的娛樂，在缺乏變化或挑戰的情況下反覆體驗，終究也會失去吸引力。","as":"Although the endless banquets initially delighted the young heir, their opulence soon began to pall, and he withdrew into introspective solitude, craving the rustic simplicity of the farmhouse where he had spent his childhood.","at":"雖然無止盡的盛宴起初令這位年輕繼承人十分開心，但那份奢華很快就讓他索然無味；他轉而退入自我省思的孤獨之中，渴望童年所住的農舍那份樸實的鄉村生活。"},{"w":"succulent","p":"adj.","d":"juicy, full of flavor.","c":"多汁的","s":"Visitors to the night market lined up for nearly an hour to taste the vendor's famous grilled chicken, which was marinated overnight and roasted slowly over charcoal. Each piece was wonderfully succulent, with crispy skin and tender meat that released rich juices with every bite. Food bloggers described it as the best street food in Taichung. The owner explains that patience, fresh ingredients, and a secret family sauce create the unforgettable flavor.","t":"夜市的遊客排了將近一個小時的隊，只為了品嚐這個攤販有名的烤雞，雞肉經過一夜醃漬，再用炭火慢慢烘烤。每一塊都極為多汁，外皮酥脆、肉質軟嫩，每咬一口都會流出濃郁的肉汁。美食部落客形容它是台中最棒的街頭小吃。老闆解釋說，耐心、新鮮食材以及家傳的秘方醬汁，造就了這令人難忘的滋味。","as":"Botanists marvel at how desert plants store water in succulent leaves, an innate adaptation that allows them to thrive in an arid, inclement habitat where less hardy species are susceptible to dehydration.","at":"植物學家讚嘆沙漠植物能將水分儲存在肥厚多汁的葉子裡；這種與生俱來的適應能力，使它們能在乾燥嚴酷的棲地中茁壯成長，而那裡較不耐旱的物種則很容易脫水。"},{"w":"satiety","p":"n.","d":"the state of being overly full; excess.","c":"飽足；厭膩","s":"Nutritionists explain that eating slowly allows the brain enough time to recognize satiety, the feeling of being completely full. Hormones that signal fullness take about twenty minutes to reach the brain, so people who eat quickly often consume far more than they need. Researchers recommend putting down utensils between bites, chewing thoroughly, and drinking water during meals. These simple habits help people recognize when they are satisfied and prevent uncomfortable overeating.","t":"營養師解釋，慢慢進食能讓大腦有足夠的時間察覺飽足感，也就是完全吃飽的感覺。傳遞飽足訊號的荷爾蒙大約需要二十分鐘才能抵達大腦，因此吃得快的人往往會吃下遠超過所需的份量。研究人員建議，每吃一口就放下餐具、充分咀嚼，並在用餐時喝水。這些簡單的習慣能幫助人們察覺自己何時已經吃飽，避免吃得過撐而不舒服。","as":"Nutritionists note that fiber-rich foods induce satiety more quickly than processed snacks, an effect that helps curb the voracious, seemingly insatiable appetites that exacerbate the obesity so prevalent in industrialized nations.","at":"營養學家指出，富含纖維的食物比加工零食更快帶來飽足感，這有助於抑制那種貪婪、彷彿永遠無法滿足的食慾，而正是這種食慾加劇了工業化國家普遍的肥胖問題。"},{"w":"intrinsic","p":"adj.","d":"within itself, inherent.","c":"內在的；固有的","s":"Educational psychologists distinguish between students who study for grades and those motivated by intrinsic curiosity, the natural desire to understand the world for its own sake. Research shows that learners driven by inner interest remember information longer and approach difficult problems with greater persistence. Teachers can encourage this inherent motivation by offering choices, connecting lessons to real life, and celebrating questions rather than focusing exclusively on test scores and rankings.","t":"教育心理學家將為了成績而念書的學生，與受到內在好奇心驅動的學生區分開來，後者是一種為了理解世界本身而產生的天生渴望。研究顯示，受內在興趣驅動的學習者記得資訊更久，面對困難問題時也更有毅力。老師可以透過提供選擇、將課程與現實生活連結，以及鼓勵提問而非只關注考試分數與排名，來培養這種與生俱來的學習動機。","as":"Philosophers have long debated whether art possesses intrinsic value or whether its worth is merely extrinsic, conferred by the shifting vogue among collectors and the speculative avarice of the auction market.","at":"哲學家長期爭論：藝術究竟具有本身固有的價值，還是其價值僅是外在賦予的──來自收藏家之間不斷變換的流行風潮，以及拍賣市場投機的貪婪？"},{"w":"potpourri","p":"n.","d":"medley, mixture.","c":"雜燴；大雜燴","s":"The school's annual talent show featured a delightful potpourri of performances, including traditional Taiwanese drumming, hip-hop dancing, a magic act, a string quartet, and a comedy sketch written by students. Parents enjoyed the unpredictable variety, never knowing what kind of act would appear next. The principal explained that the diverse mixture reflected students' wide range of interests. The event raised enough money to purchase new musical instruments for the music department.","t":"學校的年度才藝表演呈現了一場令人愉快的大雜燴，包括台灣傳統鼓藝、嘻哈舞蹈、魔術表演、弦樂四重奏，以及學生自編的喜劇短劇。家長們很享受這種難以預料的多樣性，永遠不知道下一個節目會是什麼。校長解釋，這種多元的組合反映出學生們廣泛的興趣。這場活動募得的款項足以為音樂科購買新樂器。","as":"The museum's new exhibit is a potpourri of artifacts—rare extant coins, ceremonial masks, faded placards from wartime protests—juxtaposed to illustrate how societies throughout history have commemorated their struggles.","at":"博物館的新展覽是一場文物大雜燴：有現存罕見的古錢幣、祭典面具、戰時抗議活動中褪色的標語牌；這些展品並列陳設，展現歷代社會如何紀念自身的奮鬥。"},{"w":"sanction","p":"v.","d":"to endorse, certify, officially approve.","c":"批准；認可","s":"The sports federation refused to sanction the new tournament because its organizers had not followed official safety regulations or registered qualified referees. Without formal approval, results from the competition would not count toward world rankings, and professional athletes risked suspension for participating. After several months of negotiations, the organizers improved their facilities and training standards. The federation finally authorized the event, which has since become one of the region's most respected competitions.","t":"體育總會拒絕批准這項新的錦標賽，因為主辦單位沒有遵守官方的安全規範，也沒有登記合格的裁判。未經正式核准，比賽結果將不列入世界排名，職業運動員參賽還可能遭到禁賽。經過數個月的協商，主辦單位改善了設施與訓練標準。總會終於核准了這項賽事，它此後已成為該地區最受尊敬的比賽之一。","as":"The international committee refused to sanction the experimental drug until independent laboratories could corroborate its allegedly miraculous results, citing the pernicious side effects that had afflicted patients in earlier trials.","at":"國際委員會拒絕核准這款實驗性藥物，除非獨立實驗室能證實其據稱神奇的療效；委員會並指出，先前的試驗中曾有病患深受嚴重有害的副作用所苦。"},{"w":"denote","p":"v.","d":"to indicate, show, mean.","c":"表示；意味著","s":"On hiking maps of Taiwan's national parks, red lines denotedifficult trails that require experience and proper equipment, while green lines indicate easier paths suitable for families. Small tent symbols mark campsites, and blue circles show locations with drinking water. Park rangers encourage visitors to study these symbols carefully before beginning any hike. Understanding what each marking means can prevent dangerous situations, especially in remote mountain areas with unpredictable weather.","t":"在台灣國家公園的登山地圖上，紅色線條表示需要經驗與適當裝備的困難步道，綠色線條則標示適合全家大小的較輕鬆路線。小帳篷符號標出營地位置，藍色圓圈則顯示有飲用水的地點。保育巡查員鼓勵遊客在開始任何健行之前，仔細研究這些符號。了解每個標記的意義，可以避免危險的情況發生，特別是在天氣變化莫測的偏遠山區。","as":"In traditional Maori culture, intricate facial tattoos denote a person's lineage and social rank, so an anthropologist who construes them merely as decoration overlooks their integral role in tradition and community identity.","at":"在傳統毛利文化中，繁複的臉部刺青代表一個人的血統與社會地位；因此，若人類學家只將它們解讀為裝飾，就忽略了刺青在傳統與族群認同中不可或缺的角色。"},{"w":"allude","p":"v.","d":"to hint, suggest indirectly.","c":"暗示；間接提及","s":"During her speech, the retiring principal did not mention the scandal directly, but she chose to allude to the difficult period by speaking about honesty, forgiveness, and learning from mistakes. Teachers in the audience understood exactly which events she meant. Her indirect references allowed her to acknowledge the painful history without reopening old conflicts. Many listeners admired how gracefully she hinted at the past while focusing on the school's hopeful future.","t":"在演講中，即將退休的校長並沒有直接提到那起醜聞，而是選擇透過談論誠實、寬恕與從錯誤中學習，來暗指那段艱難的時期。台下的老師們都完全明白她指的是哪些事件。她間接的提及，讓她得以承認那段痛苦的過往，卻不至於重新挑起舊有的衝突。許多聽眾欣賞她在著眼學校充滿希望的未來之際，如此優雅地暗示過去。","as":"In her memoir, the former diplomat only alludes to the clandestine negotiations that ended the war, offering cryptic hints rather than overt details, perhaps because many participants remain reticent about their roles.","at":"這位前外交官在回憶錄中，只是間接提及結束戰爭的秘密談判，給的是隱晦的暗示而非明確的細節；或許是因為許多參與者至今仍對自己扮演的角色守口如瓶。"},{"w":"insidious","p":"adj.","d":"sly, gradually and secretly harmful.","c":"陰險的；潛伏的","s":"High blood pressure is often called a silent killer because of its insidious nature; many people suffer from it for years without noticing any symptoms. Meanwhile, the condition gradually damages the heart, kidneys, and blood vessels. By the time warning signs appear, serious harm may already have occurred. Doctors therefore recommend regular checkups for all adults, since detecting this hidden, slowly developing danger early allows effective treatment and prevention. Awareness saves lives.","t":"高血壓常被稱為沉默的殺手，因為它具有潛伏的特性；許多人罹患多年卻沒有察覺任何症狀。與此同時，這種疾病會逐漸損害心臟、腎臟與血管。等到警訊出現時，嚴重的傷害可能早已造成。因此，醫生建議所有成年人定期健康檢查，因為及早發現這種隱藏、緩慢發展的危險，才能有效治療與預防。提高警覺能拯救生命。","as":"Lead poisoning is especially insidious because its effects can remain latent for years; by the time parents discern cognitive impairments, the toxin has often permeated their children's bones and caused lasting detriment.","at":"鉛中毒特別陰險，因為它的影響可能潛伏多年；等到父母察覺孩子的認知障礙時，毒素往往早已滲入孩子的骨骼，造成長久的傷害。"},{"w":"propriety","p":"n.","d":"suitability, correctness of behavior.","c":"得體；適當","s":"In traditional Japanese business culture, propriety governs nearly every interaction, from how deeply one bows to the correct way of presenting business cards with both hands. Foreign visitors who ignore these customs may unintentionally offend their hosts. International companies therefore train employees to understand appropriate etiquette before overseas meetings. Experts explain that showing respect for local standards of correct behavior can build trust and strengthen long-term professional relationships. Small gestures matter enormously.","t":"在傳統的日本商業文化中，禮節幾乎規範了每一次互動，從鞠躬的深度到以雙手遞送名片的正確方式皆然。忽視這些習俗的外國訪客，可能會在無意間冒犯主人。因此，跨國企業會在海外會議前訓練員工了解適當的禮儀。專家解釋，尊重當地得體行為的標準，能建立信任並強化長期的專業關係。小小的舉動影響深遠。","as":"Victorian etiquette manuals stressed propriety above all else, admonishing young women to eschew gaudy clothing and boisterous laughter lest they violate the rigid decorum expected of them in polite society.","at":"維多利亞時代的禮儀手冊將合宜得體置於一切之上，告誡年輕女性避免穿著俗豔的服裝、避免放聲大笑，以免違反上流社會對她們所要求的嚴格禮節。"},{"w":"advent","p":"n.","d":"arrival of an important event or thing.","c":"到來；出現","s":"The advent of smartphones transformed daily life more rapidly than almost any previous invention. Within a decade of their arrival, people were using them to navigate cities, pay for groceries, watch movies, and communicate instantly with friends worldwide. Entire industries, including taxi services and photography, changed dramatically. Historians of technology compare this emergence to the introduction of electricity or the printing press in its broad social consequences. Few inventions have spread so quickly.","t":"智慧型手機的出現，比過去幾乎任何一項發明都更迅速地改變了日常生活。在它問世後的十年內，人們已用它來在城市中導航、購買雜貨、看電影，並與全世界的朋友即時通訊。包括計程車服務與攝影在內的整個產業都發生了劇烈的變化。科技史學家將它的出現，在廣泛的社會影響上，比擬為電力或印刷術的問世。很少有發明能傳播得如此迅速。","as":"The advent of the printing press caused literacy rates to surge across Europe, enabling reformers to promulgate dissenting ideas and precipitating the decline of the monolithic authority the Church had once wielded over learning.","at":"印刷術的問世使歐洲各地的識字率急遽上升，讓改革者得以廣泛傳播異議思想，也加速了教會昔日對學術所掌握的、鐵板一塊般的權威走向衰落。"},{"w":"impious","p":"adj.","d":"lacking respect, irreverent (especially toward religion).","c":"不敬的；對神不虔誠的","s":"The tourist's impious behavior at the ancient temple shocked local worshippers, who watched him climb onto a sacred statue to pose for photographs. He ignored signs asking visitors to remain quiet and remove their hats. Temple volunteers politely asked him to leave, explaining that such disrespectful actions offended people who came to pray. The incident prompted the tourism bureau to publish guidelines about appropriate conduct at religious sites. Most visitors behave respectfully.","t":"這名遊客在古廟中的不敬行為令當地信眾大為震驚，他們看著他爬上一尊神聖的雕像擺姿勢拍照。他無視要求遊客保持安靜並脫帽的告示。廟方志工客氣地請他離開，解釋說這種不尊重的行為冒犯了前來祈福的人。這起事件促使觀光局發布了關於宗教場所適當行為的指南。大多數遊客的舉止都很有禮貌。","as":"Exiled for his impious verses, which mocked sacred rituals with irreverent levity, the reviled poet spent his final years as an expatriate, his manuscripts circulating clandestinely among a small coterie of admirers.","at":"這位詩人因其不敬神明的詩句而遭到放逐──那些詩以輕佻的態度嘲弄神聖的儀式；這位飽受唾罵的詩人晚年流亡異鄉，他的手稿只在一小群仰慕者之間秘密流傳。"},{"w":"proffer","p":"v.","d":"to offer for acceptance.","c":"提供；提出","s":"After the heated argument, the older brother decided to proffer an apology, extending his hand and admitting that he had spoken unfairly. His younger sister hesitated at first but eventually accepted the gesture with a small smile. Their mother, who had watched quietly, was relieved to see them reconcile. She later told friends that offering forgiveness first requires far more courage than continuing a quarrel out of stubborn pride. The siblings remain close today.","t":"在激烈的爭吵之後，哥哥決定主動道歉，他伸出手，承認自己說話不公平。妹妹起初有些猶豫，最終還是帶著淺淺的微笑接受了這個示好的舉動。在一旁靜靜看著的母親，很欣慰看到他們和好。她後來告訴朋友，比起出於固執的自尊繼續爭吵，率先提出和解需要更大的勇氣。這對兄妹至今仍十分親近。","as":"When the mediator proffered a compromise, the two acrimonious factions initially balked, each deeming the terms too favorable to the other, but they eventually concurred after weeks of interminable debate.","at":"調解人提出折衷方案時，兩個互相敵視的派系起初都不肯接受，各自認為條件對另一方太有利；但經過數週沒完沒了的辯論後，雙方最終達成共識。"},{"w":"spate","p":"n.","d":"rush, flood, sudden outpouring.","c":"激增；一連串","s":"Police warned residents to lock their scooters after a sudden spate of thefts in the neighborhood, with more than thirty vehicles stolen within two weeks. Most incidents occurred late at night in poorly lit alleys. Officers increased patrols and installed additional security cameras throughout the area. Within a month, the wave of crimes ended when investigators arrested a group of young men who had been selling stolen parts online. Residents felt safe again.","t":"在社區內機車竊案突然激增、兩週內有三十多輛車失竊後，警方提醒居民務必將機車上鎖。大多數案件都發生在深夜、照明不佳的巷弄裡。警方增加巡邏，並在整個區域加裝監視器。一個月內，當調查人員逮捕了一群在網路上販售贓車零件的年輕男子後，這波犯罪潮便告終結。居民們又重拾了安全感。","as":"A recent spate of burglaries has galvanized residents to form neighborhood patrols, and the police chief has exhorted citizens to remain vigilant while investigators scrutinize surveillance footage for clues about the culprits.","at":"近來接連發生的竊案激起居民組成社區巡守隊，警察局長也呼籲市民保持警覺，同時調查人員正仔細檢視監視器畫面，尋找嫌犯的線索。"},{"w":"shibboleth","p":"n.","d":"pet phrase, slogan; a custom that distinguishes a group.","c":"陳腔濫調；口號；（團體的）特徵用語","s":"The idea that hard work always guarantees success has become a popular shibboleth, repeated in motivational speeches, advertisements, and graduation ceremonies. However, economists point out that factors such as family wealth, education, and luck also strongly influence outcomes. Critics argue that relying on such familiar slogans can make people blame themselves unfairly for circumstances beyond their control. They encourage more honest conversations about the complex causes of success and failure.","t":"「努力一定會成功」的觀念已成為一句流行的口號，在激勵演講、廣告與畢業典禮上一再被重複。然而，經濟學家指出，家庭財富、教育與運氣等因素，也會強烈影響結果。批評者認為，依賴這類耳熟能詳的口號，可能會讓人們不公平地為自己無法掌控的處境責怪自己。他們鼓勵人們更誠實地討論成功與失敗背後的複雜原因。","as":"For a generation, the slogan that markets regulate themselves was a shibboleth of free-market economists, yet the 2008 financial crisis exposed its fallacious premise, leading many to recant and advocate stricter oversight.","at":"整整一個世代，「市場會自我調節」這句口號是自由市場派經濟學家的信條；然而2008年的金融危機暴露出其錯誤的前提，使許多人改變立場，轉而主張更嚴格的監管。"},{"w":"bogus","p":"adj.","d":"counterfeit, fake.","c":"偽造的；假的","s":"The company hired a new manager who claimed to have a doctorate from a prestigious university, but a background check revealed that his degree was completely bogus. The institution had no record of his enrollment, and the diploma had been purchased online from a fraudulent website. Human resources immediately canceled his contract. The incident prompted many employers to verify credentials more carefully before hiring candidates for senior positions. Several universities have also strengthened security measures.","t":"公司聘用了一名自稱擁有知名大學博士學位的新經理，但背景調查顯示他的學位完全是偽造的。該校沒有他的入學紀錄，而那張文憑是從一個詐騙網站上買來的。人資部門立即解除了他的合約。這起事件促使許多雇主在聘用高階職位人選前，更仔細地查核學經歷。數所大學也加強了防偽措施。","as":"At the airport, customs officers seized a cache of bogus designer handbags, the merchandise of a covert smuggling ring that had concocted fake certificates of authenticity to deceive gullible tourists.","at":"海關人員在機場查獲一批藏匿的仿冒名牌包，這些貨品來自一個秘密走私集團，他們捏造假的真品證書，用來欺騙容易上當的觀光客。"},{"w":"substantiate","p":"v.","d":"to confirm, prove with evidence.","c":"證實；證明","s":"The newspaper refused to publish the anonymous accusation until reporters could substantiate it with reliable evidence. Journalists spent weeks interviewing witnesses, examining financial records, and obtaining official documents. Only after multiple independent sources confirmed the story did editors approve publication. Media ethics experts praised the careful approach, explaining that printing unproven claims can destroy innocent reputations and seriously damage public trust in journalism. The resulting investigation eventually led to several official resignations.","t":"在記者能以可靠證據證實這項匿名指控之前，報社拒絕刊登。記者們花了數週時間訪談證人、檢視財務紀錄並取得官方文件。直到多個獨立消息來源都證實了這則報導，編輯才核准刊登。媒體倫理專家讚揚這種謹慎的做法，解釋說刊登未經證實的說法，可能會毀掉無辜者的名譽，並嚴重損害大眾對新聞業的信任。隨後的調查最終導致數名官員辭職下台。","as":"Although the journalist's lurid allegations of corruption made headlines, she could not substantiate them with incontrovertible evidence, so her editor warned that publishing would be imprudent before eliciting a response from the accused officials.","at":"雖然這位記者對貪腐的聳動指控登上了頭條，但她無法提出確鑿無疑的證據來證實；因此她的編輯警告，在取得被指控官員的回應之前就刊出報導，實屬不智。"},{"w":"nutritive","p":"adj.","d":"having nourishing properties.","c":"營養的；有營養價值的","s":"Scientists have discovered that seaweed has remarkable nutritive value, containing high levels of iodine, vitamins, minerals, and plant-based protein. In coastal regions of Taiwan and Japan, people have eaten various types of seaweed for centuries. Researchers now promote it as a sustainable food source that requires no fresh water or fertilizer to grow. Its nourishing qualities could help address food shortages as the global population continues to increase. Demand continues to grow.","t":"科學家發現，海藻具有驚人的營養價值，含有大量的碘、維生素、礦物質與植物性蛋白質。在台灣與日本的沿海地區，人們食用各種海藻已有數百年的歷史。研究人員如今推廣它作為一種永續的食物來源，因為它的生長不需要淡水或肥料。隨著全球人口持續增加，它豐富的營養價值或許能幫助解決糧食短缺的問題。需求持續成長。","as":"Researchers have found that a mundane-looking coastal seaweed possesses remarkable nutritive properties, making it a viable remedy for the paucity of protein in diets across regions where arable land is scarce and malnutrition is rampant.","at":"研究人員發現，一種外表平凡無奇的海岸海藻具有驚人的營養價值，可望成為可行的解方，改善耕地稀少、營養不良問題猖獗地區飲食中蛋白質不足的情況。"},{"w":"raucous","p":"adj.","d":"harsh-sounding, noisy.","c":"沙啞的；喧鬧的","s":"The raucous celebration next door continued until three in the morning, with loud music, shouting, and laughter echoing through the quiet apartment building. Several neighbors knocked on the door asking the guests to lower their voices, but the noisy party only grew louder. Eventually, the building manager called the police. The following day, the embarrassed host apologized to every resident and promised to hold future gatherings at a restaurant. Neighbors accepted his apology.","t":"隔壁喧鬧的慶祝活動一直持續到凌晨三點，響亮的音樂、叫喊聲與笑聲迴盪在原本安靜的公寓大樓裡。好幾位鄰居敲門請賓客們降低音量，但這場吵鬧的派對卻只是越來越大聲。最後，大樓管理員報了警。隔天，尷尬的主人向每位住戶道歉，並承諾以後會在餐廳舉辦聚會。鄰居們接受了他的道歉。","as":"The raucous cries of gulls reverberating off the cliffs drowned out the guide's lecture, so the throng of tourists heard only a garbled, nearly incoherent account of the island's turbulent history.","at":"海鷗刺耳的叫聲在懸崖間迴盪，蓋過了導覽員的解說，使得成群的遊客只聽到一段斷斷續續、幾乎語無倫次的島嶼動盪歷史。"}]},{"unit":42,"cards":[{"w":"quandary","p":"n.","d":"doubt, dilemma.","c":"困惑；窘境","s":"The talented high school graduate found herself in a difficult quandary when she received scholarships from two excellent universities on opposite sides of the world. One offered a famous engineering program in the United States, while the other allowed her to stay close to her aging grandparents in Taiwan. For weeks she could not decide which path to choose. Eventually, a long conversation with her grandparents helped her resolve the painful dilemma.","t":"這位優秀的高中畢業生收到了分別位於地球兩端的兩所頂尖大學的獎學金，讓她陷入了兩難的困境。其中一所提供美國知名的工程學程，另一所則讓她能留在台灣，陪伴年邁的祖父母。好幾個星期以來，她無法決定要走哪條路。最後，與祖父母的一次長談，幫助她解決了這個令人痛苦的兩難。","as":"The physician faced an ethical quandary: disclosing the terminal diagnosis might plunge the fretful patient into despair, yet withholding it would flout the principle of candor that her profession deems inviolable.","at":"這位醫師陷入道德上的兩難：說出末期診斷，可能讓本就焦躁不安的病人陷入絕望；但隱瞞不說，又違背了醫界視為不可侵犯的坦誠原則。"},{"w":"callous","p":"adj.","d":"hardened, unfeeling.","c":"無情的；麻木的","s":"The company's callousedecision to fire hundreds of workers by text message, just days before the Lunar New Year holiday, provoked national outrage. Employees who had worked loyally for decades received no explanation, no personal meeting, and no additional compensation. Labor organizations condemned the heartless way the layoffs were handled, and politicians demanded new laws requiring respectful notification procedures. The company's reputation suffered serious damage, and sales declined sharply during the following months.","t":"這家公司在農曆新年假期前幾天，以簡訊解僱數百名員工的冷酷決定，引發了全國的憤慨。為公司忠心工作數十年的員工，沒有得到任何解釋、沒有任何面談，也沒有額外的補償。勞工組織譴責這種冷血無情的裁員方式，政治人物也要求制定新法，規定必須以尊重的方式通知員工。這家公司的聲譽嚴重受損，接下來幾個月的銷售額也急遽下滑。","as":"Years of covering wars had made the photojournalist seem callous to colleagues, but in retrospect she admitted that her apparent indifference was merely a veneer protecting her from the poignant suffering she documented.","at":"多年的戰地採訪讓這位攝影記者在同事眼中顯得冷漠無情；但回顧過往，她坦承那種看似漠不關心的態度，只是一層保護殼，讓她免於被自己所記錄的痛苦深深刺痛。"},{"w":"expedient","p":"adj.","d":"convenient, useful for a purpose though not always fair or principled.","c":"權宜的；方便的","s":"Faced with a sudden budget crisis, the mayor chose the most expedient solution by cutting funding for public libraries and after-school programs, which required no approval from the city council. Although the decision quickly balanced the budget, critics argued that it harmed children and low-income families who depended on these services. They accused him of choosing convenience over fairness. Community groups began raising money privately to keep several libraries open.","t":"面對突如其來的預算危機，市長選擇了最權宜的解決辦法，刪減公共圖書館與課後輔導計畫的經費，因為這不需要市議會的批准。雖然這項決定很快便平衡了預算，批評者認為它傷害了仰賴這些服務的孩童與低收入家庭。他們指責他為了方便而犧牲公平。社區團體開始私下募款，以維持數間圖書館繼續開放。","as":"Rather than pursue a comprehensive reform of the tax code, the administration chose the more expedient solution of imposing an arbitrary temporary levy, a stopgap that critics derided as ineffectual.","at":"政府沒有推動全面的稅制改革，反而選擇了較為權宜的作法：隨意開徵一項臨時稅；批評者嘲諷這種權宜之計根本無效。"},{"w":"negligible","p":"adj.","d":"trifling, too small to matter.","c":"微不足道的；可忽略的","s":"Engineers reassured residents that the new wind turbines would produce only negligible noise, quieter than the sound of a normal conversation at a distance of three hundred meters. Independent tests confirmed that the sound levels were so small that most people could not hear them above the wind itself. Although some neighbors had initially opposed the project, their concerns faded once the turbines began operating without disturbing daily life. Property values also remained stable.","t":"工程師向居民保證，新的風力發電機只會產生微乎其微的噪音，在三百公尺外比一般對話的聲音還要安靜。獨立測試證實，音量小到大多數人在風聲之中根本聽不見。雖然部分鄰居起初反對這項計畫，但在風力發電機運轉後未曾干擾日常生活，他們的疑慮也就逐漸消散了。房價也維持穩定。","as":"Although the factory emitted only negligible quantities of each pollutant, scientists warned that their cumulative effect on the watershed could prove lethal to fish species already vulnerable to rising temperatures.","at":"雖然工廠排放的每種汙染物數量都微不足道，科學家卻警告，這些汙染物對流域的累積影響，可能對原本就容易受水溫上升衝擊的魚類造成致命後果。"},{"w":"blasé","p":"adj.","d":"indifferent, unexcited because of overfamiliarity.","c":"厭倦的；無動於衷的","s":"Having traveled to more than sixty countries, the wealthy businessman had become completely blasé about international trips, yawning through flights and barely glancing at famous landmarks. While his younger colleagues excitedly photographed the Eiffel Tower, he checked emails on his phone. His daughter eventually persuaded him to visit a remote village without internet access. The unfamiliar experience finally rekindled the sense of wonder he thought he had lost forever. He now travels far more thoughtfully.","t":"這位富有的商人已經去過六十多個國家，對國際旅行變得完全無動於衷，搭飛機時哈欠連連，對著名的地標也幾乎不看一眼。當年輕的同事們興奮地拍攝艾菲爾鐵塔時，他卻在手機上查看電子郵件。他的女兒最終說服他去一個沒有網路的偏遠村莊。這次陌生的經歷，終於重新點燃了他以為早已永遠失去的好奇與驚喜。如今他旅行時用心多了。","as":"Having toured the world's grandest cathedrals, the jaded travel writer adopted a blasé attitude toward the seemingly nondescript village chapel, giving it a perfunctory glance that blinded him to the singular frescoes his more avid companions found breathtaking.","at":"這位遊遍世界宏偉大教堂、早已麻木的旅遊作家，對那座看似平凡無奇的村莊小教堂顯得興致缺缺，只是敷衍地瞥了一眼，因而錯過了讓他那些更熱情的同伴驚嘆不已的獨特壁畫。"},{"w":"ennui","p":"n.","d":"boredom, listless weariness.","c":"倦怠；無聊","s":"After retiring from her busy career as a hospital director, the former executive was overcome by ennui, spending long afternoons staring out the window with nothing to occupy her mind. The endless free time she had once dreamed about now felt empty and dull. Her friends encouraged her to volunteer at a local literacy program. Teaching adults to read soon cured her boredom and gave her days a renewed sense of purpose.","t":"從忙碌的醫院院長職位退休後，這位前主管陷入了倦怠之中，整個漫長的下午都盯著窗外，腦中空空如也。她曾夢寐以求的無盡空閒時光，如今卻令人感到空虛又無聊。朋友們鼓勵她到當地的識字計畫擔任志工。教成年人識字很快就治好了她的無聊，也讓她的生活重新有了目標。","as":"Confined to his estate by inclement weather, the affluent aristocrat succumbed to a profound ennui, listlessly perusing novels he had read before and finding no solace even in his once-beloved hobbies.","at":"惡劣的天氣把這位富有的貴族困在莊園裡，他陷入了深深的倦怠，無精打采地翻閱早已讀過的小說，就連昔日熱愛的嗜好也無法帶給他任何慰藉。"},{"w":"comely","p":"adj.","d":"attractive, pleasant to look at.","c":"清秀的；標緻的","s":"In the classic novel, the comely young heroine attracts the attention of every wealthy bachelor in the village, yet she values intelligence and kindness far more than admiration for her appearance. Although many characters comment on her attractive face and graceful manner, she eventually marries a poor schoolteacher who respects her opinions. Literature teachers often use the story to discuss how society judges women primarily by their looks. Many students find the novel surprisingly modern.","t":"在這部經典小說中，這位清秀標緻的年輕女主角吸引了村裡每一位富有單身漢的目光，但她重視智慧與善良，遠勝過他人對她外貌的欣賞。雖然許多角色都評論她迷人的面容與優雅的舉止，她最終嫁給了一位尊重她意見的清貧教師。文學老師常以這個故事來討論社會如何主要以外貌來評斷女性。許多學生覺得這部小說出奇地現代。","as":"The comely facade of the Victorian mansion, with its ornate gables and lush gardens, concealed the sordid history of its first owner, a ruthless magnate whose fortune had been built on extortion and bribery.","at":"這棟維多利亞式宅邸外觀秀麗，有著華麗的山牆與蒼翠繁茂的花園，卻掩蓋了第一任屋主不堪的過往──那位冷酷的富豪靠著勒索與賄賂累積財富。"},{"w":"frenetic","p":"adj.","d":"frantic, frenzied.","c":"狂熱的；發狂似的","s":"The final week before the international trade fair was frenetic for the small design company, as employees worked eighteen-hour days building display booths, printing brochures, and preparing product samples. Phones rang constantly, deliveries arrived late, and last-minute changes created chaos in the office. Despite the frantic atmosphere, the team finished everything just in time. Their exhibition attracted several major clients, making the exhausting effort entirely worthwhile. Everyone took a well-earned vacation afterward.","t":"國際貿易展前的最後一週，對這家小型設計公司而言是一片忙亂，員工們每天工作十八小時，搭建展位、印製手冊並準備產品樣品。電話響個不停，貨物延遲送達，最後一刻的變更更讓辦公室陷入混亂。儘管氣氛手忙腳亂，團隊還是及時完成了一切。他們的展覽吸引了幾位重要客戶，讓這番精疲力竭的努力完全值得。事後大家都享受了一個應得的假期。","as":"The trading floor erupted into frenetic activity after a false rumor precipitated mass selling, with brokers gesticulating wildly as the index plunged toward its nadir until regulators intervened to terminate trading for the day.","at":"一則不實傳言突然引發大量拋售，交易大廳隨即陷入瘋狂忙亂，交易員激動地比手畫腳，指數一路跌向谷底，直到主管機關出面介入，宣布當日停止交易。"},{"w":"artifice","p":"n.","d":"clever trick, strategy, trickery.","c":"詭計；巧妙手段","s":"The con artist relied on elaborate artifice to convince wealthy investors that his mining company had discovered enormous gold deposits. He hired actors to pose as geologists, displayed fake rock samples, and created convincing reports filled with technical language. For two years, his clever deception fooled even experienced financiers. When the truth finally emerged, investigators estimated that he had stolen more than fifty million dollars through his carefully planned trickery.","t":"這名騙子依靠精心設計的詭計，說服富有的投資人相信他的礦業公司發現了大量金礦。他僱用演員假扮地質學家、展示偽造的岩石樣本，並製作充斥著專業術語、令人信服的報告。兩年來，他巧妙的騙局甚至騙過了經驗豐富的金融家。當真相終於曝光時，調查人員估計他透過這場精心策劃的騙局，詐取了超過五千萬美元。","as":"Over nearly a decade, the charlatan's elaborate artifice—forged diplomas, an invented aristocratic lineage, and impeccable manners—turned dozens of wealthy investors into dupes before an astute auditor finally exposed the hoax.","at":"近十年來，這名騙子精心設計的詭計──偽造的文憑、捏造的貴族血統，以及無可挑剔的禮儀──讓數十位富有的投資人上當受騙，直到一位精明的稽核人員終於揭穿了這場騙局。"},{"w":"diversity","p":"n.","d":"variety.","c":"多樣性","s":"Taiwan's remarkable biological diversity surprises many visitors, since the island contains tropical beaches, subtropical forests, and snow-covered mountains nearly four thousand meters high. Within a relatively small area, scientists have identified thousands of plant species and many animals found nowhere else on Earth. Conservation experts emphasize that protecting this rich variety of life requires careful management of national parks, especially as climate change threatens delicate mountain ecosystems. Visitors are always amazed.","t":"台灣驚人的生物多樣性讓許多遊客感到驚訝，因為這座島嶼擁有熱帶海灘、亞熱帶森林，以及將近四千公尺高、白雪覆蓋的高山。在相對狹小的面積內，科學家已辨識出數千種植物，以及許多世界上其他地方找不到的動物。保育專家強調，要保護這豐富多樣的生命，需要謹慎管理國家公園，尤其是在氣候變遷威脅脆弱的高山生態系之際。遊客們總是驚嘆不已。","as":"The Amazon rainforest's astonishing biological diversity, encompassing myriad insect species not yet catalogued, is jeopardized by rampant logging that threatens to eradicate entire habitats before scientists can even document them.","at":"亞馬遜雨林擁有驚人的生物多樣性，包含無數尚未編目的昆蟲物種；然而猖獗的伐木正危及這一切，可能在科學家來得及記錄之前，就將整片棲地徹底消滅。"},{"w":"qualm","p":"n.","d":"twinge of conscience, sudden feeling of doubt.","c":"疑慮；良心不安","s":"The young accountant felt a sharp qualm when his manager asked him to change several numbers in the annual report so that the company's losses would appear smaller. He knew that altering the figures would mislead shareholders and possibly break the law. After a sleepless night, he refused the request and reported the matter to the company's ethics committee. His uneasy conscience ultimately protected both his career and investors. He was later promoted.","t":"當經理要求這位年輕會計師修改年度報告中的幾個數字，好讓公司的虧損看起來小一點時，他感到一陣強烈的良心不安。他知道竄改數字會誤導股東，甚至可能觸法。經過一夜難眠，他拒絕了這個要求，並將此事通報公司的倫理委員會。他不安的良心最終同時保護了他的職業生涯與投資人。他後來獲得了升遷。","as":"The young soldier felt no qualm about deserting a regime he loathed, yet he was distraught at the thought that his family, left behind in the capital, might be harassed by its implacable secret police.","at":"這名年輕士兵對於背棄自己痛恨的政權毫無良心不安；但一想到留在首都的家人可能遭到該政權冷酷無情的秘密警察騷擾，他就心煩意亂。"},{"w":"expurgate","p":"v.","d":"to remove objectionable parts or passages.","c":"刪去（不當內容）","s":"Before publishing the famous poet's letters, her family decided to expurgate several passages containing harsh comments about living relatives and private medical details. They removed sentences they considered embarrassing or hurtful while preserving the letters' literary value. Some scholars criticized the edited collection, arguing that readers deserved to see the complete, uncensored texts. The unaltered originals will be released to researchers fifty years after the poet's death. Scholars eagerly await that date.","t":"在出版這位知名詩人的書信之前，她的家人決定刪去幾段內容，其中包含對在世親戚的尖刻評論以及私人醫療細節。他們刪除了他們認為令人難堪或傷人的句子，同時保留書信的文學價值。有些學者批評這本經過刪修的書信集，認為讀者有權看到完整、未經審查的原文。未經改動的原稿將在詩人過世五十年後開放給研究人員。學者們熱切期待著那一天。","as":"Soviet censors, ubiquitous in the publishing industry, routinely expurgated foreign novels, excising any passage that seemed covertly critical of the regime, so readers often encountered truncated editions without realizing how drastically the authors' intent had been modified.","at":"蘇聯的審查人員遍布出版業，經常刪改外國小說，將任何看似暗中批評政權的段落一律刪除；因此讀者讀到的往往是刪節版，卻渾然不知作者的原意已被大幅更動。"},{"w":"begrudge","p":"v.","d":"to resent, give reluctantly.","c":"吝惜；嫉妒","s":"Although she had worked just as hard as her teammate, the runner did not begrudge his victory at the national championship, congratulating him warmly after the race. She admitted feeling disappointed about finishing second, but she refused to resent a friend who had trained with such dedication. Reporters admired her generous sportsmanship. The following year, their positions were reversed, and he celebrated her first national title with equal enthusiasm and genuine joy.","t":"雖然她和隊友一樣努力，這位跑者並不嫉妒他在全國錦標賽的勝利，賽後還熱情地向他道賀。她承認對得到第二名感到失望，但她拒絕怨恨一位如此投入訓練的朋友。記者們欣賞她大度的運動家精神。隔年，兩人的名次對調，他也以同樣的熱情與真誠的喜悅，慶祝她奪得第一座全國冠軍。","as":"Although she had once begrudged her rival's prestigious award, the novelist eventually acknowledged his virtuosity, conceding in a public interview that his recondite but trenchant essays deserved the acclaim they received.","at":"雖然這位小說家曾對對手獲得的著名獎項心懷不滿，但她最終承認對方才華出眾，並在一次公開訪談中坦言，他那些艱深卻犀利的文章確實實至名歸。"},{"w":"artless","p":"adj.","d":"naive, innocent, without deception.","c":"天真的；純樸的","s":"The child's artless question, asking the famous politician why he never answered anyone's questions directly, caused the entire audience to burst into laughter. She had no intention of embarrassing him; she was simply curious and completely sincere. The politician laughed good-naturedly and admitted that she had made an excellent point. Newspapers published the innocent exchange the next day, and many readers praised the girl's honest simplicity. She later received a letter of thanks.","t":"這個孩子天真地問這位知名政治人物，為什麼他從來不直接回答任何人的問題，讓全場觀眾哄堂大笑。她無意讓他難堪，只是單純好奇、完全真誠。這位政治人物和善地笑了，並承認她說得很有道理。隔天，報紙刊出了這段天真的對話，許多讀者讚揚這個女孩誠實純真的一面。她後來收到了一封感謝信。","as":"The child's artless confession that she had broken the vase elicited laughter rather than a reprimand, for her candor was so guileless that even her irascible grandfather could not stay angry.","at":"孩子天真地坦承是她打破了花瓶，結果引來的是笑聲而非責備；她的坦率毫無心機，連脾氣暴躁的爺爺也氣不起來。"},{"w":"gratuity","p":"n.","d":"tip, gift for service.","c":"小費；酬金","s":"Travelers visiting Taiwan are sometimes surprised to learn that leaving a gratuity is generally unnecessary in restaurants, since a service charge is often included in the bill. In contrast, visitors to the United States are expected to add fifteen to twenty percent for waiters. Travel guides recommend researching local customs before any trip, because tipping practices vary widely between countries and misunderstandings can cause embarrassment for both guests and staff.","t":"來台灣的旅客有時會驚訝地發現，在餐廳用餐通常不需要給小費，因為帳單中往往已包含服務費。相較之下，前往美國的遊客則被期望額外支付百分之十五到二十的小費給服務生。旅遊指南建議在任何旅行之前先研究當地習俗，因為各國給小費的習慣差異很大，誤會可能會讓客人與服務人員都感到尷尬。","as":"In Japan, offering a gratuity is often considered a breach of decorum, since impeccable service is deemed an intrinsic part of the job rather than a favor requiring extra remuneration.","at":"在日本，給小費常被視為有失禮節，因為無可挑剔的服務被認為是工作本身固有的一部分，而不是需要額外報酬的恩惠。"},{"w":"manifest","p":"adj.","d":"evident, obvious.","c":"明顯的；明白的","s":"The coach's disappointment was manifest as he watched his team lose by thirty points; he shook his head repeatedly, threw his clipboard to the ground, and refused to speak with reporters afterward. Everyone in the stadium could see how upset he was. The next morning, however, he apologized for his behavior and scheduled additional practice sessions. His players later said that his obvious frustration had motivated them to work harder.","t":"當教練看著球隊以三十分之差落敗時，他的失望顯而易見；他一再搖頭，把戰術板摔在地上，賽後也拒絕接受記者訪問。體育場裡的每個人都看得出他有多沮喪。然而隔天早上，他為自己的行為道歉，並安排了額外的練習。他的球員們後來表示，他明顯的挫折感激勵了他們更加努力。","as":"The general's incompetence became manifest when his rash decision to besiege the fortress in winter led to a fiasco, as his supply lines collapsed and frostbitten troops were forced to retreat.","at":"這位將軍的無能在他輕率決定於冬季圍攻要塞時表露無遺：這次行動以慘敗收場，補給線崩潰，凍傷的部隊被迫撤退。"},{"w":"delve","p":"v.","d":"to dig, investigate deeply.","c":"鑽研；深入探究","s":"For her doctoral thesis, the historian chose to delve into the forgotten diaries of Taiwanese tea merchants who traded with Europe during the nineteenth century. She spent three years examining fragile documents in archives across Taipei, London, and Amsterdam. Her deep research uncovered fascinating details about international commerce, family businesses, and daily life. The resulting book received several academic awards and inspired a popular television documentary series. She is now writing a sequel.","t":"為了撰寫博士論文，這位歷史學家選擇深入研究十九世紀與歐洲進行貿易的台灣茶商那些被遺忘的日記。她花了三年時間，在台北、倫敦與阿姆斯特丹各地的檔案館中檢視脆弱的文件。她深入的研究揭露了關於國際貿易、家族企業與日常生活的精彩細節。這本研究成果寫成的書獲得了數項學術獎項，並啟發了一部受歡迎的電視紀錄片系列。她目前正在撰寫續集。","as":"To understand the origins of the feud, the historian delved into voluminous archives, poring over yellowed letters which revealed that the acrimonious rivalry between two eminent families had begun with a trivial dispute over land.","at":"為了探究這場世仇的起源，歷史學家深入研究卷帙浩繁的檔案，仔細翻閱泛黃的信件，發現兩個顯赫家族之間的激烈對立，竟始於一場微不足道的土地糾紛。"},{"w":"capricious","p":"adj.","d":"unpredictable, changing on a whim.","c":"反覆無常的；任性的","s":"Mountain weather in Taiwan is notoriously capricious; a bright, sunny morning can turn into a violent thunderstorm within an hour. Hikers who fail to prepare for sudden changes often find themselves soaked, cold, and lost in thick fog. Experienced guides always carry waterproof clothing, extra food, and emergency equipment, regardless of the forecast. They warn visitors that the unpredictable conditions have caused numerous accidents on popular trails. Preparation saves lives.","t":"台灣山區的天氣出了名地反覆無常；晴朗的早晨可能在一個小時內就變成猛烈的雷雨。沒有為突如其來的變化做好準備的登山客，常會發現自己全身濕透、又冷又在濃霧中迷路。經驗豐富的嚮導無論天氣預報如何，總是隨身攜帶防水衣物、額外的食物與緊急裝備。他們警告遊客，這種難以預測的天氣已在熱門步道上造成了無數事故。做好準備能拯救生命。","as":"The capricious monsoon, which might deliver torrential rain one week and leave fields parched the next, makes farming in the region precarious, compelling villagers accustomed to such vicissitudes to hoard grain against inevitable lean years.","at":"變化無常的季風可能這週帶來傾盆大雨，下週又讓田地乾涸，使當地農業充滿風險；早已習慣這種變遷的村民，不得不囤積糧食，以備無可避免的荒年。"},{"w":"requisite","p":"n.","d":"requirement, necessary thing.","c":"必需品；必要條件","s":"Fluency in English is an essential requisite for pilots flying international routes, since communication with air traffic controllers worldwide takes place in that language. Candidates must pass rigorous speaking and listening examinations before receiving their licenses. Aviation authorities emphasize that misunderstandings in the cockpit can have catastrophic consequences. For this reason, airlines provide ongoing language training to ensure that every pilot continues to meet this fundamental requirement. Safety depends on clear communication.","t":"流利的英語是飛行國際航線的機師必備的條件，因為與世界各地飛航管制員的溝通都是以英語進行。應試者在取得執照之前，必須通過嚴格的口說與聽力測驗。航空主管機關強調，駕駛艙內的誤解可能會造成災難性的後果。因此，航空公司提供持續的語言訓練，以確保每位機師都持續符合這項基本要求。安全仰賴清楚的溝通。","as":"Fluency in Latin was once a requisite for admission to elite universities, but as the language faced obsolescence in everyday scholarship, administrators judged the stipulation archaic and abrogated it early in the twentieth century.","at":"精通拉丁文曾是進入菁英大學的必要條件；但隨著這門語言在日常學術中逐漸被淘汰，校方認為這項規定已經過時，便在二十世紀初將其廢除。"},{"w":"replenish","p":"v.","d":"to fill again, restock.","c":"補充；重新裝滿","s":"After the typhoon, volunteers worked around the clock to replenish supplies at emergency shelters, delivering fresh water, rice, blankets, and medicine to thousands of displaced families. Donations arrived from across the island, but demand remained enormous for several weeks. Organizers created an online system to track which items were running low. This efficient approach allowed them to restock shelters quickly and ensure that no family went without essential necessities. Recovery took several months.","t":"颱風過後，志工們日以繼夜地補充緊急避難所的物資，將乾淨的飲水、白米、毛毯與藥品送給數千個流離失所的家庭。來自全島各地的捐贈陸續送達，但好幾週內需求仍然龐大。主辦單位建立了一套線上系統，追蹤哪些物資即將短缺。這種有效率的做法讓他們能迅速補足避難所的物資，確保沒有任何家庭缺乏基本的必需品。災後復原花了好幾個月。","as":"After the drought depleted the reservoirs, officials implored residents to curtail their water usage until autumn rains could replenish the supply, warning that lax conservation would exacerbate an already acute shortage.","at":"乾旱使水庫水量見底後，官員懇求居民減少用水，直到秋雨能重新補足水源；他們並警告，若節水措施鬆懈，將使原本已十分嚴重的缺水問題雪上加霜。"}]},{"unit":43,"cards":[{"w":"activism","p":"n.","d":"vigorous campaigning, advocacy for a cause.","c":"行動主義；社會運動","s":"Student activism played a crucial role in Taiwan's democratic development, as young people organized peaceful demonstrations, wrote petitions, and occupied public spaces to demand political reform. Their determined campaigning drew national attention to issues such as free elections, freedom of speech, and government transparency. Historians note that many former student leaders later became lawmakers, journalists, and professors. Today, young people continue this tradition by advocating for environmental protection and social equality through both online and offline campaigns.","t":"學生運動在台灣的民主發展中扮演了關鍵角色，年輕人組織和平示威、撰寫請願書，並佔領公共空間以要求政治改革。他們堅定的抗爭讓全國關注自由選舉、言論自由與政府透明等議題。歷史學家指出，許多昔日的學運領袖後來成為立法委員、記者與教授。如今，年輕人透過線上與線下的行動，為環境保護與社會平等發聲，延續著這個傳統。","as":"Decades of grassroots activism by indigent farmers in the river valley, who were adamant that pernicious pesticides be banned, eventually galvanized lawmakers to promulgate stricter environmental regulations across the region despite fierce opposition from chemical manufacturers.","at":"數十年來，河谷地區的貧困農民持續投入基層社會運動，堅持要求禁用有害農藥，最終不顧化學製造商的強烈反對，促使立法者在全區頒布更嚴格的環境法規。"},{"w":"aloof","p":"adj.","d":"reserved, distant, uninvolved.","c":"冷淡的；疏遠的","s":"The new neighbor seemed aloof at first, rarely greeting anyone in the elevator and declining invitations to building gatherings. Some residents assumed he was arrogant or unfriendly and stopped trying to talk with him. Months later, they learned that he had recently lost his wife and was struggling with deep grief. Once neighbors understood his situation, they gently reached out, and his distant manner gradually softened into genuine warmth and lasting friendship.","t":"這位新鄰居起初似乎很冷淡，在電梯裡很少跟人打招呼，也婉拒了大樓聚會的邀請。有些住戶以為他傲慢或不友善，便不再試著和他說話。幾個月後，他們才得知他最近失去了妻子，正陷在深深的悲傷之中。一旦鄰居們了解他的處境，便溫和地向他伸出援手，他疏遠的態度也逐漸轉變為真誠的溫暖與長久的友誼。","as":"Although critics construed the physicist's aloof demeanor at conferences as disdain, her confidants attested that she was merely reticent, preferring to ponder recondite equations rather than engage in mundane small talk.","at":"雖然批評者把這位物理學家在研討會上的冷漠態度解讀為輕蔑，但她的知己證實她只是沉默寡言，寧可思索深奧的方程式，也不願參與平淡無奇的閒聊。"},{"w":"ameliorate","p":"v.","d":"to relieve, improve, make better.","c":"改善；減輕","s":"To ameliorate overcrowding in the city's hospitals, the health ministry opened several new community clinics that treat minor illnesses and injuries. Patients with colds, sprained ankles, or routine prescriptions can now visit these neighborhood facilities instead of waiting hours in emergency rooms. Within a year, waiting times at major hospitals decreased significantly, allowing doctors to focus on serious cases. Officials plan to expand the program further, hoping to improve healthcare access throughout rural regions as well.","t":"為了改善市內醫院人滿為患的情況，衛生部開設了數間新的社區診所，治療輕微的疾病與傷害。感冒、腳踝扭傷或需要例行處方的病患，如今可以到這些社區診所就醫，而不必在急診室等上好幾個小時。一年內，大型醫院的等候時間大幅縮短，讓醫生能專注於重症病例。官員們計畫進一步擴大這項計畫，希望也能改善偏鄉地區的就醫管道。","as":"To ameliorate the malnutrition that was prevalent among rural children, the agency deployed mobile clinics and stipulated that every school lunch include fortified grains, measures that soon yielded tangible improvements in growth rates.","at":"為了改善鄉村兒童普遍營養不良的問題，該機構派駐行動診所，並規定每份學校午餐都必須包含營養強化穀物；這些措施很快就讓孩子的生長率有了具體的提升。"},{"w":"atrophy","p":"v.","d":"to waste away from lack of use.","c":"萎縮；衰退","s":"Astronauts who spend months aboard the International Space Station must exercise for about two hours every day, because without gravity their muscles quickly begin to atrophy. In weightless conditions, the body no longer needs to support its own weight, so muscles and bones gradually weaken. Scientists have designed special treadmills and resistance machines to prevent this deterioration. Research on astronauts has also helped doctors treat patients confined to bed for long periods on Earth.","t":"在國際太空站待上數個月的太空人每天必須運動大約兩小時，因為沒有重力，他們的肌肉很快就會開始萎縮。在無重力的狀態下，身體不再需要支撐自身的重量，因此肌肉與骨骼會逐漸變弱。科學家設計了特殊的跑步機與阻力訓練器材來防止這種退化。對太空人的研究也幫助醫生治療地球上長期臥床的病患。","as":"Much like the limbs of a sedentary patient confined to bed, astronauts' leg muscles begin to atrophy in microgravity, so flight surgeons prescribe a meticulous exercise regimen to obviate weakness that could leave crews incapacitated upon landing.","at":"就像長期臥床、缺乏活動的病人四肢一樣，太空人的腿部肌肉在微重力環境中會開始萎縮，因此航太醫師會開立一套嚴謹細緻的運動計畫，以預防肌力衰退導致太空人返回地面時失去行動能力。"},{"w":"benevolent","p":"adj.","d":"charitable, kindly, generous.","c":"仁慈的；慈善的","s":"The benevolent businessman donated most of his fortune to build schools and libraries in remote mountain villages, where children had previously walked for hours to attend classes. He visited each new school personally, reading stories to students and asking teachers what additional resources they needed. Although he could have lived in luxury, he preferred a simple lifestyle. Villagers honored his kind generosity by naming a new community center after him last year.","t":"這位仁慈的商人將大部分財產捐出，在偏遠山村興建學校與圖書館，那裡的孩子過去得走好幾個小時的路才能上學。他親自走訪每一所新學校，為學生朗讀故事，並詢問老師還需要哪些額外的資源。雖然他本可以過著奢華的生活，他卻偏愛簡樸的日子。村民們去年以他的名字為一座新的社區中心命名，以表彰他仁慈慷慨的善舉。","as":"Unlike the parsimonious factory owners of his era, the benevolent industrialist funded libraries and hospitals for his workers' progeny, an altruistic legacy that historians still deem laudable at a time when most employers regarded laborers as expendable.","at":"與同時代吝嗇的工廠老闆不同，這位仁慈的實業家出資為員工的子女興建圖書館和醫院；這份無私的遺澤至今仍被歷史學家認為值得讚揚——畢竟在那個年代，多數雇主都把勞工視為可以隨意犧牲的人力。"},{"w":"criterion","p":"n.","d":"standard or rule used for judging.","c":"標準；準則","s":"When selecting students for the science research program, the most important criterion was not test scores but genuine curiosity and persistence. Applicants were asked to describe a problem they had investigated independently and explain how they overcame obstacles. The judges believed that this standard would identify young people capable of original discoveries. Several students with average grades but remarkable determination were accepted, and many later produced award-winning research projects at international competitions.","t":"在甄選科學研究計畫的學生時，最重要的標準不是考試成績，而是真正的好奇心與毅力。申請者被要求描述一個他們獨立探究過的問題，並說明他們如何克服障礙。評審們相信，這個標準能找出有能力做出原創發現的年輕人。好幾位成績普通但決心非凡的學生獲得錄取，其中許多人後來在國際競賽中完成了得獎的研究計畫。","as":"Because the committee's sole criterion for the prestigious award was scholarly impact, several prolific researchers whose output was merely voluminous rather than influential were relegated to the lower tiers of the shortlist.","at":"由於委員會評選這項崇高獎項的唯一標準是學術影響力，幾位著作雖多、但只是數量龐大而缺乏影響力的多產研究者，便被降到決選名單的後段。"},{"w":"cynic","p":"n.","d":"skeptic, one who doubts others' good intentions.","c":"憤世嫉俗者；犬儒","s":"Having watched countless politicians break their promises, the elderly journalist had become a cynic who assumed that every public official secretly served personal interests. When a young mayor announced a genuine anti-corruption program, he predicted it would fail within months. To his surprise, the reforms succeeded, and several dishonest officials were prosecuted. The experience softened his skeptical attitude, and he admitted that honest leaders, though rare, do occasionally appear. He now writes more hopeful columns.","t":"看過無數政治人物食言而肥之後，這位年長的記者成了一個憤世嫉俗的人，認定每位公職人員都暗中圖謀私利。當一位年輕市長宣布一項真正的反貪計畫時，他預言這項計畫幾個月內就會失敗。出乎他意料的是，改革成功了，數名不誠實的官員遭到起訴。這次經驗軟化了他懷疑一切的態度，他也承認，誠實的領導者雖然罕見，但偶爾確實會出現。他現在寫的專欄充滿了希望。","as":"A confirmed cynic, the journalist scoffed at the senator's ostentatious charity gala, surmising that its true purpose was not generosity but a pretext for soliciting donations from affluent lobbyists seeking favorable legislation.","at":"這位記者是個徹頭徹尾的憤世嫉俗者，他嘲笑參議員那場鋪張炫耀的慈善晚宴，推測其真正目的並非行善，而是藉機向尋求有利立法的富有遊說人士募款。"},{"w":"guise","p":"n.","d":"outward appearance, often false.","c":"偽裝；外觀","s":"The criminals approached elderly residents under the guise of government health inspectors, wearing fake uniforms and carrying official-looking badges. Once inside homes, they claimed that expensive repairs were required immediately and demanded cash payments. Several victims lost thousands of dollars before police discovered the scheme. Authorities now remind citizens that genuine officials always carry verifiable identification and never request cash, urging people to call the police whenever visitors seem suspicious.","t":"這些罪犯假扮成政府衛生稽查員去接近年長居民，他們穿著假制服，並攜帶看似官方的證件。一進到屋內，他們便聲稱必須立即進行昂貴的維修，並要求支付現金。在警方發現這個詐騙手法之前，已有數名受害者損失了數千美元。主管機關如今提醒民眾，真正的官員一定攜帶可查證的身分證明，而且絕不會要求付現，並呼籲民眾在訪客看起來可疑時立即報警。","as":"Under the guise of a routine archaeological survey, the expedition leader surreptitiously removed priceless artifacts from the temple sanctuary, a flagrant act of plunder that remained undetected until an astute curator scrutinized the museum's inventory.","at":"這名探險隊隊長假借例行考古調查之名，暗中從神殿聖所搬走無價的文物；這種明目張膽的掠奪行為一直未被察覺，直到一位精明的策展人仔細檢查博物館的館藏清單才曝光。"},{"w":"iniquity","p":"n.","d":"wickedness, gross injustice.","c":"邪惡；不公正","s":"The famous novel exposes the iniquity of nineteenth-century factories, where children worked fourteen hours a day in dangerous conditions for almost no pay while wealthy owners lived in luxury. The author described the suffering so vividly that readers were shocked and outraged. Historians believe the book helped inspire laws protecting child workers. Today, teachers still use it to show students how literature can reveal injustice and motivate meaningful social change.","t":"這部著名小說揭露了十九世紀工廠的不公不義，孩子們在危險的環境中每天工作十四小時，幾乎拿不到任何報酬，而富有的工廠主人卻過著奢華的生活。作者對苦難的描寫如此生動，讓讀者感到震驚與憤慨。歷史學家相信，這本書促成了保護童工的法律。如今，老師們仍用它來讓學生了解文學如何揭露不公，並推動有意義的社會變革。","as":"In the decades before the Civil War, the abolitionist's vitriolic pamphlets denounced the iniquity of a system that subjugated millions, and her trenchant prose forced even indifferent readers to acknowledge the moral catastrophe unfolding in their own nation.","at":"南北戰爭前的數十年間，這位廢奴主義者以尖酸刻薄的小冊子痛斥一個奴役數百萬人的制度之邪惡不公，她犀利的文筆迫使連漠不關心的讀者也不得不承認身邊在自己國家正在發生的道德浩劫。"},{"w":"largess","p":"n.","d":"generosity, generous gifts.","c":"慷慨的贈與；慷慨","s":"Thanks to the largess of a wealthy alumnus, the small university was able to build a modern science laboratory, provide full scholarships to fifty students, and hire several distinguished professors. The donor, who had grown up in poverty, explained that education had transformed his life and he wished to give others the same opportunity. His generous gifts dramatically improved the university's reputation and attracted talented applicants from across the country.","t":"多虧一位富有校友的慷慨捐贈，這所小型大學得以興建現代化的科學實驗室、提供五十名學生全額獎學金，並聘請數位傑出的教授。這位在貧困中長大的捐款人解釋說，教育改變了他的人生，他希望給予其他人同樣的機會。他慷慨的捐贈大幅提升了學校的聲譽，並吸引了來自全國各地的優秀申請者。","as":"The emperor's largess, which included lavish banquets, gold coins tossed to the throng, and sumptuous gifts to loyal generals, was less a sign of generosity than a calculated strategy to quell incipient dissent.","at":"皇帝的慷慨賞賜——包括盛大的宴席、撒向群眾的金幣，以及送給忠心將領的奢華禮物——與其說是出於大方，不如說是為了平息剛萌芽的異議而精心算計的策略。"},{"w":"maim","p":"v.","d":"to disable, injure seriously.","c":"使殘廢；使受重傷","s":"Landmines left behind after wars continue to maim innocent farmers and children decades after the fighting has ended. These hidden explosives lie buried in fields and forests, causing serious injuries that often result in permanent disability. International organizations have spent years clearing contaminated land and providing artificial limbs to survivors. An international treaty banning these weapons has been signed by more than one hundred and sixty countries, significantly reducing new casualties worldwide.","t":"戰爭遺留下的地雷，在戰事結束數十年後，仍持續使無辜的農民與孩童受到重創而致殘。這些隱藏的爆裂物埋在田野與森林中，造成的嚴重傷害往往導致終身殘疾。國際組織多年來持續清除遭污染的土地，並為倖存者提供義肢。一項禁止這類武器的國際條約已有一百六十多個國家簽署，大幅減少了全球新增的傷亡。","as":"Landmines scattered across former battlefields in Southeast Asia continue to maim farmers and children decades after the cessation of hostilities, an insidious legacy that humanitarian groups implore governments to eradicate through systematic clearance programs.","at":"戰火停止數十年後，散布在東南亞昔日戰場上的地雷仍不斷炸傷農民與孩童，造成終身殘疾；人道組織懇求各國政府透過系統性的排雷計畫，徹底根除這項陰險的戰爭遺毒。"},{"w":"mercenary","p":"adj.","d":"greedy, motivated only by money.","c":"唯利是圖的","s":"Critics accused the famous athlete of being purely mercenary after he left his hometown team, which had developed his talent since childhood, to join a rival club offering twice the salary. Fans who had cheered for him for years felt betrayed and burned his jersey outside the stadium. The athlete insisted that he needed financial security for his family. Nevertheless, many supporters believed that his decision reflected greed rather than loyalty.","t":"這位知名運動員離開了從小培養他才華的家鄉球隊，轉投提供兩倍薪水的對手球隊後，批評者指責他完全唯利是圖。多年來為他加油的球迷感到被背叛，在體育場外焚燒他的球衣。這位運動員堅稱他需要為家人取得經濟保障。儘管如此，許多支持者仍認為他的決定反映的是貪婪，而非忠誠。","as":"Critics castigated the pharmaceutical firm's mercenary decision to quintuple the price of a lifesaving drug, arguing that exploiting vulnerable patients for lucrative profits violated the most basic ethics of medicine.","at":"批評者嚴厲譴責這家藥廠唯利是圖，將一種救命藥物的價格調漲五倍，認為剝削脆弱的病患來牟取暴利，違背了最基本的醫學倫理。"},{"w":"mollify","p":"v.","d":"to appease, pacify, calm.","c":"撫慰；平息","s":"The airline tried to mollify angry passengers whose flight had been delayed for nine hours by offering free meals, hotel rooms, and discount vouchers for future trips. The captain personally apologized and explained that the delay had been caused by a serious mechanical problem. Most travelers gradually calmed down and appreciated the honest explanation. The company's thoughtful response turned a potential public relations disaster into an example of good customer service.","t":"航空公司為了安撫航班延誤九小時的憤怒乘客，提供了免費餐點、飯店住宿以及未來旅行的折價券。機長親自道歉，並解釋延誤是由嚴重的機械故障所造成。大多數旅客逐漸冷靜下來，也很感謝這番誠實的說明。這家公司周到的應對，將一場可能的公關災難，轉變為良好顧客服務的範例。","as":"To mollify the irate investors who had inundated the company with complaints, the chief executive announced a generous dividend and pledged to curtail the inordinate bonuses that executives had awarded themselves.","at":"為了安撫那些以大量投訴淹沒公司的憤怒投資人，執行長宣布發放豐厚股利，並承諾削減高層主管自肥的過高獎金。"},{"w":"pragmatic","p":"adj.","d":"practical, based on experience rather than theory.","c":"務實的；實用主義的","s":"Instead of pursuing an expensive plan to build a new stadium, the city council took a pragmatic approach and renovated the existing sports facilities at a fraction of the cost. They focused on improving lighting, seating, and accessibility rather than creating an impressive landmark. Residents appreciated the practical decision, which allowed the city to spend the remaining money on public parks, bicycle lanes, and programs for young athletes throughout the community.","t":"市議會沒有推動興建新體育場的昂貴計畫，而是採取務實的做法，以一小部分的成本翻新現有的運動設施。他們專注於改善照明、座位與無障礙設施，而不是打造一座令人驚豔的地標。居民們讚賞這個實際的決定，讓市府能將剩餘的經費用在公園、自行車道，以及為全社區年輕運動員設計的計畫上。","as":"Rather than pursue a chimerical scheme that was clearly not feasible, the mayor adopted a pragmatic approach, modifying existing bus routes incrementally and evaluating each change before committing scarce funds.","at":"市長沒有追求顯然不可行的空想計畫，而是採取務實的做法：逐步調整現有公車路線，並在投入有限經費之前先評估每一項改變的成效。"},{"w":"repent","p":"v.","d":"to feel regret, desire to make amends.","c":"後悔；懺悔","s":"In the old folk tale, a greedy landlord who had cheated his tenants for decades began to repent after a terrible dream showed him the suffering he had caused. The next morning, he returned stolen money, lowered rents, and opened his granary to hungry families. Villagers were astonished by his sudden transformation. The story, still told to children today, teaches that genuine regret can inspire people to correct their past wrongs.","t":"在這個古老的民間故事中，一個欺壓佃農數十年的貪婪地主，在一場可怕的夢讓他看見自己造成的苦難後，開始懺悔。隔天早上，他歸還了不義之財、降低租金，並打開糧倉接濟飢餓的家庭。村民們對他突然的轉變感到驚訝。這個至今仍講給孩子們聽的故事告訴我們，真心的悔悟能激勵人們彌補過去的錯誤。","as":"Late in life, the octogenarian general came to repent the havoc his troops had wreaked on civilian villages, and in a poignant memoir he expressed hope that his candor might offer some solace to survivors.","at":"這位八十多歲的將軍到了晚年，開始悔恨自己的部隊當年對平民村莊造成的浩劫；他在一本令人心酸的回憶錄中表示，希望自己的坦白能為倖存者帶來些許慰藉。"},{"w":"roster","p":"n.","d":"list of names.","c":"名單；花名冊","s":"The coach posted the team roster on the gym door the morning after tryouts, and dozens of nervous students crowded around to see whether their names appeared on the list. Some cheered and hugged friends, while others walked away quietly disappointed. The coach later spoke privately with every student who had not been selected, offering specific advice for improvement. Several of them earned places on the team the following year.","t":"試訓後的隔天早上，教練把球隊名單貼在體育館門口，數十名緊張的學生擠在一起，看自己的名字是否出現在名單上。有些人歡呼並和朋友擁抱，有些人則默默失望地走開。教練後來私下與每位沒有入選的學生談話，給予具體的改進建議。其中好幾位在隔年便贏得了球隊的一席之地。","as":"Perusing the expedition's original roster, the historian discerned a salient anomaly: three crew members listed as sailors were actually felons who had joined under false names to escape the jurisdiction of English courts.","at":"歷史學家仔細研讀探險隊的原始名冊時，發現了一個明顯的異常：名冊上登記為水手的三名船員，其實是用假名入隊、企圖逃避英國法院管轄的重罪犯。"},{"w":"stunted","p":"adj.","d":"held back in natural growth.","c":"發育不良的；受阻礙的","s":"Trees growing near the top of the windy mountain are stunted, reaching only a fraction of the height of the same species growing in sheltered valleys below. Harsh winds, thin soil, and freezing temperatures prevent them from developing normally. Their twisted branches and small trunks create a strange, beautiful landscape that attracts photographers. Botanists study these slow-growing trees to understand how plants adapt to extreme environments and survive difficult conditions.","t":"生長在多風山頂附近的樹木發育不良，高度只有下方避風山谷中同種樹木的一小部分。強風、貧瘠的土壤與嚴寒的氣溫，使它們無法正常生長。它們扭曲的枝幹與矮小的樹幹，形成一幅奇特而美麗的景觀，吸引了許多攝影師。植物學家研究這些生長緩慢的樹木，以了解植物如何適應極端環境並在艱困條件下生存。","as":"Children who endure prolonged privation during infancy often exhibit stunted growth, a condition researchers regard as symptomatic of broader inequities and whose cumulative effects compensatory nutrition programs can only partially reverse.","at":"嬰兒時期長期處於匱乏狀態的孩子，往往會出現發育遲緩；研究人員認為這是更廣泛社會不平等的徵兆，而其累積的影響，補償性的營養計畫也只能部分扭轉。"},{"w":"subservient","p":"adj.","d":"excessively obedient, servile.","c":"屈從的；卑躬屈膝的","s":"Historians describe how the small kingdom became subservient to its powerful neighbor, obeying every command, paying enormous annual tributes, and changing its laws whenever the larger empire demanded. Its rulers lost nearly all independence and dared not refuse any request. Over time, citizens grew frustrated with their leaders' submissive behavior. Eventually, a popular movement demanded greater autonomy, gradually restoring the kingdom's ability to make its own decisions. Its citizens still celebrate that victory.","t":"歷史學家描述這個小王國如何變得屈從於強大的鄰國，服從每一道命令、繳納巨額的年貢，並在大帝國要求時隨時修改法律。它的統治者幾乎失去了所有的獨立性，不敢拒絕任何要求。隨著時間推移，人民對領導者卑躬屈膝的行為感到不滿。最終，一場民眾運動要求更大的自主權，逐漸恢復了王國自行做決定的能力。它的人民至今仍慶祝那場勝利。","as":"In the feudal order, peasants were fettered to the land and expected to remain subservient to their lords, and those who flouted this rigid decorum faced harsh reprisals from an implacable aristocracy.","at":"在封建體制下，農民被束縛在土地上，必須對領主唯命是從；凡是公然違反這套嚴格禮法的人，都會遭到冷酷無情的貴族階層嚴厲報復。"},{"w":"unctuous","p":"adj.","d":"insincerely flattering, excessively smooth.","c":"諂媚的；油腔滑調的","s":"Customers quickly grew uncomfortable with the car salesman's unctuous manner, as he complimented their clothes, praised their intelligence, and laughed too loudly at every comment they made. His excessive flattery seemed insincere and made them suspect he was hiding something. When they asked specific questions about the vehicle's history, he avoided answering directly. The couple left without buying anything and purchased a car from a more honest dealer. They never regretted it.","t":"顧客們很快就對這名汽車推銷員油腔滑調的態度感到不自在，他稱讚他們的衣著、恭維他們的聰明，並對他們說的每句話都笑得太大聲。他過度的奉承顯得虛偽，讓他們懷疑他在隱瞞什麼。當他們問到關於這輛車過去紀錄的具體問題時，他避而不答。這對夫婦什麼也沒買就離開了，後來向一位更誠實的經銷商買了車。他們從未後悔。","as":"The unctuous courtier showered the king with fulsome praise, yet his obsequious manner did not delude the perspicacious queen, who perceived the duplicity behind every flattering word and quietly warned her husband not to trust him.","at":"這名油腔滑調的朝臣對國王極盡阿諛奉承，但他卑躬屈膝的模樣騙不了眼光敏銳的王后，她看穿了每句奉承話背後的虛偽與心機，並悄悄提醒丈夫不要信任此人。"},{"w":"vestige","p":"n.","d":"trace, remaining evidence.","c":"遺跡；痕跡","s":"Hikers exploring the forest discovered a vestige of an abandoned Japanese-era village, including crumbling stone walls, rusted cooking pots, and the outline of an old schoolhouse. Nature had nearly erased the settlement, covering the foundations with moss and tree roots. Local historians studied the remains to learn how residents once lived in this remote area. The site has since been protected as a cultural heritage location for future generations. Tours are now available.","t":"在森林中探險的登山客發現了一處日治時期廢棄村落的遺跡，包括崩塌的石牆、生鏽的炊具，以及一座舊校舍的輪廓。大自然幾乎抹去了這個聚落，青苔與樹根覆蓋了建築的地基。當地的歷史學家研究這些遺跡，以了解居民過去如何在這個偏遠地區生活。此地此後已被列為文化資產地點加以保護，留給後代子孫。現在已有導覽行程。","as":"Rising above the olive groves, the crumbling aqueduct is the sole extant vestige of a once-opulent Roman city, and archaeologists hope its weathered stones will corroborate conjectures about why the settlement was abruptly abandoned in the fifth century.","at":"矗立在橄欖林之上、逐漸崩塌的引水道，是一座昔日富庶的羅馬城市僅存的遺跡；考古學家希望這些飽經風霜的石塊，能證實關於該聚落為何在五世紀突然遭到遺棄的種種推測。"}]},{"unit":44,"cards":[{"w":"canard","p":"n.","d":"made-up sensational story, false rumor.","c":"謠言；假新聞","s":"The widely shared canard claimed that drinking hot lemon water every morning could cure serious diseases, including cancer and diabetes. Millions of people forwarded the message to friends and family members without checking its accuracy. Doctors and scientists repeatedly explained that no research supported such claims and warned that believing the false story might lead patients to delay proper treatment. Fact-checking organizations eventually published detailed articles exposing the hoax and its misleading origins.","t":"這則被廣泛分享的謠言聲稱，每天早上喝熱檸檬水可以治癒包括癌症與糖尿病在內的重大疾病。數百萬人在沒有查證的情況下，將這則訊息轉傳給親友。醫生與科學家一再說明沒有任何研究支持這類說法，並警告相信這則假消息可能會讓病患延誤接受適當的治療。事實查核組織最終發表了詳細的文章，揭露這個騙局及其誤導性的來源。","as":"The canard that the vaccine caused infertility became rampant online, and despite incontrovertible evidence to the contrary, health officials struggled to neutralize a falsehood that had already permeated entire communities.","at":"「疫苗會導致不孕」這則謠言在網路上猖獗流傳；儘管有無可辯駁的反證，衛生官員仍難以消除這個早已滲透整個社區的謊言。"},{"w":"carnage","p":"n.","d":"slaughter, great destruction of life.","c":"大屠殺；大量殺戮","s":"Historians describe the Battle of the Somme in 1916 as one of the worst examples of carnage in modern warfare, with more than one million soldiers killed or wounded over five months. Commanders ordered repeated attacks across open fields against well-defended positions, resulting in enormous losses for very little territory. The terrible slaughter shocked the public when news reached home. Today, memorials across Europe honor the soldiers who lost their lives there.","t":"歷史學家形容1916年的索姆河戰役是現代戰爭中最慘烈的殺戮之一，在五個月內有超過一百萬名士兵陣亡或受傷。指揮官們一再下令士兵穿越開闊的田野，攻擊防守堅固的陣地，以極大的傷亡換取極少的土地。當消息傳回國內時，這場可怕的殺戮震驚了大眾。如今，歐洲各地的紀念碑都在追悼在那裡犧牲的士兵們。","as":"Survivors' accounts of the carnage at the Somme, where a single morning of fighting left nearly twenty thousand British soldiers dead, attest to the catastrophic toll of industrialized warfare and the obstinacy of generals who persevered with doomed frontal assaults.","at":"倖存者對索姆河戰役大屠殺的描述——光是一個早上的戰鬥就造成近兩萬名英軍陣亡——證明了工業化戰爭帶來的災難性傷亡，也揭示了將領們固執地堅持注定失敗的正面突擊。"},{"w":"defamatory","p":"adj.","d":"damaging someone's reputation with false statements.","c":"誹謗的；破壞名譽的","s":"The famous chef sued the magazine for publishing defamatory claims that her restaurant used expired ingredients and mistreated its employees. She provided health inspection reports, supplier receipts, and statements from staff proving that the accusations were completely false. The court agreed that the article had seriously damaged her reputation without evidence. The magazine was ordered to pay substantial compensation and publish a formal apology on its front page. Her business recovered quickly.","t":"這位知名主廚控告一家雜誌刊登誹謗性的說法，聲稱她的餐廳使用過期食材並虐待員工。她提出衛生檢查報告、供應商收據以及員工聲明，證明這些指控完全不實。法院同意這篇文章在毫無證據的情況下嚴重損害了她的名譽。該雜誌被判須支付大筆賠償金，並在封面刊登正式道歉啟事。她的生意很快便恢復了。","as":"The senator sued the tabloid for publishing scurrilous, defamatory claims that he had accepted bribes, and the court, finding the allegations wholly fabricated, ordered the paper to recant them on its front page.","at":"這位參議員控告小報刊登粗鄙且毀謗的內容，指稱他收受賄賂；法院認定這些指控完全是捏造的，命令該報在頭版公開撤回。"},{"w":"deluge","p":"v.","d":"to flood, overwhelm.","c":"淹沒；使應接不暇","s":"After the popular singer announced a surprise concert, excited fans began to deluge the ticket website with millions of requests within the first few minutes. The system crashed almost immediately, leaving thousands of frustrated customers unable to purchase tickets. The organizers apologized and scheduled three additional performances to satisfy the enormous demand. Technology experts noted that even large websites can be overwhelmed when so many people try to access them simultaneously.","t":"在這位人氣歌手宣布一場驚喜演唱會之後，興奮的歌迷們在最初幾分鐘內便以數百萬次的請求湧入售票網站。系統幾乎立刻當機，讓數千名沮喪的顧客買不到票。主辦單位道歉，並加開三場演出以滿足龐大的需求。科技專家指出，當這麼多人同時嘗試連線時，即使是大型網站也可能不堪負荷。","as":"After the network aired its controversial documentary, viewers deluged the station with complaints, many so caustic and garbled that the staff could not identify which scenes had elicited such outrage.","at":"電視網播出那部具爭議性的紀錄片後，觀眾的投訴如洪水般湧入電視台，其中許多內容尖酸又語無倫次，工作人員根本無法辨認究竟是哪些片段引發了如此強烈的憤怒。"},{"w":"deprecate","p":"v.","d":"to express disapproval of, belittle.","c":"不贊成；輕視","s":"Although many parents deprecate the use of smartphones in classrooms, some teachers argue that these devices can be valuable learning tools when used responsibly. Critics complain that phones distract students and encourage cheating during tests. Supporters counter that students can use them to research topics, record experiments, and practice languages. Most schools now try to balance these views by allowing phones only during specific activities under careful teacher supervision. The debate continues.","t":"雖然許多家長不贊成在教室裡使用智慧型手機，但有些老師認為，只要負責任地使用，這些裝置可以成為有價值的學習工具。批評者抱怨手機讓學生分心，還助長考試作弊。支持者則反駁說，學生可以用手機查資料、記錄實驗和練習語言。如今，大多數學校試圖在這些意見之間取得平衡，只允許在老師仔細監督下的特定活動中使用手機。這場辯論仍在持續。","as":"Although early critics deprecated jazz as a vulgar, transient fad, musicologists now revere its pioneers, figures such as Louis Armstrong and Duke Ellington, whose improvisational virtuosity transformed the entire realm of twentieth-century music.","at":"雖然早期評論家貶低爵士樂，認為它不過是粗俗又短暫的流行，但如今音樂學家十分崇敬路易斯．阿姆斯壯、艾靈頓公爵等爵士樂先驅，因為他們精湛的即興技藝徹底改變了二十世紀的整個音樂領域。"},{"w":"devout","p":"adj.","d":"deeply religious, sincere.","c":"虔誠的","s":"Every morning before sunrise, the devout elderly woman walks to the neighborhood temple to light incense, offer fresh fruit, and pray quietly for her family's health. She has followed this routine for more than sixty years, regardless of weather or illness. Younger residents admire her sincere faith and discipline. When she was hospitalized last winter, temple volunteers took turns maintaining her daily offerings until she was able to return. Everyone welcomed her back.","t":"每天早上日出之前，這位虔誠的老婦人都會走到社區的廟宇上香、供奉新鮮水果，並靜靜地為家人的健康祈禱。無論天氣或身體狀況如何，她六十多年來始終維持這個習慣。年輕的居民們欽佩她真誠的信仰與自律。去年冬天她住院時，廟裡的志工們輪流替她維持每天的供奉，直到她能夠回來。大家都熱烈歡迎她回來。","as":"A devout Buddhist, the monk eschewed materialism entirely, subsisting on a frugal diet of rice and vegetables and spending his days in silent meditation in pursuit of nirvana, the liberation from suffering that he believed no possession could provide.","at":"這位虔誠的佛教僧侶完全摒棄物質享受，僅靠簡樸的米飯與蔬菜維生，終日靜坐冥想，追求涅槃的境界——他相信那種脫離苦痛的解脫，是任何財物都無法給予的。"},{"w":"diminutive","p":"adj.","d":"small, tiny.","c":"微小的；嬌小的","s":"Despite her diminutive size, the gymnast possessed extraordinary strength, performing powerful flips and landings that astonished judges and spectators. Standing barely one hundred and forty-five centimeters tall, she was often the smallest athlete at international competitions. Coaches explained that her small frame actually gave her an advantage in rotation and balance. She eventually won three Olympic gold medals, proving that physical size matters far less than skill and determination. She now coaches young gymnasts.","t":"儘管身材嬌小，這位體操選手卻擁有非凡的力量，她強而有力的空翻與落地動作讓裁判與觀眾大為驚嘆。她的身高只有一百四十五公分左右，在國際比賽中往往是最矮小的選手。教練們解釋，她嬌小的體型實際上讓她在旋轉與平衡方面佔有優勢。她最終贏得了三面奧運金牌，證明了體型的重要性遠不及技巧與決心。她如今擔任青年體操選手的教練。","as":"Despite her diminutive stature, the intrepid Victorian botanist trekked through treacherous Andean passes, cataloging a plethora of indigenous orchids that previous expeditions, deterred by inclement weather, had failed to document in any detail.","at":"儘管身材嬌小，這位維多利亞時代無畏的植物學家仍徒步穿越險峻的安地斯山隘口，記錄下大量當地原生的蘭花；先前的探險隊都因惡劣天候而卻步，未能完成這些紀錄。"},{"w":"dulcet","p":"adj.","d":"sweet or melodious to the ear.","c":"悅耳的；甜美的","s":"Every evening, the dulcet sound of a flute drifted from the small house at the end of the lane, delighting neighbors who paused on their balconies to listen. The elderly musician played gentle folk melodies that reminded many residents of their childhood. Parents said the soothing music helped their babies fall asleep. When the musician moved away, the neighborhood organized a farewell concert to thank him for years of beautiful, sweet-sounding performances.","t":"每天傍晚，悠揚悅耳的笛聲從巷子盡頭的小屋飄出，讓在陽台上駐足聆聽的鄰居們十分愉悅。這位年長的音樂家吹奏著溫柔的民謠旋律，讓許多居民想起了自己的童年。家長們說，這舒緩的音樂能幫助寶寶入睡。當這位音樂家搬走時，社區舉辦了一場告別音樂會，感謝他多年來美妙動聽的演奏。","as":"The dulcet tones of the cello created a tranquil atmosphere that contrasted sharply with the cacophony of traffic outside the concert hall, offering the engrossed audience a brief respite from urban life.","at":"大提琴甜美悅耳的音色營造出寧靜的氛圍，與音樂廳外刺耳的車流喧囂形成強烈對比，讓全神貫注的聽眾暫時從都市生活中獲得喘息。"},{"w":"excoriate","p":"v.","d":"to criticize severely.","c":"嚴厲批評；痛斥","s":"Environmental groups continued to excoriate the oil company for its slow response to the massive spill, accusing executives of caring more about profits than protecting wildlife and coastal communities. Their harsh statements appeared in newspapers and on television for weeks. Scientists also criticized the company's inadequate cleanup methods. Under intense public pressure, the company eventually replaced its leadership and committed billions of dollars to restoring the damaged coastline. Recovery took years.","t":"環保團體持續嚴厲抨擊這家石油公司對大規模漏油事件的反應遲緩，指責其高層在意利潤更甚於保護野生動物與沿海社區。他們嚴厲的聲明連續數週出現在報紙與電視上。科學家們也批評該公司清理方法不足。在巨大的輿論壓力下，這家公司最終撤換了領導階層，並承諾投入數十億美元修復受損的海岸線。復原花了好幾年。","as":"In a scathing review, the critic excoriated the novelist's latest work as verbose and banal, deriding its interminable descriptions of scenery and its predictable, formulaic plot, which she likened to a tedious lecture that refused to end.","at":"這位評論家在一篇尖銳的書評中嚴厲抨擊該小說家的新作冗長又陳腐，並嘲諷書中沒完沒了的景物描寫和老套、可預料的情節，還把整本書比作一場拖沓冗長、永遠講不完的演講。"},{"w":"frail","p":"adj.","d":"weak, delicate.","c":"脆弱的；虛弱的","s":"After spending three months in the hospital recovering from pneumonia, the elderly man had become extremely frail, unable to walk more than a few steps without assistance. His family arranged for a physical therapist to visit their home three times a week. Through gentle exercises and nutritious meals, he gradually regained his strength. Within six months, the once weak patient was walking to the park every morning with his grandchildren.","t":"在醫院住了三個月從肺炎中康復後，這位老先生變得極為虛弱，沒有人攙扶就走不了幾步路。他的家人安排一位物理治療師每週到家裡三次。透過溫和的運動與營養的餐點，他逐漸恢復了體力。六個月內，這位曾經虛弱的病人已經每天早上和孫子們一起走路去公園了。","as":"Though her frail body had been ravaged by a malignant tumor, the poet continued to write with remarkable gusto, completing a final collection that critics hailed as the zenith of her career.","at":"雖然虛弱的身軀已被惡性腫瘤摧殘，這位詩人仍以驚人的熱情持續寫作，完成了最後一部詩集，評論家盛讚那是她創作生涯的巔峰。"},{"w":"futility","p":"n.","d":"uselessness, pointlessness.","c":"徒勞；無用","s":"After spending hours trying to repair his ancient laptop, the student finally recognized the futility of his efforts and decided to buy a new computer. Every time he fixed one problem, another appeared, and replacement parts were no longer manufactured. His friends had warned him that the old machine was beyond saving. He later laughed about the experience, admitting that he had wasted an entire weekend on a pointless task.","t":"在花了好幾個小時試圖修理他那台老舊的筆電之後，這名學生終於認清了自己努力的徒勞，決定買一台新電腦。每當他修好一個問題，另一個問題就會出現，而且替換零件也早已停產。他的朋友們曾警告他，那台舊電腦已經無藥可救。他後來笑著談起這段經歷，承認自己把整個週末浪費在一件毫無意義的事情上。","as":"Recognizing the futility of resisting an enemy army that had besieged the city for nearly six months, the emaciated garrison finally succumbed, its commander negotiating an amnesty that spared the remaining civilians.","at":"面對已圍城將近六個月的敵軍，骨瘦如柴的守軍終於認清再抵抗也是徒勞，只好投降；指揮官談妥了一項特赦協議，讓城內剩下的平民得以倖免。"},{"w":"impromptu","p":"adj.","d":"offhand, spur of the moment, unplanned.","c":"即興的；無準備的","s":"When the scheduled speaker's flight was canceled, the school principal asked a student to give an impromptu speech at the graduation ceremony with only five minutes to prepare. Although nervous, the teenager spoke honestly about friendship, failure, and hope for the future. Her unrehearsed words moved the audience to tears. Many parents later said that her spontaneous speech was more memorable than any carefully prepared address they had ever heard.","t":"當預定演講者的班機被取消時，校長請一名學生在畢業典禮上發表一場即席演講，只給了她五分鐘準備。雖然緊張，這名青少女仍誠懇地談起友誼、失敗以及對未來的期望。她未經排練的話語讓觀眾感動落淚。許多家長事後表示，她這場即興的演講，比他們聽過的任何精心準備的致詞都更令人難忘。","as":"The senator's impromptu speech, delivered without notes after his teleprompter malfunctioned, proved far more cogent than his usual scripted remarks, and the candor of his spontaneous asides won over even his most contemptuous critics.","at":"參議員的提詞機故障後，他不看稿即興發表演說，結果比平常照稿念的講話更具說服力；他臨場脫口而出的坦率話語，甚至贏得了最輕蔑他的批評者的認同。"},{"w":"libel","p":"n.","d":"false written statement that damages someone's reputation.","c":"（書面）誹謗；中傷","s":"The politician filed a lawsuit accusing the newspaper of libel after it published an article falsely claiming that he had accepted bribes from construction companies. His lawyers argued that the printed accusations had seriously damaged his reputation and career. During the trial, the reporter could not provide any evidence supporting the story. The judge ruled in the politician's favor, ordering the newspaper to pay compensation and retract the defamatory article.","t":"這位政治人物提起訴訟，指控一家報紙刊登不實文章、聲稱他收受建設公司的賄賂，構成書面誹謗。他的律師主張，這些刊登出來的指控嚴重損害了他的名譽與政治生涯。審判期間，這名記者無法提出任何支持該報導的證據。法官判這位政治人物勝訴，命令報社支付賠償並撤回這篇誹謗性的文章。","as":"Deeming the editor culpable, the jury ruled that his article constituted libel because it besmirched a respected judge with mendacious accusations of bribery that he had never bothered to verify.","at":"陪審團認定該名編輯有罪，裁定他的文章構成書面誹謗，因為文中以不實的收賄指控玷污一位受人敬重的法官，而他從未費心查證這些指控。"},{"w":"malevolent","p":"adj.","d":"wishing harm to others, ill-intentioned.","c":"惡意的；狠毒的","s":"In the popular fantasy series, a malevolent sorcerer plots to destroy the peaceful kingdom by poisoning its rivers and turning its citizens against one another. He takes pleasure in causing suffering and never shows mercy to his enemies. Readers find the character genuinely frightening because his cruelty seems to have no limits. The young heroes must work together to defeat his wicked plans and restore harmony to their land. Fans eagerly await the final book.","t":"在這部熱門的奇幻系列中，一名心懷惡意的巫師策劃透過污染河流、挑撥人民互相對立，來摧毀這個和平的王國。他以製造痛苦為樂，對敵人從不手下留情。讀者覺得這個角色真的很可怕，因為他的殘忍似乎沒有極限。年輕的英雄們必須同心協力，擊敗他邪惡的計畫，讓他們的國土恢復和諧。書迷們熱切期待著最後一集。","as":"In Shakespeare's Othello, the malevolent Iago, consumed by resentment after being passed over for promotion, perpetrates an elaborate subterfuge, manipulating the gullible general into believing that his innocent wife has been unfaithful.","at":"在莎士比亞的《奧賽羅》中，心懷惡意的伊阿古因未獲升遷而滿腔怨恨，策劃了一場精心的詭計，操弄輕信他人的將軍，讓他相信自己無辜的妻子不忠。"},{"w":"nullify","p":"v.","d":"to cancel, make legally invalid.","c":"使無效；取消","s":"The court decided to nullify the contract after discovering that one of the companies had provided false financial information during negotiations. Because the agreement was based on deliberate deception, the judge ruled that it had no legal force. Both parties were required to return any payments already exchanged. Legal experts explained that contracts signed under fraudulent circumstances can be canceled to protect honest businesses from unfair losses. The case attracted national attention.","t":"在發現其中一家公司於協商期間提供不實的財務資訊後，法院決定使這份合約無效。由於這份協議是建立在蓄意欺騙的基礎上，法官判定它不具法律效力。雙方都必須歸還已經交付的款項。法律專家解釋，在詐欺情況下簽訂的合約可以被撤銷，以保護誠實的企業免於蒙受不公平的損失。此案引起了全國的關注。","as":"The high court voted to nullify the restrictive voting statute, ruling that its arbitrary literacy tests had been designed to disenfranchise minority citizens and thus constituted an egregious breach of constitutional guarantees.","at":"最高法院表決廢止這項限制性的投票法規，裁定其中武斷的識字測驗是為了剝奪少數族裔公民的投票權而設計，因此嚴重違反了憲法保障。"},{"w":"pathetic","p":"adj.","d":"sad, pitiful, arousing sympathy.","c":"可悲的；可憐的","s":"The pathetic sight of the abandoned puppy, shivering in the rain with its ribs showing and one leg injured, moved the young girl to tears. She wrapped it carefully in her jacket and carried it home, where her parents helped her take it to the veterinarian. After weeks of care and good food, the pitiful creature transformed into a healthy, playful dog that followed her everywhere with devotion. They remain inseparable today.","t":"那隻被遺棄的小狗在雨中發抖，肋骨清晰可見，一條腿還受了傷，這可憐的景象讓小女孩流下了眼淚。她小心地用外套把牠包起來帶回家，她的父母幫她帶牠去看獸醫。經過數週的照顧與好好的餵養，這隻可憐的小動物變成了一隻健康活潑的狗，忠心耿耿地跟著她到處跑。他們至今仍形影不離。","as":"The pathetic plight of the forlorn refugees, huddled in makeshift tents with neither food nor medicine, prompted even the most phlegmatic observers to exhort wealthy nations to provide immediate aid.","at":"孤苦無依的難民擠在臨時帳篷裡，既沒有食物也沒有藥品，這悲慘可憐的困境讓即使是最冷靜淡漠的觀察者，也呼籲富裕國家立即提供援助。"},{"w":"plaintiff","p":"n.","d":"the person who brings a lawsuit.","c":"原告","s":"In the famous case, the plaintiff was a small farmer who sued a giant chemical corporation, claiming that pesticides from its factory had contaminated his fields and destroyed his crops. Few people expected him to win against the company's expensive lawyers. However, scientific evidence clearly supported his claims. The jury awarded him millions of dollars in damages, and his victory inspired other farmers to file similar lawsuits across the country.","t":"在這起著名的案件中，原告是一位小農，他控告一家大型化學公司，聲稱其工廠的農藥污染了他的田地並毀了他的作物。很少人預期他能打贏這家公司昂貴的律師團。然而，科學證據明確支持他的主張。陪審團判給他數百萬美元的損害賠償，他的勝訴也激勵了全國其他農民提起類似的訴訟。","as":"The plaintiff, a disgruntled former engineer, claimed that the firm had coerced her into concealing safety defects, and her lawyers submitted internal memos that lent credence to her account of working under constant duress.","at":"原告是一名心懷不滿的前工程師，她指控公司逼迫她隱瞞安全缺陷；她的律師提交了內部備忘錄，使她所說長期在脅迫下工作的說法更具可信度。"},{"w":"potent","p":"adj.","d":"powerful, strong, effective.","c":"強而有力的；效力強的","s":"Researchers warn that some energy drinks contain potent combinations of caffeine and other stimulants that can cause heart problems, especially in teenagers. A single can may contain more caffeine than three cups of coffee. Doctors have reported cases of young people experiencing rapid heartbeats and severe anxiety after consuming several drinks in one day. Health authorities in several countries have banned sales of these powerful beverages to anyone under eighteen.","t":"研究人員警告，有些能量飲料含有咖啡因與其他興奮劑的強效組合，可能引發心臟問題，尤其是對青少年而言。一罐飲料所含的咖啡因可能比三杯咖啡還多。醫生們曾通報年輕人在一天內喝了好幾罐之後，出現心跳過快與嚴重焦慮的案例。數個國家的衛生主管機關已禁止將這些強效飲料販售給未滿十八歲的人。","as":"Penicillin proved a remarkably potent weapon against virulent infections that had once been lethal, yet decades of indiscriminate prescribing by doctors and overuse in livestock have allowed resistant bacteria to proliferate in hospitals worldwide.","at":"盤尼西林被證明是對抗那些曾經致命的猛烈感染的強效武器；然而數十年來醫師浮濫開立處方、畜牧業過度使用，已讓抗藥性細菌在全球各地的醫院大量繁殖。"},{"w":"profuse","p":"adj.","d":"abundant, overflowing, given freely.","c":"豐富的；大量的","s":"After accidentally spilling coffee on the famous author's manuscript, the embarrassed assistant offered profuse apologies, repeating how sorry he was at least a dozen times. The author laughed and assured him that she had saved digital copies of every page. Still, the young man continued apologizing throughout the afternoon. His colleagues later teased him gently about his abundant expressions of regret over such a minor accident. He brought her flowers the next day.","t":"在不小心把咖啡灑在這位知名作家的手稿上之後，尷尬的助理連連道歉，至少重複說了十幾次他有多抱歉。作家笑著向他保證，她已經把每一頁都存了電子檔。儘管如此，這個年輕人整個下午還是不停地道歉。他的同事們後來溫和地取笑他，為了這麼小的意外表達了那麼多的歉意。隔天他還送了花給她。","as":"The ambassador offered profuse apologies for his inadvertent insult to the visiting delegation, hoping to forestall any escalation of tensions and preserve the amicable relations the two nations had nurtured for decades.","at":"大使為自己無意間冒犯來訪代表團一事再三致歉，希望能避免緊張情勢升級，並維護兩國數十年來悉心培養的友好關係。"},{"w":"reputed","p":"adj.","d":"generally believed, supposed.","c":"被普遍認為的；據說的","s":"The old mansion is reputed to be haunted by the ghost of a wealthy merchant who died there more than a century ago. Local residents claim to have heard footsteps and piano music late at night, although no one has ever provided convincing evidence. The supposed ghost stories attract curious tourists every summer. Historians, meanwhile, are more interested in the building's architecture and the merchant's important role in regional trade.","t":"這棟古老的宅邸據說有一位一百多年前死在那裡的富商鬼魂出沒。當地居民聲稱曾在深夜聽到腳步聲和鋼琴聲，儘管從來沒有人提出令人信服的證據。這些傳聞中的鬼故事每年夏天都吸引好奇的觀光客前來。與此同時，歷史學家則對這棟建築的建築風格，以及這位富商在地區貿易中的重要角色更感興趣。","as":"The reputed founder of the city, a legendary nomadic chieftain, is celebrated in folk songs, though historians remain dubious that he ever existed, citing a paucity of archaeological evidence from the period in which he supposedly lived.","at":"據傳這座城市的創建者是一位傳奇的遊牧部落首領，民間歌謠至今仍傳頌著他；然而歷史學家以他據稱生活的那個時期考古證據稀少為由，懷疑此人是否真的存在過。"}]},{"unit":45,"cards":[{"w":"appalled","p":"adj.","d":"shocked, dismayed.","c":"震驚的；驚駭的","s":"Visitors to the beach were appalled to discover thousands of plastic bottles, fishing nets, and food containers scattered across the sand after a powerful storm. Many had expected a clean, beautiful coastline and could hardly believe how much trash the waves had deposited. Shocked by the scene, several families spontaneously began collecting garbage. Their efforts inspired a monthly volunteer cleanup program that now attracts hundreds of participants from across the region.","t":"在一場強烈暴風雨過後，海灘上的遊客驚駭地發現沙灘上散落著數千個塑膠瓶、漁網與食物容器。許多人原本期待看到乾淨美麗的海岸線，簡直不敢相信海浪帶來了這麼多垃圾。震驚於眼前的景象，好幾個家庭自發地開始撿拾垃圾。他們的努力促成了一項每月一次的志工淨灘計畫，如今吸引了來自整個地區的數百名參與者。","as":"Touring the textile mill, the inspector was appalled by its sordid conditions, in which children toiled amid pungent fumes for nominal wages, and she promptly denounced the situation as deplorable in her report.","at":"視察這座紡織廠時，督察員對廠內骯髒惡劣的環境大感震驚：孩童在刺鼻的煙霧中辛苦工作，只領取微薄的工資；她隨即在報告中痛斥這種情況令人憤慨。"},{"w":"bagatelle","p":"n.","d":"thing of little importance, trifle.","c":"瑣事；微不足道的事物","s":"To the billionaire investor, the fifty-thousand-dollar fine for violating parking regulations at his private airport was a mere bagatelle, hardly worth discussing with his lawyers. He paid it immediately without complaint and continued his busy schedule. Ordinary citizens, however, were outraged that the penalty was so small compared with his enormous wealth. Critics argued that fines should be proportional to income, so that wealthy individuals would treat laws as seriously as everyone else.","t":"對這位億萬富翁投資人而言，因違反其私人機場停車規定而被處以的五萬美元罰款，只是一件微不足道的小事，幾乎不值得和律師討論。他毫無怨言地立即繳清，繼續他忙碌的行程。然而，一般民眾對於這筆罰款與他龐大財富相比如此之小感到憤慨。批評者主張罰款應與收入成比例，這樣富人才會像其他人一樣認真看待法律。","as":"To the profligate heir, the regulators' fine was a mere bagatelle, a trivial sum that hardly impeded his lavish spending and certainly did not induce him to repudiate his reckless business practices.","at":"對這位揮霍無度的繼承人來說，主管機關開出的罰款不過是微不足道的小錢，既幾乎沒有妨礙他奢侈揮霍，更不可能讓他放棄魯莽的經營手法。"},{"w":"brigand","p":"n.","d":"bandit, robber.","c":"土匪；強盜","s":"In medieval Europe, merchants traveling through dense forests feared attacks by brigand who hid among the trees and ambushed caravans carrying valuable goods. These armed robbers stole silk, spices, and gold, sometimes holding wealthy travelers for ransom. To protect themselves, traders often journeyed in large groups accompanied by hired guards. Folk tales from this period frequently portray such bandits as either ruthless villains or romantic heroes who stole only from the rich.","t":"在中世紀的歐洲，穿越茂密森林的商人們害怕遭到土匪襲擊，這些人躲藏在樹林間，伏擊載運貴重貨物的商隊。這些武裝強盜搶奪絲綢、香料與黃金，有時還挾持富有的旅人勒索贖金。為了保護自己，商人們往往結成大隊同行，並雇用護衛隨行。這個時期的民間故事經常將這些強盜描繪成冷酷無情的惡棍，或是只搶劫富人的浪漫英雄。","as":"In eighteenth-century Calabria, armed brigands routinely lurked along the tortuous mountain passes, accosting itinerant merchants and robbing them with near impunity, since royal troops rarely ventured into such rugged and isolated terrain.","at":"十八世紀的卡拉布里亞，武裝土匪經常埋伏在蜿蜒曲折的山間隘道，攔截四處遊走的商人並加以搶劫，而且幾乎從未受到懲罰，因為王室軍隊很少深入如此崎嶇偏僻的地形。"},{"w":"callow","p":"adj.","d":"inexperienced, immature.","c":"缺乏經驗的；稚嫩的","s":"When he first joined the newspaper at twenty-two, the callow reporter made embarrassing mistakes, misquoting sources, missing deadlines, and asking politicians questions that revealed his lack of preparation. Senior editors patiently corrected his articles and taught him how to verify information carefully. Over the next decade, the once inexperienced journalist developed remarkable investigative skills. He eventually won a national award for exposing corruption in the city's construction industry. He now mentors young reporters.","t":"這位年輕記者二十二歲剛進報社時稚嫩青澀，犯了許多令人尷尬的錯誤：錯誤引述消息來源、錯過截稿期限，還向政治人物提出暴露自己準備不足的問題。資深編輯們耐心地修改他的文章，並教他如何仔細查證資訊。在接下來的十年間，這位曾經缺乏經驗的記者培養出非凡的調查能力。他最終因揭發該市營建業的貪腐而贏得一項全國性的獎項。他如今指導年輕記者。","as":"The callow lieutenant, brash and eager to prove his valor, ignored the veteran sergeant's warnings and led his platoon into an ambush that a more seasoned commander would have discerned at once.","at":"這名稚嫩的中尉魯莽又急於證明自己的英勇，不顧老練士官的警告，帶著整個排走進了一場埋伏；換作經驗較豐富的指揮官，必定一眼就能識破。"},{"w":"corpulent","p":"adj.","d":"fat, heavy-bodied.","c":"肥胖的","s":"Historical portraits show that King Henry VIII of England became extremely corpulent in his later years, after a serious jousting accident prevented him from exercising. His armor from that period measures more than one hundred and thirty centimeters around the waist. Historians believe that his heavy diet of roasted meats, pies, and wine contributed to his weight gain. His declining health may also have affected his notoriously unpredictable temper and decisions.","t":"歷史肖像顯示，英格蘭國王亨利八世在一次嚴重的馬上長槍比武意外使他無法運動之後，晚年變得極為肥胖。他那個時期的盔甲腰圍超過一百三十公分。歷史學家認為，他以烤肉、派餅與葡萄酒為主的豐盛飲食，是造成他體重增加的原因之一。他每況愈下的健康狀況，可能也影響了他出了名陰晴不定的脾氣與決策。","as":"The corpulent figures in Rubens's paintings, once considered paragons of beauty and prosperity, may seem incongruous to modern viewers steeped in a fashion culture that idolizes extreme thinness, a contrast revealing how much ideals of the body shift across centuries.","at":"魯本斯畫作中那些豐腴肥胖的人物，曾被視為美麗與富足的典範；但對深受推崇極度纖瘦的時尚文化薰陶的現代觀眾而言，這些形象可能顯得格格不入；這樣的對比顯示，人們對身體的審美標準在不同世紀間有多大的變化。"},{"w":"decapitate","p":"v.","d":"to cut off the head of.","c":"斬首；砍掉…的頭部","s":"Vandals entered the historic park during the night and used hammers to decapitate several stone statues of famous poets, leaving only the bodies standing on their pedestals. Residents were shocked when they discovered the headless figures the next morning. Police reviewed security footage and arrested three teenagers within a week. Skilled craftsmen spent months carving replacement heads, and the city installed additional cameras to protect its cultural monuments. The statues were restored.","t":"破壞者在夜間闖入這座歷史公園，用鐵鎚敲斷了幾尊著名詩人石像的頭部，只留下身軀立在基座上。隔天早上，居民們發現這些沒有頭的雕像時大為震驚。警方調閱監視器畫面，在一週內逮捕了三名青少年。技藝精湛的工匠們花了數個月雕刻替換的頭像，市府也加裝了更多監視器來保護其文化古蹟。這些雕像已被修復。","as":"During the Reign of Terror, the guillotine was used to decapitate thousands of alleged enemies of the revolution, many of whom were condemned after cursory trials in which the verdict seemed inevitable from the outset.","at":"恐怖統治時期，斷頭台斬首了數以千計被指控為革命敵人的人；其中許多人只經過草率的審判就被定罪，判決結果似乎從一開始就已注定。"},{"w":"divergent","p":"adj.","d":"differing, going in different directions.","c":"分歧的；不同的","s":"The twin sisters grew up in the same house and attended the same schools, yet they developed remarkably divergent interests and personalities. One became a quiet mathematician who spent hours solving complex problems, while the other became an outgoing actress who loved performing on stage. Psychologists studying twins find such differing paths fascinating, since they reveal how individual choices and experiences shape people even when genetics and environment are nearly identical.","t":"這對雙胞胎姊妹在同一個家中長大、就讀同樣的學校，卻發展出截然不同的興趣與個性。一個成了安靜的數學家，花好幾個小時解決複雜的問題；另一個則成了外向的女演員，熱愛在舞台上表演。研究雙胞胎的心理學家覺得這種不同的人生道路非常有意思，因為它們揭示了即使遺傳與環境幾乎相同，個人的選擇與經歷仍會塑造一個人。","as":"Although the finches descended from a common ancestor, the divergent beak shapes they evolved on separate islands enabled each species to exploit a different food source, a phenomenon that illustrates adaptation to disparate habitats.","at":"雖然這些雀鳥源自共同的祖先，但牠們在不同島嶼上演化出形狀各異的鳥喙，使每個物種都能充分利用不同的食物來源；這個現象說明了生物如何適應截然不同的棲息環境。"},{"w":"emissary","p":"n.","d":"representative, envoy sent on a mission.","c":"使者；密使","s":"The president sent a trusted emissary to the neighboring country to negotiate the release of fishermen who had been detained after accidentally entering disputed waters. The experienced diplomat met privately with government officials for several days, carefully discussing compromises that would satisfy both sides. His patient efforts succeeded, and the fishermen returned home safely. Newspapers praised the envoy for resolving the tense situation without damaging relations between the two nations.","t":"總統派遣一位信任的特使前往鄰國，協商釋放因誤入爭議海域而遭扣留的漁民。這位經驗豐富的外交官連續數天與政府官員私下會面，仔細討論能讓雙方都滿意的妥協方案。他耐心的努力獲得了成功，漁民們平安返家。報紙讚揚這位特使在不損害兩國關係的情況下化解了緊張的局勢。","as":"Hoping to avert an imminent war, the king dispatched a trusted emissary to the rival court, instructing him to cajole its belligerent ruler into accepting a truce before skirmishes along the border escalated further.","at":"國王希望避免一觸即發的戰爭，於是派遣一名親信特使前往敵對的宮廷，命他設法哄勸那位好戰的君主接受停戰，以免邊境上的小規模衝突進一步升級。"},{"w":"livid","p":"adj.","d":"furious; pale or bluish from anger.","c":"狂怒的；（臉色）鐵青的","s":"The homeowner was absolutely livid when he discovered that the construction company had accidentally demolished his garden wall and destroyed the rare orchids he had cultivated for twenty years. His face turned red, and he shouted at the workers until the site manager arrived to apologize. The company eventually rebuilt the wall and paid generous compensation. Nevertheless, the furious man insisted that no amount of money could replace his beloved plants.","t":"當這位屋主發現營建公司不小心拆掉了他花園的圍牆，還毀了他培育二十年的珍稀蘭花時，他簡直氣炸了。他滿臉通紅，對著工人們大吼，直到工地主任趕來道歉。這家公司最終重建了圍牆，並支付了優渥的賠償。儘管如此，這位怒不可遏的男子仍堅稱，再多的錢也無法取代他心愛的植物。","as":"Livid that a rival had appropriated his findings without credit, the chemist launched into a furious diatribe at the symposium, his voice stentorian and his face pale with rage, until the moderator admonished him to desist.","at":"這位化學家得知對手竊用他的研究成果卻未註明出處，氣得暴跳如雷，在研討會上發表了一篇激烈的抨擊演說，聲如洪鐘、臉色因憤怒而發白，直到主持人告誡他停止。"},{"w":"martinet","p":"n.","d":"strict disciplinarian.","c":"嚴格執行紀律的人","s":"The new boarding school principal was a martinet who punished students for the smallest violations, such as untied shoelaces, wrinkled uniforms, or arriving thirty seconds late to class. He conducted daily inspections of dormitory rooms and demanded complete silence in hallways. Some parents appreciated his emphasis on discipline, but many students felt anxious and oppressed. After a year of complaints, the school board asked him to adopt a more balanced approach.","t":"新任的寄宿學校校長是一位紀律極為嚴苛的人，會因為最微小的違規而處罰學生，例如鞋帶沒綁、制服有皺褶，或上課遲到三十秒。他每天檢查宿舍房間，並要求走廊保持絕對安靜。有些家長欣賞他對紀律的重視，但許多學生感到焦慮與壓抑。經過一年的抱怨後，校董會要求他採取更平衡的做法。","as":"A notorious martinet, the headmaster would reprimand pupils for the most trivial infractions, such as an untucked shirt, and even the most precocious students grew timorous in his presence, rarely daring to raise their hands even when they knew the answer.","at":"這位校長是出了名的嚴厲紀律執行者，連襯衫沒紮好這種芝麻小事都會斥責學生；即使是最早慧聰穎的學生，在他面前也變得畏畏縮縮，即使知道答案也很少敢舉手。"},{"w":"penchant","p":"n.","d":"strong liking or tendency.","c":"傾向；嗜好","s":"My grandfather has a penchant for collecting old radios, and his living room is filled with more than two hundred models from the 1930s to the 1970s. He spends weekends searching flea markets and repairing broken sets with remarkable patience. Visitors are always amazed to hear music playing from devices older than their parents. His strong fondness for these antiques has made him a well-known expert among collectors across Taiwan.","t":"我的祖父對收藏老收音機情有獨鍾，他的客廳擺滿了兩百多台從1930年代到1970年代的機型。他週末都在跳蚤市場尋寶，並以驚人的耐心修理壞掉的收音機。訪客們聽到比他們父母年紀還大的收音機播放出音樂時，總是驚訝不已。他對這些古董的濃厚喜愛，讓他成為全台收藏家之間知名的專家。","as":"The novelist's penchant for embellishing every scene with lurid detail earned her a voracious readership, though critics who favored laconic, understated prose dismissed her work as melodramatic and unworthy of serious literary attention.","at":"這位小說家偏好在每個場景中加入聳動的細節來渲染，因此吸引了一大群如飢似渴的讀者；不過偏愛簡潔、含蓄文風的評論家，則對她的作品不屑一顧，認為內容過於灑狗血，不值得文學界認真看待。"},{"w":"raconteur","p":"n.","d":"skilled storyteller.","c":"善於講故事的人","s":"The retired sea captain was a natural raconteur, entertaining guests at dinner parties with thrilling tales of storms, pirates, and exotic ports he had visited during forty years at sea. He paused at exactly the right moments to build suspense and imitated the voices of colorful characters he had met. Children and adults alike gathered around to listen. His grandchildren eventually recorded his stories and published them as a popular book.","t":"這位退休的船長是個天生說故事的高手，在晚宴上以他四十年航海生涯中經歷的暴風雨、海盜與異國港口等驚險故事娛樂賓客。他總能在恰到好處的時刻停頓以營造懸疑，還會模仿他遇過的各種有趣人物的聲音。大人小孩都圍過來聆聽。他的孫子們最終把他的故事錄下來，出版成一本受歡迎的書。","as":"A gifted raconteur, the retired diplomat could enthrall even the most lethargic dinner guests with jocose anecdotes about his peregrinations across three continents, from tense border negotiations to a disastrous banquet with a foreign prince.","at":"這位退休外交官是個很會說故事的人，他講述自己遊歷三大洲的詼諧軼事——從緊張的邊界談判到與外國王子共進的一場災難性晚宴，就連最無精打采的晚宴賓客也聽得入迷。"},{"w":"rail","p":"v.","d":"to complain bitterly, scold with abusive language.","c":"責罵；抱怨","s":"Every evening, the elderly man would sit in front of the television and rail against politicians, rising prices, and young people who spent too much time on their phones. His family grew accustomed to his daily complaints and often teased him gently about his grumpy speeches. Nevertheless, they admitted that some of his criticisms were surprisingly insightful. His granddaughter eventually encouraged him to express his opinions by writing letters to newspapers.","t":"每天晚上，這位老先生都會坐在電視機前痛罵政治人物、不斷上漲的物價，以及花太多時間滑手機的年輕人。他的家人已經習慣了他每天的抱怨，還常常溫和地取笑他那些脾氣暴躁的長篇大論。儘管如此，他們也承認他的一些批評出乎意料地一針見血。他的孫女最終鼓勵他透過投書報紙來表達自己的意見。","as":"For years, the reformer railed against the sinecures that party bosses granted to loyal cronies, denouncing the practice as a blatant waste of public funds that perpetuated a culture of corruption.","at":"多年來，這位改革者不斷痛罵黨內大老把閒差肥缺分給忠心親信，抨擊這種做法明目張膽地浪費公帑，並使貪腐文化得以延續。"},{"w":"raiment","p":"n.","d":"clothing, garments.","c":"衣服；服飾","s":"The museum's new exhibition displays the elaborate raiment worn by Qing dynasty emperors, including silk robes embroidered with golden dragons, jeweled belts, and ceremonial hats decorated with pearls. Each garment required months of skilled work by imperial tailors and embroiderers. Visitors are fascinated by the rich colors and intricate patterns. Curators explain that clothing in imperial China communicated rank and status, with specific colors reserved exclusively for the emperor. Photography is permitted.","t":"博物館的新展覽展出清朝皇帝所穿的華麗服飾，包括繡有金龍的絲綢龍袍、鑲有珠寶的腰帶，以及綴滿珍珠的禮帽。每一件衣服都需要宮廷裁縫與刺繡師數個月的精湛工藝。參觀者對豐富的色彩與繁複的圖案深深著迷。策展人解釋，在中國帝制時期，服裝傳達了階級與地位，某些特定顏色是專屬於皇帝的。展場允許拍照。","as":"Archaeologists unearthed the queen's burial raiment, a voluminous robe embroidered with gold thread, whose opulence reveals a royal court far more lavish than the austere one portrayed in official annals.","at":"考古學家出土了王后的陪葬衣裳——一件以金線刺繡的寬大長袍；其華麗程度顯示，當時的王室遠比官方史冊中所描繪的簡樸宮廷奢華得多。"},{"w":"rift","p":"n.","d":"split, break in friendly relations; crack.","c":"裂縫；不和","s":"A bitter argument over their late father's property created a deep rift between the two brothers, who had been extremely close since childhood. For nearly ten years, they refused to speak, attended family gatherings separately, and communicated only through lawyers. When one brother became seriously ill, however, the other rushed to the hospital. Their emotional reunion finally healed the painful division, and they later regretted the years they had wasted.","t":"一場關於已故父親遺產的激烈爭吵，在這對從小感情極好的兄弟之間造成了深深的裂痕。將近十年來，他們拒絕交談，分開參加家族聚會，只透過律師溝通。然而，當其中一位兄弟病重時，另一位立刻趕到醫院。他們動人的重逢終於化解了這段痛苦的隔閡，兩人事後也為浪費掉的那些年感到後悔。","as":"What began as a minor dispute over royalties became a permanent rift between the two songwriters, as acrimonious interviews exacerbated their grievances and exposed a deeper artistic incompatibility that no mediator could resolve.","at":"原本只是版稅上的小糾紛，最後卻演變成兩位詞曲創作者之間永久的決裂；雙方在訪談中言詞尖刻，加深了彼此的怨懟，也暴露出任何調解人都無法化解的深層藝術理念不合。"},{"w":"ruminate","p":"v.","d":"to think deeply, ponder repeatedly.","c":"沉思；反覆思考","s":"After receiving job offers from two excellent companies, the young engineer spent the entire weekend walking along the river to ruminate on her decision. She carefully considered each position's salary, location, training opportunities, and workplace culture. Rather than choosing quickly, she wanted to reflect deeply on her long-term goals. By Monday morning, she felt confident about her choice and accepted the offer that promised greater opportunities for learning. She has never regretted it.","t":"在收到兩家優秀公司的工作錄取通知後，這位年輕工程師花了整個週末沿著河邊散步，反覆思考她的決定。她仔細考量每個職位的薪資、地點、培訓機會與職場文化。她不想倉促決定，而是希望深入思考自己的長期目標。到了星期一早上，她對自己的選擇充滿信心，接受了那份能提供更多學習機會的工作。她從未後悔過。","as":"Confined to a prison cell for years, the dissident had ample time to ruminate on the vicissitudes of his political career, and his introspective journals later became a landmark text of twentieth-century literature.","at":"這位異議人士被關在牢房多年，有充裕的時間反覆思索自己政治生涯的起伏變遷；他那些內省的日記後來成為二十世紀文學中具里程碑意義的作品。"},{"w":"sullen","p":"adj.","d":"gloomy, silently resentful, ill-humored.","c":"慍怒的；悶悶不樂的","s":"After his parents took away his phone for failing two examinations, the teenager remained sullen for several days, refusing to join family meals and answering questions with single words. He spent most evenings alone in his room, silently resentful. His mother eventually sat down with him and helped him create a study plan. As his grades gradually improved, his gloomy mood disappeared, and he admitted that the punishment had been fair.","t":"在父母因他兩科考試不及格而沒收他的手機後，這名青少年好幾天都悶悶不樂，拒絕和家人一起吃飯，回答問題時也只說一兩個字。他大多數晚上都獨自待在房間裡，默默生著悶氣。他的母親最終坐下來陪他，幫他擬定了一份讀書計畫。隨著成績逐漸進步，他陰鬱的心情也消失了，他還承認這個處罰是公平的。","as":"The formerly gregarious boy grew sullen after his family relocated, and his teachers, noticing his apathy toward schoolwork and his refusal to speak in class, worried that he was maladjusted to his new surroundings.","at":"這個原本活潑合群的男孩在舉家搬遷後變得悶悶不樂；老師們注意到他對課業漠不關心、上課也不肯開口，擔心他無法適應新環境。"},{"w":"taut","p":"adj.","d":"tightly stretched; tense.","c":"緊繃的；緊張的","s":"The rope bridge across the deep canyon must be kept taut at all times, since loose cables could cause it to swing dangerously in strong winds. Engineers inspect the tension weekly and tighten the supports whenever necessary. Visitors crossing the bridge can feel the firmly stretched ropes vibrating beneath their hands. Despite its frightening appearance, the structure has operated safely for decades thanks to this careful maintenance and constant attention.","t":"橫跨深谷的吊橋必須隨時保持繃緊，因為鬆弛的纜繩可能會在強風中劇烈擺盪。工程師每週檢查張力，並在必要時拉緊支撐。走過吊橋的遊客能感覺到繃得緊緊的繩索在手下震動。儘管外觀令人害怕，多虧這樣細心的維護與持續的關注，這座橋數十年來一直安全地運作。","as":"As the climber ascended the sheer cliff, the rope grew taut beneath her weight, and the anxious spectators below watched in consternation as her tremulous fingers searched for a hold on the crumbling rock.","at":"攀岩者沿著陡峭的懸崖向上攀爬時，繩索因她的體重而繃得緊緊的；底下焦急的觀眾驚慌地看著她顫抖的手指在鬆動的岩壁上摸索著力點。"},{"w":"wistful","p":"adj.","d":"sadly longing, thoughtfully yearning.","c":"渴望的；惆悵的","s":"Looking through old photographs of her childhood village, the elderly woman grew wistful, remembering the rice fields, the small schoolhouse, and friends she had not seen in fifty years. The village had since been replaced by highways and apartment buildings. Her grandchildren noticed her longing expression and asked her to share stories about those days. Talking about the past made her smile, though a hint of sadness remained in her eyes.","t":"翻看著童年村莊的舊照片，這位老婦人不禁惆悵起來，想起了稻田、小小的校舍，以及五十年沒見的朋友們。那座村莊早已被高速公路與公寓大樓所取代。她的孫子們注意到她滿是思念的神情，便請她說說那段日子的故事。談起往事讓她露出了微笑，不過她的眼中仍帶著一絲哀傷。","as":"Leafing through faded photographs of his childhood village, the elderly expatriate grew wistful, recalling the idyllic summers and rustic simplicity of a way of life that had long since vanished.","at":"翻閱著兒時村莊褪色的照片，這位年邁的旅外人士不禁流露出惆悵的神情，回想起那些田園詩般的夏日，以及早已消逝的純樸鄉村生活。"},{"w":"yen","p":"n.","d":"strong desire, longing.","c":"渴望；熱望","s":"After months of living abroad, the exchange student developed a strong yen for Taiwanese beef noodle soup, bubble tea, and the lively atmosphere of night markets. She searched every Asian restaurant in the city, but nothing tasted quite like home. Her mother eventually mailed her a package of spices and a handwritten recipe. Cooking the familiar dish in her tiny apartment finally satisfied her deep craving and eased her homesickness.","t":"在國外生活了幾個月後，這名交換學生變得非常想念台灣的牛肉麵、珍珠奶茶以及夜市熱鬧的氛圍。她找遍了城裡每一家亞洲餐廳，但沒有一家的味道像家鄉。她的母親最後寄給她一包香料和一份手寫食譜。在她小小的公寓裡煮出這道熟悉的料理，終於滿足了她深切的渴望，也緩解了她的思鄉之情。","as":"Despite a lucrative career in finance, she had always harbored a yen for the stage, and at forty she jettisoned her corporate job to pursue acting, a decision her colleagues deemed imprudent.","at":"儘管在金融界有著收入豐厚的事業，她始終懷抱著對舞台的渴望；四十歲那年，她拋下公司的工作去追求演戲，同事們都認為這個決定太過輕率。"}]},{"unit":46,"cards":[{"w":"ascertain","p":"v.","d":"to find out about, discover.","c":"查明；確定","s":"Before publishing the shocking story, the editor asked reporters to ascertain whether the anonymous documents were genuine by contacting independent experts and comparing signatures with official records. The team spent two weeks verifying every detail, examining dates, letterheads, and the language used in each memo. Only after confirming their authenticity did the newspaper print the investigation. Media experts praised the careful process, which protected both the public and the newspaper's credibility.","t":"在刊登這則驚人的報導之前，總編輯要求記者們聯絡獨立專家、將簽名與官方紀錄比對，以查明這些匿名文件是否為真。團隊花了兩週時間核實每一個細節，檢查日期、信頭以及每份備忘錄中使用的語言。直到確認文件的真實性之後，報社才刊出這篇調查報導。媒體專家讚揚這個謹慎的流程，它同時保護了大眾與報社的公信力。","as":"To ascertain whether the manuscript was bona fide or an ingenious hoax, curators subjected its parchment to radiocarbon dating and scrutinized its handwriting alongside extant letters known to be the author's.","at":"為了查明這份手稿是真跡還是一場巧妙的騙局，館方人員對其羊皮紙進行放射性碳定年，並仔細比對其筆跡與現存、確知出自作者之手的信件。"},{"w":"burgeoned","p":"v.","d":"grew, flourished.","c":"激增；迅速發展","s":"Taiwan's bubble tea industry burgeonededuring the past three decades, growing from a few small shops in Taichung into a global business with thousands of stores across Asia, Europe, and North America. Entrepreneurs experimented with new flavors, toppings, and creative marketing, attracting young customers worldwide. Economists note that the drink's rapid expansion has created countless jobs and increased international interest in Taiwanese culture, tourism, and food products. Its popularity continues to grow.","t":"台灣的珍珠奶茶產業在過去三十年間蓬勃發展，從台中的幾家小店成長為一個在亞洲、歐洲與北美擁有數千家門市的全球事業。創業家們嘗試新的口味、配料與創意行銷，吸引了世界各地的年輕顧客。經濟學家指出，這種飲料的迅速擴張創造了無數的就業機會，也提升了國際間對台灣文化、觀光與食品的興趣。它的人氣持續成長。","as":"In the years after the railway arrived, the sleepy fishing village burgeoned into a bustling port, attracting a heterogeneous population of merchants and laborers and lining its formerly tranquil waterfront with myriad warehouses.","at":"鐵路通車後的幾年間，這個沉寂的小漁村迅速發展成繁忙的港口，吸引了形形色色的商人與勞工，昔日寧靜的濱水區也蓋滿了數不清的倉庫。"},{"w":"charisma","p":"n.","d":"quality of leadership inspiring enthusiasm.","c":"個人魅力；領袖氣質","s":"The young teacher's natural charisma transformed her history class into the most popular course in the school. Students were captivated by her energetic storytelling, warm humor, and genuine interest in their opinions. Even those who had previously disliked history began reading extra books and asking thoughtful questions. Colleagues tried to imitate her methods, but they admitted that her magnetic personality was difficult to copy, since it came from sincere enthusiasm.","t":"這位年輕老師天生的個人魅力，將她的歷史課變成了全校最受歡迎的課程。學生們被她充滿活力的講故事方式、溫暖的幽默感，以及對他們意見的真誠關心所吸引。即使是過去不喜歡歷史的學生，也開始閱讀課外書籍並提出深入的問題。同事們試著模仿她的教法，但他們承認，她充滿吸引力的個性很難複製，因為那是發自內心的熱忱。","as":"Historians still debate whether the movement's rapid growth owed more to its founder's magnetic charisma, which attracted thousands of ardent adherents, or to an economic crisis that made his promises of salvation so appealing.","at":"歷史學家至今仍在爭論，這場運動之所以迅速壯大，究竟主要歸功於創始人那種吸引數千名熱情追隨者的個人魅力，還是因為經濟危機使他承諾的救贖顯得格外誘人。"},{"w":"dearth","p":"n.","d":"lack, scarcity.","c":"缺乏；稀少","s":"Many rural hospitals in Taiwan face a serious dearth of doctors, as young physicians prefer working in large cities with better salaries, modern equipment, and more career opportunities. Patients in remote mountain villages sometimes travel several hours to receive basic medical care. The government has introduced scholarships requiring medical graduates to serve in underserved areas for several years. Officials hope these programs will gradually reduce the shortage and improve healthcare access nationwide.","t":"台灣許多偏鄉醫院面臨醫師嚴重短缺的問題，因為年輕醫師偏好到薪資較高、設備較現代、職涯機會較多的大城市工作。偏遠山村的病患有時要花好幾個小時的車程才能接受基本的醫療照護。政府推出了獎學金計畫，要求醫學系畢業生在醫療資源不足的地區服務數年。官員們希望這些計畫能逐漸減緩醫師短缺，並改善全國的就醫可近性。","as":"A chronic dearth of qualified teachers in rural districts has compounded existing educational inequities, prompting legislators to offer higher remuneration and housing subsidies to entice young aspirants into the profession.","at":"鄉村地區長期缺乏合格教師，使原本就存在的教育不平等更加惡化，促使立法者提供更高的薪酬和住房補助，以吸引有志的年輕人投身教職。"},{"w":"derived","p":"adj.","d":"received from a source, descended from.","c":"衍生出的；源自的","s":"Many common English words are derived from Latin and Greek, which is why studying roots can dramatically improve students' vocabulary. For example, the word 'telephone' combines Greek elements meaning 'far' and 'sound,' while 'benevolent' comes from Latin words meaning 'wishing well.' Teachers encourage learners to analyze these origins rather than memorizing definitions blindly. Understanding where words come from helps students guess the meanings of unfamiliar terms they encounter on examinations.","t":"許多常見的英文單字源自拉丁文與希臘文，這就是為什麼學習字根能大幅提升學生的詞彙量。例如，「telephone」結合了希臘文中「遠」與「聲音」的意思，而「benevolent」則來自拉丁文中「祝願他人好」的詞彙。老師們鼓勵學習者分析這些字源，而不是盲目地背誦定義。了解單字的來源，能幫助學生在考試中推測遇到的陌生字詞的意思。","as":"Although much of the English lexicon is derived from Latin, many ubiquitous everyday words, such as 'sky' and 'egg', originate in Old Norse, an obscure legacy of the Viking settlers who once occupied northern England.","at":"雖然英語詞彙大多源自拉丁文，但許多隨處可見的日常字詞，例如 sky 和 egg，其實來自古諾斯語；這是曾經占據英格蘭北部的維京移民所留下、鮮為人知的遺產。"},{"w":"disseminate","p":"v.","d":"to scatter, spread.","c":"散佈；傳播","s":"During the typhoon, government agencies used text messages, radio broadcasts, and social media to disseminate emergency information quickly to millions of residents. Alerts described evacuation routes, shelter locations, and safety instructions in several languages. This rapid communication system helped families prepare before the storm reached land. Disaster experts praised Taiwan's ability to spread accurate information efficiently, noting that clear warnings can significantly reduce injuries and deaths during natural disasters. Many lives were saved.","t":"颱風期間，政府機關利用簡訊、廣播與社群媒體，迅速將緊急資訊傳播給數百萬名居民。警報以多種語言說明疏散路線、避難所位置與安全須知。這套快速的通訊系統幫助家家戶戶在颱風登陸前做好準備。災害專家讚揚台灣能有效率地傳播正確資訊，並指出清楚的警告能在天然災害期間大幅減少傷亡。許多生命因此獲救。","as":"Gutenberg's printing press enabled reformers to disseminate pamphlets far more rapidly than church authorities could repress them, and the resulting flood of dissenting views precipitated a schism that permanently divided Western Christianity.","at":"古騰堡的印刷機讓改革者散播小冊子的速度遠快於教會當局壓制的速度，隨之湧現的大量異議觀點，促成了一場永久分裂西方基督教的大分裂。"},{"w":"dormant","p":"adj.","d":"asleep, resting, inactive.","c":"休眠的；靜止的","s":"Mount Fuji is considered a dormant volcano, having not erupted since 1707, but scientists warn that it could become active again in the future. Researchers continuously monitor underground temperatures, gas emissions, and small earthquakes around the mountain. Although it appears peaceful and attracts millions of tourists each year, the sleeping volcano still contains magma deep beneath its surface. Japanese authorities have prepared detailed evacuation plans in case of an eruption.","t":"富士山被視為一座休眠火山，自1707年以來就不曾噴發，但科學家警告它未來可能會再次活躍。研究人員持續監測山體周圍的地下溫度、氣體排放與小型地震。雖然它看起來平靜，每年吸引數百萬名遊客，這座沉睡的火山地底深處仍蘊藏著岩漿。日本當局已擬定詳細的疏散計畫，以防火山噴發。","as":"Mount Vesuvius had lain dormant for generations before its eruption in AD 79 obliterated Pompeii, burying the city's hapless inhabitants beneath meters of ash and volcanic debris that preserved their final moments with eerie precision.","at":"維蘇威火山沉寂了好幾代人之久，直到西元七十九年爆發，徹底摧毀了龐貝城，將城中不幸的居民埋在數公尺厚的火山灰與碎屑之下，也以令人毛骨悚然的精確度保存了他們生命的最後一刻。"},{"w":"encomium","p":"n.","d":"high praise, formal tribute.","c":"讚美；頌詞","s":"At the retirement ceremony, the university president delivered a moving encomium honoring the professor who had taught physics for forty-five years. She praised his brilliant research, his patient mentoring, and his generous support for struggling students. Former students stood to applaud as she described how his lessons had inspired countless scientific careers. The professor, deeply touched by the formal tribute, thanked everyone with tears in his eyes. The ceremony ended with a long standing ovation.","t":"在退休典禮上，大學校長發表了一篇感人的頌詞，向這位教授物理學四十五年的教授致敬。她讚揚他卓越的研究、耐心的指導，以及對學習困難學生的慷慨支持。當她描述他的課如何啟發了無數人的科學生涯時，昔日的學生們紛紛起立鼓掌。這位教授深受這篇正式頌辭感動，含著眼淚向大家道謝。典禮在全場起立鼓掌聲中結束。","as":"At the scientist's memorial, her former student delivered a moving encomium that extolled her impeccable integrity, her assiduous research, and the latent talent she had recognized and cultivated in so many young researchers.","at":"在這位科學家的追思會上，她昔日的學生發表了一篇感人的頌詞，讚揚她無可挑剔的正直品格、勤奮不懈的研究，以及她在許多年輕研究者身上發掘並培育的潛在才華。"},{"w":"factitious","p":"adj.","d":"artificial, sham, not genuine.","c":"人為的；虛假的","s":"Critics argued that the sudden public enthusiasm for the new smartphone was entirely factitious, created by paid social media influencers, fake online reviews, and carefully staged lines outside stores. Investigative journalists discovered that many people waiting in line had been hired by the company to create an impression of excitement. Consumer advocates warned buyers to be skeptical of artificial popularity, recommending independent reviews before making expensive purchases based on apparent trends.","t":"批評者認為，大眾對這款新智慧型手機突如其來的熱情完全是人為製造的，是由付費的社群媒體網紅、虛假的網路評論以及精心安排的店外排隊人潮所營造出來的。調查記者發現，許多排隊的人其實是公司花錢請來製造熱潮假象的。消費者權益倡議者提醒買家，對人為炒作的人氣要抱持懷疑，並建議在根據表面上的潮流做出昂貴的購買決定前，先參考獨立的評測。","as":"Economists argued that the advertising blitz had generated a factitious demand for the gadget, preying on consumers' insatiable but transient appetite for novelty, and predicted that sales would collapse once the vogue faded.","at":"經濟學家認為，這波廣告攻勢為該產品製造了虛假的需求，利用的是消費者對新奇事物永不滿足卻又短暫的胃口，並預測一旦熱潮退去，銷量就會崩跌。"},{"w":"genocide","p":"n.","d":"planned destruction of an entire people.","c":"種族滅絕","s":"After World War II, the international community adopted a convention defining genocide as a crime and committing nations to prevent and punish it. The agreement was inspired by the Holocaust, during which millions of Jewish people and others were deliberately murdered. Legal scholars explain that the term refers specifically to actions intended to destroy an entire national, ethnic, or religious group. Museums and schools teach this history so that future generations remember and prevent such crimes.","t":"第二次世界大戰後，國際社會通過了一項公約，將種族滅絕定義為罪行，並要求各國承諾防止與懲治此罪。這項協議的起因是納粹大屠殺，在那期間，數百萬猶太人與其他族群遭到蓄意殺害。法律學者解釋，這個詞特指意圖摧毀整個國家、民族或宗教群體的行為。博物館與學校教授這段歷史，好讓後代子孫銘記並防止這類罪行再次發生。","as":"The international tribunal indicted the former general for genocide, presenting comprehensive evidence that he had orchestrated the extermination of an ethnic minority and dismissing his claim of mere wartime chaos as fallacious and abhorrent.","at":"國際法庭以種族滅絕罪起訴這名前將軍，提出全面的證據證明他策劃了對一個少數民族的屠殺，並駁斥他所謂「只是戰時混亂」的說詞既謬誤又令人憎惡。"},{"w":"hyperbole","p":"n.","d":"exaggerated figure of speech.","c":"誇張法；誇飾","s":"When the student complained that his backpack weighed a thousand kilograms and that he had waited a million years for lunch, his teacher laughed and explained that he was using hyperbole. Such deliberate exaggeration, she noted, is common in everyday speech and literature, where it creates humor or emphasizes strong feelings. Students then practiced identifying overstatements in poems and advertisements. Many were surprised to discover how frequently writers use this technique.","t":"當這名學生抱怨他的書包重達一千公斤、他等午餐等了一百萬年時，老師笑著解釋他正在使用誇飾法。她指出，這種刻意的誇張在日常對話與文學中很常見，能製造幽默或強調強烈的情感。學生們接著練習在詩和廣告中找出誇張的說法。許多人驚訝地發現，作家使用這種技巧的頻率竟如此之高。","as":"When the senator declared that a modest fuel tax would 'annihilate the middle class', analysts dismissed the claim as hyperbole, noting that its pecuniary impact on typical households would be trivial and that such histrionics impede rational debate.","at":"當參議員宣稱一項溫和的燃料稅會「消滅中產階級」時，分析師認為這只是誇大其詞，並指出此稅對一般家庭造成的經濟影響微乎其微，而這種誇張的作秀只會妨礙理性的討論。"},{"w":"internecine","p":"adj.","d":"mutually destructive, relating to conflict within a group.","c":"內訌的；兩敗俱傷的","s":"The political party lost the national election largely because of internecinedisputes among its own leaders, who spent months attacking one another publicly instead of campaigning against their opponents. Rival factions leaked embarrassing documents, criticized each other's policies, and competed for influence. Voters grew tired of the constant infighting and lost confidence in the party's ability to govern. Analysts concluded that the destructive internal conflict had weakened everyone involved. Recovery took years.","t":"這個政黨在全國大選中落敗，主要是因為黨內領袖之間的內鬥，他們花了好幾個月互相公開攻擊，而不是向對手展開競選。敵對的派系洩露令人難堪的文件、批評彼此的政策，並爭奪影響力。選民對不斷的內鬨感到厭倦，也對這個政黨的執政能力失去信心。分析人士斷定，這場具破壞性的內部衝突讓所有相關的人都元氣大傷。重新振作花了好幾年。","as":"Internecine strife between rival factions so debilitated the revolutionary movement that the regime it had sought to oust was able to quell the uprising with little resistance and execute its leaders within a matter of weeks.","at":"敵對派系之間的自相殘殺嚴重削弱了這場革命運動，以致於它原本試圖推翻的政權，幾乎不費吹灰之力就平定了這場起義，並在短短幾週內處決了起義領袖。"},{"w":"munificent","p":"adj.","d":"generous, lavish.","c":"慷慨的；豐厚的","s":"The small rural school received a munificentedonation of ten million dollars from a former student who had become a successful technology entrepreneur. The money funded a new library, science laboratories, and full scholarships for every graduate who attended university. The donor explained that his teachers had believed in him when his family was struggling financially. Villagers celebrated his generous gift, which transformed educational opportunities for an entire generation of children.","t":"這所偏鄉小學收到了一位成為成功科技創業家的校友捐贈的一千萬美元鉅款。這筆錢用於興建新的圖書館、科學實驗室，並為每位升大學的畢業生提供全額獎學金。這位捐贈者解釋說，在他家境困難時，他的老師們都相信他。村民們慶祝他慷慨的捐贈，它改變了整整一代孩子的受教機會。","as":"Thanks to a munificent bequest from an anonymous alumnus, the university was able to underwrite full scholarships for indigent students and restore its library, an imposing edifice dating to 1890.","at":"多虧一位匿名校友慷慨的遺贈，這所大學得以為清寒學生提供全額獎學金，並修復建於一八九〇年、宏偉壯觀的圖書館。"},{"w":"nepotism","p":"n.","d":"favoritism toward relatives.","c":"裙帶關係；任人唯親","s":"Employees complained about nepotism after the company's owner appointed his inexperienced son as vice president, bypassing several qualified managers who had worked there for decades. The young man had graduated only a year earlier and had never managed a team. Morale declined sharply, and several talented employees resigned. Business experts warn that favoring relatives over qualified candidates can damage productivity, discourage loyal workers, and ultimately harm a company's long-term success.","t":"在公司老闆越過好幾位已在公司工作數十年的合格主管，任命他毫無經驗的兒子為副總裁之後，員工們抱怨任人唯親。這位年輕人一年前才剛畢業，從未管理過任何團隊。士氣急遽下滑，好幾位優秀的員工辭職。商業專家警告，偏袒親屬而非合格人選，可能會損害生產力、打擊忠誠員工的士氣，最終危害公司的長期成功。","as":"Shareholders protested the chairman's nepotism when he named his inexperienced son to head the firm's flagship division, relegating a seasoned executive whose expertise had long been an integral asset to the company.","at":"董事長任命毫無經驗的兒子掌管公司的旗艦部門，並將一位資深主管降職，股東們紛紛抗議他任人唯親；而這位主管的專業長久以來一直是公司不可或缺的資產。"},{"w":"obloquy","p":"n.","d":"dishonor, disgrace, public criticism.","c":"辱罵；恥辱","s":"The once-respected judge endured years of public obloquy after investigators revealed that he had accepted expensive gifts from lawyers appearing in his courtroom. Newspapers published harsh editorials, former colleagues refused to associate with him, and strangers insulted him in restaurants. He resigned in disgrace and eventually moved abroad to escape the constant criticism. His downfall became a cautionary example discussed in law schools throughout the country. He has never returned home since then.","t":"這位曾經備受尊敬的法官，在調查人員揭露他收受出庭律師的昂貴禮物之後，承受了多年的公開辱罵。報紙刊登嚴厲的社論，昔日同事拒絕與他往來，陌生人在餐廳裡當面辱罵他。他在恥辱中辭職，最終移居國外以逃避不斷的批評。他的垮台成為全國法學院討論的一個警世範例。此後他再也沒有回過國。","as":"After his duplicity was exposed, the senator, once revered by voters, endured relentless obloquy from the press, and former allies, loath to be associated with the scandal, quietly abandoned him.","at":"在他的欺騙行為曝光後，這位曾深受選民尊崇的參議員遭到媒體無情的抨擊與唾罵，昔日的盟友也不願與醜聞扯上關係，悄悄地離他而去。"},{"w":"potentate","p":"n.","d":"ruler, monarch, powerful person.","c":"統治者；君主；有權勢者","s":"The ancient potentate ruled his vast empire with absolute authority, commanding enormous armies, collecting heavy taxes, and building magnificent palaces decorated with gold and precious stones. No one dared to question his decisions, and those who opposed him were exiled or imprisoned. Historians studying his reign note that his powerful rule brought both impressive architectural achievements and tremendous suffering for ordinary citizens who paid for his extravagant projects. His palaces still attract tourists.","t":"這位古代君主以絕對的權威統治他廣大的帝國，指揮龐大的軍隊、徵收沉重的賦稅，並興建以黃金與寶石裝飾的宏偉宮殿。沒有人敢質疑他的決定，反對他的人不是被流放就是被監禁。研究他統治時期的歷史學家指出，他強大的統治既帶來了令人讚嘆的建築成就，也讓為他奢華工程買單的平民百姓承受了巨大的苦難。他的宮殿至今仍吸引遊客。","as":"Surrounded by a fawning entourage, the potentate governed his vast realm by fiat, issuing arbitrary decrees on taxation, marriage, and trade that no court or council in the kingdom dared to challenge.","at":"在一群阿諛奉承的隨從簇擁下，這位君主以命令統治他廣大的國土，隨意頒布關於稅收、婚姻與貿易的專斷法令，國內沒有任何法院或議會敢於挑戰。"},{"w":"prerogative","p":"n.","d":"exclusive power or right.","c":"特權；專有權","s":"In Taiwan, granting special pardons to convicted criminals is the prerogative of the president, a power that no other official possesses. This exclusive right is rarely used and usually applies only in exceptional circumstances, such as serious health conditions or significant new evidence. Legal scholars debate whether such authority should be limited further. Supporters argue that it provides an important final safeguard against injustice within the legal system. Recent cases remain controversial.","t":"在台灣，給予受刑人特赦是總統的特權，這是其他任何官員都沒有的權力。這項專屬的權利很少使用，通常只適用於特殊情況，例如嚴重的健康問題或重大的新證據。法律學者爭論這種權力是否應該受到進一步的限制。支持者則認為，它為司法體系中的不公正提供了一道重要的最後防線。近期的案例仍具爭議。","as":"Under the constitution, granting pardons is the president's exclusive prerogative, yet critics contend that using it to exonerate cronies convicted of extortion sets a dangerous precedent that future leaders could invoke to shield their own associates from justice.","at":"根據憲法，赦免權是總統獨享的特權；然而批評者認為，用這項權力替犯下勒索罪的親信脫罪，將開創危險的先例，未來的領導人可能援引此例，讓自己的親信逃避法律制裁。"},{"w":"prevarication","p":"n.","d":"lie, deviation from the truth.","c":"支吾其詞；撒謊","s":"When asked directly whether his company had known about the product defects, the executive responded with a long prevarication, discussing industry standards, customer satisfaction, and future improvements without ever answering the question. Reporters grew frustrated by his evasive statements. Internal documents released later proved that managers had known about the problems for years. His misleading answers damaged public trust even more than the defects themselves. The company's chief executive resigned soon afterward.","t":"當被直接問到公司是否早已知道產品有瑕疵時，這位主管支吾其詞地說了一大段話，談論業界標準、顧客滿意度與未來的改進，卻始終沒有回答問題。記者們對他閃爍其詞的說法感到沮喪。後來公開的內部文件證明，管理階層多年前就知道這些問題。他誤導人的回答對大眾信任的損害，甚至比產品瑕疵本身還嚴重。公司的執行長不久後便辭職下台。","as":"Under incisive cross-examination by the defense attorney, the witness's prevarication soon became apparent to the jury, as his evasive answers grew increasingly incoherent and his alibi could not be corroborated by any of his alleged companions.","at":"在辯護律師犀利的交互詰問下，證人的說謊行為很快就在陪審團面前露出馬腳：他閃爍其詞的回答越來越前言不對後語，而他的不在場證明也無法獲得任何一位他所稱的同伴證實。"},{"w":"sophistry","p":"n.","d":"false reasoning, deceptively clever argument.","c":"詭辯","s":"The debate judge criticized the team's argument as pure sophistry, explaining that their clever-sounding logic contained a hidden flaw that made their conclusion false. They had claimed that because some successful people dropped out of school, education must be unnecessary for success. Although the reasoning sounded persuasive at first, it ignored millions of counterexamples. The judge encouraged students to recognize deceptive arguments that use clever language to disguise faulty thinking.","t":"辯論賽的評審批評這支隊伍的論點純屬詭辯，並解釋他們聽起來很聰明的邏輯中藏有一個錯誤，使結論不能成立。他們主張，因為有些成功人士中途輟學，所以教育對成功而言並非必要。雖然這個推論乍聽之下很有說服力，卻忽略了數百萬個反例。評審鼓勵學生辨識那些用巧妙言詞掩飾錯誤思維的欺騙性論點。","as":"Through relentless questioning, Socrates exposed the sophistry of his interlocutors, demonstrating that arguments which seemed cogent at first rested on dubious premises and could readily be construed to support contradictory conclusions.","at":"蘇格拉底透過不斷追問，揭穿了對話者的詭辯，證明那些乍看之下頗具說服力的論點，其實建立在可疑的前提上，而且很容易被解讀成支持相互矛盾的結論。"},{"w":"tyro","p":"n.","d":"novice, beginner.","c":"新手；初學者","s":"As a complete tyro in rock climbing, the office worker nervously watched experienced climbers scale the steep cliff with apparent ease. Her instructor patiently taught her basic safety techniques, including how to tie knots and position her feet correctly. During her first attempt, she climbed only three meters before asking to come down. Six months later, however, the former beginner successfully reached the top of the same challenging route. She now teaches others.","t":"身為一個攀岩的新手，這位上班族緊張地看著經驗豐富的攀岩者輕而易舉地爬上陡峭的崖壁。她的教練耐心地教她基本的安全技巧，包括如何打繩結以及正確擺放雙腳。第一次嘗試時，她只爬了三公尺就要求下來。然而六個月後，這位曾經的初學者成功登上了同一條具挑戰性路線的頂端。她如今教導其他人。","as":"Although still a tyro in the laboratory, the young researcher displayed such adroit technique and perspicacious judgment that her mentor soon entrusted her with the lab's most delicate experiments, a singular honor for a first-year student.","at":"雖然在實驗室裡還是個新手，這位年輕研究者卻展現出靈巧熟練的技術和敏銳的判斷力，指導教授很快就把實驗室裡最精細的實驗交給她負責，這對一年級學生來說是非比尋常的殊榮。"}]}];
